1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 d6 5. Nc3 O-O 6. Nf3 Nbd7 7. O-O e5 8. e4
exd4 9. Nxd4 a5 {So as to play 10......Nc5 without White answering b4.} 10. Be3
Nc5 11. f3 $2 {Blocks the Bishop and proves to be a handicap later on.} ({
Better is} 11. h3) 11... Re8 12. Qc2 a4 {Threatening a3.} 13. a3 c6 {So as to
play ......Qb6 followed by ......Nb3.} 14. b4 axb3 15. Nxb3 Nxb3 16. Qxb3 Rb8
17. Rad1 Be6 18. Qa4 Nd7 19. Ne2 Nb6 20. Bxb6 Qxb6+ 21. Kh1 Ra8 22. Qb4 Qxb4
23. axb4 Bxc4 24. Rfe1 Ra2 25. Nc1 Rb2 26. Nd3 Bxd3 27. Rxd3 Rxb4 28. Rxd6 c5
29. Rc1 Ra8 30. Rcd1 (30. Rxc5 Ra1+ {wins the Bishop.}) 30... c4 31. Rc1 c3 {
Here White offered a draw which was not accepted so White resigned. A
reasonable game.} 0-1

