{Opponents age about} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bc4 Nc6 4. d3 Bg4 5. h3 Bxf3 6.
gxf3 g6 7. Bg5 Bg7 8. c3 Nf6 9. f4 Qd7 10. Bb5 a6 11. Ba4 b5 12. Bb3 O-O-O {
Setting a simple trap.} 13. Bxf7 $4 {White falls into the trap} e6 14. Qg4 $4
Nxg4 15. hxg4 Qxf7 16. Na3 Rde8 17. f5 b4 18. cxb4 $4 Bxb2 19. Rb1 $4 Bxa3 20.
Rb3 $4 Bxb4+ 21. Ke2 $4 Nd4+ 22. Ke3 $2 Nxb3 23. axb3 Qg7 24. f6 Qf8 25. Bh6 $4
Qxf6 26. Rc1 $2 Qh4 27. d4 $4 Qxh6+ 28. f4 c4 $4 {I was getting bored and not
concentrating. I played PxP but found I could not do so as it put me in check,
and as I had touched that P I had to move it.} 29. bxc4 Qh2 30. d5 $4 Qd2+ 31.
Kf3 Qxc1 32. dxe6 Rxe6 33. f5 gxf5 34. exf5 Qe3+ 35. Kg2 Re4 36. f6 Rxg4+ 37.
Kh2 Qg1+ 38. Kh3 Qg3# {I wish all my games wereas easy as that, slaughter.
Hayes I (6) v Barnhill Jr (0)} 0-1

