1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Qb6 4. Bxc6 Qxc6 5. d4 $4 Qxe4+ 6. Be3 cxd4 7. Nxd4
$4 (7. Qxd4) 7... Qxg2 8. Rf1 Qxh2 9. Nc3 d6 10. Qd3 a6 {To prevent 11.Nb5} 11.
O-O-O Nf6 12. Na4 Nd7 {or White plays 13.Nb6} 13. Rfe1 g6 {White's attack is
building up. My Queen is stranded and by capturing Pawns I am behind in
development. I must castle quickly as I have not a very good defensive
position, and the Queen has no good retreat.} 14. Bg5 $2 e5 15. Nf3 Qxf2 16.
Re2 Qg3 17. Nc3 Nc5 18. Qe3 Bg7 {It is worth a Pawn to safegaurd the King.} 19.
Rxd6 O-O 20. Red2 Ne6 21. Ne4 Qg4 22. Nf6+ {I need an exchange so I can push
my KS Ps} Bxf6 23. Bxf6 Qf4 $1 24. Qxf4 Nxf4 $1 (24... exf4 {The text is
better than}) 25. Rd8 Bg4 $2 ({Better is....} 25... Be6 {though the e-Pawn is
lost.}) 26. Nxe5 Raxd8 27. Bxd8 Be6 28. a4 $2 Ne2+ 29. Kd1 Nf4 30. b4 Nd5 $1
31. Ba5 $4 b6 32. Nd7 Nc3+ $1 33. Kc1 Bxd7 34. Rxd7 bxa5 35. bxa5 Nxa4 36. c4
$2 Nc5 $1 {This move shows the weakness of White's 33rd.} 37. Ra7 $2 Nb3+ 38.
Kc2 Nxa5 39. Kc3 Rc8 40. Rxa6 Nxc4 ({Not} 40... Rxc4+ $2 41. Kd3 {Winning the
Knight as the Rook will be needed elsewhere.}) 41. Kd3 h5 {I had won the first
4 rounds as White against E.Gregg & A.Evans and with Black against Joyner &
Alaway. The competition was open to 3rd, 4th, 5th, & 6th form} 0-1

