{Opponent age 14 (Southall Grammar)} 1. e3 e5 2. Nc3 d5 3. Nf3 $2 e4 4. Nd4 Nf6
5. d3 Bb4 6. a3 Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 O-O 8. Be2 c5 9. Nb3 Qd6 10. d4 $2 (10. dxe4)
10... c4 11. O-O $4 cxb3 12. cxb3 Nc6 13. c4 Ne7 {This Knight is heading for
g4 thus building up a KS attack.} 14. c5 Qc7 15. Qe1 $2 Ng4 $1 16. Bxg4 Bxg4
17. Bd2 Bd7 18. Bb4 Rfe8 19. Rc1 Nf5 20. c6 $2 bxc6 21. f3 Nh6 22. fxe4 Rxe4
23. Bd2 Rae8 24. a4 $2 Rxd4 25. Qf2 {Prevents the Black Knight from moving.}
Rde4 26. Rce1 $2 Bc8 $1 27. Bc3 $2 Ba6 28. Re2 $2 Bxe2 29. Qxe2 Rxe3 30. Qd2
Qb6 $4 {I was becoming overconfident and not thinking.} 31. Bd4 Re2 32. Qd3 c5
33. Bc3 c4+ 34. Qd4 {He was under the impression that he was threatening mate.}
Qxd4+ 35. Bxd4 cxb3 36. Rb1 Rc8 37. Bxa7 (37. Rxb3 $4 Rc1#) 37... Ra8 $2 38.
Rc1 $2 (38. Rxb3 Rxa7 39. Rb8+) 38... b2 $1 39. Rb1 Rxa7 40. Rd1 $2 Rxa4 41.
Kf1 $2 Rc2 42. Re1 b1=Q $4 43. Rxb1 g6 44. Kg1 d4 45. Rd1 Ra3 $1 46. h3 Nf5 47.
Kh1 d3 48. Kg1 Rxg2+ 49. Kxg2 Ne3+ 50. Kf3 Nxd1 51. Ke4 d2 52. Kd4 Nf2 53. Kc4
d1=Q 54. Kb4 Re3 55. Kc4 Re8 56. Kc5 Rc8+ 57. Kb6 Qb3+ 58. Ka7 Rc1 59. Ka6 Ra1#
{Black kept getting horribly cramped. Some of my later moves are weak due to
lack of concentration due to overconfidence.} 0-1

