1. d4 {Opponent info; Age 12 plays Bd 1 for HCGS 1st & 2nd form teams} Nf6 2.
Nf3 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. Bg5 d5 5. e3 O-O 6. Bd3 Nbd7 7. O-O c5 8. Re1 Qb6 9. b3
Nh5 $2 {This leaves 2Pawns undefended.} 10. Bxe7 Re8 11. Nxd5 Qc6 12. c4 b6 {
So as to play f6 trapping the B} 13. e4 cxd4 14. e5 {To prevent .......f6} Nc5
$2 15. Nxd4 Qb7 16. h3 $2 Ne6 17. Nf3 Nhf4 $3 18. Nxf4 $2 Nxf4 19. Ba3 ({
both moves lose a Pawn} 19. Bd6) (19. Bg5) 19... Rxe5 $1 20. Rxe5 Bxe5 21. Qe1
$5 Bxa1 22. Qe8+ Kg7 23. Be4 $3 Be6 $1 ({Not} 23... Bd7 $4 24. Bf8+ Kf6 25.
Qe7#) 24. Qxe6 Nxe6 25. Bxb7 Rd8 26. Bd5 Nd4 27. Ng5 $4 Ne2+ 28. Kf1 $4 Nc3 $3
{This prevents the White Bishop from moving due to the threat of mate on d1,
whilst at the same time attacking the a-Pawn & KBishop this is why 28.Kf1 was
a blunder.} 29. Nxf7 $4 Rxd5 30. cxd5 Kxf7 31. d6 Ke6 32. f4 Nxa2 $2 33. g4 Nc3
34. f5+ $1 Kd7 35. fxg6 hxg6 36. h4 Nb5 $1 37. Bc1 Nxd6 38. h5 gxh5 39. gxh5
Ke6 40. Kg2 Kf5 41. Kh3 Bf6 42. h6 $2 Kg6 43. Kg4 Nf7 44. Kf4 $4 Bg5+ 0-1

