{Opponent info: Age 14.9 (on 01\09\59) William Ellis School Highgate Bd 29 for
Middlesex boys} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d6 4. d5 e5 5. Bg5 Bg7 6. e4 O-O 7.
Be2 Nbd7 8. Nf3 Nc5 9. b4 Na6 {Hoping for P-b5} 10. a3 c6 11. O-O cxd5 12. Nxd5
Nc7 13. Nxf6+ Bxf6 14. Bh6 Re8 15. Qd2 b5 $6 16. Rac1 ({At the time I thought} 
16. cxb5 d5 17. exd5 e4 {attacking Knight & Rook}) 16... Bb7 17. Qe3 a6 18.
Rfd1 bxc4 19. Rxc4 Ne6 $1 {Threatening 20......g5.} ({At the time I thought} 
19... Bxe4 20. Qxe4 d5 {forking Queen & Rook, but I realised I could not take
with the Pawn , after the Queen moves, as he plays 21.RxQ. Luckily I had 2nd
thoughts.}) 20. g3 (20. h4 {loses a Pawn}) 20... g5 21. h3 $2 (21. h4) 21...
Kh8 {so as to play 22......Rg8 23......Rg6} 22. Nh2 Rg8 23. Ng4 (23. Bh5) 23...
Bc8 {to get rid of the KRook} 24. f4 Nd4 $2 25. fxe5 Bxg4 $1 26. Bxg4 ({Not} 
26. hxg4 $4 Bxe5 {followed by} 27. Z0 Qf6 28. Z0 Nxe2+ 29. Kh1 Bxg3) 26... Bxe5
(26... dxe5 {might be better}) 27. Rcxd4 Qf6 $3 ({Not} 27... Bxd4 $4 28. Qxd4+
f6 (28... Rg7 $4 29. Qxg7#)) 28. R4d2 ({now if} 28. Bxg5 $4 Qxg5 29. Qxg5 $2 ({
and if} 29. Re1 $2 Qxe3+ $1 30. Rxe3 Bxd4) 29... Bxd4+ {Wins Rook for Bishop.})
28... Qxh6 29. Qf3 Rgf8 30. Rc2 $2 Qg6 31. Bf5 Qf6 {Now White can't move the
Bishop without losing a Pawn.} 32. Rh2 $2 Rac8 33. h4 $2 Rc3 $1 34. Rd3 $8 Rfc8
35. hxg5 (35. Rxc3 {loses only a Pawn}) 35... Rc1+ 36. Kf2 $4 {losing move}
R8c2+ 37. Ke3 Re1+ (37... Rxh2) (37... Qxg5+ $3) 38. Re2 Qxg5+ 39. Kf2 Rcxe2+
40. Qxe2 Rxe2+ 41. Kxe2 Bxg3 42. Rxd6 Bxd6 {The game took over 3 hours. A good
game, one of my best.} 0-1

