threatens Q-f2+} 10. Rf1 $2 Nxh2 $1 11. Nxh2 Qxg3+) 10... Qf2+ 11. Kd2 Qxg2 12.
Nxc7+ Kd7 13. Nxa8 Qf2 {I must seek freedom by exchanges. by playing} 14. Qg1 {
I force the exchange of Qs} ({Black threatens} 14. Z0 Qe3+ 15. Ke1 Nf2) 14...
Qxg1 15. Rhxg1 h6 16. h3 Nf6 17. Ne1 $2 ({I was going to play} 17. Ne1 Z0 18.
Nc2 Z0 19. Nb4 Z0 20. Nd5 Z0 {To play} 21. Nac7 {safely}) 17... Kd8 18. g4 Be6
19. Nf3 Kd7 20. g5 $1 Nh5 $8 (20... Ne8 {can't take the White N}) (20... hxg5
21. Nxg5 Rxa8 22. Nxe6 Kxe6 23. Rxg7) 21. Nb6+ $1 {I had to lose the N so I
gave him double isolated Ps} axb6 22. h4 Ne7 23. a4 Ra8 24. e4 {To prevent P-e5
} (24. Z0 e4 25. dxe4 Bxc4) 24... Ng6 25. b3 Ngf4 26. d4 Ng6 $2 27. d5 Bh3 {
Here I offered a draw - accepted. I was happy to draw with the Middlesex U-16
champ 1959. At this stage I had 2pts and was 18th out of 108+} 1/2-1/2

