1. e4 c5 2. Ne2 d6 3. Nbc3 Nf6 4. d3 g6 5. g3 Bg7 6. Bg2 Qb6 7. Be3 (7. b3 $4
Nxe4 $1) 7... Qxb2 8. e5 Nfd7 9. Qb1 (9. exd6 Bxc3+) (9. Rb1 Qa3 10. Rxb7 Bxb7
11. Bxb7 Bxe5 12. Bxa8 Bxc3+ {wins}) 9... Qxb1+ 10. Rxb1 Nb6 {to prevent 11.
Rxb7 or 11. Bxb7} 11. Nd5 Nxd5 12. Bxd5 Nc6 13. exd6 exd6 14. Bf4 Kd7 $2 {
to prevent doubled Pawns in case of 15.Bxc6} 15. Bxf7 Nb4 16. c3 $4 Nxd3+ 17.
Kf1 Nxf4 18. Nxf4 Bxc3 19. Be6+ $1 Kd8 ({if I now play} 19... Kc7 $4 {or Ke7??}
20. Nd5+ {wins the Bishop}) 20. Bxc8 Kxc8 (20... Rxc8 {loses the b-Pawn}) 21.
Nd5 Bd4 22. Kg2 b6 {so as to bring the Queens Rook into play} 23. Rhe1 (23.
Rhe1 Z0 {White threatened} 24. Re6 Kd7 25. Re7+ Kd8 26. Re6 Kd7 27. Re7+ Kd8
$11) 23... Rf8 $3 24. f3 Rf7 {prevents 25.Re7} 25. Re6 Kd7 26. Re4 Re8 27. Rf4
Rxf4 28. Nxf4 Kc6 {stops the Knight returning to d5} 29. h4 b5 30. g4 b4 31.
Rd1 a5 32. g5 a4 33. Kf1 Re3 34. Ne2 $4 Rxf3+ 35. Kg2 $4 Rf2+ 36. Kh3 Rxe2 37.
Rf1 Rxa2 38. Rf7 b3 39. Rxh7 a3 40. Rf7 Rf2 0-1

