1. Nf3 c5 {Offering to transpose to a sicillian} 2. c4 Nc6 3. e4 {this leaves
the d-Pawn weak} d6 4. d3 (4. d4 $142) 4... g6 5. Nc3 Bg7 6. Nd5 e6 7. Nf4 Nf6
8. g3 b6 9. Bg2 Bb7 10. Qa4 (10. O-O $142) (10. Qc2 $142) 10... O-O 11. O-O Qc7
{Black's position is very strong} 12. Bh3 {this serves no particular purpose}
h6 13. g4 {useless he must watch against b4-b5} g5 14. Ne2 a6 {a wasted move}
15. Bg2 h5 {giving up a Pawn for an attack} 16. gxh5 {D.H.Smith is rather
greedy and grabs a Pawn. Will he burn his bridges?} Nxh5 17. Nxg5 Bf6 18. Nf3
Kg7 {Now we see the white Queen is on the wrong wing} 19. Nf4 Nxf4 20. Bxf4 Rh8
{being a greedy player he expects me to be one too and to take the bP as he
does not defend it.} 21. Rab1 Rag8 22. Qc2 Kf8 23. Rfe1 Be5 24. Bxe5 {
exchanging his defensive pieces} Nxe5 25. Nxe5 dxe5 26. f3 f5 27. Qc3 $2 {why?}
Qg7 (27... Qh7 {might be better}) 28. Qc2 $2 Qh6 29. Kf1 $2 {White is lost}
Qxh2 30. Re2 $2 Qg3 $1 31. Rd1 Rh1+ 32. Bxh1 Qg1# 0-1

