1. Nf3 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. d4 O-O 5. O-O d6 6. c4 Nbd7 7. Nc3 e5 8. d5
a5 9. e4 Nc5 10. Bg5 h6 11. Bxf6 Bxf6 12. Ne1 {I thought he had done this to
play 13.f4} Bg7 {to play ......f5} 13. Nd3 Nd7 14. Rc1 f5 {I decided in this
game I would win or die gloriously (Amen)} 15. exf5 gxf5 (15... Rxf5 16. Be4)
16. Qc2 Nb6 17. Ne2 Bd7 18. b3 Kh8 (18... a4 {might have been better}) 19. a4 {
to prevent 18.....a5} Rg8 20. c5 Nc8 21. cxd6 cxd6 22. Qc7 b6 (22... Qxc7 {
loses a P.} 23. Rxc7 Rd8 (23... Be8 24. Rxb7) 24. Rxb7) 23. Qxd8 Rxd8 24. Nc3
Ne7 25. Nb2 e4 26. Rfd1 Rac8 27. Nc4 $8 Be8 $8 {Adjourned.} 28. Bf1 {[sealed
move]resumption on 22/2/60} Bxc3 29. Rxc3 Bf7 $4 30. Bh3 $1 Nxd5 $4 31. Nxd6
Be6 (31... Rxc3 32. Nxf7+) (31... Rxd6 32. Rxc8+) 32. Rxc8 Bxc8 33. Nf7+ {
An interesting game. In my adjourned analysis I had not reckoned on 30.Bh3!
The sealed moves I considered were: 28.Bf1; 28.f3; 28.Nb1; 28.g4; 28.Ne2; 28.
Na2} 1-0

