{Player info: Age 15; Our Lady & St Anselm's; Middlesex Jr} 1. Nh3 e5 2. g3 d5
3. d3 c5 4. Bg2 h6 {So the White KN has nowhere to move} 5. f4 Nc6 6. O-O Bg4
7. Nf2 Bh5 8. f5 ({the idea is to win the B by} 8. f5 Z0 9. g4) 8... f6 9. g4
Bf7 10. e4 d4 11. Nd2 g6 12. Nh1 gxf5 13. Rxf5 Be6 14. Rf2 Qe7 15. Ng3 O-O-O
16. Nh5 Bf7 17. Ng3 Bg6 18. Nf5 Qd7 19. Bh3 Kb8 {Removing the K from a
dangerous diagonal.} 20. Nf1 Nge7 21. N1g3 Nxf5 22. Nxf5 h5 23. Nh4 hxg4 24.
Nxg6 Rxh3 25. Rxf6 Bg7 26. Rf5 g3 27. Kg2 Rxh2+ 28. Kxg3 Rh7 29. Qf3 Qd6 30.
Bg5 $4 Qxg6 31. Kf2 Rdh8 32. Rg1 Rh2+ 33. Ke1 Rxc2 34. Be3 Rc1+ $1 35. Bxc1
Qxg1+ 36. Kd2 Rh2+ {Resigns the Q is lost. An interesting game. A lot of
useless N moves by White, and not a very impressive opening by the first
player either.} 0-1

