{Opponent info: Age 9!; Minet I; Middlesex Jr} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Nc3 g6 4.
b3 Bg7 5. Bb2 Nf6 6. Bc4 $2 Nxe4 7. Qe2 Nxc3 8. Bxc3 Bxc3 9. dxc3 O-O 10. O-O-O
Nc6 11. Rhe1 Qa5 $4 12. Kb2 a6 13. Bd5 Re8 $2 14. Bxc6 bxc6 15. Rxd6 Be6 $1 16.
Rxe6 $1 (16. Rxc6 $4 Bd7 {wins the R}) 16... fxe6 17. Qxe6+ Kg7 (17... Kf8 18.
Ng5 $18) 18. Qe5+ Kg8 {Adjourned.} 19. Qe6+ {[sealed move]} ({I thought his
sealed move would be} 19. Ng5 {whe I would play......} e6 20. Nxe6 Ra7 {
with the threat of} 21. Z0 Rae7) 19... Kh8 20. Ng5 Rg8 (20... Z0 {the threat is
} 21. Qf7 Z0 22. Qxh7#) 21. Qxe7 Rg7 22. Qf6 $3 Qb6 $4 ({I should have given
the exchange back with. or 22.......Qc7} 22... Qd8 {there is no other move}) (
22... Qb6 {I had played this in order to meet......} 23. Re7 {....with....} Ra7
{but did not realise until too late that I would be mated by.} 24. Re8#) 23.
Re7 {mate is unstopable. I should never have got my Queen stranded on a5. I
was psychologically outplayed. He insisted on singing, whistling, jumping up &
down on his chair & talking to himself. He took three times as long as me for
his moves. It really drfove me mad.} 1-0

