1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be2 b5 7. Be3 e6 8. O-O
b4 9. Na4 Nxe4 10. Bf3 Bb7 11. Rc1 Nd7 12. c4 bxc3 13. Bxe4 cxb2 $4 14. Bxb7
bxc1=Q 15. Qxc1 Be7 16. Nc6 Qc7 17. Bxa8 Qc8 18. Nxe7 Kxe7 19. Qxc8 Rxc8 20.
Bf3 Rc2 21. h3 Rxa2 22. Bc6 $2 {with 3 Pawns v 2 Bishops I haven't a hope} Ne5
23. Nc3 $4 Rc2 24. Bb7 Rxc3 25. Bxa6 d5 $4 26. Bd4 {2 Pawns v Bishop is much
better} Rc6 27. Bb5 Nf3+ 28. gxf3 Rc8 29. Bxg7 $4 Rg8 30. Kh2 Rxg7 31. Rg1 Rxg1
32. Kxg1 d4 33. Kf1 e5 {getting the Pawns onto Black squares} 34. Ke2 f6 35.
Kd3 Ke6 36. Bc4+ Kf5 37. Ke2 Kf4 38. Be6 h6 ({not} 38... h5 $4 39. h4 $1) 39.
h4 f5 40. Ke1 Kxf3 41. Bxf5 e4 $2 (41... Kf4 $1) 42. h5 Kf4 43. Bg6 Kf3 44. Kd2
e3+ 45. fxe3 dxe3+ 46. Ke1 Kg4 47. Ke2 Kf4 48. Bf7 Ke4 49. Bd5+ $4 Kf4 $4 50.
Bf3 Kg5 51. Kxe3 Kf5 52. Be4+ Kg4 53. Bg6 Kg5 54. Ke4 Kf6 55. Kf4 Kg7 56. Kf5
Kg8 57. Kf6 Kh8 58. Be4 Kg8 59. Kg6 Kh8 60. Kxh6 Kg8 61. Kg6 Kh8 62. h6 $2 Kg8
63. Kg5 Kh8 64. h7 $2 Kg7 {Only in a very casual game is it possible to
recover from a 2 piece deficit.} 1/2-1/2

