{Opponent Info: HGCS I Bd} 1. c4 c5 {hoping to transpose to a sicillian.} 2.
Nc3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Na4 $2 {Attempting a Pawn snatch already.} e6 5. Nxc5 {
Greedy! He'll burn his fingers if not careful} b6 6. Bg2 Nc6 7. Na4 Bb7 8. e3
Rc8 9. d4 Ba8 10. Ne2 Nxd4 $1 {Regaining the P due to my lead in development.}
11. Bxa8 Nxe2 12. Qxe2 (12. Bg2 Nxc1 13. Rxc1 {Retaining his better B might
have been better for White.}) 12... Rxa8 13. O-O Ne7 14. Rb1 O-O 15. b3 d5 16.
Rd1 Qc7 17. cxd5 Nxd5 18. Bb2 Bxb2 $1 19. Rxb2 $1 ({Not} 19. Nxb2 $4 Nc3) 19...
b5 $2 {I touched this Pawn by mistake and had to move it.} 20. Qxb5 Rab8 21.
Qd3 Rfd8 (21... Rbd8 $142) 22. Rc2 Qa5 $2 {This move shows the casual way I
played, being disturbed by all and sundry} 23. Rc5 Nb4 $2 24. Rxa5 Rxd3 25.
Rxd3 Nxd3 26. Rxa7 Nb4 {Adjourned I had two choices at the adjournment resign
or play on. I had won the competition but could be caught and have to share
1st place, so needed a draw to win outright. I tried for a draw. I wasn't
hopeful.} 27. Nc5 {[sealed move] Surprise! play resumed 13/5/60} ({I had
prepared for} 27. a3 Nc6 28. Ra6 Rxb3 29. Rxc6 Rxa3 30. Nc5 Rc3 {with a faint
hope of exchanging off all the Ps to draw.}) 27... Rc8 28. Ra5 $2 Nxa2 29. Rxa2
Rxc5 30. b4 $2 {throws away the win} (30. Rb2 $142) 30... Rc1+ $1 31. Kg2 Rb1
$1 {Obeying end-game principles. Get the Rook BEHIND the passed Pawn} 32. Ra8+
Kg7 33. Rb8 Kf6 {The game was played, with the boardon a chair, in a crowded
hall with frequent disturbances hence the inferior moves (Black's 23rd). I
have 10.5/11 now. L.Wheately is at least 1.5 pts back with only 1 Rd to play}
1/2-1/2

