1. e4 c5 2. f4 d6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 g6 5. Bc4 Bg7 6. O-O a6 7. a3 $2 b5 8.
Bxf7+ $4 {This sacrifice does nothing but leave Black with a won game. 
(Perhaps this is the influence of World Champion Tal)} Kxf7 9. Ng5+ Ke8 10. b4
c4 11. d3 cxd3 12. cxd3 (12. Qxd3 {With attacking chances might be better.})
12... h6 $1 13. Nf3 Nxe4 $1 {I have often played this move to my advantage in
the Sicillian.} 14. dxe4 Bxc3 15. Qd5 $2 Bxa1 {With my extra Bishop I want to
exchange.} 16. Qxa8 Qb6+ 17. Kh1 Bd7 18. Qd5 (18. Z0 Bc6 {was threatened
winning the Queen}) 18... Qc6 19. Qd3 Qc4 20. Rd1 Qxd3 21. Rxd3 Bc6 22. e5 $2
Bxf3 23. Rxf3 dxe5 24. Rh3 exf4 25. Bxf4 Rf8 26. Rf3 ({naturally not.} 26. Bxb8
$4 Rf1#) 26... Nc6 27. Bxh6 Rxf3 28. gxf3 Bb2 29. Bd2 Bxa3 30. h4 Bxb4 31. Bxb4
Nxb4 32. Kh2 Nd5 33. Kh3 Nf6 (33... b4 $142) 34. f4 e6 35. Kg3 b4 36. Kf2 b3 {
A fine game with a bad sacrifice backfiring.} 0-1

