1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 g6 5. Bg5 Bg7 6. O-O Nxe4 $1 7. c3 (7. dxe4
Bxb2 8. Nbd2 Bxa1 9. Qxa1) 7... Nxg5 8. Nxg5 O-O 9. Re1 e6 10. Nf3 Nc6 11. Nbd2
b6 12. Qc2 Bb7 13. Re3 Rc8 $1 14. Rae1 d5 {Strong centre} 15. Bb3 d4 16. cxd4 (
{If White was in a sacraficial mood} 16. Rxe6 $2 fxe6 17. Bxe6+ {which is
spectacular, but would lose.}) 16... Nxd4 $1 17. Qd1 Nxf3+ 18. Nxf3 Bxb2 19.
Qd2 Bd4 20. Nxd4 cxd4 (20... Qxd4 {I was going to play this for no apparent
reason. The text secures the c-file}) 21. Re5 Rc5 22. Qb4 Rxe5 23. Rxe5 Qc7 24.
Re1 Qc3 $1 {Forces the Queen exchange due to the threat of mate.} 25. Qxc3 dxc3
26. Bc4 Bd5 27. Rc1 Bxc4 28. dxc4 Rd8 {defending the c-Pawn} 29. h3 (29. Rxc3
$4 Rd1#) 29... Rd2 30. Kf1 Rxa2 31. Rxc3 Kf8 32. g4 Ke7 33. Rd3 Ra4 (33... Rc2
$142) 34. Rc3 Kd6 35. Ke2 Kc5 36. Kd3 e5 {Loosening the White King's sphere of
influence} 37. f3 f5 38. g5 $2 Kb4 39. Kc2 Ra2+ 40. Kd3 Ra3 41. Rxa3 Kxa3 42.
Kc3 a5 {A very good game} 0-1

