1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qg4 {I was pleased winning the previous game 
(v Mr Bentley) and was experimenting in this relativly unimportant game.} g6 5.
e5 Ne7 6. a3 Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 Nd7 8. Bd3 c5 9. Bh6 $2 (9. dxc5 $1) 9... c4 10. Be2
Nf5 11. Bg5 Qa5 12. Kd2 Nb6 13. Bd1 (13. Bf1 $142) 13... Na4 14. Ne2 b5 15. h4
$1 h6 16. Bf6 $1 h5 17. Qf4 {The Queen can't leave the 4th due to the threat
of .......Nxd4} Rg8 18. Rh3 $3 {Long range defence and KS attack.} Rb8 19. Kc1
Qc7 {Black finde he is not making much headway, unlike White who has the
innitiative at last!} 20. g4 $3 {Thewinning move} hxg4 (20... Ne7 21. Qg3 {
is not much better}) 21. Qxg4 Nh6 22. Qg5 Nf5 23. h5 $1 Kf8 24. h6 $1 Qa5 25.
h7 {A VERY interesting game indeed. Black's QS barrage is cleverly blockaded
and a KS counter finds all Black's pieces badly placed. After move 20 Black
was lost.} 1-0

