{Opponent Info: Age 11-12; Middlesex Jr (U-18); Drayton Manor Sch C.C.} 1. c4
e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 Bc5 4. d3 O-O 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. O-O d5 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Nc3 Nf6
9. a3 Be6 10. b4 Bd4 11. Nxd4 $4 {The losing move. I should have realised the
Pawn on d4 would be very powerful} ({I should have played} 11. Bb2) 11... exd4
12. Ne4 ({not} 12. Nb5 $4 a6) 12... Nxe4 13. Bxe4 Bd5 14. Bxd5 Qxd5 15. Bb2
Rfe8 {My weak e3 square begins to show.} 16. Rc1 Re7 17. Rc5 Qd6 18. Re1 a5 19.
Qb3 {to play 20.Rd5 winning the d-Pawn} axb4 20. axb4 Rae8 21. Kf1 $2 {This
will allow mating threats with Qh1 in future.} Qh6 22. h4 Qd2 23. Rd5 $2 (23.
Qc2 $142) 23... Rxe2 24. Rxe2 Qxe2+ 25. Kg2 Re3 $1 26. Bxd4 $4 Rxd3 $1 ({
hoping for} 26... Nxd4 $4 27. Rd8+ Re8 28. Rxd4) ({the text isbetter than} 
26... Qf3+ 27. Kh3 Qh1+ 28. Kg4) 27. Qb2 $2 Qf3+ 28. Kh2 Qxd5 29. Qe2 Qd7 30.
Qxd3 Qxd4 31. Qf5 Qd8 32. Qe4 Qe7 {Exchanging Queens is suicide for me.} 33.
Qf5 Qd8 34. Qe4 {Hoping for the draw by repetition.} Qc8 35. b5 Na7 36. Qd5 c6
37. bxc6 Nxc6 (37... bxc6) 38. Qc5 h6 {tired of the mating threats} 39. Kg2 Qc7
40. Kg1 b6 41. Qe3 Qd8 42. Qe4 Na5 43. Qe5 {prevents the b-Pawn advance} Nc4
44. Qb5 Nd2 45. Qe2 Qd5 {threatening trouble with 46.......Nf3+} 46. f4 Nf3+
47. Kf2 Nd2 48. Qe8+ Kh7 49. Ke3 Nc4+ 50. Kf2 Qc5+ 51. Kg2 Qd5+ 52. Kf2 Qd4+
53. Kg2 Nd6 54. Qb8 Nc4 55. Qc8 $2 Qe4+ 56. Kf2 Nd2 57. Qc7 Qf3+ 58. Ke1 ({not
} 58. Kg1 $4 Qf1+ 59. Kh2 Nf3#) 58... Qe3+ 59. Kd1 Nf1 60. Kc2 Qc5+ $1 {
this demnonstrates the weakness of 55.Qc8?} 61. Qxc5 bxc5 62. Kc3 Nxg3 63. Kc4
Ne2 64. Kxc5 Nxf4 65. Kd4 Ng6 66. h5 Nf4 67. Ke4 Nxh5 68. Kf5 Ng3+ 69. Kg4 Ne2
70. Kh5 g6+ 71. Kg4 f6 72. Kh4 h5 73. Kh3 g5 74. Kg2 f5 75. Kf3 Nd4+ 76. Kg3
h4+ 77. Kh3 Kg7 78. Kg2 Kf6 79. Kh2 Ke5 80. Kg2 Ke4 81. Kh3 Kf3 82. Kh2 g4 83.
Kh1 h3 84. Kh2 g3+ 85. Kg1 h2+ 86. Kh1 g2+ 87. Kxh2 Kf2 {A rather farcial
end-game but there was a vague chance that Black casually pushing Pawns might
stalemate me.I might have done better to reach a stalemate position with only
my Queen able to move then sacrifice the Queen. This game shows the difficulty
of playing Queen and Pawn end-games.} 0-1

