5. Qf3 $1 e6 $8 6. Nb5 $1 Qe7 $2 (6... f6 {is necessary}) (6... Z0 {threat} 7.
Nd6+ Ke7 8. Qxf7+ Kxd6 9. Qxg7 {wins}) 7. Bf4 $2 (7. Nc7+) 7... e5 $2 8. Be3 $2
Na6 9. Bd5 Rb8 10. Nxa7 Nb4 11. Nxc8 Rxc8 12. Bb7 $2 (12. Bb3 $142) 12... Rc7
13. Bd5 Nxc2+ 14. Kd2 Nxa1 15. Qd1 Nf6 16. Qxa1 O-O 17. Nf3 Nxd5 18. exd5 Qd6
19. b3 $4 Qxd5 $2 (19... e4 $1) 20. b4 $4 e4 21. Qc1 Qxd3+ 22. Ke1 exf3 23.
gxf3 Bc3+ 24. Bd2 Re8+ 25. Kd1 cxb4 26. Re1 Qxf3+ 27. Kc2 Bxd2+ 28. Kxd2 Rxe1 (
28... Rxc1 29. Rxe8+ Kg7 30. Kxc1) 29. Qxc7 $2 Qxf2+ 30. Kd3 Qe3+ 31. Kc4 Rc1+
32. Kd5 Rxc7 33. Kd6 Qc5# {I played this game after a long cycle ride to the
venue and was worn out, hence the dim moves} 0-1

