Nf3 Bb7 6. O-O e6 7. d3 Be7 8. a3 O-O 9. Bf4 Rc8 10. Re1 d5 11. cxd5 Nxd5 12.
Bd2 Bf6 13. Rc1 Re8 14. Qb3 Ba8 15. Nb5 Ne5 16. Nxe5 Bxe5 17. e4 $2 {
thisleaves the d-Pawn weak and blocks the Bishop} Nf6 18. Bf1 $2 {defends the
d-Pawn but leaves the e-Pawn in the lurch} Nxe4 $1 19. dxe4 Qxd2 20. Rcd1 Qxb2
21. Qxb2 Bxb2 22. Nd6 Bxa3 $1 23. Nxc8 Rxc8 {three united Pawns for the
exchange} 24. Ra1 Bb4 25. Red1 $2 a5 26. Ba6 Rb8 27. Rd3 $2 Bxe4 28. Rd7 g6 29.
Rad1 Bd5 $1 30. Rc7 a4 31. Rc8+ Rxc8 32. Bxc8 a3 33. Rc1 a2 34. Ba6 Bc3 {
Quite an enjoyable game I played 5 other games with R.Hornsby 3 of which I won
and 2 I lost (all quick friendly)} 1-0

