Ne4+ 14. Ke1 Nxd2 15. Bxd2 Bxf3 16. gxf3 Nc6 17. Bg2 Nd4 18. Nxd4 Qh4+ 19. Kf1
Qxd4 20. Rd1 Rac8 21. e3 $2 Qc4+ 22. Kg1 Qxc2 23. Kf2 Qa2 24. f4 Rc2 25. Ke2
Qxa3 26. Rc1 Rxc1 27. Bxc1 $2 Qxb4 28. Bh3 Rc8 29. f5 Rc2+ 30. Kf3 Qb1 31. fxe6
fxe6 32. Rd1 Rxc1 33. Rxd7 Qa2 34. Rd8+ {there is no perpetual check} Kf7 35.
Rd7+ Kf6 36. Rd6 Qxh2 37. Rxe6+ Kg5 {An easy win. J.Rigarlsford had 6/11} 0-1

