1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 bxc6 5. Nxe5 Qe7 6. d4 d6 7. Nxc6 Qxe4+
8. Qe2 Qxe2+ 9. Kxe2 Bb7 10. d5 {Collins-Humphries Hayes CC B Tourn 8/7/60} Ne7
{probably better than 10.Nf6} 11. Nxe7 Bxe7 12. c4 O-O 13. Re1 Bf6 14. Nc3 Rab8
15. Kd3 {Black's Bishops make the white King vulnerable here.} Bc8 $1 16. Rb1
Bf5+ 17. Ne4 Rfe8 18. g4 $1 Rxe4 (18... Bxg4 $4 19. Nxf6+ $5 gxf6 20. Rg1 $1)
19. Rxe4 Bxe4+ 20. Kxe4 Be5 $2 (20... Re8+ $1 21. Kf3 Re1) 21. f4 $1 Bf6 22. g5
$1 {Forcing Black to close the g-file or block the Rook from it.} Be7 23. b3
Re8 24. Kf3 f6 25. h4 Rf8 26. Kg4 Kf7 27. Bb2 Ke8 28. Re1 Kd7 29. Re2 {To
prevent a future .....Rf2 after the Pawn exchange} Rh8 30. Kf5 g6+ 31. Kg4 f5+
32. Kf3 Re8 33. Re6 c6 34. Kg3 c5 ({I expected} 34... cxd5 35. cxd5 Rc8) 35. h5
$1 Bd8 $5 (35... gxh5 36. Rh6 {is good for White.}) 36. hxg6 $1 hxg6 (36...
Rxe6 37. dxe6+ Kxe6 38. gxh7 {wins}) 37. Rxg6 Re2 $2 38. Rg7+ Ke8 $2 39. Rg8+
Kd7 40. g6 $3 Rxb2 41. Rxd8+ $3 Kxd8 42. g7 {An enjoyable game} 1-0

