1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 d5 4. e3 b6 5. Bg2 Bb7 6. Nc3 Bb4 7. Qb3 $2 (7. Qc2
$142) 7... Ba5 {It's a pity I had not castled, for if I had I could play 7.....
..dxc without him replying 8.Qa4+} 8. Qc2 O-O 9. b3 Nc6 10. Ba3 Nb4 11. Bxb4 ({
If White had played} 11. Qb1 {Black must not play} Nd3+ $4 {hoping for} 12.
Qxd3 (12. Ke2 $3) 12... dxc4) 11... Bxb4 12. a3 Be7 {Best it leaves the a-Pawn
as a target} 13. Nge2 c5 14. cxd5 Nxd5 15. O-O ({Not for example} 15. Nf4 $4 {
because of....} Nxe3 $3) 15... Rc8 16. Nxd5 Bxd5 ({not} 16... cxd4 $4 {due to}
17. Nxe7+) 17. Bxd5 cxd4 18. Qd3 (18. Bc4 dxe3 19. Qb1 exf2+ 20. Kxf2 Bf6 (
20... Rxc4 21. bxc4 Bc5+ $4 22. Kg2 Qa8+)) 18... Qxd5 19. e4 Qd6 20. Qxd4 Qxd4
21. Nxd4 Bf6 $1 22. Rad1 Rc3 $1 23. Rfe1 Bxd4 24. Rxd4 Rxb3 25. Ra4 a5 26. f4 {
To prevent 26......e5......Ra8....b5} Rc8 27. e5 Rc2 $1 28. Rd1 g6 29. Ra1 Rbb2
$1 {It's all over} 30. h4 {Useless} Rg2+ 31. Kf1 Rxg3 32. Ke1 $4 Rg1# {This
game and the final had to be played off in one morning, hence it was hurried
and only lasted an hour. An enjoyable game.} 0-1

