1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nge7 4. d4 d5 $2 5. Nxe5 Qd6 6. Nc3 dxe4 7. Nxc6
Nxc6 8. d5 a6 9. Nxe4 Qb4+ 10. Nc3 Bd7 $4 ({why not?} 10... axb5) 11. dxc6 bxc6
12. Qe2+ Qe7 13. Bxa6 $4 {I was a piece up , had to hurry, was overconfident
hence the hasty blunder} Rxa6 14. Qxe7+ Bxe7 15. O-O O-O 16. Re1 Bb4 17. Bd2 c5
18. a3 Ba5 19. b4 Bb6 ({not} 19... cxb4 $4 20. axb4 $1) 20. b5 Raa8 21. a4 c6
22. Re7 Ra7 23. bxc6 Bxc6 24. Rxa7 Bxa7 25. Nb5 $2 {I should have tried to
keep the passsed Rook Pawn} Bxb5 26. axb5 Bb6 27. Ba5 Ra8 28. Bc3 Rxa1+ 29.
Bxa1 f6 30. c4 {to prevent c4} Kf7 31. Kf1 Ke6 32. Ke2 Bc7 $2 33. Kf3 h5 (33...
Bxh2 $4 34. g3) 34. h3 h4 35. Ke4 Bb6 36. f4 g6 37. Bc3 f5+ 38. Kf3 Bd8 39. Be1
Be7 $2 40. b6 Kd6 {Adjourned drawn. I intended playing 41.Ba5 with a possible
win. There was no time to continue the game and it was agreed a draw. We were
both joint winners of the trophy. The competition was open to staff and pupils.
} 1/2-1/2

