1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e3 c6 6. Nf3 Qa5 7. Bxf6 (7. Bd3
dxc4 8. Bxc4 Ne4 $1) 7... Nxf6 8. a3 {to prevent ....Bb4} Ne4 9. Qa4 {forces
the Queen exchange} Qxa4 10. Nxa4 dxc4 11. Bxc4 b5 12. Bd3 f5 $2 {leaves 2
backward Pawns} 13. Nc3 Nf6 14. O-O Bd6 15. Ng5 h6 (15... Z0 16. e4 $140 fxe4
17. Ncxe4 Nxe4 18. Bxe4) 16. Nf3 Kf7 17. Rac1 Bb7 18. Nd2 g5 19. f3 f4 20. e4
e5 21. d5 $1 cxd5 22. Nxb5 {gaining ar least a QS Pawn majority} Bb8 $2 23. Nc7
$1 {winning at least the exchange} dxe4 24. fxe4 ({not} 24. Bxe4 $4 Bxe4 25.
Nxe4 Bxc7 $1) 24... Bxe4 25. Bxe4 Nxe4 26. Nxe4 Bxc7 27. Rxc7+ Ke6 28. Rd1 Rhd8
$2 29. Rxd8 Rxd8 30. Rxa7 Kf5 31. Nc3 Rb8 32. b4 Rc8 33. Ne2 Rd8 34. Rc7 Rd1+
35. Kf2 e4 36. Rc5+ (36. Z0 $140 e3+ 37. Kf3 Rf1#) 36... Kg6 37. Rc1 Rd3 38.
Rc3 e3+ 39. Ke1 Rd2 40. Rb3 g4 $4 41. Nxf4+ {Interesting. I played one other
game with P.Adams but had to rush it due to the time and I lost after a mad
attack.} 1-0

