1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e3 c6 6. Nf3 Qa5 7. Bxf6 Nxf6 8. a3
Ne4 9. Qa4 Qxa4 10. Nxa4 dxc4 11. Bxc4 b5 12. Bd3 Nxf2 {Black improves on his
12th move (12.f5 yesterday)} 13. Kxf2 bxa4 14. Bc2 Rb8 15. Rab1 Ba6 16. Bxa4
Bb5 ({I expected...} 16... Bd3) 17. Bc2 Be7 18. b4 O-O 19. Ne5 Rfc8 20. Rbc1 f6
21. Nd7 Rb7 22. Nc5 {Forcing Black to lose the two Bishops} Bxc5 23. dxc5 Bc4
$4 24. Bxh7+ Kxh7 25. Rxc4 Rd8 26. Rd4 Rxd4 27. exd4 Kg8 28. Re1 Kf7 29. Kf3 a5
30. Rb1 a4 $2 {A weak move freeing my Rook and the Pawn is eventually lost.}
31. Re1 Rd7 32. Ke4 f5+ 33. Ke3 (33. Kd3 e5 $1) 33... Kf6 34. Rb1 Rb7 35. Kd3
Rb5 36. Kc4 g6 37. Rd1 Rb8 {Black has no constructive plan and can do nothing}
38. h4 Rb7 39. Rh1 {beginning a plan to get the Rook to a7} Rb8 40. h5 gxh5 41.
Rxh5 Kg6 42. Rh1 Kg7 {preventing the entry of my Rook on the seventh} 43. g4
fxg4 44. Rg1 g3 45. Rxg3+ Kf6 46. Kd3 $1 Rh8 47. Rf3+ Ke7 (47... Kg7 {The
White King penetrates the seventh}) 48. Kc4 Rb8 {Notethe black Rook is tied to
the defence of b5, whereas the white Rook is mobile} 49. Rh3 $1 {Black can no
longer gaurd the seventh} Rb5 50. Rh7+ {Black can resign} Kd8 51. Ra7 {At last
the Rook is at a7} Rb8 52. Rxa4 Rb5 53. Ra8+ $1 Kd7 54. Rh8 $1 {I can now
force the exchange of Rooks} Rb7 55. Rh7+ Kc8 56. Rxb7 Kxb7 57. a4 Ka6 58. b5+
Kb7 59. Kb4 Kc7 60. bxc6 Kxc6 61. a5 Kb7 62. Kb5 Kc7 63. a6 Kb8 64. Kc6 Ka7 65.
Kd7 Kb8 66. c6 Ka7 67. c7 {A very good game! An excellently played end-game by
White. About the best end-game I have played to date.} 1-0

