1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. c4 a6 4. a4 $6 {doubtful} Qc7 5. g3 b6 6. Bg2 Bb7 7. d3
d6 8. b3 Nf6 9. O-O g6 10. Bb2 Bg7 11. Qe2 (11. e5 {Might be better}) 11... O-O
12. Nc3 Nc6 13. Rfe1 Nb4 14. Na2 Nc6 15. Nc3 Rfe8 16. Rad1 d5 $1 {This advance
needed careful calculation} 17. exd5 exd5 18. Qd2 (18. Nxd5 Nxd5 19. Qxe8+ Rxe8
20. Rxe8+ Bf8 {is interesting}) 18... d4 19. Ne2 Re7 20. Bc1 Rae8 21. Qc2 Na5
22. Nf4 Bxf3 23. Rxe7 Bxd1 24. Rxe8+ Nxe8 25. Qxd1 Nf6 {To prevent 26.Nd5} 26.
Bd2 Bh6 $2 27. Nd5 Nxd5 28. Bxh6 Nc3 29. Qc2 Qe5 30. Bd2 (30. Z0 g5 31. Z0 Qf6)
30... Nc6 $4 31. Bxc6 Qe2 $1 {Threatening 32.....Nd1} 32. Bf3 Qxf3 33. Bxc3
dxc3 34. Qxc3 g5 35. a5 g4 {Threatening perpetual check} 36. Qd2 bxa5 37. Qg5+
Kf8 38. Qxc5+ Kg7 39. Qg5+ Kf8 40. Qd2 Kg8 41. Qxa5 $4 Qd1+ {I lost one other
game to P.Adams very stupidly.} 1/2-1/2

