{Opponent Info: Gunnebury Grammar Sch, W.3} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4.
O-O Nf6 5. d4 exd4 6. e5 {My first 6 moves took 30 seconds, including writing
them on my scoresheet.} Nh5 $2 (6... d5 $142) 7. Bxf7+ Kxf7 8. Ng5+ Kf8 9. Qxh5
Qe7 10. Nd2 g6 ({after} 10... Nxe5 11. Re1) 11. Nxh7+ {Giving the Knight up
for 2 Pawns and getting 3 connected passed Pawns} Rxh7 (11... Qxh7 $142) 12.
Qxg6 d5 {Move 12 and I have 4 united passed Pawns!} 13. Nf3 $1 Bh3 $4 14. Bh6+
$1 ({thinking that} 14. gxh3 Qg7 {wins} ({NOT} 14... Rg7 $4 15. Bh6)) 14... Rg7
15. Bxg7+ Qxg7 16. Qxg7+ Kxg7 17. gxh3 Re8 18. Rfe1 $2 {dozy} Nb4 19. Re2 d3
20. cxd3 Nxd3 21. Kh1 Nf4 22. Rc2 Nd3 23. Kg2 Rg8 24. Rg1 Kf7+ 25. Kf1 Rxg1+
26. Kxg1 b6 27. Ng5+ Kg6 28. e6 $3 Nf4 $4 ({not} 28... Kxg5 $4 29. Rxc5 Nxc5 (
29... Kf6 30. Rxd5) 30. e7) 29. Rxc5 $3 Nxe6 30. Rc6 {Not having played for 2
weeks (on holiday) I was a little out of touch and played unevenly. M.T.Walsh
came 29th= on 3.5pts} 1-0

