{Opponent info: Downer Grammar Sch, Edgeware} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4.
Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be2 Bg7 7. Be3 O-O 8. O-O a6 9. Nb3 b5 10. a3 {timid} Bb7
11. Bd3 Nc6 12. Nd2 Rc8 13. f4 e6 14. Nf3 Ne7 {to strengthen f5} 15. h3 Nh5 16.
Qe1 Bxc3 $2 17. bxc3 Nf6 18. Bd2 {to protect e4 & c3} Nd7 {leaves holes on the
KS} 19. Rb1 Qb6+ $2 {doubtful as will be shown by White's 21st} 20. Kh1 (20.
Be3 $2 Qa5) 20... h5 21. c4 $1 Nc5 $8 22. cxb5 Nxd3 23. cxd3 axb5 24. a4 Ba6
25. axb5 Bxb5 26. Ba5 Qa6 27. Rf2 $2 Bxd3 28. Rb6 Qc4 29. Rxd6 Qxe4 30. Qxe4
Bxe4 31. Ng5 Bd5 32. Rd7 Nf5 33. Bb4 Rc1+ $3 34. Kh2 Ra8 $3 {Threatening ....
Ra1 then ....Rh1#} 35. Rxf7 e5 $1 36. Rxf5 {forced because of Ra1} gxf5 37.
fxe5 Raa1 {threatening 38.......h4 & 39.......Rh1#} 38. Kg3 h4+ $1 39. Kxh4 {
forced} Rc4+ 40. Kh5 Rxb4 41. Rxf5 Raa4 42. g4 Kg7 43. e6 Ra8 44. Rf7+ (44.
Rxd5 Rh8+ 45. Nh7 Rxh7+) 44... Kg8 45. Rf5 Bc6 46. e7 Be8+ 47. Kh4 {Draw
agreed An interesting end-game, but I was still not back in gear after my
fortnight's holiday away from chess. hence some inferior moves also I was
preoccupied with my G.C.E.results I got just before this game. D.C.George came
4th= with 6pts} 1/2-1/2

