{Opponent Info: Haberdashers', Hampstead} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4
Nd7 5. Bc4 Ngf6 6. Qf3 {to prevent 6....NxN} e6 7. Bg5 $2 Be7 8. Ne2 $2 Nxe4 9.
Bxe7 Qxe7 10. Bb3 (10. Qxe4 Qb4+ $1) 10... Nef6 11. O-O-O O-O {Dangerous in
view of the oncoming KS attack} 12. h4 {with a Knight deficit desperate
measures are called for} g6 {weakening the KS} 13. g4 e5 14. h5 e4 15. Qg3 Kh8
{to relieve the pinned f-Pawn} 16. hxg6 fxg6 17. Nf4 {threatening 18.Nxg6
winning the Q} Kg7 {what else?} 18. Ne6+ Kh8 19. Nxf8 {I preffered to win the
exchange instead of keeping the Knight on e6} Nxf8 20. Qe5 (20. g5) 20... Qxe5
21. dxe5 Nxg4 $2 {Greedy} 22. Rd8 $1 Kg7 23. e6 $1 Bxe6 {what else?} 24. Rxa8
Nxf2 $4 {greedy} 25. Rf1 Bxb3 $4 (25... e3 $142) 26. Rxf2 Bf7 27. Rxa7 Ne6 {
or he loses a Bishop to 28.Rxb7} 28. Rxb7 Ng5 29. a4 {Black is paralysed} Kg8
30. Rfxf7 (30. a5 $142) 30... Nxf7 31. Rxf7 $5 {Black can't stop the a-Pawn An
interesting game I now have 2.5/3 and am lying equal fourth in the
championship!} 1-0

