{Opponent Info:Willesden County Grammar N.W.10} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4
4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. Bb5+ Bd7 8. Bxd7+ {White gives up his
"good" Bishop for my bad one} Nbxd7 9. O-O O-O 10. f4 a6 11. f5 Ne5 12. fxg6
hxg6 ({Not} 12... fxg6 $4 13. Ne6) 13. Nf3 Nc4 14. Qc1 Nxb2 $6 {This move is
unsound but puts White off his game} 15. Rb1 {playing it safe.} (15. Qxb2 {if}
Nxe4 16. Bd4 {should win}) 15... Nc4 16. Rxb7 Nxe3 17. Qxe3 Rb8 18. Rfb1 Rxb7
19. Rxb7 {White's powerfully placed Rook is no compensation for his weak Pawns}
e6 {or else I lose a Pawn after 20......Qe7} 20. h3 {weak} (20. Qa7 $142) 20...
Qa5 21. Rb3 {over cautious} Rc8 {siezing the innitiative} 22. Qd3 Ne8 {piling
on the pressure} 23. Nd4 Qc5 $1 {this pin on the Knight wins the game} 24. Nce2
Bxd4+ 25. Nxd4 $4 (25. Qxd4 $142 Qxc2 26. Rb2) 25... e5 {wins a piece} 26. Qxa6
Qxd4+ 27. Kh2 Rxc2 {An enjoyable game. My time at the end 35 mins his time 55
mins. J.W.Dineen came 21st= with 4.5 pts} (27... Rxc2 {if} 28. Rb8 Qf2 29.
Rxe8+ Kg7 {and White cannot prevent mate}) 0-1

