{Opponent Info: St Pauls Sch W.11} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5.
f3 g6 6. Nc3 Bg7 7. Be3 O-O 8. Qd2 a6 9. g4 b5 {Compare with game v R.Mathews 
(2/12/60) after White's 10th move.} 10. a3 Bb7 11. h4 Nbd7 12. h5 {White has
done best out of the opening.} e5 {After the Knight moves I can reply to 13.
hxg with 13.......fxg as there is now no fork on e6.} (12... Z0 {he now
threatens} 13. hxg6 {where I must reply} hxg6 {opening the h-file with a
strong attack.} (13... fxg6 14. Ne6 {[c.f. game with J.W.Dineen from rd 5]}))
13. Nb3 ({interesting would be} 13. hxg6 exd4 14. gxh7+ Nxh7 15. Bxd4) 13...
Nb6 14. Na5 Rb8 15. O-O-O Ne8 16. Be2 {allows doubling of the Rooks} Qc7 17.
Bh6 $1 f6 $1 {The only move. The Queen must help defend the 2nd rank.} 18. hxg6
hxg6 19. Rh3 g5 {shuts the Q off} 20. Rdh1 Ba8 {I am nearly in Zugzwang} 21.
Bd3 Nc4 $4 {This move loses a lost game.} 22. Bxc4+ bxc4 23. Nd5 $1 Qd8 24.
Bxg7 Kxg7 25. Qh2 Kf7 26. Rh7+ Ng7 {An instructive game. H.P.Brown came 9th=
with 5.5 pts} (26... Ke6 27. Re7+) 1-0

