{Opponent Info: Age 15yr 5m; Drayton Manor Grammar Sch [Time Limit 30 moves in
75 Mins then 6 moves in 15 min]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5.
Nc3 g6 6. Be2 Bg7 7. f4 e6 {A Schvenigen set up. I was wary of him playing f5}
8. Be3 O-O {Perhaps a little too commital in view of White's obvious
intentions of a KS Pawn rush The following alternatives may have been better} (
8... a6) (8... Nc6) 9. g4 {This is very commital but not bad. White should
however not leave his King bare. The threats are: 10.f5, 10.g5, 10.e5} ({
I was concerned about} 9. e5 dxe5 10. fxe5) 9... Re8 {This placing of the Rook
is unfortunate, firstly as the Knight may need to retreat to e8 and also
because the Rooks become the object of a possible fork on c7.} 10. h4 {
Impressive I now have 4 possible Pawn advances to consider.} e5 {This breaks
up the White K-side pawns but allows a White Knight on b5.} (10... a6 {may
have been better}) 11. fxe5 dxe5 12. Ndb5 {This shows why I shold have played .
...a6.} Na6 (12... Z0 {White threatens} 13. Qxd8 Rxd8 14. Nc7) 13. g5 Qxd1+ 14.
Rxd1 Ng4 (14... Nd7 {is possibly better}) 15. Bc1 (15. Bxa7) 15... Be6 {
connecting the Rooks} 16. Rg1 h5 (16... f5 {is risky}) 17. gxh6 Nxh6 18. h5 $1
Kh7 $8 (18... gxh5 $4 19. Bxh6) 19. hxg6+ fxg6 20. Rh1 Rh8 $2 {waste of a move.
} 21. Rd6 $1 Rhe8 ({if} 21... Bf7 22. Rd7 {wins a Pawn}) 22. Rxa6 $1 bxa6 23.
Nc7 {Adjudicated, but a draw agreed. Total time 2.5 hrs This was H.C.G.S v
Draton Manor Hayes won 3.5-2.5 (6 boards) Hayes had an age handicap of 1 so
needed 3pts to win.} 1/2-1/2

