1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. O-O Bc5 5. d4 Nxd4 $2 6. Nxe5 Ne6 7. Nc3 Bd6
$2 8. Nd3 (8. Nf3 $142) 8... Nxe4 $4 9. Bd2 $4 ({Why I did not take the Knight
is incomprehensible to me} 9. Nxe4 {I saw that he could play} Bxh2+ 10. Kxh2
Qh4+ 11. Kg1 Qxe4 {and for some unknown reason I was under the impression that
he would then win.}) 9... Nxd2 10. Qxd2 Qh4 $1 11. g3 {I should resign} Qxc4
12. b3 Qc6 13. Rfe1 O-O 14. Re4 Ng5 15. Qxg5 Qxc3 16. Rae1 h6 17. Qd5 {
prevents17.......b6 followed by 18.......Bb7} Rb8 18. Re8 b6 19. Rxf8+ Bxf8 20.
Re8 $2 Bb7 21. Qxd7 $2 Bc6 22. Rxf8+ Rxf8 {I am sadly off form. How I could
play such atrocius chess as in this game and against D.Green (14/10/60) is
utterly beyond me. Black didn't play well either.} 0-1

