{Opponent Info: Capt of EMI B} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Qxd4 $2 {
loses a move} Nc6 5. Qd1 Nf6 6. Nc3 g6 7. Bb5 a6 $2 {Bad but this is not
immediately apparent} 8. Bxc6+ bxc6 9. e5 Ng4 (9... dxe5 10. Qxd8+ Kxd8 11.
Nxe5) 10. exd6 exd6 $4 {The losing move. This leaves the King dangerously open
andleaves f6 vey weak.} 11. Qd4 $1 Nf6 12. Ne4 $1 Qe7 (12... Bg7 13. Nxd6+) 13.
O-O ({or} 13. Qxf6 Qxf6 14. Nxf6+ {should win}) 13... Nxe4 {loses the exchange
but what else?} (13... Bg7 14. Nxd6+) 14. Qxh8 f6 {trying to trap the Queen}
15. Bh6 Bb7 16. Qxf8+ (16. Bxf8) 16... Qxf8 17. Bxf8 Kxf8 18. Rfe1 d5 19. Nd4
Kf7 {To prevent 20.Ne6+} 20. Nb3 a5 21. f3 Nd6 22. Nc5 Bc8 23. b3 Nb5 24. c4
Nc3 25. Re3 d4 26. Rd3 Bf5 27. Rd2 (27. Rxd4 $4 Ne2+) 27... Rd8 28. g4 Bb1 29.
Nb7 Rd7 30. Nxa5 c5 31. Kf2 Ra7 32. Nc6 Rd7 $2 ({Much better is....} 32... Rxa2
$1 {I considered this for some time but then rejected it for some reason.}) 33.
b4 d3 34. bxc5 Bxa2 $1 {setting a last desperate trap.} 35. Rc1 ({if} 35. Raxa2
$2 Nxa2 36. Rxa2 $4 d2 {wins}) 35... Na4 $2 36. Ra1 $2 (36. Rxa2 d2 37. Rd1 Nc3
{but White simply wins by} 38. Raxd2) 36... Nc3 37. Nb4 Bxc4 38. Rc1 Rb7 39.
Nxd3 Bxd3 40. Rxc3 Ba6 41. c6 Rb8 42. c7 Re8 43. Ra3 Bc8 44. Rad3 Re7 45. Rc3 {
46.Rd8 wins All my troubles stemmed from move 10.} 1-0

