{[Time Limit 30 moves in 75 Mins then 6 moves in 15 min]} 1. c4 f5 2. g3 e5 3.
Bg2 g6 {A sort of Leningrad System} 4. b3 {Fianchettoing the Bishop will dis
uade .....e4 in the future} Bg7 5. Bb2 d6 6. Nf3 Ne7 ({possibly better is} 6...
Nf6) 7. d3 O-O 8. Nc3 b6 $4 9. Nxe5 $1 {This does really not win a Rook and
two Pawns for Knight and Bishop but wins the exchange as the Bishop escapes
from a8} Bxe5 (9... dxe5 {11 should have been played as becomes apparent on
move}) 10. Bxa8 c6 11. d4 {Now Black's 9th moveblunder shows up as White gains
amove and is able to attack c6 with the d-Pawn so that theimprisoned Bishop
escapes with only the loss of a pawn} Bf6 12. d5 c5 13. O-O Qd7 $2 14. Qc2 {
Defending the Bishop means the Knight can move and freeing the Queens Rook and
making e4 a possibility.} Na6 15. Nb5 $1 {eventually wins the a-Pawn} Bxb2 16.
Qxb2 Nc7 17. Bc6 Nxc6 18. dxc6 Qxc6 19. Nxa7 Qb7 20. Nb5 Nxb5 21. cxb5 Qd5 22.
Rfd1 Qe4 $2 23. Rxd6 Bb7 {I saw this coming a few moves back} 24. f3 Qe3+ 25.
Kf1 Bxf3 $4 {A last hope of perpetual check} 26. exf3 Qxf3+ 27. Kg1 $1 (27. Qf2
$4 Qh1+ {with perpetual}) 27... Qe3+ 28. Qf2 Qe5 29. Rad1 Re8 30. Rxb6 Qe2 31.
Qxe2 Rxe2 32. Rb7 Re8 33. Rc7 Ra8 34. b6 Kf8 35. b7 Rb8 36. Rc8+ Rxc8 37.
bxc8=Q+ Kf7 38. Qd7+ Kf6 39. h4 h5 40. Re1 f4 41. Qe7+ Kf5 42. Qe6# {A very
enjoyable game. I am now right back on form after being off form against L.
Wheatley (21\10\60) and D.Green (14\10\60). I played well. HCGS won 6-0} 1-0

