1. c4 c5 2. g3 Nc6 3. Bg2 e6 4. Nc3 {To prevent 4......d5} a6 {Presumably to
prevent 5.Nb5} 5. b3 g6 6. Bb2 Bg7 7. e3 {Creating a weaknes on d3 but it's
not as bad as Black's on d6} Nge7 8. Nge2 b6 9. Qc2 Bb7 10. Nb5 {Looks
enterprising..} (10. O-O {Might be better}) 10... O-O {The only feasible move}
11. Nd6 (11. Nbc3 {might be better}) 11... Bxb2 12. Qxb2 Qc7 13. Ne4 $6 f5 $2 (
{Much beter is} 13... Ne5 $1) 14. Nf6+ $2 (14. N4c3 $142) 14... Rxf6 $2 15.
Qxf6 Rf8 (15... e5 $142) 16. Qc3 {Defending d3} d5 ({Black should play} 16...
Ne5) 17. O-O Ne5 {Too late} 18. Rac1 d4 $2 19. exd4 Bxg2 $1 20. Kxg2 Ng4 $2 ({
He should have tried} 20... Qb7+ {hoping for...} 21. Kg1 ({however after the
check I can play} 21. f3) ({or...} 21. d5) 21... Nf3+ {wins}) 21. dxc5 Qxc5 22.
d4 Qc6+ 23. Kg1 Rc8 24. Nf4 g5 $6 25. Nh5 $3 {leading to great complications
and threatening 26.d5} e5 $2 {Looks good but loses a Pawn} 26. dxe5 $1 Qh6 27.
Nf6+ {The check wins easily} Nxf6 28. exf6 Nd5 29. Qe5 Nxf6 $2 {Hoping his
mating threat will win.....it won't} 30. Qe6+ Kg7 31. Qxc8 Qh3 {Prevents 32.
Kg2, but not my reply} 32. Qb7+ Kg6 33. Rcd1 $1 f4 ({now if....} 33... Ng4 34.
Rd6+ Kh5 $2 35. Qf7#) 34. Qg2 g4 35. Qxh3 gxh3 36. Rd6 Kf5 {Black is an
incurable optimist} 37. Rxb6 Ne4 ({not} 37... fxg3 $4 38. fxg3+) 38. Rd1 Kg4
39. gxf4 Kf3 40. Rd3+ Ke2 41. Re3+ {An interesting game somewhat similar to
the one against J.Bartlett Previously today. I played well and enjoyed both
games.} 1-0

