{Opponent Info: Welsh Champion 1960. The time limit was 24 moves per hour.} 1.
e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be2 Bg7 7. Be3 O-O 8. O-O
Nc6 9. f4 $2 {Possibly a mistake. It leads me into difficulties.} Qb6 {Black
took 25 minutes over this move} 10. Na4 {I took 25 minutes over this move} (10.
Qd3 {Might be better [P.Bennett]}) 10... Qa5 11. Nxc6 bxc6 {Black now has a
good open file.} 12. Nc3 Rb8 13. Rb1 {What else?} Be6 14. Qd2 {To gaurd the
Knight after the b-Pawn goes.} Bxa2 15. Nxa2 Qxa2 16. Ra1 Qxb2 17. Rfb1 Qxb1+
18. Rxb1 Rxb1+ 19. Bf1 Nxe4 20. Qd3 d5 21. Bd4 (21. Bxa7 Ra8 (21... Bc3 22. Z0
Nd2)) 21... Bxd4+ 22. Qxd4 Rfb8 23. g3 {I have nothing else. Black threatens
to double Rooks on the eighth rank, win the Bishop and if I move my Queen from
thr defence of d2 Black plays ...Nd2!} Re1 24. Kg2 {or else I lose a Bishop}
Rbb1 25. Bd3 {My time 55 min} Rbd1 {His time 1hr 4 mins} 26. Qxa7 Rd2+ 27. Kh3
Nf2+ 28. Kh4 Rh1 $4 ({Black has an easy win by....} 28... Nxd3) 29. Qb8+ {
Drawn by perpetual check. P.Bennett was last years Welsh U-18 Bd 1. He also
tied for Welsh Champion in 1961. Cedars won 5-2 (8 bd match) [Cedars had a
strong team including: Bd1 Dave Rumens-He was 2-4 in the 1960 World Jr Ch Bd2
Keith Oliff -He was British Boys Co-Champion in 1959 In this match he lost in
10 (!) moves to Mr.Holt. Bd3 Patrick Bennett Welsh Champ 1960 & 61 The Cedars
chess club had a substantial impact on British chess in the 1960s (SP)]}
1/2-1/2

