{Opponnet Info: Age 17yr 7m [Time Limit 30 moves in 75 Mins then 6 moves in 15
min]} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 c5 4. exd5 exd5 5. Nf3 ({Inever played} 5. dxc5
{beacause of} d4) 5... Nf6 6. Bg5 Be7 7. dxc5 h6 8. Be3 $1 {Hanging on the the
Pawn on c5} (8. Bxf6 $2) 8... Qa5 9. Qd4 {still hanging on to the Pawn} Nc6 10.
Bb5 a6 11. b4 axb5 12. bxa5 Nxd4 13. Nxd4 Rxa5 14. Ndxb5 {Threatening15.Nc7+ &
16.Nxd5} O-O 15. O-O Bf5 $2 16. Nd4 Rxc5 $4 17. Nxf5 Rxc3 18. Nxe7+ Kh8 19. Bd4
Rxc2 20. Bxf6 gxf6 21. Nxd5 Rc6 22. a4 Ra8 23. g3 {Gives the King an escape}
Kg7 24. Ra3 Rc5 25. Rd1 Raa5 26. Nb6 ({if} 26. Nc3 {Black will be able to
eventually force the exchange of QS Pawns with} b5 {I would be left with
trying to get a KS Pawn through}) 26... Rc6 27. Rb1 Ra6 {Adjudicated, after 2.
5 hrs play, as a win for White. It is surprising that a good player such as A.
Brereton should give away a piece in such a simple fashion. Ealing County
Grammar were an age group higher so HCGS only needed 3pts to win the match.
HCGS won 3.5-2.5 (6 boards)} 1-0

