{Time limit 30 moves in 75 mins.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5.
Nc3 g6 6. Bg5 Bg7 7. Bc4 e6 $2 8. Ndb5 O-O 9. Nxd6 Qa5 ({or} 9... Qc7) ({or} 
9... Qb6) 10. Bd2 Nc6 ({Here I considered} 10... Qb4 {but White would play} 11.
Ncb5) 11. Ncb5 Qd8 12. Bc3 $2 a6 $1 {Wins two pieces for a Rook} 13. Nxc8 {
[Time 42 mins]} axb5 {[Time 28 mins]} 14. Qxd8 Rxd8 15. Nb6 bxc4 $2 (15... Ra6
$142) 16. Nxa8 Rxa8 17. f3 b5 18. O-O e5 $1 {Secures an outpost for the Knight
at d4.} 19. Rfd1 b4 20. Be1 Nd4 {Time 37 mins} 21. c3 (21. Rd2 $142) 21... Nc2
22. cxb4 Nxa1 23. Rxa1 Nd7 24. a4 Nb6 25. a5 Kf8 $4 {I thought the Knight
could not be taken, I forgot that the Pawn would be unstoppable. A costly loss
of concentration at the vital moment.} 26. axb6 Rb8 27. Bf2 Ke8 28. Ra7 Bf6 29.
Rc7 Bd8 30. Rxc4 Bxb6 31. Kf1 Bd8 32. Bc5 Kd7 33. Ke2 Ra8 34. Kd3 Ra1 35. Rc2
f5 36. exf5 gxf5 37. Kc4 Kc6 38. b5+ Kb7 39. Rd2 Bf6 40. b6 e4 41. Rd7+ Ka6 42.
Ra7# {A costly lapse of concentration on move 25. L.J.Dent was graded 5b 
(169-176 ECF) in the national gradings 1961. Hayes lost the match 2.5-5.5 (8Bd)
} 1-0

