1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be3 ({I prefer the text
to this} 6. Bg5) 6... g6 7. Qd2 Bg7 8. O-O-O b5 9. f3 {I want a set-up similar
to that played against me by H.P.Brown (1/9/60). This supports the e-Pawn, and
keeps open the c1-h6 diagonal while opening up the second rank for the Queen.}
Bb7 10. g4 Nc6 11. h4 (11. Nxc6 Bxc6 {threatening 12.....b4}) 11... h5 {
weakening but White is well on top.} ({Black can't play....} 11... e6 12. Nxc6
Bxc6 13. Qxd6 {The d Pawn drops. This is one advantage of White's opening play,
pressure on the d-file.}) 12. g5 Nd7 13. f4 Qa5 {doubtful. Alternatives may be
better.} (13... Nc5) (13... O-O) (13... b4) (13... e6 {still loses a Pawn} 14.
Nxc6 Bxc6 15. Qxd6) 14. Qf2 {White now threatens 15.Nb3 14.Qf2 also supports d4
} (14. Nb3 Bxc3 {is good for Black.}) 14... b4 {premature} 15. Nb3 Qc7 (15...
Qd8 $142) 16. Nd5 Qd8 (16... Qc8 {b6 needs to be defended against forks}) 17.
f5 {leaves a hole on e5 but is strong} Nce5 {Threatens 18......Ng4} 18. Bh3
Bxd5 {or he loses the b-Pawn in a few moves.} 19. Rxd5 O-O 20. Rhd1 Nc4 21. Bd4
{very strong} Ndb6 22. f6 $3 exf6 23. gxf6 {inferior} ({better was} 23. Bxb6 $3
) 23... Nxd5 ({after} 23... Bh6+ {I would play} 24. Rg5 Bxg5+ 25. hxg5 {
then sacrifice on h5 and probably win by attacking down the h-file}) 24. fxg7
Re8 25. exd5 Ne5 26. Qf4 $1 {Threatening to keep the Pawn.} Qc7 ({after} 26...
Kxg7 27. Bxe5+ dxe5 28. Qxb4) 27. Qh6 ({if I play} 27. Re1 $4 Nd3+) 27... f5
28. Bxe5 dxe5 (28... Rxe5 $4 29. Qh8+ Kf7 30. Qxa8) 29. Qxg6 Qxg7 30. Qxh5 f4
31. Be6+ $1 Kf8 32. Qf5+ Ke7 33. d6+ Kd8 34. Nc5 $1 e4 35. Nb7+ $3 Qxb7 36.
Qf6+ Re7 37. dxe7+ Kc7 38. Rd7+ Kc6 39. Rxb7 Kxb7 40. Bd5+ Ka7 41. Bxa8 Kxa8
42. Qb6 e3 43. e8=N $1 e2 44. Nc7# {A very enjoyable game. I was on top all
through. I played very well but my concentration was not as deep as it should
be. I was very pleased with the result of the opening system. Apart from the
club swiss there is an all play all in sections. The section winners then play
each other. Section D consists of the second five best players.} 1-0

