1. e4 {Time limit 30 moves in 75 min} e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 Nxe4 $2 {Black
obviously doesn't know the opening.} 4. Qe2 $1 {setting thewell known pitfall}
d5 $4 {Black now proceeds to lose his piece.} ({if} 4... Nf6 $4 5. Nc6+ $3) (
4... Qe7 $142 5. Qxe4 d6 6. d4 f6 7. f4 Nd7 8. Nc3 $1 dxe5 9. Nd5 Qd8 {and
Black must lose a Pawn} (9... Qd6 $2 10. fxe5 fxe5 11. dxe5 Qc6 (11... Qxe5 12.
Nxc7+ $1 Kd8 13. Qxe5 Nxe5 14. Nxa8) 12. Bb5 $1 Qg6 (12... Qxb5 $4 13. Nxc7+)
13. Qxg6+ hxg6 14. Nxc7+ {wins})) 5. d3 Bd6 $4 6. Nf3 O-O 7. dxe4 Re8 8. Be3 (
8. e5 {is no better}) 8... dxe4 9. Nfd2 Nc6 10. Nc3 Nb4 11. O-O-O {I
considered this quite safe as my extra piece helps to repulse any QS attack.
To castle KS could have taken a while and I did not like the King in the
centre. Also I am threatening the e-Pawn} Bf5 12. Kb1 a5 {Not very impressive
as an attack.} 13. Nc4 Qd7 14. Nxd6 cxd6 15. Nb5 {Wins a Pawn or secures d4}
Be6 (15... d5 $142) 16. Rxd6 $1 (16. Nxd6 $4 Red8 17. Z0 Ra6) 16... Qc8 ({if} 
16... Bxa2+ 17. Ka1 Qc8 18. c3) 17. Nc3 Rd8 18. Rxd8+ Qxd8 19. a3 f5 {
Defending the e-Pawn} 20. Qb5 ({if now} 20. axb4 axb4 21. Nb5 Qa5 $1 {with a
strong attack}) 20... Ba2+ $4 {A miscalculation which loses the Bishop.} 21.
Nxa2 $1 Qd1+ 22. Nc1 Qxc2+ 23. Ka1 f4 $2 24. Bc4+ $1 Kh8 25. Bxf4 Qxf2 26. axb4
axb4+ 27. Na2 Qxf4 28. Qxb4 e3 $4 29. Rf1 $1 {Wins the Queen} Rd8 30. Rxf4 Rd1+
31. Nc1 Rxc1+ 32. Ka2 h5 33. Qf8+ Kh7 34. Bd3+ Kh6 35. Rf6+ Kg5 36. Qxg7+ Kh4
37. Qg3# {An enjoyable if not a very difficult game. Quite interesting. Hayes
won the match 7-1 (8Bd)} 1-0

