{Opponent Info: HCGS I Bd5} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 Nc6 $2 {Useless. The
Knight is immediatly dislodged.} 4. d5 Na5 $4 {Hopeless. Loses a piece on move
4!!} 5. b4 c6 6. bxa5 Qxa5+ 7. Bd2 Qc7 8. Nc3 c5 $2 {Very Weak. Black's game
now becomes very cramped.} (8... Nf6 $142) 9. Bc4 Nf6 10. O-O a6 11. a4 Be7 12.
Be3 Nd7 13. Nd2 {so as to play f4} Qa5 (13... O-O $142) 14. Ne2 Nb6 15. Bb3 O-O
16. f4 Bf6 $2 {This is very weak and allows f5 which cramps Black's game even
more. It allows all of the White pieces to form a KS attack. It also blocks
off Black pieces from the defence of the KS.} 17. f5 $1 Nd7 18. Ng3 b5 {
Black's only hope is to advance on the QS} 19. Nh5 Qc3 20. Rf3 c4 21. Bg5 Qd4+
22. Be3 Qc3 23. Ba2 Qb4 24. Rg3 Bh4 $4 25. Rxg7+ Kh8 26. Qg4 Bf6 27. Bh6 {
Throwing everything into the attack.} Qb2 (27... Bxg7 $4 28. Qxg7#) 28. Nxf6 $3
{Forces the win by a pleasing combination.} Qxa1+ 29. Nf1 Qd4+ 30. Kh1 Nxf6 31.
Rxh7+ Nxh7 32. Qg7# {An easy game but a good sacrificial combination at the
end.} 1-0

