{Opponent Info: Age 17; John Ruskin Grammar Sch [Time limit 36 moves in 90
minutes]} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. Nc3 O-O 5. e3 (5. e4 $142) 5... d6
6. Bd3 Nbd7 7. Qc2 {White can achieve nothing on the b1-h7 diagonal} e5 8. d5
Re8 9. e4 Nc5 10. Be3 Nxd3+ 11. Qxd3 Ng4 {Threatening to exchange off the
other Bishop and f5.} 12. Bd2 f5 13. h3 Nf6 14. Bg5 (14. exf5 e4 15. Nxe4 Bxf5
$1 {wins}) 14... h6 15. Bh4 $2 {Weak. The Bishop is cut-off.} g5 16. Bg3 f4 17.
Bh2 Re7 18. g3 {Sacrificing a Pawn for freedom.} Bxh3 19. gxf4 Bg2 (19... exf4
$4 20. Bxf4 $1) 20. Rg1 Bxf3 21. Qxf3 exf4 22. Qg2 {The threat was 22.....Qe8
winning the e-Pawn} Qf8 23. f3 Nd7 24. Nb5 Nc5 (24... Ne5 {might be better.})
25. O-O-O a6 26. Nd4 Bxd4 27. Rxd4 Qf6 28. Qd2 {Threatening 29.BxP!} Rf8 29.
Rg4 {The Rook is weak here.} Kh7 30. b4 $2 (30. Rg1 $142) 30... Nd7 {I was
going to play this anyway} 31. Qf2 $2 Ne5 32. Rg2 Nxf3 $1 33. e5 $2 Qxe5 34.
Qc2+ Qf5 35. Rd1 Qxc2+ 36. Rxc2 Nxh2 37. Rxh2 Rfe8 38. Kd2 Kg6 39. Rdh1 Rh7 40.
Re2 {Time: 75 mins.} Rxe2+ {Time: 45 mins} 41. Kxe2 Re7+ 42. Kf2 ({Not} 42. Kf3
Re3+ 43. Kg4 Rg3#) 42... Re3 43. Re1 Rxe1 44. Kxe1 Kf5 45. a4 Ke4 46. b5 a5 47.
c5 $1 Kxd5 ({Not} 47... dxc5 48. b6 $3) 48. cxd6 cxd6 49. Kf2 g4 50. Kg2 f3+
51. Kf2 h5 52. Kf1 g3 53. Kg1 f2+ 54. Kf1 h4 55. Kg2 h3+ 56. Kf1 h2 57. Kg2
h1=Q+ {An enjoyable game. G.E.Beales came 19th= with 6 pts} 1-0

