{Opponent Info: Age 17yr 11m; Erith Grammar Sch [Time limit 36 moves in 90
minutes]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. c3 dxc3 5. Nxc3 Nc6 6. Bc4 e6 7. O-O
Nf6 8. Qe2 Be7 9. Rd1 Bd7 10. Nb5 O-O 11. Nxd6 Bxd6 12. Rxd6 e5 {[Time 21 mins]
} 13. Bg5 {[Time 9 Mins]} Qc7 {[Time 27 mins]} 14. Rad1 {[Time10 mins] Tragic.
I have lost my concentreation and it is only the second game of the tournament.
I thought for only one minute on this move and I saw his reply immediately I
played it.} Nd4 15. Nxd4 Qxd6 16. Nf5 Qc7 17. Rc1 Bxf5 18. exf5 Qe7 19. h4 h6
20. Be3 Rac8 21. Rd1 a6 {Thea-Pawn could not be taken anyway.} 22. Bb3 Rfd8 23.
Re1 Qb4 24. f3 Nd5 25. Bf2 Nf6 26. g4 Kf8 27. Be3 e4 28. Rf1 $2 exf3 29. Qxf3
Qxg4+ 30. Qxg4 Nxg4 31. Bf4 {My Bishops are very strong but cannot save the
game.} Rc5 32. f6 Nxf6 33. Bxh6 Rc6 34. Bg5 Rd7 35. Rf4 $2 {I would normally
resign but Black was short of time so I played on.} Nh7 36. Rf1 Nxg5 37. hxg5
Rg6 {[Time 1hr 25m]} 38. Rf5 {[Time 37 mins]} f6 39. Kf2 Rxg5 {To lose my
concentration in the second game of a tournament is rather depressing. The
train journeyand the morning game have probably tired me. A.E.Johnson came
14th= with 6.5 pts} 0-1

