{Opponent info: 17yr 10m; Owen's Sch, E.C.1 [Time limit 36 moves in 90 minutes]
} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. c4 Bg7 4. Nc3 O-O 5. b3 d6 6. Qc2 Nbd7 7. g3 e5 8. Bg2
exd4 9. Nxd4 Re8 10. O-O Ne5 11. Bg5 h6 12. Bd2 Nfd7 {Threatening 13......Nxc4}
13. e3 Nc5 14. b4 Na6 15. Nd5 c6 16. Nf4 Bd7 17. a3 Rc8 {This turns out better
than expected.} 18. Rab1 Nc7 {Rather a roving Knight.} 19. h3 Ne6 {Trying to
relieve my cramped position.} 20. Bc3 $2 Nxf4 $1 21. exf4 Nxc4 22. Nxc6 $4 {
He is under the impression he can regain the Pawn.} Bxc6 23. Bxg7 Kxg7 $4 ({
of course I can win a piece by.....} 23... Bxg2 {I saw this a few moves back
and even pionted the fact out to a fellow player whilst White was considering
his move. However on returning to my seat I took the wrong Bishop for no
apparent reason. This just shows how the train journey had tired me and how I
was fading in my play.}) 24. Qxc4 Bxg2 25. Qd4+ Qf6 26. Qxf6+ Kxf6 27. Kxg2 Rc3
28. a4 d5 29. Rfd1 Rd8 30. Rd4 Rc4 31. Rbd1 ({If} 31. Rxc4 dxc4 32. Z0 a6 33.
Z0 b5) 31... Rxd4 32. Rxd4 Ke6 33. g4 Rc8 34. f5+ Ke5 35. Rd1 d4 36. fxg6 fxg6
37. Re1+ Kd6 38. f4 d3 39. Kf3 Rf8 $2 {My tiredness shows again.} 40. Rd1 Kd5
41. Rxd3+ Kc4 42. Rd7 Kxb4 43. Rxb7+ Kxa4 44. Rxa7+ Kb5 45. Rh7 g5 46. f5 Rf6
47. Rg7 Rf8 48. Rg6 Rh8 49. f6 Kc5 50. f7 Rf8 51. Rxh6 Rxf7+ 52. Ke4 Rf8 53.
Rh5 Kd6 $1 {A last hope.} 54. Rxg5 Rh8 55. Rh5 $4 Rxh5 $1 56. gxh5 Ke7 57. h6
Kf7 58. Kf5 Kg8 59. h4 Kh7 60. Kg5 Kh8 61. Kg6 Kg8 62. h5 Kh8 63. Kg5 Kh7 {
A great pity I missed the combination (after seeing it) due soley to tiredness.
Once again I scrape a draw from a lost position. K.M.Hogan came 40th= with 5
pts} 1/2-1/2

