{Opponent Info: Age 17; John Ruskin Grammar Sch [Time limit 36 moves in 90
minutes]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nxd4 {Unusual and not very
good. Black wants a draw and exchanges.} 5. Qxd4 d6 6. Bc4 e5 $2 {Weak leaved
the d-Pawn in the lurch} 7. Qd5 Be6 $2 (7... Qd7 $142) 8. Qxb7 Bxc4 $2 9. Qc6+
Ke7 10. Qxc4 Rc8 11. Qd3 Nf6 12. Bg5 Ke8 13. O-O h6 14. Be3 Rc7 15. Nc3 Ng4 16.
Bd2 Qd7 17. Rfd1 Be7 18. h3 Nf6 19. Be3 Rb7 20. b3 g6 21. a4 {Threatening 22.
Nb5 Black's backward d-Pawn is coming under heavy attack.} Qc6 22. f3 ({if} 22.
Nb5 {and the ensuing exchanges I will lose my e-Pawn so I defend it.}) 22...
Kd7 23. Qd2 g5 24. Nd5 Rc8 25. Rac1 Nxd5 26. Qxd5 Qxd5 27. Rxd5 a6 28. Kf2 Rbc7
29. c4 {Now Black will never be able to play.....d5.} Ke6 30. Rcd1 Rb7 31. R5d3
Rd8 32. Ke2 Rdd7 33. Kd2 Bd8 34. Kc2 Bb6 $2 {This loses immediately.} 35. Bxb6
Rxb6 36. c5 $3 Rc6 37. b4 a5 38. Rxd6+ $1 Rcxd6 39. Rxd6+ Rxd6 40. cxd6 Kxd6
41. bxa5 Kc6 42. Kc3 Kb7 43. Kc4 Ka6 44. Kd5 f6 45. Ke6 Kxa5 46. Kxf6 Kxa4 47.
Kxe5 Kb4 48. Kf6 Kc4 49. e5 Kd5 50. e6 Kd6 51. e7 Kd7 52. Kf7 {After my rest
after this morning's game I felt less tired and played better. P.J.Wilson came
40th= with 5pts} 1-0

