{Opponent Info: Age 16yr 9m; St Aloysius College, N.6 [Time limit 36 moves in
90 minutes]} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O b5 6. Bb3 Be7 7.
Re1 O-O 8. c3 d5 $1 {The Marshall variation.} 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11.
Rxe5 Nf6 12. d4 {More accurate than 12.Re1 as played by Capablanca against
Marshall in 1918.} (12. Re1) 12... Bd6 13. Re1 (13. Re2 $142) 13... Ng4 14. h3
({Not} 14. g3 Nxh2 $1) 14... Qh4 {[Time 12 mins]} 15. Be3 {[Time 12.5 min]} (
15. Qf3 $142 $1 {as in Capablanca v Marshall but 15.Be3 is good enough.}) (15.
hxg4 $4 Qh2+ 16. Kf1 Qh1+ 17. Ke2 Bxg4+ 18. Kd2 Bf4+ $1) {On the prevous move
I could not take the Knight [see variation] but now I'm threatening it.} 15...
Nxe3 16. Rxe3 {[Time 14.5 mins]} Qf4 {[Time 33 mins]} 17. g3 {[Time 16.5 mins]}
Qf5 {[Time 35 mins]} 18. h4 {[Time 17m 45s]} Bb7 19. Nd2 {[Time 21 mins]} c5
20. Bc2 {[Time 22 mins]} Qd7 {[Time 45 mins]} (20... Qh3 {Achieves very little.
}) 21. Be4 {[Time 24 mins] Exchanging Black's attacking pieces.} Rfe8 {[Time
47 min]} 22. Bxb7 {[Time 24m 30s]} Qxb7 23. Rxe8+ Rxe8 24. dxc5 Bxc5 25. Nb3 {
[Time 26 min]} Bb6 {[Time 50min]} 26. Qd3 {[Time 27 min]} g6 {To rule out any
back rank mates.} 27. Rd1 Qa7 28. Nd4 Rd8 29. Qe4 b4 30. Rd3 bxc3 {[Time 1h]}
31. bxc3 Bc5 32. Kg2 $1 Qb6 33. Rd2 {[Time 35.5 min]} Rb8 {[Time 1h 10s]} 34.
Nc6 Qb7 35. Qf3 Rc8 36. Ne5 $1 Qxf3+ 37. Kxf3 $2 Bb6 {[Time 1h 25s]} 38. Rc2 $2
{Now I can only draw. After all my good play, tiredness causes my
concentration to go. How depressing.} (38. c4 $142) 38... Bd4 {Once again
tiredness causes my concentration to sag and I allow a won game to be drawn. G.
Kvakovszky came 31st= with 5.5 pts} 1/2-1/2

