{Player Info: Age 17yr 5m; 3rd in Middlesex U/18 Boys Ch 1960; Michenden
Grammar Sch N.21 [Time limit 36 moves in 90 minutes]} 1. d4 f5 {For the first
time in a tournament.} 2. c4 Nf6 3. g3 (3. b3 {White does better to
fianchettothe other Bishop.}) 3... g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. Nc3 d6 6. e3 c6 7. Nge2 O-O
8. O-O Qc7 9. Bd2 e5 10. dxe5 dxe5 11. e4 Na6 12. exf5 Bxf5 {Black has come
off best out of the opening and White's last move was definitely bad. Black's
QBishop ruins White's game.} 13. Nc1 {What else?} Rad8 14. Nb3 Nb4 15. Nc1 Bh6
16. f4 exf4 17. gxf4 {[Time 1hr] White's position is hopeless. He offered draw
here.} Rd7 {So as to double Rooks. [Time 15min]} 18. Qe1 $4 Nc2 19. Qh4 Nxa1
20. Qxh6 Rxd2 21. N1e2 Nc2 22. Ng3 $2 Rxg2+ $1 23. Kxg2 Ne3+ 24. Kf2 $4 Nxf1 $4
({At the time neither of us saw....} 24... Neg4+ {but the end of the game was
played quickly and without much thought.}) 25. Kxf1 Bd3+ {White should resign.}
26. Kg2 Bxc4 27. f5 Bd3 28. h4 Qg7 29. Qe3 Bxf5 30. Nxf5 gxf5+ 31. Kf1 Re8 32.
Qxa7 Qg3 33. Qf2 Qxf2+ 34. Kxf2 {[Time1hr 20m]} Ne4+ {[Time 25 mins] N.D.
Tomkin came 31st= with 5.5pts} 0-1

