{Opponent Info: Age 17; St Clement Dane's School W.12 [Time limit 36 moves in
90 minutes]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Nc3 Bb4 6. Bd2 Qc7 7.
Bd3 Nc6 8. Nf3 Nge7 9. a3 Bc5 10. Na4 $2 Ba7 11. Qe2 b5 12. Nc3 Bb7 {Black has
equalised out of the opening.} 13. g3 {A weak move; possibly preparing 14.Bf4}
Ng6 14. h4 Nge5 15. Nxe5 Nxe5 16. Bf4 Nxd3+ 17. Qxd3 Qc6 18. f3 {Creates a
weakness on g3} Rd8 {preparing 19.....d5} 19. Be3 Bb8 {Taking advantage of the
weak g-Pawn.} 20. Ne2 d5 {Eliminating my main weakness.} 21. O-O-O Bc7 22. Nd4
{leaves the g-Pawn too weak.} Qd6 23. exd5 Qxd5 24. Qb3 $2 Qxb3 25. Nxb3 {
leaving 2 pawns en prise.} Rxd1+ 26. Rxd1 Bxg3 27. Nc5 Bxf3 28. Rd4 Bd5 {
The a-Pawn must go anyway so I didn't try to save it. This move blocks the
d-file.} 29. Nxa6 Bd6 $1 {Preventing 30.Rb4 and "killing" the Knight.} 30. Rg4
g6 31. Bd4 Rg8 32. Nc5 f5 33. Rg1 {The Rook must retreat to the first rank due
to the strength of my Bishops which control all the vital squares.} e5 34. Re1
e4 35. Bf2 Bxc5 36. Bxc5 Kd7 {Now I control the White squares.} 37. Kd2 Kc6 38.
Bb4 {This blocks the b-Pawn White's only chance was to advance on the Qside.}
h6 39. Ke3 g5 40. hxg5 hxg5 41. Be7 f4+ 42. Kf2 g4 43. Bh4 g3+ 44. Kg1 f3 45.
Bxg3 Rxg3+ 46. Kf2 Rg2+ 47. Ke3 Rxc2 {A fair game. K.P.Tan came 40th= with 5
pts. London 1961: I started badly due to tiredness and couldn't concentrate,
however I improved and did better later but tiredness still caused me to be
somewhat off-form. I came 19th= with 6 pts} 0-1

