{Opponent Info; Age 19. [Time Limit 30 moves in 75 Mins then 6 moves in 15 min]
} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Be3 e6 7. Qd2 Be7 8.
O-O-O O-O 9. f3 {This system works best if Black has a fianchettoed KBishop.}
Bd7 {The strong Schvenigen set up.} 10. g4 a6 11. h4 b5 {My time so far. Now I
thought for 25 mins leaving myself short of time. If I advance the h-Pawn to
h6 Black blocks the attack with g6.} 12. Nce2 $1 {Without the advance ....b4
in the following variation my Knight would be useless on a3, hence the move
played. The best move. I think I can play 13.NxN and 14.Nd4 having got rid of
my embarassing Knight's position.} (12. g5 {Does no good}) ({I considered} 12.
Nb1 {to be followed by.....} Z0 13. Na3 {and if...} b4 14. Nc4) 12... Rc8 13.
Nxc6 $1 Bxc6 14. Nd4 Bb7 {Not really necessary as my Knight is better than the
Bishop so I wouldn't swap.} 15. Kb1 $2 e5 {This wins Rook and two pawns for
Knight and Bishop. I was short of time and had played the last move quickly
thinking it was a "safe" move.} 16. Nf5 Nxe4 $1 17. Nxe7+ Qxe7 18. fxe4 Bxe4 {
With two threats.} 19. Bd3 Bxh1 20. Rxh1 {I now have the two Bishops.} d5 {
Threatening to advance in the centre smotrhering the two Bishops} 21. Bf5 Rc4
$2 {I now had 20 mins for my next 9 moves. I spent 10 of them on my next.} ({
Possibly better is} 21... Rcd8) 22. Qxd5 Rd8 {I have 10 mins for 8 moves.} ({
if now} 22... g6 23. Bd3 ({Not} 23. Qd7 Qxd7 24. Bxd7 Rd8 $1)) ({If} 22... e4
23. Qd7) 23. Qg2 e4 {Threatening 24.....g6} (23... g6 24. Bd3) 24. g5 g6 {
I am in time trouble and Black has over 30 mins left. Therefore he should play
something more enterprising than 24......g6 makes my last easy. I have 7.5
mins left.} 25. Bg4 {7 mins left} b4 {. Anotrher unenterprising move by Black.}
26. Re1 {5 mins left.} Qe5 {25 mins left} 27. Qe2 {3 mins left.} Rc6 28. Qf2 {
2 mins left.} Rcd6 {Black has all the time in the world but blunders.} 29. Bf4
e3 $2 30. Bxe3 $1 {My flag was right up and I played this very quickly.} (30.
Bxe5 exf2 31. Rf1 $1) 30... Qd5 31. b3 ({I was considering} 31. Bc5 {but
realised I would be mated by....} Qd1+) 31... a5 {Adjudicated Win for White.
Aood game. This is the first I have been in time trouble.} (31... a5 32. Bc5
Rc6 (32... Qd2 33. Re2) 33. Qe2 $3 Rf6 34. Be7 Re8 35. Bf3 {Hcgs lost the
match (6Bd) 1-5 William Ellis School went on to win Zone K}) 1-0

