1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Bc4 Bb4+ (4... Bc5 {is more usual.}) 5. Bd2
Bxd2+ 6. Qxd2 Qe7 {Trying to hang onto the Pawn.} 7. O-O Ne5 {Still trying to
hang onto the Pawn by exchanging Knights.} 8. Nxe5 Qxe5 9. Qd3 {To play Nd2}
Nf6 10. Nd2 O-O 11. Rad1 Re8 12. f4 Qh5 13. Qxd4 c6 $2 {Now Black's position
is wrecked.} (13... d6 $142) 14. e5 {[Adjourned]} Ng4 {[Sealed move] Play
restarted 20\2\61} 15. h3 Nh6 16. Ne4 {Compare my development and position
with Black's.} Nf5 $2 ({Correct is} 16... Qg6 {....but the position is very
complicated.}) 17. Qd3 $1 {Threatening 18.Ng5} b5 ({If} 17... h6 {I have a
beautiful combination} 18. g4 Qg6 19. Nd6 $3 {and Black must resign.}) 18. Bb3
a5 $2 {Now he is massacred.(but what else was there?)} 19. Ng5 $1 Rf8 ({
What to do. If....} 19... Nh6 20. Qxh7+ Kf8 21. Bxf7 {etc}) 20. g4 {Wins a
piece.} Qg6 21. gxf5 Qh5 22. Kh2 {To gaurd the h-Pawn after 22....h6.} a4 23.
Bxf7+ Rxf7 24. Nxf7 Qxf7 25. a3 b4 {Threat 26.....Ba6} 26. Rg1 {Threatening 37.
f6} bxa3 27. bxa3 d5 {Now my e-Pawn is fearfully strong.} 28. f6 $1 g6 29. f5
$1 Qc7 30. Rde1 Ba6 31. Qg3 {The best move allowing the e-Pawn to move.} Qa5
32. fxg6 Qd2+ 33. Kh1 Qh2+ $1 {His last fling.(Psychological of course)} 34.
Kxh2 {Resigns (At last) A very enjoyable game. The adjournment position (after
e5) was extremely complicated with many combinations hovering about. I had
several useful pins throuhgout the game.} 1-0

