{Opponent Info: Bd 1 for the club; Middlesex player.} 1. e4 e5 {I didn't want
to play the Sicillian which Mr Holt plays a lot.} 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4
Nf6 5. O-O b5 6. Bb3 Be7 7. Re1 O-O 8. c3 d6 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7
12. Nbd2 cxd4 13. cxd4 Nc6 {I want to play13.....d5 to rid me of the weakness
on d6 but must protect the e-Pawn first but even now I can't play it.} 14. a3 {
I didn't expect this. I expected Nf1-e3 or 14.a4} Re8 {Still making my
elaborate preparations to play d5.} 15. d5 {This gains some space but blocks
the centre and play is somewhat restricted to the c-file. This move didn't
worry me particularlyas my Knight can quite happily go to a5 and c4. It is
true my Bishops are restricted but they gaurd the vital squares on the c-file
and can defend the KS. How is White to make any headway?} Na5 16. b4 {"Fixing"
the QS and forcing the exchange of my rather restricted Knight for his
potentially good one on d2.} Nc4 17. Nxc4 {Surely there must have been a
better plan for White?} Qxc4 (17... bxc4 {If I were trying to win at all costs
I would play this but it's risky.}) 18. Bd2 Qc7 {I still didn't know whether
d7 is the best square for the QBishop so I reserve the option by playing 18....
Qc7 which I have to play anyway.} 19. Rc1 Bd7 {Better then 19.....Bb7 as now I
can keep an eye on the KS especially f5 where White may want to post a Knight.}
20. Re3 Rec8 {Moving this Rook gives the Knight or Bishop retreat squares or a
base to access other squares.} 21. Rc3 {If White is to win he must surely
attack on the QS.} Qb7 22. Bd3 Rxc3 23. Rxc3 Rc8 {I am willing to draw 
(against the club champion!) so I exchange off.} 24. Qe2 {Why?} Rxc3 25. Bxc3
Nh5 $1 {Threatening to post the Knight strongly at f4 and involving a simple
trap into which White falls.} 26. Nxe5 {Played without too much thought
thinking he has won a Pawn.} Nf4 $1 27. Qf3 dxe5 ({Not} 27... Nxd3 $4 28. Nxd3)
28. Bxe5 Ng6 {THe Knight prevents an eventual e5.} (28... Nxd3 {I would have
difficulty blocking the centre Pawns.}) 29. Bd4 Qc7 $1 {Prevents 30.Bc5! which
would be strong.} 30. Bb2 {Prevents 30.....Qc1+} Bd6 {Gaurding e5.} 31. Qh5 f6
$1 {Fixing e5 for good.} (31... Nf4 {fails against} 32. Qg5 f6 33. Bxf6 Bxh3 $3
34. e5 $3) 32. Qd1 Be5 33. Bc1 (33. Bxe5 Nxe5 {is strong.}) 33... Nf4 $3 34.
Bf1 ({if now} 34. Bxf4 Bxf4 35. Bc2 {to prevent 35.....Qc1 which wins.} Qc3 {
wins.}) 34... Qc3 $1 {Black is practically in Zugzwang. I threaten Qa1 winning.
} 35. Bxf4 {What else?} Bxf4 {Zugzwang!!} 36. g3 Be5 $1 {This is about my best
result to date. I played very well and didn't lose my concentration, for once.
I played the end-game excellently and in the final position was going to win a
Pawn. White gained some space from the opening but no prospects and the
position reached after about move 16 is cramped but I can defend easily
against anything and it is for these reasons that I don't play the Ruy Lopez
much.} (36... Bc1 {fails to} 37. a4) (36... Qc1 {fails to} 37. Qe2) 0-1

