1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. d3 d5 5. cxd5 Nxd5 6. Bg2 O-O 7. a3 c6 {
Strenghtening the Knight and keeping the h1-a8 diagonal closed.} 8. Qc2 Nd7 9.
Bd2 Qc7 {preparing .....e5.} 10. Nc3 N5f6 ({Not} 10... e5 $4 11. Nxd5) 11. O-O
e5 12. Rfd1 Nb6 13. Rac1 Bf5 14. b4 Nc4 15. Nh4 Nd6 {Adjourned} ({Not} 15...
Nxa3 $4 16. Qb3) (15... Nxd2 $2 16. Nxf5 {With the better position.}) {Play
resumed 4/3/61} 16. Nxf5 {[sealed move]} Nxf5 {Threatening 17.....Nd4} 17. e3
Qd7 {Unpinning my c-Pawn thus preventing 18.Nd5 or 18.Nb5.17....Qd7 also
prevents 18.d4} ({I didn't like....} 17... Qe7 {as White may get a Bishop on
b4.}) 18. Ne2 {preparing 19.d4} Rfd8 19. Bc3 Ne8 {Intending to go to d5 via c7.
} 20. Bh3 {This looks good but leads to simplifying exchanges.} Nxe3 $1 {
White apparently hadn't thought this possible.} 21. Bxd7 Nxc2 22. Bxe8 Nxa3 $1
({Not} 22... Rxe8 $4 23. Rxc2 $18) 23. Bxc6 ({Not} 23. Bxf7+ {When he ends up
a Pawn down.}) 23... bxc6 24. Bb2 Nb5 25. Rxc6 Rac8 26. Rxc8 Rxc8 27. Rc1 Rxc1+
28. Nxc1 Kf8 29. Nb3 Ke7 30. Kf1 Kd6 31. Ke2 f6 {This doesn't turn out too
well.} 32. d4 exd4 (32... f5 $142) 33. Nxd4 Nc7 (33... Nxd4+ {Leeaves me in
difficulties.}) 34. Kd3 Kd5 35. Nc2 Ne6 36. Ne3+ Kc6 37. Kc4 f5 38. b5+ Kb7 (
38... Kb6 {Loses a tempo.}) 39. Bxg7 Nxg7 40. Nd5 Ne6 41. Nf6 h5 42. f4 h4 43.
Nd7 hxg3 44. hxg3 g5 {An interesting game. HCGS I won the match 5.5 - 0.5}
1/2-1/2

