1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 bxc6 5. Nxe5 d5 6. exd5 ({I also
considered...} 6. Nxc6) 6... Qe7 {More or less forcing an exchange of Queens.}
7. Qe2 cxd5 8. d4 f6 {A very doubtful move forcing off the Queens.} 9. Nd3 {
The Knight won't have much future at f3 as Black gaurds e5 and g5 but the
d-Pawn is undefended.} Qxe2+ 10. Kxe2 {I can't castle but that doesn't really
matter for I will control the e-file for Black's Pawns are badly placed and he
will have development difficulties.} Bd6 11. Re1 Ne7 ({Not} 11... Bxh2 $4 12.
g3 {Winning the Bishop.}) 12. h3 {Prevents any future ....Bg4 and prepares for
g4 which prevents .....Nf4} ({Not as good is...} 12. g3) 12... O-O 13. Nc3 a5 {
so as to play .....Ba6 but I can now play Nb5.} 14. Bf4 {I want to exchange
off as Black has two good Bishops. Also I can now play 15.Kd2 without blocking
the Bishop} Bxf4 15. Nxf4 c6 16. Na4 {Intending to play 17.Nc5 and if Black
plays 17.....Nf5 the d-Pawn can be defended by 18.c3} Ba6+ 17. Kd2 Nf5 18. c3
Rab8 19. Kc2 Rfe8 20. Nc5 Rxe1 $2 {Gives up the e-file.} 21. Rxe1 Bc8 22. b3
Nd6 {The Knight is no good here as I have just defended c4.} 23. g4 {Prevents
the Bishop check on f5.} g5 $2 {Ruining his KS Pawn structure.} 24. Nfe6 $1 {
prevents 24.....f5.} Bxe6 {Loses a Pawn but his position is crumbling.} 25.
Rxe6 Rd8 26. Rxf6 Ne4 {Worth a try but everything loses.} 27. Nxe4 dxe4 28. Kd2
$1 {Safer than taking the c-Pawn.} (28. Rxc6) 28... c5 29. Ke3 cxd4+ 30. cxd4
Kg7 31. Rf5 Kg6 32. Rxa5 Rc8 33. Rc5 Rf8 34. d5 {A good positional game. Each
of the four teams involved (Middx, Essex, Kent, Surrey) had a couple of
players on each board (12 boards in total) Scores were Surrey 7.5, Middx 7,
Essex 5-5, Kent 4 More details are in the SCCU buletin for Feb '61 which can
be found at: https://www.ecforum.org.uk/viewtopic.php?t=10581} 1-0

