{Opponent Info: HCGS II Bd} 1. e4 c5 2. c4 {Leaves the d-Pawn backward} g6 3.
Nc3 Bg7 4. Nge2 Nc6 5. d3 {Not a very happy Pawn structure with a hole on d4.}
a6 (5... e6 {Comes to grief against.} 6. Nb5) 6. g3 Nf6 7. Bg2 d6 8. Rb1 $2 {
Unusual and withour much point.} Nd7 {Preparing 9.....Qa5 and opening the long
diagonal.} 9. Be3 {Again rather pointless.} Nd4 10. Nxd4 $4 (10. Bxd4 cxd4 {
Leaves White in difficulties.}) 10... cxd4 11. Nd5 $2 dxe3 12. Nxe3 Qa5+ 13. b4
Bc3+ 14. Ke2 Bxb4 15. Qb3 Bc5 16. Rhd1 Bxe3 17. Kxe3 Nc5 18. Qb2 O-O 19. d4 Nd7
(19... Ne6 {Serves no purpose}) 20. Bh3 Rb8 21. Bxd7 $2 Bxd7 22. Rd3 Qc7 {
Stabilising the position.} 23. Rb3 b5 24. cxb5 (24. a4 Qxc4) 24... Rxb5 25.
Rxb5 Bxb5 26. Rc1 Qd7 27. f4 Rc8 28. Rxc8+ Qxc8 29. d5 Qc4 30. Qd2 a5 31. h4 (
31. Qxa5 $4 Qe2+ 32. Kd4 Qd3#) 31... a4 32. g4 Qf1 33. a3 {Loses even quicker.}
Qh3+ 34. Kd4 Qxa3 35. Qc3 Qc5+ 36. Qxc5 dxc5+ 37. Kc3 c4 38. Kb4 Kf8 0-1

