{Time limit 24 moves in 1st Hr then 6 moves per 15 min} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3.
d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be2 Bg7 7. Be3 {[1 min]} a6 {[1 min]} 8. Qd2 {
[3']} Nc6 {Aiming to play 9.....NxN when White must recapture with Queen or
Bishop which rules out Bh6. After this I can play B-d7-c6} 9. Nxc6 {This gives
me a strong centre.} bxc6 10. f4 {This blocks the c1-h6 diagonal} (10. f3 {
Is in vogue at the moment.}) 10... O-O 11. Bf3 {Thretening an eventual e5.} d5
$1 {[17'] Leading to simplifying exchanges which bring me equality. This move
had to be calculated very carefuly.} 12. exd5 {[16']} ({If} 12. e5 Nd7 {
is good.}) ({If} 12. O-O-O e6) 12... cxd5 {[17']} 13. Nxd5 {[23']} Nxd5 {[18']}
14. Qxd5 {[32']} (14. Bxd5 {is similar.}) 14... Qxd5 {[19']} 15. Bxd5 {[32']}
Bxb2 {[19']} 16. Rb1 {[35']} Rb8 {[21']} 17. Kf2 {[41']} ({If} 17. Bd4 $2 Bc3+
$1 {I needed to see this on move 11.}) 17... Bf5 {[25'] At the time I was not
very happy about this as I can't play ....e6, but I need not have worried.} 18.
Bb3 {[42']} (18. Ba7 {Was an interesting alternative.}) 18... Bf6 {[35'] This
position is not as easy as it looks.} ({I considered.....} 18... Bc3 {which
blockades the c-Pawn but White would play.} 19. Bc5 {...forcing...} Rfe8) 19.
Rbd1 {[49']} Rfd8 {[41']} 20. Rxd8+ {[51']} Rxd8 {[41']} 21. c4 {[54']} e5 $1 {
Giving my Bishops good scope.} 22. fxe5 {[55']} Bxe5 {[45']} 23. Bh6 {[58']
Entrapping my King but White may find his Bishop out of touch and it mat
itself get trapped.} Bd4+ {Intending 24.....Bc5 blocking the c-Pawn.} 24. Be3 {
[59']} Be5 {[53']} 25. h3 {[1hr 4'] The Rook could move without endangering
the h-Pawn but White may intend g4.} Be4 {My Bishops are central and very
strong.} 26. Bb6 {[1hr 6']} Rd2+ {[1hr 8'] Adjourned.} 27. Ke3 {[1hr 9'] Play
resumed 7/3/61 The sealed move and the best.} (27. Kf1 $2 Bxg2+ 28. Ke1 Bc3 29.
Rh2 Rxa2+ 30. Kd1 Bf3+ {Wins.}) (27. Ke1 Bc3 28. Be3 (28. Bf2 Rxa2+ {Wins.}) (
28. Rf1) 28... Rxa2+ (28... Rxg2+ 29. Kf1 Rxa2) 29. Kd1 Ra1+ 30. Bc1 Bb2 31.
Kd2 Bxc1+ 32. Rxc1 Rxc1 33. Kxc1 Bxg2 {Wins.}) 27... Bxg2 {[1hr 8' 30s] Forced.
} 28. Kxd2 {[1hr 9' 30s]} (28. Rg1 Rd6 29. Bc7 Bd4+ 30. Kd2 Bxg1+ 31. Bxd6 Bxh3
{Wins.}) (28. Re1 Rd6 29. Bc5 Re6 30. Rd1 Bd6+ 31. Kd4 Bxc5+ 32. Kxc5 Bxh3 {
Wins.}) 28... Bxh1 {[1hr 8' 30s]} 29. Ba4 $3 {The only move which does not
lose. White now threatens 30.Bd7 and the Pawn has a protected passage. This
move really surprised me as I suspected it but not immediately.} (29. c5 Bb7
30. Z0 Bc8) 29... Bb7 {[1hr 12']} 30. Bd7 {[1hr 11'] Now I will have to give
up a Bishop for a Pawn.} Bh2 31. a4 $1 {[1hr 14'] Intending 32.a5 thus
allowing c5} ({If} 31. c5 Bg1) 31... Kf8 {[1hr 18']} 32. Bc5+ {Temporarily
blocking the c-Pawn.} Kg7 33. Bb6 Kf6 (33... f5 {is no better.}) 34. Bd8+ Kg7 (
34... Ke5 $4 35. Bc7+) 35. c5 Bg2 $1 {Now I have the choice of which Bishop to
give up. I am attacking the his h-Pawn. I can defend my a-Pawn by Bf1.} 36. c6
f5 37. h4 Bf1 {[1hr 29' 30s] The a-Pawn must be defended.} 38. c7 {[1hr 34']}
Bxc7 {[1hr 29 30s]} 39. Bxc7 Kh6 {[1hr 29' 30s]} 40. Bd8 {[1hr 37']} Kh5 {
[1hr 30']} 41. Bc6 Kg4 42. Ke3 h6 43. Bf3+ {[1hr 44']} Kg3 {[1hr 32']} 44. h5 {
[1hr 53']} gxh5 {[1hr 34']} ({Not} 44... g5 $4 45. Bxg5) 45. Bxh5 {[1hr 53']}
f4+ {[1hr 34']} 46. Kd2 {[1hr 55']} f3 $1 {[1hr 38' 30s] Now the Pawn is very
strong and secures me the draw.} 47. Ke1 {[1hr 55']} Bh3 {[1hr 41'] Here I
offered a draw but was refused.} 48. Bb6 Bd7 {The 48th move was the 2hr time
control.} 49. a5 {[2hr 2']} Bb5 {[1hr 52' 30s]} 50. Be3 {[2hr 7']} Bc4 {
[1hr 55']} 51. Bg6 {[2hr 9']} (51. Bxh6 $4 f2+) 51... Bb5 {[1hr 56']} 52. Bf7 {
[2hr 11']} Bd3 {[1hr 29 45s]} 53. Bf2+ {[2hr 12'] Adjourned and draw agreed 
[Black 2hr 5'] I play Kf4 and White can't win. A very good game. White's 29.
Ba4! surprised me but the position at the end left him with no winning chances.
Hayes won the match 5-3.} 1/2-1/2

