1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 {In vogue at the moment.} 6.
Bd2 {This "odd" move was played after 20 mins thought.} cxd4 {Played after 2
mins thought.} 7. Nb5 Bc7 {Prevents 8.Nd6} 8. f4 a6 {I could not maintain the
extra Pawn so I force the roaming Knight to move. I would play ...a6 later
anyway.} 9. Nxd4 Ne7 10. Ngf3 Nbc6 11. Bb4 Nxb4 12. axb4 Bd7 ({Not} 12... b5 $2
13. Bxb5+ $1) 13. c3 {Unnecessary at this stage.} b5 {Fixing the QS and
gaining space.} 14. Qd2 Bb6 {A waiting move to see if he castles QS.} 15. O-O-O
{He did. This is rather dangerous for him.} Qc7 {Pinning the c-Pawn.} ({
Much better is...} 15... Qc8 {as becomes obvious in a few moves time, I was
not feeling to well at this time and didn't concentrate too well.}) 16. Kc2 {
Extremely odd.} Nc6 {Threatening 17.....Nxb4+} 17. Ra1 {Preventing 17....Nxb4+
due to my unprotected Rook. This is why 15.....Qc8 was better.} Ke7 $6 {
Not very good. It defends my QRookbut compromises my King. However KS castling
was dangerous due to my lack of KS minor pieces.} 18. Be2 $2 Nxb4+ 19. Kd1 Nc6
20. Qe1 Rhc8 $2 ({At this stage I felt quite unwell and went to pieces rather!
Slightly better was.....} 20... Rac8 {eg...} 21. Rxa6 $2 Nxd4 $1 22. Nxd4 Bxd4
23. cxd4 $2 Qc2#) 21. Qh4+ {Here I couldn't concentrate so I offered a draw
which he accepted.} 1/2-1/2

