1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 d6 {For the first time in my life.} 4. d4 exd4 5.
Nxd4 Bd7 6. Bxc6 Bxc6 7. Nxc6 bxc6 {White exchanges only help Black.} 8. b3 {
A good move. I intended fianchettoing my KBishop which would then be very
strong.} Be7 9. Bb2 Bf6 10. Bxf6 Nxf6 11. Nd2 O-O 12. O-O Re8 13. Re1 Rb8 14.
Qf3 {Threatening 15.e5} Qd7 15. Rad1 Rb5 {Black has done best out of the
opening.} 16. Nc4 Qe7 17. e5 {rather risky to say the least.} d5 {Neatly
taking advantage of White's compromised position. This also defends the c-Pawn.
} 18. Ne3 ({Not} 18. exf6 $4 Qxe1+) (18. Nd2 Nd7 19. Qe3 {looks better.}) 18...
Qxe5 19. c4 Ra5 {The Rook is quite safe here.} 20. Nc2 Qd6 21. Rxe8+ Nxe8 22.
Qe3 Nf6 23. Re1 {Giving up the a-Pawn with no compensation.} Rxa2 24. Nd4 g6 $1
{Avoiding the threat, and giving the King a "Role"} (24... Z0 {The threat is}
25. Nf5 {followed by} Z0 26. Qe8+ Nxe8 27. Rxe8+ Qf8 28. Ne7+ {wins.}) 25. cxd5
Qxd5 (25... cxd5 26. Nb5 {Is embarassing for me.}) 26. Qf4 Ne4 $1 {Again
taking advantage of White's weak position.} 27. h3 Qxd4 28. Rxe4 Ra1+ 29. Kh2
Qd6 30. Re8+ Kg7 31. Qxd6 cxd6 32. Rc8 Ra6 33. Kg3 Rb6 34. Kf4 c5 35. Rd8 Rxb3
36. Rxd6 Rb6 37. Rd7 a5 38. Rd5 Rb5 39. Rd3 a4 40. Ra3 Rb3 $4 {I was now
playing quickly on the assumption that anything would win.} ({Better was.} 
40... Rb4+) 41. Rxa4 Rb4+ 42. Rxb4 cxb4 43. Ke4 Kf6 44. Kd4 Kf5 45. Kc4 Ke4 46.
Kxb4 Kd3 47. Kc5 Ke2 48. f4 f5 $2 49. Kd5 Kf2 $2 50. g4 fxg4 $4 51. hxg4 Kf3
52. f5 Kxg4 53. f6 h5 54. f7 g5 55. f8=Q Kg3 56. Qf5 Kh4 57. Qf6 Kg4 58. Ke4
Kh4 59. Kf3 Kh3 60. Qxg5 {After losing a won game like this I felt like giving
up chess. I just didn't think during the ending (moves 32-60). I was pleased
with the opening. I must concentrate more.} 1-0

