{Mr Stephens was a reserve put in after board 3 did not turn up. He started
with 12 mins already on his clock.} 1. d4 {[12']} Nf6 2. Bf4 d5 {[1'] The
position of his Bishop would make it difficult to play ....e5 in a Kings
Indian set-up} 3. e3 {[13' 30s]} e6 {[2']} 4. Bd3 {[15']} c5 {[2' 30s]} 5. dxc5
{[16'] Hardly the best move.} Bxc5 {[2' 45s]} 6. c3 {[18'] A rather pointless
move.} Nc6 {[3']} 7. Nf3 {[20'] White has played the opening badly & now faces
the threat of ...e4 & ...e5.} O-O {[3']} 8. O-O {[24']} Re8 {[3' 15s]} 9. Ne5 {
[26']} Bd6 {[7' 15s] My Bishop didn't have much future on c5.} 10. Nxc6 {
[29' 30s] Strengthens my centre.} bxc6 {[7' 30s]} 11. Bxd6 {[31']} Qxd6 {
[7' 30s] My position is much better than White's.} 12. Nd2 {[32']} e5 {[7' 30s]
} 13. e4 {[35']} Bb7 {[10' 15s]} (13... d4 {is no good e.g.} 14. cxd4 exd4 15.
Nb3 c5 16. Rc1 Nd7 17. Qc2) 14. Re1 {[38' 30s]} Rad8 {[11' 30s]} 15. Qf3 $4 {
[42']} dxe4 {[12']} 16. Nxe4 {[43']} Qxd3 {[13']} 17. Nxf6+ {[44']} gxf6 {[13']
} 18. Qxf6 {[45']} Qg6 {[15']} 19. Qf3 {[46']} Rd3 {[16' 30s]} 20. Re3 {[49']}
Red8 {[19'] The threat is 21....c5. The Queen must cover d1 to the threat of
mate.} 21. Rf1 {[52']} Ba6 {[23'] Relieving the threat of the previous move
but now I put on even more pressure.} 22. Rfe1 {[56']} e4 {[25' 30s] If White
tries to win the Pawn I exchange Queens get a Rook on the 7th rank and
probably win the Pawn back together with mating threats on the back rank.
White lost on time. The time limit was 24 moves in 1st hour then 6 moves per
15 mins. (we played on unofficialy and I won in 70 moves. Hayes won the match
5-3} 0-1

