1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bc4 e6 7. Be3 Qc7 8. Bb3
b5 {This struck me as being somewhat premature.} 9. f3 Be7 10. Qd2 O-O 11.
O-O-O Rd8 (11... Bb7 12. Bxe6 {Is good for White.}) 12. Kb1 Nc6 13. Nce2 {
Doubtful as it allows black to play....Ne5....Nc4} (13. g4 {was alright.}) ({
I also considered...} 13. Nxc6 {followed by Ne2...Nd4}) 13... Ne5 14. Nc1 {
After much thought. This Knight will defend b2.} Nc4 15. Qe2 ({I also
considered..} 15. Qf2 {with eventual threats of...Bb6. However I need f2 for
my Bishop.}) 15... Bb7 16. Bf2 {Intending 17.Bg3 to prevent...d5} Rac8 17. g4 {
To pevent .....Nh5 after Bg3} Nxb2 {Unsound as my peculiarly placed pieces are
well placed for defence.} 18. Kxb2 Qc3+ 19. Kb1 d5 20. Be1 {There are other
moves but this is the best.} Qc7 21. exd5 (21. e5 {Is just as good.}) 21...
Bxd5 22. Bxd5 Nxd5 23. Ndb3 Bf6 24. Nd3 $1 {At last this Knight proves its
worth. I don't think anything else would save me.} Nc3+ (24... b4 $142) 25.
Bxc3 Qxc3 26. Qd2 Rxd3 {Aast chance.} 27. cxd3 (27. Qxd3 $4 Qb2#) (27. Qxc3 $4
Rxd1+) 27... Qe5 28. d4 Qd5 29. Rhf1 Rc4 30. Rc1 g6 31. Rxc4 Qxc4 32. Rc1 Qd5
33. Qd3 a5 34. Nxa5 Bxd4 35. Nb3 e5 36. Nxd4 {An interesting game. Juniors won
6.5-5.5} 1-0

