{Opponent Info: ex Middlesex Champion; E.M.I. Bd 1 [Time control was 30 sec a
move]} 1. e4 {The first move was made by the Chairman of the council.} c5 {
I didn't want to play a dull opening.} 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bc4 {White is playing 10
opponents so he plays drawish variations.} Nc6 4. O-O Nf6 5. Re1 e6 6. c3 Be7
7. d4 cxd4 8. cxd4 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nc3 Nxc3 11. bxc3 O-O {I probably had
better moves but didn't have time to think.} 12. Bf4 {Putting the dampers on
my intended 12.....Qc7} Bf6 {Attempting a strategic regrouping.} 13. Qe2 Ne7
14. Bd3 Nd5 15. Bd2 Bd7 16. c4 Ne7 17. Qe4 g6 18. Ne5 ({Not} 18. Qxb7 $2 Bc6 $1
) 18... Bc6 19. Qf4 Rc8 $4 {White returned almost immediately and I hadn't got
a move ready. I hadn't even thought about my move and just picked up a "safe"
piece.} 20. Qxf6 Qxd4 $2 21. Bh6 {I found it impossible to play at the speed
required. [Hayes Harlington Chess Week Finale - their 6th Annual display of
Teenagers and Old Stagers held at Townfield Sohool on March 18th. (Taken from
the SCCU buletin for March 1961)]} 1-0

