{Time limit: 24 moves in the 1st hour then 6 moves in 15 minutes.} 1. e4 c5 2.
Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 h6 8. Bh4 Be7 9. Nb3
a6 {[4']} (9... Nxe4 10. Bxe7 Nxc3 11. Qxd6 {Looks good for Black} ({....but
White plays} 11. Bxd8 Nxd1 12. Rxd1 Kxd8 13. Rxd6+)) 10. Qf3 {[3' 15s]} O-O {
[5']} 11. O-O-O {[3' 30s]} e5 {Doubtful.} 12. f5 g6 {Unnecessary.} 13. g4 g5
14. Bf2 {[9']} b5 15. h4 Kg7 {Black is getting worried.} 16. hxg5 {[15']} hxg5
17. Be3 {[16'] Forcing another retreat by Black.} Nd7 (17... Nh7 18. Qh3 {
Is very strong for White}) 18. Nd5 {[19' 15s]} Bb7 (18... Z0 {Threatens......}
19. Nxe7 Nxe7 (19... Qxe7 20. Qh3 $1) 20. Rxd6) 19. Be2 {To bring the QRook to
the KS.} Na5 $2 {A Mistake, but in Black's position mistakes are easy to make.}
20. Nxa5 Bxd5 21. Qh3 $3 {Wins a piece.} Rh8 22. Qxh8+ Qxh8 23. Rxh8 Rxh8 {
[29']} 24. Rxd5 {[32']} Nf6 25. Rd1 Nxe4 26. Bf3 Nc5 27. Bxc5 dxc5 28. Rh1 Rc8
({He could have tried.....} 28... Rh4) 29. Nb3 c4 30. Nd2 {Threatening 31.Bb7
winning a Pawn} a5 31. Ne4 f6 32. Rd1 Kf7 33. Nd6+ Bxd6 34. Rxd6 Ke7 35. Re6+
Kf7 36. Bd5 Rc5 37. Be4 Rc7 38. Rb6 Rc5 39. Rc6 Rxc6 40. Bxc6 b4 41. Bd5+ Ke7
42. Bxc4 Kd6 43. c3 Kc5 44. Bb3 {1 Adjudicated a win for White. A neat game.
HCGS won 5 -} 1-0

