{Time limit 48 moves in 2 hrs then 24 moves per hr.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. Qd2 O-O 8. f3 Nc6 9. O-O-O d5 {
A promising pawn casrifice which I hadn't seen before.} 10. Nxc6 bxc6 11. exd5
cxd5 {[2']} 12. Nxd5 {[5']} Nxd5 {[5' 30s]} 13. Qxd5 {[5' 30s]} Qc7 {[12']} 14.
Qc5 $2 {[10'] After this I was soon in difficulties. I played this under the
impression that I could get the exchange of Queens.} ({I could not play....} 
14. Qxa8 $2 {....because of....} Bf5 $1) (14. Bd3 {Is better as it prevents 14.
....Bf5}) 14... Qb7 {[13']} 15. Bd4 $2 {[13'] Leading to more difficulties.} (
15. Qa3 {Looks better.}) 15... Bf5 {[16'] Now I really am in trouble.} 16. Qb5
{[26'] This also turns out very badly but I didn't have much choice.} (16. a3 {
Comes to grief against....} Bh6+) 16... Qc7 {[25']} ({Here Black was under the
impression he could regain the Pawn by.} 16... Rfc8 17. Qxb7 Rxc2+ 18. Kb1 Rc7+
{but he didn't play this because it allows too many exchanges. However I was
ready for this and would have won a piece by....} 19. Qe4 {...Black hadn't
seen this move, I had! So it's a pity he didn't try to regain the Pawn.}) 17.
Qa4 {[30'] What else?} ({If....} 17. Qc5 Bh6+ {wins at least the exchange.})
17... Rfc8 {[40']} ({I expected...} 17... Qf4+ {to which I would have resigned.
}) 18. Bd3 {[37' 30s] Everything loses.} Qf4+ 19. Rd2 {[38'] Now I have 2
Bishops a Rook and a Pawn all pinned.} ({If...} 19. Kb1 e5 {Black hadn't seen
this either. Unfortunately I had.}) 19... Bxd3 {A very good attack by Black}
0-1

