1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 c5 4. d5 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. Nf3 g6 7. e4 Bg7 8. Be2 {
Rather passive.} O-O 9. O-O a6 {[1']} 10. Bg5 Qc7 11. Rc1 b5 12. b4 {Not very
good.} (12. a3 $142) 12... c4 13. a4 Qb7 14. a5 {A rather pointless move.} Re8
15. Qc2 {[17']} Nbd7 {[8']} 16. Bf4 Qc7 17. Nd4 $2 {Creates a weakness at d4}
Bb7 18. Bf3 $2 {Loses a Pawn for a worse position.} Nxd5 $1 19. exd5 Bxd4 20.
Ne4 {[25]} Be5 {[13']} 21. Bxe5 Nxe5 $6 (21... Rxe5 {Saves the exchange but
White risks a lot by accepting it.}) 22. Nf6+ $5 {Wins the exchange fpr
several Pawns and a smashed KS.} Kf8 23. Nxe8 Nxf3+ 24. gxf3 Rxe8 {[14']} 25.
Rcd1 Re5 {Threatens the d-Pawn and a KS attack.} 26. Rfe1 Rg5+ 27. Kf1 {
safer than h1.} (27. Kh1 {The King has no escape squares and is on the long
diagonal.}) 27... Qd7 28. Re3 {Anything else is suicidal.} Qh3+ 29. Ke2 Qxh2 (
29... Bxd5 $2 30. Qc3) 30. Qc3 Re5 {[24']} 31. Rxe5 Qxe5+ 32. Qxe5 dxe5 33. d6
Ke8 34. Rh1 {[42']} (34. d7+ $142 Kd8 35. Rd6) 34... h5 {[22']} 35. Rd1 Kd7 {
Now White is quite lost. I manoeuvre my Bishop to d3 and then win the d-Pawn.}
36. Ke3 g5 37. Rg1 f6 38. Rh1 h4 39. Rh3 {[52'] Not even trying to save the
d-Pawn.} Kxd6 {[24']} 40. Rh2 Bc8 41. Rh1 Bf5 42. Rd1+ Bd3 43. Rd2 Ke6 44. Rd1
f5 45. Rg1 {Adjourned. White resigned. Played quickly as I had another match
the same evening. HCGS I won the mach 3.5 - 2.5} (45. Rg1 f4+ 46. Kd2 Kf5) 0-1

