{Time limit 24per hour followed by 6 every 15 min. D.G.Levens is graded 5a 
(177-184 ECF) in the BCF gradings 1961.} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4
Bc5 (4... Nf6 {Is the most usual continuation.}) 5. Be3 Bb6 (5... Qf6 {so as
to answer the threatened..} 6. Nxc6 {with} Bxe3 {is given in most opening
books.}) 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. Bc4 d6 ({I considered.....} 7... Qe7 {but White would
reply} 8. Nf5) 8. O-O O-O 9. h3 {I don't think this was necessary, I wasn't
foing to develop my Bishop to g4 anyway.} Nxd4 10. Bxd4 Bxd4 11. Qxd4 {[14']}
Re8 {[16']} 12. f4 {[15']} Be6 {[23'] Forcing the Bishop onto an unfavourable
diagonal.} 13. Bd3 c6 {Not the best move as the d-Pawn is left terribly weak.
I realised this at the time but hoped to force .....d5 and also I am now
threatening 14.....Qb6 forcing an exchange of Queens. However I never get the
chance to play ....d5 and the d-Pawn causes me a lot of trouble.} 14. f5 Bc8 ({
13....c6 causes me trouble already. I can't play....} 14... Bd7) 15. Kh1 {
Preventing the Queen exchange.} Qc7 ({I considered....} 15... Re5 {...followed
by...} 16. Z0 Qe7 {...and....} 17. Z0 d5 {If White puts his Rook on e1 I can't
play this.}) 16. Rae1 Bd7 {Good moves are conspicuous by there abscence.} 17.
g4 h6 18. Rg1 {[25']} Nh7 {[47']} (18... Rad8 {Looked quite good but the
a-Pawn would be left en prise.}) ({However....} 18... Re5 {followed by.....}
19. Z0 d5 {Looks reasonable.}) 19. h4 Qd8 20. Qf2 f6 ({if...} 20... d5 21. e5)
21. Bc4+ Kf8 ({If} 21... Kh8 {I face a terrific KS attack.}) 22. Qf4 Re5 {
[56'] This has been in the offing for some time.} 23. Rd1 Qe7 $2 {[57'] Time
trouble.} (23... Qc7 {...to be followed by....} 24. Z0 Ke7 {looks better.}) 24.
Rg3 {[40']} Rd8 {[58']} 25. Rgd3 Be8 26. Be6 (26. Qd2 $2 Rxe4 $1) 26... Bf7 {
[59' 45s]} 27. Bxf7 Kxf7 28. Qd2 Nf8 (28... Rxe4 29. Nxe4 Qxe4+ 30. Qg2 {
isn't good enough.}) 29. Kh2 ({White said that if he played...} 29. Rxd6 {
I had a perp by...} Rxe4 {but I can't find it.}) ({Anyway...} 29. Kg1 {is
better.}) 29... Qc7 $1 30. Rxd6 Ke7 $1 {My best chance.} 31. Rxd8 Rd5+ 32. Kg2
Rxd2+ 33. R8xd2 {Adjourned. Agreed drawn. Clocks White 1hr-----Black 1hr 19'
30s An interesting game. Hayes lost the match 3.5-4.5. Cedars won the
Middlesex league. I am now leading the scoring averages for Hayes in the Middx
league (and this was the last match) with 5W 4D 1L=70% avg Bd 4.7} (33. R8xd2 {
My best line is} Qf4 34. Rd3 g5 {And I can probably hold on.} ({Not} 34...
Qxg4+ $4 35. Rg3 $1)) 1/2-1/2

