{[Time limit is 24 moves in 1Hr] Opponent Info: Plays for Middlesex seniors.} 
1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. g3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. Bg2 Be6 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. O-O Bc5 $2 {
This leads to great complications from which I emerge a Pawn down.} 8. Nxe5
Nxe5 (8... Bxf2+ {might be an improvement.}) 9. d4 Nxc3 (9... Bxd4 10. Qxd4
Nxc3 11. Qxc3 Nc6 12. Bxc6+ {with a won game for White.}) 10. bxc3 Nd7 11. dxc5
({Also good if not better was} 11. Bxb7 Rb8 12. dxc5 Rxb7 13. c6) 11... c6 {
This leads to great difficulties.} (11... Rb8 {might have been better.}) (11...
Nxc5 {didn't look very good} 12. Qxd8+ Rxd8 13. Be3 {With advantage to White
due to my weak b-Pawn} ({or} 13. Ba3)) 12. Qd6 Qa5 {Played after much thought.
[Time 36 min]} ({If} 12... Qe7 13. Qc7 Nxc5 $4 14. Qxe7+ Kxe7 15. Ba3 $1) ({If
} 12... Nf6 13. Rd1 Qxd6 14. cxd6) 13. Be3 (13. Bg5 Qxc5) 13... Rg8 {[50 min]
I hadn't much choice White threatened 14.?d4 so I had to defend the g-Pawn.
Now I have 10 mins for 11 moves.} ({Therefore not} 13... Qxc3 $4 14. Bd4) 14.
Rac1 Qxa2 {[54'] I didn't have time to analys the position so I decided to
take the Pawn and hope for the best.} (14... h6 {Looks good.}) 15. Bg5 Nf6 $2 {
Not the best but played in a hurry.} (15... f6 {looks best.}) 16. Bxf6 gxf6 17.
Rfd1 Qxe2 $2 {Hoping for the best in time trouble.} (17... Qa4 {Looks best.})
18. Bxc6+ $1 bxc6 19. Qxc6+ Ke7 20. Qb7+ Kf8 21. Qxa8+ Kg7 22. Qb7 Re8 23. Re1
Qd2 24. Qb1 Bh3 {A last hope. I had just scraped through the time control.} 25.
Qa1 {Quite interesting I got the worst of the opening but could just have hung
on with 14.....h6! if I hadn't been in time trouble. The match was tied 4-4 
(8Bd)} ({If} 25. Qc2 $4 Rxe1+) 1-0

