1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. Bf4 {Not very good really} Nd7 5. Nc3 c5 6. d5
Nb6 7. Qd2 a6 {I want to play .....f5 and don't want to play my QBishop to d7
should White play Bb5+} 8. Bd3 $2 c4 9. Be2 Qc7 10. Be3 f5 (10... Z0 {
Threatening....} 11. Bxb6 Qxb6 12. Bxc4 {but I could play.....} Qxb2) 11. Nd4
$2 fxe4 12. Nxe4 Nxd5 13. f4 {A bit odd.} Nxe3 {Unnecessary.} (13... Ngf6 $142)
14. Qxe3 Qb6 (14... Nf6 $142) 15. O-O-O d5 16. Nc3 e6 $4 {How ridiculous. Even
more so because I had considered...} 17. Nxd5 {...but forgot about it.} Bxd4 $2
(17... Qd6 $142) 18. Rxd4 Qc5 $2 19. Bxc4 $2 (19. Nf6+ $142 Nxf6 20. Rd8+ $1)
19... b5 $2 20. Bb3 $2 {Inow saw that my Queen was threatened and the only
safe square was c6. Afterwards White said that he hadn't seen he could win my
Queen.} Qc6 21. Qe5 {An offday indeed.} 1-0

