{Opponent Info: Hayes C.C Bd 4 or 5.} 1. d4 f5 2. e3 {Passive.} Nf6 3. Nd2 {
This is Mr.Ayers' speciality} g6 {Intending to play the leningrad.} 4. Bc4 {
Forcing me to transpose into a normal Dutch.} e6 5. Ngf3 Nc6 6. a3 {On 6....
Na5 to reply 7.Ba2} d5 {Leaves a hole on e5 but it's necessary.} 7. Bb5 Bd7 8.
b4 {Not very good.} ({Not} 8. Ne5 $2 Nxe5 $1) 8... Ne4 {Threatening 9.....Nc3}
9. Nxe4 fxe4 {Securing attacking chances on the KS.} 10. Bxc6 Bxc6 (10... bxc6
{Loses a Pawn.}) 11. Ne5 Bb5 {A good diagonal.} 12. a4 $2 {He played this
without thinking} Bxb4+ 13. Bd2 Bxd2+ 14. Qxd2 Ba6 15. f4 exf3 16. Nxf3 Qe7 {
To castle QS.} 17. Rb1 $2 Qa3 18. Qb4 $4 {5 This allows mate in} ({Correct is.
} 18. Rb4) 18... Qxe3+ {I now lead the championship with 4.5 out of 5.} (18...
Qxe3+ {I mate by....} 19. Kd1 Be2+ 20. Ke1 Bxf3+ 21. Kf1 Qe2+ 22. Kg1 Qxg2#)
0-1

