1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 {Alternatives are.}
(6... Nbd7) (6... e5) 7. Be2 cxd4 {Transposing into a siciliian.} 8. Nxd4 a6 {
I had already taken 5 times as long on my clock as White.} 9. Be3 Nc6 10. O-O
Qb6 {This unsettles White.} 11. Na4 {White proceeds to lose a tempo.} ({
Better...} 11. Nc2 {and if.....} Qxb2 $4 12. Na4 {Wins my Queen.}) 11... Qc7
12. Nc3 Nxd4 13. Bxd4 Be6 14. b3 {Opens the long diagonal.} Bd7 {The Bishop
was no good at e6.} 15. Kh1 {Not really necessary.} e6 {My d-Pawn is not
really weak. I am preparing for .....d5 and also prevent 16.Nd5} 16. Qd3 Bc6
17. Rf3 {Beginning a doubtful attacking plan.} (17. Rad1 $142) 17... Rad8 18.
Rh3 $2 e5 {Wins a Pawn.} 19. Be3 (19. fxe5 dxe5 {loses a piece.}) 19... exf4
20. Bd4 ({Not} 20. Bxf4 $2 Nxe4 21. Nxe4 {Forced.} Bxe4 22. Qxe4 Bxa1) 20...
Rfe8 21. Qf3 {This leads to interesting complications.} Bd7 22. Rh4 g5 23. Bxf6
gxh4 (23... Bxf6 24. Nd5 Bxa1 25. Nxc7 gxh4 26. Nxe8 Rxe8 27. Qxf4 $18) 24.
Bxd8 Qxd8 ({Not} 24... Rxd8 25. Nd5 $1) 25. Rd1 $2 Bxc3 26. Qxc3 Rxe4 {I am
two Pawns up but they are too weak to offer many winning chances, especially
as I was now in time trouble.} 27. Bf3 Re3 28. Qd4 Qe7 29. h3 ({Not} 29. Qxd6
$4 Re1+) (29. Qxf4 $4 Re1+) 29... Bxh3 $2 {Playedin time trouble- a doubtful
move.} 30. Qxf4 Qe5 {A real time trouble mistake. I immediately realised it
wasn't good and offered a draw which he accepted. He shouldn't have! Being in
time trouble I would probably have lost. An interesting debut for Middlesex
seniors. It is strange that I got the same opponent in both the middle Jnr 
(U-18) and Snr matches ( a 4,800-1 chance) Middlesex won the Aboyna Shield 28
- 22.} 1/2-1/2

