1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. g3 g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. d3 d6 6. Nge2 Bg4 {Preventing 7.Nf4
and exchanging my worst Bishop for his best Knight.} 7. Be3 Bxe2 ({I want to
play} 7... e6 {...however...} 8. f3 {wins. So I exchange the Bishop first.}) 8.
Nxe2 Bxb2 9. Rb1 Qa5+ {This leads to great complications.} 10. Bd2 Qxa2 11.
Rxb2 Qxb2 12. Bc3 Qa2 {The best square. It allows me to trap the Bishop later
after ....f6...by Qf7.} 13. Bxh8 f6 14. O-O Qf7 15. Qb1 O-O-O (15... b6 {
Looks even more risky.}) 16. Qb3 Qxb3 $2 (16... Qf8 $142) 17. cxb3 Nh6 18. Bh3+
{This gain of a tempo saves his QBishop.} Kc7 19. Bg7 Nf7 20. Be6 Ng5 21. Bd5
Nf3+ 22. Kg2 Ncd4 23. Nxd4 Nxd4 24. f4 e6 25. Bc4 (25. Bxf6 exd5 26. Bxd8+ Kxd8
27. exd5 Nxb3 {With a fair game for Black.}) 25... Rd7 {I have to play this
now or next move.} 26. Bxf6 b5 ({I had originally intended.} 26... d5 27. Bxd4
dxc4 {Intending cxb but White has.} 28. Be5+) 27. Bxd4 bxc4 28. Be3 cxd3 29.
Rd1 d5 30. Rxd3 ({Not} 30. Bxc5 $2 Kc6 $1) 30... d4 31. Bf2 Kd6 32. b4 Kc6 33.
bxc5 Kxc5 34. Kf3 Kc4 35. Ke2 a5 {A faint hope which gets fainter as the
Queening square being the wrong colour.} 36. g4 a4 37. f5 exf5 38. gxf5 gxf5
39. exf5 Re7+ {Semi-Zugzwang.} 40. Kd2 Rf7 41. Rxd4+ Kb3 42. Rf4 a3 43. Bd4 Rd7
44. Ke3 a2 45. Rf1 Kc4 ({The plan of....} 45... Ka3 46. Z0 Rb7 47. Z0 Rb1 {
....might be better.}) 46. Ba1 Re7+ 47. Kf4 Rb7 48. Rf2 Kb3 {Puts an end to it
but I was completely lost anyway.} 49. Rb2+ {An interesting game. As usual I
started off determined to play carefully but as usual I started to play too
quickly.} 1-0

