{Opponent Info: London U-12 Champion; Southern Counties U-12 Champion.} 1. d4
f5 2. Bg5 g6 ({Not} 2... h6 3. Bh4 g5 4. Bg3 f4 5. e3 $1) 3. c4 Bg7 4. Nc3 Nf6
5. e3 d6 6. g3 O-O 7. Bxf6 (7. Z0 {The threat is....} Ne4 8. Nxe4 fxe4 {
and my QBishop is in danger.}) 7... Bxf6 8. Bg2 c6 9. h4 {Intending 10.h5} e5
10. d5 c5 {Leaves the d-Pawn weak.} 11. e4 {Prevents 11.....e5.} f4 12. h5 {
Prevents12.....h5 followed by 13.....Bg4.} (12. gxf4 {Is bad for me.}) 12... g5
13. g4 {More or less forced or my h-Pawn is left weak.} h6 14. f3 {
Strengthening the g-Pawn. This position is rather ridiculous but Black was
playing for a draw so he was quite happy.} Bd7 15. Bf1 {Bringing my Bishop
back into play and preventing 15.....b5.} Na6 16. a3 Nc7 {Adjourned. The game
resumed on 4/6/61} 17. Nb5 {[Sealed move] I wanted to obtain some winning
chances by breaking up the pawns. Also I will be able to chose when to open up
the game by b4.} Nxb5 18. cxb5 Qa5+ 19. Qd2 Qxd2+ 20. Kxd2 a6 21. bxa6 bxa6 22.
Bc4 Rfb8 23. Kc2 Bb5 24. Bxb5 Rxb5 $2 {I now have good squares for my Knight
at c4,c6,a4.} (24... axb5 {Was better.}) 25. Nh3 {Tring to get my Knight to c4
via f2,d1,c3,b1,d2} Rab8 26. Ra2 ({If I play....} 26. Rab1 {...I can't perform
the Knight manoeuvre}) 26... Rb3 27. Rf1 Kf7 28. Ng1 Bd8 (28... Re3 $142) 29.
Ne2 Ba5 30. Nc1 R3b7 (30... Re3 {Is risky here...on account of...} 31. Nd3 {
getting the Rook stranded.}) 31. Nd3 Rc8 (31... Rb3 $4 32. Nb4 $1) 32. Rb1 c4
$2 {A weakening move.} 33. Nb4 $1 Bxb4 {...or the Knight goes to c6.} 34. axb4
Rb6 ({The alternative is....} 34... Rxb4 35. Rxa6 Ke7 36. Ra7+ Kd8 37. Rh7 Rb3
38. Rf1 Rcb8 39. Rxh6 {etc and Black draws.}) 35. Kc3 Rcb8 36. Ra4 Rc8 37. Rba1
Rcb8 38. Kxc4 Ke7 39. Kb3 $2 {This makes matters unduly difficult.} a5 $1 40.
Rc1 Rxb4+ 41. Rxb4 Rxb4+ 42. Ka3 Kd7 {The difficulty is winning Black's a-Pawn
in that it keeps leaving my b-Pawn en prise. However I control the c-file and
can keep out Black's King.} 43. Rc3 Rb5 44. Rc6 a4 45. Rc3 {Prevents the Rook
check and loss of the f-Pawn.} Kd8 46. Ka2 {My King and Rook must change
places.} Kd7 47. Ra3 Rb4 ({Not....} 47... Ra5 {as I would eventually threaten
b3.}) 48. Rc3 Rb5 {Hoping for a draw by repetition.} 49. Kb1 Rb6 50. Kc2 Ra6
51. Ra3 Kc7 52. Kc3 Kb7 53. Ra1 ({If} 53. Kb4 {Black can play.} Rb6+) (53. Ra2
{Is more exact.}) 53... Ka7 54. Ra2 {Protecting the b-Pawn.} Kb6 55. Kb4 Ra5
56. Rxa4 Rb5+ (56... Rxa4+ {appears to lose} 57. Kxa4 Ka6 58. b3 Kb6 59. b4 Ka6
60. b5+ Kb6 61. Kb4 Ka7 62. Ka5 Kb7 63. b6 Kb8 64. Kb4 Kb7 65. Kb5 Kb8 66. Kc6)
57. Kc3 Rc5+ 58. Kd2 Rb5 59. b4 Kb7 60. Kc3 Kc7 61. Kc4 Rb7 62. Ra6 Kd7 ({Not} 
62... Rb6 $4 63. Ra7+ Rb7 64. Rxb7+ $18) 63. Ra3 {Protecting the 3rd rank.} (
63. b5 {Was the alternative.}) 63... Rc7+ 64. Kb3 Rc8 65. b5 Kd8 66. Kb4 Rc2
67. Ka5 Kc8 68. Kb6 Kd7 (68... Kb8 69. Ra7) 69. Ka6 Rc8 70. Rb3 Ra8+ 71. Kb7
Rc8 72. b6 Rc5 73. Ra3 {Allowing 47.Ka7} Rc2 74. Ka7 Kd8 75. b7 Rc7 76. Ka8 {
Not a faultless but an interesting marathon.} 1-0

