1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. g3 b6 5. Bg2 Bb7 6. Nf3 Nbd7 7. O-O Be7 8. Ne5
O-O ({If...} 8... Nxe5 9. dxe5 Ng4 10. cxd5 exd5 11. Nxd5 Bxd5 12. Qxd5 Qxd5
13. Bxd5 Rd8 14. Bc6+ Kf8 15. f4) 9. b3 c5 10. e3 Rc8 11. Bb2 cxd4 12. exd4 Qc7
13. Nb5 Qb8 14. Qe2 {Observing his undefended KBishop.} a6 15. Nc3 dxc4 16.
Nxc4 (16. Nxd7 Nxd7 17. d5 $6 {...isn't too good after....} e5) 16... Bxg2 17.
Kxg2 b5 18. Nd2 Bb4 (18... b4 $142) (18... Rc7 $142) 19. Rac1 Bxc3 20. Bxc3
Qb7+ 21. Qf3 $1 Qxf3+ 22. Nxf3 Nd5 23. Bd2 $1 f6 24. Rfe1 Kf7 25. Kf1 N7b6 26.
Nh4 $1 Rxc1 $2 {Expecting to be able to trade off Rooks.} 27. Rxc1 Rc8 28. Rc5
$1 b4 $2 29. Ng2 $1 Rxc5 30. dxc5 Nd7 31. Ne3 Nxc5 32. Nxd5 exd5 33. Bxb4 Nd3 {
[57']} 34. Bd2 Ke6 {He offered a draw here.} 35. Ke2 Ne5 36. f4 Nc6 37. Kd3 f5
38. b4 Kd6 39. a4 Na7 40. Be3 Nc8 41. Bc5+ {Stalemating the Knight.} Kc6 42.
Kd4 {After exhausting his Pawn moves Black will be in Zugzwang.} g6 43. h3 Nd6
{Loses but there is no alternative.} 44. Bxd6 Kxd6 45. g4 $4 {Much too
careless.} (45. b5 {Wins easily.}) 45... fxg4 46. hxg4 h5 47. gxh5 gxh5 48. b5
axb5 49. axb5 $4 (49. a5 $3) 49... h4 50. b6 h3 51. b7 Kc7 52. f5 h2 53. f6
h1=Q 54. f7 Qe4+ 55. Kc3 Qe7 {45 I'm hopelessy out of form due to lack of
practice (2 serious games since easter). I played well up to move} 0-1

