1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. e3 g6 4. Bd3 Bg7 5. O-O e5 6. dxe5 Nxe5 7. Nbd2 f5 {
Preventing 8.e4 and making the development of my QBishop difficult.} 8. Nxe5
Bxe5 9. Nf3 Bg7 10. c4 {Trying to break his control of e4.} Be6 11. Qc2 Nf6 12.
Ng5 (12. cxd5 Bxd5 {Is a nuisance.}) 12... Bg8 $2 {Turns out not too well.} 13.
cxd5 Nxd5 14. e4 $1 {Black hadn't realised I could play this.} h6 15. Nf3 Nb4
16. Qa4+ Nc6 17. Qc2 Qd6 $2 18. Bb5 O-O-O {Removes the pin and threatens 19....
Nd4} 19. Bxc6 bxc6 20. exf5 gxf5 21. Qxf5+ Be6 22. Qe4 Rdf8 {[40 mins]} 23. Re1
{[57']} Bd5 24. Qg4+ {[59 3/4 min]} Kb8 25. Nh4 {Adjudicated Drawn (I should
have won) I think I would have won if we played on from the finishing position.
Hayes won the match 6.5-1.5 (8Bd)} ({Not} 25. Qxg7 Bxf3 $1 {Black was
threatening to play BxN with a big attack anyway}) 1/2-1/2

