{Time limit 36 moves in 90 mins then 24 per hour.} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 {Rather old
fashioned.} d6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. Bb5 Bd7 5. Bxc6 Bxc6 6. d3 e6 7. O-O Nf6 8. h3 Be7
9. Nc3 O-O 10. g4 {Not a particularly frightening attack.} Qc7 11. g5 {Rather
commital, more preparation is needed.} Nd7 12. h4 {[6']} f5 $1 {[54'] Putting
an end to his attack.} 13. exf5 Rxf5 (13... exf5 {..is less enterprising.}) 14.
d4 Qb6 15. dxc5 Qxc5+ 16. Kh2 e5 17. Qe2 ({If...} 17. fxe5 Raf8) 17... Re8 18.
Ne4 Qb4 19. Ng3 Rff8 20. c3 Qa5 21. fxe5 dxe5 22. Nd2 Rxf1 23. Qxf1 Rf8 24. Qe2
Bd6 25. Nde4 Bc7 ({Somewhat better was...} 25... Bb8) 26. Be3 a6 27. a3 Bxe4
28. Nxe4 Qa4 29. Qd3 Qc6 30. Rd1 Nb6 31. Bxb6 Bxb6 32. Qd5+ Qxd5 33. Rxd5 Rf4
$1 34. Rd6 Bc7 $1 35. Rd7 Rxe4 36. Rxc7 Re2+ 37. Kg3 Rxb2 38. Rc8+ Kf7 39. Rc7+
Kg6 40. Kg4 {Threatening Mate!} h5+ 41. gxh6 Kxh6 42. Re7 Rb5 43. a4 Ra5 44.
Rxb7 Rxa4+ 45. Kf5 Rxh4 46. Rb6+ Kh7 47. Rxa6 Rc4 48. Kxe5 Rxc3 49. Kf5 {
Adjourned. I sealed 49.....Rc5+ but agreed to a draw without resuming. Not bad
for my first game for several weeks.} 1/2-1/2

