{Time limit 36 moves in 90 mins then 24 per hour.} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5
exd5 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Bg5 Be7 6. Bxf6 {White should wait for Black to play .....
h6 before exchanging.} Bxf6 7. Nc3 O-O 8. Bd3 $2 (8. Be2 $142) 8... Re8+ 9. Be2
c5 {Keeping the game from becoming drawish.} 10. O-O Bg4 11. Re1 Nc6 12. dxc5 {
Now he gains a pawn but his Pawn structure on the QS is ruined.} Bxc3 13. bxc3
Qa5 14. Qxd5 Qxc3 {[6'] Threatening 15.....RxB} 15. Qc4 {This allows me to
simplify into a favouravle endgame! but the alternatives were better.} (15. Qf5
$2 Bxf3 16. gxf3 Rxe2 $1) 15... Qxc4 16. Bxc4 Bxf3 17. gxf3 Nd4 {Regaining the
Pawn. In this position his Pawns are totally weak and my Knight is as good as
his Bishop.} 18. Red1 Nxf3+ 19. Kg2 Ne5 20. Bb5 Red8 21. Re1 $2 {[43'] White
tries to retain as many pieces as possible but this loses a Pawn.} Rd5 22. Rab1
Rxc5 23. Ba4 b6 24. Rb5 (24. Rb5 {Played on the assumption that.....} Rxb5 25.
Bxb5 Ng6 26. Re8+ Rxe8 27. Bxe8 {His BvN will compensate for his weak Pawns.
However...}) 24... Rxb5 25. Bxb5 f6 $1 26. f4 Ng6 27. Kg3 {White does not get
the time to play Re8+} Kf8 28. h4 Rc8 29. Bd3 Kf7 30. h5 Nf8 31. Be4 {
Threatening 32.Bd5+} Rc5 32. c4 {Same threat.} f5 {The only move worth playing.
} 33. Bd5+ {[64']} Kf6 {[44']} 34. Re8 Nd7 {White now sees the chance to
regain his Pawn.} 35. Re6+ Kf7 36. Rxb6+ $2 {...but overlooks...} Rxd5 $1 37.
Rb5 Rxb5 38. cxb5 Ke6 39. Kf3 Kd5 40. Ke3 Nf6 0-1

