{Time control 24 per hour then 6 every 15min} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 exd4 4.
Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 {Presumably to prevent me getting a Knight or Bishop on b5
but this was not really necessary.} 6. Bd3 ({I idn't like....} 6. Bc4 {because
of 6.....b5, 7.....b4, and 8.....NxP}) 6... Be7 7. Be3 Bg4 $2 {Wasting a tempo
as I had intended playing 8.f3 anyway.} 8. f3 Be6 9. Qd2 Nbd7 10. O-O-O Nc5 11.
Nxe6 Nxd3+ 12. Qxd3 fxe6 13. Ne2 {Bringing the Knight to a better position and
threatening 14.Qb3} e5 14. g4 {The most promising move I think.} Qd7 {[16']}
15. Ng3 {[20']} O-O-O {[21']} 16. Qb3 {[27']} Rhf8 17. h3 {To defend the
g-Pawn after f4.} g6 $2 ({Better would be....} 17... Ng8 {'fixing' my f Pawn})
18. f4 Qb5 $2 {This turns out badly for Black.} 19. Qxb5 axb5 20. f5 $1 {
This offers the best chance of a win.} d5 21. Bg5 {[41']} dxe4 22. Bxf6 Rxf6 $2
(22... Bxf6 $142) 23. g5 $1 Ra6 {This too turns out badly.} 24. f6 Bc5 $2 {
Doubtful the Bishop is immediately attacked.} (24... Rxa2 $2 {would have
threatened mate but after...} 25. Kb1 {the Bishop would be lost.}) 25. Rxd8+
Kxd8 26. Nxe4 Bf8 27. Rd1+ Ke8 28. Rd5 c6 {peculiar, but what else?} 29. Rxe5+
Kf7 30. a3 Ra8 31. Nd2 Re8 32. Rxe8 Kxe8 33. b4 {Furthet limiting the scope of
the Bishop.} h6 34. h4 hxg5 35. hxg5 Bd6 36. Ne4 Bf4+ 37. Kb2 b6 38. Kb3 Kf7
39. a4 bxa4+ {[1hr 20']} 40. Kxa4 {[62'] Adjudicated Win for White hayes won
the match} 1-0

