1. c4 e5 2. g3 Bc5 {Unusual, but he plays the movesin a difefrent order.} 3.
Bg2 Nf6 4. Nc3 O-O 5. d3 Bb4 $2 {Breaking all the rules.} 6. Bd2 c6 {Wanting
to play 7.....d5.} 7. Nf3 Re8 8. O-O d5 $2 {This turns out badly.} 9. Nxd5 $1
cxd5 {Loses a pawn.} ({but after.....} 9... Nxd5 10. cxd5 Bxd2 11. Nxd2 cxd5
12. Qb3 {White stands much better.}) 10. Bxb4 dxc4 {Black proceeds to exchange
off with disasterous consequences.} 11. dxc4 Qxd1 12. Rfxd1 Bg4 $2 {very risky
as his b-Pawn is undefended.} 13. Bc3 (13. Nxe5 {is less safe.}) 13... Bxf3 14.
Bxf3 Nc6 15. Bxc6 bxc6 16. Rd6 {Black's position is hopeless. He has a
weakness on the back-row,a6, e5 & c6 also a useless Knight against a good
Bishop and I have the d-file.} Rac8 17. f3 {lessening the scope of the Knight.}
Nh5 {Where's he going?} 18. Rad1 Nf6 19. Kf2 Kf8 20. h3 Rc7 {Black has no plan.
} 21. Ba5 Rb7 22. b3 Rc8 23. Bc3 Re7 $2 {What else?} 24. Rd8+ Rxd8 25. Rxd8+
Ne8 $2 (25... Re8 {Would prolong the agony somewhat.}) 26. Bb4 f6 27. Bxe7+
Kxe7 28. Ra8 Kd6 $2 {0 [45'] Putting an end to it by playing without thinking
but the result was hardly in doubt. Black had a lost game after about 12 moves.
HCGS won 6 -} 29. Rxe8 {[30']} 1-0

