1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O d6 ({Normal is} 4... Nxe4) 5. Re1 Be7 6.
c3 O-O 7. h3 {Prevents 7.....Bg4 which I don't like.} a6 8. Ba4 h6 {Not really
necessary} 9. d4 b5 10. Bc2 Nh7 {To put a piece on g5 or to play ...f5} 11.
dxe5 dxe5 (11... f5 {He loses his e-Pawn.}) 12. Nbd2 Be6 13. Nf1 Qxd1 14. Rxd1
Rad8 15. Be3 g5 16. N3h2 {Preventing 16.....g4 and intending an evenual Ng4} b4
17. Bb3 $1 {The best move I think.} bxc3 (17... Bxb3 {Is very risky.}) 18. bxc3
Bxb3 19. axb3 Rxd1 20. Rxd1 Rd8 {His position being inferior he should not
endevour to exchange Rooks.} 21. Rd2 Rxd2 22. Nxd2 {The Knight is well placed
here.} Nf6 23. Ng4 Nxg4 {I don't know if this is best, certainly Black gains
nothing by it.} 24. hxg4 f6 25. Kf1 Kf7 26. Ke2 Nd8 $2 (26... Ke6 {Is surely
better.}) 27. Kd3 c5 $2 (27... Ke6 $142) 28. Kc4 Ne6 29. Kd5 Nc7+ {Black now
has a lost game.} 30. Kc6 Nb5 31. Bxc5 Bxc5 32. Kxc5 Nxc3 33. Kb6 Ke7 {The
King advances too late.} 34. Kxa6 Kd7 35. b4 Kc7 36. b5 Kb8 37. b6 Nd1 {
Desperation.} 38. Nb3 Nxf2 39. Nc5 Nxe4 (39... Nxg4 {Makes no difference.}) 40.
Nxe4 {I now have 6.5 out of 8 in the championship} 1-0

