1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Bd3 {Loses a tempo} Bxc3+ {Not necessary as it
allows 8.Ba3} 5. bxc3 dxe4 6. Bxe4 Nf6 7. Bf3 Nbd7 8. Ba3 c6 9. Ne2 Nb6 10. Qd3
{To prevent 10.....Nc4} Qc7 11. O-O Bd7 12. Rab1 O-O-O {Just asking to be
attacked, but I have good defensive resources.} 13. c4 e5 14. c5 {Making his
QBishop ueseless.} Nbd5 15. Rb3 Kb8 16. Rfb1 Bc8 17. c4 ({Better would be...} 
17. g3 {first.}) 17... Nf4 18. Nxf4 $2 Rxd4 19. Qc3 Rxf4 20. Bc1 Rd4 21. Be3
Rd7 22. Bg5 {Threatening 23.BxN PxB 24.Bg4!} Rhd8 23. h3 (23. Bxf6 gxf6 24. Bg4
f5 $1 25. Bxf5 $2 Rd1+) 23... Rd3 24. Qc2 Rxb3 25. Rxb3 Be6 26. Rb4 {
Threatening 27.BxN PxB 28.QxPh} Qa5 27. Qb2 Qc7 28. a4 Rd4 29. Be2 a5 30. Rb6
Bxc4 $2 (30... Bxc4 $2 {here I thought I could play after....} 31. Be3 Re4 32.
Bf3 Rxe3 33. fxe3 Nd7 34. Rb3 Bxb3 35. Qxb3 {etc. but.....}) 31. Be3 Re4 32.
Bf3 Rxe3 33. fxe3 Nd7 34. Rxc6 {The move I had forgotten.} Qd8 35. Rd6 Qc7 36.
c6 Nb6 37. Qxe5 $2 {Played rather confidently.} Nc8 38. Rd5 Bxd5 39. Qxd5 bxc6
40. Qxc6 Qxc6 41. Bxc6 Kc7 42. Bd5 f6 43. g4 Kd6 44. Be4 h6 45. Kf2 Nb6 46. Bc2
Kc5 47. h4 Kb4 48. e4 Nxa4 49. g5 Nc3 50. gxh6 gxh6 51. Ke3 Nb5 52. Kf4 Nd4 53.
Bb1 a4 54. e5 fxe5+ 55. Kxe5 Nf3+ 56. Kf4 Nxh4 57. Ba2 Ng2+ 58. Kg4 Ne1 59. Kh5
Nd3 60. Kxh6 Nc1 61. Bb1 Kc3 62. Kg5 Kb2 63. Be4 Nb3 64. Kf4 a3 {Not faultless
but very interesting and a neat endgame with N+P v B Hayes lost the match 3.5
- 4.5} 0-1

