{Time limit 30 moves in 90 mins then 5 moves per 16 mins} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6
3. c4 Bg7 4. Nc3 O-O 5. e4 d6 6. Be2 Nbd7 7. O-O e5 8. Bg5 exd4 9. Nxd4 h6 10.
Be3 Re8 11. Qc2 Nc5 12. f3 a5 13. Rad1 Nfd7 $2 {This turns out badly} ({
possibly berrer was....} 13... Be6) 14. Qc1 {[14']} Kh7 {[15']} 15. Ndb5 Bxc3 {
My position has suddenly become worse due mainly to 13.....Nd7? I played 15....
.BxN to prevent 16.Nd5} 16. Qxc3 b6 {Loses a Pawn.} 17. Qd2 h5 $4 (17... Bb7 {
was necessary.}) 18. Qd5 Qe7 {What else?......Resigns?} 19. Nxc7 Nf6 20. Qxd6 (
{Not} 20. Qxa8 $4 Bb7 21. Qa7 Qxc7 22. Z0 Ra8) 20... Ra7 21. Nxe8 Nxe8 22. Qxb6
{[24']} Rc7 {[43']} 23. Qxa5 Bb7 24. Bxc5 Rxc5 25. Qd8 Qe5 26. Rd7 Qxb2 27.
Qxe8 Qxe2 28. Qxf7+ Kh6 29. h4 {I played too quickly. 13.....Nd7 was
definitely wrong. This game was part of the 16 team Jamboree to Celebrate the
80th birthday of Sir George Thomas. Middlesex U-18 finished 14th with 3 points.
Essex came first with 7.5. Teams were drawn against different opponents over
the 10 boards.} 1-0

