{Opponent info: Grade 5b (ECF 169-1760 Time limit 24 per hour then 6 every 15} 
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O Bd6 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. d4 (7. d3 {
Might be better as the removal of Black's e-Pawn gives his KBishop more scope.}
) 7... Bg4 8. dxe5 Bxf3 ({Not...} 8... Bxe5 $2 9. Qxd8+ $1) 9. Qxf3 Bxe5 10.
Bg5 {A bit risky as Black has not yet castled.} h6 11. Rad1 $2 Bxh2+ 12. Kh1
hxg5 $5 ({Why not....} 12... Bd6) 13. Rxd8+ Rxd8 14. g3 {or else he gets a
perpetual check.} Bxg3+ 15. Kg2 Bf4 16. Rd1 {To prevent 16.....Rd7} Rh2+ 17.
Kg1 Rxd1+ 18. Qxd1 Be5 {This serves no purpose as the Bishop must continue to
defend the Rook} (18... g4 $142) 19. Qf3 g6 (19... g4 20. Qf5) 20. Ne2 g4 {
Not particularly good.} (20... Rh4 $142) 21. Qe3 Rh3 22. Qg5 Rh5 23. Qe3 Bxb2
24. c3 (24. Qb3 Rb5) 24... Ba3 25. Ng3 Re5 26. Qf4 {Taking advantage of
Black's Bishop being out of play.} Re6 27. Qxc7 Nd7 (27... Nxe4 28. Nxe4 Rxe4 {
Black's King becomes very exposed.}) 28. Qc8+ (28. Qxb7 Nc5) 28... Ke7 29. Qxb7
Rd6 30. Qxa6 Bc5 31. Qe2 Ne5 {Adjudicated Win for Black Hayes Lost the match.}
0-1

