1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bc4 g6 7. Be3 Bg7 8. f3
({More prudent is....} 8. Qd2) 8... Qb6 9. Bb5 O-O 10. Nf5 Qc7 11. Nxg7 Kxg7
12. Qd2 Kh8 13. Bxc6 bxc6 ({Not...} 13... Qxc6 {..which gives me an outpost at
d5.}) 14. O-O (14. O-O-O {is too rash.}) 14... Bb7 {Not very good. There must
be something better.} 15. Bd4 e5 {More or lesss forced but how weakening.} 16.
Bf2 Ng8 17. Rfd1 Rfd8 ({Not...} 17... Ne7 18. Bh4 {Threatening 19.Bf6+ and 20.
Qh6}) 18. Kh1 {Prevents checks from b6.} a6 19. Na4 {Threatening 20.Bb6
forcing Black's weakening reply.} c5 20. Nc3 Rab8 21. b3 {My position is
superior so I have time to play such strengthening moves.} f6 ({On....} 21...
c4 {I intended....} 22. Rac1) 22. Bh4 g5 23. Bf2 Qf7 24. Qe2 {'Observing'
Blacks a-pawn and preparing to double Rooks.} f5 25. Rd2 fxe4 26. Nxe4 Bxe4 {
Desperation.} 27. Qxe4 Qe6 28. Qc6 $1 {Wins at least a Pawn.} Qf6 29. Qxa6 $2 (
29. Rad1 $142) 29... e4 $1 {His best chance which he found despite time
trouble. Black now only had a few seconds for his next move so I decided to
not give him time to think. Unfortunately he didn't need to. I did!} 30. fxe4
$4 {?? Tragic played in a flash although I had 30 mins on my clock.} Qxa1+ 31.
Bg1 Qe5 {2 A pity. It would have been a good game. Hayes won 4 -} 0-1

