1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 O-O 5. f3 d6 6. Bd3 e5 7. d5 c6 8. Nge2
cxd5 9. cxd5 Nbd7 (9... a6 {Is the alternative.}) 10. O-O a5 11. f4 exf4 12.
Nxf4 Ne5 13. Be2 Re8 14. Nd3 Nxd3 15. Qxd3 Bg4 16. Bg5 (16. Bxg4 Nxg4 {Is good
for Black.}) 16... Qb6+ 17. Kh1 Bxe2 18. Qxe2 Nd7 ({I considered....} 18...
Nxe4 19. Nxe4 f5 {Followed by 20......Qd4 but White plays} 20. Rad1 {then 21.
Rf4. This might have been a better line due to his weak b-Pawn.}) 19. Qd2 Rac8
20. Rf3 Bxc3 $2 21. Rxc3 Ne5 ({Not} 21... Rxc3 22. Qxc3 Rxe4 $2 23. Qc8+ Nf8
24. Bh6) 22. Bf6 {Threatens 23.Qh6} Ng4 23. Bd4 Qb5 24. Rb3 {[59' 45s]} Qd7 {
[58']} 25. h3 a4 26. Rc3 Rxc3 27. Bxc3 Ne5 28. Rf1 {[1hr 11'] Adjourned. Play
resumed 19/2/62} Kg7 {[sealed move]} 29. Qf4 Kg8 ({Not} 29... Qe7 30. Bxe5+ {
and White gets a passed Pawn.}) 30. Qf6 Re7 $4 {This loses outright.} 31. Bd2
Ng4 32. hxg4 Qxg4 33. Qxe7 f5 34. Bc3 Qh4+ $6 {Alast hope WHite might have
played 35.Kg1 without thinking.} 35. Qxh4 {I came 3rd in the Championship
behind B.Gillman and M.Stapley (!!)} 1-0

