{Time limit 24 per hour then 6 every 15} 1. d4 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nc3 e6 4. g3 Bb4
5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 O-O 7. Bg2 c6 {This move lessens the scope of thw White
KBishop, prepares for a possible ....d5 and gives my Queen more scope.} 8. Nf3
d6 {Prepares for .....e5.} (8... d5 {leaves a hole on e5 and I would find it
difficult to play ....e5.}) 9. O-O Nbd7 10. Bf4 {Falling in with my plans this
Bishop must move when I play ....e5.} Qe7 11. Qc2 {[34']} ({Why not} 11. Qd3)
11... e5 {[13'] Siezing the innitiative.} 12. Bg5 h6 {This leaves a not so
serious hole on g6.} 13. Bc1 e4 14. Nh4 Qe6 15. Bh3 {[45']} (15. Ng6 {followed
by...} Z0 16. Nf4 {...is not very good for White.}) 15... Ng4 {[19'] Freeing
my position.} 16. f3 g5 ({If...} 16... exf3 17. exf3 Ngf6 18. Bxf5 Qxc4 {
is not so good for Black.}) 17. fxg4 fxg4 ({Not as good is...} 17... gxh4 {
which leaves many weaknesses}) 18. Rxf8+ Nxf8 19. Bg2 gxh4 20. Bxe4 hxg3 21.
hxg3 h5 {To free the Queen.} 22. Bg5 {Very aggressive but not worth a Pawn.}
Qxc4 23. Bh7+ $6 (23. Rf1 Be6 {merely leaves him a Pawn down.}) 23... Nxh7 24.
Qg6+ Kh8 25. Bf6+ (25. Rf1 {Is not any better.}) 25... Nxf6 26. Qxf6+ Kh7 27.
Qe7+ Kg6 28. Qxd6+ Qe6 29. Qf4 {[70']} Bd7 {[39']} (29... Qxe2 {is not
necessary}) 30. Rf1 Re8 31. e4 Re7 32. e5 Rf7 33. Qe4+ Kg7 34. Re1 Rf3 35. Re3
Qf5 {Quite interesting.} 0-1

