{Opponent Info: Haberdashers' Aske's Sch, Elstree. Time limit 36 moves in 90m
then 24 moves in 60m} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6.
Be3 e5 {The Boleslavsky system} 7. Nb3 Be7 8. Be2 O-O 9. O-O a5 {This leaves a
hole on b5.} 10. f4 a4 {This proves to be a weakness.} 11. Nd2 Nd4 {Doubtful.}
12. Nc4 Nxe2+ 13. Qxe2 Qc7 14. Nb6 Ra6 {[15']} 15. Ncd5 {[21'] A strong move.}
(15. Nbxa4 {Does not win a Pawn because of.....} Bd7 16. b3 Bxa4 17. Nxa4 Nxe4)
15... Nxd5 16. Nxd5 Qd8 17. fxe5 dxe5 18. Rad1 Bd6 {About the only move.} 19.
Kh1 {So as to play Bc5} Be6 20. Nb4 Ra8 $2 ({Essential is....} 20... Ra5) 21.
Bc5 Bxc5 {The only chance.} 22. Rxd8 Rfxd8 23. a3 (23. Nd3 {Is playable.})
23... Bxb4 24. axb4 Rd4 {Threatening the b-Pawn and 25......Bc4} 25. Qb5 $1 {
Crushing.} Bc4 26. Qxb7 Rad8 27. Rg1 Rd1 {This loses immediately.} 28. Qc6
Rxg1+ 29. Kxg1 Rd1+ 30. Kf2 Rd2+ 31. Kg3 {Very streightforward. D.M.Bindefeld
came 37= with 4pts.} 1-0

