{Opponent info: Wimbledon Coll S.W.14; Middlesex U/18 Bd1. Time control 36
moves in 90m then 24 moves in 60m.} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6
5. d4 exd4 6. Qxd4 Qxd4 7. Nxd4 Ne7 (7... Nf6 {Looks better.}) 8. Be3 Ng6 9.
O-O Bd7 10. f4 O-O-O 11. Nc3 Bc5 12. Nf5 {Played after much thought.} ({If...} 
12. Nce2 $2 {Then....} Bg4 {wins a piece.}) 12... Bxe3+ 13. Nxe3 Rhe8 14. Rad1
{[30']} c5 {[23']} 15. g3 {My f-Pawn needed more protection to give my KRokk
more scope.} Bc6 16. Rxd8+ Rxd8 17. Rd1 Rd4 18. e5 ({Not...} 18. Rxd4 $4 cxd4)
18... Ne7 19. Kf2 b5 20. Ne2 {Forcing the Rooks off.} Rxd1 21. Nxd1 Nd5 22.
Nec3 Nxc3 (22... Nb4 {gets nowhere after...} 23. Ne3) 23. Nxc3 b4 24. Nd1 (24.
Ne2 {The Knight is stuck.}) 24... Bd5 25. b3 {Slightly risky.} ({so is..} 25.
a3) 25... c4 {[54']} 26. Ne3 {[55']} cxb3 27. axb3 ({Not} 27. cxb3 {When Black
moves his a-Pawn to a4}) 27... Be4 28. Ke2 Kd7 29. Kd2 Kc6 30. g4 {Some
counter reaction on the KS was required.} Kd7 {Black doesn't seem quite sure
of the best thing to do.} 31. Nf5 g6 32. Ng3 ({If} 32. Nd4 c5) 32... Bd5 {[72']
} 33. Kd3 {[75']} c5 {[85']} 34. Nf1 {[76']} a5 35. Ne3 Bb7 36. c4 ({Not...} 
36. Kc4 Kc6 {Threatens mate.}) (36. Nc4 Ba6 {is good.}) 36... Ke6 37. h4 Bf3
38. g5 {Blocking the KS for good.} Bc6 39. Kc2 a4 {This Black's only chance of
a win} 40. bxa4 Bxa4+ 41. Kb2 {Black's only chance of a win now lies in
sacrificing his Bishop for mt c-Pawn} Bd7 42. Kb3 Bc6 43. Kc2 Be4+ 44. Kb2 Bd3
45. Kb3 Be2 {Black must sacrifice when my King is at a2, b2 ,c2 so that I must
recapture with the Knight then his King has access to my Pawns.} 46. Kb2 Bxc4
47. Nxc4 Kf5 48. Nd6+ Kxf4 49. Nxf7 Kf5 (49... Kg4 $4 50. e6) 50. Kb3 {I must
fix his c-Pawn on c5 so as to be able to capture with the Knight} Ke6 51. Nd8+
Kxe5 52. Kc4 {Preventing 52.....Kd5 or d4} Kf5 53. Nb7 Kg4 54. Nxc5 Kxh4 55.
Ne4 $1 ({Not} 55. Kxb4 Kxg5) 55... Kg4 56. Kxb4 Kf5 57. Nf6 h5 (57... Kxg5 58.
Nxh7+ $11) 58. gxh6 {Forced.} Kxf6 59. Kc4 g5 60. h7 $1 {By pushing my Pawn to
h8 I gain two moves.} Kg7 61. h8=Q+ Kxh8 62. Kd4 Kg7 63. Ke4 Kg6 64. Kf3 Kf5
65. Kg3 g4 66. Kg2 Kf4 67. Kf2 g3+ 68. Kg2 Kg4 69. Kg1 Kh3 70. Kh1 {P.N.Lee
won the Championship with 8.5 pts. He drew with A.S.Hollis at the Sir George
Thomas Jamboree in 1961. He won the British Championship in 1965} 1/2-1/2

