{Time control 36 moves in 90m then 24 moves in 60m.} 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. g3
b6 4. Bg2 Bb7 5. Nc3 Bb4 6. O-O O-O 7. d3 Bxc3 8. bxc3 d6 9. Qc2 Nbd7 10. a4 a5
{I intended building up a KS attack so I blocked the QS.} 11. Ba3 Nh5 {To play
.....f5.} 12. Nd4 {Doubtful.} Bxg2 13. Kxg2 e5 14. Nb5 f5 15. Rfd1 {White
seems quite unconcerened about my KS manoeuvres} Ndf6 16. d4 e4 17. c5 {
Complicating matters.} bxc5 ({Not} 17... dxc5 $2 18. dxc5 $1) 18. dxc5 d5 19.
c6 Rf7 20. c4 Ng4 {I am probably going to lose the d-Pawn so I thought I might
as well play for an attack 20.....Ng4 also vacates f6 for the Queen.} 21. Rxd5
(21. cxd5 $142) 21... Qf6 22. e3 $4 {White completely overlooks the QRook.} ({
Correct was} 22. Rad1 {when I can't take the c-Pawn....} Qxc6 {because of.} 23.
Rd8+ Rxd8 24. Rxd8+ Rf8 (24... Qe8 25. Rxe8+ Rf8 26. Rxf8#) 25. Rxf8#) 22...
Qxa1 23. h3 ({A better idea was} 23. Bb2 Qa2 24. Rd4 {with the threat of 25.
Nc3 but I save myself with.....} Rb8) 23... Qf6 $2 {I was worried about the
safety of my Queen.} ({Correct is....} 23... Nxe3+) (23... Nh6 {Would also win
but it would be very tedious with my Queen stuck.}) 24. Bb2 $4 {Now he is
slaughtered.} ({Correct is....} 24. hxg4) 24... Nxe3+ 25. fxe3 Qxc6 26. Nd4 Qg6
27. Qf2 f4 $1 28. g4 fxe3 29. Qxe3 Nf4+ 30. Kh2 Nxd5 31. cxd5 Qd6+ 32. Kg2 Qxd5
33. Nf5 Rd8 34. Nd4 c5 35. Nb3 Rf3 {This game was revenge for my game against
H.P.Brown in the Middlesex Championship 18 months ago. H.P.Brown came 37th=
with 4.5 pts.} 0-1

