{Time control 36 moves in 90m then 24 moves in 60m.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 Be7 8. Qf3 Qc7 9. O-O-O Nc6 10. Nb3
Bd7 11. g4 Rc8 12. Kb1 b5 $6 13. Bxf6 Bxf6 14. Bxb5 $1 Bxc3 ({Not....} 14...
axb5 $2 15. Nxb5 Qd8 (15... Qb8 16. Nxd6+ Kf8 (16... Ke7 17. Nxc8+) 17. Nxc8)
16. Nxd6+ Kf8 (16... Ke7 17. Nxc8+) 17. Nxc8) 15. Qxc3 ({The alternative} 15.
Bxc6 Bxc6 16. Qxc3 Bxe4 17. Qxc7 Rxc7 18. Rd2 Ke7 {is not to White's advantage.
}) 15... axb5 16. Qxg7 {[11']} Rf8 ({The alternative is...} 16... Ke7 17. Qg5+
Kf8 18. Qxb5 Nb4 19. Qe2 Qxc2+ 20. Qxc2 Nxc2 21. Rxd6) 17. Qxh7 Ne7 18. c3 e5
$1 {A good move preventing me opening the e-file. It also lets Black play .....
Be6} 19. f5 Qc4 20. Rhe1 Bc6 21. f6 {Doubtful.} (21. Nd2 $142) 21... Ng6 22.
Nd2 Qe6 23. Qh3 (23. h3 $4 {Black threatened......} Rh8 24. Qg7 Kd7 25. Z0 Rcg8
) 23... Bd7 (23... Qxf6 {Offered Black better chances.}) 24. Qd3 Nf4 25. Qf1
Qxg4 26. Nf3 {[35']} Qe6 {[34']} 27. Ng5 Qg4 ({Not..} 27... Qxf6 28. Nh7) 28.
Rxd6 $3 {Anything else loses.} Qxg5 29. Rxd7 $1 {This obtains at least a draw.}
Qxf6 $2 {Black miscalculates and loses.} (29... Kxd7 {would have drawn.}) 30.
Qxb5 {Crushing.} Qc6 31. Qxe5+ Ne6 ({Not.....} 31... Kxd7 $2 32. Rd1+ $1) 32.
Rd6 ({Not} 32. Red1 $2 Qxd7 {With good chances.}) 32... Qc4 33. Red1 Rg8 34. b3
$3 {This seals the win.} Rb8 {A useless attempt for survival.} ({If..} 34...
Qxc3 {White mates in 5 by....} 35. Rxe6+) 35. Rxe6+ Qxe6 36. Qxb8+ Ke7 37. Qxg8
Qxe4+ 38. Kc1 Qe3+ 39. Rd2 Qxc3+ 40. Kd1 Qf3+ (40... Qa1+ {Lasts longer.}) 41.
Re2+ Kd7 42. Qg2 Qd3+ 43. Rd2 {A remarkable sacrificial game! One of the best
sacrificial games I have played. J.A.S.Rokos came 11th= with 6.5pts This game
won Black a Best Game Prize (£1''10''0) [About £19]} 1-0

