{Opponent info: Bd4 for Surrey} 1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. d4 d6 4. c4 Nb6 5. f4
dxe5 6. fxe5 Nc6 7. Be3 Bf5 8. Nc3 e6 9. Nf3 Qd7 {[1']} 10. Be2 O-O-O 11. O-O {
All fairly standard procedure but this was the first time I had played against
Alekhines Defence and I didn't know the correct variation so I had to work
everything out. After the game I was surprised to find out that I had played
the "Book" moves as far as move 11.} Bg4 {Now I was in trouble Black threatens
12.....BxN followed by 13.....NxP} 12. d5 $5 {As it turns out this was the
wrong move but it is very complicated. In the time at my disposal I could find
no other way of saving the pawn. However according to M.C.O. the correct moves
are:} (12. a4) (12. c5 $1 Nd5 13. Nxd5 Qxd5 14. Ng5 $1) 12... exd5 13. Bxb6
axb6 14. cxd5 Bxf3 15. dxc6 {This loses but would not have done so against a
lesser player.} Bc5+ {A useful intermediate move.} 16. Kh1 Bxg2+ $3 {Anything
else would give away his advantage.} (16... Bxc6 $4 17. Bg4) (16... Qxd1 17.
cxb7+) 17. Kxg2 Qxc6+ 18. Bf3 Qg6+ {More forcing than 18.....RxQ} 19. Bg4+ Kb8
20. Qf3 h5 {[21']} 21. Rad1 {[45']} hxg4 22. Qxf7 $2 (22. Rxd8+ {Lasts longer.}
) 22... Qc2+ 23. Kg3 (23. Kh1 Qxh2#) 23... Qxh2+ 24. Kxg4 Qh3+ 25. Kg5 Be3+ 26.
Kg6 Qg4# {4 A very interesting game. The match ended 4 -} 0-1

