1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. Bc4 Bg7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. h3 {Prevents 6......Bg4
or Ng4 which Black would play after 6.Be3} Nxe4 {Attempting to gain equality
by this exchange but his KS is weakened.} 7. Bxf7+ (7. Nxe4 d5 {is not as good.
}) 7... Rxf7 8. Nxe4 e5 {Trying to take advantage of the fact that my King is
still in the centre but it doesn't turn out too well for Black.} 9. dxe5 Qe8
10. O-O dxe5 11. Qe2 {Played after much thought. Black was threatening to gain
a tempo by 11....Rd7.11.Qe2 also 'observes' the e-Pawn and threatens to place
the Queen on the a2-g8 diagonal where Black is very weak.} Be6 $2 {Not the
best as he soon finds.} 12. Neg5 Re7 (12... Rd7 13. Nxe5) 13. Nxe6 Rxe6 14. Qc4
{Wins a pawn.} Kh8 15. Qxc7 Nc6 16. Qxb7 ({Not..} 16. Rd1 $2 Re7 17. Qd6 Rd8)
16... Rb8 17. Qa6 Nd4 {The best chance.} 18. Qxa7 (18. Qa3 $2 Nxc2) 18... Nxf3+
19. gxf3 Reb6 20. Qa3 ({possibly better was....} 20. c3) 20... Qc8 21. Qa4 Rb4
({Not} 21... Qxh3 22. Qg4 {With an easy win.}) 22. Qa7 Qxh3 23. c3 {Preventing
23.....Ra4 but allowing Black to draw by Rg4+} R4b6 {Black does not want a
draw. This prevents 24.Qe3} 24. Qa4 Qxf3 {We were both short of time now.} 25.
Qd1 Qh3 26. Re1 Qf5 27. Qe2 g5 28. Qe4 {28 My 13th Queen move out of} Qf7 29.
b3 Rf8 30. Be3 Rh6 {Adjudicated Drawn hayes won the match 4.5 - 3.5} 1/2-1/2

