1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 g6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. d3 O-O 6. Nf3 d6 7. O-O c6 8. Qc2
Nbd7 9. b4 {[2'] I felt in a winning mood in this game so I decided to play
aggressively} Nb6 {[11'] This Knight is rather at a dead end on b6} 10. Bb2 {
[2' 30s]} Bf5 {The Bishop is devoid of all prospects on f5.} 11. a4 {[5']} a5 {
[24']} 12. b5 {[7']} Nfd7 (12... cxb5 13. Nxb5 {Is strong for White.}) 13. Nh4
{Threatening to weaken Black's KS and also to win the c-Pawn} Rc8 14. Nxf5 gxf5
{This Pawn is very weak.} 15. Qd2 {This 'observes' the a-Pawn but loses a
tempo.} (15. f4 $142) 15... Nc5 16. Qc2 Nbd7 17. f4 $1 {This prepares the
decisive KS attack.} Ne6 18. e3 exf4 19. gxf4 (19. exf4 {would be wrong.})
19... Kh8 20. d4 $1 {Strenghtening the centre and attacking the f-Pawn.} Qf6
21. Bh3 {Winning at least a Pawn. Black was now very short of time.} Nxd4 22.
exd4 Qxd4+ 23. Kh1 Qxc4 24. Bxf5 {[30']} Rfd8 {Played with only a few seconds
to spare.} 25. Rf3 {Protecting the Knight in view of .....cxb and threatening
to go to h3} Rc7 26. Rg1 {Threatening 27.RxB!!} Nf6 27. Bxh7 Qe6 (27... Nxh7
28. Rxg7) 28. Qg2 Ne8 29. Nd5 {33 A very good attack which showed Black
getting tied up on the QS, then being unable to get his pieces to the KS in
time. Championship score (1st 30 bds) Middlesex 14.5 - Surrey 15.5 Total score
(60bds) Middlesex 27 - Surrey} 1-0

