{Time limit 24 per hour then 6 every} 1. d4 f5 2. e4 fxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f3 exf3
5. Nxf3 e6 6. Bd3 Be7 {I had never played against the Staunton Gambit (4.f3)
before and I played the opening in a too cramping fashion.} 7. O-O O-O 8. Qe2
b6 {This leads to all sorts of trouble as Black's position is much weaker than
I realised.} 9. d5 $1 Bc5+ 10. Kh1 exd5 $2 {Much too greedy.} 11. Nxd5 $1 {
Suddenly my position collapses. I can't find any satisfactory reply for Black.}
Nxd5 $6 12. Qe4 Nf6 13. Qxa8 Nc6 {If now I can now move my Queen I threaten ...
Ba6....if!} 14. Bb5 Ng4 15. Bg5 Qe8 16. Bh4 Qe4 {Threatens 17....Ba6} (16...
Qh5 {is no better.}) 17. Ng5 Qe5 (17... Qe8 {too passive.}) 18. Bc4+ d5 19.
Rxf8+ Bxf8 20. Bxd5+ Be6 {As good as resignation.} (20... Qxd5 21. Qxc8) 21.
Bxe6+ {Rather a wild game. Hayes lost the match 3.5 - 4.5} 1-0

