1. d4 f5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. g3 e6 4. Bg2 c6 5. c4 Bb4+ 6. Bd2 Bxd2+ 7. Nbxd2 (7.
Qxd2 {Is probably better as the QKnight is better on c3.}) 7... O-O 8. O-O d6
9. Qc2 {This doesn't serve much purpose.} Nbd7 10. e4 f4 (10... fxe4 11. Nxe4
Nxe4 12. Qxe4 Nf6 {Leads to a rather lifeless position.}) 11. Ng5 {Threatening
12.e5 & 12.NxeP} (11. gxf4 {leaves him too weak on the KS.}) 11... Qe7 12. Bh3
e5 13. d5 ({If...} 13. Ne6 Nb6) 13... cxd5 {If I let White exchange my d-Pawn
is left too weak.} 14. cxd5 Nc5 15. Bg2 {The Bishop doesn't have much scope on
g2.} h6 16. Ngf3 g5 17. b4 Na6 18. a3 Bd7 19. Qb2 Kh7 ({If...} 19... g4 {
threatening 20......f5 then....} 20. Nh4) 20. Kh1 $2 {Overlooking the threat.}
g4 21. Nh4 f3 22. Nhxf3 gxf3 23. Bxf3 Ng4 24. Kg1 Qg5 25. Bxg4 Bxg4 26. Nb3 Bf3
{41.05/0 Championship: Essex 11 - Middlesex 8 (1bd to be adj) Amboyna: Essex
26.5 - Middlesex 22.5 Ebony: Essex 37.5 - Middlesex} 0-1

