1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 cxd4 6. cxd4 f6 {Black would do
better to develop some pieces.} 7. Bb5 Bd7 8. Nc3 Qc7 {This is not very good
as I play Bf4 next and can play Rc1 later on.} (8... Qb6 $142) 9. Bf4 fxe5 $2 {
This loses at least a pawn.} 10. Bxc6 exf4 11. Bxd7+ Qxd7 (11... Kxd7 12. Ne5+
{is even worse for Black.}) 12. Ne5 Qe7 13. Qh5+ g6 14. Nxg6 hxg6 $2 (14... Qf7
15. Nxf4 {is better for Black.}) 15. Qxh8 Qg7 {This is the equivalent of a
resignation.} 16. Qxg7 Bxg7 17. Nb5 Kd7 18. Rc1 Ne7 19. Rc7+ Ke8 (19... Kd8 {
Was better but Black was beyond caring at this stage.}) 20. Rxb7 Rc8 $4 {
Black didn't bother to think about this.} 21. Nd6+ Kd8 22. Nxc8 Kxc8 23. Rxe7
1-0

