1. d4 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nc3 e6 4. a3 {It was not worth wasting a move to prevent
4.....Bb4} Be7 5. g3 c6 6. Bg2 d5 7. c5 {This releases the tension in the
centre and eases Black's game.} Nbd7 {My intention is to force....e5} 8. Nf3
O-O 9. O-O Nh5 {With this move I had in mind the moves .....g5 & .....f5 with
a KS attack or ....Bf6 & ....e5} 10. e3 Qe8 {Defending the Knight and adding
support for the e-Pawn.} 11. b4 Bf6 12. Bb2 e5 13. dxe5 Nxe5 14. Qd2 {wastes a
tempo.} Nc4 15. Qc2 g6 {Intending to get the Knight back into play via g6 & e6}
16. Nd4 $4 {Overlooking Black's reply.} Nxe3 17. fxe3 Qxe3+ 18. Kh1 Qxd4 19.
Rad1 Qe5 20. Rfe1 Qc7 (20... Nxg3+ {Is flashy & nothing else.}) 21. Qf2 Bxc3 $1
{I wanted to bring my QRook into the game so I must move my QBishop.} (21...
Bd7 {cuts off the Queen so I must defend e6.}) ({If...} 21... Qf7 22. Nxd5 $1)
({If...} 21... Ng7 22. Bxd5+ $1) 22. Bxc3 Qf7 23. Re2 Bd7 ({If...} 23... Be6
24. Rde1 Rae8 25. Qd4 Ng7 (25... Nf6 26. Qxf6 {is good for Black.}) 26. Rxe6 $1
{wins.}) 24. Rde1 Rae8 25. Qd4 Ng7 26. Rxe8 Rxe8 27. Rxe8+ Bxe8 28. Qe5 a6 29.
Bf1 Bd7 30. Bd3 Be6 {Time was called but White resigned. (we had a bye in the
zonal semi-final) HCGS won the match3.5 - 2.5} 0-1

