1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. d4 Bg7 4. e3 O-O 5. Nf3 d6 6. Be2 Nbd7 7. O-O e5 8. dxe5
Nxe5 9. Nxe5 dxe5 10. Qc2 {White can hardly claim to have gained any advantage
from the opening.} c6 11. e4 Be6 12. Be3 {[14']} Qc7 {[5']} 13. f3 {[19']} Rfd8
14. Rfd1 b6 {An exchange of Rooks would leave my a-Pawn en-prise although
White probably wouldn't be able to take it streight away. However this move is
somewhat weakening as my minor pieces are not too strong on the QS.} 15. b3 {
[23']} Ne8 {Trying for some counterplay with ...Nd6 and .....f5} 16. Rd2 Rxd2
17. Qxd2 Rd8 {Black really isn't making much progress considering the number
of pointless moves which White is making.} 18. Qc2 Nd6 19. c5 Ne8 20. cxb6 axb6
21. Na4 c5 {This was forced much as I dislike giving up d5 for his Knight.} 22.
Rc1 Qb7 23. Rd1 {I offered a draw here.} Rxd1+ 24. Qxd1 Qb8 {Here he offered a
draw which I accepted. Here my opponent (who, on all known form, I should have
beaten without great difficulty) was determined to draw and made no attempt to
win (e.g.moves 8, 9 ,13 ,15 show this.) Possibly I should have played a more
aggresive opening. Hayes won the match 4.5 - 3.5} 1/2-1/2

