1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 Nbd7 {
This is the first time I have met this move. As usual I play this opening
inaccurately.} 8. Qf3 Be7 9. Bc4 {Taking advantage of the fact that Black has
not played ....Qc7 , to put the Bishop on a good diagonal.} Nc5 {Defending the
e-Pawn which was threatened by the Bishop in some variations.} 10. O-O-O ({
I considered...} 10. b4 Ncd7 11. Bxe6 fxe6 12. Nxe6 Qb6 13. Nxg7+ Kf7 14. Nf5 {
but couldn't see enough possibilities to justify this risk.}) 10... Qc7 {
Threatens 11.....Nxe4} 11. Bb3 b5 12. a3 (12. e5 Bb7 13. Qg3 {was an
alternative I considered.}) 12... Bb7 {I haven't played the opening too well
and Black has equalised.} 13. Bxf6 Nxb3+ 14. Nxb3 Bxf6 15. Nd4 Rc8 16. Qd3 Qc4
(16... Z0 {Threatening.....} 17. Ndxb5 axb5 18. Nxb5 Qc6 19. Nxd6+ Kf8 20. Nxc8
) 17. f5 {setting Black some problems.} Qxd3 (17... exf5 18. Qxc4) (17... e5 {
The Bishop is useless.}) 18. Rxd3 Ke7 ({Not...} 18... exf5 19. Nxf5 Bxc3 20.
Nxd6+) 19. Re1 $2 {Inaccurate now I get into trouble.} Rc4 20. Nf3 {About best
in the circumstances.} Bxc3 21. Rxc3 Rxc3 22. bxc3 Rc8 23. Nd2 {The Pawn is
too weak to bother about defending.} Rxc3 24. Kb2 Rc7 25. Re3 Kf8 26. fxe6 fxe6
27. Nf3 {My object is to exchange off as many Pawns as possible and to get my
Rook into active play and also to post my Knight effectively.} h6 28. c3 Rf7
29. Re2 Ke7 30. Kc2 {Centralising my King to get the Rook into play.} Rf4 31.
Kd3 e5 {I don't know whether this is good or bad. It prevents 32.Nd4 but I
didn't intend this anyway. It defends the Rook after Ke3 but g5 does that as
well. However it leaves the d-Pawn backward.} (31... g5) 32. Nd2 Bc8 33. Ke3
Be6 34. Re1 g5 {[75']} 35. Ra1 {[59'] Threatening to get good play for my Rook
after exchanges on the QS.} Bd7 {Trying to prevent a QS breakthrough.} 36. c4 {
Opening lines to get my Rook into playand also trying to exchange all QS Pawns.
} Rf8 37. cxb5 axb5 {Looks better than taking with the Bishop but this may not
be so.} (37... Bxb5) 38. Rb1 ({If...} 38. Nb1 {..intending 39.Nc3 then....} Rc8
$1) 38... Ra8 ({If now...} 38... Rc8 {then...} 39. Kd3 {and Black still can't
get through.}) 39. Rb3 Ra4 40. Nb1 Bc6 41. Nc3 Rc4 42. Kd3 Rc5 {Black is
getting quite tied up.} 43. g3 Ke6 44. Rb4 {Adjourned. During the adjournment
I decided that I might just be able to draw. Black has an extra Pawn but it is
backward and he will have trouble keeping his b-Pawn defended. Also White's
position is very solid and Black will have trouble in breaking through. I
intended merely manoeuvering on the b-file with my Rook keeping the second
rank defended when necessary if Black did nothing in particular.} Kd7 {[Sealed
move] Play resumed 11\5\62.} 45. Rb2 Ke6 {Blackdecided his sealed move was
wrong.} 46. Rb4 g4 47. Rb2 d5 {Removing his backward Pawn and increasing the
scope of his Bishop.} 48. exd5+ Bxd5 49. Nxd5 {Black's Bishop was better than
my Knight and in any case I wanted to prevent ......Bc4+} Kxd5 50. Rb4 {
I wanted to exchange the a-Pawn and play h3 & Re4} h5 51. a4 bxa4 52. Rxa4 e4+
{Giving up any hopes of winning.} 53. Ke3 (53. Rxe4 $4 Rc3+ $19) 53... Rc2 (
53... Rc3+ 54. Kd2 {Was no better.}) 54. Rxe4 Rxh2 55. Re8 {Now Black's King
stays completely out of play.} Rh3 56. Kf4 Kd4 57. Kg5 Kd3 58. Kf4 Kd2 59. Re7
Rh2 60. Kg5 Re2 $4 {Losing.} 61. Rxe2+ Kxe2 62. Kxh5 Kf3 63. Kh4 Ke4 64. Kxg4
Ke5 65. Kg5 Ke6 66. Kg6 Ke7 67. Kg7 Ke6 68. g4 Ke5 69. g5 Ke6 70. Kh7 {Never
say die!} 1-0

