{Opponent info: N.Counties U-18 Champion; England U-18 Bd3 1962 Glorney Cup} 1.
e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bc4 Qc7 7. Bb3 e6 8. O-O
Be7 9. a4 O-O 10. Be3 Nc6 11. f4 b6 12. Qe1 Bb7 13. Qg3 ({Not} 13. Bxe6 $4 {
intending...} fxe6 ({because of...} 13... Nxd4 $1) 14. Nxe6) 13... Rfe8 {
The thought of White playing 14.f5 15Bh6 didn't appeal to me so I decided to
rearrange my pieces so as to strengthen g7.} 14. Rad1 Bf8 15. Qf3 {Now that my
g-Pawn was defended his e-Pawn was threatened. However his Queen is not well
placed on the same diagonal as my QBishop.} g6 16. g4 Bg7 17. g5 {This doesn't
cause Black much trouble.} Nd7 18. Rd2 Nc5 19. Nxc6 (19. Ba2 {Must have come
into consideration.}) 19... Bxc6 20. Bd4 Nxb3 21. cxb3 b5 {HCGS lost the match
2.5 - 3.5 Liverpool won the competition.} 1/2-1/2

