1. d4 d5 2. Nd2 {He always plays this.} Nf6 3. e3 Bf5 4. Bd3 Bg6 5. Ngf3 e6 6.
Bxg6 {This is bad as the h-file is opened for Black.} hxg6 7. c4 c6 8. Qc2 Nbd7
9. c5 {Doubtful.} Qc7 10. e4 {This too is wrong, for White's position is too
weak for the centre to be opened.} e5 11. b4 {Exchanging in the centre merely
improves Black's position.} O-O-O {Increasing the pressure.} 12. Bb2 exd4 13.
Bxd4 (13. Nxd4 Rxh2) 13... Qf4 14. g3 {The weaknesses on g2 & h3 make White's
task impossible now.} Qg4 15. Bxf6 gxf6 {prevents e5 or Ne5 later on.} (15...
Nxf6 {my Kbishop is useless}) 16. O-O {Suicidal.} (16. O-O-O $142) (16. exd5
Re8+) 16... Bh6 17. Rfd1 {Now White is completely lost.} Rde8 {Winning a pawn
with a teriffic attack.} 18. Qd3 (18. exd5 Re2) 18... Bxd2 19. Nxd2 Qh3 20. Nf1
Rxe4 21. f3 Ne5 22. Qa3 Re2 23. Rd2 Qg2# 0-1

