1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e4 {This seems wrong for it loses
two tempi.} dxe4 6. Nxe4 Bb4+ 7. Nc3 c6 8. Bd3 Qa5 9. Qd2 Bxc3 10. bxc3 (10.
Qxc3 $4 Qxg5) 10... e5 {Seizing the innitiative.} 11. Bxf6 {Now Black's pieces
can be developed more easily.} (11. dxe5 {is obviously not very good.}) 11...
Nxf6 12. c5 {This lessens the scope of my Queen but gives d5 for my Knight and
the e6-a2 diagonal for my Bishop.} e4 {That this Pawn may become weak did not
worry me for it cramps White even more.} 13. Bc2 O-O 14. Ne2 Bg4 {Threatens 15.
....BxN where White must reply 16.KxB. The Bishop attacks e2 & d1 which may
have nuisance value.} 15. Ng3 Rad8 {The e-Pawn is immune at the moment.} 16.
O-O Qxc5 17. Bxe4 Rfe8 18. Rae1 (18. Rfe1 {Was surely better.}) (18. Bxh7+ {
intending.....} Kxh7 $4 ({Loses to...} 18... Nxh7) 19. Qc2+ Kg8 20. dxc5) 18...
Qd6 {I thought this squre was better than a5 as the Queen is centralised.} (
18... Qa5) 19. Qd3 g6 {Considerably lessening the scope of Whites pieces.} 20.
h3 Be6 21. Re2 $4 {Defending the a-Pawn which was immune anyway.} b5 22. Bf3
Bc4 23. Rxe8+ Rxe8 24. Qd2 Bxf1 25. Kxf1 Qe6 26. Kg1 {There seems no reason
for allowing the Queen exchange.} Qe1+ 27. Qxe1 Rxe1+ 28. Kh2 Nd5 29. Ne2 g5 {
Prevents Nf4 after BxN} 30. g4 Ra1 31. Ng3 Rxa2 32. Ne4 a5 33. Nxg5 Rxf2+ 34.
Kg3 Rxf3+ {making things unnecessarily difficult.} 35. Nxf3 a4 36. Ne1 a3 37.
Nc2 a2 (37... Nxc3 $142) 38. Na1 Nxc3 39. Kf3 b4 40. Ke3 Kg7 41. Kd3 Kf6 42.
Kc4 Nd5 43. Kc5 Ke6 44. Kxc6 b3 45. Kc5 (45. Nxb3 Nb4+ 46. Kc5 Nc2 47. Kc6 Ke7
$3 48. Kc7 Nxd4 $3) 45... b2 0-1

