1. c4 c6 {Hoping to transpose into a Slav defence.} 2. g3 d5 3. cxd5 cxd5 4.
Bg2 Nf6 5. d4 Nc6 6. Nf3 e6 (6... Bf5 {seems better after 6.....e6 his QBishop
remains shut in.}) 7. O-O Be7 8. Nc3 O-O 9. Bf4 Nh5 10. a3 {Strengthening the
QS.} Nxf4 {I was not worried about this.} 11. gxf4 {My doubled Pawn isn't weak
it controls e5 and also allows a possible attack along the g-file.} f5 {
Doubtful. This leaves an even bigger hole on e5.} 12. Ne5 Nxe5 13. fxe5 Bd7 (
13... f4 {gaining some spave was playable, but then White would always have
the chance of playing e4.}) 14. b4 ({I intended to sacrifice by...} 14. Nxd5
exd5 15. Bxd5+ Kh8 16. Bxb7 {When my central Pawns are rather strong, but after
} Rb8 {I lose my b-Pawn.}) 14... Be8 {Protects the d-Pawn.} 15. f4 g5 {Black
suddenly becomes energetic.} 16. e3 g4 17. Qb3 {Again threatening 18.Nxd5} Kh8
18. Rac1 {I considered sacrificing the Knight for two Pawns but decided it was
not worth taking the risk as I had the somewhat better position anyway.} h5 19.
Nxd5 $1 {Now I get three Pawns for the piece and a vastly superior position as
well.} exd5 20. Qxd5 Qxd5 21. Bxd5 Bc6 (21... Rb8 22. Rc7 {is no better.}) 22.
Bxc6 bxc6 23. Rxc6 Rac8 24. Rfc1 Rxc6 25. Rxc6 h4 {The only chance.} 26. Rc7
Bd8 27. Rxa7 h3 28. e6 (28. Ra8 {Might be quicker.}) 28... Bh4 29. d5 $4 {
A terrible blunder due to playing without due thought as the game seemed
completely lost for Black. I realised immediately that I had gone wrong.} Rc8
30. Kf1 Rc1+ $4 {Missing his opportunity.} ({Correct was.....} 30... g3 31.
hxg3 h2 $1 32. Kg2 Rc2+ $3 33. Kh1 Bxg3 34. Z0 Rc1+ {is unstopable.}) 31. Ke2
Rc2+ (31... g3 32. d6) 32. Kd3 Rxh2 33. d6 Rd2+ {Gains a move but to no avail.}
34. Kxd2 h2 35. e7 Bxe7 ({he could have tried...} 35... Be1+ {so as to Queen
with check after I take the Bishop with a Possible perpetual check}) 36. dxe7
1-0

