1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. dxc5 ({Better was..} 6. Qg4
{now his QS Pawns are mashed.}) 6... Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 Qc7 8. Bb5+ {This is not
particularly brilliant either.} Bd7 9. Bxd7+ {Thus he has lost a tempo.} (9. c4
$142) 9... Nxd7 10. f4 Qxc5 {Better than capturing with the Knight as the
attack on the c-pawn gains a tempo and the Queen is very penetrating on this
diagonal.} 11. Qd4 {This doesn't help to solve the Pawn problem.} Rc8 {Forcing
him into an even more unfavourable exchange.} 12. Qxc5 Nxc5 {Now the Knight
has the commanding square of e5. The c-Pawn looks feted.} 13. Ne2 Ne4 14. Bd2 (
14. Bb2 {Allowing him to castle would have been better.}) 14... Ne7 15. Rb1 b6
16. Rb3 Nc6 {Heading for c5} (16... Nf5 {Is useless.}) 17. a4 {Presumably to
allow Ra3} Na5 18. Rb4 Nc4 19. Bc1 O-O 20. O-O Rc7 {Black has all the time in
the world to attack the c-pawns.} 21. Rf3 Rfc8 22. Ng3 {This doesn't help for
I exchange and manoeuvre my other Knight to e5.} Nxg3 23. Rxg3 Na5 24. Bd2 Nb7
25. h4 {White is stuck.} Nc5 26. Rd4 Ne4 27. Re3 Nxd2 28. Rxd2 Rxc3 29. Rxc3
Rxc3 30. Kf2 Rc4 31. Ke3 Rxa4 32. Rd4 Rxd4 33. Kxd4 a5 34. Kc3 a4 35. Kb4 b5
36. Ka3 f6 37. c3 fxe5 38. fxe5 g5 0-1

