1. c4 e6 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c5 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. d4 d5 6. cxd5 Nxd5 7. dxc5 Bxc5 8.
O-O Qb6 {Compare White's hypermodern policy with Black's development.} 9. b3 {
The QBishop will have good prospects on the long diagonal.} O-O 10. Bb2 Rd8 11.
Qc1 f6 {Prevents Qg5 but weakens Black's position somewhat.} 12. Nc3 {
Threatening 13.Na5} Nxc3 13. Qxc3 Nd4 14. Qc4 Nxf3+ 15. Bxf3 Bd7 16. e3 $6 {
Threatens 17.Bxb7 but gives away the exchange for a risky attack.} ({I had
considered...} 16. Bxb7 Bxf2+ 17. Rxf2 Qxb7 {the position is too loose.}) 16...
Bb5 17. Qg4 Bxf1 18. Bxf6 Rd7 19. Kxf1 ({I had originally intended....} 19. Bd5
{..but after..} Re8 {I'm stuck.}) 19... Rf8 20. Bb2 (20. Bc3 {Might have been
better as it covers d2.}) 20... Bxe3 $1 {suddenly it all looks lost for White.}
21. Re1 $8 (21. fxe3 Qxe3 {wins streight off. What to do?}) 21... Bh6 {Risky.}
22. Rxe6 Qb5+ 23. Kg2 (23. Be2 Qc5 {is a nuisance.}) 23... Qf5 (23... Bd2 24.
Rd6 $3) 24. Qxf5 (24. Rxh6 Qxg4 25. Bxg4 Rd2) 24... Rxf5 25. Bg4 Rf8 26. Re2 (
26. Rxh6 Rd2) (26. Ba3 Rfd8) 26... Rd2 {Black exchanges off but doesn't
realise the power of White's Bishops.} 27. f4 {Lessening the scope of Black's
Bishop.} Rxe2+ 28. Bxe2 Rd8 29. Bc3 {Prevents 29.....Rd2} g6 30. Kf3 Bg7 31.
Bc4+ Kh8 32. Bxg7+ Kxg7 33. a4 {It is naturally my intention to make the QS
self supporting as it is now and to advance the King with the KS Pawns.} Kf6
34. g4 Rd2 35. h3 Rc2 {This allows the Black King to be driven back and makes
White's task of eliminating the KS Pawns easier.} 36. g5+ Kg7 37. Kg4 Rc3 {
It is hard to understand why he watsed time on moves like this.} 38. h4 h5+ {
Black thinks (wrongly) that by isolating the KS Pawns he weakens White's
position.} 39. gxh6+ Kxh6 40. Bf7 {Threatens 41.h5} Kg7 41. Bd5 b6 42. h5 gxh5+
43. Kxh5 Kf6 44. Kg4 {He refused a draw here} Rc1 45. Bc4 Rc3 {Now I have an
easy draw.} 46. f5 Re3 47. Kf4 Re1 48. Be6 Re5 (48... Rxe6 {is no use...} 49.
fxe6 Kxe6) 49. Bd7 Rc5 50. Ke4 a6 51. Kd4 Rc1 {[87']} 52. Be6 {[59']} b5 53.
axb5 axb5 54. Kd5 b4 55. Kd4 Rc3 56. Ke4 {I refused a draw offer here.} Rh3 57.
Kd4 Rxb3 {I now haven't lost a match or tournament game since March 17th.}
1/2-1/2

