1. g3 Nf6 2. Bg2 d5 3. d4 {I don't know why I played this as I intended 3.d3.}
g6 4. Nf3 (4. c4 $142) 4... Bg7 5. c4 dxc4 6. Qa4+ Nbd7 7. Qxc4 O-O 8. Nc3 Nb6
9. Qd3 {If I can now force e4 I have the better game.} Be6 {This move in
conjunction with .....c5 gives Black the better game.} 10. b3 ({I considered..
} 10. Ne5 {but then} Bd5 {is good for Black.}) 10... c5 $1 11. dxc5 $2 {
Now Black gets right on top.} Qxd3 12. exd3 Nfd7 13. Bb2 (13. Bd2 {is no
better.}) (13. d4 Nxc5) 13... Nxc5 14. Ke2 {A sad necessity.} Rac8 {
Threatening 15....Nxd3} 15. Rac1 Bf5 {[47']} 16. Rhd1 {[28']} Rfd8 17. Ne1 Rd7
18. Rd2 Rcd8 19. Rcd1 {The d2 Rook is vulnerable to the KBishop.} e5 {This
move seems to ease White's game.} ({I was much more worried about variations
such as...} 19... Bh6 20. f4 g5 21. d4 Ne6 22. d5 gxf4 $1 23. dxe6 Rxd2+ 24.
Rxd2 Rxd2+ 25. Kxd2 f3+ {However this variation may be too simplifying.}) 20.
Ne4 Ne6 21. Bf3 {The threat of 22.g4 forces Black to exchange one minor piece
and retreat his QBishop.} Nd4+ 22. Bxd4 Rxd4 23. g4 Bc8 24. g5 $1 {This move
was aimed at preventing Black from getting his KBishop on h6 and possibly
prevent a possible ....f5.} Nd5 25. Nc2 Nf4+ ({Not...} 25... Rxe4+ 26. dxe4 $1
Nc3+ 27. Ke1) 26. Ke3 {[65'] Adjourned} R4d7 {[72'] [sealed move] Play resumed
17\8\62 I had not thought much about this but intended to play 27.h4} ({
I now assumed that Black had sealed} 26... f5 {and this seems best.} 27. Nxd4
$4 (27. Nf6+ Bxf6 28. Nxd4 (28. gxf6 Nd5+ 29. Bxd5+ R4xd5 30. d4 e4) 28... Bxg5
) (27. Ng3 Nd5+ 28. Bxd5+ R4xd5 $17) (27. Nc5 Nd5+ 28. Bxd5+ R4xd5 29. Na4) ({
However White would do better with} 27. Nc3 $1 R4d7 28. h4 $1 {and although
Black has the better of it a win is hard to find}) 27... fxe4 28. Bg2 Nd5+ $3)
27. h4 $1 ({Black expected..} 27. Bg4 {27.....h5 was played to stop this.
However if I play Bg4 Black has the best of it.} Rc7 28. Bxc8 Rdxc8 {Black
threatens the Knight}) 27... h5 (27... f5 28. gxf6 Bh6 29. Ng5 Bxg5 30. hxg5)
28. Nc5 {This looks risky but if I just sit tight and do nothing Black plays
both Bishops on the QS.} Rc7 29. d4 {This turns out badly with correct play by
Black but I had little choice. However Black now had to make 8 moves in about
12' and doesn't find the best line.} exd4+ 30. Kxf4 Rxc5 31. Nxd4 {It may have
well have been advised to delay this capture.} Be5+ 32. Ke3 Re8 $2 {Due to the
pressure.} ({Much better was..} 32... Rc3+ 33. Ke2 Re8 34. Be4 Bf4 35. Rd3
Rxe4+ 36. Kf3 Rxd4 37. Rxc3 Bg4+) 33. Be4 Rc3+ 34. Rd3 Rxd3+ 35. Rxd3 b6 36.
Nc6 Bb7 {Black is over his time rush but he suddenly finds that White has
actually got the better game from the exchanges!! White's King is very well
placed his Rook is better placed than Black's and he ends up with the better
Pawns.} 37. Nxe5 (37. Nxa7 $4 Bb8) 37... Rxe5 38. f3 Re7 39. Rc3 {Agreed drawn.
An extreemly complicated and interesting game.} 1/2-1/2

