1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. f4 Bg7 {Tis leads to a
good game for White} 7. e5 dxe5 8. fxe5 Ng4 9. Bb5+ Kf8 $4 ({According to M.C.
O. the correct continuation is....} 9... Nc6 10. Nxc6 Qxd1+ 11. Nxd1 a6 12. Ba4
Bd7 13. h3 Nh6 14. Nxe7 {With advantage to White [Pilnick - kashdan Ney York
1948]}) ({If....} 9... Bd7 {simply..} 10. Qxg4) 10. Ne6+ {Rather neat. This
game was published in the chess column of the "New Statesman" and won me a 10/
6 voucher. Middlesex 42.5 - kent 37.5 with three games for adjudication.} 1-0

