1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Bg5 Bg7 7. Be2 Nc6 8.
Nxc6 bxc6 9. Qd2 Qb6 10. Rb1 O-O 11. O-O Rb8 12. Be3 Qc7 (12... Qa5 {Might be
better.}) 13. Rfd1 Rd8 14. h3 Nd7 15. Bh6 Bh8 16. a3 Qa5 $4 {A terrible
blunder I realised my mistake immediatly.} 17. b4 $4 {White misses his chance.}
({Correct is...} 17. Nd5 $3) 17... Qe5 ({Not...} 17... Qxa3 18. Rb3 $18) 18.
Rb3 Nf6 19. Bf4 Qe6 20. e5 Ne8 21. Bg4 Qc4 22. Be2 Qe6 23. Bg4 Qc4 {A
remarkable escape on move 17. Fleming Score Middlesex 21.5 - Essex 8.5
Middlesex won the 60 board match 42.5 - 16.5 (with 1 for adj [it was drawn])}
