{Opponent info: GBR Ladies Champion 1961. [R.A.C. Grade 4a ~193 - 200 ECF]} 1.
c4 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 e5 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. d3 d6 6. Nf3 O-O 7. O-O Nbd7 8. b4 {
[5'] This move is rather risky as it opens a diagonal for Black's KBishop and
leaves my QKnight undefended but 8.b4 gains more space and prepares a QS
attack.} a5 {[20']} ({I expected....} 8... e4 9. Nd2) 9. b5 ({If} 9. Qb3 axb4
10. Qxb4 Ra6 11. Z0 Rb6 {is good for Black.}) 9... Nc5 10. Qc2 {Defends the
Knight and prevents ....e4} Bd7 11. a4 Qc8 12. Ba3 Ne6 13. e3 Ne8 {To play ....
f5 but Black is too cramped.} 14. Rab1 {Removing the Rook from the long
diagonal so as to move the c3 Knight.} f5 {Black is too weak on the QS to try
a QS advance.} 15. Nd5 {Wins a tempo.} Kh8 16. c5 $1 {The decisive
breakthrough.} dxc5 17. Bxc5 Nxc5 18. Qxc5 {Threatening 19.Ne5 & Ne7} b6 19.
Qe7 Nd6 20. Nxb6 cxb6 21. Qxd6 (21. Nxe5 $2 Re8) 21... Rf6 22. Qxe5 Qf8 23. Ng5
Rd8 ({Not} 23... Rd6 $4 24. Qxd6) 24. Qd5 $2 {I was now running short of time
and went wrong in a completely won position.} (24. Qb2 $142) (24. d4 $142) (24.
Qc3 $142) 24... h6 25. Nf3 Rd6 26. Qb3 Be6 27. Nh4 $6 {All this was played
rather quickly and this move is rather doubtful.} Kh7 ({Possible was....} 27...
Bxb3 28. Nxg6+ Kg8 29. Nxf8 Bf7 30. d4) 28. Qc2 (28. Qa3 $142) 28... Rxd3 29.
Rfd1 $6 Bb3 30. Qxd3 Rxd3 31. Rxd3 Bc2 {All this was played in a rush.} 32.
Rbd1 Bxd1 33. Rxd1 Qb4 34. Bc6 Qg4 35. Rd6 g5 {The score gives the following: 
[Adjudicated win for White.] Black Resigned A pity about the time limit
otherwise I had an easy win. I was pleased with the opening.} (35... g5 36. f3
Qxa4 37. Nxf5 {Threatening 28.Rd7. Queen checks are useless. if} Qa1+ 38. Kg2
Qe5 39. Be4) 0-1

