1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. c3 Nf6 4. Qc2 {I don't think this is a very promising
line for White.} Qc7 {Now White can't play 5d4 unless he recaptures with the
Knight.} 5. Be2 Nc6 6. O-O (6. d4 {seemed the obvious move.}) 6... Bg4 7. Re1
g6 ({I considered} 7... d5 {but wanted to move my King from the centre fairly
quickly.}) 8. d3 ({Why not ....} 8. d4 {White tends to play rather passively.})
8... Bg7 9. Nbd2 O-O 10. h3 Bd7 11. Nb3 b5 {On account of White's passive play
I have been able to gain space.} 12. Bf4 e5 {This move strengthens my control
of the centre; gives my QBishop a good square at e6; threatens an eventual KS
advance by .....f5 ; and is perfectly safe as White can't get a piece on d4.}
13. Be3 ({If} 13. Bg3 {Black will have a good move of...} Bh6 {later on}) 13...
a5 14. d4 c4 15. Nbd2 exd4 16. Nxd4 Nxd4 17. Bxd4 d5 18. exd5 (18. e5 {
probably loses a Pawn.}) 18... Bf5 19. Qd1 Nxd5 20. Bxg7 Kxg7 21. Bf3 ({If..} 
21. Nxc4 {he gets into trouble after...} Rad8) 21... Rad8 22. Be4 ({If..} 22.
Bxd5 {I will be able to double rooks on the d-file with the better game.})
22... Bxe4 23. Rxe4 Nf4 {Once my Knight gets to d3 White will be lucky to
survive.} 24. Qc2 Nd3 25. a4 {After all his passive play White decides to be
more aggressive but he is too late and this move turns out badly.} Qb6 26. Re2
Rfe8 27. Ne4 {White skating on thin ice.} bxa4 28. Rxa4 {This loses outright.}
({He was forced to play..} 28. Qxa4 {but Black has the better after...} f5 29.
Ng3 Rxe2 30. Nxe2 Qxf2+ ({or...} 30... Nxb2)) 28... Qc6 $1 29. Ng3 ({If} 29. f3
f5 30. Ng3 Rxe2 31. Nxe2 Ne1 $1) 29... Rxe2 30. Nxe2 Ne1 $1 31. Qc1 Qxg2# {
A neat finish after 28.....Qc6!} 0-1

