1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 {[30s]} 4. Qg4 {[10']} Nf6 {[4']} 5. Qxg7 {[15']}
Rg8 6. Qh6 Rg6 7. Qe3 {[13']} dxe4 {[8']} (7... Nxe4 {Allows White to play} 8.
Bd3) 8. Bd2 Bxc3 9. Bxc3 Nbd7 ({I considered...} 9... Qd5 {but then..} 10. Qf4
{is quite good for White.}) 10. Nh3 {[30'] The fact that White has to play
moves like this shows that he has lost all his opening advantage.} Nb6 11. Nf4
Nbd5 12. Nxd5 exd5 13. h3 Qd6 14. g4 {[44']} Bd7 {[20']} 15. f4 {This is all
very aggressive but Black has been given a protected passed Pawn on e4.} O-O-O
16. Be2 h6 17. O-O-O (17. O-O {Would be much too risky.}) 17... Nh7 18. Rdg1 f5
{[30']} 19. gxf5 {[57']} ({Not} 19. g5 $2 hxg5 20. fxg5 f4 $1) 19... Bxf5 20.
Bg4 Bxg4 {Doubtful.} 21. hxg4 Nf6 22. g5 hxg5 23. fxg5 Nd7 24. Qh3 Rdg8 25. Bd2
Qe7 26. Qh7 R6g7 27. Qf5 e3 28. Be1 c6 ({Not} 28... Rxg5 $4 29. Rxg5 Qxg5 30.
Qxg5 Rxg5 31. Rh8+) 29. Rh6 {This gives up a Pawn in order to secure threats
on my Knight.} Rxg5 30. Rxg5 Qxg5 31. Qe6 Rf8 32. Rh7 e2+ 33. Kb1 Qf5 34. Qxf5
Rxf5 35. Re7 Rf4 {Has Black blundered??!} 36. Re8+ Kc7 37. Bg3 Ne5 $3 {3 Time
was called and we agreed a draw. Rather ab amusing position at the end. Hayes
won 5 -} (37... Ne5 $3 {I may have been rather generous here because of the
following variation.} 38. Kc1 {Forced.} Rf1+ 39. Kd2 e1=Q+ 40. Bxe1 Nf3+ 41.
Kd1 Nxd4 {Say...} 42. Re3 Nf3 43. Re2 {What else?} Rxe1+ 44. Rxe1 Nxe1 45. Kxe1
{and Black may have a win.}) 1/2-1/2

