1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f3 O-O 6. Be3 e5 7. d5 c6 8. Bd3 {
Not a particularly good square for the Bishop.} (8. Nge2 {Might have been
better.}) 8... cxd5 9. cxd5 Nbd7 10. Qd2 Nc5 {[13']} 11. g4 {[3']} Nxd3+ {[25']
} 12. Qxd3 Bd7 13. Nge2 {[3' 30s]} Qa5 14. O-O (14. O-O-O {is too risky.}) (14.
Kf2 {Has no particular advantage.}) (14. h4 {Was playable.}) 14... a6 {[35']}
15. Rfc1 {[7' 30s]} b5 16. a3 {[9'] Preventing 17....b4 which would have been
quite good for Black.} Ne8 {Intending .....f5} 17. b4 Qd8 18. Ng3 {Prevents ...
..f5} Qh4 19. Kg2 {Allowing h3 if necessary} Bh6 20. Nd1 Ng7 ({Now if...} 20...
Bxe3 21. Nxe3 {and Black still can't play .....f5}) 21. Rc7 Bxe3 22. Rxd7 $6 {
This move was very risky although it eventually wins the d-Pawn it leaves me
very weak on the Black squares.} Bd4 23. Ra2 h5 24. gxh5 {This too is risky. I
was persuing my Pawn winning policy.} (24. h3 {was sounder.}) 24... Nxh5 25.
Nxh5 Qxh5 {Threatens 26.....Qg5+ and 27.....Qg1.} 26. Kh1 {Played after much
consideration as the position is very awkward.} Rac8 27. Rxd6 {By now I was
obliged to take it.} Rc1 28. Rc6 (28. Rxa6 Rfc8 {Was a bit too dangerous.})
28... Rc8 29. Rxc8+ Rxc8 30. Re2 {I was faced with the difficulty of defending
d1, g1, f3, h2} Rc1 31. Re1 Bf2 {Adjourned. Drawn} (31... Bf2 {Possible
continuation.} 32. Rf1 ({Not} 32. Re2 $4 Rxd1+) 32... Bg3 33. Qd2 Ra1 34. d6
Bh4 35. d7) 1/2-1/2

