1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Be3 a6 7. Bc4 e6 8. a3
Be7 9. Qd2 O-O 10. f3 Bd7 11. O-O-O b5 12. Nxc6 {Lessening Black's control
over b4.} Bxc6 13. Bb3 {Better here than a2 which doesn't protect c2.} Qc7 {
[18']} 14. g4 {[7']} Nd7 15. h4 Nc5 (15... Ne5 16. Z0 Nc4 {seems better.}) 16.
Ba2 d5 {Loses a pawn but Black gets good play for all his pieces.} 17. exd5
Rfd8 18. Qf2 Bb7 {Better than taking the Pawn.} (18... Bxd5) 19. dxe6 Nxe6 20.
Rxd8+ Rxd8 21. Kb1 {Threatening 22.Bb6} Qc6 {[43']} 22. Ne4 {[17']} b4 {
Opening files to my King.} 23. axb4 Bxb4 24. Qe2 {The position is rather
tricky with somany pieces and so few Pawns.} a5 25. Rd1 Rb8 26. Qc4 Qe8 {
This leaves my Queen rather short of squares.} 27. h5 Bc6 {Threatening 28.....
Bb5 when my Queen is in rather an embarassing position.} 28. h6 Ba3 ({Now if...
} 28... Bb5 29. hxg7 Bxc4 30. Nf6+) 29. Bc1 Kf8 {This relieves the threatend
fork on f6 but is not too good.} 30. hxg7+ Kxg7 $4 (30... Nxg7 {Was necessary,
distasteful as it is.}) 31. Qc3+ Nd4 32. Qxd4+ {Middlesex won 17.3 - 2.5} (32.
Qxd4+ Kf8 33. Bh6+ Ke7 34. Qe5#) 1-0

