1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f3 e5 6. d5 c6 7. Be3 O-O 8. Nge2
cxd5 9. cxd5 a6 10. Nc1 b5 11. b4 {It was important to prevent 12.....b4, but
the move creates a weakness on c4 and the Pawn itself becomes somewhat weak.}
Nbd7 {Heading for c4} 12. Be2 Qc7 13. Qd2 Nb6 14. O-O {[5']} Nh5 {This move
doesn't accomplish very much.} 15. Bxb6 Qxb6+ 16. Kh1 Bd7 (16... f5 {seems a
good alternative.}) 17. g3 {Prevents ....Nf4 and facilitates an eventual f4 if
necessary.} Rfc8 (17... Bh3 {Doesn't achieve much.}) 18. Nd3 {The Knight is
better in the centre on general principles.} Nf6 {Relinquishing the KS.} 19.
Kg2 {Preventing .....Bh3 and strengthening the centre.} Be8 {This Bishop is
getting in the way of Black's other pieces.} 20. Rfc1 Nd7 {Again Black heads a
Knight for c4.} 21. a3 {I considered 21.a4 but it had more disadvantages than
advantages.} (21. a4) 21... Qd8 {Frees b6 for the Knight.} 22. Nb2 {
Strengthening c4} h5 {Intending .....Kh7 followed by.....Bh6} 23. Bd3 Kh7 24.
Rc2 Nb6 25. Ne2 {To reply to 25.....Bh6 with 26.f4} Bh6 26. f4 {Black would
have had much the better game had I not been able to play this.} Qe7 {Trying
to take advantage of my weak e-pawn after......Nc4} 27. Rac1 Rxc2 28. Bxc2 $1 (
{Not} 28. Rxc2 $2 exf4 29. Nxf4 Nc4 $1 30. Nxc4 bxc4 31. Rxc4 Bb5 {When Black
gets a good game for his Pawn.}) 28... Nc4 29. Nxc4 bxc4 30. Rf1 Rc8 31. Qc3 {
Hayes won 5.5 - 2.5} 1/2-1/2

