1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. c3 d3 5. Bxd3 Nf6 6. O-O g6 7. Be3 Bg7 8. Na3
({The c-pawn starts to get in his way.} 8. Nbd2 $142) 8... O-O 9. Qc2 {Not
particularly good.} Nbd7 {Amongst other things this prevents 10.e5} 10. Rad1 a6
{Now White's a3 Knight is lacking a future.} 11. Nd4 {[4']} Nc5 {[6'] I now
tried to exchange off my Knights for his Bishops leaving him with two not very
strong Knights.} 12. f4 Nxd3 13. Qxd3 b5 14. Qc2 {He seems to like his Queen
on c2.} Qc7 {Prevents 15.e5 and threatens to win a Pawn by 15.....Bb7} 15. Nb1
{Showing up the drawbacks of having a Pawn on c3.} Bb7 16. Nd2 Ng4 17. Qd3 Nxe3
18. Qxe3 {[56']} Qb6 {[15']} 19. f5 Rac8 {Middlesex won 10.5 - 9.5} 1/2-1/2

