1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Nf3 Bb4 {Not a very inspired opening but I was
in no mood for play as the match which was more of a garden party was played
in a ridiculous atmosphere with dozens of spectators, cameramen, etc...} 5.
Qa4+ Nc6 6. e3 O-O 7. Bd2 a6 8. cxd5 Nxd5 9. Qc2 Bxc3 10. bxc3 {better than
the Bishop recapture.} Re8 {Trying to force .....e5} 11. e4 Nde7 12. Bd3 Ng6 {
I didn't like having to play this.} (12... e5 {fails to} 13. d5) 13. e5 f5 14.
exf6 Qxf6 15. Bg5 {White is obviously on top.} Qf7 16. Ne5 $2 {This seems to
throw away much of White's advantage.} ({White said he didn't play} 16. Nh4 {
because of.....} e5) 16... Ncxe5 17. dxe5 Kh8 {so that after I play ......NxP
he does not gain a tempo playing Bxh7+} 18. O-O Nxe5 19. Bxh7 Qh5 {This eases
Black's position considerably although some of the Pawns are not happy.} 20.
Bf4 Qxh7 21. Qxh7+ Kxh7 22. Bxe5 Re7 ({After} 22... c6 {my Bishop is stuck.})
23. Rfd1 {Threatens 24.Rd8 and 25.Rad1} b5 ({Not} 23... Bd7 24. Bxc7 Ba4 25.
Bd6) 24. Rab1 Bb7 25. Rb4 Bd5 26. Rh4+ Kg6 ({I might have preffered...} 26...
Kg8 {had this not been a friendly match.}) 27. Rd3 Bxa2 {Most certainly I
would not have played this in a proper match. I didn't bother to work out the
consequences.} 28. Rg3+ Kf5 (28... Kf7 29. Rxg7+ Ke8 30. Rh8+) 29. Rh5+ Ke4 30.
Re3+ Kd5 31. Bf6+ Kd6 32. Bxe7+ Kxe7 33. f4 Rd8 34. f5 Rd1+ $2 35. Kf2 Rd2+ $2
36. Re2 Rxe2+ 37. Kxe2 Bc4+ 38. Kd2 e5 39. Rh8 Bd5 40. g4 a5 41. Rc8 c6 42. g5
Be4 43. Rc7+ Kf8 {Adjudicated Win for White. Not very good although it wasn't
very serious. The match was between HCGS and represententative Schools form
the H & H Schools league (The Rest). HCGS 2.5 - The Rest 3.5} 1-0

