1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 {I needed only a draw to come first in section A so I
selected this in preference to the sharper 2.....Nf6} 3. f4 d6 (3... exf4) (
3... Bc5) 4. Nf3 Bg4 5. Bb5 Nge7 {Black's somewhat unusual variation seems to
be quite effective, particularly as White didn't seem very happy against it.}
6. d4 {White tries to maintain the innitiative but this results in a releasing
of the tension.} a6 7. Bxc6+ ({After} 7. Bc4 exd4 {seems playable.}) 7... Nxc6
8. dxe5 Bxf3 9. Qxf3 dxe5 10. O-O ({Better seems..} 10. fxe5 Nxe5 11. Qg3 Ng6
12. Nd5) 10... Bc5+ 11. Be3 {This allows Black complete equality} Bxe3+ 12.
Qxe3 {This game assured me of winning section A on my own with 8/9 (7wins 2
draws).} 1/2-1/2

