1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 Nf5 8. Bd3
h5 9. Qh3 $1 {[Yanovsky-Marchand Dallas1941]} ({Yanovsky annotates thus:
"superior to} 9. Qf4 cxd4 10. cxd4 Qa5+ $1 {[Bogoljubov - Flohr Nottingham
1935] Qh3! was recommended by Alekhine"}) 9... cxd4 {The threat was b4.} (9...
Qa5 $2 10. Bxf5 $1) 10. Bxf5 exf5 11. cxd4 Nc6 12. Ne2 (12. Nf3 {Is probably
better here. I played 12.Ne2 to keep the 3rd rank open for the Queen}) 12... g5
13. Qf3 Be6 14. c3 f6 {Black has rather the better of it now.} 15. Ng3 g4 16.
Qd3 fxe5 17. Nxf5 Qd7 ({If} 17... e4 18. Ng7+) ({Suicidal would be...} 17...
Bxf5 18. Qxf5 exd4 19. cxd4 Nxd4 20. Qg6+ $1 Kf8 {Forced.} 21. Bh6+ Ke7 22.
Bg5+) 18. Ng3 O-O-O 19. O-O (19. dxe5 Nxe5 {Doesn't look very happy.}) 19... h4
(19... e4 {is an excellent alternative.}) 20. Ne2 Rdf8 ({Again....} 20... e4 {
looked good.}) 21. dxe5 Nxe5 22. Qe3 Nc6 ({If now....} 22... Nc4 23. Qc5+) (
22... Nf3+ 23. gxf3 gxf3 24. Nf4 {Is spectacular but not much else.}) 23. Nd4 {
Attempting to exchange off his Bishop or keep it off the b1-h7 diagonal.} Nxd4
24. cxd4 Kb8 {Not very ambitous} 25. Qe5+ Ka8 26. Bf4 Qf7 27. g3 Bd7 28. Qe2 {
Prevents 28.....Bb5.} hxg3 ({Qe2 also answers...} 28... Re8 {with...} 29. Be5)
29. fxg3 Qh7 {Threatening 30.....Bb5} 30. Rac1 $6 Bb5 31. Qb2 Bc4 ({Black
doesn't play....} 31... Bxf1 {in view of} 32. Rc7 {however after....} Qxh2+ 33.
Qxh2 Rxh2 34. Kxh2 {Black stands fairly well.}) 32. Rf2 Rhg8 1/2-1/2

