1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 c5 4. d5 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. e4 g6 7. f4 Bg7 8. Bb5+
Nfd7 ({Not} 8... Nbd7 $4 9. e5 $1) ({Not} 8... Bd7 $4 9. e5 $1) 9. a4 {A
useful move in this type of position.} O-O 10. Qf3 Na6 11. Nge2 (11. Bxa6 {
Has more disadvantages than good points.}) 11... Nb4 12. O-O a6 13. Bc4 Nb6 {
This appears to gain a tempo but in fact slows down his QS advance.} 14. Bb3 (
14. Ba2 {May be quicker.}) 14... c4 {This gains another move but is not too
strong.} 15. Ba2 Bd7 $2 {In view of what follows taking the Bishop may be
better.} (15... Nxa2) 16. Bb1 $1 {Now I threaten 17.f5 which is very strong.}
Nc8 {Black realises that this Knight is misplaced.} 17. f5 Be5 (17... gxf5 18.
exf5 Z0 {followed by} 19. Qh5 Z0 {then} 20. f6) 18. f6 Rb8 19. Bh6 Re8 20. Bg7
{Protecting the Pawn allowing the Queen to move. If I can get my Queen to h6
Bh8 wins.} Qb6+ {Prevents 21.Qe3, 22.Qh6} 21. Kh1 Qc5 22. g4 {Intending 23.Qh3,
24.Qh6} Nd3 23. Bxd3 cxd3 24. Qxd3 $2 ({Better would be....} 24. Nf4 {Which
must win}) 24... Bxg4 {Black's position improves.} 25. Qd2 Bxc3 26. Nxc3 $2 ({
I considered...} 26. Qh6 {but it's too complicated for my liking. However it
appears to be better.}) 26... Re5 {The saving move, temporarily at least.} 27.
Qf4 Bh3 28. Rf3 Rh5 29. Ne2 {Threatening 30.Ng3} Qc2 30. Rf2 {The Rook tends
to get in the way here.} g5 31. Qe3 Qxb2 32. Rg1 Qb6 33. Qg3 {Adjourned Play
resumed 3/10/62} Qb4 {[Sealed move] I was somewhat relieved at this.} ({
What I think the soundest move is.} 33... h6 $1 {after which I would have been
in a quandry. It would probably have continued.} 34. Qf3 g4 $2 (34... Rh4 35.
Rg3 {if} Qb1+ ({My plan after.....} 35... Bd7 36. Rf1 Z0 37. Rfg1 Z0 38. Bxh6)
(35... Rf4) 36. Ng1 Rf4 37. Rxh3 $3 Rxf3 38. Rxh6 $18) 35. Qf4) ({If he sealed
} 33... g4 $2 34. Nf4 $1 {However after 35.....Bd7 I am rather at aloss for a
continuation. As above I would probaly continue Rf1---g1 followed by Bxh6}) 34.
Qf3 Rh4 ({Not} 34... g4 $4 35. Rxg4 $1) 35. Rg3 ({P.Adams thought that} 35. Ng3
{was better as Black can't reply....} Rf4 36. Qe3 Rxf2 {because of...} 37. Qxg5
) 35... Qb1+ 36. Ng1 Rf4 37. Qh5 $1 {Setting a neat trap} Qxe4+ ({Not} 37...
Rxf2 38. Qxh7+ $3) 38. Rff3 Rxf3 (38... Bg4 39. Qxg5) 39. Nxf3 g4 40. Bh6 Qg6
41. Qh4 {I didn't want to allow an exchange of Queens.} Nb6 {Attempting to
bring his QS pieces into the game.} 42. Ng1 {This allows a draw.} (42. Ng5 Qxf6
) 42... Qe4+ 43. Nf3 Qg6 44. Ng1 {Allowing the draw but there is nothing
better.} Re8 $4 {A costly lapse of concentration Black for more than he has a
right to. He sees that after} 45. Nxh3 Re1+ 46. Ng1 Qe4+ 47. Rg2 Kh8 ({He sees.
...} 47... Rxg1+ 48. Kxg1 {allows him mate....... but he doesn't see that my
Queen covers e1} Qe1+) 48. h3 (48. Qxg4 $4 Rxg1+) 48... gxh3 49. Qxh3 Nxd5 {
As good as anything.} 50. Qg3 Qg6 51. Qxe1 (51. Bg7+ {is quicker.}) 51... Qxh6+
52. Rh2 Qxf6 53. Qe8+ Kg7 54. Rg2+ Kh6 55. Qf8+ Kh5 56. Rh2+ Kg5 57. Qg8+ Kf5
58. Rf2+ Nf4 59. Qg3 Ke4 60. Qf3+ Ke5 61. Qc3+ Ke6 62. Qxf6+ Kxf6 63. Rxf4+ {
Black plays on now for no particular reason other than no-one likes resigning.}
Ke6 64. Rb4 b5 65. axb5 axb5 66. Rxb5 d5 67. Ne2 Ke5 68. Rb7 f5 69. Rxh7 Ke4
70. Nc3+ Kd4 71. Nxd5 Kxd5 72. Kg2 Ke4 73. Kf2 Kf4 74. Rh4+ Kg5 75. Ra4 f4 76.
Kf3 Kf5 77. Rxf4+ Ke5 78. Ke3 Kd5 79. Re4 Kd6 80. Kd4 Kc6 81. Re5 Kd6 82. Ke4
Kc6 83. Rd5 Kc7 84. Kd4 Kc6 85. Kc4 Kb6 86. Rc5 Kb7 87. Kb5 Ka7 88. Rc7+ Ka8
89. Kc6 Kb8 90. Rh7 {A very complicated game indeed. peter Adams won section B.
} 1-0

