{Opponent info: GBR Girls U-18 Champion} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4
Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bc4 e6 7. Bb3 Be7 8. Be3 ({Fischer - Tal Candidates 1959
played} 8. f4 {here which prevents..} d5 {this wouldn't be too good for Black.}
) 8... O-O 9. f4 a6 10. Qf3 Qc7 11. O-O-O Nxd4 12. Rxd4 ({If} 12. Bxd4 $2 e5
13. Be3 Bg4) 12... e5 $6 {With this move Black tries to gain some freedom but
allows White too much play on the KS and also the diagonal for my Bishop is
opened.} 13. Rd3 {Better than 13.Rd2 (strengthening the c-Pawn) as it allows
the Rook to move along the 3rd rank later on.} (13. Rd2) 13... Bd7 $2 {Black
has the choice of passively defending the KS by by say .....PxP & .....Be6 or
counterattacking on the QS with .....b5. Either of these seem better than the
move chosen as the Bishopwhen on c6 blocks the Black Queen , and allows White
to play f5 after which Black has little hope.} (13... exf4) (13... Be6) (13...
b5) 14. f5 Bc6 {Much too slow and passive.} 15. g4 Nd7 {The Knight would have
to move anyway . Black's position was very difficult.} 16. g5 Nc5 {What else
is there? This however takes the Knight completely away from the KS (it was
covering f6 to some extent).} ({It's doubtful there is anything better such as.
....} 16... g6 17. f6 (17. fxg6 {followed by....} Z0 18. h4 {doesn't look very
pleasant for Black.})) 17. Bxc5 dxc5 18. f6 {Seems clearer than 18.g6} (18. g6)
18... Bd8 ({Naturally not.} 18... gxf6 $2 19. gxf6 {and wins in about two
moves.}) 19. Qh5 {Threatens 20.Rh3. and also g6 followed by PxP} Bd7 {The ony
move to prevent immediate departure.} (19... Bxe4 {is spectacular but useless.}
) 20. Nd5 {Piling on the pressure. This shows another of Black's weaknesses,
namely the hole on d5.} Qc6 {The reply is the same whatever she plays.} 21.
Ne7+ $1 Bxe7 22. fxe7 c4 {The alternatives are worse...} (22... Rfc8 23. Qxf7+
Kh8 24. Rf1 $3) (22... Rfe8 23. Bxf7+ Kh8 24. g6 $1 h6 25. Bxe8 Bxe8 26. Qf5 $3
) 23. exf8=R+ Rxf8 24. Bxc4 Qxe4 25. Rxd7 Qxh1+ {allowing a neat finnish.} 26.
Rd1 Qe4 27. Qxf7+ Rxf7 28. Rd8# {A very good game.} 1-0

