1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bc4 b5 5. Bb3 a5 6. a3 c6 7. Nf3 {His
weaknesses are on e5 and the a2-g8 diagonal. Therefore I contest on these.} ({
After} 7. dxc6 Bxc6 (7... Nxc6 {Black gets a good game.})) 7... Na6 $2 {
Much too artificial.} (7... cxd5 $142) 8. dxc6 Bxc6 9. Ne5 (9. Bxf7+ Kxf7 10.
Ne5+ Kg8 11. Nxc6 {is not too good after....} Qd5) 9... Bd5 10. Qf3 {Black
took the Queen without a moments notice, but realising his mistake resigned.
Black was much too hasty. Uni won 3.5 - 1.5 My time [7'] his [3']} (10. Qf3 {
even after...} Bxb3 (10... e6 11. Bxd5 Qxd5 12. Qxd5 Nxd5 13. d4) 11. Qxb3 Qd5
{forced} 12. Qxd5 Nxd5 13. d4 {Black may well be lost.}) 1-0

