1. e4 b6 {Apparently this is his usual defence. I have never played against it
in a serious game.} 2. d4 Bb7 3. Nc3 g6 {This looks rather doubtful.} 4. f4 {
I didn't know anything about this opening but this seemed good.} Nh6 {This
seems questionable.} 5. Bc4 {5Bd3 may be better as it turns out.} e6 6. Nf3 f5
7. Bd3 {Even though this involves moving the Bishop again it seems best.} (7.
Qe2 $2 {or 7.Qe3? Lose against.} fxe4 {I can't recapture} 8. Nxe4 {due to} d5)
(7. e5 {Seems to block off the position too much.}) 7... fxe4 (7... Bg7 {
seems better as 7.....fxe4 opens the position up to my adavntage.}) 8. Bxe4
Bxe4 (8... Nc6 9. d5 {doesn't look very good for Black. After 8.....Bxe4 he is
just as badly placed.}) 9. Nxe4 Nc6 10. O-O (10. d5 {Would be premature I
think.}) 10... Nb4 $2 {The knight move loses several tempi.} (10... Bg7 $142)
11. a3 Nd5 12. c4 Nf6 {[20']} 13. Qd3 {[19']} c6 {Trying to prevent d5 but
weakening his d6} 14. Re1 {"pinning" the e-pawn and threatening d5} Nxe4 15.
Qxe4 {d5 is unstoppable} Nf5 16. d5 $1 Bc5+ {Gaining a tempo temporarilybut it
will be lost when I play b4 aslo the Bishop is rather vulnerable here.} 17. Kh1
Nd6 {[42']} 18. Qe2 {[28']} ({Much better than} 18. Qe5 Nf7 {When Black's
position has improved slightly.}) 18... Qc8 {This gives up a piece for two
Pawns but he had to lose something anyway. 18.....Qc8 complicates things
somewhat and may be his best chance.} 19. b4 cxd5 20. bxc5 (20. cxd5 {is good
too.}) 20... Nxc4 (20... Qxc5 {is just as bad after..} 21. cxd5 Qxd5 22. Bb2)
21. cxb6 Nxb6 22. Bb2 Rf8 23. Rac1 Qb7 24. Qb5 Ke7 {The threat was 25.RxP+} 25.
Qb4+ Ke8 26. Be5 Rc8 27. Ng5 $1 Rxc1 28. Rxc1 h6 29. Nxe6 $1 dxe6 30. Rc7 {
Quite a godd game. Southampton Uni won 3.5 - 2.5} 1-0

