1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. e4 Nxe5 5. Nf3 (5. f4 {is more aggressive.})
5... Bb4+ 6. Bd2 Qe7 7. Nc3 {Better than exchanging.} Bxc3 {Much as I disliked
this I didn't want to allow 8.Nd5} 8. Bxc3 Nbc6 9. Nxe5 Nxe5 10. Qd4 (10. f4
Ng6) 10... f6 {about the safest move and not as bad as it looks.} 11. O-O-O {
[26']} d6 {[7']} 12. f4 Nc6 13. Qd2 {[31']} Bg4 {seems doubtful.} ({maybe} 
13... Be6 {was better}) (13... Qxe4 $4 14. Re1) 14. Re1 O-O-O 15. h3 Bd7 16. g4
h5 {[18'] The best move I think. I had got a cramped position due to playing
the opening too quickly} 17. gxh5 {[51']} (17. g5 fxg5 18. fxg5 {Gives me e5
for my Knight and an open f-file looks quite good for Black.}) 17... Rxh5 {
[18']} 18. h4 Qf7 {My intention is to force .....f5} ({After the game White
suggested I should have played....} 18... g6 {in an attempt to win the h-Pawn
but my f-Pawn is left weak and his Bishops would come in to play on the open
lines.}) 19. Be2 Rh6 20. Reg1 {[58'] putting pressure on the g-Pawn.} Re8 {
4 [27'] Having spent 27' over 20 moves I spent 40' over the next} 21. Bd3 Be6
22. b3 Bd7 {Played after much thought. I intended something on the lines of....
Nd8, ....Ne6, ....Bc6} 23. Rh2 Re7 {Again after much thought. The g-Pawn needs
protecting and this way, laterally, seems best.} 24. Qf2 g6 {[59'] This was
impossible last move due to f5.Now I can play ....f5} 25. Qg3 f5 26. exf5 Bxf5
27. Qg5 {I played rather quickly throughout. White has the better of it at the
end.} 1/2-1/2

