1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e3 c6 6. a3 {According to Alekhine
this move (as in Alekhine Capablanca 34th Match game), whose main aim is to
avoid the Cambridge Springs Defence should promise no more than equality.} Be7
7. Nf3 O-O 8. Qc2 {In the above game Alekhine played 8.Bd3 here. Possibly
White did not want to waste a tempo here after 8.Bd3 PxP but as he plays
thisnext move it was hardly worth the bother. Perhaps he expected me to play 8.
....PxP streight away.} (8. Bd3 dxc4) 8... a6 (8... dxc4) (8... h6 9. Bf4 g5 {
seems a good alternative.}) 9. Bd3 dxc4 10. Bxc4 Nd5 11. Bxe7 Qxe7 12. Rd1 Nxc3
{Simplifying by exchanging. Also Ne4 is ruled out by White.} 13. Qxc3 ({After} 
13. bxc3 {I can safely play} Qxa3) 13... Nb6 {Giving two tempi unless White is
willing to give up his Bishop.} 14. Ba2 (14. Bd3 {Does not appear any better.})
14... Nd5 15. Qc2 Bd7 {My object is to force .....c5 as .....e5 is temporarily
out of the question.} 16. O-O Rac8 17. Rc1 Rc7 {Intending todouble the Rooks
or play .....Rd8 & .....Bc8} 18. b4 {Preventing .....c5 for good but blocking
the QS} f5 $1 {My best chance. I have the better of it on the KS with
attacking possibilities. My e-Pawn is not really weak.} 19. Bb1 Be8 20. Qc5 {
White was obviously worried by the attacking possibilities I had suddenly
acquired hopes for a Queen exchange. However the Queen is rather out of play
on C5.} Qf6 21. e4 {Opening a passage for his pieces to the KS.} fxe4 22. Bxe4
Bg6 {Either forcing off my Bad Bishop for his good one or 23.BxN which would
be quite good for me.} 23. Bxg6 (23. Bxd5) 23... Qxg6 24. Ne5 Qg5 {
Threatenening towin the exchange by 25.....Nf4 26.....Ne2+} 25. Qc2 Rf6 26.
Rce1 Rh6 27. Nf3 Qg4 28. Qe4 ({Better than} 28. Re4) 28... Nf4 29. Ne5 Qh4 30.
h3 ({I expected} 30. Nf3 {which seems easier for him.}) 30... Qg5 {Threatening
31......Nxh3+ Adjourned White [1hr 2'] Black [48']} 31. Kh2 {[sealed move]
Play resumed 30\11\62 Definately not the best.} (31. Kh1 $4 Nxh3 $19) (31. Re3
Nxh3+ 32. Rxh3 Rxh3 33. Nf3 Rxf3 34. Qxf3 Rf7 $17) (31. Ng4 Rg6 {best and if}
32. Ne5 Nxg2 $1 33. Nxg6 Nxe1+ 34. Kh2 (34. Kh1 Qxg6 35. Qxg6 hxg6 36. Rxe1 Kf7
$19) 34... Qxg6 35. Qxg6 hxg6 36. Rxe1 Kf7 $19) 31... Rc8 ({If} 31... Rh4 {then
} 32. Qf3 Z0 33. Qg3 {is good for White. Therefore I bring the other Rook into
play 31.....Rc8}) 32. Qf3 Rf8 33. Qg3 Rf5 (33... Qf5 34. Re3 Z0 35. Rf3 {
is good for White}) (33... Qxg3+ 34. fxg3 {Doesn't seem particularly marvelous
for Black.}) 34. Re4 ({Likewise} 34. Qxg5 {is not too hot for him.}) 34... Rhf6
{The Rook was beginning to become out of play on h6 also the Knight needed
protection after 35.QxQ} 35. Qxg5 Rxg5 36. g3 Nh5 {Threatening 37.....NxP} (
36... Ng6 {doesn't seem any better. I neede g6 for my Rook to defend the
e-pawn.}) 37. Ng4 (37. Nd7 Rf7) 37... Rf3 {Now I threaten 38.....NxP &.....RxaP
} (37... Rfg6 {Doesn't look too good.}) 38. Ne3 (38. Rxe6 $13) 38... Kf7 39.
Kg2 Rf4 40. Rxf4+ Nxf4+ 41. Kh2 Nd5 ({After} 41... Ng6 {I can try to force ....
e5 isn't particularly good as it doesn't prevent Nf5 .....e5 can be stopped by
f4.41.....Ng6 decentralises the Knight}) 42. Nc4 {Threatens 43.Nd6+, 43.Nh5
and 46.Nxb7} Nc7 {I can't defend the Pawn so counterattack.} 43. Nd6+ Ke7 44.
Nxb7 Nb5 45. Nc5 Nxa3 (45... Nxd4 {Wouldn't be too good as his d-pawn is weak
anyway and now his Pawns are isolated. Also I am threatening Nc2}) 46. Rc1 {
to stop 46.....Nc2} Nb5 47. Nxa6 Nxd4 {1 Aot of tactical threats. Uni A won 4 -
} 0-1

