1. c4 Nf6 2. g3 e5 3. Bg2 c6 4. d3 d5 5. Qc2 Bf5 {Obvious but not all that
good.} 6. e4 {This seems best, d5 isn't really weak} Be6 7. Nf3 Nbd7 (7... Bd6
8. c5 {Seems quite good for White.}) 8. O-O Bd6 9. Ng5 {Allows f5 and NxB
which seems better for me than him.} ({I can't play} 9. Nc3 {because of} dxc4)
9... Bg4 {Black decides to keep the Bishop despite moving ot for the 3rd time
and possibly losing a Pawn.} 10. cxd5 {This I thought would win a pawn or give
Black trouble in recovering it.} cxd5 11. exd5 ({I considered} 11. Qb3 {
but it's bad after...} Nc5) 11... Nb6 12. Nc3 Rc8 13. Re1 {Prevents 13.....Be2
and threatens 14.d4!} O-O 14. Bd2 Nbxd5 15. Bxd5 $2 (15. a3 $142 {preventing ..
..Bb4 or Nb4 would have been better here as I still have variuos threats})
15... Nxd5 16. d4 g6 17. dxe5 Bb4 {[22'] Winning back the Pawn as my Knight
needs the protection of the Bishop on d2} 18. Qe4 {[48']} Bxc3 19. bxc3 Nxc3
20. Bxc3 Qxg5 21. Bb4 Rfe8 22. Bd6 Rc6 23. h4 {I was short of time here} ({
looks better} 23. Rab1) 23... Qf5 24. Qxf5 Bxf5 25. Rac1 Rec8 26. Rxc6 Rxc6 27.
Rd1 Bg4 28. Rb1 (28. Rd3 {to prevent.....Be2. Then} Be2) 28... Bf3 29. Be7 b5
30. Bf6 {Now I can threaten mate on the back rank} b4 31. Kh2 a5 32. a3 Rb6 33.
Rb3 Be4 34. axb4 axb4 {I could probably win the b-Pawn but the game would
still be drawn Uni won 3.5 - 1.5} 1/2-1/2

