{Opponent info: Hampshire County Champion; Grade 6a (161-168 ECF)} 1. e4 e6 2.
d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. b4 cxd4 ({If} 6... cxb4 7. Nb5 bxa3+ 8.
c3 {with the better game after....} Z0 9. Bxa3 ({or} 9. Nd6+)) 7. Qxd4 $2 Bb6 {
The alternatives are better.} (7... Bc7) (7... Nc6 8. Qg4 Bc7 $1 9. f4 Kf8 {
Followed by...} 10. Z0 a5) 8. Qg4 Kf8 9. Bd3 Qc7 10. Nge2 Qxe5 {The
alternatives would be more prudent.} (10... Nc6) (10... f5) 11. Bf4 f5 $4 {
Showing how completely out of form I was. A ridiculous move.} 12. Qg3 Qf6 13.
Bxb8 Ne7 {I decided not to resign but to try for a despairing KS attack.} 14.
Bd6 Bd7 15. O-O Rg8 16. Rfe1 g5 17. Be5 Qf7 18. Nb5 Bxb5 19. Bxb5 f4 20. Qh3
Nf5 21. Rad1 g4 22. Qc3 f3 23. Nd4 (23. gxf3 gxf3+ 24. Ng3 Nxg3 25. Bxg3 h5 {
is not as good.}) 23... g3 24. hxg3 ({I expected} 24. Nxe6+ Ke7) 24... Nxd4 25.
Rxd4 {Threatens 26.Rf4} Bxd4 26. Bd6+ Kg7 27. Qxd4+ Kg6 28. Bd3+ Kh6 29. Bf4+
Rg5 30. Bxg5+ Kxg5 31. Qh4# {What a fiasco! This was my first match for the
University (after 3 months holiday) and I was hopelessly out of form and
practice. The match was drawn.} 1-0

