1. c4 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. Nc3 c6 5. e4 {Prevents.....d5} Qc7 6. d4 d6 7.
Nge2 Nbd7 (7... e5 {Seems more forcing.}) 8. O-O O-O 9. h3 {Prevents .....Ng4
after Be3} Re8 (9... e5 {immediately seems better, possibly}) 10. Be3 Nb6 {
This definately seems doubtful and .....e5 shouls have been played. The Knight
only gets in the way on b6.} (10... e5) 11. Qd3 Be6 {Black seems determined
not to play .....e5 and this doesn't help.} 12. d5 {Obvious and good.} cxd5 13.
cxd5 ({I considered} 13. Nb5 {here but it's not so good.}) 13... Bd7 14. b3 {
Preventing 14.....Nc4 and threatening a4 still further limiting Blacks scope.}
Qc8 $2 {Not very good. The Queen is very badly placed here as c8 is needed for
a Rook and this b6 Knight has no retreat squares.} 15. Kh2 Nh5 {Intending .....
f5 but .....e6 seems to free his position more.} 16. a4 {Threatens to win the
Knight.} Qd8 17. g4 {I control the whole board and Black is forced back on
both wings.} Nf6 18. a5 Nc8 19. f4 {Threatens 20.e5} e5 {At last.} 20. f5 {
Threatening g5 followed by f6} Ne7 $2 {Loses a piece but his position was very
difficult.} ({If} 20... gxf5 21. exf5 $1) 21. g5 Nxf5 22. exf5 Bxf5 23. Rxf5
gxf5 24. gxf6 Qxf6 {Black could resign, though he has slight chances.} 25. Rg1
Kh8 26. Bd2 {Rearranging my pieces.} e4 27. Qe3 Qd8 28. Qg5 Be5+ 29. Kh1 (29.
Nf4 $4 Qxg5) 29... Qd7 30. Bf4 Bxf4 31. Qf6+ Kg8 32. Nxf4 Kf8 33. Bf1 a6 {
Prevents 34.Bb5} 34. Nh5 $1 Rac8 {He can't prevent mate.} 35. Rg8+ Kxg8 36.
Qg7# {A good game.} 1-0

