1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. O-O e5 5. d3 f6 {The saemisch variation
reversed.} 6. c4 Be6 {This doesn't turn out too well.} (6... d4) (6... dxc4) 7.
cxd5 Bxd5 8. Nc3 Nge7 9. Qa4 (9. Nxd5 Nxd5 10. Qb3 {Threatening 11.NxP}) 9...
Be6 {This loses time.} 10. Be3 Nd5 {Now my QKnight is weakened and I can't
play .....b6} 11. Nd2 Qd7 (11... Rc8 {may be better.}) 12. Rac1 b6 13. Nxd5
Bxd5 14. Bxd5 Qxd5 15. b4 {Winning a Pawn. I had played the opening rather
lethargically.} Kf7 {I shall have to move the Bishop next move and I want to
connect the Rooks.} 16. bxc5 Bxc5 17. Ne4 Nd4 18. Bxd4 Qxd4 ({If} 18... Bxd4
19. Rc7+ ({or} 19. e3)) 19. Rc4 Qd5 (19... Qb2 {Doesn't achieve much and the
Queen is out of play.}) 20. Nxc5 bxc5 21. Rfc1 Rhc8 22. Qa3 {best.} (22. Qb5) (
22. Rb1) 22... Kg6 {The King seems safer here than on the 1st & 2nd Ranks.} 23.
Rxc5 Rxc5 24. Rxc5 Qb7 (24... Qd4 {seems no better.}) 25. Qc1 Rb8 26. a4 {
With a possible threat of 27.Rb5} a6 27. Qc4 Qa8 {Threatening 28.....Rb1+} 28.
Qg4+ Kh6 29. Qh4+ Kg6 30. Qg4+ Kh6 {White was short of time here.} 31. e4 {
Removing the mating threat but leaving the d-Pawn weak.} Qa7 {The threat was
32Rb7} 32. Rd5 Rb7 33. Qh4+ Kg6 34. g4 h6 35. Rd8 $2 ({Much better seems...} 
35. Qh5+ Kh7 36. Qf5+ g6 37. Qxf6) 35... Kh7 36. Qg3 Rd7 37. Re8 Re7 38. Rxe7 {
[Adjourned]} Qxe7 39. Qf3 Qb4 $6 {The result of not analysing the adjourned
position. I now lose a Pawn but not necessarily the game.} (39... g6 {seemed a
good alternative.}) 40. Qf5+ Kg8 41. Qc8+ Kh7 42. Qxa6 Qb3 {The best chance. I
now threaten to draw by perpetual check.} 43. h3 h5 44. gxh5 ({Not} 44. f3 Qd1+
45. Kf2 Qd2+ 46. Kg3 $4 h4+ 47. Kxh4 Qf2+ 48. Kh5 g6#) 44... Qd1+ 45. Kg2 Qxh5
46. Qe6 Qd1 47. Qf5+ Kh6 48. h4 $2 (48. Qd7 {Would have won easily.}) 48...
Qxa4 {If 49.h5 Qe8} 1/2-1/2

