1. c4 f5 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. g3 d6 5. Nf3 Bg7 6. Bg2 O-O 7. O-O d5 {This
transposition into a Stonewall doesn't seem too good. Black would do better to
force .....e5} 8. c5 {Gaining space on the QS. I also considered......} (8. b3)
(8. Qd3) (8. Ne5) 8... e6 9. b4 c6 10. Bg5 Nbd7 11. a4 (11. b5 {Was playable.})
11... Qc7 {Draws the White QBishop onto a better diagonal} 12. Bf4 Qd8 13. b5 (
13. Nd2 {First looks good.}) 13... Ne4 (13... cxb5 {would be semi-suicidal.})
14. Qc2 Nxc3 15. Qxc3 Nf6 16. Ne5 {Again 16.Nd2 seems better here. I had
considered this but played the whole game rather too hurriedly} Bd7 17. f3 Nh5
18. Nxd7 Nxf4 19. gxf4 Qxd7 20. Rab1 {I have rather the better of it as I am
not weak on the KS and have the better of it on the opposite wing.} Rfb8 (20...
Rab8 {leaves his a-Pawn weak.}) 21. e3 {Strengthening the Pawns and allowing
Rf2 & Bf1} a6 22. b6 {In blocking off the position like this I had seen the
sacrifice on a6. I also considered 22.Rf2 and if Black exchanges I soon regain
the Pawn with the better position due to Black's b-Pawn.} Kf7 23. a5 Rh8 24.
Rf2 Bf6 25. Bf1 h6 26. Bd3 g5 27. fxg5 Bxg5 28. f4 Bf6 (28... Bh4 {seems
better as the Bishop gets in the way on f6.}) 29. Qd2 Rag8+ 30. Kh1 Rg7 31. Qe2
Ke7 32. Bxa6 {My best winning chance.} Ra8 (32... bxa6 33. Qxa6 {Seems very
bad for Black.}) 33. Bxb7 Qxb7 34. Ra1 Ra6 {More or less forced.} 35. Qh5 {
Black suddenly discovers he is in trouble on both wings.} Rh7 36. Qg6 Rh8 37.
Rg2 {Threatening 38.Qg7+} Qa8 38. b7 $1 {A surprise for Black.} Qb8 ({
Naturally not...} 38... Qxb7 39. Qg7+) 39. Rb2 Rf8 {This doesn't turn out too
well.} 40. Qxh6 Kd7 $2 41. Qh5 $4 {Played without due consideration.} (41. Qxf8
{Would win easily. I was playing too quickly.}) 41... Bd8 42. Qe2 (42. Qh7+ {
May be better.}) 42... Rxa5 43. Rxa5 Bxa5 44. Qa6 Qc7 45. Ra2 Be1 46. Rg2 Bh4
47. Rb2 Rb8 48. Rb1 Bd8 49. Rb6 Bh4 {I was playing too quickly (as usual) and
should have seen 42.QxR} 1/2-1/2

