1. e3 c5 2. Nf3 g6 3. c3 Bg7 4. d4 {White appears to be transposing into some
sort of Colle System} Qc7 5. Nbd2 b6 6. Qb3 Nf6 7. Ne5 {This followed by 8.f4
if Black had already played .....d5} O-O 8. Bc4 e6 9. O-O d6 {Now Black gains
several tempi.} 10. Nef3 d5 11. Be2 c4 12. Qc2 Nc6 {preventing 13.Ne5} 13. e4 {
His best chance gaining space.} dxe4 14. Nxe4 Nxe4 15. Qxe4 Bb7 16. Qh4 b5 {
White does well if he can play Bh6.} ({If} 16... Ne7 17. Bf4 {Black can't
defend the c-Pawn and Knight.} (17. Bh6 {is prevented due to} Nf5)) 17. Ng5 h6
18. Ne4 Qe7 19. Qh3 Nxd4 {This secures Black a slight advantage.} 20. cxd4 Bxe4
21. Bxh6 Qb4 22. Bxg7 Kxg7 23. Qe3 Bd5 24. Rab1 Rac8 25. a3 Qd6 26. Qe5+ {
So as to get rid of his weak d-Pawn but Black still has the advantage of a QS
Pawn majority} Qxe5 27. dxe5 a6 28. Rbc1 Rc5 29. f4 Rfc8 30. Bf3 (30. Rc3 {
Seems a good alternative.}) 30... c3 31. b4 {This gives Black a passed Pawn.} (
31. bxc3 {is not very good.}) 31... Rc4 32. Bxd5 exd5 33. Rfd1 Rxf4 (33... d4 {
is not so clear}) 34. Rxd5 c2 35. Rd2 ({If} 35. Rd6 Re4 36. Rxa6 Rxe5 37. Rd6
Re3 38. Rd2 Rxa3 39. Rdxc2 Rxc2 40. Rxc2 Rb3) 35... Rfc4 36. Kf2 Kf8 37. Kf1
Rc3 {Prevents Rd3 & Kd2} 38. Ke2 Rxa3 {This seems best.} 39. Rdxc2 Rxc2+ 40.
Rxc2 Rb3 41. e6 ({If} 41. Rc6 Rxb4 42. Rxa6 Re4+ 43. Kd3 Rxe5) 41... Rxb4 (
41... fxe6 42. Rc6) 42. exf7 Kxf7 43. Rc7+ Kf8 44. Rc6 a5 45. Rxg6 a4 46. Rg3
Rb2+ 47. Kd1 b4 48. Kc1 a3 49. h4 b3 50. h5 $2 {This loses outright.} ({
White could still draw by....} 50. Rc3 $1 {Preventing my check on the next
move.}) 50... Rc2+ 51. Kd1 (51. Kb1 a2+ 52. Ka1 Rc1+ 53. Kb2 Rb1+) 51... Rxg2
$1 (51... a2 52. Rxb3 a1=Q+ 53. Kxc2 {and Black's win is very difficult.}) 52.
Rxg2 (52. Rxb3 a2 53. Ra3 a1=Q+ 54. Rxa1 Rg1+) 52... a2 53. h6 a1=Q+ 54. Ke2
Qa2+ 55. Kf1 Qxg2+ 56. Kxg2 b2 57. h7 Kg7 0-1

