1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. d4 d6 4. exd6 cxd6 {This was the first time I had
played Alekhines Defence in a match and didn't know the variations too well.
After this move I envisaged reaching a sort of sicillian position.} 5. Nf3 g6
6. Bc4 Nf6 (6... Nb6 {Gains a tempo but the Knight is in the way here.}) 7. O-O
d5 $2 {I had doubts about this move but still played it as it seems quite
agressive. However it allows Ne5 and therefore 7.....Bg7 was better.} (7... Bg7
$142) 8. Be2 {This is good...} ({Also good would be....} 8. Bb5+ Bd7 9. Bxd7+ {
Black seems obliged to play} Nbxd7 {when the d7 Knight is not so well placed.})
8... Bg7 9. c4 O-O 10. Nc3 dxc4 {or else White plays 11.c5} 11. Bxc4 Qc7 {
I was not at all happy with my position hereabouts.} 12. Be2 a6 13. Bg5 {
This surprised me I had expected 13.Ne5 followed by f4 and possibly Bf3 with a
very strong position for White.} (13. Ne5 Z0 14. f4 Z0 15. Bf3) 13... b5 14.
Rc1 Qd8 ({If} 14... Qb6 15. Bxf6 Z0 16. Ne5 {is good for White}) 15. a3 {
This is unnecessary} (15. Ne5 {Would still be strong.}) 15... Bb7 16. Qd2 Nbd7
17. Rfe1 e6 18. Qf4 Qb6 (18... Qb8 19. Qh4) 19. Ne5 {Better late than never.}
Rac8 {straightforward development seems best} 20. Bf3 ({Rather more
enterprising seems} 20. h4) 20... Bxf3 21. Nxf3 Qb7 22. Bh6 {here he offered a
draw which I accepted. These matches (2 - 2.5 hrs) are too short to allow many
definite results.} 1/2-1/2

