1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e3 c6 6. Nf3 Qa5 7. Qc2 Bb4 8. Bxf6
Nxf6 ({I considered....} 8... gxf6 {but it's a bit loosening.}) 9. Nd2 dxc4 (
9... c5 {seems a good alternative, probably better.}) 10. Nxc4 Qg5 11. a3 Be7 (
{I didn't play this..} 11... Bxc3+ {as I didn't want to allow...} 12. bxc3 Z0
13. Nd6+) 12. g3 h5 {Aggressive, but it may have been better to let White
castle K-Side before showing my attacking intentions.} 13. h4 {This seems best.
} Qh6 14. Bg2 g5 15. hxg5 Qxg5 16. Bf3 {Probably to unpin the g-Pawn (after ...
..h5 for example) and putting pressure on my h-Pawn.} Bd7 {After much thought.
I was somewhat stuck here. I didn't want to move my Knight as it allows Knight
e4.} (16... Nd5 17. Ne4) (16... Ng4 17. Ne4) 17. b4 {To prevent an eventual ...
..c5} Rd8 (17... O-O-O {is much too dsngerous e.g.} 18. b5 cxb5 $2 19. Nxb5
Bxb5 20. Nd6+ {etc.}) 18. Ne4 Nxe4 19. Qxe4 Bc8 20. Qe5 {White decides to
exchangeoff now that I cover d6 with my Rook and can bring my KBishop into
play.} Qxe5 21. Nxe5 h4 {or else I lose the h-Pawn.} 22. gxh4 Bxh4 ({Not...} 
22... Rxh4 23. Rxh4 Bxh4 24. Bh5 {Draw agreed as we had won the match.})
1/2-1/2

