1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 Nf6 3. c4 e6 4. d4 dxc4 5. Qa4+ Bd7 6. Qxc4 Bc6 7. Nf3 Bd5 8.
Qa4+ Nbd7 9. Nc3 Bc6 10. Qc2 {As a result of these somewhat unusual opening
manoeuvres I have some advantage as I can control the centre and my minor
pieces are better than Blacks.} Be7 11. O-O O-O 12. e4 Qe8 {Rather cramping
unless she intended an eventual .....e5} (12... Nb6 {seems better.}) 13. Rd1
Rd8 {Again too cramping and the Qs is left weak.} 14. Bf4 b6 $2 {This loses
after a neat finish.} ({If now.....} 14... Rc8 {I intended} 15. a3 {followed by
} Z0 16. e5 {and...} Z0 17. Ne4 {with a strong innitiative.}) 15. d5 $1 ({Not} 
15. Bxc7 Rc8 16. Bf4 Bxe4) 15... exd5 ({No better is} 15... Bb7 16. dxe6 fxe6
17. Ng5 Nc5 18. e5 {etc.}) 16. exd5 Bb7 17. Bxc7 Rc8 18. d6 {A neat little
game.} (18. d6 {if....} Bd8 19. Re1 {etc.}) 1-0

