1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. Nxe5
{As in Bronstein - Pachman Interzonal 1958} Na5 ({Pachman played.....} 8...
Nxe5) 9. Nd2 Be6 {Doubtful in view of 10.f4 then f5} 10. f4 Nxb3 11. axb3 {
The a-file will prove useful.} Be7 12. Qe2 {Threatening 13.RxP!} Nxd2 13. Bxd2
c5 $2 {Loses at least a Pawn but he had it very difficult.} (13... O-O $2 14.
Nc6 Qd7 15. Nxe7+ Qxe7 16. f5 {wins a piece}) (13... Bd7 {offered a temporary
solution.}) 14. Rxa6 $1 {Better than 14.Nc6 etc below.} (14. Nc6 Qd7 15. Nxe7
Qxe7 16. f5 Bd7 17. Qxe7+ Kxe7 18. dxc5) 14... O-O $2 {hastens the end.} 15.
Nc6 Qe8 16. Nxe7+ Qxe7 17. Rxa8 Rxa8 18. f5 Ra6 19. Qxb5 Bc8 20. Re1 Kf8 21.
Rxe7 Kxe7 22. Qxc5+ Kd7 23. Qxd5+ {White won the game in the opening. Black
was lost after about 13 moves.} 1-0

