1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 d6 3. g3 f5 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. d4 e4 6. f3 exf3 7. Nxf3 Be7 {
I played this in preference to 7......g6 as has been played by Tal, as Barden
says .....Be7 is better. I can't say I agree.} 8. b3 O-O 9. O-O Nbd7 10. Qc2 g6
{Again according to Barden} 11. Bh6 Re8 (11... Rf7 $4 12. Ng5) 12. Rad1 Ng4 13.
Bf4 Bf8 14. e4 fxe4 15. Nxe4 Ndf6 16. Nxf6+ Nxf6 17. Nh4 Kg7 {To prevent 18.NxP
} 18. Qc3 h6 19. Bc1 g5 20. Qd2 $1 c6 21. Nf5+ Kg8 22. h4 $1 Bxf5 23. Rxf5 g4
$6 24. Qf4 Bg7 25. d5 c5 {Forced.} 26. Bb2 Rf8 27. Bxf6 Rxf6 28. Rf1 {For this
move I set up the position by playing through the game but left out 27......
RxB and hence I thought that my Rook at f5 was at f8 ..........Therefore:} Qe7
$4 29. Rxf6 {Rather an unfortunate way to lose a game, although things weren't
going too well anyway.} 1-0

