1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. f4 Nc6 7. Be3 Bg7 8. h3
h5 {A doubtful move weakening the KS and making castling very dangerous.} 9.
Qd2 a6 10. O-O-O Qc7 11. Nf3 {I intended to take advantage of Black's
black-square weaknesses on the KS. Also exerting pressure on the d-file.} Bd7 {
Black now gets into some trouble.} 12. Ng5 {Prevents 10.....0-0-0 and
threatening 11.Na4 - Nb6 or Nc5 as the e-Pawn is now defended.} Rc8 {Now he
becomes very cramped.} 13. Bc4 Nd8 14. Bb3 Bc6 15. f5 {Opening the
positiononto the Black King.} b5 {Rather an ill times advance.} 16. Qf2 {
Threatening 17.Bb6 followed by BxN also to open the KS and gain pressure on
the f-file.} a5 $2 {Suicidal but Black was probably lost anyway.} 17. Bb6 Qb7
18. Bxd8 Rxd8 19. Nxf7 {Alternatives are also good.} (19. Bxf7+) (19. fxg6)
19... Nxe4 20. Nxe4 Bxe4 21. Nxh8 Bxh8 22. fxg6 Bxg6 23. Be6 b4 24. Bf5 Bf7 25.
Rhf1 Bf6 26. Qg3 Qb5 27. Bg6 $2 {Carelessness due to overconfidence with the
result that an easy win becomes a maze of complications.} Bg5+ 28. Kb1 Bxg6 29.
h4 Rc8 (29... Qc4 {was a plausible alternative.}) 30. Ka1 Bxc2 31. Rde1 ({
I considered} 31. hxg5 {here but the passed Pawn isn't strong enough.}) 31...
Bd2 $6 ({Black may well to give back the Bishop by} 31... Bxh4) 32. Rxe7+ $1 {
Everything else seems a dead loss} Kxe7 33. Qg7+ Ke6 $2 ({Better is...} 33...
Kd8 34. Rf8+ Qe8 {Now he loses his Queen (the point of the combination)}) 34.
Qf7+ Ke5 35. Qxh5+ Kd4 36. Qxb5 Bd3 37. Qb6+ Ke5 38. Qxa5+ Rc5 {This just
hastens the end.} 39. Qxc5+ dxc5 40. Rd1 Kf4 41. Rxd2 c4 42. a3 Ke3 43. Rd1 Ke2
44. axb4 $1 Kxd1 45. b5 Ke2 (45... c3 46. bxc3 Bxb5 47. h5 Kc2 48. h6 Bd3 49.
c4 {etc.}) 46. b6 Be4 47. h5 Bxg2 48. h6 {As usual I had played carelessly due
to overconfidence but I played well from move 30 onwards. I now lead the
tournament with 3/3 (I had a win by default in Rd 2.)} 1-0

