{Opponent info: Grade 5a (177-184 ECF)} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Ne2 dxe4 4. Ng3 f5
5. Bc4 Nf6 6. c3 Bd6 7. O-O Bxg3 8. fxg3 Nd5 9. g4 O-O 10. gxf5 exf5 11. Qb3 c6
12. a4 b6 13. Na3 Be6 14. Nc2 g5 15. Ne3 f4 16. Nc2 Qd6 {Due to White's
peculiar opening play I have a won position.} 17. Nb4 Rf6 {so as to defend the
Bishop and move the Knight.} 18. g3 f3 {Giving back the Pawn to gain an
overwhelming position.} 19. Bxg5 Rg6 20. Bxd5 cxd5 21. Bh4 ({Not} 21. Be3 $2
Rxg3+ $3) ({or..} 21. Bd2 $2 Rxg3+ $3) 21... Nc6 ({if...} 21... Qf4 22. Kh1 {
Threatening 23.NxP}) 22. Nxc6 Qxc6 23. Qc2 Qc7 24. Qd2 Rf8 25. Kf2 Rf5 26. Ke1
Rh5 27. Qf2 Rxh4 $6 {Whether this is sound or not I don't know, but I played
it without a moments hesitation and without working out any variations heaven
knows why. I should have concentrated more but for some reason played too
impetuously.} 28. gxh4 Rg2 29. Rg1 Bh3 30. Kd2 ({If} 30. Rxg2+ Bxg2 31. Qg3+
Qg7) 30... Qf4+ 31. Kc2 e3 32. Rxg2+ Bxg2 33. Qg1 Qxh4 $4 {Again played
without any consideration.} ({I had an easy win by......} 33... Qe4+ 34. Kc1 f2
) 34. Qxe3 Qe4+ $2 {Again without any thought.} (34... Qxh2 $142) 35. Kd2 Kf7
36. Qxe4 dxe4 37. Ke3 Ke6 38. c4 Bh3 39. a5 Kd6 {I was playing so hastily I
didn't have time to resign.} 40. axb6 axb6 41. b4 Bf5 42. c5+ bxc5 43. dxc5+
Kc6 44. Ra6+ Kc7 45. Rf6 Bg6 46. h4 Kb7 47. b5 Kc7 48. Rc6+ Kb7 49. Re6 Bf5 50.
Re7+ Kb8 51. h5 Kc8 52. c6 {A terrible mess, I had an easily won game but
impetuosity lost it. I didn't concentrate at all. (My time, for 52 moves -
under an hour!!)} 0-1

