1. c4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. c5 e5 {Equalising.} 4. e3 e4 5. Ne2 f5 6. Nf4 Nf6 7. Be2
Be7 8. Nc3 c6 9. b4 O-O 10. Bd2 {White is going through the most peculiar
manoeuvres} g5 11. Nh3 h6 12. f4 g4 13. Nf2 Kh7 14. g3 Rg8 15. a4 h5 16. h4 {
Blocking off the KS completely. Had I not advanced so quickly he probably
wouldn't have been able to do this.} Be6 17. Qb3 Nbd7 (17... a6 $142) 18. b5
Rb8 19. Nfd1 Qc8 {Envisaging a possible 20 .....NxP 21.PxN d4} 20. bxc6 bxc6
21. Qc2 Ne8 22. Na2 Bd8 23. Nb4 Ba5 24. Na6 Bxd2+ 25. Kxd2 Rb7 26. a5 Nc7 27.
Nc3 Nb8 28. Nxb8 Qxb8 29. Rhb1 a6 30. Qa4 Bd7 31. Rb6 Nb5 32. Rb1 Qa7 {Rather
an odd game. I think I advanced too quickly on the KS.} 1/2-1/2

