1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. c3 Qb6 6. Be2 cxd4 (6... Nge7 {
is more usual}) 7. cxd4 Bb4+ 8. Nc3 Nge7 9. a3 Bxc3+ 10. bxc3 Bd7 {I didn't
fancy castling straight into a big attack so I bided my time.} 11. O-O Na5 {
Still biding my time and the Knight is well placed here.} 12. a4 $1 {His
Bishop will be very powerful on a3} Qc7 13. Bb2 Ng6 14. g3 {A quiet purposeful
move preventing 14.....Nf4} Bc6 15. Nd2 b6 {Intending .....Bb7 & .....Nc4 and
if BxN or NxN then .....PxB or N} 16. f4 Ne7 17. g4 g6 18. Ba3 {very strong.}
Bb7 19. Bb5+ Bc6 20. Bd3 Bb7 21. Bb5+ Bc6 22. Bd6 {White had gained time on
the clock here.} Qd7 23. Bd3 Nb7 24. Bb4 h5 ({An alternative 'Semi-desperado'
line was.....} 24... a5 25. Ba3 b5 {gaining some space.}) 25. h3 hxg4 26. hxg4
Qd8 27. Nf3 Kf8 $2 {Intending tobring my King to g7 but this is unsound. My
opponent said he thought I had a draw by just staying put but I hadn't fancied
this. I had rather underestimated my chances in a passive defence but this
would have been better.} 28. Kf2 Kg7 $2 29. f5 $1 Nxf5 (29... exf5 30. gxf5
gxf5 31. Bxf5 Nxf5 32. Rg1+ {and the f8 square is covered. however this is
little different to the game.}) 30. gxf5 exf5 31. Bxf5 $1 f6 32. Rg1 {Passsive
defence would have been better. Hayes lost 3.5 - 4.5} 1-0

