1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 dxe5 6. fxe5 Nc6 7. Be3 Bf5 8. Nc3
e6 9. Nf3 Qd7 10. Be2 O-O-O 11. O-O Bg4 {(R.A.C. v Inwood Book 6 [Game 339])}
12. c5 {he found this correct move after 25 mins thought.} Nd5 13. Nxd5 Qxd5
14. h3 {Looks better for White.} ({M.C.O. gives...} 14. Ng5 {with advantage,
however...} Bxe2 15. Qxe2 Nxd4 {All the following are at least equal for Black.
} 16. Qd2 (16. Qd1 Qxe5 17. Bxd4 ({If..} 17. Nxf7 Qxe3+ 18. Kh1 Bxc5) 17...
Qxg5 {Threats 18.....Bxc5 & .....e5.}) (16. Qe1 Nc2) (16. Qg4 h5 $1 17. Qh3 Nf5
18. Bf2 Rd7) (16. Qf2 Nf5) (16. Qh5 Qxe5) 16... Nf5 17. Nxf7 (17. Qxd5 Rxd5 18.
Bf2 Bxc5 19. Bxc5 Rxc5 20. Nxf7 Rf8 21. Ng5 Rxe5 {etc.}) 17... Qxd2 18. Bxd2
Rxd2 19. Nxh8 Bxc5+ 20. Kh1 Rxb2) 14... Bf5 ({Not.....} 14... Bxf3 15. Bxf3 Qd7
16. Bxc6 Qxc6 17. Rxf7) 15. Qd2 h6 {To prevent 16.Ng5} 16. b4 {Now White gets
a terrific attack. My best may well be to bring the King back to the KS} f6 (
16... g5 {seems too slow.}) 17. b5 Ne7 18. Rfc1 ({If} 18. Qa5 Qe4) 18... c6 19.
Qa5 Kb8 20. exf6 $1 {Opening the Black diagonal at just the right moment.} gxf6
21. Bf4+ Ka8 22. Rc3 ({If he were to play} 22. b6 Nc8 23. bxa7 {then I can do
well Leaving his Pawn on a7.}) 22... Nc8 23. Qc7 e5 24. bxc6 $1 (24. dxe5 Bxc5+
25. Kh1 Bb6) (24. Nxe5 Qxd4+) 24... bxc6 25. Rb3 Bd6 {played instead of
resigning.} ({I now intended....} 25... Nb6 26. cxb6 Rh7 {but this was
unplayable due to.....} 27. b7#) 26. Rb8# {Not too good, although I'm not sure
where I went wrong.} 1-0

