1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. e3 Bg7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Bd3 b6 7. O-O Bb7 8. b3
Nbd7 9. Bb2 c5 10. Rc1 Ne4 11. cxd5 Nxc3 12. Bxc3 Bxd5 13. Qe2 e5 $2 {This was
one of my super overconfidence days when I expected to win easily. This move
which is very doubtful gives up a Pawn for piece freedom and the d-file} 14.
Nxe5 Nxe5 15. dxe5 Qe7 16. e4 Bc6 17. f4 Rad8 18. f5 Bxe5 {This probably loses
with best play but was the best chance.} 19. f6 Bxh2+ (19... Qd6 {Probably
loses prety quickly.}) 20. Kxh2 (20. Kh1 Qd6 21. Z0 Rfe8 22. Z0 Qf8) 20... Qd6+
21. e5 Qxd3 22. Qg4 Qe4 23. Rf4 Qd5 24. Rg1 Kh8 ({Very bad seems} 24... h5) ({
or...} 24... h6) 25. Qg5 Qd3 {Whilst I am in a lost position, this offers the
best chance.} 26. Qh6 Rg8 27. Rh4 $2 {Missing his chance.} (27. Qxh7+ $3 {
Wins straight off.}) 27... g5 {The move on which I had been relying.} 28. Rh3
Qg6 $2 {The losing move, about which I hardly gave any thought.} (28... Qf5 {
witha comfortable win is best.}) 29. Qxg6 Rxg6 30. e6 $1 fxe6 {To allow 31.e7
is just as bad.} 31. f7+ Rg7 32. Rf1 Rf8 33. Rh5 {The move I had missed.} Be4
34. Rxg5 Bg6 35. Rf3 a6 {I'm in Zugzwang} 36. Kg1 $2 ({Now he misses the
decisive} 36. Rxg6 $1) 36... a5 37. a3 b5 38. b4 cxb4 39. axb4 axb4 40. Bd4 b3
41. Kf2 b4 42. Ke3 b2 43. Bxb2 b3 44. Kf2 e5 {Relieving the threat of 45.RxB
which White missed for 9 consecutive moves. Not that it makes any difference.}
45. Bxe5 Bxf7 46. Bxg7+ Kg8 47. Bxf8+ Kxf8 48. Rgf5 b2 {I thoughtI might as
well let him mate me.} 49. Rxf7+ Kg8 50. Rb7 h5 51. Rxb2 {Waste of time} h4 52.
Rb7 h3 53. gxh3 Kh8 54. Ra3 $2 1-0

