1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bc4 e6 7. Bb3 Be7 8.
Be3 a6 9. f4 Na5 10. Qf3 Nxb3 11. cxb3 {It seemed to me I would be able to
utilise the c-file before Black.} e5 12. Nde2 {[6']} Bd7 (12... Bg4 {seems
better as now I get in f5.}) 13. f5 Bc6 14. Rd1 {preventing 14.....d5} Qa5 {
Threatening 15......NxP} 15. O-O {[10']} h5 {in oreder to prevent 16.g4, 17.g5}
16. a3 Rc8 17. b4 {[14']} Qc7 18. Rc1 {Threatening 19.Nd5 etc.} Qb8 19. Bb6 Nd7
20. Bf2 Nf6 21. Rfd1 {[20']} b5 22. Bh4 {All this positional meandering has
gained me an advantage.} Ng4 ({Not...} 22... Nxe4 23. Nxe4 Bxh4 24. Rxc6 Rxc6
25. Nf6+ Bxf6 26. Qxc6+ {with a huge advantage. White may even have better
moves than these.}) 23. Bf2 (23. Bxe7 Qb6+ {etc.}) 23... Bg5 24. Rb1 {Black
appears to be gaining an upper hand , but in fact he still has the worst of it.
} Nxf2 {Eliminating the Knight which he could use to cover d5} 25. Qxf2 h4 26.
Rd3 Bd8 {He was now in time trouble} 27. Kh1 Bb6 {Better is to keep the Bishop
defending the h-Pawn.} 28. Qf3 f6 29. Qg4 Qc7 30. Rh3 Qb7 {[74']} 31. Rxh4 {
[40']} Rxh4 32. Qxh4 Qf7 33. Rd1 Ke7 34. Qg3 Rh8 35. h3 Rd8 36. Qd3 Qg8 37. Ng3
{Intending...... Adjourned. Play resumed 5/3/63} Bd4 {[sealed move] Play
resumed 5/3/63} ({If...} 37... g5 $4 38. fxg6 Qxg6 39. Nf5+ {etc.}) (37... Qh8
38. Nd5+ {etc.}) (37... Qb3 38. Rd2 Bd4 39. Nge2) (37... Qc4 38. Nge2 Qxd3 39.
Rxd3 {and advance on the KS.}) 38. Nge2 Ba7 39. a4 {This move which wasn't too
good with Black's Bishop on b6 is now strong.} Qc4 40. Qxc4 bxc4 41. b5 axb5
42. axb5 Bxe4 $1 {This move which took me completely by surprise seems his
best chance.} (42... Bd7 43. Nd5+ Kf7 44. b6) (42... Ba8 43. Ra1) (42... Bb7
43. Ra1) 43. Nxe4 d5 44. N2c3 $1 {Giving back the piece to secure a won
endgame. If the attacked Knight moves Black has good chances.} dxe4 (44... d4
45. Na4 {is good.}) 45. Rxd8 Kxd8 46. Nxe4 Bd4 47. Nd2 c3 48. bxc3 Bxc3 49. Nc4
Bd4 50. g4 Kd7 ({After...} 50... e4 {he would probably lose the Pawn.}) 51. Kg2
Ke7 {Black can do nothing.} 52. Kf3 Kd7 53. Ke4 Ke7 54. h4 Kd7 55. g5 fxg5 56.
hxg5 Ke7 57. Nxe5 1-0

