1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 c5 7. Bc4 Bg7 8.
Ne2 O-O 9. O-O cxd4 10. cxd4 Nc6 11. Bb2 (11. Be3 {is more usual here.}) 11...
b6 12. Bb3 $2 {Now he gets into tremendous difficulties.} Ba6 {Threatens 13....
..BxN followed by winning the d-Pawn.} 13. Bd5 {This seems the only move.} Rc8
{again threatening ....BxN} 14. Re1 {Apparently saving the Pawn.} ({if....} 14.
Bxc6 Rxc6 15. d5 ({however....} 15. e5 $142 {although after.....} Bh6 {Black
is still on top.}) 15... Bxb2 16. dxc6 {wins a piece.}) 14... Nb4 $1 15. Qa4 {
The only move although he is probably lost anyway.} (15. Rc1 Nd3 16. Rxc8 Qxc8
{etc.}) (15. Nc3 Nd3 16. Re2 Nxb2 17. Rxb2 Rxc3) 15... Nxd5 16. exd5 (16. Qxa6
Nb4 {Queen moves then ......Nc2}) 16... Bb7 17. Nf4 Qd6 $1 18. Nd3 ({If} 18.
Qxa7 Qxf4 19. Qxb7 Rc2 {etc.}) 18... Qxd5 19. f3 Rc4 $1 20. Qxa7 (20. Qd1 {
Seems no improvement.}) 20... Bxd4+ 21. Bxd4 Qxd4+ 22. Nf2 {Overlooking my
23rd move.} ({but after....} 22. Kh1 Bxf3 {He is just as badly off.}) 22... Rc2
23. Rf1 Rxf2 $1 24. Rxf2 (24. Qxb7 Rxa2+ {etc.}) 24... Qxa1+ 25. Rf1 Qd4+ 26.
Kh1 Qd3 27. Kg1 Qa6 28. Qxa6 Bxa6 29. Rb1 Rc8 30. h4 Rc6 0-1

