1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 e5 $2 {Without any hesitation
I played White's moves against the grunfeld. I should have realised that the
extra move would make a difference.} 6. Nxc6 bxc6 7. c4 {Winnning a pawn.} Bc5
8. Nc3 {White is in no hurry to take the Pawn.} Qb6 $2 {Trying to hang on to
the Pawn, I should have just continued my development.} 9. O-O dxc4 10. Na4 {
White now has a won game and it's just a matter of time before I resign.} Qb5
11. Nxc5 Qxc5 12. Be3 Qb5 13. Qd6 Ne7 14. Rfd1 Be6 15. Bg5 f6 {The
alternatives 15.......Resigns} (15... O-O 16. Bxe7) (15... Qb7 16. Bxe7 Z0 17.
Bxc6+) 16. Qxe6 fxg5 17. Rd7 Qc5 18. Bxc6 {I played, for some reason, with no
forethought whatsoever for the first few moves and then it didn't matter any
more} 1-0

