1. e4 {I wasn't supposed to be playing in the match and just went down on the
offchance of a game. I was substituted in for a defaulting player and started
with 30 mins on my clock.} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 cxd4 {
According to M.C.O. 9th Edn col 48 (j) this is inferior.} 6. Qg4 ({M.C.O. gives
} 6. axb4 dxc3 7. Nf3 Qc7 8. Qd4 Ne7 9. Bd3 Nd7 10. O-O Nc6 11. Qxc3 Qb6 12. b5
$16) 6... Ne7 7. Qxg7 Rg8 8. Qxh7 Qa5 9. Rb1 dxc3 10. axb4 Qxb4 11. Qd3 d4 12.
g3 {The results of the opening are difficult to asses both sides seem to have
chances.} Nbc6 13. f4 Nd5 (13... cxb2+ {doesn't achieve much.}) 14. Qb5 Qe7 {
Whilst this isn't bad.....} ({....} 14... cxb2+ {seems better}) 15. Ne2 {
Threatening his advanced Pawns.} a6 16. Qc4 {Now Black is stuck for a good
continuation.} b5 {An unfortunate lapsus mentus} 17. Qxc6+ 1-0

