{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs} 1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. g3 d5 5. cxd5
Nxd5 6. Bg2 c6 7. O-O O-O 8. Qb3 {Not a very good square for the Queen.} Nb6 $1
9. d3 e5 10. Be3 Be6 11. Qc2 Nd5 $1 12. Bc5 (12. Nxd5 cxd5 {Gives Black too
strong a centre. However the Bishop is not too well placed on c5.}) 12... Re8
13. Ne4 {Not as good as it looks.} b6 14. Ba3 {Now the Bishop is cut off.} c5
15. Nc3 Nc6 16. Ng5 {Now Black gets well on top.} Qxg5 17. Nxd5 Nd4 $1 18. Qd1
Bxd5 19. Bxd5 Rad8 20. Bg2 Qg4 21. Re1 Qh5 {[57']} 22. Rc1 {[53']} f5 {[65']} (
{Unfortunately the combination I had intended is too risky i.e.} 22... e4 $6
23. Bxe4 Rxe4 24. dxe4 Nf3+ {etc.}) 23. f3 {[59']} Bh6 24. e3 e4 $6 {[80'] I
could have played 24......Ne6 with the better game but decided to play this
very risky sacrifice. A calculated risk.} 25. g4 $1 {By far the best.} (25.
exd4 Bxc1 26. Qxc1 exd3 {etc.}) 25... Nxf3+ {[85']} 26. Bxf3 Qg5 27. Qb3+ Kh8
28. dxe4 fxe4 {[88']} 29. Bg2 {[78'] About the best.} Qxg4 {Threatening 29.....
.Rd2} 30. Qc3+ Kg8 31. b3 $1 {So as to bring the Bishop into the attack.} Rd3
32. Qc4+ {The best chance.} Re6 33. h3 Qf5 34. Rf1 Bxe3+ 35. Kh1 {[90']} Qe5 {
[105']} 36. Bb2 Bd4 (36... Qd6 {is good after....} 37. Bxe4 $2 ({but not after.
..} 37. Rce1) 37... Rd2) 37. Bxd4 Rxd4 ({I didn't fancy...} 37... cxd4 {
when the c-file is open.}) 38. Qe2 Rdd6 {Losing the e-pawn but there is
nothing better.} 39. Rce1 e3 40. Qf3 Rf6 {[119' 30s] I just about made it on
the clock.} 41. Qxe3 Rxf1+ 42. Bxf1 Qxe3 43. Rxe3 Rd7 44. Bb5 Rc7 45. Rd3 {
Now the Rooks must go.} Kf7 46. Rd7+ Rxd7 47. Bxd7 Kf6 48. Kg2 Ke5 49. Kf3 h5
50. h4 b5 51. Bxb5 g5 52. hxg5 Kf5 53. g6 Kxg6 54. Be8+ Kf6 55. Bxh5 Ke5 56.
Ke3 Kd6 57. Kd3 Kc6 58. Kc4 a6 59. Bg4 Kb6 60. a4 Ka5 {A last try.} 61. Bc8 ({
Not} 61. Kxc5 $4 {Stalemate!}) 61... Kb6 62. Bxa6 Kxa6 63. Kxc5 {Interesting
even if a very unsound sacrifice. I don't know why I made the sacrifice when I
was in the better position anyway. The Congress was split into the premier and
reserve tournaments. The reserve tournaments each had six players and was
split into sections A-J (No I gp) The congress was played at Richmond Comunity
Centre from Friday 12th to Monday 15th April 1963. [R.D Keene won the Surrey
Jr (U-16) Section.]} 1-0

