{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nf6 {This is the first time I
have played against this move.} 3. e5 Nd5 4. Nc3 e6 5. Nxd5 exd5 6. d4 Nc6 7.
dxc5 Bxc5 8. Qxd5 d6 {I've never seen this move before. I expected 8......Qb6}
(8... Qb6) 9. Be2 {The cautios line.} ({I didn't fancy} 9. Bc4 Be6 (9... Nxe5
10. Nxe5 Qe7)) 9... Qa5+ {This equalises.} 10. Qd2 Qxd2+ 11. Bxd2 dxe5 12. Bb5
f6 13. Be3 {Togive my Knight a retreat square also the Bishop exchange is
favourable to me.} Bxe3 14. fxe3 Bf5 15. O-O-O Ke7 16. Bxc6 {Much as I
disliked giving up a Bishop for a Knight it seemed best.} bxc6 17. Rhf1 Be4 18.
Nd2 Bxg2 19. Rg1 Bd5 20. Rxg7+ Bf7 21. Ne4 Rag8 22. Rxg8 Rxg8 23. Ng3 Bg6 24.
e4 {Puts the Pawn on a White square but about best.} Ke6 25. b3 Rb8 (25... Rg7
$142) 26. c4 Rb7 27. Kc2 h5 {The superiority of his Bishop over my Knight
begins to show.} 28. c5 Rd7 29. Rxd7 Kxd7 30. Kd3 Ke6 (30... h4 31. Nf5 Bxf5
32. exf5 {and his h-Pawn falls.}) 31. b4 h4 32. Nf1 f5 33. exf5+ Bxf5+ 34. Kc4
$1 Bb1 35. a4 Bc2 36. a5 {Here he offered a draw (much to my surprise) which I
accepted.} ({I considered....} 36. Nd2 Bxa4 37. Nf3 h3 ({However Black plays...
.} 37... Bc2 $3 38. Nxh4 $2 Be4 {and the Knight is paralysed.}) 38. Ng5+ Kf5
39. Nxh3) 1/2-1/2

