{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. b3 d5 5. Bg2
O-O 6. O-O Ne4 {Hampering his QS development to some extent.} 7. Bb2 c6 {
This doesn't turn out as well as I expected. Probably fianchettoing the
QBishop and playing ......c5 is best.} 8. Nbd2 Nd6 9. c4 dxc4 {Now he gets an
"overwhelming" centre but if he is allowed to play c5 he would be well on top
and my pieces would have even less scope.} 10. bxc4 Be6 11. Qc2 (11. c5 Nc4 {
is fair for Black.}) 11... Na6 {The best means of development for the Knight.}
12. a3 f5 $6 {Trying to get some play at the risk of leaving some holes in the
position. 13.e4 is prevented. I even envisioned a possible ......f4 later on.}
13. Ng5 Bf7 14. Nxf7 Nxf7 ({After} 14... Rxf7 15. d5 {is strong.}) 15. e3 {
Much too cautious} (15. d5 $142) (15. e4 $142) 15... e5 {The thematic freeing
move however it is rather risky.} 16. d5 {[46']} (16. dxe5 Nxe5 17. Qc3 $4 Nf3+
) 16... e4 $6 {very risky.} (16... Qc7 {was reasonable.}) 17. Bxg7 Kxg7 18.
dxc6 ({The alternative was} 18. Qb2+ Kg8 19. Qxb7 Qb6 20. Qxb6 axb6 21. dxc6)
18... bxc6 19. f3 {If he doesn't play this his Bishop has no scope and my
Knights reach d3} exf3 20. Bxf3 Qb6 21. Qc3+ Kg8 22. Rab1 Qc7 23. c5 {Giving
his Knight a good square on c4 and cutting off my aKnight.} Qe5 {Seizing the
innitiative.} 24. Rfc1 (24. Qxe5 Nxe5 {Hisc-Pawn is en prise, his Pawns are
weak and my Rooks get good play on the open files.}) 24... Rad8 25. Rb2 {
[77'] Allowing a nice combination.} ({if} 25. Bxc6 $4 Qxc3 {wins his Knight}) (
{Necessary was..} 25. Nb3 {but I still have the better of it.}) 25... Nxc5 $3 {
Winning the exchange.} 26. Qxe5 ({Obviously he can't play} 26. Qxc5) ({and
after} 26. Bxc6 Nd3) 26... Nxe5 27. Rxc5 {The only feasible alternative.} (27.
Rcc2 {meets the same reply.....}) 27... Rxd2 $1 28. Rxe5 (28. Rxd2 Nxf3+ {
The point of the combination.}) 28... Rxb2 29. Bxc6 Rc8 30. Rc5 Kg7 31. Rb5 Rd2
32. Rd5 Rxd5 33. Bxd5 Rc3 {Avery neat combination. I was playing much quicker
than the required 40 in 2hr.} 0-1

