{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours.} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5.
Bd3 c5 6. c3 Nc6 7. Ne2 cxd4 8. cxd4 Be7 ({A more usual set up would be
reached by} 8... Qb6 9. Nf3 Bb4+) 9. O-O Qb6 10. Nf3 {[5']} f6 {[37'] A double
edged continuation as his e-Pawn is left weak.} 11. Nf4 Nf8 {[35'] Black's
position is obviously difficult.} 12. Re1 {[10']} Bd7 {Black's best chance is
to castle QS.} 13. a3 {[20']} ({I considered} 13. Be3 {but did not want to
black the e-file anymore.}) 13... O-O-O {[42']} 14. Be3 {[25'] Discouraging 14.
....PxP amongst other things} Kb8 {[50']} (14... Qxb2 $4 {is hopelessly risky.}
) 15. b4 {[26'] Prevents the Knight manouevre c6-a5-c4 later on} Rc8 {[56']}
16. h4 {I didn't want to be bothered by .....g5} f5 {Black submits to the
Pawn-wedge. White gets slight sacrificial chances later on by: Bxf5 and Nxd5}
17. Nd2 {Intending to go to c5.} Bxh4 (17... Nxd4 $4 18. Nb3) 18. Qh5 ({
I also considered..} 18. Nb3) 18... Qd8 {[77']} (18... Be7 {may be slighlty
better as he can follow it up with .....g5}) 19. g3 {[50']} g5 (19... Be7 {
would make his previous move a waste of time.}) 20. Ne2 {Strengthens thee
QPawn as the e3 Bishop may have to move.} f4 {This gives back the Pawn but his
pieces gain more freedom. White however still has much the better of it.} 21.
gxf4 gxf4 22. Nxf4 Bg5 {[87'] Black was now beginning to realise his time
troubles.} 23. Nf3 Bxf4 24. Bxf4 Ng6 25. Bg5 Qf8 {Black is still in
difficulties.} 26. Bxg6 $1 {Transposing into a position where all Black's
pieces are inferior to White's and his g-Pawn is weak.} hxg6 27. Qg4 Rh5 28.
Bf6 {Closing the f-file and covering h8} Qh6 {[99']} 29. Kg2 {[76']} Rg8 {
Black can do nothing.} 30. Rh1 Nd8 {Hoping to play .....Nf7 but he doesn't get
the chance.} 31. Ng5 $1 {Threatening 32.BxN} Rf8 {Missing the threat in time
trouble, but it's doubtful he would last long anyway.} 32. Bxd8 Rxd8 33. Nf7
Qf8 {[115']} (33... Qd2 34. Rad1 $1 (34. Nxd8 $4 Rg5)) 34. Nxd8 Qxd8 35. Rxh5
gxh5 36. Qxh5 Qg8+ 37. Kh2 Be8 38. Qh4 Bf7 39. Rg1 Qe8 40. Rg7 Bg6 41. Rxg6 {
After this round the scores were: R.A.C., B.A.Jones, D.J.Masters, 2.5 J.G.
Collins, J.Horrocks 2 Coates 0.5} 0-1

