{Opponent info: J.Horrocks is partially blind and uses a special board.} 1. e4
e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Bd2 c5 5. e5 Ne7 6. Nce2 {Not so bad as it looks.}
Bxd2+ 7. Qxd2 Ng6 8. c3 {Black threatened 8......PxP 9.QxP Nc6 attacking the
e-Pawn twice.} Nc6 9. Nf3 cxd4 10. cxd4 f6 11. exf6 Qxf6 12. h4 {White's
attack proves surprisingly strong considering the placing of his minor pieces.}
O-O 13. h5 Nge7 14. Ng3 {[33']} Nf5 {[25']} ({I considered...} 14... e5 {
but White gets quite a good position out of it.}) 15. Nxf5 Qxf5 16. Bd3 Qf4 17.
Qc2 {Now White gets a huge attack but Black just survives and gets the better
endgame.} (17. Qxf4 Rxf4 {was good for Black.}) 17... Nxd4 18. Nxd4 Qxd4 19.
Bxh7+ Kh8 20. h6 {Quite a crowd now collected. The general opinion being that
I wouldn't last long.} Qb4+ 21. Kf1 (21. Kd1 Qd4+ 22. Bd3 g5) 21... Qc4+ 22.
Bd3 Qxc2 23. hxg7+ Kxg7 24. Bxc2 Rh8 {Black now has slightly better of the
endgame as he controls most of the centre and White has to defend on both
sides of the board.} 25. Ke2 Bd7 26. Bb3 Bc6 27. Rxh8 Rxh8 28. Rd1 Kf6 29. Ke3
Rh4 30. f4 (30. g3 Re4+ 31. Kd3 Bb5+ 32. Kd2 (32. Kc3 Re2) (32. Kc2 Re2+) 32...
Re2+) 30... Rh2 31. Rd2 a6 32. Bc2 e5 33. fxe5+ {[77']} Kxe5 {[55']} 34. Bd1
Rh4 35. Kf2 Rf4+ 36. Kg3 Rf8 {He offered a draw here, but I had to win to come
=1st.} 37. Kh4 Rg8 38. g4 (38. Bf3 $142) 38... Kf4 39. Rf2+ Ke3 40. Re2+ {[94']
} Kd3 {[70']} 41. Kg3 Ba4 $1 42. b3 {Forced} Bc6 43. Kf4 $2 {Loses a piece
although it was difficult for him.} Rf8+ 44. Kg5 Rf1 45. Kh6 Rxd1 46. Rh2 Be8
47. g5 Re1 48. Kg7 d4 49. Kf6 Kc3 50. Rh8 d3 51. Rh3 Kc2 52. Rg3 d2 53. Rg2 {
[115']} Kc1 {[86'] I came 1st= with D.J.Masters with 3.5 pts. I won £2-5-0 
(Half of 1st [£3] and 2nd [£1-10-0] prizes) Paul (R.A.C's Brother) won the
1st class A (=4 -1)} 0-1

