1. f4 d5 2. Nf3 c5 3. e3 g6 4. d4 Bg4 5. c3 Nf6 6. Be2 {[1']} Bxf3 {[11']} 7.
Bxf3 Bg7 8. Nd2 Nc6 9. O-O {[7']} O-O {[15'] Rather underestimating White's
next move.} 10. dxc5 {[14'] About the only constructive move but quite
promising.} a5 11. e4 {[18']} dxe4 {11......e5 or 11......d5 aren't any good.}
12. Nxe4 Qc7 13. Nxf6+ Bxf6 14. Bxc6 Qxc6 {White made no attempt to win in
this game and offered me a draw several times.} 15. Qf3 {There seems no piont
in giving the Pawn back straight away.} (15. Be3 $142) 15... Qxc5+ 16. Be3 Qb5
{[29']} 17. Qf2 {[36']} Rfd8 {[30'] Preventing 18.Bd4 which would leave White
with an isolated QPawn.} 18. Rad1 a4 {[32']} 19. a3 {He had to prevent 19.....
a3} Qc4 {Prevents 20.Bd4} 20. Kh1 {[45']} Qb3 {[36']} 21. Rde1 {Rather tame.}
Rd7 22. f5 Rad8 23. fxg6 fxg6 24. h3 {[65']} Rd1 {[42']} 25. Bc1 Rxe1 26. Qxe1
Qc4 {Threatening to win by 27.....Bh4} 27. Rf4 Qd5 28. Re4 Qh5 29. Kh2 Rd1 30.
Qe3 (30. Qe3 h6 $2 {Better was.....} 31. Qxh6 ({Not} 31. Rxa4 $4 Be5+ 32. g3
Qf5 $1 {Threatens 32......Qc2+ and 32......Qf1}) 31... Be5+ 32. g3 Qf5 33. Re2
{When I can just about draw by.....} Qf1) 30... h6 $2 {Pushing too hard. This
threatens 31.....Bg5 but is very weakening. However White (foolishly) offered
a draw which I accepted. Rather a skittles game but this is only to be
expected when the match only lasts 2.5 - 3.5 hrs} 1/2-1/2

