1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 Bc5 4. Nc3 O-O 5. Nf3 Nc6 ({Not} 5... e4 6. Ng5) 6.
O-O d6 7. a3 Be6 (7... a5 $142) 8. b4 Bb6 (8... Bd4 9. Nxd4 exd4 10. Nb5 {
Is good for White}) 9. d3 Qd7 {Ng5 is good for me later on.} 10. Re1 {so as to
reply to 10......Bh3 with 11.Bh1 This leaves f2 weak} Ng4 11. e3 f5 12. Ng5 {
Threatening 13.NxB QxN 14.Bd5} Kh8 (12... h6 13. Nxe6 Qxe6 14. Bd5) 13. b5 {
Forcing Black's awkward reply.} Nd8 {This Knight is still here at the end of
the game unable to move.} 14. a4 a6 15. a5 $5 {This doesn't turn out too well.}
(15. bxa6 $142 Rxa6 16. Nb5 Z0 17. Ba3) 15... axb5 16. Nxb5 Rxa5 (16... Bxa5 {
pins the Bishop.}) 17. Ba3 h6 18. Nxe6 ({In view of what follows} 18. Nf3 {
seems better.}) 18... Qxe6 19. Qb3 {Threatens 20.NxPd but overlooks the
strength of his reply.} f4 $1 20. d4 ({The alternative is} 20. Bh3 {but I
didn't like} f3) 20... fxg3 21. fxg3 exd4 $1 22. Nxd4 {Forced} (22. exd4 {
loses to.....} Rxb5 23. Qxb5 Bxd4+) 22... Qe5 23. Rad1 Re8 24. Bc1 Bxd4 {
This seems to miss an almost immediate win.} ({by....} 24... Ra1 25. Qc3 Rxc1
26. Rxc1 Nxe3 {etc. The move played is certainly not bad and ought to win.})
25. Rxd4 Qxd4 26. exd4 Rxe1+ 27. Bf1 Rf5 $2 {This is definitely wrong.} (27...
Ra1 {seems to win easily.}) 28. Bf4 Nxh2 {This too is doubtful.....} ({...but
if} 28... g5 29. Qf3 {Black makes no progress.}) 29. Kxh2 Rxf1 30. Qe3 {
is better than......} ({.....} 30. Qd3 Rh5+) 30... Rf8 (30... Nf7 {looks just
about playable}) 31. Qe7 Kg8 32. d5 $1 {Trapping the Knight for good.} Rf2+ 33.
Kh3 $1 g5 $2 {After this it seems he is lost} 34. Be3 R2f7 35. Qe4 {
Threatening 36.Bd4 & 37.Qg6} c5 {A useless attempt to keep the Bishop off the
long diagonal} 36. Bd2 Rf5 (36... Rh7 37. Bc3 Rff7 38. Qe8+ Rf8 39. Qg6+) 37.
Bc3 {24 Southampton won 26 -} (37. Bc3 {Putting Black in zugzwang. Time was
now called for adjudication but Black resigned as I now demonstrated the
following remarkable win.} b6 $8 (37... Rf2 {[R moves]} 38. Qg6# {and mates}) (
37... Kh7 38. g4) 38. Qe7 R5f7 39. Qxd6 Kh7 $1 40. Qxb6 {Now threatening the
c-Pawn. If this falls then I win easily by marching my teo passesd Pawns
through.} Nb7 {The only move to prevent this.} 41. Qb1+ $3 Rf5 {or it's mate}
42. g4 {Wins a Rook.} (42. Qxb7+)) 1-0

