{Opponent info: Hampshire county champion.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4
d6 5. f4 e5 {Rather unusual.} (5... c5 $142) 6. fxe5 dxe5 7. d5 {Taking
control of the centre. The e-Pawn gets in Blacks way.} O-O 8. Nf3 Qe7 {It
wasn't necessary to defend the e-Pawn} 9. Bg5 h6 10. Bxf6 Bxf6 11. Be2 Bg7 12.
O-O f5 13. Qc2 f4 {Releasing the tension in the centre.} 14. a3 g5 {Black's
position in the centre isn't strong enough to warrant a KS attack.} 15. h3 h5 {
This is much too rash.} (15... Nd7 $142) 16. Nh2 $1 g4 ({if...} 16... Qf7 17.
Qd1) 17. hxg4 hxg4 18. Bxg4 ({I didn't play....} 18. Nxg4 {because of.....} Qh4
) 18... Bxg4 19. Nxg4 Qc5+ {Regaining the Pawn but with a bad game.} ({Better
it seems was....} 19... Qh4 {with some counterplay.}) 20. Qf2 $1 {Taking
control of the KS as well.} Qxc4 21. Qh4 Qc5+ 22. Rf2 {This may save me a move
later on if I want to double the Rooks.} Na6 {Development of sorts but the
Knight proves to be useless here.} 23. Rc1 Rae8 {Hoping to be able to force
off Queens by 24......Qe7} 24. Qg5 $1 Qe7 25. Nh6+ Kh7 26. Qxe7 Rxe7 27. Nf5
Rd7 28. Nb5 {Now Black has to pay for his earlier lack of development and
positional foresight.} b6 29. b4 {Preventing 30......Nc5 Black obviously can't
last long now.} Rf6 30. Rfc2 {the a-Pawn won't run away.} Rff7 31. Nxa7 c5 32.
Nc6 cxb4 33. axb4 Kg6 {Putting a quick end to it but he was completely lost
anyway.} (33... Bf6 {or33......Bf8} 34. d6 {threatens to win by eg.} Rf8 35.
Ra2 Ra8 36. Rca1 {etc...}) 34. Nxg7 Kxg7 35. b5 Nc5 36. Nxe5 {Southampton Uni
won the match 3.5 - 1.5} 1-0

