1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. O-O e5 5. d3 g6 6. Nc3 {Unfortunately I did
not take much notice of this move.} Bg7 7. e4 Nge7 $2 {An oversight I didn't
consider the Knight move to be anything bit routine.} (7... d4 {is quite good.}
) 8. exd5 Nxd5 9. Nxd5 Qxd5 10. Nxe5 Qd6 ({I considered....} 10... Qxe5 {
but it's not quite good enough.}) 11. Nc4 Qe7 ({If} 11... Qd8 12. Be3) 12. Bf4
{Wins a second Pawn.} Be6 {Shutting the e-file at least.} 13. Bd6 Qd7 (13...
Qg5 14. f4) 14. Bxc5 Bxc4 {or else 15.Nd6+} 15. dxc4 O-O-O (15... Qxd1 16.
Raxd1 {and the Black King is stranded.}) (15... Bxb2 16. Qxd7+ Kxd7 17. Rab1 {
Bishop moves.......} Bg7 18. Rxb7+) 16. Qxd7+ Rxd7 17. c3 ({Interesting is} 17.
Ba3 f5 18. g4) 17... Rd2 18. Bxc6 bxc6 19. Bxa7 Rxb2 20. Bd4 {White is correct
to force off the Bishops.} Bxd4 21. cxd4 Rd8 {This should lead to a forced
loss.} ({Possibly the only chance (against correct play by White) was.....} 
21... Re8 {to try to establish both Rooks on the seventh rank.}) 22. Rfd1 Rc2 (
22... Re8 {was still playable.}) 23. d5 {White must lose a Pawn. This way one
pair of Rooks go as well.} Rxc4 24. dxc6 Rxc6 (24... Rxd1+ 25. Rxd1 {My King
is stuck on the QS.}) 25. Rxd8+ Kxd8 26. Kg2 g5 (26... Rc5 $142) 27. g4 $2 {
This is bad.} ({Correct was} 27. a4 Rc3 28. a5 {etc.}) 27... Rc4 28. Kg3 Ra4 {
His a-Pawn is held up on the 2nd or 3rd rank and he will have difficulty
advancing his f or h Pawns.} ({Also good was..} 28... Rc3+ 29. f3 Ra3) 29. h4
$2 {And this is a downright blunder.} Ra3+ 30. f3 gxh4+ 31. Kxh4 Rxf3 32. Kg5
f6+ 33. Kh4 (33. Kh6 Rg3) (33. Kh5 $4 Rh3#) 33... Ra3 ({Also playable is...} 
33... f5) 34. Rd1+ Ke7 35. Rd2 Kf7 {Total time for the game 2 hours. I think
I'd do better generally if I didn't think of winning always , but defend when
necessary.} 1/2-1/2

