1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 Be7 8. Qd3
O-O 9. O-O-O {Threatens 11.NxN then 12.BxN when I have to reply 12......PxB or
lose my d-Pawn.} Nxd4 10. Qxd4 Qa5 11. e5 dxe5 12. fxe5 Rd8 13. Qe3 $2 {
Loses a Pawn.} ({I intended after} 13. Qf4 Rxd1+ 14. Kxd1 Nd5) 13... Rxd1+ 14.
Kxd1 Ng4 15. Qf4 Bxg5 16. Qxg4 Qxe5 17. Bd3 Qe3 18. Ne4 {All this is forced.}
Bh6 {Keeping White tied up.} ({Very risky was} 18... Qc1+ 19. Ke2 Qxh1) 19. Rf1
e5 ({If now....} 19... f5 20. Qh4 Bd7 21. Qe7 {is good for White}) 20. Qh5 {
White decides his best chance is to keep the Queens on.} ({I expected} 20. Qf3)
20... Be6 {The e-Pawn is immune. I threaten 21......f5 also 21......Rd1
followed by .....RxB+} 21. Rf3 Qg1+ 22. Bf1 {or else the g-Pawn goes.} Rd8+ 23.
Ke1 Qd4 {Better than 23......Bc4} 24. Qh4 $2 {Suicide.} ({The only move apart
from 24.Resigns was} 24. Bd3) 24... Bd2+ 25. Ke2 (25. Kd1 Bg5+ 26. Rd3 Qxd3+
27. Bxd3 (27. cxd3 Bxh4) 27... Bxh4) 25... Bc4+ 26. Rd3 Bxd3+ 27. cxd3 Qxd3+
28. Kd1 Qxf1+ 29. Kc2 Qd3+ 30. Kd1 Bc3+ 31. Kc1 Qd1# 0-1

