1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. d4 d6 4. Nf3 Bg4 5. Be2 e6 6. O-O Be7 7. c4 Nb6 8. exd6
cxd6 9. Nc3 Nc6 10. b3 O-O 11. Be3 d5 12. c5 Nd7 13. b4 Nxb4 14. Rb1 Nc6 15.
Rxb7 {'A Pocket Guide to the Chess Openings' breaks off here "With advantage
to White"} Bxf3 {So as to occupy c4 with the Knight} 16. Bxf3 Na5 17. Rb1 Nc4
18. Bf4 Bg5 19. Bxg5 Qxg5 20. Be2 $2 {Overlooking the threat in my last move} (
20. Rb7 $142) 20... Ne3 $1 {Winning a pawn but leaving me in a difficult
position.} 21. fxe3 Qxe3+ 22. Kh1 ({After} 22. Rf2 {the game might proceed...}
Qxc3 23. Rb3 Qa5 24. Re3 e5 25. dxe5 Qxc5 26. Bd3 g6) 22... Qxc3 23. Rb5 $1 {
A very good move cutting off the Black Queen's retreat to a5. I now spent an
hout and 10 minutes over my next move} e5 $5 ({If} 23... Qe3 24. Rf3 {and
White gets a very strong KS attack.}) 24. dxe5 Qxe5 25. Bf3 {A surprise} ({
I expected} 25. c6 Nf6 26. Bf3 Rfd8 {When White has strong pressure.}) 25... a6
{An improvement on the above variation made possible by his Pawn still being
on c5.} 26. Ra5 Qc3 ({I also considered} 26... Qc7) 27. Qe1 Qc4 ({If now} 27...
Qc2 28. Rf2 Rfe8 29. Qf1 {is OK for him}) (27... Qxe1 28. Rxe1 Rfe8 29. Rf1 {
is also OK for him.}) 28. Qc1 {Allowing me to improve the position of my
Knight.} Ne5 ({Not} 28... Rac8 29. Qxc4 dxc4 30. c6 Ne5 31. Rxa6) 29. Qxc4 ({
Not} 29. c6 Qxc6 30. Qxc6 Nxc6 31. Bxd5 Nxa5) 29... Nxc4 30. Ra4 Rac8 ({Not} 
30... Nd2 31. Rc1) 31. Rc1 ({Not} 31. Bxd5 $2 Ne3 $1) 31... Rxc5 32. Rxa6 {
He has little choice here.} g6 33. a4 $2 {White's only hope is to follow
Black's example and give his King an escape square.} d4 ({Not} 33... Re8 34. h3
$1) 34. Be2 {or else 34......d6 etc.} Re8 $1 35. Bf1 d3 $1 {Black's d-Pawn has
been untouchable in this game.} 36. Ra7 (36. Bxd3 Nb2 $1) 36... d2 0-1

