1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. e3 e6 5. Bxc4 c5 6. O-O cxd4 {Now I get an
IQP but good play for my pieces} ({Alternatively} 6... a6) 7. exd4 Be7 ({If} 
7... Nc6 8. Nc3 a6 9. Qe2 Nxd4 $2 10. Nxd4 Qxd4 11. Rd1 Qg4 12. Nd5 $18) 8. Nc3
Nc6 9. Qe2 {Sacrificing my d-Pawn for control of the centre and good play for
all my pieces.} Nxd4 {Black accepts the challenge but it proves fatal.} 10.
Nxd4 Qxd4 11. Rd1 Qb6 ({If} 11... Qg4 12. Bb5+ Kf8 13. Qd3 {is very strong.}) (
{If} 11... Qc5 12. Be3 ({or even} 12. b4 Qxb4 13. Nb5)) 12. Be3 Qa5 (12... Qc7
$2 13. Nb5) (12... Bc5 $4 13. Na4) 13. Bd4 $1 {The best move preventing 13.....
.e5 pinning the Knight & envisioning a leter Be5, opening up the Queen to onto
Black's weak e-Pawn, oening the 3rd rank and possibly threatening 14.BxN BxB
15.Bb5+} Bd7 {KS castling is risky so Black continues his development} 14. Rd3
{Again the best move.14.Rd3 intends to either double on the d-file or attack
on the KS.} (14. a3 {is a bit slow.}) ({Not quite good enough is....} 14. Bxf6
Bxf6 15. Ne4 Be7 16. Nd6+ Bxd6 17. Rxd6 {if} Bc6 (17... Z0 {with the idea} 18.
Rad1) 18. Bxe6) ({If} 14. Bb5 Bxb5 15. Nxb5 Rc8 16. Nxa7 {but this allows the
exchange of Black's useless KBishop.}) 14... Bc6 {Possibly intending 15.......
Qg5 16.f3 when I have blocked the 3rd rank.} 15. Rg3 {Forcing Black to do
something definite about his KS.} ({If now White gets over-confident with} 15.
Bxf6 Bxf6 16. Bxe6 fxe6 17. Qxe6+ Kf8 {is good enough.}) 15... O-O {Casrtling
into it.} ({After} 15... g6 {his Knight is hopelessly pinned & his King and
h-Rook are badly placed.}) 16. Qe3 {Again the best move. The threat now is 17.
Qh6! Also possible is 17.Rg5} Rac8 $2 {Desperately trying for some play Black
overlooks a next reply.} 17. Bxe6 $1 {Taking advantage of Black's last move.} (
{17.Bxe6 is clearer than...} 17. Qh6 g6 18. Rh3 Rfd8 19. Bxf6 Bxf6 20. Qxh7+
Kf8 {and White has no easy win.}) 17... Rc7 $1 {Although the Rook isn't happy
here this is the only move.} ({If now} 17... fxe6 18. Qxe6+ Rf7 19. Qxc8+) (
17... Rce8 18. Qh6 g6 19. Bxf6 Bxf6 20. Rh3 {17......Rc7 defends his second
rank which allows 20......PxB!}) 18. Rg5 {Taking control of my 5th rank.} Qb4 {
This loses the exchange at best but the alternative was......} (18... Qa6 {
the Queen is completely out of play and White can play such things as....} 19.
Bg4 $1 {Threatening 20.Be2 & 21.Be5}) 19. a3 Qd6 {Black now appears to have
recovered somewhat . However, although his pieces are centralised and my
KBishop is en prise, I can win the exchange.} (19... Qxb2 20. Ne4 {and Black
must resign.}) 20. Bh3 {Now 21.Be5 is unstopable.} ({Naturally not} 20. Be5 $2
Qxe6 21. Bxc7 Qxe3 22. fxe3 Ne8 23. Re5 Bf6) 20... Qd8 21. Be5 Bd6 {Allowing a
neat finish but all was lost for Black some time ago.} 22. Rxg7+ $1 Kh8 23.
Rxh7+ {My best correspondence game to date.} 1-0

