1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bg5 e6 7. Qd2 Be7 8.
O-O-O O-O 9. f4 Nxd4 10. Qxd4 h6 11. Bh4 Qa5 12. Bc4 a6 (12... e5 {Gives him d5
}) (12... Bd7 13. e5 $1) 13. Rhf1 b5 $2 ({I now decided that......} 13... b5 $2
{seemed good, noting that after} 14. Bb3 Bb7 15. Bxf6 Bxf6 16. Qxd6 $2 {
I stand well. I didn't give it much extra thought and played 13......b5?}) 14.
e5 {Now I get in a hopeless mess} dxe5 15. fxe5 bxc4 {The only move.} (15...
Nd5 16. Bxd5 $1) 16. exf6 Bxf6 17. Bxf6 gxf6 18. Ne4 {This was a surprise but
seems good.} (18. Rxf6 Qg5+ {is good e.g.} 19. Kb1 e5) (18. Qxf6 Qg5+) (18.
Qxc4 {I have Bishop for Knight but White probably wins easily and this may be
the best.}) ({However} 18. Ne4 e5 19. Nxf6+ Kg7 20. Qe4 $3 {I considered
resigning, but decided I had fair chances.}) 18... f5 $8 19. Nf6+ Kh8 $1 ({
He now offered "if"....} 19... Kg7 20. Nh5+ Kg6 21. Qf6+ Kxh5 22. Rf3) 20. Nh5+
({If} 20. Nd7+ e5 21. Nxe5 (21. Qh4 $1 Bxd7 22. Qxh6+ Kg8 23. Rxd7 {seems good}
) 21... Kh7) 20... e5 21. Qh4 {Not so good as if the Knight was on d7} Qb6 $8 {
White threatened 22.Rd6} 22. Nf6 Kg7 23. Rf3 f4 {Just managing to defend all
the vital squares.} ({Naturally not.} 23... Qxf6 $4) 24. Ne4 {White manoeuvres
his Knight but gets nowhere.} ({He can't play...} 24. Rd6 {because....} Qg1+ {
is good for me.}) (24. Nd5 $142) (24. Nh5+ $142) 24... Bf5 {Taking advantage
of the fact that Black wasn't being threatened to develop a piece.} 25. Nd6 {
Cutting off my Queen's defence of g6 & h6.} Be6 {Threat 26......Rd8} 26. g4
Rad8 (26... Rad8 {However White plays} 27. g5 (27. Rh3 Rh8 28. Qe7 Rd7 29. Ne8+
Rxe8 30. Qxe8 Rxd1+ 31. Kxd1 Bxg4+ $19) 27... Rh8 (27... h5 $1 {Threatening 28.
.....Bg4}) 28. gxh6+ Rxh6 29. Nf5+ Bxf5 30. Qxd8 Rxh2 31. Qxb6 ({However White
plays} 31. Qg5+ Bg6 32. Qxe5+ Kh7 33. Rd6 (33. Rc3 Qe3+ 34. Qxe3 fxe3 $13)
33... Qe3+) 31... Rxc2+ $11) 27. Rh3 Rh8 28. Qe7 {Pretty well forced. Now I
have a forced win which takes 16 moves!!} Rd7 29. Nf5+ (29. Ne8+ Rxe8 $1 30.
Qxe8 Rxd1+ 31. Kxd1 Bxg4+) 29... Bxf5 30. Qxe5+ ({Not} 30. Rxd7 Bxd7 31. Qxd7
Rd8) 30... f6 $3 {Apparently giving everything back but actually forcing the
win.} 31. Rxd7+ Bxd7 32. Qe7+ Kg6 33. Qxd7 Rd8 34. Qf5+ Kg7 35. b3 {All this
is forced} Qd4 36. Kb1 c3 37. a4 Rd5 $1 {Forcing White to leave c2 undefended.}
({Now if} 37... Qg1+ 38. Ka2 Rd1 39. b4 $1 {and he escapes.e.g.} Qd4 (39... Qf1
40. Rd3 $1) 40. Qc5 $1) 38. Qc8 (38. Qe6 Re5) 38... Qd1+ 39. Ka2 Qxc2+ 40. Ka3
Qb2+ 41. Kb4 a5+ 42. Kc4 c2 43. Kxd5 Qe5+ 0-1

