1. e4 e6 2. c4 d5 3. cxd5 exd5 4. exd5 Nf6 5. Bb5+ Bd7 6. Qe2+ Qe7 7. Bxd7+
Nbxd7 8. Nc3 Nb6 9. d4 O-O-O 10. Bg5 (10. Nb5 a6) (10. Bf4 Nfxd5) (10. Bg5 h6)
10... Nbxd5 11. Qxe7 Bxe7 {Black has got much the better of the opening.} 12.
Nf3 Bb4 13. O-O $6 {White decides to sacrifice a Pawn for some play.} ({If now
} 13. Bxf6 Nxf6 {leaving Black the better endgame.}) ({If} 13. Rc1 Rhe8+) 13...
Nxc3 14. bxc3 Bxc3 15. Bxf6 gxf6 16. Rad1 Rd5 17. Rd3 Ba5 {Intending to bring
pressure on the d-Pawn.} 18. Re3 Rhd8 19. Re7 R5d7 {Forcing White to awkwardly
defend the d-Pawn laterally} 20. Re4 Bb6 21. Rd1 f5 ({If now} 21... c5 22. Rc1)
22. Rf4 c5 23. Ne5 Re7 ({If instead} 23... Rd5 24. Nxf7 Rxd4 25. Rdxd4 Rxd4 26.
Rxd4 cxd4 27. Nd6+ Kd7 28. Nxf5 d3 29. Kf1 Ke6 {and if} 30. g4 (30. Ne3 Bxe3
31. fxe3 Ke5 32. Ke1 Ke4 33. Kd2 b5 $19) 30... Kd5 {I thought 23......Re7 was
clearer.}) 24. Rxf5 f6 ({If} 24... Rd5 25. Nxf7 $1 Rxf5 26. Nd6+) 25. Nc4 Rxd4
26. Nxb6+ axb6 27. Rb1 c4 $2 {Beginning a doubtful plan. I expected the c-Pawn
to prove stronger than it actually was.} (27... Re6 $142) 28. Rxf6 c3 29. Rc1
Rc4 30. g3 {Now I spent a very long time trying to find a win. After a lot of
analysis I decided on.....} Re2 (30... Rd7 31. Re6) (30... c2 31. Kg2 (31. Rd6)
31... Rd7 32. Re6 Rd1 33. Re1 Rxe1) 31. Rf3 $1 ({If now} 31. Rd6 $2 Rxa2 32.
Rd3 c2 33. f4 b5 34. f5 b4 35. f6 Rc7 36. Rf3 ({If} 36. Rb3 Rd7 $1) 36... Rb2
$1 37. f7 Rxf7 38. Rxf7 Rb1 39. Rff1 Rxc1 40. Rxc1 b3) 31... c2 32. Rd3 Kc7 33.
Kf1 ({Hoping for} 33. f4 Kc6 34. f5 Kb5 35. f6 Rc8 36. f7 Kb4 37. Rf3 Rf8 {
or variations something like this.}) 33... Re5 34. Rd2 Rec5 35. f4 b5 36. Kg2
Kb6 37. f5 Rxf5 38. Rcxc2 ({Not} 38. Rdxc2 Rfc5 {forces} 39. Rxc4 bxc4 {
With good chances for Black.}) 38... Rfc5 ({Not} 38... Kc5 $2 39. a4) 39. Rb2
Rc7 40. h4 Ka5 41. Kh3 Ka4 42. Rd5 1/2-1/2

