1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O b5 6. Bb3 Be7 7. a4 b4 8. d4
O-O (8... Nxd4 9. Bxf7+) 9. Nxe5 Nxe4 10. Qf3 (10. Bd5 Nf6 11. Nxc6 ({or...} 
11. Bxc6 dxc6 12. Nxc6 Qd6 13. Nxe7+ Qxe7 14. Bg5 {leaves Black well developed}
) 11... dxc6 12. Bxc6 Rb8 13. Be3 Rb6 $1 {and Black has good attacking chances.
}) 10... Nf6 11. Nxc6 dxc6 12. Qxc6 {Much more risky than I realised at the
time.} (12. Be3 $142) (12. Nd2 $142) 12... Rb8 13. Bf4 $2 {This seems to lose
the game. Black's Bishops become very powerful.} (13. Be3 $142) (13. Qc4 $142)
13... Qxd4 14. Bxc7 $4 (14. Qxc7 Bb7 {is fairly suicidal}) 14... Bb7 {by far
the best.} (14... Bd7 15. Qxa6) 15. c3 (15. Qb6 Bc5 $1 {with a teriffic attack}
) 15... Qg4 16. f3 Qh5 17. Qc4 {All this was forced.} (17. Qb6 Bxf3 $3 18. Qxb8
Bc5+) 17... Rbc8 18. Qf4 Qc5+ 19. Kh1 Qxc7 20. Qxc7 Rxc7 0-1

