1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bg5 e6 7. Be2 Be7 8.
O-O h6 9. Be3 O-O 10. f4 Nxd4 11. Qxd4 Qa5 12. Kh1 Rd8 {Prevents 13.e5} ({Not} 
12... Bd7 $2 13. e5) 13. a3 (13. Bf3 $142) 13... Bd7 14. Bd2 {Threatening 15.
Nd5 but blocking the d-file.} Qc7 15. Qf2 Bc6 16. Bd3 ({If} 16. f5 {I intended.
.....} Bxe4 17. fxe6 fxe6 18. Nxe4 Nxe4 19. Qf7+ Kh8 {Which is reasonable.})
16... a6 {Intending 17......b5 & 18......Qb7} 17. f5 e5 {Played on the
assumption I could force ......d5} ({If now} 17... Ng4 18. Qg3 Ne5 19. Bxh6) ({
If} 17... d5 18. fxe6 fxe6 {I am left with a weak Pawn. Therefore 17......e5})
18. Rae1 Kh8 (18... d5 19. exd5 Bxd5 20. Qg3) 19. Qg3 d5 $2 {Not the right
moment but it does give my ieces some play.} 20. exd5 Bxd5 21. Qxe5 Qc6 {
The best move giving me tactical chances.} 22. Nxd5 ({He doesn't fancy} 22.
Qxe7 Bxg2+) 22... Nxd5 23. f6 ({Not} 23. c4 {as his Bishop on d2 is too weak.})
23... Bxf6 24. Qh5 {Threat 25.Qxf7 & 25.Bxh6} Kg8 25. Qf5 g6 26. Qf3 {I was
now in a quandry. The h-pawn is en prise, my Bishop can't move, the f6 square
is very weak and White threatens to pin my Knight which is rather open to
attack.} Rd7 $1 {Defending f7, allowing the Bishop to move and allowing the
Knight to be defended by Rb8-d8} (26... Kg7 27. Be4) (26... Ne7 27. Rxe7 $3)
27. Bxh6 Bxb2 28. Be4 {I want to unpin the Knight and keep it protected, but
also protect f7. White is threatening 29.Rd1 followed by 30.BxN and if the
Rook recaptures f7 falls.} (28. Be4 Qe6 {covers f7. However this isn't good
with his Rook on e1.} (28... Z0 29. Rd1 Z0 30. Bxd5 Rxd5)) 28... Rad8 29. Bg5 (
29. Rd1 Qe6 30. Rfe1 Nf6 $1) 29... f6 30. Bxd5+ Qxd5 31. Qxd5+ Rxd5 32. Bxf6
Bxf6 33. Rxf6 Rd1 (33... Kg7 {was the alternative}) 34. Rxg6+ Kf7 35. Rge6 R8d2
36. h3 Rxe1+ 37. Rxe1 Rxc2 38. a4 Rc5 ({If} 38... Rc4 39. Rb1 Rxa4 40. Rxb7+ {
and the Black rook is badly placed in front of the Pawn.}) {White now set up
the Position with my Rook at c4 hence..} 39. a5 $2 Rxa5 {Rather an unfortunate
lapse by White at the end although I had good drawing chances.} 1/2-1/2

[Event "P.C.C. A-P-A A6 1963"]
[Site "?"]
