1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 c6 5. Bg2 Be7 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Ne5 Nbd7 8. f4
Nxe5 9. fxe5 Nd7 10. O-O (10. b3 f6 {seems good for Black}) (10. c5 b6 11. b4 {
is also good for him}) 10... a6 11. e4 {Very forceful I now gain control of
the centre and KS in return for the c-pawn.} dxc4 12. Qe2 (12. Qg4 Kh8 13. Bf4
Qb6 $1) 12... b5 13. Bf4 ({I wanted to play something along the lines of 13.d5
but my e-Pawn is loose. Therefore.....} 13. Bf4 {if then....} f6 14. exf6 Nxf6
15. Rad1 {Threatening 16.e5.}) 13... Qb6 14. Rad1 Bd8 15. Kh1 Bb7 {Black's
position is very strong on the QS but his pieces have little scope and I have
good KS attacking chances.} 16. Qg4 Kh8 17. Qh5 {Threatens 18.Be3 with good
play.} ({If I now try to take advantage of his pinned e-Pawn by....} 17. d5 {
he replies either} Nc5 ({or} 17... cxd5 18. exd5 Nc5)) (17. Be3 {looks quite
good , it prevents c5, and if say....} Bc7 18. Qh5 g6 19. Qf3 {threatening 20.
Bh6 However my e-Pawn is weakened.}) 17... Kg8 (17... c5 18. Be3) 18. Bh3 $1 {
A neat move threatening 19.Be3 and 20.Rxf7} b4 {Black decides to advance
quickly on the QS.} 19. Ne2 Qa5 $2 {Black is probably lost but this doesn't
help matters. Over-the -Board he might have got away with it.} 20. Bd2 $1 {
Threat 20.a3 and 20.Rxf7} Qxa2 21. Rxf7 $1 ({If now} 21. Bxb4 c5 22. dxc5 Bxe4+
23. Kg1 Bg6 24. Qf3 Ra7 {is OK for Black.}) 21... c3 {Black decides his only
hope is to fish in troubled waters on the QS.} ({If now} 21... Rxf7 22. Bxe6 g6
23. Bxf7+ (23. Qf3) 23... Kxf7 24. Qxh7+ {etc.}) 22. Rxd7 cxb2 (22... cxd2 23.
Rxb7 Z0 24. Qg4) 23. Qg4 Rf7 (23... g6 24. Qxe6+ Qxe6 25. Bxe6+ Kh8 26. Bh6)
24. Qxe6 b1=Q 25. Qe8+ Rf8 26. Be6+ Qxe6 27. Qxe6+ Kh8 28. Rxb1 Bc8 29. Qd6 1-0

[Event "P.C.C. A-P-A A6 1963"]
