1. c4 Nf6 2. d4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 e6 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Be2 c5 8. d5 exd5
9. exd5 Na6 10. O-O Nc7 11. Bd3 a6 12. a4 Bd7 13. a5 Rb8 14. h3 b5 15. axb6
Rxb6 16. Qc2 Nfe8 17. g4 f5 18. g5 {I played this as it seemed to give me all
the opportunities for a breakthrough; Black having no counterplay.} Qa8 19. Ra5
Bh8 {Blacks pieces are very badly placed. He intends the Knight manoeuvre
-g6-r4} 20. Re1 Ng7 21. Re2 Kf7 $2 {Played to strengthen the e-file but it
weakens his position.} 22. Be3 {With a neat threat which takes advantage of
Black's last move.} Qb7 $2 23. Bxc5 $1 dxc5 24. Ne5+ Ke7 25. Nxg6+ ({Not} 25.
Nc6+ $2 Kd6 $1) 25... Kf7 26. Ne5+ (26. Nxf8 Kxf8 {is not as good.}) 26... Ke7
27. Rxc5 {Now he can't move his fRook or his F-Pawn goes, nor can his gKnight}
(27. Rxc5 Z0 {I threaten.....} (27... Be8 28. Rxc7+ Qxc7 29. Ng6+ Kf7 30. Re7+)
28. Ng6+ Kf7 29. Re7+ Kxg6 30. Rxd7) 27... Kd8 28. Ra5 Bc8 $2 (28... Rd6 29. Z0
{threatening} Qb6+ {was his only move.}) 29. c5 Nxd5 (29... Nxd5 30. Nxd5 Qxd5
31. cxb6 Qxa5 $2 32. Qc6) (29... Rb5 30. Nc6+ Kd7 31. Re7#) (29... Rg6 30. Qd2)
(29... Nh5 30. cxb6 Qxb6+ 31. Kh2) 30. Nxd5 Rc6 31. Nxc6+ Qxc6 32. Qb3 Ne6 33.
Qb6+ Qxb6 34. cxb6 Kd7 35. Bxa6 Bd4+ 36. Kh2 Bxa6 37. Rxa6 Nc5 38. Ra7+ Kc6 39.
Nf6 Kxb6 40. Nxh7 Rg8 41. Rf7 Rg7 42. Rxg7 Bxg7 43. Nf6 Kc6 44. h4 Nd3 45. Kg3
Bf8 46. g6 Nc5 47. Rc2 Kd6 48. Rxc5 1-0

