1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. Bg2 Bg7 6. Nf3 O-O 7. O-O ({
I would prefer} 7. e4) 7... c6 8. Nc3 Be6 $1 {White hadn't considered this
reply.} 9. Ng5 {This doesn'y yurn out too well.} Nxc3 10. bxc3 (10. Nxe6 {
Loses a Pawn.}) 10... Bc4 {Very strong.} ({I also considered.} 10... Bd5) 11.
Re1 e5 {The freeing move.} 12. Nf3 Qa5 {Black has come out of the opening on
top.} 13. Bb2 ({Not.} 13. Qc2 $2 exd4 14. Nxd4 $4 Bxd4 $1 15. cxd4 Qxe1+) 13...
Nd7 14. Qc2 Rfe8 15. Nd2 {White gets rid of my strong Bishop to see it
replaced by a strong Knight.} Nb6 16. Nxc4 Nxc4 17. e3 Rad8 $3 {With a hidden
threat.} 18. Qb3 $2 {Which White misses.} Nxb2 19. Qxb2 exd4 20. Qb4 {Resigns
is no better.} ({The Point. White's Rokk on e1 is weak. He can't reply......} 
20. cxd4 Bxd4) ({Or....} 20. exd4 Rxe1+ 21. Rxe1 Bxd4) 20... Qxb4 21. cxb4 dxe3
22. Rad1 exf2+ 23. Kxf2 Rxe1 $4 {In my hurry to get it over with I didn't
bother to think.} 24. Rxd8+ {As usual, rushing when I thought the game was won.
University won the match 4 - 1.} 1-0

