1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 c6 5. Bg2 Nbd7 6. Nf3 dxc4 {Not very good
as it allows me to play e4.} 7. e4 Bb4 8. Qe2 {[4']} Nb6 $2 9. O-O Bxc3 $2 10.
bxc3 h6 {Black is very badly placed as a result of inferior play.} 11. Ba3 Na4
$2 {Pointless the Knight is eventually lost.} 12. Qxc4 b5 $2 {Hopelessly
weakening.} 13. Qd3 a5 14. Qc2 Ba6 15. Rfe1 Qb6 16. Rab1 {Threatens 17.QxN} Rb8
17. Ne5 Qc7 18. Nd3 h5 $4 19. e5 Nd5 20. Bd6 Qd8 $2 (20... Qc8 $142) 21. Bxd5
exd5 22. Bxb8 Qxb8 23. Qxa4 Qd8 24. Qa3 h4 25. Qd6 Qc8 26. e6 hxg3 27. exf7+
Kxf7 28. Qe7+ Kg6 29. Nf4+ Kh7 30. Nh5 $4 {Trying to find a clever finish but
actually prolonging the game.} gxf2+ 31. Kxf2 ({If...} 31. Kg2 fxe1=N+ $1)
31... Qf5+ 32. Kg1 Qxh5 33. Rb2 {The game is still a win but requires care.
After his opening play I was convinced my opponent was an idiot and I played
accordingly.} Qh6 34. Rg2 Bc8 35. Rf1 $4 Bh3 36. Rxg7+ $4 {Played with great
speed & confidence.} Qxg7+ 37. Qxg7+ Kxg7 38. Rf2 Rf8 39. Rxf8 Kxf8 40. Kf2 Ke7
41. Ke3 Kf6 42. Kd2 Kf5 43. Kc2 Ke4 44. Kb3 Kd3 45. a4 bxa4+ {Another one of
my fiascos due to overconfidence & playing too quickly} 0-1

