1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3
d6 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7 12. Nbd2 Bd7 13. Nf1 Rac8 14. dxe5 ({
More usual is} 14. Ne3 {but I had a different idea in mind.}) 14... dxe5 15.
Bg5 {Intending to exchange off Black's Knight and occupy d5.} Rfd8 16. Qe2 (16.
Bxf6 {seemed playable and if.....} Bxh3 17. Bxe5 $1) 16... Be6 17. Ne3 Nc4 18.
Bxf6 Bxf6 19. Bb3 {I didn't see the full consequences of this move which
reults in a weakening of my KS.} Nxe3 {Forced but best.} 20. Bxe6 {Better than
20.QxN etc.} (20. Qxe3 c4 $1 21. Bc2 Be7 22. Z0 Bc5) 20... Nxg2 21. Bxf7+ (21.
Bxc8 {Loses a piece.}) 21... Qxf7 22. Kxg2 Rc6 {Black is suddenly on top. I
now spent a long time looking for my next move} 23. Rad1 {I lose my a-Pawn...
after 23......RxR. Also Black threatens to double Rooks on the d-file.} (23.
Red1 {I lose my e-pawn} Rxd1 24. Rxd1 Qg6+) (23. a4 c4 {is good.}) 23... Rf8
24. Rd5 Qg6+ 25. Kh2 Bg5 26. Nxe5 {This required careful calculation but seems
sound.} Bf4+ 27. Kh1 Qh6 28. Qg4 {The only move.} (28. Qd3 c4) 28... Bxe5 29.
Rxe5 Rg6 30. Qh5 ({When I played 26.NxP I intended....} 30. Qd7 {and if...}
Rgf6 31. Rf5 {but I now realised this would allow....} Qxh3+) ({If} 30. Rh5 Qd2
31. Qe2 Rxf2 $1) 30... Rxf2 31. Qxh6 ({I didn't like....} 31. Rxc5 Qxh5 32.
Rxh5 {which saves the h-Pawn but leaves my Rook out of play.}) 31... Rxh6 32.
Rxc5 (32. Re3 {May be playable.}) 32... Rxh3+ 33. Kg1 Rhh2 34. Rd1 $2 {The
losing move I missed Black's following manoeuvre.} ({The correct line was} 34.
Rc8+ Kf7 35. Rf1 Rhg2+ (35... Rxf1+ {(-0.27)} 36. Kxh2 Rf2+ 37. Kg3 Rxb2 38.
Rc7+ Kf6 39. Rc6+ Ke5 40. Rxa6 Kxe4 41. a4 Rb3 42. axb5 Rxb5 {Dick used an
engine for this particular line done decades later.}) 36. Kh1 Rxf1+ {When I
can draw as the Black KS Pawns aren't as strong as they look. I considered
this but thought the Black KS Pawns were too strong.} 37. Kxg2 {[60s analysis]}
) 34... Rfg2+ $1 {So as to threaten mate on his next move} 35. Kf1 Rxb2 36. Kg1
Rbg2+ 37. Kf1 Rxa2 38. Kg1 Rag2+ 39. Kf1 Rh1+ 40. Kxg2 Rxd1 {The match rules
stated that the match was to last 3hrs. The Clocks were set for 90 mins and
the game was to be lost by whoever's flag fell first. We now only had a few
minutes each so I played on.} 41. Rc8+ Kf7 42. Rc7+ Kf8 43. Rc8+ Ke7 44. Rc7+
Rd7 45. Rc6 Ra7 46. Rb6 a5 47. Rxb5 a4 48. Rb2 a3 49. Ra2 Ke6 50. Kf3 Ke5 51.
Ke3 Ra4 52. Kd3 h5 53. c4 h4 54. c5 h3 55. c6 Kd6 56. Rc2 Kc7 {Resigns I was
down on time as well. The B.C.F U-21 beat The Chess Education Society 12.5 - 9.
5 [W.Hartston was on bd5!)} 0-1

