1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d3 Bc5 {Good alternatives are......} (3... Nf6) (3... d5
) 4. Be2 (4. g3 {White could transpose into a Kings Indian with.}) 4... d6 5.
O-O f5 6. Nc3 {Now I get a strong KS innitiative.} ({Also good was...} 6. Be3
Bb6 7. exf5) 6... f4 {Severely cramping White.} 7. Nb5 {Trying to force d5.} a6
8. d4 Bb6 9. d5 Nce7 ({Better than..} 9... axb5 10. Bxb5 $1 {after which Black
is weak on the QS and White gets a passed a-Pawn.}) 10. Nc3 h6 {Black has
plenty of time to prepare his KS attack.} ({Not} 10... g5 $2 11. Nxg5 Nxd5 12.
Nxd5 Qxg5 13. Nxb6 cxb6 14. Qxd6) 11. Nh4 {This slows Black down temporarily.
White's only hope was to advance quickly on the QS.} g6 {Prevents the check at
h5.} 12. a3 {White can undertake nothing.} Nf6 13. Qd3 g5 14. Nf3 (14. Nf5 Bxf5
15. exf5 Qd7 {winning a Pawn.}) 14... Ng6 15. b4 Bg4 {Intending to exchange
off the Knight then to play .....g4.} ({If immediately.....} 15... g4 16. Nd2 {
and as soon as...} g3 {then} 17. Nf3) 16. Nd2 h5 17. h3 {This hastens the end
but it was only a matter of time.} Qe7 {This piece sacrifice is the quickest
route to victory. I played 17......Qe7 in preference to 17......Qd7 so as to
be able tp penetrate on the black squares if necessary, as White has his Queen
defending h3.} 18. hxg4 (18. Nf3 Bxf3 19. Qxf3 g4 20. hxg4 hxg4 21. Qd3 Nxe4
22. Nxe4 Qh4) 18... hxg4 19. Bxg4 {Resigns is no better} Nxg4 20. Rd1 Nxf2 {
Southampton Uni won 3.5 - 1-5} 0-1

