1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 {I didn't want to play a Q.G.D so I
transposed to a catalan.} c6 5. Bg2 Bd6 ({Somewhat better is....} 5... Be7 {
I think.}) 6. Bg5 {Black's 5......Bd6 has maent that I will be able to play e4
threatening a fork with e5 and if .......PxP, NxP will threaten the Queen on
f6 (after BxN) and the Bishop on d6.} h6 (6... Z0 7. Bxf6 Qxf6 8. e4 dxe4 9.
Nxe4) ({I thought he might play} 6... Qa5 {as} 7. Bxf6 gxf6 {merely
strengthens his centre.}) 7. Bxf6 Qxf6 8. Nf3 Nd7 9. e4 ({I considered} 9. a3 {
to prevent the Bishop check, which occurs in the game, but the extra move
allows Black to force....} e5 {or .....e5 after ......PxP}) 9... dxe4 10. Nxe4
Bb4+ 11. Nc3 Bxc3+ 12. bxc3 O-O 13. O-O Rd8 {The Rook doesn't turn out to be
so well placed as Black had hoped. White has got much the better out of the
opening and Black will have to play well to survive.} ({The immediate....} 
13... e5 {is answered by} 14. Re1) 14. Re1 {Prevents 14......e5} c5 {He must
play this to get any freedom at all.} 15. d5 $1 {This is very strong.} Nb6 {
Black may have been relying on this but White has a neat reply} ({If} 15...
Qxc3 16. dxe6 fxe6 17. Rxe6 Qxc4 18. Ne5 $1 Qxe6 19. Bd5 Nxe5 20. Bxe6+ Bxe6
21. Qe2 Rd5 22. f4) 16. Ne5 $1 {Protecting both c-Pawns and further
restricting Black's game.} exd5 17. cxd5 Qd6 (17... Bf5 {Would seem to free
his game somewhat but White is still on top.}) 18. Qh5 {Black probably
overlooked this strong move which prevents 18......f6, and allows me to play
c4 strengthening my grip.} Rf8 19. c4 Nd7 20. Rab1 {Steadily increasing the
pressure.} Nxe5 21. Qxe5 Qa6 (21... Qxe5 22. Rxe5 {and Black is lost. His
Bishop is immoble and White can play Re7 & d6 and his b-Pawn falls.}) 22. d6
Qxc4 (22... Qxa2 {is playable.}) 23. Bxb7 Bxb7 24. Rxb7 Rad8 $2 {This loses
Black was scared of the d-pawn advancing further.} ({After} 24... Qxa2 {
Black has good drawing chances.}) 25. Rxa7 Qd3 26. Qxc5 Rxd6 {With all the
major pieces on Black probably thought he had reasonable drawing chances.
However with White's pieces better placed he has all the chances for a win.}
27. a4 Ra6 ({Not for example...} 27... Rf6 {hoping for a counterattack because
of..} 28. Qxf8+ $3) 28. a5 Ra8 29. Rxa8+ Rxa8 30. Re7 $1 {Very strong.} (30.
Ra1 Ra6 {isn't too good.}) 30... Qa6 (30... Ra6 31. Rb7 Z0 32. Rb6) 31. Qe5 Rf8
32. Rb7 Qe6 {Desperation. White threatens 33.Nb6.32......Resigns would be
better.} 33. Qxe6 fxe6 34. a6 Ra8 35. a7 Kh7 36. Re7 e5 37. Kg2 Kg6 38. Kf3 Kf6
39. Rb7 g5 40. Rb6+ Kf5 {Putting an end to it.} ({If} 40... Kg7 41. Kg4 Z0 42.
Kh5 {and the Black Pawns go.}) 41. g4# {1 Southampton Uni won 7 -} 1-0

