{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours.} 1. d4 f5 2. e4 fxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nc6 {
I didn't Know this variation at all.} 5. f3 d5 ({After} 5... exf3 6. Nxf3 {
I'm quite well placed.}) 6. fxe4 {I'm more or less forced to play this now.}
dxe4 {Rather better than 6......NxP which I expected} 7. d5 Ne5 8. Qd4 Nf7 9.
Bxf6 {[29']} exf6 {[1'30s]} 10. Qxe4+ ({Better is} 10. Nxe4 {as soon becomes
apparent.}) 10... Be7 11. Nf3 O-O 12. O-O-O f5 {At this stage I had taken
about 45 minutes whilst Black who knows it all as book had only taken a few
minutes.} 13. Qd3 Bf6 14. g3 {[52']} Qd6 15. Bg2 Bd7 16. Qc4 $2 {Probably the
losing move. However White's position isn't particularly good. My f-Knight
couldn't move without leaving e5 weak.} (16. Rhe1 {Was probably better.}) 16...
b5 {[16'] I'd missed this} 17. Qd3 {[70']} Qc5 18. Rhe1 {[75']} Rae8 19. Nb1 {
I was hoping to play Nd2-b3-d4} ({Good moves are conspicuous by their absence.
eg.} 19. Nd4 $2 Rxe1 $1) 19... Nd6 {[33']} 20. Nbd2 {[97'] The only move to
cover both c4 & e4. I now had to make 20 moves in 23' Black had 1hr 27'} ({Not
} 20. Qa3 $2 Nc4 $3) 20... f4 {[42']} 21. Nb3 {[102')} Qf2 {[53']} 22. Qd2 $2 {
[105'] In time trouble I miss his reply.} Bxb2+ 23. Kb1 {[105']} Qb6 24. Rxe8 {
[112']} (24. Bf1 {to cover c4} fxg3 {attacking the Knight.}) 24... Bxe8 25. Ng5
{[113']} Nc4 26. Qd3 {Threatening mate no less!} Bg6 27. Be4 Qf6 28. Nxh7 Na3#
{After taking so long over the opening I would have been lucky to survive.
Hayes lost the match 2.5 - 3.5} 0-1

