1. d4 e5 {A gambit type line which my opponent was apparently familiar with.}
2. dxe5 Nc6 3. Nf3 ({If} 3. f4 {My opponent intended.} d6 {with good play})
3... Qe7 4. Nc3 {Giving the Pawn back for central control.} Nxe5 5. e4 c6 {
To prevent 6.Nd5} 6. Nxe5 Qxe5 7. f4 Qc7 8. Bd3 (8. Bc4 b5 9. Bd3 b4) 8... Bc5
9. Qg4 g6 10. f5 d6 11. Bf4 Bd4 {Rather an odd position} 12. Qg3 Be5 13. O-O
Bd7 ({Not} 13... Nf6 14. fxg6 fxg6 15. Bxe5 {Winning the Knight}) 14. Bc4 {
Now Black is embarassed for a continuation.} O-O-O {Giving up a Pawn for some
play} 15. Bxf7 gxf5 {Opening files to my King.} 16. Bxe5 dxe5 17. exf5 Nh6 18.
Be6 Bxe6 19. fxe6 Rhg8 20. Qe3 Qg7 21. g3 Rd4 {Black has quite good
counterplay now.} 22. Rad1 Ng4 23. Qe2 Rxd1 24. Rxd1 Qe7 {Winning back the
Pawn but giving me all the play} 25. Ne4 $1 {Best. Black threatened 25......
Qc5+ etc.} (25. Qe4) (25. Rd7 {Were both very bad.}) 25... Qxe6 26. Qd3 {
With a neat threat which Black overlooks.} h5 $2 ({His only chance seems to be.
...} 26... Nf6) 27. Nd6+ Kb8 28. Qh7 1-0

