1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. d4 Nxd4 {Seems to equalise} 6. Nxe5
Bc5 7. c3 Ne6 8. Bc2 {White is now badly behind in development.} O-O {[22']} 9.
Nf3 {[27']} d6 {[23']} 10. O-O Bd7 11. Nbd2 Bc6 12. h3 {Black has won the
opening and is well on top.} Ba7 {Intending something like ......Nf5-g6-e5
without having to worry about Nb3.} 13. Re1 Nc5 14. Nd4 {This doesn't help his
development.} Qd7 15. Nxc6 Qxc6 16. e5 {Trying to get some play.} dxe5 17. Rxe5
Qd6 {Better than......} (17... Rad8 18. Qe2) 18. Re1 (18. Rg5 {is rather risky.
}) 18... Rad8 19. Qf3 b5 {Prevents 20.Nc4. The b-Pawn was rather weak.} 20. Nf1
Qd5 {[57'] We were both very short of time, 4 moves to make in 3 minutes.} 21.
Qxd5 Nxd5 22. Ne3 Rfe8 23. Rd1 Nf6 {So as to occupy e5 with an eye on f2.} 24.
Bd2 Nce4 25. Be1 g6 26. Rxd8 Rxd8 27. Rd1 Re8 {Threatening 28......Nxf2} 28.
Ng4 ({If} 28. Nd5 Nxd5 29. Rxd5 Nf6 30. Rd1 Re2) 28... Nxg4 29. hxg4 Nf6 30. g5
Ng4 31. c4 {To prevent 31......Re2.32.Rd8+ Kg7 33.Bc3+ Adjudicated. White
resigned before adjudication.} (31. c4 {Black wins by.....} Rxe1+ 32. Rxe1
Bxf2+ 33. Kf1 Bxe1 34. Kxe1 Ne3 {and now...} 35. cxb5 (35. Bd3 bxc4 36. Be4 Nf5
37. Kd2 Nd6 38. Bd5 Kg7 39. Kc3 f6 40. gxf6+ Kxf6 41. Bxc4 Nxc4 {and Black
Queens in 3 moves before White.}) 35... Nxc2+ 36. Kd2 Nb4 37. a3 axb5 $1) 0-1

