{Time control 24 moves per hour.} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 dxc4 4. a4 ({
Interesting is} 4. e3 b5 5. Nxb5 $6 {?} cxb5 6. Qf3 Qc7 $1 7. Qxa8 Bb7 8. Qxa7
e5 $1 {Threat ......Nc6} 9. d5 Bc5 {What does White reply?} 10. Bxc4) 4... Nf6
({M.C.O. (9th Edn) gives...} 4... e5) 5. Nf3 Bg4 {Doubtful. Now I get a sort
of Krause Attack with a couple of extra tempi.} 6. Ne5 Nbd7 {Doubtful. Now I
get a wedge in the centre.} 7. Nxg4 Nxg4 8. e4 {[4'] The match lasted only 2.5
hrs so I was determined to play aggressively and quickly when I saw my way
clear.} Ngf6 9. e5 Nd5 10. Bxc4 e6 11. O-O Be7 12. Qg4 g6 {[30']} 13. Ne4 {[9']
} N7b6 {Black was steadily going downhill and was well behind me on the clock.}
14. Bb3 {[13']} h5 {[32'] Black is reduced to these drastic measures already.}
15. Qf3 {[15']} g5 $2 {[37'] Hopelessy weakening but he was probably lost
anyway.} 16. h3 {[28']} Kd7 $2 {[42'] Getting short of time Black could find
nothing better.} (16... Z0 {White threatened...} 17. a5 {Forcing} Nc8 ({if} 
17... Nd7 18. Bxg5 $1)) ({The only reasonable move for Black was....} 16... a5)
17. Qxf7 {[27' 30s]} Kc7 {He could resign.} 18. Nc5 {[31']} Qg8 19. Nxe6+ Kd7
20. Nc5+ Kc7 21. Ne6+ Kd7 22. Nxg5 {Black lost on time. Hayes won the match 6.
5 - 1.5} 1-0

