1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7. d5 e6 8. Be2 exd5
9. exd5 Nh5 {AS played by Spassky.} 10. O-O Re8 {The Rook gains little from
the e-file.} ({A better plan was} 10... f5 {preventing White from advancing on
the KS.}) 11. Bd3 Bxc3 {Played with the idea of putting the Knight on g7.
However he is left very weak on the Black squares.} (11... f5 {was still best.}
) 12. bxc3 Ng7 13. h3 Bf5 (13... Nd7 $142) 14. Bxf5 Nxf5 15. g4 Ne3 $2 {
The 5-times moved Knight is now exchanged for my unmoved Bishop, leaving Black
hopelessy placed.} (15... Nh4 $142 {to which I would have replied.} 16. Nh2 $1)
16. Bxe3 Rxe3 17. Qd2 Re8 18. Rab1 (18. f5 {is quicker.}) 18... b6 {Anything
loses.} 19. f5 Kg7 {Trying totrengthen his Black squares.} ({if} 19... gxf5 20.
Qh6 Z0 21. Ng5) 20. f6+ $1 Qxf6 (20... Kg8 21. Qh6) 21. Ng5 Qe5 22. Rxf7+ Kg8
23. Rbf1 Re7 {Shortens the agony Black had no move.} ({Now} 23... Qg3+ 24. Kh1
{and Black has no move}) (23... Qe3+ 24. Qxe3 Rxe3 25. Rf8+ Kg7 26. Ne6+ Kh6
27. g5+ {followed by.....} Kh5 28. R8f7 Z0 29. Rxh7#) 24. Rf8+ Kg7 25. Ne6+ {
2 Uni won the match 3 -} 1-0

