1. e4 e5 2. Bc4 Nf6 3. d3 Bc5 4. Be3 Bb6 5. Nc3 c6 6. Bxb6 axb6 7. Qd2 d5 8.
exd5 cxd5 9. Bb3 {Now Black has the better of it with his strong centre.} ({
Somewhat better was} 9. Bb5+ Nc6) 9... O-O 10. O-O-O $2 {White can't hope to
get a KS attack as quickly as Black on the QS as he doesn't have any central
control.} Nc6 11. Nge2 Na5 12. Ba4 d4 13. Nb1 (13. Nb5 {is risky.}) ({if} 13.
Ne4 Nxe4 14. dxe4 Nc4 {is strong.}) 13... Be6 14. b3 Qc7 15. Kb2 Nc6 {Threat
16......Ra5 followed by 17......b5. There are various combinational
possibilities knocking about.} 16. c4 {Desperate measures.} Ra5 17. Na3 Rfa8
18. Nb5 Qe7 19. a3 Rc8 {To play 20......Nd7 then 21......Nc5} 20. h3 {White
can do nothing more on the QS.} Nd7 21. f4 f6 22. g4 Nc5 23. Ra1 Nxa4+ 24. bxa4
Rxa4 25. Qc2 Rca8 26. Qb3 Na5 $2 {The result of playing quickly as the time
control was drawing near. This is the trouble with theses short matches, as it
is an advantage not to adjourn so one hurries to try to finish in one session.}
27. Qxa4 Nxc4+ 28. Qxc4 Bxc4 29. dxc4 exf4 30. Nexd4 Qe3 31. Rae1 Qd2+ 32. Kb3
({I would have preffered} 32. Ka1) 32... Qd3+ 33. Kb4 Qd2+ 34. Kb3 Qd3+ 35. Kb4
{3 University lost the match 2 -} 1/2-1/2

