1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 b6 5. Bg2 Bb7 6. Nf3 Be7 7. cxd5 exd5 8. O-O
O-O 9. a3 Nbd7 10. b4 Ne4 11. Qc2 c5 {Slightly premature .The Knight on e4
needs more support first.} 12. bxc5 bxc5 13. Rb1 Bc6 (13... Rb8 14. Bf4) (13...
Qc7 14. Bf4) 14. dxc5 Bxc5 {Black's pieces, which are apparently strongly
placed are lacking in support especially the c6 Bishop.} 15. Nxe4 dxe4 16. Nd2
{Showing up Black's weaknesses.} Rc8 (16... f5 {Holds the Pawn but is very
weakening.}) 17. Nxe4 Bxe4 18. Qxe4 (18. Bxe4 $4 Bxf2+) 18... Nf6 19. Qf3 {
The best square. On f3 the Queen gaurds the e & h Pawns, and prevents 19......
Nh5} ({If instead} 19. Qh4 Qe8) 19... Re8 20. Bg5 h6 21. Rfd1 Qe7 22. Bxf6 {
About the only move to hold all the Pawns.} gxf6 $6 ({I intended to answer} 
22... Qxf6 {with} 23. Rd3) 23. Qg4+ Kf8 24. Qh5 Kg7 ({Not} 24... Qxe2 25. Qxh6+
Kg8 26. Qxf6 {Gaurds f2}) 25. Qg4+ Kf8 26. Qh5 {The repetition was to gain
time on the clock.} Kg7 27. Rb7 Rc7 ({Not} 27... Qe6 28. Bd5) 28. Rdb1 (28.
Rxc7 Qxc7 29. Qg4+ Kf8 30. Rd7 {Doesn't get me anywhere definite.}) 28... Bb6
29. Qg4+ Kf8 30. Rxc7 Qxc7 31. e3 Qc2 32. Rd1 Re5 33. Qb4+ {I was getting
short of time here.} Kg7 34. Qd2 {A safe move made in a hurry.} ({I avoided} 
34. Qd6 Bc5 {winning the a-Pawn.}) 34... Qxd2 35. Rxd2 Rxe3 $5 {? We were both
in time trouble here.} 36. Ra2 $4 ({Obviously} 36. fxe3 Bxe3+ 37. Rf2 {wins
but I didn't have time to see it.}) 36... Re1+ 37. Bf1 {1 Once again the clock
secures my opponent half a point. (c.f. previous game) Uni won the match 4 -}
1/2-1/2

