{Time control 24 moves per hour.} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. g3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5.
Bg2 Be6 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. O-O Be7 8. d3 {[6']} Nb6 {[2' 30s]} 9. Be3 {[9'30s]} O-O
{[3'30s]} (9... f5 {would prevent 10.d4. but castling is perfectly good.}) 10.
d4 exd4 11. Nxd4 Nxd4 12. Bxd4 {[13']} c6 {[11']} 13. Rc1 {[19'] The Rook
doesn't have much scope here and a minority attack was White's best plan.} Nd5
{[23']} ({If} 13... Nc4 {threatening 14......Nxb or 14......c5 15.Be3 NxB
White replies....} 14. Na4 {followed by occupation of c5.}) 14. a3 (14. Na4 {
is answered by....} Qa5) 14... Qa5 {A good square for the Queen. The threat is
15......Rd8} 15. Nxd5 Bxd5 16. e4 (16. Bxd5 Qxd5 {I double on the d-file.})
16... Be6 {[27']} 17. Bc3 Qb6 {[33']} 18. Qd4 $2 {Very doubtful. He is left
with one bad Bishop, one moderate Bishop , a weak Pawn structure, whilst I
have two good Bishops and control of the d-file.} Qxd4 19. Bxd4 Rfd8 20. Be3 $2
{Loses a pawn} ({Due to my ability to play 20.....Bb3 White can't contest the
d-file.e.g.} 20. Rfd1 Rd7 21. Rd2 Rad8 22. Rcd1 Bb3) (20. Bc3 Rd3 {I have much
the better of it.}) 20... Bf6 {[35']} 21. Rb1 {[56']} Ba2 {[36'30s] Missing
the road at first but White was sos hort of time so I didn't take too long
over this.} 22. Rbc1 ({Not} 22. Ra1 $2 Bc4) 22... Be6 {[41']} 23. Rb1 Bc4 {
[42'30s] Winning the Pawn.} 24. Rfe1 {[59']} ({Not} 24. Rfd1 Bd3) 24... Bd3 {
[44']} 25. Ra1 {Having got over his time-trouble White finds the correct move.}
({Bad would be} 25. Rbd1 $2 Bxb2 26. Z0 {threatening....} Bc3) 25... Bxb2 26.
Ra2 Bc3 27. Rc1 {Again best.} (27. Rd1 Bc4 28. Rxd8+ Rxd8 {threatens 29......
Rd1+}) 27... Ba5 28. Rb2 Ba6 ({Not} 28... Rd7 29. Bh3 Rc7 30. Bf4) 29. a4 {
[80']} Rd7 {[52']} 30. Bh3 {Adjourned.} Rdd8 {[Sealed move] Play resumed 3/3/
64 Black has a fairly clear win once he has disentangled the QS. White's
pieces have no scope. I intended ......Bc7-e5-d4} 31. Bf1 {There seems no
reason to provoke this exchange.} Bxf1 32. Kxf1 Rd7 33. Ke2 h6 {Strengthening
the position.} (33... Bb6 34. Bxb6 axb6 35. Rxb6 Rxa4 36. Rcxc6 $1) 34. Rcc2 f6
35. h4 {White's best bet was to sit tight.} Kf7 36. g4 g5 37. hxg5 hxg5 38. e5
$6 {White's passive position did not warrant this opening of the KS.} fxe5 39.
Bxg5 $2 {Doubtful} (39. Rc5 $142 Bb6 40. Rxe5 Bxe3 41. Rxe3) 39... Rg8 40. f4 (
40. Rc5 {Loses his bRook!!} Rxg5 41. Rxa5 b6 $1 42. f4 Rxg4 43. Rxe5 Rg2+)
40... Bb6 41. Rc4 Bd4 42. Rd2 Ke6 ({Not} 42... c5 43. Rxc5) 43. fxe5 (43. f5+ {
Loses a piece.}) 43... c5 ({Not} 43... Kxe5 44. Bf4+) 44. Be3 Rxg4 45. Kf3 Rh4
46. Bxd4 cxd4 ({Not} 46... Rhxd4 47. Rcxd4 $1 cxd4 48. Ke4) 47. Rc5 Rh3+ 48.
Ke4 Re3+ 49. Kf4 Rf7+ 50. Kg4 Rxe5 51. Rc4 Re4+ {1 University won the match 4 -
} 0-1

