1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 c5 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Bd3 d5 7. O-O Nc6 8. Ne2 {
An attempt to take advantage of the position of Black's Bishop.} dxc4 9. Bxc4
cxd4 10. exd4 {In return for an isolated Pawn I have good play for all my
pieces.} Qc7 11. Qc2 Na5 12. b3 b5 $6 {Very risky. Black is more ambitious
than he has a right to be.} 13. Bf4 Qc6 14. Ne5 Qe8 (14... Qb6 {seems playable.
}) 15. Bd3 h6 {Not really necessary.} 16. a3 Be7 (16... Bd6 {was playable but
a bit risky.}) 17. b4 Nb7 18. Nc6 a6 19. a4 {The decisive breakthrough on the
QS, winning me a Pawn.} bxa4 20. Rxa4 Bd7 21. Nxe7+ Qxe7 22. Rxa6 {My b-Pawn
is safe as show in the variation below.} Nd5 (22... Rxa6 23. Bxa6 Qxb4 $4 24.
Rb1) 23. Bd2 Nd6 {Preparing to blockade the b-Pawn.} 24. Rfa1 Rxa6 25. Rxa6 Rc8
26. Qb2 Bb5 27. Bxb5 Nxb5 28. Ra5 Qb7 29. Ra1 Rc4 30. Qb3 Qc7 31. Qd3 {The
threat is 32.Ra8+ a theme that reoccurs throughout the game.} Qc6 32. Rb1 Qc7
33. h3 ({Not} 33. Rc1 $2 Rxc1+ 34. Nxc1 Nxb4 $1) 33... Qc6 34. Qg3 Qc7 35. Qd3
Qc6 {I decided that the positional manoeuvering wasn't getting me anywhere so
I decided on a direct KS assault.} 36. g4 Ndc3 {Black decides not to sit tight
any longer, but this may have been his best plan.} 37. Nxc3 Nxc3 {Adjourned.}
38. Bxc3 {[Play resumed 17/2/64] The sealed move.} ({I chose 38.Bxc3 in
preference to} 38. Rc1 {as I thought it would have surprise value.} Ne2+ 39.
Qxe2 Rxc1+ 40. Bxc1 Qxc1+ 41. Kg2 {Black has good drawing chances with only
Queens on.}) 38... Rxc3 39. b5 (39. Qf1 {Is playable but hardly attractive.})
39... Qc7 {By far the best move.} ({e.g.} 39... Rc1+ 40. Rxc1 Qxc1+ 41. Kg2 Qb2
42. Qc4 {followed by...} Z0 43. Qc6 {etc.}) (39... Qc8 40. Qe4 Rxh3 41. b6 $1
Qb8 (41... Rc3 42. b7 Qb8 43. Ra1 {etc.}) 42. Qe5 Qb7 43. d5 {followed by......
} Z0 44. Qc7) (39... Rxd3 40. bxc6 Rc3 41. Rb6 Kh7 {best} 42. f4 Kg6 43. Kf2 {
etc.}) 40. b6 $6 {I hadn't done much anaysis and had completely overlooked
Black's next move.} Qxb6 {Obvious and the only move, but now I gat a very
strong position.} ({I had only considered} 40... Qc6 $4 41. Qxc3 $1) 41. Qe4
Qc7 42. Rb7 Qc8 43. Ra7 Ra3 44. Rb7 Ra1+ ({Rather better it seems was...} 44...
Rxh3 45. Qb1 Rc3 46. Kg2 Qf8) 45. Kg2 Rc1 $2 {loses a Pawn.} (45... Ra3 $142)
46. Ra7 Rc6 47. Qf3 Qe8 (47... f6 {Holds the Pawn but after} 48. d5 exd5 49.
Qxd5+ Kh8 50. Qf7 Qg8 51. Qd7 {leaves him in a very unhappy position.}) 48.
Rxf7 Rd6 (48... Qxf7 {Leaves him better drawing chances.}) 49. Rf4 ({Not} 49.
Qf4 Rd8 {Winning my d-Pawn.}) 49... g5 {Very weakening. Better was to sit
tight.} 50. Re4 Qd8 51. Qe3 Kf7 52. h4 {Taking advantage of the weakness
caused by his 49th.} Qf6 53. hxg5 hxg5 $2 ({His last hope was} 53... Qxg5 {
but his chances aren't very good.}) 54. f4 Kg6 55. Rxe6 (55. fxg5 {Probably
wins although Black makes life difficult by NOT replying...} Qxg5 $2 56. Rxe6+
Rxe6 57. Qxe6+ {Forcing a Queen exchange.} Kg7 (57... Kh7 58. Qf5+) 58. Qe5+)
55... Rxe6 56. f5+ Kf7 57. fxe6+ Ke7 58. Qa3+ Ke8 59. Qa8+ ({and not the
crushing} 59. Qd6 $4 {because of} Qf2+ $3) 59... Ke7 60. Qb7+ Ke8 61. Qf7+ Qxf7
62. exf7+ Kxf7 63. Kf3 Ke6 64. Ke4 {1 University won 3 -} 1-0

