1. d4 g6 2. e4 Bg7 3. c4 d6 4. f4 c5 5. d5 e6 6. Nc3 exd5 7. exd5 Ne7 {An
interesting move. Whites thematicmove in this sort of position is 8.f5 , hence
Black decides to occupy this square. Also the long black diagonal is kept open.
However on e7 the Knight does not cover e5.} ({After} 7... Nf6 {we are in the
usual line of the 4-Pawns attack against the King's Indian.}) 8. Nf3 a6 9. Bd3
Bf5 10. Ne4 {I don't want to exchange my bishop.} Qc7 ({Rather more
enterprising was.} 10... Bxe4 11. Bxe4 b5) 11. a4 {To prevent the above line.}
Nd7 12. O-O O-O 13. a5 Nf6 14. Ng3 {So as to play f5. The Knights are well
placed on the KS.} Bxd3 15. Qxd3 b5 16. axb6 Qxb6 17. f5 {Verys strong Black
has no good move now.} Rae8 {This is very cramping. Probably better was 17.....
.Ra7 although his position was hardly to be envied.} 18. fxg6 hxg6 ({Not} 18...
fxg6 19. Ng5 Z0 20. Ne6) ({Nor} 18... Nxg6 19. Ng5 Z0 20. h4 Z0 21. h5) 19. h4
{Threat 20.Ng5, 20.h5} Nh5 $2 {Suicidal, but what could he play?} (19... Ng4
$142) 20. Nxh5 gxh5 21. Ng5 Ng6 {[53']} 22. Qf3 {[35']} Bd4+ {[60'] Black
could resign.} 23. Kh1 Kg7 {Shortening the agony. Anything else lost in the
long run.} 24. Qxh5 Rh8 25. Rxf7+ Kg8 26. Qxg6+ {1 University won the match 4 -
} 1-0

