1. d4 Nf6 2. g3 d5 3. Bg2 e6 4. Nf3 c5 5. O-O Nc6 6. c3 {This set up doesn't
turn out too well.} (6. c4 $142) 6... Be7 7. b3 {This too is doubtful. Better
to try to force e4.} O-O 8. Qc2 Ne4 9. Ne5 f5 10. Bb2 {[35']} Bd7 {[14']} 11.
Nd2 Rc8 {Threatening 12......PxP Black now has much the better of it.} 12. f3 {
A useful move which allows the folllow up e4.} Nf6 ({I also considered the
variation} 12... Nxc3 13. Nxc6 Nxe2+ 14. Kf2 Rxc6 15. Kxe2 cxd4 16. Qd3 e5 {
Which is good for me. However I didn't see the point in taking chances as I ws
on top anyway.}) 13. Qd1 g5 {To prevent 14.f4 & intending ......f5} 14. e4 f4 {
Securing a strong position on the KS.} 15. Nxc6 Bxc6 16. exd5 $2 {Probably the
losing move.} (16. e5 {was essential although Black is still on top.}) 16...
Nxd5 {Now White's weakness on e3 is ruinous.} 17. Bh3 Bd7 18. Qe2 Ne3 19. Rf2
$2 (19. Rfc1 $142 {but it would only prolong the game.}) 19... cxd4 20. cxd4
Rc2 21. gxf4 gxf4 22. Rb1 Bh4 {Alternatives also win.} (22... Bb4) (22... Qa5)
23. Rg2+ Nxg2 24. Qxg2+ ({If} 24. Bxe6+ Bxe6 25. Qxe6+ Rf7 {is easy for Black.}
) 24... Qg5 25. Qxg5+ Bxg5 26. Ne4 Bf6 {Threatening 27......RxB} 27. Nxf6+ Rxf6
28. d5 Rg6+ 29. Kh1 Kf7 30. Bg4 Ke7 {Adjourned. White could have resigned but
instead he sealed.} 31. Ba3+ {[Sealed Move] About the only move. Play resumed
27/2/64} Kd8 32. Rd1 e5 33. Bxd7 Kxd7 34. Rc1 Rxc1+ 35. Bxc1 Kd6 36. Bb2 Kxd5
37. Bc3 e4 38. fxe4+ Kxe4 39. Be1 Ke3 40. Bb4 f3 41. Bc5+ Ke2 1-0

