1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5. Nxc6 {This is the usual move
against 4......Nf6, but against 4......Bc5 5.Be3 is better, as now my KBishop
has a strong diagonal.} (5. Be3 $142) 5... bxc6 6. Bc4 Qh4 {Taking the
innitiative already.} 7. Qf3 (7. O-O {Was rather better his King is now open
to attack.}) 7... d5 {Defending against the threatened mate and opening up the
QBishops diagonal.} 8. Bd3 {He gains nothing by giving up the e-Pawn.} Nf6 9.
exd5 {Black has various threats 10......PxP, 10......Ng4, 10......Bg4 9.PxP
opens the e-file and he would probably have done better with 9.Nc3 with some
hopes of castling QS.} (9. Nc3 $142) 9... O-O $1 {I now have a vast lead in
dvelopment.} 10. Qg3 $4 {Suicide.} ({The only move was} 10. O-O {but Black
would have been well on top.}) 10... Re8+ 11. Kf1 (11. Be3 Bxe3 12. Qxh4 Bg5+)
11... Qh5 12. Nc3 Ng4 13. Be2 (13. Ne4 Rxe4 $1 14. Bxe4 Nxh2+ 15. Kg1 Bd6 16.
Qd3 Ba6 17. Qd2 Re8 {With a very strong attack.}) 13... Rxe2 $1 14. Nxe2 Ba6
15. Be3 $2 {Putting a quick end to it.} (15. Qh3 Nxh2+ $1) ({His only move was
} 15. f3 $1 Re8 16. fxg4 Bxe2+ 17. Ke1 Qxd5 {etc.}) 15... Nxe3+ {1 University
won the match 4 -} 0-1

