1. d4 Nf6 2. e3 {This didn't please me particularly. I didn't want a stodgy
blocked position in a 2hr 15 min match. White, I suspect, had hopes of a draw.}
d5 3. Bd3 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. f4 cxd4 {[10'] Hoping to be able to open the
position somewhat.} 6. exd4 Bg4 7. Nf3 Qc7 {With thoughts of castling QS.} 8.
O-O e6 9. h3 Bh5 10. Qa4 {Threatening 11.Ne5} Bxf3 11. Rxf3 Bd6 (11... Nd7 {
possibly ofefred better chances.}) 12. Na3 {Forcing the exchange of Knight for
Bishop.} O-O (12... a6 {is no good.}) 13. Nb5 Qd7 14. Nxd6 Qxd6 15. f5 {
Possibly a bit premature.} e5 {Risky but I didn't want a draw.} 16. dxe5 Nxe5
17. Rg3 {Better than 17.Re3 etc.} (17. Re3 Qc5 18. Qd4 Qxd4 19. cxd4 Nxd3 20.
Rxd3 Ne4) 17... Qb6+ $6 {Fishing in troubled waters.} (17... Nxd3 {is sound
but I was hoping for more.}) 18. Be3 Qxb2 $6 {And this should lose against
correct play, but I was relying on my opponents hopes of drawing to prevent
him looking hard for a win. This is a risky policy which I wouldn't employ in
a tournament but in a 2hr 15' match one has to take chances tow in.} 19. Rb1
Qxc3 20. Bd4 Qc7 21. Re1 $2 {White misses his chance.} ({Correct was} 21. Ba1
$3 {maintaining the pin and allowing the queen to come to the KS. e.g.} Nxd3
22. Qh4 {wins in all variations. Granted 21.Ba1 was a difficult move to find.})
21... Nxd3 {Securing at least equality. However White can just achieve his
draw.} 22. Rxg7+ Kxg7 23. Bxf6+ Kxf6 24. Qh4+ {2 White gets a perpetual check.
University won 3 -} 1/2-1/2

