1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3
O-O 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Bb7 12. Nbd2 Qc7 (12... cxd4 {is more usual 
[as in my game v A.Bamford Hants v Sussex 64]}) 13. d5 Bc8 14. b4 Nb7 (14...
cxb4 15. cxb4 Nc4) 15. a4 bxa4 {Otherwise White plays 16.a5 killing my QS
chances.} 16. Rxa4 Bd7 17. Ra2 Bb5 18. Nf1 Bxf1 {More or less forced as his
Knight is better than my Bishop after 19.Ne3} 19. Rxf1 ({Not} 19. Kxf1 $2 cxb4
20. cxb4 $4 Qc4+) 19... Nd7 ({Unfortunately I can't win a Pawn by} 19... cxb4
20. cxb4 Qc4 {because of} 21. Ra4) 20. Qe2 cxb4 21. cxb4 a5 22. b5 Nbc5 23. Be3
Nb6 (23... Ra7 {was possibly stronger.}) 24. Rfa1 f5 $2 {The natural freeing
move but played without due consideration as time was getting short.} 25. exf5
Nxd5 $4 {I intended this move when I played my last & gave it little thought
before playing it.} 26. Bxc5 $4 ({Despite having more time than me White
misses the win of a piece by} 26. Qc4) 26... Qxc5 27. Rxa5 Rxa5 28. Rxa5 Nc3 {
Much the best move.} 29. Qe3 Qxe3 30. fxe3 Rb8 (30... Bd8 {is no good when my
Rook is pretty useless and my d-Pawn is weak.}) 31. Bb3+ Kf8 {4 Here he
offered a draw which I accepted. University lost the match 3 -} 1/2-1/2

