{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 g6 4. e4 d6 5. f4
Bg7 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Be2 Re8 (7... c5 $142 {transposing into the Yugoslav
variation of the Kings Indian.}) 8. O-O b6 (8... c5 $142 {Black must attack
the Black centre.}) 9. Bd3 Bb7 10. Ng5 (10. Ng5 {threatening........} Z0 11. e5
{when Black can't reply....} dxe5 12. fxe5 Nfd7 13. Nxf7) 10... Nc6 {Attacks
the d-Pawn but blocks the c-Pawn and leaves Black too passively placed.} 11. e5
Nd7 12. Be3 Ne7 {Probably best as it allows ......c5.} (12... d5 13. b3 {
isn't much good for Black.}) 13. g4 {Intending a KS pawn storm and preventing
13......Nf5} h6 14. Nf3 ({I didn't play} 14. Nge4 {because of} d5) 14... Kh8 ({
Now he can't play........} 14... c5 {because of} 15. exd6) ({If} 14... f5 15.
exf6 Bxf6 16. Bxg6) 15. Qd2 {Threatens f5 & Bxh6} Ng8 {Defending the h-Pawn}
16. Rae1 {[35']} a6 {Black has no constructive moves} 17. Re2 Bxf3 {Black
decides that passivity will result in ultimate suffocation, so he makes a bid
to get some play.} 18. Rxf3 dxe5 $1 19. fxe5 Qh4 $2 {Trying to get some play
but the f-Pawn goes. It was probably indefensible anyway.} 20. Rxf7 Rad8 (20...
Qxg4+ 21. Rg2 {loses the Knight.}) 21. Rg2 Bxe5 $6 {Hoping to benefit from the
complications.} 22. Bxg6 {Threatening mate.} (22. dxe5 $4 Nxe5 $1) 22... Bg7 $4
{Overlooking the other threat.} ({Correct was} 22... Ndf6 {and if} 23. Bf2 Qh3
$1) 23. Rxd7 Rf8 24. Rxd8 Rxd8 25. Bf7 e5 26. d5 Nf6 27. Bf2 Qh3 28. Qe3 Qxe3
29. Bxe3 Rf8 30. Be6 1-0

