1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 O-O 5. Nf3 c5 6. Bd3 d5 7. O-O Nc6 8. Ne2 {
As in my game v R.C.Mitchell} cxd4 9. exd4 dxc4 10. Bxc4 Qc7 11. Bf4 ({I played
} 11. Qc2 {v Mitchell but} Na5 {is a good response.}) 11... Bd6 12. Bxd6 {[7']}
Qxd6 {[8']} 13. a3 b6 14. Qd3 {mainly to prevemt 14......Ne4} Bb7 15. b4 {
To prevent 15......Na5} Rfd8 16. Rfd1 Rac8 17. Rac1 ({I considered forcing a
favourable exchange of Bishops by} 17. Ba6 {....but Black replies....} Bxa6 18.
Qxa6 e5) 17... Ne7 {Black has got rather the better of the opening his pieces
being better than White's.} 18. Ne5 Ned5 {[28'] 18......Bd4 or 18......Ne4
don't achieve much.} 19. f3 {[30']} Qe7 {[35']} 20. Rc2 Nh5 21. Qd2 {Prevents
21.....Qg5} Qh4 22. Rdc1 {[49']} (22. g3 {is very weakning.}) 22... Ndf4 {
[61'] Black gets a good attack. This move opens the long diagonal and removes
my Knight (e2) which was a good defensive piece.} 23. Nxf4 Nxf4 24. Qe3 Qg5 $1
{Threat 25......Nh3+.} ({Were Black to play} 24... Nh5 {or g6} 25. Nxf7 $1) 25.
Kh1 {[65']} ({If now say} 25. Qe1 {or d2} f6 26. Z0 Rxc4 $1) 25... f6 {[83']}
26. g3 {[72'] Better than 26.Nd3} fxe5 $6 ({safer was} 26... Nd5) 27. gxf4 Qg4
{The best and only move.} 28. d5 $8 Rxd5 $4 {Black was very short of time here
and goes right off the rails.} (28... Qxf4 $8) 29. Bxd5 Rxc2 {Threatening mate.
} 30. fxg4 {The Black Queen is suddenly "Takeable"} Bxd5+ 31. Kg1 Rg2+ 32. Kf1
Rxg4 33. Qxe5 1-0

