{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. e4
d6 6. Ne2 e5 7. d5 c6 8. O-O cxd5 9. cxd5 b5 {I had already made sure of 1st
prize so I was playing rather wildly and too quickly.} 10. a3 a5 11. Nbc3 Ba6
12. h3 Nbd7 13. Be3 Nb6 14. b3 Nfd7 15. a4 bxa4 $2 ({Rather better was....} 
15... b4 16. Nb5 Bxb5 17. axb5 Nc5) 16. Nxa4 Nxa4 17. Rxa4 {[22']} Nc5 $2 {
[16'] Doubtful I thought I had sufficiently good play for my pieces to
compensate for the isolated Pawns} 18. Bxc5 dxc5 19. Qd2 {[31']} Bb5 {[18']}
20. Ra3 Qb6 21. Rfa1 Rfc8 $2 ({Correct was...} 21... Bxe2 {Now I lose a Pawn
and the game.}) 22. Nc3 Bf8 {The Pawns could no longer be satisfactorily
defended.} 23. Nxb5 {[37']} Qxb5 {[26']} 24. Bf1 $1 Qb4 {[42'] After playing
the first 23 moves in 26'. I took a while on this but it ultimately loses,
keeping the Queens on doesn't seem any better.} 25. Qxb4 {[42']} cxb4 {[42']}
26. Rxa5 Rab8 {Exchanging a pair of Rooks may have been slightly prefferable.}
27. Bc4 Bc5 28. Ra6 Bd4 29. R1a4 Kf8 {[51']} ({If} 29... Rxc4 30. bxc4 b3 31.
Ra8 $18) 30. Kf1 Ke8 {[52']} 31. Rc6 {[71']} Rd8 {[57']} 32. Ke2 Rb7 {[58']}
33. Ba6 Rbb8 34. Rc4 Bc3 35. f3 Kf8 {Black can do nothing but mark time.} 36.
g4 Ke7 37. Kd3 Ke8 38. Rc7 Rb6 39. Bb7 Rf6 40. Ke2 Kf8 41. Bc6 h6 {or else he
plays 42.g5 and forces the Rook to abandon defence of the f-Pawn or get cut
off on f5.} 42. Raa7 Bd4 43. Rab7 Bc3 44. h4 g5 {Forced if 45.g5 is to be
prevented, but now the h-Pawn is a target for White.} 45. h5 $1 Rf4 46. Bd7 $1
{Forces an immediate win.} Rf6 47. Rc6 Kg7 (47... Rxc6 {Loses straight off.})
48. Rbb6 Bd4 49. Ra6 Rf4 50. Bf5 {A well played ending by White. R.A.C. won
£3 for 1st prize.} 1-0

