{Time limit 24 moves per hour. E.E. Zepler is the professor of Electrical
Engineering} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 c6 5. O-O d5 6. Ne5 O-O 7.
Nd2 Nbd7 8. f4 Qc7 9. e3 e6 10. b3 c5 11. c3 $2 (11. Bb2 $142) 11... cxd4 12.
cxd4 Qc3 {I don't know why I played this. I realised it was very risky but I
was underestimating my opponent.} 13. Ba3 Qxe3+ 14. Kh1 Re8 $2 {Now the game
is lost.} ({Correct was....} 14... Qxd4 15. Bxf8 Bxf8) 15. Bb2 $1 Nxe5 {
Forced if my Queen is to escape.} 16. fxe5 Ng4 (16... Ne4 {Would give back the
Pawn and still leave my Queen in a hopeless position.}) 17. Qxg4 {[25']} Qxd2 {
[50'] I now had 1o minutes for 7 moves.} 18. Qf3 Re7 ({Not} 18... Rf8 $2 19.
Ba3) 19. Bc3 Qc2 20. Rf2 Qf5 ({If} 20... Qe4 21. Qd1) 21. Qe2 Qh5 22. Bf3 Qh6
23. Bd2 g5 24. h4 f6 25. Bh5 $1 Bh8 {There's nothing else.} 26. Raf1 Rf7 ({
Equally hopeless is....} 26... f5) 27. Bxf7+ Kxf7 28. Bxg5 Qg6 29. Rxf6+ Bxf6
30. Rxf6+ {J.C.R won the match 4.5 - 1.5} 0-1

