{Time control 40 moves in 90 minutes.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. c4 e6 4. d4 cxd4
5. Nxd4 Nf6 6. Nc3 Bb4 {I decided to try this outrather than go in for a
Schveningen set up.} 7. Be2 Qc7 8. O-O Nc6 9. Nxc6 bxc6 10. Qc2 O-O 11. Be3 d5
{Ensuring at least an equal game.} 12. exd5 cxd5 13. f4 {Preventing a possible
......e5 after say Bd4} Bb7 14. a3 Bc5 15. Bxc5 Qxc5+ 16. Kh1 dxc4 {Not really
expecting to hang on to it.} 17. Na4 Qc6 18. Bf3 {[48']} Qc7 {[54']} ({I had
originally intended....} 18... Nd5 {but my position is very compromised so I
decided to go for a positional advantage.}) 19. Bxb7 Qxb7 20. Qxc4 Rac8 21. Qe2
Nd5 {Leaving White's Knight stranded.} 22. f5 exf5 23. Rxf5 Qd7 {[70'] I now
had 17 moves to make in 20'.} 24. Rxd5 Qxd5 25. Nb6 {[60']} Qe6 {[75'] I
decided that my only winning chance was to get a passed pawn.} 26. Qxe6 fxe6
27. Nxc8 Rxc8 28. b4 Kf7 29. h3 e5 30. Rd1 Ke6 31. a4 e4 32. Kg1 Rc7 {So as to
advance the King without allowing the White Rook access to d7.} 33. Kf2 {[70']}
Ke5 {[81']} 34. b5 axb5 35. axb5 Rb7 $2 ({I was very short of time and I
thought that the alternative line.....} 35... Rc2+ {was too risky. However
after 35......Rc2+} 36. Ke3 Rc3+ 37. Ke2 Rb3 38. Rd7 Rxb5 39. Rxg7 {Black has
all the chances. I now nearly managed to lose in the rush.}) 36. Rb1 Rb6 37.
Ke3 h5 38. h4 Kf5 39. Rb4 g6 {Here I offered a draw which he accepted. Black
is more or less in Zugzwang.} ({e.g.} 39... g6 40. g3 $1 {and black can only
try...} Kg4 $6 41. Kxe4 Kxg3 42. Kd5 {25 etc. and Black is very badly placed.
As it was I had lessthan a minute on my clock anyway. The match was a draw 25 -
}) 1/2-1/2

