1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ne4 4. a3 d6 5. Nd2 ({If} 5. Qc2 Bf5) (5. Nf3 Bg4)
5... Nxd2 6. Bxd2 dxe5 7. Bc3 Qxd1+ 8. Rxd1 f6 9. g3 {I rather overestimated
my position here.} Be6 10. e3 a5 11. Nf3 a4 12. Nd2 Nd7 13. f4 {Otherwise
Black develops his pieces with the better game.} Bc5 14. Kf2 {The King isn't
badly placed here.} exf4 $2 {Gives White the better game.} (14... O-O $142) 15.
gxf4 {Now White has the better centre.} Kf7 16. Bd4 Rhd8 17. Bd3 {Threat 18.f5}
g6 18. h4 Bg4 19. Be2 (19. Rdg1 f5) 19... Bxe2 20. Kxe2 Bxd4 21. exd4 Ra6 {
Threat 22......Nb6} 22. Kd3 Rb6 23. Kc3 Re8 24. Rh3 f5 25. c5 Rbe6 26. Nc4 Rd8
{Threat 27......Nxc5} 27. Rdd3 Re4 {Here we had to adjourn. I didn't want to
have to carry on so I offered a draw which he accepted. White has the better
of it at the end. Unfortunately I didn't leave the time to continue the game
ata later date. University won the match.} 1/2-1/2

