1. d4 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. Nf3 d5 5. Nc3 {Better alternatives were.......
} (5. O-O) (5. c4) (5. Nbd2) 5... O-O 6. O-O Nbd7 7. Re1 c5 8. e4 $2 {Much too
impetuous this loses a Pawn.} dxe4 9. Nxe4 Nxe4 10. Rxe4 cxd4 11. Nxd4 $4 {
Loses a piece.} (11. Bg5 $142) 11... Nc5 12. Rf4 {Anything else loses a piece
since the Knight is pinned. White should resign.} e5 13. Rh4 exd4 14. Be4 {
This would be a mistake were it not for the fact that he is completely lost
whatever he does.} Nxe4 15. Rxe4 Bf5 16. Re1 Rc8 17. Bf4 Rxc2 18. g4 Qh4 19.
Bg3 Qxg4 20. Rc1 Qxd1 21. Rcxd1 d3 22. Bf4 Bxb2 23. Bd2 Rxd2 24. Rxd2 Bc3 25.
Rxd3 Bxe1 26. Re3 Bb4 {[23'] And at last he resigned. My opponent only looked
14 years old. Jamboree Result 1st Uni A 5.5 2nd Southampton 5 3rd = Andover 3.
5 Itchen G.S. Uni B 6th = Wnichester Coll 2.5 Woolston 7th = King Edward IV
Sch 1 St. Mary's Coll} 0-1

