1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 Nbd7 5. Nf3 c6 6. Bg2 dxc4 {I don't like
this (for Black) as it gives White the centre.} 7. a4 Bb4 ({I would prefer.} 
7... c5) 8. O-O O-O 9. Qc2 Bxc3 10. Qxc3 Nb6 $2 {A miserable move.} 11. a5 Nbd5
12. Qc2 Nd7 (12... Ng4 {is immediate suicide.}) 13. Qxc4 f5 {Desperate
measures to try for some play, very weakening.} 14. Nd2 {After much thought. I
intend to open up the position with 15.e4.} (14. Bg5 {isn't patricularly good.}
) 14... N7f6 15. e4 fxe4 16. Nxe4 Nxe4 17. Bxe4 Bd7 18. Bd2 Qf6 19. Bb4 {
Black is loath to part with his Knight but now the Bishop cripples him.} Rf7
20. Bd6 Qg5 $2 {[30'] Just asking for trouble.} 21. f4 {[60']} Qg4 22. Qd3 g6 (
{If} 22... h6 $2 23. Be5 Z0 {threatens} 24. Bg6 Z0 25. Kg2 Z0 26. h3) 23. Kg2 {
The Black Queen finds she is short of squares.} Ne7 24. Rac1 Nf5 {Leads him
into more difficulties.} 25. h3 Qh5 26. g4 Nh4+ 27. Kg3 Qh6 28. Qe2 $1 g5 29.
fxg5 Qxg5 30. Rxf7 Kxf7 31. Rf1+ Kg8 {I had expected an easy win here. However,
the longer I looked the worse it appeared.....} 32. Kh2 ({If} 32. Bxh7+ Kxh7
33. Rf7+ Kg8 34. Rxd7 Nf5+ $1 35. Kg2 Nxd6 36. Rxd6 Rf8 {is OK for Black.}) ({
If} 32. Qf2 Nf5+) 32... Ng6 33. Qf2 Be8 34. a6 bxa6 35. Be5 {Threat Bxc6} Rc8
36. Bd3 $1 Qe7 (36... a5 $4 37. Ba6 $1) 37. Bxa6 Rd8 38. Bf6 Qd6+ 39. Kg1 Rd7
40. h4 Rf7 {Adjudicated win for White} (40... Rf7 {Black threatens to draw by
41.....RxB If} 41. g5 ({However White plays} 41. Qe3 $1 {with a general plan of
} c5 (41... Z0 42. Bc4 Z0 43. h5) 42. Bc4 cxd4 43. Bxd4 Rxf1+ 44. Kxf1 {
Black has 2 Pawns en-prise. In other variations White just pushes the KS Pawns
and wins.}) 41... c5 {is good.}) 1-0

