1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. c4 d6 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7. d5 Nbd7 {Not
very good.} (7... e6 $142 8. Bd3 exd5 9. exd5 Re8+) (7... Na6 $142) 8. Be2 {
Now he can't play 8......e6} ({Due to Black's 7th I could play...} 8. Bd3) 8...
a6 {[19']Black has no good move.} 9. a4 {[6'] Not really necessary, but useful
later on.} Qa5 {Waste of time in this position.} 10. O-O Ne8 {His only chance
of counterplay is by ......f5} 11. Bd2 Qd8 ({If now} 11... Nc7 $4 12. Nb5 Qb6
13. a5) ({maybe} 11... f5 {offered more hope}) 12. g4 Bxc3 $2 {Rather
desparate.} 13. Bxc3 Ndf6 14. Nd2 {This retreat of the Knight is no hardship,
as it has the good square e4 to move to later on.} Ng7 15. e5 Nfe8 16. Ne4 Qc7
({Black can gain a little rlief by....} 16... f5 {also I want to play f5
eventually.} 17. Nxd6) 17. Ng3 e6 {This attempt to break White's grip only
opens the game for White's pieces.} 18. dxe6 Nxe6 19. Ne4 ({If} 19. exd6 {NOT}
Nxd6 $4 ({But...} 19... Qxd6) 20. Be5 Rd8 21. Ne4) 19... dxe5 20. Bxe5 Qd7 $2 {
In severe time-trouble Black blunders. However his position is nearly hopeless.
.....} ({....e.g. If} 20... Qb6 21. a5 {and if} Qb4 $4 22. Bc3 {wins the Queen.
}) 21. Bd6 Qc6 22. Bf3 Qb6 23. Bxf8 Kxf8 24. Qd2 {To defend the Pawns and also
'eyeing' h6} Nd4 25. a5 ({If} 25. f5 {to play 26.Qh6} gxf5 {covers h6.}) 25...
Qc7 {Black threat 26......Nb3.} 26. Qd3 {Things were difficult here.} ({
I want to recapture QxN after ......NxB} 26. Qe3 {is no good because of...} Nc2
) 26... Qxf4 {A dangerous move especially as he was in bad time-trouble.} (
26... Nxf3+ 27. Qxf3 (27. Rxf3 $2 Bxg4)) 27. Bd1 Qc7 28. Ng5 Ne6 29. Nxh7+ Kg7
30. Nf6 Kf8 {With secs to spare} 31. Nd5 Qd7 32. Qxg6 f5 33. Qh6+ Kf7 {Uni won
the match 3.5 - 0.5 (one board was defaulted by both sides)} 1-0

[Event "Southampton League Div 1"]
