1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 c6 4. Bg2 d5 5. cxd5 cxd5 6. Nf3 Bg7 7. O-O b5 {
I thought my opponent was playing for a draw so I tried to take the
innitiative. A bit risky though} 8. Nc3 Qb6 ({Maybe better was} 8... a6 {
as we now have a general exchange off which didn't please me.}) 9. Qb3 {
White said afterwards that he expected to win a Pawn here!} a6 10. Nxd5 Nxd5
11. Qxd5 Bb7 12. Qc5 ({Better for White it seemed was} 12. Qb3 Bxd4 13. Nxd4
Bxg2 14. Kxg2 Qxd4) 12... Qxc5 13. dxc5 Nd7 14. Rb1 Nxc5 15. Be3 Na4 {I just
had an edge here} 16. Bd4 O-O 17. b3 {What I wanted really.} ({If he wanted a
draw} 17. Bxg7 {was easiest. I end up witha well placed Bishop for a mediocre
Knight now.}) 17... Nc3 18. Bxc3 (18. Bxg7 {is answered by} Nxe2+) ({If} 18.
Rb2 Bxd4 19. Nxd4 Bxg2 20. Kxg2 Rfd8) 18... Bxc3 19. Rbc1 b4 20. Ne1 $2 {
Rather doubtful. It cuts off his Rook and gives mr the d-file.} Bxg2 21. Kxg2 (
{I'd have preffered} 21. Nxg2 Z0 22. Ne3 Z0 23. Nc4) 21... Rfd8 22. Nd3 Rd6 23.
Rfd1 Rad8 24. f4 f6 25. Nf2 {This Knight just didn't seem to know what to do.}
Rd2 26. Kf3 f5 27. Rxd2 Rxd2 {White was in bad time-trouble here.} 28. Nd1 ({If
} 28. a3 a5 29. Z0 Rb2) 28... Bd4 29. Ne3 Bxe3 30. Kxe3 Rxa2 31. Rc4 a5 32. Rc5
Ra3 33. Kd2 Rxb3 34. Rxa5 Rb2+ 35. Kd3 Kf7 36. h4 $2 {Making life easy for me.}
Rb3+ {1 Uni won the match 4 -} 0-1

