1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5. Nxc6 bxc6 6. Bc4 Qh4 7. Qf3 d5 8.
Bd3 Nf6 9. exd5 O-O {[6'] Up to here as in our game earlier this year which
White had apparently forgotten about.} 10. O-O {[30'] The best move.} cxd5 {
[9'] The first move where I had to think about it.} 11. Bf4 c6 {[16']} 12. Qg3
{Results in an advantageous position for Black.} Qxg3 13. Bxg3 Nh5 {White
doesn't want to give up Bishop for Knight so I gain a few tempi pushing him
around.} 14. Bc7 a5 15. Be2 ({If} 15. Nd2 Ra7 16. Be5 f6 {17.B where?}) 15...
Nf6 16. Nc3 Re8 {Prevents the White Bishop retreating to e5.} 17. Bf3 Bf5 18.
Na4 Bf8 {Only a temporary retreat.} 19. c4 (19. c3 {is less complicated but
leaves his Knight stranded.}) 19... Bd3 20. Rfd1 Bc2 (20... Bxc4 21. Nb6 Ra7
22. Nxc4 $14) 21. Nb6 $2 {Loses outright.} ({White misses the fact that after} 
21. Rd2 Bxa4 22. b3 {Regains th piece.}) 21... Bxd1 22. Rxd1 Ra7 23. Bf4 Bc5
24. Na4 Rae7 {A neat manoeuvre to get my Bishop back into play.} 25. g3 Ba7 26.
Bd2 Ne4 27. Bxe4 {More or less forced.} Rxe4 28. Bxa5 Rxc4 29. b4 Rc2 30. Bb6
Bxb6 31. Nxb6 Rb8 $1 {Much the quickest way to finish it.} ({If} 31... Ree2 {
White makes a nuisance of himself with...} 32. a4) (31... Rxa2 32. Rc1) 32.
Nxd5 {Equivalent to resigning.} cxd5 33. Rxd5 Rxa2 34. Kg2 Rb2 35. b5 R2xb5 {
Since I hadn't taken the Pawn with the wrong Rook there wasn't much cause for
not resigning.} 36. Rd3 g5 37. h3 Kg7 38. g4 R8b6 {2 Uni won the match 3 -} 0-1

