1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. e3 O-O 6. Bd2 e6 (6... b6 $142) 7.
Rc1 Nbd7 8. cxd5 Nxd5 9. Be2 c6 {From now on my position gets worse.} (9... c5
$142) (9... b6 $142) 10. O-O N5b6 $2 {Rather a doubtful strategy} 11. Ne4 Nf6
12. Nfg5 $2 {Waste of time} Nfd5 {Threat 13......f5} 13. Nf3 Qc7 $2 (13... Qe7
$142) 14. b4 Qe7 15. Qb3 e5 {Giving up the QBishop which I didn't like but it
was the only way to gain some freedom. White threatened 16.b5} 16. dxe5 Bxe5
17. Nxe5 Qxe5 18. Nc5 Rb8 19. Bf3 Be6 20. Nxe6 Qxe6 21. Bd1 Rbd8 22. Qb2 h5 $2
{[62'] I was getting short of time and tried to find a safe move.} (22... Nd7
$142) 23. e4 $1 Qf6 $2 {In the rush overlooking his 25th move, but Black's
position was very difficult.} ({Not} 23... Qxe4 24. Bh6) 24. Qxf6 Nxf6 25. Bg5
Nxe4 26. Bxd8 Rxd8 27. Bb3 Rd7 28. Rfe1 Nd2 29. Rcd1 Rd4 30. Re8+ Kg7 {We both
just made the time control} 31. Bc2 {Adjourned. The game resumed 10/12/64} Nbc4
{The sealed move.} 32. Re7 Na3 33. Re2 {Forced but good.} Nxc2 34. Rexd2 Rxd2
35. Rxd2 Nxb4 {The game is now an easy win for White} 36. Rb2 a5 37. a3 Nd5 38.
Rxb7 Nc3 39. Ra7 (39. Z0 {39.Ra7 otherwise} Nb5 40. a4 Nc3 {forces off the QS
Pawns}) 39... a4 40. Ra6 Kf8 41. Rxc6 $2 {The game should be drawn. White
should have brought his King accross.} Nb5 42. Ra6 Nxa3 43. Rxa4 Nb5 44. Re4
Nc7 45. Kf1 Ne6 46. Ke2 Kg7 47. Ke3 Kf6 48. Rc4 Kf5 49. Ra4 Kf6 50. Ra6 Kf5 51.
Ra5+ Kf6 52. f4 Ng7 53. Ke4 {[124']} Ne8 {[105']} 54. Ra6+ Kg7 55. h3 Nf6+ 56.
Ke5 Nd7+ 57. Kd6 Nf6 58. Ra4 Ne8+ 59. Ke7 Nf6 60. g3 Ng8+ 61. Ke8 Nh6 $2 (61...
Nf6+ {Seems to draw. I thought I could set up an impregnable position with the
Knight defending f7. However I get myself in zugzwang.}) 62. Ra7 Kf6 ({No
better is} 62... Kg8 63. g4) 63. Kf8 Ke6 ({If} 63... Kf5 64. Kg7) 64. Ra6+ Kd5
({If} 64... Kf5 65. Kg7) 65. Kg7 Nf5+ 66. Kxf7 Nxg3 67. Rxg6 h4 68. Re6 Ne4 69.
Rh6 Nd6+ 70. Rxd6+ Kxd6 71. f5 Kd7 72. f6 {2 Uni won the match 3 -} 1-0

