{Opponent grade: 3b ~ ECF 201 - 208} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. Nc3 Nf6
5. d3 d6 6. Bg5 Be6 ({M.C.O. gives} 6... h6) 7. Nd5 Bxd5 8. Bxd5 h6 9. Bxc6+
bxc6 10. Bh4 Rb8 11. Rb1 ({Not} 11. b3 Bb4+) 11... g5 $6 {The pin was a
nuisance.} 12. Bg3 h5 13. h4 {Best} g4 14. Nd2 ({Not} 14. Ng5 Ng8 15. Z0 f6)
14... Ng8 {Intending 15......Nh6 & 16.....f5} 15. Nb3 Bb6 {[46']} 16. d4 {[49']
} f6 {[51']} 17. c4 Qe7 18. O-O Nh6 19. Rc1 exd4 {Forced} 20. Nxd4 Bxd4 21.
Qxd4 c5 22. Qc3 Nf7 23. f4 gxf3 24. Rxf3 Ne5 25. Rf5 Rb4 26. b3 Ng4 27. a3 Rb7
(27... Rb8 {was probably better}) 28. b4 cxb4 29. axb4 Kf7 30. Rcf1 Kg6 31. b5
{[96'] Adjourned. The game rsumed 19/12/64} Rf8 $2 {[96'] The sealed move
loses the game in one move.Better QR to b8 when White has nothing definite.} (
31... Rbb8) 32. Qd3 {[106']} Rbb8 {.....Resigns was best.} 33. e5 dxe5 (33...
dxe5 {There was a vhance White might have played} 34. Rg5+ Kf7 35. Qg6+ Ke6 {
with some chances.}) 34. Rxe5+ {J.Penrose played on Bd1 for Hampstead.} 1-0

