1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. Bf4 O-O 6. e3 c5 7. dxc5 Qa5 ({
M.C.O. 9th Edn gives......} 7... Ne4 8. Nxd5 Qa5+ 9. b4 Qa3 $11) 8. Qd2 {
or else he plays 8......Ne4} dxc4 9. Bxc4 Rd8 10. Nd4 (10. Qe2 {is answered by}
Ne4) 10... Nc6 {11......e5 is now threatened.} (10... Nh5 {Threatening 11......
e5, is answered by} 11. Bxb8) 11. O-O-O {About the only move.} ({If} 11. O-O
Qxc5 {is too strong.}) 11... Bf5 (11... e5 {is answered by} 12. Nxc6) 12. Qe2
Ne4 $6 {Black has the better of it, but this is a bit impetuous.} (12... Qxc5
$142) 13. Bxf7+ $5 {Neatly taking the opportunity presented by Black's last
move. Black now thought for 30'} Kxf7 (13... Kh8 14. Qc4 {is no good for Black}
) 14. Qc4+ Kf8 15. Nxc6 Qxc5 $2 {Black plays the moves in the wrong order......
...} (15... bxc6 {was no good}) ({but Black can draw by.....} 15... Rxd1+ $1
16. Rxd1 Qxc5 17. Qxc5 Nxc5 {When it is up to White to find the good moves.
The game equalises after..} 18. e4 $1 (18. Nxe7 Nd3+ (18... Kxe7 19. Bd6+) 19.
Rxd3 Bxd3) 18... Bxe4 19. Nxe4 Nxe4 20. Nxe7 $1) 16. Rxd8+ ({Not} 16. Qxc5 $2
Rxd1+ {and Black draws.}) 16... Rxd8 17. Qxc5 Nxc5 18. Nxd8 e5 {Black should
resign.} 19. e4 Bd7 20. Be3 Nd3+ 21. Kc2 Nb4+ 22. Kb3 a5 23. Nxb7 1-0

