{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours: Opponent grade 6b ~ 153-160 E.C.F} 1. e4 c5 2.
Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Nf3 Bb4 7. Bd2 d6 8. Bd3 O-O 9. O-O
Be6 10. Re1 b5 $2 {I didn't know the opening very well.} (10... Nbd7 $142 11.
Z0 Nc5) 11. a4 $1 {This put me in a mess.} bxa4 {About the only move} 12. Nxa4
{My a-Pawn is now rather a liability and White's pieces have much the better
of it on the QS.} Nc6 13. c3 Ba5 ({If} 13... Bc5 14. Nxc5 {Wins the a-Pawn})
14. Bc2 Nd7 {Hoping to get some play with .....f5} 15. Ng5 Bc4 {I can't let
White play 16.NxB or the pawn on e6 will be very weak.} 16. b3 Bb5 17. Nf3 Ne7
18. c4 $2 {This forces Bishops off. Surely White must have something better
than this.} Bxd2 19. Qxd2 Bxa4 20. Rxa4 Qc7 {White's good position of a few
moves back has suddenly become a not-so-good one. Black's d-Pawn is easily
defensible and my Knights have good squares at c5, d4, b4.} 21. Rd1 Nc5 22. Ra2
Rfd8 23. Rda1 Qb7 24. Qe3 Nc6 25. Rb2 Nb4 26. Nd2 Nxc2 ({I considered...} 26...
Nc6 {with the idea of moving it to d4, but she answers with} 27. Nf3) 27. Rxc2
Qb4 28. Qc3 Qxc3 29. Rxc3 Rdb8 30. f3 Rb4 31. Kf2 Rab8 32. Ra3 $1 {Now White
can escape with a draw} ({If} 32. Rb1 {I push the a-Pawn and probably win.})
32... R8b6 33. Ke2 Kf8 34. Kd1 Ke7 35. Kc2 g6 36. Nf1 {Miss D.Dobson came
=21st with 4 pts} 1/2-1/2

