{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. g3 O-O 5.
Bg2 d6 6. e4 Nbd7 7. Nge2 e5 8. h3 {Better than 8.0-0 as in Rd1} Re8 9. Be3 Nf8
({Black decides to vary from the usual} 9... exd4 10. Nxd4 a5 {and goes for a
KS attack} ({or} 10... c6)) 10. d5 h6 11. O-O g5 {Intending 12......Ng6} 12. f4
{Black hadn't expected this. It secures good attacking chances for White on
the KS.} gxf4 {About best} 13. gxf4 exf4 {Otherwise White plays f5 which
leaves Black in trouble on the KS.} 14. Nxf4 Bf5 {Neatly bringing the Bishop
into the defence.} 15. Qf3 $1 {A neat Pawn sacrifice which gives White a
strong attack.} (15. Qd3 Bg6 {is passive}) (15. Nh5 {is answered by} Nxh5)
15... Nxe4 ({If} 15... Bxe4 16. Nxe4 Nxe4 17. Nh5) 16. Nh5 Bg6 {The only move.}
({If} 16... Nxc3 17. Qxf5 Ne2+ 18. Kh1) 17. Nxg7 Kxg7 18. Qf4 (18. Bd4+ Kg8 19.
Bf6) 18... Ng5 {Black decides to sacrifice the exchange.} ({If} 18... Qg5 19.
Nxe4 $1 Rxe4 20. Qxg5 hxg5 21. Bxe4) ({If} 18... Nxc3 19. Qxh6+ Kg8 20. bxc3 Z0
21. Bd4) 19. h4 Rxe3 20. Qxe3 Ngh7 21. Qd4+ Kg8 22. Qf4 Kg7 23. Be4 Nf6 24.
Rae1 N8d7 25. Bxg6 fxg6 ({Now he loses a piece but} 25... Kxg6 {loses just as
quickly}) 26. Ne4 Qf8 (26... Nxe4 27. Qf7+ {Mates quickly}) 27. Nxf6 Qxf6 ({If
} 27... Nxf6 28. Re6 Nh5 29. Qxf8+ Rxf8 30. Re7+ Kg8 31. Rxf8+ Kxf8 32. Rxc7 {
etc.}) 28. Qxf6+ Nxf6 29. Re7+ {C.North came =12th with 4.5 pts} 1-0

