{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours: Opponent grade 5b ~ ECF 169 - 176} 1. d4 f5 2.
c4 Nf6 3. g3 g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. Nc3 d6 6. Nf3 O-O 7. d5 {This set me quite a
problem. I want to play ......e5} Na6 {Intending 8......Nc5 & 9......e5} ({
but if.....} 7... e5 8. dxe6 Bxe6 9. Nd4 {forces....} Bc8) 8. Rb1 Nc5 9. Nd2 {
Whte does not like the idea of me controlling e4} e5 10. b4 Ncd7 11. e4 f4 {
White is manoeuvering on the QS so I go for KS counterplay.} 12. Nb3 b6 13. Ba3
{Intending 14.c5} ({If} 13. gxf4 exf4 14. Bxf4 Nxe4) 13... a6 {To answer 14.c5
with 14......b5} 14. c5 b5 15. Bc1 Qe7 16. O-O h5 17. a4 bxa4 18. Nxa4 Nh7 19.
Nb2 h4 20. g4 {My best plan now was probably to continue with the KS attack.
However I decided to win a Pawn on the QS rather riskily.} dxc5 21. bxc5 Nxc5
22. Nxc5 Qxc5 23. Nd3 Qe7 24. Qb3 Rf7 (24... Kh8 {Is not as good. 24......Rf7
reinfoces the c-Pawn.}) 25. h3 Nf6 $2 {Not the best. White gets good play now.}
({I considered} 25... f3 {but I was short of time and didn't want to risk it.
However it is best e.g.} 26. d6 cxd6 27. Bxf3 Be6 28. Qd1 Bc4 {etc.}) 26. Ba3
Qe8 27. f3 Bf8 28. Bxf8 Kxf8 29. Qc3 Re7 30. Rfc1 Nh7 {Intending...} 31. Qb4
Ng5 $2 {Getting short of time I make an outright blunder after which the game
seems lost.} 32. Rxc7 Nf7 (32... Kf7 {May be a better attempt but the e-Pawn
goes.}) 33. Qc5 Qd8 34. d6 Nxd6 ({If} 34... Qxd6 35. Rxc8+) ({If} 34... Rd7 35.
Nxe5) 35. Rxe7 Qxe7 36. Nxe5 Kg7 37. Rb6 Nf5 38. Qc3 Nd6 39. Nc4+ Qf6 40. Qxf6+
Kxf6 41. Rxd6+ Be6 42. Na5 {C.B.Gillman came =12th with 4.5pts} 1-0

