{Time control 40 moves in 2 hours.} 1. d4 d5 2. e3 Nf6 3. Bd3 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5.
f4 Bg4 6. Nf3 e6 7. Nbd2 Bd6 {Threatening 8......cxd when I must reply cxd} 8.
h3 Bh5 9. g4 Bg6 10. Nf1 $6 {Intending 11.Ng3 and allowing me to answer 11.....
.cxd with 12exd. However in view of Black's reply the exchange of Bishops
would have been better.} ({If now} 10. f5 exf5 11. gxf5 Bh5) (10. Bxg6 $142)
10... Ne4 {Preventing 11.Ng3 . Also I can't move my f3N as ....Qh4+ is a
nuisance. I there fore block off h4 to the Black Queen.} 11. h4 h5 12. Ng5 {
Seems the best way out of the problem. 12.....f5 is prevented and Black's
Knight on e4 is removed.} Be7 ({If} 12... Nxg5 13. hxg5 {and Black's h-Pawn is
en prise.}) 13. Bxe4 Bxe4 (13... dxe4 14. Ng3 {is good}) 14. Nxe4 dxe4 15. g5
f5 {or else 16.Ng3 wins a Pawn.} 16. Qb3 Qd7 17. a3 {I didn't like putting my
8th Pawn on a black square but black threatened 17......cxd and if 18.cxd the
Knight goes from b4 to d3} (17. Z0 cxd4 18. cxd4 Nb4 19. Z0 Nd3+) 17... g6 18.
Rh2 Na5 19. Qa2 c4 {This ultimately leads to a draw.} 20. Nd2 Rc8 21. b4 {
The freeing move} cxb3 22. Nxb3 Nc4 23. Re2 {Allows the Knight to go to d2
without leaving the e-Pawn en prise} Kf7 24. Nd2 Qd5 25. Nxc4 Qxc4 26. Qxc4
Rxc4 27. Rb2 {Active defence.} b6 28. Rb3 {J.R.Dicken came =12th with 4.5pts}
1/2-1/2

