{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. c3 dxc3 5.
Nxc3 e6 6. Bc4 Nc6 7. O-O d6 8. a4 {This doesn't achieve much in this position}
Nf6 9. Qe2 {With a threat of e5 also 10.Rd1 puts pressure on the d-Pawn.} Qc7
10. Bf4 Be7 11. Rac1 Qb8 12. Rfd1 Bd7 13. Rd2 Ne5 {Pressure on the d-Pawn was
getting too hot. The ensuing exchange gives my Bishops more scope. .......maybe
} 14. Nxe5 {His f5 Bishop has a bleak future.......} ({.....maybe} 14. Bxe5 {
was better}) 14... dxe5 15. Bg5 {Prevents 15......0-0} (15. Be3 $142) 15... Bc6
16. h3 h6 17. Bh4 {Offering his e-Pawn for a long attack.} O-O ({very risky was
} 17... Nxe4 18. Nxe4 Bxh4 19. Nd6+ {and if...} Kf8 $2 20. Qh5 $1) 18. Rd3 Qc7
19. Bg3 Rad8 20. Rcd1 Rxd3 21. Bxd3 ({If} 21. Rxd3 {he is open to moves like ..
...} Bxe4) 21... Rd8 22. Bc2 Rxd1+ 23. Qxd1 Qd6 {Going into an endgame a Pawn
up.} ({Also good was} 23... Qa5 24. Z0 Qb4 25. Z0 Qd4) 24. Qxd6 ({If} 24. Qe2
Qd4 {is good}) 24... Bxd6 25. f3 Nh5 26. Bf2 g6 27. Be3 Kg7 28. Kf2 f5 29. Bd2
{White was short of time and plays 'safe' moves.} Nf6 30. Be3 Bb4 {Threatens
31......BxN followed by the winning of the e-Pawn.} 31. Bd2 $2 ({In the time
rush White misses the easier} 31. exf5) 31... fxe4 32. fxe4 Bxc3 33. Bxc3 Bxe4
34. Bxe4 $2 ({Short of time White misses} 34. Bb3 $1 {when the win is very
difficult for Black.}) 34... Nxe4+ 35. Ke3 Nxc3 36. bxc3 Kf6 37. Ke4 h5 38. g3
b5 39. axb5 axb5 40. h4 g5 41. hxg5+ Kxg5 {D.M.Gostyn came = 21st with 4pts}
0-1

