{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hours} 1. e4 e6 {I started with nearly 25 minutes on
my clock.} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Bd3 ({
More usual.} 7. Qg4) (7. a4) (7. Nf3) 7... Nbc6 8. Nf3 c4 {Whilst this
releases the tensionin the centre I intended to try for some play on the KS.
Also it simplifies the position slightly which was to my advantage as I was
behind on time.[Best]} 9. Be2 O-O 10. O-O f5 ({[Better]} 10... b5) 11. exf6
gxf6 $6 {I thought this would lead to interesting complications although I
didn't realise what attack White would get.} ({[Better]} 11... Rxf6) 12. Bh6
Rf7 13. Nh4 Ng6 14. Bh5 (14. Nxg6 {Would be very good for me.}) 14... Nce7 15.
Qg4 e5 16. Qg3 {[All moves from 12.Bh6 to 16.Qg3 are best]} Bf5 {[1.39] Black
is probably threatening the c-Pawn! Black's e-Pawn is weak.} (16... Nf5 {
[is 0.84]}) 17. Bxg6 {White tries another way (to win the e-Pawn)} ({If White
can exchange off the Knight on g6 he can win the e-Pawn. However he can't} 17.
Nxf5 Nxf5) (17. Nxg6 Bxg6 18. dxe5 Nf5 $1) ({[Better]} 17. Rae1) 17... Bxg6 18.
Nxg6 ({[Better 18.dxe]} 18. dxe5 fxe5 19. Qxe5 Bxc2 $13) 18... Nxg6 19. h4 {
Apparently winning the e-Pawn} Kh8 20. h5 Ne7 $1 {Saves the pawn.} 21. dxe5 Nf5
22. Qf4 Nxh6 23. Qxh6 ({Not so good} 23. e6 Re7 24. Qxh6 Rxe6) 23... fxe5 24.
Qe6 Qf6 $1 ({Not so good is} 24... Re7 25. Qf6+ Kg8 {When Black is hopelessy
positionally placed.}) 25. Qxf6+ {[-0.09]} ({If now} 25. Qxd5 {[0.66]} Rg8 {
with a strong attack. e.g.} 26. Qxc4 $2 Rxg2+ 27. Kxg2 Qf3+ 28. Kh2 Qxh5+ {
& mates.}) 25... Rxf6 26. Rad1 Rd8 27. Rfe1 Re6 ({Not} 27... Rf5 28. g4 Rg5 29.
f3 e4 $2 30. fxe4 $1) 28. f4 e4 29. Kf2 Ra6 {Very useful. It takes the attack
off the d-pawn and ties up a White Rook.} ({[Better]} 29... Kg7) 30. Ra1 ({Not
} 30. Rxe4 Rxa3 {Which is good for Black.}) 30... Kg7 31. Ke3 Kf6 32. g4 Rg8
33. Rg1 {Now both White Rooks are tied up defending pawns. An important point
at the end. I was getting short of time now.} Ke6 34. Kd4 Rg7 35. f5+ Kf6 $1 (
35... Kd6 36. f6) 36. Kxd5 e3 {[0.21]} 37. Kxc4 Rc7+ 38. Kd3 ({If} 38. Kb3 Rb6+
39. Ka2 Rxc3 {at least draws.}) 38... Rd6+ {I was now so short of time I
couldn't write the moves down.} 39. Kxe3 Rxc3+ {[0.10] Now I had only seconds,
so White moves like lightning to try to get a win on time. Hence......} 40. Kf4
$4 Rd4# {With my superior Rooks I have at least a draw anyway. White has no
winning chances at all. Black may well have had a win at the end anyway.
Tournament Result 1.D.N.L.Levy 7pts 2D.J.Strauss 6.5pts =3rd R.A.C 6pts D.Parr
R.C.Vaughan I won £1 which was a 1/3 of thirs prize. Comments in [ ] were
made by Dick with a P.C. many years later.} 0-1

