1. Nf3 f5 2. b3 {Whilst this isn't wrong it's a bit peculiar.} d6 3. e3 $6 {
This ,however, is decidedly doubtful} ({Correct is} 3. d4) 3... e5 4. Bc4 {
White's idea is to get me to push my Pawns to d5 & e4, and then to put his
Knight on e5. Allrather odd.} Nf6 5. Bb2 d5 6. Be2 e4 7. Ne5 Bd6 8. Bh5+ $2 {
White's play up to here has been eccentric, but this is just a waste of time.}
g6 9. Nxg6 $4 {Going right off the rails.} hxg6 10. Bxg6+ Ke7 {How can White
save his Bishop?} 11. h4 Qg8 12. h5 ({equally hopeless was} 12. Bh5 Qxg2 13.
Rf1 f4 {etc.}) 12... Qxg6 13. hxg6 Rxh1+ 14. Ke2 Rxd1 15. g7 {15.Resigns was
more polite.} Rg1 $1 16. Bxf6+ Kf7 17. g3 f4 {Putting an end to it.} 18. exf4 (
18. gxf4 Kxf6) 18... Bg4+ 19. Ke3 {1 Uni won the match 4 -} 0-1

