1. e4 e6 2. d3 {The easiest way to avoid the French Defence.} d5 3. Nd2 c5 4.
g3 Nc6 5. Bg2 Nf6 6. Ngf3 dxe4 7. Nxe4 e5 8. Nxf6+ Qxf6 9. Bg5 {Not
particularly good as the Bishop gets chased away again.} Qd6 10. O-O {White is
better developed in the sense that he has more pieces in play but he has no
good plan of attack, whereas Black has various opportunities.} h6 11. Be3 Be6 {
With thoughts of castling QS.} 12. Nd2 Qd7 {Best. Now White has no
enterprising moves apart from f4 which he is reluctant to play.} 13. Ne4 b6 {
White's position is now void of opportunities.} 14. Qd2 {Not too good blocking
his Bishop's retreat. Relatively best was an advance on the QS.} f5 15. Nc3 g5
{Threatening to win the Bishop showing the weakness of 14.Qd2} 16. Bxg5 $2 {
Played after a lot of thought. He didn't like 16.f4 when his KS is openend up,
but 16.f3! seems OK (temporarily)} (16. f4) (16. f3 $1) 16... hxg5 17. Qxg5 Kf7
$1 ({I wanted to play} 17... Be7 {& if} 18. Qg7 ({However he plays} 18. Qg6+)
18... O-O-O {& if he tries to win the Bishop by} 19. Bxc6 $2 Qxc6 20. Qxe7 Rxh2
$1 $19) 18. Rfe1 {There's nothing better.} Be7 19. Qe3 Rag8 {Threatening 20....
..f4! White was now hopelessy short of time.} 20. Bxc6 (20. f4 {Lasts a bit
longer but the result isn't in doubt} c4 {etc.}) 20... Qxc6 21. Qxe5 Bf6 ({Not
} 21... Rxh2 $4 22. Kxh2 Bf6 23. Qxf6+ $1) 22. Qf4 (22. Qxf6+ {Just leaves him
a Rook down.}) 22... Rxh2 {2 Uni won the match 3 -} 0-1

