1. d4 e6 2. e4 d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. exd5 exd5 5. Bb5+ Nc6 {Playable} (5... Bd7 {
Is probably better}) 6. Ngf3 Nf6 ({a better plan was} 6... Bd6 7. Z0 Nge7) 7.
O-O Bd6 8. dxc5 Bxc5 9. Nb3 Bd6 10. Bg5 Be6 11. Nbd4 Qd7 {This is about the
only move. The weakening of the KS isn't too bad as it gives me attacking
chances.} 12. Bxf6 gxf6 13. Re1 Kf8 {I mustn't leave the King on the open file.
} ({If} 13... O-O-O 14. Bxc6 bxc6 15. Qe2 $1) 14. Nh4 {With the idea that I
can't now counter Q-d2-h6 with ......h5 because of NxB+b and Ng6+} Be5 (14...
h5 15. Qd2 Z0 16. Ng6+ fxg6 17. Nxe6+) 15. c3 Ke7 {Intending 16......Ra-g8} (
15... a6 {would have cleared the air.}) 16. f4 $1 {Threatening 17.f5} Bxf4 (
16... Bxd4+ {isn't very inviting.}) 17. Qa4 Qc7 {The only move but good enough
as it turns out.} 18. g3 $2 {Allowing a good chance to slip.} ({I expected} 18.
Nhf5+ Kd8 19. Bxc6 bxc6 20. Nxe6+ fxe6 21. Rxe6) 18... Be5 (18... Nxd4 {
is best answered by} 19. gxf4) 19. Bxc6 Bxd4+ 20. Qxd4 bxc6 21. Nf5+ Kd7 22.
Qxf6 Rae8 $2 {A time-trouble error which loses a pawn.} ({Correct was} 22...
Qd8) 23. Ng7 Ref8 24. Nxe6 fxe6 25. Qxe6+ Kd8 26. Rf1 Rxf1+ 27. Rxf1 {We were
both in bad time trouble now.} Re8 28. Qf6+ Qe7 {A split second decision. All
the moves up to 36 were made in a mad time-scramble.} 29. Qxe7+ Rxe7 ({Not} 
29... Kxe7 30. Re1+) 30. Kf2 Kd7 31. Rd1 Re4 32. Rd4 Re7 33. Kf3 Ke6 34. Ra4
Kf5 35. Ra6 c5 36. h4 Rd7 {Threat 37.......d4} 37. Rc6 c4 38. g4+ Ke5 39. g5
Rb7 {Time was called, and we agreed a draw. The position is rather unclear.}
1/2-1/2

