1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Bd3 c5 5. Nf3 {Not a particularly good
variation for White} Nc6 6. exd5 $2 {White miscalculates.} (6. Be3 $142) 6...
cxd4 7. dxc6 (7. a3 Bxc3+ 8. bxc3 Qxd5) 7... dxc3 8. O-O {The best move.
Anything else loses outright.} bxc6 9. Ne5 Qc7 {Better than the alternatives.}
(9... Bb7) (9... Ne7) 10. f4 {Opens a diagonal to his King but if 10.Nc4 Ba6} (
{If} 10. Bf4 Bd6 11. Re1 cxb2 12. Rb1 {and maybe} f6) (10. Nc4 Ba6) 10... Rb8 {
Threat ......PxP & ......Bc5+} 11. Be4 $6 {Complicating things but unsound.}
Bc5+ ({Not} 11... cxb2 12. Bxc6+ Kf8 13. Bxb2 Bc5+ 14. Bd4) 12. Kh1 cxb2 13.
Bxc6+ Kf8 ({I considered} 13... Ke7 {for a long time but} 14. Qg4 {is a
nuisance.}) 14. Bxb2 ({If} 14. Rb1 bxc1=Q 15. Rxb8 Qxd1 16. Rxd1 Qxb8 17. Rd8+
Ke7 18. Re8+ Kd6 $1 {etc.}) 14... Rxb2 15. f5 {Hoping for something.} Nf6 16.
fxe6 Bxe6 17. Qd2 Ke7 $2 ({Much better was} 17... Rb8 {with an easy win. I
still retain an advantage after the ensuing exchanges but the win is harder.})
18. Qc3 Qb6 (18... Bd6 19. Qxb2 Bxe5 20. Qa3+ Bd6 21. Qa4 Bxh2) 19. Nd3 Qxc6 {
I thought for a long time over this.} (19... Bd4 20. Qa3+) (19... Rxa2 20.
Qxc5+ Qxc5 21. Nxc5 {etc.}) 20. Qxb2 Bd6 {My Bishops are very strong and I
have good attacking chances on the KS} 21. Qd4 Qc7 22. Nf4 Rb8 {Threatening ...
...Be5 & ......Rb4} 23. c3 Bc4 24. Rf2 Kf8 25. Rd1 h5 {I had 10' to get to
move 36.25......h5 is to aid ......Ng4} 26. h3 Be5 27. Qe3 Bd6 {Threat 28......
Bc5} 28. Qd4 Rd8 29. Rfd2 Be7 30. Qe3 Rxd2 31. Qxd2 Qe5 {We were both short of
time here.} 32. Nd3 Qa5 33. Nb4 Qc5 {Threat 34......Ne4 35.Qmoves Nf2+} 34. Qf4
g6 35. Qb8+ Kg7 36. Qb7 a5 {Black has done best out of the time rush.} 37. Nc6
$2 {Loses quickly} Bd6 {Threat 38......Bd5} 38. Nxa5 ({If} 38. Nd4 Bd5 39. Qa6
Bxa2 (39... Ne4)) 38... Be2 $1 ({Not} 38... Qe5 $2 39. Rxd6 {2 The match
finished here, and White resigned. Black has an easy win. Southampton Uni won
the match 6 -}) 0-1

