1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 d6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. Bc4 Nf6 8.
Qd2 O-O (8... Ng4 $11) 9. f3 Bd7 10. h4 Rc8 11. Bb3 Na5 12. g4 ({Also good} 12.
h5 Nxh5 13. Bh6 Bxh6 14. Qxh6 Z0 15. g4) 12... Nxb3 (12... Nc4 {Is more usual})
13. axb3 a6 14. h5 {[5']} e5 {Leaves his d-Pawn weak} 15. Nde2 Be6 {[22']} 16.
Bh6 {[8']} Bxh6 17. Qxh6 (17. Qxh6 Z0 {Threatening} 18. hxg6 fxg6 19. g5 Nh5
20. Ng3) 17... Qe7 18. O-O-O {[12']} Kh8 $2 {[30']} (18... Rfd8 $142) 19. Qg5
$1 {[16'] White threatens 20.Rxd6 and if QxR 21.QxN and 22.h6} (19. hxg6 fxg6
20. Qxg6 Rg8 21. Qh6 {Wins a pawn but improves Black's position too much. 19.
Qg5! pins the Knight usefully.}) 19... Rg8 {He can't escape without loss.} ({
Relatively best was.} 19... Nd5 20. Qxe7 Nxe7 21. Rxd6) 20. Rxd6 $1 gxh5 {
[41'] There's nothing better.} 21. Qxe5 {[20'] Threat 22.g5} hxg4 {[46']} 22.
Nd5 {Wins outright.} Rc5 23. Nxf6 $1 Rxe5 (23... Rxc2+ 24. Kxc2 Bxb3+ 25. Kxb3
{Gets him nowhere.}) 24. Rxh7# {1 Uni A won the match 4 -} 1-0

