1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 Nbd7 7. f4 Qa5 8.
Qf3 e6 9. O-O-O Be7 10. a3 Qc7 {To prevent 11.Bc4} 11. g4 b5 12. Bxf6 Nxf6 13.
g5 Nd7 14. Bh3 Nb6 {To prevent Bxe6} 15. Rhg1 Bd7 16. f5 e5 17. Nde2 ({I
considered} 17. Ne6) 17... f6 18. gxf6 Bxf6 19. Qd3 Ke7 20. Ng3 h5 21. Qf3 Be8
22. Nf1 b4 23. axb4 Rc8 {Threatening 24......Na4} 24. Qf2 {Threatening 25.QxN}
Bf7 25. Ne3 Rhd8 26. Bf1 Ra8 27. Be2 Qb7 {White theatened Bxh5} 28. Bf3 a5 29.
b5 $6 a4 30. Qe2 ({Safer} 30. Kd2) 30... a3 {(=)} 31. Kb1 $2 {Adjourned.} axb2
{The sealed move. The game resumed 13/3/65 Black now had reams of analysis and
I got mashed, having hardly looked at the position. I had refused a draw on
move 30.} (31... a2+ {is no good.}) 32. Kxb2 Na4+ 33. Nxa4 Rxa4 34. Nd5+ $2 (
34. c4 $142) 34... Bxd5 35. Rxd5 Qa7 $1 {I'd missed this.} 36. Rg2 {If the
Rook moves off the g-file his Bishop goes to g5 later.} Qa5 37. Qd3 Rc8 38. c3
Ra2+ 39. Kc1 Rxc3+ 40. Kb1 Ra1+ 41. Kb2 Qa3# {His analysis beat my casual play.
The match was a draw 2.5 each.} 0-1

