1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. a3 Bxc3+ 5. bxc3 dxe4 6. Qg4 Nf6 7. Qxg7 Rg8 8.
Qh6 Rg6 {I was probably better to leave the Rook on g8, but I was playing too
quickly.} 9. Qh4 Qd5 10. Ne2 c5 $4 {Absolute rubbish. I was playing at
lightning speed and had seen the fork but still let him play it.} 11. Nf4 Qf5
12. Nxg6 Qxg6 13. Qg5 {White now tries to exchange everything off.} e3 14. Qxg6
exf2+ 15. Kxf2 hxg6 16. Bb5+ Kf8 17. Re1 a6 18. Bd3 Nc6 {My object is to
exchange my Knights for his Bishops.} 19. dxc5 Ne7 20. c4 Bd7 21. Bg5 Neg8 22.
Bxf6 Nxf6 23. Be4 Nxe4+ {White has given up his two Bishops, and this seems a
doubtful policy for him.} 24. Rxe4 Rc8 {White's Pawns are very weak.} 25. Rd4
Ke7 26. Rad1 Ba4 27. Rb1 Bc6 28. Rb3 Rh8 29. Rh3 Rc8 30. Rh7 {Waste of time.}
Be8 31. g4 Kf8 $1 {White threatened 32.h4, 33.h5 which is now prevented.} 32.
Rh3 Rxc5 33. Rb3 Bc6 {Threatening 34......e5 36......Rxc4} 34. Rc3 b5 35. Rd8+
Ke7 36. Rd4 e5 37. Rdd3 bxc4 {[60']} 38. Re3 Kf6 39. h4 e4 40. Rh3 Kg7 41. h5
Bd7 42. h6+ Kh7 43. Kg3 f5 44. gxf5 gxf5 {Loses.} (44... Bxf5 {May be better.})
45. Kf4 {Adjourned. Play resumed 23/3/65} Ba4 $1 {My only chance.} ({If} 45...
Be8 46. Rcg3 Bg6 47. Rxg6 $1 {etc.}) 46. Rcg3 $2 {The one move which saves me.}
({Correct was} 46. Rh2 $1 {when Black has no moves.}) 46... Bxc2 47. Rg7+ Kh8
48. h7 Rc8 49. Rhg3 Rc6 50. Re7 Rc8 51. Reg7 Rc6 52. Ra7 Rc8 53. Rh3 Bd3 54.
Rg3 c3 55. Rag7 Rc6 56. Re7 Rc8 57. Reg7 Rc6 {Rubbish. Uni lost the match.
According to the header in the scorebook this was a combined League and
Robertson Cup Final match. No reason is given for this combination.} 1/2-1/2

