1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 d6 3. Nc3 e5 4. d5 Be7 5. e4 O-O 6. Bd3 Nbd7 7. Nge2 Nc5 8. Bc2
a5 9. h3 Bd7 10. g4 c6 11. Ng3 cxd5 12. exd5 $1 {Better than.....} ({.....} 12.
cxd5) 12... Ne8 13. Be3 Rc8 14. Qd2 b6 15. O-O-O Qc7 {Slow} 16. Nf5 Bxf5 17.
Bxf5 Rd8 18. g5 g6 19. Bb1 f5 20. gxf6 Bxf6 21. h4 Ng7 22. Rdg1 Kf7 {Desperate
measures} 23. Bh6 Rg8 24. Bxg7 Rxg7 25. h5 Qe7 26. Qe2 Bg5+ 27. Kd1 Kg8 28. h6
Rf7 29. Qg4 $2 ({Correct} 29. Rg2) 29... Rxf2 $1 {I thought this move was
desperation so I didn't give my next move any thought.} ({Naturally} 29... Bf6
30. Bxg6 $18) 30. Qxg5 $2 {Overlooking his next move on the assumption that he
had just abandoned his Bishop.} Rf1+ 31. Rxf1 Qxg5 32. b3 Rf8 33. Nb5 Qg4+ 34.
Ke1 Qg3+ 35. Kd1 Qg4+ 36. Ke1 Qg3+ 37. Kd1 Rxf1+ 38. Rxf1 Nb7 39. Nc7 Nc5 40.
Ne8 Qg2 41. Ke1 Qb2 42. Nf6+ Kh8 43. Be4 Nxe4 44. Nxe4 Qb1+ 45. Kd2 Qxf1 {
A costly lapse in concentration. Exeter won the match 4.5 - 3.5} 0-1

