{Opponent info: Grade 5b ~ E.C.F. 169-176} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. g3 d5 4. cxd5
Nxd5 5. Bg2 Be6 6. d3 ({If} 6. Qb3 Nb4 {is probably best} 7. Bc6+) 6... Nc6 7.
Nf3 Qd7 8. Ng5 {In the corresponding position with the colours reversed i.e.
against the Sicillian ......NN5 equalises for Black.However White should be
aiming at more than equality.} Nb6 9. Nxe6 Qxe6 10. O-O Be7 11. Be3 O-O {[12']}
12. Qc1 Kh8 ({Not} 12... f5 $4 13. Bxb6 axb6 14. Bd5) 13. Nb5 Qd7 {[18']} 14.
Bc5 Rfe8 15. Bxe7 Nxe7 $1 {At least equalises. Otherwise I hadn't a very good
game.} 16. Nc3 ({Not} 16. Qxc7 $4 Qxb5) ({or} 16. Nxc7 $4 Rec8) ({or} 16. Bxb7
Qxb5) 16... c6 17. f4 exf4 18. Qxf4 Rf8 19. Ne4 Nbd5 20. Qf3 Ng6 21. Rf2 ({
Missing a good chance. Better was} 21. Ng5 {threatening the f-Pawn. If....} f6
$2 (21... Nf6 {saves me.}) 22. Nxh7 $1) 21... Qe7 {Prevents 22.Ng5. Also
threatening to cause trouble by 22......Ne5 23.Qf5 g6} (21... Qe7 22. Z0 Ne5
23. Qf5 g6) 22. Qf5 Ne5 23. Rc1 g6 24. Qg5 Qxg5 25. Nxg5 Ne3 26. d4 (26. Ne4
$142) 26... h6 27. dxe5 $2 (27. Ne4 $142) 27... hxg5 28. h3 Nxg2 29. Rxg2 Rac8
30. Rc5 Kg7 {Adjudicated. Drawn.} 1/2-1/2

