{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 Be7 5. Bg2 O-O
6. Nf3 dxc4 7. O-O Nbd7 8. e4 Rb8 9. a4 ({Not} 9. Qa4 Nb6 10. Qxa7 $4 Ra8) 9...
a6 10. a5 b5 11. axb6 cxb6 12. Bf4 Ra8 13. Nd2 {Wins back the Pawn at least.}
b5 {So as to open the b-file.} 14. Nxb5 Nb6 ({White threatened} 14... Z0 15.
Bc7 Qe8 16. Nd6 $1 {winning the exchange.}) 15. Nc7 $6 {A slight miscalculation
} (15. e5 $142) 15... Ra7 16. e5 Nfd5 ({Not} 16... Nfd7 $2 17. Nb5) 17. Nxd5 {
Not what I'd intended when playing 15.Nc7?!} ({I'd missed that after} 17. Nb5 {
Black plays} Rd7 {and if} 18. Nc3 Nxf4 $19) 17... exd5 18. Be3 Bf5 19. f4 Qd7
20. Nb1 Bh3 21. Nc3 Rb8 22. Qd2 Bb4 23. Bxh3 Qxh3 24. f5 Nd7 25. Qc2 Bxc3 26.
bxc3 Rab7 27. Bc1 Rb6 28. Rf4 Qh5 {I now spent too much time trying to find a
win} 29. Kg2 {Threatening to win the Queen. I was now very short of time.} ({If
} 29. Rh4 Qf3 30. f6 g6 {is no longer good for me.}) 29... g5 30. fxg6 Qxg6 31.
Rf5 Kh8 32. Qf2 {I was hopelessly short of time now.} Rb1 33. Rxb1 Rxb1 34. Bd2
$4 (34. Ba3 $142) 34... Rb2 35. Rf4 {It seems lost now.} Qd3 36. e6 {I now had
virtually no time at all and had given up keeping the score.} Rxd2 37. exd7
Rxf2+ 38. Kxf2 Qc2+ 39. Kf1 Qb1+ {In the mad time rush Black had given up
scoring.} 40. Kf2 Qb6 {Black had not got the score down and claimed a win on
time. In fact I had survived the time rush but resigned anyway. A Pity to
spoil the game leaving myself so short of time. Southampton University got 2.
5pts in the prliminary round and were put in Section C of the Championships.}
0-1

