{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs. Opponent info: Irish Glorney Cup player in 1963
} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O d6 6. Re1 Be7 {This order of
moves loses Black a tempo in the closed Morphy as my KBishop goes straight
back to c2.} 7. c3 O-O 8. h3 b5 9. Bc2 Re8 10. d4 Bf8 11. Bg5 h6 12. Bh4 g5 {
Weakens his KS} 13. Bg3 ({I considered} 13. Nxg5) 13... Bg7 14. Qd3 {Intending
15.h4} exd4 15. Nxd4 (15. cxd4 {is answered by} Nb4) 15... Ne5 16. Qd1 c5 17.
Nb3 {Threatening 18.Nxc5} Nc4 18. Qc1 a5 19. a4 b4 20. N1d2 Be6 21. f4 Nxd2 22.
Qxd2 $1 Bxb3 23. Bxb3 {The possibilty of Bxf7+ saves my e-Pawn.} Nh5 24. Bh2
gxf4 25. Bxf7+ Kxf7 26. Qd5+ Re6 ({Not} 26... Kg6 $4 27. Qf5#) (26... Kf8 $142)
27. Qxh5+ Kg8 28. Qd5 Qe8 29. Rac1 Ra7 30. Bxf4 Kh8 31. Kh2 ({Not} 31. Bxh6 $2
Rae7 32. e5 Rxh6 $1) 31... Rf6 32. g3 ({Not} 32. Bxh6 $4 Rxh6 $1) 32... Qxa4
33. Bxd6 Rf2+ 34. Kg1 Rxb2 {Once again I was very short of time.} 35. Qxc5 Qd7
({If} 35... Bxc3 36. Rxc3 $1) 36. g4 {This is the only move but good enough.
However I only had a few seconds left now.} Ra6 {Now my flag was about to fall.
I only have time for one more move and it loses.} 37. e5 $2 ({Correct was} 37.
Red1) 37... Qb7 {White lost on time. Again I lose on time. I decided to play
much faster in the next round. Southampton University got 5pts in this round.}
0-1

