{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 {Had White played c4 I was
going to play the Blumfeld counter gambit} 3. Bg5 d5 4. e3 Be7 5. Bd3 b6 6. O-O
Ba6 {An idea I had on the spur of the moment.} 7. Bxa6 Nxa6 8. c4 {Threatening
9.Qa4+} O-O 9. cxd5 Nxd5 10. Bxe7 Qxe7 11. Qe2 Nb8 12. Rc1 Rc8 13. Nc3 Nxc3 14.
Rxc3 Nd7 15. Rac1 Nf6 ({If} 15... c5 16. b4) 16. e4 h6 17. Qc2 a5 18. Rc6 Qd7
19. Rd1 Qe7 20. h3 Qd7 21. d5 exd5 22. exd5 Ne8 ({If} 22... Nxd5 23. Ne5) 23.
Ne5 Qe7 24. Nc4 Rd8 25. Ne3 Qe5 {Here he offered a draw, and as I was playing
so badly I accepted. Southampton University scored 4.5pts this round and came
equal first in scetion C along with St.Andrew's} 1/2-1/2

