1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. Nc3 d6 6. e4 c5 7. dxc5 dxc5 8. Qxd8
Rxd8 9. Be3 {White mistakenlydecides to put pressure on my c-Pawn} Na6 10. Na4
$2 {Overlooking my reply} Nb4 11. Rd1 (11. Ke2 {is no better}) 11... Nc2+ 12.
Ke2 Rxd1 13. Kxd1 Nxe3+ 14. fxe3 Ng4 15. Ke2 Ne5 16. Nf3 {Rather belated
development.} Nxc4 17. Rd1 Bg4 18. h3 Bxf3+ 19. Bxf3 Ne5 {Stronger than......}
({......} 19... Nxb2 20. Nxb2 Bxb2 21. Rb1) 20. Nxc5 {Now I simplify into a
won Pawn endgame.} Rc8 21. Nb3 Rc2+ 22. Rd2 Rxd2+ 23. Nxd2 Nxf3 24. Kxf3 Bxb2
25. Nc4 Bc3 {White's Knight has no scope at all.} 26. e5 Kg7 27. Ke4 Kh6 28.
Kd5 Be1 29. g4 Kg5 30. e6 fxe6+ 31. Kxe6 Bb4 32. a3 Bc5 33. a4 Kh4 34. e4 Kxh3
35. Ne5 Kg3 36. Nd7 Ba3 37. Nf8 h5 38. Nxg6 hxg4 39. Kf5 {The match ended here
and White resigned.} (39. Kf5 Kf3 40. Ne5+ Ke3 41. Nxg4+ Kd4 {and Black plays..
..} 42. Z0 a6 43. Z0 b5 {etc.}) 0-1

