1. Nf3 d5 2. c4 d4 3. e3 c5 4. b4 {I didn't know this opening at all and spent
a long time here.} Nc6 ({M.C.O. gives} 4... g6) ({or} 4... f6 {here. I prefer
my move.}) 5. b5 ({If} 5. bxc5 e5) 5... Na5 {Not so bad as it looks. I'd taken
about 30' here.} ({If} 5... Nb8 {I loses a Pawn.}) 6. exd4 cxd4 7. d3 (7. Bb2
d3 {Threatens Nxc4}) 7... g6 8. Bb2 Bg7 9. Nbd2 e5 10. Be2 Ne7 11. O-O b6 {
I want to be able to answer 12.Nb3 with Nb7} 12. Nb3 Nb7 13. Qc2 {White now
tries to force c5} Bd7 14. a4 Rc8 15. Nfd2 O-O 16. Ba3 f5 {To prevent 17.Ne4
as d6 is weak.} 17. Rac1 Be6 18. Qb1 Rf7 19. c5 $2 {After all his preparation
this move is a mistake as it lets my Knight onto d5.} (19. Bf3 $142) 19... bxc5
20. Bxc5 $2 {Loses the exchange.} Nd5 21. Bf3 Nc3 22. Rxc3 dxc3 23. Bxb7 Rxb7
24. Nc4 Rd7 25. Nca5 Bd5 {To prevent 26.Nc6} 26. Rc1 Kh8 27. Rxc3 Be4 ({If} 
27... e4 28. d4) 28. Be7 Rxe7 29. Rxc8 Qxc8 30. dxe4 Qc3 31. Qd1 Re8 32. exf5
gxf5 33. h3 e4 34. Nc6 {To prevent 34......Be5} ({If} 34. Qd7 Qe1+ 35. Kh2 Be5+
) 34... e3 35. fxe3 Qxe3+ 36. Kh1 ({If} 36. Kf1 Bc3) 36... Qg3 (36... Qg3 {If}
37. Ne7 Be5 38. Kg1 Bf6) 0-1

