{Opponent info: London U/18 Champion} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5.
Bg5 O-O 6. f4 c5 7. d5 Qa5 8. Bd3 e6 {Although this is the correct procedure
it should be preceeded by ......h6!} 9. dxe6 Bxe6 10. Nge2 Nc6 11. O-O a6 (
11... h6 $142) 12. f5 Bd7 13. Qd2 Ne5 14. Rad1 b5 15. Nf4 {This is very strong.
} h6 $2 {Losing my b-Pawn. The position is very complicated.} ({If} 15... gxf5
16. Bb1 {and my d-Pawn goes.}) 16. Bxf6 {23 I don't know if White saw through
to move} Bxf6 17. Ncd5 Qd8 ({If} 17... Qxd2 18. Nxf6+ Kg7 19. N6h5+ gxh5 20.
Nxh5+) 18. Nxf6+ Qxf6 19. Nd5 Qg5 ({If} 19... Qg7 20. f6 Qh7 21. Ne7+ {is
hardly enticing.}) 20. Qxg5 ({I thought he might try} 20. Ne7+ Qxe7 21. f6)
20... hxg5 21. Nf6+ Kg7 22. Nxd7 Nxd7 23. cxb5 axb5 24. Bxb5 Nf6 25. a4 Ra7 ({
If} 25... Nxe4 26. Bc6) 26. fxg6 Nxe4 27. Rxf7+ Rfxf7 28. gxf7 Kxf7 29. Bc6 Kf6
$6 {Knight moves is no better.} 30. Bxe4 Rxa4 31. Bd5 Ke5 32. g3 Rb4 33. b3 Rb8
34. Kg2 Rf8 35. Bc4 Rd8 36. Rd5+ Kf6 37. Kf3 Kg6 38. Kg4 {A good game by White}
1-0

