{Time limit 44 moves in 2 hours} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. exd5 Qxd5 5.
Ngf3 cxd4 6. Bc4 Qd8 7. Nb3 Nc6 ({M.C.O. 9th Ed gives} 7... Nf6 8. O-O Nc6 9.
Nbxd4 Nxd4 10. Nxd4 Be7 11. c3 a6 12. Qe2 Qc7 $11) 8. Nbxd4 Nxd4 9. Qxd4 {
Forcing off the Queens, but if.......} ({........} 9. Nxd4 e5 {ia good for
Black e.g.} 10. Nf3 Qxd1+ 11. Kxd1 Bg4) 9... Qxd4 10. Nxd4 a6 ({If} 10... e5
11. Nb5) 11. O-O b5 ({I thought he might play.} 11... a5) 12. Bb3 ({and here I
expected.} 12. Bd3) 12... Nf6 13. h3 Bb7 14. a4 {This seems a wrong plan which
leaves his a-pawn weak.} b4 15. a5 O-O-O {With this Black gets a slight
innitiative. 16.Ba4 was threatened.} 16. Be3 Nd5 {Rather unpleasant for White.}
17. Rac1 Nxe3 18. fxe3 e5 19. Nf3 Bc5 20. Rfe1 f6 21. Kf2 Rd6 22. Rcd1 {[90']}
Rhd8 23. Rxd6 Rxd6 24. Ke2 {White was getting short of time here.} Rd8 25. Bc4
Kc7 26. g3 {White can make no progress.} Rd6 27. h4 Bc8 {Threatening 28......
Bg4} 28. Nh2 Bf5 29. Rc1 Kb7 30. Bd3 Bxd3+ 31. cxd3 Rc6 {White can hardly save
his a-Pawn} 32. Nf3 Bd6 33. Rxc6 {More or less forced.} Kxc6 34. Nd2 Bc7 35. g4
Bxa5 36. g5 fxg5 37. hxg5 Bd8 38. Ne4 a5 39. b3 Be7 40. Kd2 Kb5 41. Kc2 a4 42.
bxa4+ Kxa4 43. Kb2 Kb5 $1 44. Kb3 Bc5 45. Ng3 {Hastings won the match 15.5 - 6.
5. I was the only Hayes player to win! Dr.Learner beat Karaklaic at Bognor
last year.} 0-1

