1. d4 g6 2. c4 Bg7 3. Nc3 f5 4. g3 Nc6 5. e3 {I wanted to play the KKnight to
f4 not f3} Nf6 6. Bg2 d6 7. Nge2 Bd7 {This seems to weaken the long White
diagonal and particularly b7, rather unnecessarily.} (7... e5 {Was playable.})
8. d5 Na5 ({I would have preffered....} 8... Ne5) 9. Qd3 {Threat 10.b4} c5 ({
and here I would have preffered..} 9... b6 10. Z0 Nb7 11. Z0 Nc5) 10. Nf4 {
Now Ne6 is in the air and 10......e5 is prevented.} Qc8 {Black is getting
rather tied up.} 11. b3 g5 {Drastic measures which don't achieve much.} ({
If now} 11... Ne4 12. Bb2 Nxc3 {is unplayable.}) 12. Nfe2 b6 13. Bb2 Nb7 {
While White develops Black has to go through awkward manoeuvres.} 14. f4 {
Forcing 15......g5 which puts an end to any slight counterplay.} ({I considered
} 14. h4 h6 15. hxg5 hxg5 16. Rxh8+ Bxh8 17. O-O-O {but it's doubtful.}) ({If} 
14. O-O-O Ng4) 14... g4 ({Not} 14... gxf4 15. Nxf4) 15. O-O {The most solid
move.} Nd8 16. Rae1 {Preparing e4.} Nf7 17. Nc1 (17. Nc1 {Threatening
something like......} Z0 18. e4 fxe4 19. Nxe4 Bf5 20. Bxf6 Bxe4 21. Bxe4 Bxf6
22. Bxh7) 17... O-O 18. Qd2 Rb8 19. e4 {Now or never as Black was preparing
counterplay with ......b5. Black was now very short of time.} e5 $6 {This
surprised me. Black is trying to complicate things.} 20. dxe6 Bxe6 21. exf5
Bxf5 22. Re7 Re8 {Black decides he must contest the e-file even at the cost of
the a-Pawn. He was now very short of time.} 23. Rxa7 Qe6 24. Nd5 (24. Nd5 {
Threatening......} Z0 25. Nxf6+ Bxf6 26. Bd5) 24... Ne4 25. Bxe4 Qxe4 ({If} 
25... Bxe4 26. Nc7) 26. Bxg7 Kxg7 27. Qc3+ Qd4+ ({Short of time Black misses a
slightly better line} 27... Kf8 28. Qf6 $1 Qd4+ {forced} 29. Qxd4 cxd4 {
although Black is still badly placed.}) 28. Qxd4+ cxd4 29. Ne7 Be4 {To prvent
30.Nc6} 30. Rd1 ({Not} 30. Re1 d3 $1) 30... Ra8 31. Rxa8 Rxa8 32. Rxd4 Bf3 33.
Nf5+ Kg6 34. Nh4+ Kf6 35. Nxf3 gxf3 36. Kf2 Re8 {Championship (20) Amboyna
Shield (50)} 1-0

