{Opponent info: Miss Rogers is an ex GBR Girls U/18 champion.} 1. d4 d5 2. c4
dxc4 3. Nf3 c6 4. e4 Bg4 5. Bxc4 e6 {Black's opening system seems somewhat
doubtful} 6. O-O Nd7 7. d5 $1 Nb6 ({If} 7... Bxf3 8. gxf3 Ne5 9. Bb3 {Black is
badly placed.}) 8. dxe6 Qxd1 {Black decides to go in for the complications.} ({
Black's best reply now is...} 8... Bxe6 9. Bxe6 fxe6 10. Qb3 {witha big
advantage to White.}) 9. exf7+ Ke7 10. fxg8=N+ $1 ({If} 10. fxg8=Q Rxg8 $1 11.
Rxd1 Nxc4 {Blacks KS Pawns remain undoubled.}) 10... Ke8 ({The alternative was
} 10... Rxg8 11. Bg5+ Ke8 12. Rxd1 Nxc4 {Where Black's Pawns are undoubled but
White has an extra piece developed.}) 11. Rxd1 Nxc4 12. Rd4 Bxf3 ({If} 12...
Nd6 13. e5) 13. gxf3 Nb6 ({I expected} 13... Ne5) 14. Nh6 gxh6 15. Nc3 Bg7 16.
e5 $1 {Blocking off the Bishop} ({If} 16. Rd1 Nc4 {is a nuisance.}) 16... Rg8
17. Kf1 Kf7 18. f4 Bf8 19. f5 Bc5 {Her h-Pawn was doomed anyway.} 20. Rh4 Bf8
21. Bxh6 Bxh6 22. Rxh6 Kg7 23. Re6 ({If} 23. Rd6 Nc4) 23... Raf8 24. f6+ Kg6
25. Rd1 Rf7 26. Re7 $6 {A time-trouble error, although it may be the quickest
way to win.} Rxe7 27. fxe7 Kf7 28. Rd8 Re8 29. Ne4 Kxe7 ({If now} 29... Rxe7
30. Ng5+ Kg7 31. f4) 30. Rxe8+ Kxe8 (30... Kxe8 {This was the time control.
Black resigned as I win another Pawn.} 31. Nd6+ Ke7 32. b3 $1) 1-0

