1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. e4 Nxe5 5. f4 Nec6 6. Be3 {To prevent 6......
Bc5} Bb4+ 7. Nc3 d6 8. Bd3 Na6 ({More usual is} 8... a5) 9. Nf3 Bg4 {Not a
particularly good squre for the Bishop.} 10. O-O Bxc3 {The doubled Pawns are
here almost an advantage. Better probably was 10.......Bc5} (10... Bc5) 11.
bxc3 Nc5 {rather doubtful.} 12. Bxc5 dxc5 13. h3 Bd7 14. e5 Ne7 15. Ng5 Nf5 16.
Qe1 {To prevent Knight forks & 16......f6 and allowing for a possible e6.} Qe7
{Now the Knight gets trapped but he had little choice in view of the threat of
e6.} 17. g4 Nh6 18. Rb1 Bc6 19. Be4 ({If} 19. e6 O-O-O $1) 19... Bxe4 20. Qxe4
c6 21. Rfd1 Rd8 22. Rd6 {Expecting to win the endgame.} Rxd6 23. exd6 Qxe4 24.
Nxe4 b6 25. Nxc5 Kd8 26. Na4 $6 Re8 27. Rd1 ({The position is very tricky} 27.
Nxb6 {was not good enough.}) 27... Re2 28. c5 $6 {This wins as Black was short
of time. However........} ({.......correct was} 28. a3 $1 Ra2 29. c5 b5 30. Nb6
) 28... bxc5 $2 {Missing his chance in the time rush.} ({but....} 28... b5 $1
29. Nb6 axb6 30. cxb6 Re8 $19) ({If} 28... Rxa2 29. cxb6 $1) 29. Nxc5 Rxa2 30.
Rb1 Kc8 31. d7+ Kc7 32. Rb7+ 1-0

