1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 {Hoping to play the Blumfeld Counter Gambit} 3. e3 c5 4. c3
d5 5. Bd3 Nc6 6. Nbd2 Bd6 7. O-O e5 {Secures at least equality.} 8. dxe5 Bxe5 (
{8......Bxe5 was prefferable to} 8... Nxe5 9. Nxe5 Bxe5 10. Nf3 {as I gain a
tempo and the innitiative.}) 9. Nxe5 Nxe5 10. Bc2 ({If} 10. Nf3 Bg4) 10... O-O
11. e4 Be6 12. exd5 Bxd5 13. Re1 Qc7 14. Ne4 {Threatening 15.Bf4. However I
now establish a Knight on d3 which severely restricts White's game.} Bxe4 15.
Bxe4 Rad8 16. Qc2 Nxe4 17. Rxe4 ({I'd prefer.} 17. Qxe4) 17... Nd3 18. Be3 Rd7
19. g3 Rfd8 (19... Rfd8 20. Z0 {Black threatens....} Qc6 21. Rh4 {Rook moves}
Nxb2 22. f3 f5 {etc.}) 20. Qe2 h6 21. Rb1 Qc6 22. Bf4 {White wants to keep the
long diagonal closed in view of .....Nxb2 & if 22.c3 f5 is a nuisance. However
Black has a strong reply on move 23.} Kf8 23. f3 {Loses a lost game.} g5 $1 24.
Be3 ({Now if} 24. Bc1 Nxc1 25. Rxc1 Rd2) ({or if} 24. Bd2 Nf2 $3) 24... f5 25.
Rc4 ({If} 25. Re6 Qxe6 26. Bxc5+ Nxc5 {defends the Queen.}) 25... b5 {White
can resign.} 26. Bxc5+ Nxc5 27. Qe5 Rd1+ 28. Rxd1 Rxd1+ 29. Kg2 bxc4 30. Qh8+
Ke7 31. Qg7+ Kd8 32. Qf8+ Kc7 33. Qxf5 Rd2+ 34. Kg1 Ne6 35. Qe5+ Kb7 36. Qe1
Qd5 {1 University won the match 4 -} 0-1

