1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. f4 d5 4. fxe5 Nxe4 5. d3 Ng5 {White seemed rather ill
at ease against this.} 6. d4 Bb4 7. Bd3 Nc6 8. Nge2 ({I'd prefer} 8. Be3) ({or
} 8. a3) 8... Bg4 9. Bb5 $2 {Doubtful} Ne4 (9... Ne4 {Threatening.....} 10. Z0
Nxc3 11. Z0 Qh4+) 10. O-O {Loses a piece but White was probably lost anyway.}
Bxc3 11. bxc3 Nxc3 12. Bxc6+ bxc6 {There is no indication in teh score why the
two competions were combined. Uni won the match 3 - 2 R.C.Mitchell (22 August
1927 – 18 September 2003) stood as Labour candidate in Southampton (Test) in
the 1964 & 1966 Elections. Dick added these notes much later. He was M.P for
Southampton (Test) 1966-1970 and M.P for Itchen 1971-1983. His obituary 
(including a picture of him in a simul of M.Ps v Kortschnoi) appeared in the
Daily Telegraph on 25 Sept 2003. He played for the British Correspondence
Chess Association v other Countries.} 0-1

