1. d4 e6 2. e4 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. Bd3 c5 6. c3 Nc6 7. Ne2 Be7 8. O-O
b6 {Positional but passive.} 9. Re1 Bb7 10. Nf3 Qc7 11. a3 Nf8 ({Again too
passive Black must aim for......} 11... f6) 12. Bd2 {White has plenty of time
to strengthen his position.} c4 {Black now pesues a policy of blocking the QS,
which leaves White free to attack on the KS.} 13. Bc2 b5 14. g3 Ng6 15. h4 a5
16. Nh2 a4 $2 {Now White can win on the QS.} 17. f4 O-O-O 18. f5 Nf8 19. Nf4
Qd7 20. Qg4 {Wins a Pawn at least.} Rg8 $2 {Loses a lost game.} 21. f6 Nxe5 ({
Now if} 21... gxf6 22. Qxg8 {and the Queen gets out safely.}) 22. dxe5 ({If} 
22. Rxe5 Bd6 23. fxg7 $2 Ng6 {etc.}) 22... Bc5+ 23. Be3 Bxe3+ 24. Rxe3 g6 25.
Rd1 Bc6 26. Nf3 Kb8 27. Nd4 h6 {Black hopes to block the position completely.}
28. Nh3 Qb7 {Black marks time.} 29. Qf4 Rh8 30. Nf2 Rc8 31. Ng4 h5 {Now White
can break through} 32. Nh2 Qd7 33. Kf2 Nh7 34. Nhf3 Qb7 35. g4 Nf8 36. Rg1 hxg4
37. Qxg4 Nd7 38. Ng5 Nc5 39. Rh3 Rh5 {Apparently blocking the h-Pawn, but
White has a trick up his sleeve.} 40. Nxc6+ Rxc6 41. Nxf7 $1 Qxf7 42. Bxg6 Rf5+
43. Bxf5 exf5 44. Qg8+ Qxg8 45. Rxg8+ {A very interesting game.} 1-0

