1. e4 e5 2. f4 Nc6 3. Nf3 d6 4. Bc4 Be6 {Doubtful as he gets isolated doubled
Pawns.} 5. Bxe6 fxe6 6. fxe5 dxe5 (6... Nxe5 {Loses a Pawn.}) 7. d3 Bc5 8. Ng5
Qd7 9. Qg4 Nd4 10. Kd1 {This is no great inconvenience.} Nf6 11. Qh3 O-O-O 12.
Nd2 {Intending to put pressure on his other e-Pawn.} h6 13. Ngf3 Nxc2 $6 {
Black trys to take advantage of his "lead in development". Ufortunately this
lead doesn't quite compensate for his inferior Pawn position.} 14. Nxe5 Qd4 ({
If} 14... Ne3+ 15. Ke2) (14... Qd6 15. Ndc4 $1) 15. Qxe6+ Kb8 16. Kxc2 Rhe8 17.
Nc6+ {Wrecking his Pawns again} bxc6 18. Qc4 Qe3 {The best move offering a lot
of chances due to my lack of development. Black threatens 19......Rd5 and .....
.Ng4--f2} 19. Rf1 {The best move. Obtaining active play for the Rook and
covering the f-file.} Rd4 20. Qc3 ({Not} 20. Qxc5 $4 Qxd3+ 21. Kd1 Qxf1+) 20...
Bb4 21. Rf3 Qg1 {Forced if he is to keep an innitiative, but also quite
promising, pinning my Bishop and threatening the KS Pawns.} 22. Qxc6 Red8 {
The threat was 23.RxN} 23. Rf5 $1 {Again the best move .....} R8d6 {Loses a
piece but he was short of time.} ({If instead...} 23... Bxd2 24. Bxd2 Qxa1 25.
Bf4 {etc. with a good attack.}) 24. Rb5+ Kc8 25. Qb7+ Kd7 26. Rxb4 Rxd3 27.
Qb5+ ({If} 27. e5 Qc5+) 27... Kd8 28. e5 R6d5 29. Qb8+ Kd7 30. Rc4 Ne8 31. e6+
Ke7 32. Qb4+ c5 33. Qb7+ Kxe6 34. Re4+ Kf5 {Allows a neat finish.} 35. Qf7+ Nf6
36. g4+ (36. g4+ {If} Kg5 37. Nf3# {A good game}) 1-0

