{Opponent info: County Champion 1963} 1. Nf3 c5 2. c4 g6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Bg7
5. e4 d6 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. f3 O-O 8. Be3 Nc6 9. Qd2 Bd7 10. Be2 a6 11. h4 Qb8 12.
Kf2 ({After} 12. a4 {it would be very difficult for Black to obtain
counterplay on the QS.}) 12... Nxd4 13. Bxd4 b5 14. Nd5 {This results in
wholesale exchanges and a drawish end-game.} Nxd5 15. cxd5 {Forced.} Bxd4+ 16.
Qxd4 Rc8 17. Rac1 Rxc1 18. Rxc1 Ra7 19. Ke1 Rc7 {Black has a slight advantage
but not nearly enough to win.} 20. Rxc7 Qxc7 21. Kd1 f6 22. a3 Kf7 23. Kd2 e5
24. Qe3 {White isn't taking any chances.} Kg7 25. g3 f5 26. exf5 Bxf5 27. Bd3 (
{If White were trying to win he should have played......} 27. g4) 27... Bxd3
28. Qxd3 Qc5 29. Ke2 a5 30. g4 Kf6 31. Qd2 Qc4+ 32. Qd3 Qxd3+ 33. Kxd3 h5 {
The only chance for a win.} 34. Ke4 {White plays correctly the alternatives
lose} (34. gxh5) (34. g5+) 34... hxg4 1/2-1/2

