1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. O-O d6 6. d3 Be6 {I wasn't keen
on a symetrical position.} 7. Bb3 Qe7 8. Na4 d5 {More or less ensuring
equality.} 9. Nxc5 Qxc5 10. exd5 Nxd5 11. Ng5 {White gets the two Bishops but
Black has superior development and better centrality.} Qe7 12. Nxe6 Qxe6 {
The pin does't matter.} 13. f4 {A strong move.} O-O ({If now} 13... O-O-O {
my f-Pawn is weak.}) 14. d4 $6 ({I expected} 14. f5 {but White had other plans.
}) 14... exd4 ({Not of course} 14... Nxd4 15. c3) 15. Qf3 Rad8 16. f5 Qd6 17.
Bxd5 Qxd5 18. Qg3 {Regaining his Pawn by threatening c7 and Bh6} f6 19. Bf4 {
Black ow hangs onto his extra Pawn.} ({If} 19. Qxc7 Nb4 20. Z0 Rc8 {is good
for Black.}) 19... Ne5 20. Rfe1 Rfe8 21. Rad1 c5 {Black strengthens his
position} 22. Rd2 Nc6 {Much clearer than.......} ({.......} 22... Nc4 23. Rde2)
23. Bc7 Rxe1+ 24. Qxe1 Rc8 25. Rf2 {White defends his f-pawn.} ({Not} 25. Re2
$4 Rxc7) 25... Kf7 26. Bg3 Re8 27. Qd1 Qe4 28. Qh5+ Kg8 29. Rf1 Qe2 {The only
move but it wins} 30. Qf3 Qxf3 31. Rxf3 Re2 32. Rf2 Re1+ ({If now} 32... Rxf2
33. Bxf2 Nb4 34. c3) 33. Rf1 Re3 ({Now} 33... Rxf1+ 34. Kxf1 Nb4 {isn't quite
good enough.}) 34. Re1 Rxe1+ 35. Bxe1 Kf7 36. Kf2 g6 37. fxg6+ hxg6 38. Kf3 Ke6
39. a3 Ne5+ 40. Ke2 ({If} 40. Ke4 f5+ 41. Kf4 d3 $1 {However Black now wins
another pawn.}) 40... Nc4 41. b3 Nxa3 42. Kd3 Kd5 43. c4+ dxc3 44. Bxc3 f5 45.
Bg7 Nb5 46. Bh6 Nd4 47. Kc3 b5 48. Bg7 b4+ 49. Kd3 {Shortens the torture.} Nxb3
{We were now placed 3rd behind Cambridge I & Glasgow, ahead of Oxford I,
London I, Sheffield, Leeds etc. Southampton scored 5/8 Rd1} 0-1

