{Opponent info: GBR U/18 Champion} 1. d4 f5 2. c4 e6 3. g3 Nf6 4. Bg2 Be7 5.
Nc3 O-O 6. Nf3 d5 7. Qd3 c6 8. a3 a5 9. O-O b6 10. Bf4 {This move is of
doubtful value as the Bishop is driven back and the c-Pawn comes under fire.}
Ba6 11. b3 Ne4 12. Ne5 g5 13. Bc1 Nd6 14. Na4 b5 15. Nc5 ({15.Nc5 gives up a
pawn but I preffered it to} 15. cxb5 {etc.}) 15... bxc4 16. bxc4 Nxc4 {Best}
17. Nxc4 Bxc5 18. Qe3 ({18.Qe3 after much thought. If} 18. dxc5 Bxc4 19. Qe3
Qe7 {I can't play} 20. Qxg5+ {as the e-pawn is loose & my Pawns rather weak.})
18... Qf6 ({If now} 18... Bxd4 19. Qxd4 Bxc4 20. Bb2 {is good for White}) 19.
Ne5 {Better than.........} ({..........} 19. dxc5 Bxc4 ({Not} 19... Qxa1 $4 20.
Bb2)) 19... Be7 20. Bd2 a4 21. Rfc1 Bb5 22. f4 g4 23. Rab1 Kh8 24. h3 gxh3 $2 {
Giving White attacking chances on the h-file.} 25. Bxh3 Rg8 26. Kf2 Qg7 27. Rh1
Bf6 28. Rh2 Nd7 29. Rbh1 Nf8 {Black suddenly finds himself on a desperate
defence.} 30. Bg2 Ra7 31. Bb4 {Black is unable to prevent the attack building
up.} Be7 {Black may have wished afterwards that he had exchanged this Bishop
for my Kight rather than the Bishop.} 32. Bc5 Bxc5 33. dxc5 Rb7 {With ideas of
an eventual .......Rb3} 34. Rh3 Qe7 {Allows a neat wining combination but it
was very difficult.} 35. Qd4 $3 {Obviously threatening a discovered mate, but
in fact it forces mate.} Qg7 {As good as anything} (35... Qg7 36. Ng6+) 36.
Rxh7+ $1 {A very neat finish. Southampton Uni scored 3/8 in Rd2 Results 1.
Cambridge I 12.5pts 2. Oxford I 11 3. London I 10.5 4. Glasgow 9 5.
Southampton 8.5 6. London II 8 7. Sheffield 7.5 8. Leeds 7 9. Newcastle 3.5 10.
Wales II 3.5} 1-0

