{Opponent info: Ex-Southern counties champion.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 e5 4.
Nc3 d6 5. e4 g6 6. Be2 Bg7 7. g4 $6 {Decidning on immediate action.} h5 8. g5
Nh7 9. Nf3 Bg4 10. Rg1 Nd7 11. Rg3 {so as to play h3} Nb6 12. b3 f5 $6 {
The only chance of counterplay.} 13. gxf6 Qxf6 14. Nb5 Kd7 15. Be3 a6 16. Nc3
a5 {Black can attempt very little.} 17. a4 {White is in a hurry and this
prevents 17...a4.} Rhf8 18. Qd2 Nc8 19. O-O-O Ne7 20. Kc2 {20......Nf5 was a
threat so the Knight needed further protection} b6 21. Rdg1 Bxf3 22. Bxf3 Rf7
23. Bg2 $1 g5 24. f3 {Preventing 24......g4 and winning at least a pawn.} Rg8 {
Loses the exchange but this is no worse than anything else as White would soon
crash through on the g-file.} 25. Bh3+ Kd8 26. Be6 Bh6 27. Bxf7 Qxf7 28. h4 Ng6
29. hxg5 h4 30. Rh3 Bf8 31. Bf2 Qd7 32. Rh2 h3 33. Rg4 Nf4 34. Ne2 Nxe2 35.
Qxe2 {Black has no hope now.} Rxg5 36. Bh4 Be7 37. Bxg5 Nxg5 38. Qe3 {4 A good
win. I played well. hants lost on Bds 1-4} 1-0

