1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 Bg7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3 c6 7. Bd3 dxc4 8. Bxc4
Nbd7 9. O-O Nb6 10. Bd3 Nfd5 11. Be5 Bg4 12. Bxg7 Kxg7 13. h3 Bxf3 14. Qxf3
Nxc3 15. bxc3 e5 $1 {Secures Black a QS Pawn majority. White is playing too
lethargically.} 16. Qe2 exd4 17. cxd4 Re8 18. Rfd1 Nd5 19. Qb2 Qb6 20. Rab1 Re7
21. Rdc1 f5 {Undermining White's Pawn structure.} 22. Bc4 Qxb2 23. Rxb2 Rd8 24.
g3 {Trying to prevent ......f4} Kf6 25. a4 {Hoping for counterplay on the QS.}
g5 26. Bd3 f4 {This breakthrough should win for Black.} 27. e4 {The best try.}
Nb6 28. Rb4 ({If} 28. a5 Rxd4) 28... Red7 29. e5+ {White's skating on thin ice.
} Ke7 30. a5 Rxd4 31. Rxd4 Rxd4 32. Bxh7 Nc4 33. gxf4 gxf4 34. a6 b5 {It was a
toss up whether I resigned here.} 35. Kg2 Nxe5 36. Re1 Kf6 {Black has an easy
win.} 37. Bc2 Rc4 38. Be4 Ra4 39. h4 Rxa6 40. Rd1 Ra4 $4 (40... c5 {and White
must resign. Black was obviously overconfident}) 41. Bxc6 Nxc6 42. Rd6+ Kf5 43.
Rxc6 Kg4 44. Rc5 f3+ 45. Kh2 Ra2 (45... Rb4 $142) 46. Rxb5 Rxf2+ 47. Kg1 Rg2+
48. Kf1 Kxh4 49. Ra5 {White has an easy draw.} Rg7 50. Kf2 Rf7 51. Ra6 Kg5 52.
Ra3 Kg4 {Never say die.} 1/2-1/2

