{Time limit 2hr 15' for 30 moves.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5.
Nc3 a6 6. Bc4 g6 7. Be3 Bg7 8. Qd2 O-O 9. O-O Nbd7 10. Bh6 Qc7 11. Bxg7 Kxg7
12. Be2 Nc5 13. f3 Qb6 {Threat 14......e5} 14. Kh1 Bd7 15. Nb3 Rac8 16. Rad1
Na4 17. Nxa4 Bxa4 18. Bd3 Rc7 19. Qf2 Qc6 20. Nd4 Qc5 21. Nb3 {I could
normally beat White easily and in this game he makes no attempt to win, hoping
to hold on for a draw.(The match was 4hr 30' session) Hence White's futile
attempt to exchange off. Hardly what I'd call Chess!} Qxf2 22. Rxf2 Rfc8 23. h3
Nd7 24. f4 Nb6 25. Nd4 Bd7 26. b3 d5 {Trying to work up some winning chances.}
27. e5 e6 28. Re1 Bc6 29. Re3 {Knowing that he needn't play more than 30 moves
White at last shows a glimmer of aggression.} Nd7 30. Rg3 Nc5 31. f5 Bd7 32.
fxe6 Bxe6 33. Nxe6+ fxe6 34. Rf6 Re8 35. h4 Nxd3 36. cxd3 ({Stopped for
adjudication. I eventually agreed a draw as I can't quite win. White thought
he was going to win at the end! In fact,} 36. cxd3 Rc1+ 37. Kh2 Re1 {draws
easily for Black.}) 1/2-1/2

