1. e4 e6 2. Nf3 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 c4 5. Bxc4 $4 {White would presumably expect
to lose rather easily on the current run of play (He plays for the Univ C team)
. His only hope therefore is overconfidence on my part and complications on
his part . 5.Bxc4 however must be too rash.} dxc4 6. Qa4+ Nc6 7. Qxc4 Qd5 8.
Qe2 ({If} 8. Qa4 {or 8.Qb3 then} Qd3 $1) 8... f6 9. d4 fxe5 10. dxe5 Bd7 {
White has some chances on the KS so my King goes the other way.} 11. O-O O-O-O
12. Rd1 Qa5 13. a3 Be7 14. Nbd2 {Too slow all out attack on the QS is his only
chance.} Be8 {A useful pin on the Knight} 15. Qc4 Qd5 16. Re1 Qxc4 17. Nxc4 b5
{Quickest} 18. Nd6+ Bxd6 19. exd6 Nf6 20. Rxe6 Bf7 21. Re2 Rxd6 22. Bf4 Rd7 23.
g3 Bh5 {The beginning of the end.} 24. Kg2 Nd5 25. Be5 Rf8 26. Nd4 {Crumble,
crumble!} Nxd4 27. Rd2 Bf3+ 28. Kh3 Nb3 29. Rxd5 Rxd5 30. Bxg7 Rh5# 0-1

