{Time limit: 75' for 36 moves.} 1. d4 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. Bf4
d6 6. e3 O-O 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. O-O a6 {With the fast rate of play I was playing
the opening very quickly as White's passive play wasn't worrying me. 8......a6
is rather inexact.} ({Better was} 8... c6 {preventing 9.Nd5 as well as 9.Nb5})
9. Rc1 Qe8 (9... c6 {Was more correct.}) 10. Nd5 Qd8 (10... Nxd5 {is bad.}) 11.
Ng5 Nb6 12. Nxb6 cxb6 13. Qb3 h6 14. Nf3 ({I was expecting} 14. c5+ d5 15. Nf3
{with advantage to White.}) 14... Be6 15. d5 {This causes Black little trouble.
} Bf7 16. h3 Nd7 (16... Nd7 {Threatening......} 17. Z0 Nc5 18. Qc2 Nxd3 19.
Qxd3 Bxb2) 17. Qc2 Rc8 18. Qd2 a5 {so as to play 19......Nc5 without the reply
20.b4} 19. b3 Nc5 20. Rfe1 g5 {having stabilised the QS Black is ready to
advance on the King's wing.} 21. Bh2 Qd7 22. Nd4 Bg6 23. Bc2 Rf6 24. a3 {
White tries for QS counterplay.} Rcf8 25. f3 {Preventing 25......Ne4 amongst
other things.} R6f7 26. b4 axb4 27. axb4 Bxd4 28. Qxd4 Na6 29. Qxb6 $6 {
Possibly the fatal mistake. White wins an important Pawn at the cost of
deserting the KS and allowing Black what turns out to be a decisive attack.
Note that the Queen never gets back to the KS.} Rf6 30. e4 {The threat was 30..
....g4} f4 31. Bd3 {White's only chance is action on the QS.} h5 32. Kf2 g4 33.
hxg4 hxg4 34. Bg1 gxf3 35. gxf3 Qh3 36. Rb1 {To give the King more escape room.
} Bh5 37. Red1 ({If} 37. Be2 Qg3+ 38. Kf1 Rg6) 37... Bxf3 38. Rdc1 Qg3+ 39. Kf1
Bg2+ 40. Ke2 f3+ 41. Kd2 f2 42. Qxb7 Rf3 $1 43. Be2 Qf4+ 44. Kc2 {A very good
KS attack. A good game.} 0-1

