1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O d6 6. c3 Bg4 7. d4 b5 8. Bb3
Be7 {For the second time this season I play an inferior variation against the
Ruy Lopez and get away with it.} 9. Be3 O-O 10. Nbd2 Kh8 11. Qb1 Nh5 $2 {
Much too rash! Black's position is quite tenable but not good enough for KS
excursions.} 12. Bd5 {Apparently winning the e-Pawn.} exd4 $1 {By far the best
chance otherwise I'm left a Pawn down with a poor position.} 13. cxd4 $1 {
Refusing the offer.......} ({........if} 13. Bxc6 dxe3 14. Bxa8 exd2 15. Bd5
Bxf3 16. gxf3 Bg5 {and a strong attack to follow.}) 13... Qe8 14. Rc1 Bd7 15.
Bxc6 Bxc6 16. d5 Bd7 17. Rxc7 {White has won a pawn but Black's pieces 
(surprisingly) are well placed for counterplay.} f5 {Opening lines.} 18. e5 {
The position becomes very involved now.} f4 19. Bd4 {Clearly best.} Bf5 20. Qe1
({The alternative was} 20. Qd1 {"eyeing" the Knight.}) 20... Qd8 21. Rac1 dxe5
22. Bxe5 ({White considered} 22. Qxe5 {but Black replies} Bd6 $1 {and g7 is
strong enough.}) 22... Re8 23. Ne4 ({If} 23. Nd4 Bd6) 23... Qxd5 24. Nc3 Qe6 {
I preffered this to.....} ({.......} 24... Qd8 {as 24.......Qe6 maintained the
tension.}) 25. Nd4 Qg6 ({Not} 25... Qf7 26. Bd6) 26. Nxf5 Bf6 $1 ({If} 26...
Qxf5 27. Bxg7+) 27. Nd6 {Apparently wining but Black isn't finished yet.} Bxe5
(27... Rxe5 28. Nf7+ {28.........Resigns}) 28. Nf7+ Kg8 29. Nxe5 Qd6 {The long
standing Rook-Queen pin regains Black his piece.} 30. Qe4 {More complications.}
Rad8 ({If} 30... Qxc7 $2 31. Qd5+) 31. Qd5+ Qxd5 32. Nxd5 Rxd5 ({If} 32... Rxe5
$4 33. Ne7+ Kf8 34. Nc6) 33. Nf3 Red8 34. Kf1 Nf6 35. Rc8 {4 An interesting
game full of combinative points right up to the end. The match ended 4 -}
1/2-1/2

