1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. exd5 exd5 5. Bb5+ Nc6 6. Qe2+ Be6 7. dxc5 Bxc5
8. Nb3 Bb6 9. Nf3 Nge7 ({I'd have preffered} 9... Nf6 {but didn't like} 10. Ng5
({or} 10. Bg5)) 10. O-O O-O 11. Bxc6 bxc6 12. Bg5 Qd7 {Now White gets a pawn
but loses all his innitiative and Black gets ample compensation.} 13. Ne5 Qc7
14. Bxe7 Qxe7 15. Nxc6 Qb7 16. Ne5 ({I had expected.} 16. Ncd4) 16... Bf5 17.
Qd2 Rfe8 18. Nf3 Be4 {Now Black gets a strong KS attack.} 19. Ne1 ({Again I
expected.} 19. Nfd4) 19... Re6 20. c3 {White decides to fortify d4} Rb8 $1 21.
Nd4 {White decides to equalise by giving back the b-Pawn. However Black's
advantage is retained after the exchange of Queens.} Bxd4 22. cxd4 (22. Qxd4
$142) 22... Qxb2 23. Qxb2 Rxb2 24. f3 {White offered a draw here thinking all
was over.} Bb1 $1 {A nasty shock for White who could now resign.} 25. f4 Ree2
26. a4 Be4 27. Rc1 {Threatening mate.} h6 28. Nf3 Rxg2+ 0-1

