1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Bg5 h6 7. Be3 Bb4 8.
Bd3 Qa5 9. Qd2 Bxc3 10. bxc3 Ng4 11. Nb3 Qc7 12. Bf4 Nge5 13. O-O d6 14. Be3
Ng4 15. f4 Nxe3 16. Qxe3 Qb6 $6 {Black seeks equality by exchanging. However,
White is much better developed, has KS attacking chances and Black's d-Pawn is
weak. Hence Black gets a very difficult game.} 17. Rae1 Qxe3+ 18. Rxe3 O-O 19.
f5 {Opening up the position for the White pieces.} Ne5 20. Be2 b6 21. Nd4 exf5
22. exf5 Bb7 23. Nb5 Rfd8 24. Rf4 f6 {Attempting to solidify his set-up but
giving the Knight a good square.} 25. Nc7 Rac8 26. Ne6 Rd7 27. Rd4 a6 28. Rg3
Rb8 29. c4 {Further restricting Black.} Bc6 30. Rh4 Kh8 31. Rb3 Ba4 {Black was
short of time here. This Bishop proves to be badly placed against c5.} 32. Rb2
Rdb7 {Missing c5} 33. c5 b5 34. cxd6 Rd7 $4 {A time rush blunder but Black was
completely lost.} 35. Rxa4 Rxd6 36. c4 Rdb6 1-0

