1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. c4 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bg4 5. Be2 Nc6 6. d3 e6 7. Be3 Be7 8. Nd2
Bxe2 9. Qxe2 O-O 10. O-O a6 11. Nb3 Qb6 12. f4 Nd7 13. g4 Nd4 {White plans an
all-out KS attack . Black intends to contain this attack and counterattack on
the QS.} 14. Bxd4 cxd4 15. Nd1 Nc5 16. Nd2 e5 17. f5 a5 18. Nf3 f6 19. h4 Qd8
20. h5 {Pretty well the end of his attack.} Rf7 21. Nh4 {Intending 22.Ng6} Qb8
22. Rf3 b5 23. b3 h6 24. Qc2 b4 {Black now has all the innitiative.} 25. Nf2
Bd8 26. Nh3 {Waste of time.} a4 {The decisive breakthrough} 27. Rff1 Rfa7 28.
bxa4 {There's little else.} Rxa4 29. Nf2 b3 30. Qb2 Rxa2 31. Rxa2 Rxa2 32. Qb1
Na4 33. Nd1 Nc3 34. Qc1 {=Resigns} Ne2+ {A good game. [Dick joined the Physics
department at Lancaster University on September 1st 1968]} 0-1

