1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. d5 {Rather
unusual but probably unfamiliar to my opponent, who may possibly have known
all the more usual lines.} Na7 8. Qe2 f5 9. Bb3 d6 10. c4 {oping to open up
the posuition somewhat} Be7 11. Bc2 Nf6 12. Be3 {Threatening the b-Pawn.} bxc4
(12... Bd7 $142) 13. Qxc4 O-O $2 {Overlooking my reply.} 14. Nxe5 dxe5 (14...
Kh8 $142) 15. d6+ Rf7 ({If} 15... Kh8 16. dxe7 Qxe7 17. Bc5) 16. dxe7 Qxe7 17.
Bb3 Bb7 18. Qxf7+ Qxf7 19. Bxf7+ Kxf7 20. Bxa7 Rxa7 21. Nc3 Nd5 22. Rfd1 Nxc3
23. bxc3 Ke6 24. c4 Be4 {To provoke 25.f3 for what it's worth.} 25. f3 Bc6 26.
Rab1 e4 27. f4 Ra8 28. Kf2 h6 29. Ke3 g5 30. g3 Rg8 31. Rd2 a5 32. Rbd1 h5 33.
Rd8 gxf4+ 34. gxf4 Rg2 35. R1d2 Rg1 36. Rh8 Ba4 37. Rh6+ Ke7 38. Rxh5 Bd1 39.
Rxf5 Re1+ 40. Kd4 Bf3 (40... Bf3 41. Rxa5 {After hangig on for so long Black
could have tried} Kf6 42. Re5 c5+ 43. Kxc5 e3 {although} 44. Rd3 {is decisive.}
) 41. Rxa5 1-0

