1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Bd2 c5 5. dxc5 Bxc5 6. exd5 exd5 {Despite the
isolated Pawn Black's pieces are easily developed and White's QBishop is
poorly placed.} 7. Bb5+ Nc6 8. Nf3 Nf6 9. Qe2+ {This serves little purpose.}
Be6 10. Rd1 {[30'] White begins to get very cramped in the centre.} O-O {[12']}
11. O-O Bg4 {Whites position is cramped with ......Re8, ......Nd4 and such
like in the offing.} 12. Bxc6 {Relieving me of my isolated Pawn.} bxc6 13. Qd3
{The Queen will run short of squares.} Qc8 $1 {A useful move.} 14. Rde1 {
I feel there must be better than this for White. Control of the e-file is not
crucial.} Bf5 15. Qe2 {After 20' thought.} Bxc2 16. Be3 ({I expected} 16. Bg5 {
which is harder for me.}) 16... Bxe3 17. Qxc2 Bf4 {The best file for the
Bishop.} 18. Ne2 Bd6 19. Rc1 c5 20. Qd2 Qa6 21. b3 Rfe8 22. Rc2 d4 {Forcing
the Knight to move.} 23. Ng3 Ne4 24. Nxe4 Rxe4 25. Rc4 Rae8 26. Ra4 Qb6 27. Qa5
Qxa5 28. Rxa5 R8e7 29. Nd2 {Threatening 30.Nc4 winning the c-Pawn. Black can
gain a move by 29......Rh4 or by........} Re1 $1 30. g3 ({Now if} 30. Nc4 Bxh2+
$1) 30... Rxf1+ 31. Kxf1 f6 32. Nc4 d3 33. Ne3 (33. Ra6 Be5) 33... Kf7 34. Ke1
c4 {Threatening 35......Bb4+} 35. Rd5 cxb3 36. axb3 ({Not} 36. Rxd6 $4 b2)
36... Bb4+ 37. Kd1 d2 38. Rd3 {White only had a few seconds now.} a5 39. h3 g5
40. h4 (40. h4 gxh4 {White loses a second Pawn.} 41. gxh4 Re4 42. h5 {The
Knight is immobile.} Rh4 {etc.}) 40... gxh4 {Lancaster won the match 4 - 2.
This was the first match Lancaster had ever won in the Lancashire league.} 0-1

