1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qb3 c5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. e3 O-O 7. Bd3 d5 {
I didn't know this line very well so I decided to simplify, with unhappy
consequences.} 8. cxd5 exd5 9. dxc5 Be6 10. Nd4 Bxc5 {Black has the
innitiative.} 11. Nxc6 bxc6 12. Qc2 Bd6 13. e4 {A 'Do or Die' sort of move.}
Nxe4 ({I expected.} 13... d4) 14. Nxe4 dxe4 15. Bxe4 f5 {[60']} 16. Bf3 {
[30'] My exposed King is a problem.} Qa5+ 17. Bd2 Qe5+ 18. Be2 Bd5 {Black has
a powerful position but was very short of time.} 19. Bc3 Qe6 {Not really
threatening the a-Pawn.} 20. O-O $6 {What else?} Rae8 (20... Bxa2 $4 21. Rxa2
Qxa2 22. Bd2 Kh8 23. Bc4) 21. Rfe1 Qh6 22. h3 Qg5 23. g3 $4 ({The game may be
beyond saving but} 23. Bf1 {gives some hope.}) 23... Bxg3 $1 {The end!! The
only move now is "Resigns". However Black was very short of time (~2' to reach
move 36.)} 24. Bg4 Bf4 $4 {In the rush he throws away the win.} (24... Rxe1+ {
was correct.}) 25. Rxe8 Rxe8 26. Qxf5 Qxf5 27. Bxf5 g6 {A lucky escape.}
1/2-1/2

