1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 e6 4. Nc3 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. e4 g6 7. f4 Nbd7 ({
This is the beginning of his trouble. If} 7... Bg7 8. Bb5+ Nbd7 {is quite
playable for Black.}) 8. g4 {Setting Black problems.} ({I also considered.} 8.
Qa4 {which is strong.}) 8... h5 {After much thought. He had no good moves.} 9.
g5 Nh7 10. Bd3 a6 11. a4 Bg7 12. Nf3 O-O 13. O-O Re8 14. h4 {White has plenty
of time to solidify his position.} b6 15. f5 Be5 {Else the Bishop gets trapped.
} 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. Bf4 Ra7 18. Bxe5 Rxe5 19. Qd2 Rae7 20. Rf4 Qc7 ({Rather
better is} 20... Qe8 21. Z0 {and} gxf5) 21. b3 Re8 22. Raf1 R8e7 23. Qf2 gxf5
$2 {Short of time this loses although Black was very badly placed.} 24. exf5
Re3 25. Rf3 R3e5 26. f6 Re8 27. g6 Nf8 28. Qd2 $1 Qd7 29. Bf5 Rxf5 30. Rxf5 {
A good attack. Dingwall is a high board player for Gloucester.} 1-0

