{Time limit: 35 moves in 1hr 45'} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. exd5 exd5 5.
Ngf3 Nf6 6. Bb5+ Nc6 7. O-O Be7 8. dxc5 Bxc5 9. Nb3 Be7 10. Ne5 Bd7 11. Bxc6
bxc6 12. Nd4 Rc8 13. Nxd7 Qxd7 {There seemed no reason for White to give up
his good Knight for my poor Bishop.} 14. Qf3 Ne4 {Gaining space and equality.}
15. Nf5 Bf6 16. c3 O-O 17. Be3 ({If} 17. Qg4 Kh8) 17... Rb8 {Awkward for White}
18. Rad1 Rfe8 19. Bc1 Re5 {Black now has some innitiative.} 20. Nd4 Bg5 {
After much though.} (20... c5 {Was an alternative}) 21. Bxg5 Nxg5 22. Qh5 ({If
} 22. Qg3 Rbe8 23. f4 Ne4 {etc}) 22... g6 23. Qh4 Ne4 24. f3 Nd6 25. Qf6 Rbe8
26. f4 R5e7 27. f5 {Black's position is quite sound and after White's attack
is over will control the e-file.} c5 28. Nb3 {We were both in a time scramble
now.} Nxf5 29. Nxc5 Qc8 30. b4 $1 {About the only move.} Ne3 {I could fid
nothing better in the rush.} 31. Rde1 Qc7 32. Na6 Qb7 33. Nc5 {He offered a
draw here but I didn't have time to accept.} Qc7 34. Na6 Qb6 35. Qxb6 (35. Qxb6
axb6 36. Rf6 {[Sealed] Black plays} Ng4 $1) 35... axb6 {He sealed [35.Rf6]
here but we agreed a draw.} 1/2-1/2

