1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 Bg7 5. e3 e6 6. Nb5 Na6 7. h3 Bf8 {Black
was obviously unhappy.} 8. a3 c6 9. Nc3 Bg7 10. c5 O-O {Else 11.Bd6} 11. Bxa6
bxa6 12. Qa4 {[7']} Bb7 13. Nf3 Re8 14. g4 Nd7 15. Ne5 Bxe5 16. Bxe5 Nxe5 17.
dxe5 Qg5 18. f4 Qh4+ 19. Ke2 {[15'] This was a short match and the game was
played at some speed.} Qe7 20. Qd4 a5 21. g5 {Intending to manoeuvre the
Knight to f6.} Ba6+ 22. Kf3 Reb8 23. b4 axb4 24. axb4 Bc4 25. Rhb1 Rb7 26. Nd1
{Still with thoughts of f6.} Rab8 27. Qc3 Qc7 28. Qa3 a5 $2 {The fatal mistake
and just the move I wanted. Black loses at least a Pawn. White gets a Rook on
the 8th and the Knight on f6.} 29. Qxa5 Qxa5 30. Rxa5 Rxb4 31. Rxb4 Rxb4 32.
Ra8+ Kg7 33. Rc8 Bb5 34. Nf2 {Now Black is completely lost.} h5 ({Now he is
mated but if} 34... Rb2 35. Ng4 Be2+ {he loses the c-Pawn and eventually the
game.}) 35. gxh6+ Kxh6 36. Ng4+ Kg7 37. Nf6 Rc4 ({Now he is mated in 8 at the
worst. If} 37... Rb1 38. Kg4 Rg1+ 39. Kh4 Z0 {.......followed by....} 40. Rg8+
Kh6 41. Ne8 g5+ 42. fxg5+ Rxg5 (42... Kh7 43. Nf6#) 43. Rxg5 {etc.}) 38. Kg4 {
[37']} Rc1 39. Rg8+ Kh6 40. Rh8+ Kg7 41. Rh7+ Kf8 42. Kg5 {Lancaster won the
Jamboree (7 teams)} 1-0

