1. d4 f5 2. e4 fxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 c6 {When I last played against the
Staunton Gambit (7 years ago) I played.......} ({........} 4... Nc6) 5. Bxf6
exf6 6. Nxe4 d5 7. Ng3 Bd6 8. Bd3 g6 ({If} 8... O-O 9. Qh5) ({Or} 8... Qc7 9.
Qh5+) 9. Qd2 Qc7 {Prevents 10.O-O-O} 10. N1e2 Be6 11. O-O-O Nd7 12. f4 f5 13.
Rde1 O-O-O 14. Rhf1 Rhe8 15. Kb1 Nf6 16. Qc1 c5 {I have to get this in before
White does.} 17. c4 Kb8 18. Nc3 $2 {Loses a Pawn for little compensation.
White thought that 19. Nb5 was stronger than it was.} cxd4 19. Nb5 Qc5 ({If} 
19... Qb6 20. Nxd6 Qxd6 (20... Rxd6 21. c5) 21. c5) 20. Nxd6 Rxd6 21. cxd5 $2 {
Loses another Pawn.} Qxd5 22. b3 Qxg2 23. Re2 Qc6 24. Qxc6 bxc6 ({Not} 24...
Rxc6 25. Bb5) 25. Rfe1 Nd5 26. Re5 Nxf4 27. Bc4 Kc8 28. Ne2 Ng2 29. Rg1 ({
I'd expected} 29. Rd1 Ne3 30. Rxd4 Nxc4) 29... Ne3 30. Bxe6+ Rexe6 31. Rxe6
Rxe6 32. Nxd4 Rd6 33. Re1 Ng4 34. Nf3 Rd3 35. Ng5 h6 36. Nf7 Nxh2 37. Re8+ Kc7
38. Nxh6 f4 39. Re7+ Kb6 40. Re2 Rh3 41. Nf7 f3 42. Rf2 Ng4 43. Rf1 f2 44. Ng5
Re3 0-1

