1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 cxd4 6. axb4 dxc3 7. Qg4 Ne7 8.
Qxg7 Rg8 9. Qxh7 Qc7 10. f4 {All this is very precarious. I remember playing a
similar game v G.K. Sandiford [19/5/62] in which White simplified down and his
h-Pawn became a real problem.} Nbc6 11. bxc3 ({Possibly safest was} 11. Nf3
cxb2 12. Bxb2 Nxb4 13. Bd3) 11... Nxe5 12. fxe5 $6 {White makes a death or
glory fight of it. White is relying on his superiority on the KS.} ({I expected
} 12. Bd2 N5c6 {etc}) 12... Qxc3+ 13. Kf2 Qxa1 14. Nf3 {Now Bishop or Knight
to g5 is unstopable. I decided to get the King to safety, give up the f-Pawn
and make use of the exposed position of the White King.} Bd7 15. Bg5 Rxg5 $1
16. Nxg5 Qd4+ 17. Kf3 O-O-O 18. Qxf7 ({A forelorn hope was offered by} 18. Bd3
Qxe5 19. Nxf7 Rf8 ({Not} 19... Qf6+ 20. Ke2 Rf8 21. Rf1) 20. Rf1 Be8 {etc.})
18... Nf5 {Threatening 19......Qe6+ 20.Kg4 Nh6+} ({I also considered} 18... Nc6
{but it's not very clear after} 19. Qf4) 0-1

