1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 c6 5. f3 Nh5 {A bit doubtful} 6. Bxb8 Rxb8
7. cxd5 e6 {White could win the a-Pawn anyway and Black prefers this method.}
8. dxe6 Bxe6 9. g3 {Else 9......Qh4+} Qb6 10. Qd2 Rd8 11. e3 Bg7 12. Na4 {
Probably straightforward development was better.} Qc7 13. Nc5 O-O 14. g4 Nf6
15. Nxe6 $2 {Doubtful. Opening lines.} fxe6 16. Bc4 Nd5 17. f4 {I briefly
considered his reply but gave it little attention.} Nxe3 $1 18. Qxe3 Bxd4 19.
Qe2 {Keeping the e-file shut.} ({Not} 19. Qb3 Rxf4 20. Ne2 $2 Bf2+) 19... Qa5+
20. Kf1 Rxf4+ 21. Nf3 Rxf3+ (21... Rdf8 {was the alternative.}) 22. Qxf3 Rf8
23. Bxe6+ Kg7 24. Bf5 $2 {Loses but it wasn't obvious.} (24. Qxf8+ {Had to be
played.}) 24... gxf5 25. g5 {Everything loses.} Re8 26. Rd1 {There is no move.}
({If} 26. Qd3 Qd5) 26... Re3 27. Qf2 ({If} 27. Qh5 Qd5) 27... Qb5+ 28. Kg2 Qd5+
(28... Re2 $4 29. Rxd4 $1) 29. Kg1 Rd3 {A good game by Black.} 0-1

