1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 c6 5. Bg2 Nbd7 6. Nf3 Bb4 {This doesn't
turn out well} 7. O-O b6 {Again a bit doubtful. Black played the whole game in
very pessimistic fashion as if he thought that it was just a matter of time
before he lost.} 8. cxd5 cxd5 $2 {leads to endless trouble.} 9. Nb5 {Things
are suddenly difficult for Black.} O-O $2 ({Possibly best is} 9... Ba6 10. Qa4
Bxb5) 10. Bf4 Bb7 {Loses the exchange but he was in dire straights anyway.} 11.
Qb3 Be7 12. Bc7 Qe8 ({If} 12... Qc8 13. Rac1 {is terible for Black.}) 13. Nd6
Bxd6 14. Bxd6 h6 15. Rfc1 Rc8 16. Bxf8 Qxf8 17. Rc2 Ne4 18. Rac1 a6 19. Rxc8
Bxc8 20. Qc2 Nd6 {Black could resign.} 21. Nd2 Qd8 22. e4 e5 23. dxe5 Nxe5 24.
f4 Ng4 25. Qc7 Qf8 26. e5 Ne8 (26... Nc4 {is hardly any better.}) 27. Qxc8 Qb4
28. Qxe8+ Kh7 29. Nb3 a5 30. Qxf7 1-0

