1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 d5 5. Qa4+ Nc6 6. cxd5 {I prefer this to 6.
a3 given by Pachman in 'Indian Systems'} Nxd5 7. Bd2 O-O 8. Nf3 Nxc3 9. bxc3
Be7 10. Ba6 $1 {Results in a lasting innitiative for White at the cost of a
Pawn.} Nxd4 {About the only move.} 11. cxd4 ({Not} 11. Bxb7 Nc2+ 12. Qxc2 Bxb7)
11... bxa6 12. Ba5 Bd7 13. Qc2 Bd6 ({I had expected} 13... Bb5 {to which I
would probably have replied} 14. Kd2) 14. O-O Rc8 15. a4 {Preventing 15......
Bb5} Qe7 ({If} 15... Qe8 16. Ng5 {and unless} f5 {Ne4}) 16. Qd3 {Regaining at
least one Pawn.} Bc6 $6 {It is difficult to find a move for Black. This is O.K.
if correctly followed up.} 17. e4 ({If} 17. Qxa6 {Black draws with} Bxf3 18.
gxf3 Bxh2+) ({Or} 17. Nd2 $4 Qg5 {Wins a piece.}) 17... Bb7 $4 {An oversight
which loses outright.} ({About best was} 17... Bb4 {but White may still have a
fairly straightforward win.}) 18. e5 Bb4 19. Bxb4 Qxb4 20. Rfb1 1-0

