{Time limit 90 mins each for all moves.} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 3. Nxe5 Qf6 4. d4
d6 5. Nf3 (5. Nc4 fxe4 6. d5 {is an alternative.}) 5... fxe4 6. Qe2 d5 7. Nc3
Bb4 8. Bd2 Ne7 9. Ne5 ({After the game White said he had considered.} 9. Qb5+ {
and if} Nbc6 ({However} 9... c6 $1 {leaves Black on top. After the text move
he will have trouble saving his d-Pawn.}) 10. Nxd5 $1) 9... Bd6 10. Qh5+ (10.
f4 $6) 10... g6 11. Bg5 $2 {Leads to a loss.} (11. Qg5 {was best probably
losing a Pawn.}) 11... Qe6 12. Qh4 $2 (12. Qe2 {better or 12.Qd1 but Black
would still be right on top.}) 12... Nf5 13. Qg4 Nxd4 14. Qxe6+ Bxe6 15. Bf6
O-O 16. Ng4 {Threatening mate.} Nxc2+ 17. Kd2 Bxg4 18. Bh4 Nxa1 19. Nxd5 g5 20.
Bxg5 Rxf2+ 21. Ke3 {Putting a quick end to it.} Bc5+ 22. Kxe4 Bf5+ 23. Ke5 Nd7#
{A neat win. The Greco is a good opening in this type of (3hr) match,
especially when the oppoent isn't familiar with it.} 0-1

