1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 e5 $5 7. fxe5 dxe5 8.
d5 ({Not} 8. Nxe5 $2 c5 9. d5 Nxe4) ({Or} 8. dxe5 $2 Qxd1+ 9. Kxd1 Ng4 10. Nd5
Na6) 8... Nbd7 (8... c5 $142 {(Pachman)}) 9. b4 ({Alekhine-Ed Lasker NY 1924
went} 9. Bd3 Nc5 10. Bc2) 9... a6 10. Bd3 Ng4 {Black decides his chances lay
on the kS.} 11. h3 Nh6 12. Bg5 {Probably not best as it helps Black's KS play.}
f6 13. Bh4 g5 14. Bf2 f5 15. Qc2 f4 16. O-O-O Qe7 17. Qb3 a5 {Doubtful. Black
must make rapid progress on the KS before White does on the QS.} 18. c5 Nf7 {
Else 19.d6+} 19. a3 axb4 20. axb4 Kh8 ({If} 20... Ra1+ 21. Bb1 Z0 {threatens.}
22. Na2) 21. Kb2 b6 {Again Black is playing on the wrong side of the board.}
22. c6 Nf6 23. Ra1 Rxa1 24. Rxa1 Ne8 {It's too late on the KS now.} 25. Ra7 {
Threat 26.Bxb6} Qf6 26. Nb5 g4 {Desperation.} 27. hxg4 Bxg4 28. Nxc7 Nxc7 29.
Rxc7 Rb8 30. Qa3 Nd6 31. Qa7 Qf8 {Loses outright but there was no hope.} 32.
Rxg7 Ra8 33. Rxh7+ Kg8 34. Qe7 Qxe7 35. Rxe7 Bxf3 36. gxf3 b5 37. Rxe5 Kf7 38.
Bc5 Nc4+ 39. Bxc4 bxc4 40. c7 Rc8 41. Rf5+ Ke8 42. Rf8+ Kd7 43. Rxc8 Kxc8 44.
d6 Kd7 45. e5 c3+ 46. Kxc3 Ke6 47. c8=Q+ Kd5 48. d7 Kxe5 49. Qe8+ ({Not} 49.
d8=Q {Stalemate}) 49... Kf5 50. Qe4+ ({Not} 50. d8=Q {Stalemate}) 50... Kf6 51.
d8=Q+ 1-0

[Event "Lancaster, Morecambe & District K.O."]
