1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 dxc4 4. a4 e6 {I couldn't remember much about the
Slav Defence. Also having beaten S.S. twice this season I was playing without
undue effort.} 5. Nf3 Bb4 6. e4 b5 7. Bd2 Nf6 8. axb5 Bxc3 ({If} 8... cxb5 9.
Bxc4 $1) 9. Bxc3 Nxe4 ({Black was also playing very quickly.} 9... cxb5 {
seems to win a Pawn although White has some compensation.}) 10. Bxc4 Nxc3 11.
bxc3 Bb7 12. O-O Nd7 13. Qe2 {Intending to pressurise his a-Pawn.} ({I also
considered} 13. Qb3 {and if} O-O 14. Bxe6) 13... O-O 14. Ra3 ({Not} 14. Bxe6 $2
Re8) 14... Nb6 15. Bd3 Nd5 16. g3 cxb5 17. Bxb5 Qf6 18. Ne5 Qe7 19. Rfa1 a5 20.
c4 Nc7 21. Rxa5 $2 {Played without much thought. I was expecting to win
without any effort.} (21. Bc6 $142) 21... Rxa5 22. Rxa5 Qb4 {I'd missed this.}
23. Ra1 {Giving back the Pawn.} (23. Ra7 Qb1+ 24. Qf1 Qe4 $1) 23... Nxb5 24.
cxb5 Qxd4 25. Rc1 Qd5 26. Nc6 Qg5 27. Qe3 $2 {Rubbish. Completely overlooking
the b-Pawn.} Qxe3 $2 {Black either doesn't see it or doesn't want it.} ({On} 
27... Qxb5 {I intended.} 28. Qc5 Z0 {Threatening} 29. Ne7+) 28. fxe3 Ra8 29.
Nd4 Kf8 30. Rc7 Bd5 31. b6 Ra1+ 32. Kf2 Rb1 33. Nc6 {Threatening mate.} Rb2+
34. Ke1 Bxc6 35. Rxc6 g6 36. Kd1 Ke7 37. Kc1 $2 Rb5 38. Kc2 $2 {I was getting
nowhere fast here.} (38. Rc7+ $142 Kd6 39. Rxf7 {etc.}) 38... h5 39. Rc7+ Kd6
40. Rxf7 Rxb6 41. Rg7 Ke5 42. Rxg6 Ke4 43. Rh6 Kxe3 $2 (43... Rd6 $142 {
Cutting off my King.}) 44. Rxh5 Kf3 $2 (44... Rd6 $142) 45. Rg5 $2 Rb4 $2 (
45... Rd6 $142) 46. h4 Re4 47. h5 Re2+ 48. Kd3 Rh2 49. Kd4 Re2 50. h6 e5+ 51.
Rxe5 Rh2 52. Re6 Kxg3 53. Ke5 Kg4 54. Rg6+ Kh5 55. Kf6 Ra2 56. h7 Ra6+ 57. Ke5
Kxg6 58. h8=Q {Black ow expressed his intentio of hanging on for 60 moves for
a draw.} Ra5+ 59. Kd4 Kf7 60. Qh7+ {A Queen v Rook is won not by checkmating
but by separating King and Rook winning the Rook. A stalemate only occurs in
certain positions on the edge of the board. Still playing without bothering
unduly I proceeded to force Black where he wanted to go!} Ke6 61. Qg8+ $2 ({
Correct} 61. Qe4+ {followed by trying to get the Queen on to the b-file.})
61... Kd7 62. Qf7+ Kc6 63. Qe6+ Kb7 64. Qd7+ Ka6 65. Kc4 Kb6 66. Kb4 Ra7 67.
Qd6+ Kb7 68. Kb5 Kc8 69. Qf8+ Kb7 $4 (69... Kc7 {Seems to draw.}) 70. Qd8 Ra8
71. Qd7+ Kb8 72. Kb6 {A terrible game, full of mistakes. I made no effort at
all expecting to win easily throughout.} 1-0

