1. d4 e6 2. c4 h6 $6 3. e4 Bb4+ 4. Bd2 Bxd2+ 5. Qxd2 Ne7 6. Bd3 d5 7. cxd5 exd5
8. e5 a6 {Black is playing hopelessly passively. White was playing at great
speed in order to get the game finished quickly.} 9. Nc3 Nbc6 ({Black should
be aiming for.} 9... c5) 10. Nge2 Bf5 11. Bxf5 Nxf5 12. O-O ({If} 12. g4 Nh4 {
is troublesome.}) 12... Nce7 $2 {Cutting off the other Knight's retreat.} 13.
g4 Nh4 {Just about the end of the game for this piece.} 14. f4 Qd7 15. f5 g6
16. Qe1 g5 17. Ng3 {Preventing 17......h5} O-O-O 18. Rc1 c6 19. Na4 {Black has
weaknesses everywhere.} Kb8 20. Nc5 Qc7 21. e6 Ka7 22. exf7 Nc8 {Giving up the
exchange. White intended Ne6 and Pe8} 23. Ne6 Qxf7 24. Nxd8 Rxd8 25. Qe6 Qf8
26. Qe1 ({If} 26. Rce1 Qb4 {Hence the text move.}) 26... Nb6 27. b3 Nd7 28. Qc3
Nf6 29. Qc5+ Qxc5 30. Rxc5 Re8 ({If} 30... Nxg4 31. f6) 31. Rcc1 Rf8 32. Rce1
Kb6 ({If} 32... Nxg4 33. Re6 Nf6 {seems better for Black.}) 33. h3 Rf7 34. Re6
Kc7 35. Kf2 Ng8 36. Rfe1 Kd7 37. Nh5 Kc7 38. Re8 Nf6 39. Nxf6 Rxf6 40. R1e7+
Kb6 ({If} 40... Kd6 41. Rxb7 {Threatens mate.}) 41. Rb8 Ng6 42. Rbxb7+ Ka5 43.
Re6 1-0

[Event "Lancaster Club Championship"]
