{Time control 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 3. Nxe5 Qf6 4. d4 d6 5.
Nc4 {This seems better than 5.Nf3 as in the game v J.G.Lomax [L&M Lge
Lancaster v Post Office 17/2/71]} fxe4 6. Nc3 Qf7 $2 {I was tired out (from
playing Squash) in this game and played listlessly} (6... Bf5 $142) 7. Be2 ({
There seems no apparent reason for ot playing.} 7. Nxe4) 7... Nf6 8. d5 c6 {
Giving up a Pawn for freedom and more control of the centre.} 9. dxc6 {[22']}
d5 {[6']} 10. Ne5 Qe6 11. cxb7 Bxb7 12. Bb5+ Nc6 {[8']} 13. Qd4 Be7 14. Nxc6 {
[45']} Bxc6 {[10']} 15. Bg5 h6 ({If now} 15... O-O 16. Bxc6 Qxc6 17. Bxf6 Bxf6
18. Qxd5+) 16. Bh4 {[49']} g5 17. Bg3 O-O 18. O-O Bxb5 19. Nxb5 Qc6 20. Nc3 Bc5
21. Qa4 {[58'] White was short of time.} Qe6 {[25']} 22. Ne2 h5 23. Nd4 Qb6 24.
Nb3 h4 25. Nxc5 $2 ({Short of time White goes wrong} 25. Be5 {was better})
25... hxg3 26. Qd4 ({If say} 26. Nb3 gxh2+ 27. Kxh2 (27. Kh1) 27... Ng4+ 28.
Kg1 (28. Kg3 Qd6+ 29. Kxg4 Qf4+) 28... Qh6) 26... gxh2+ 27. Kxh2 Qd6+ 28. g3
Rac8 29. b4 Rc7 30. Kg2 Re7 {To defend the e-Pawn so the Knight can move.} 31.
Rh1 Kg7 32. Rh2 Qe5 {Forcing Queens off at the best moment.} 33. Qxe5 Rxe5 34.
Rah1 $2 {Leaving f2 too weak.} Ng4 35. Rh7+ Kg6 36. Rh8 Rxf2+ 37. Kg1 Ref5 38.
Rg8+ Kf7 39. Rhh8 Rf1+ 40. Kg2 Ne3+ {It's mate in 4. Not a bad game after a
doubtful start.} 0-1

