1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 {A good opening against this opponent who plays rather
timidly.} 3. d3 Nc6 4. exf5 {Hardly in keeping with his previous move.} d5 5.
Bg5 Qd6 6. Qd2 Bxf5 7. Be2 h6 8. Bh4 g5 9. Bg3 Qf6 {Tolet out the Bishop and
'eye' the b-pawn. Also with thoughts of a KS attack.} 10. Qe3 O-O-O ({After
some thought. If.....} 10... Bd6 11. d4) ({Or...} 10... d4 11. Nxd4) 11. Bxe5
Nxe5 12. Qxe5 ({If} 12. Nxe5 d4) 12... Qf7 {Better than 12......QxQ} (12...
Qxe5 13. Nxe5 Bg7 14. d4 Bxc2) 13. Qe3 ({If now} 13. Qxh8 Bg7 14. Nxg5 $1 hxg5
15. Qh5 Qxh5 16. Bxh5 Bxb2 $19) 13... Bg7 14. c3 Re8 15. Qd2 ({Not} 15. Qxa7
Bxd3) 15... Nf6 16. O-O Nh5 17. Re1 Nf4 18. d4 Be4 {White is hopelessly
cramped.} 19. Bf1 Nh3+ $3 {With only a few mins each for the 20th move.} 20.
gxh3 ({The alternative was} 20. Kh1 g4 {and wins}) 20... Qxf3 21. Rxe4 dxe4 22.
Qe2 {There seeems to be no reason for White to want the Queens off.} Rhf8 23.
Nd2 Qxe2 24. Bxe2 e3 25. Bg4+ Kd8 26. fxe3 Rxe3 27. Rf1 Rxf1+ 28. Kxf1 h5 29.
Kf2 $2 {Making it much easier for Black. White loses Bishop & Knight for Rook.}
Rd3 30. Ke2 Rxd2+ {The rest is superfluous.} 31. Kxd2 hxg4 32. hxg4 Kd7 33. h3
Kd6 34. Kd3 b5 35. b3 c5 36. dxc5+ Kxc5 37. a3 a5 38. b4+ axb4 39. axb4+ Kd5
40. Kc2 Kc4 41. Kd2 {A bright start to my defence of the Club Championship.}
0-1

[Event "Lancaster Club Championship"]
