1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. f4 d6 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. c3 e6 {I had played R.E.D. a number
of times recently and anihilated him, he was thus very 'under-confident' and
played as if it was just a matter of time (It was).} 6. Bd3 Nf6 7. e5 dxe5 8.
fxe5 Nd5 9. Bg5 Nde7 ({If} 9... f6 10. Bh4 g5 11. Nxg5 {etc.}) 10. Nbd2 Bd7 ({
If} 10... Nxe5 11. Nxe5 Bxe5 12. Bxg6) 11. Ne4 Na5 {Threshing about already.}
12. b4 Nac6 13. Qd2 h6 14. Bh4 Qc8 15. O-O Nf5 16. Bf6 Bxf6 17. Nxf6+ Ke7 18.
g4 a6 $4 {Giving up. Black couldn't explain why he'd played this. He seemed
just completely demoralised.} ({After} 18... Ng7 19. Nh4 {He wouldn't last too
long anyway.}) 19. gxf5 exf5 20. Bc4 Be6 $2 {Putting an even quicker end to it.
} 21. d5 Nxe5 22. Nxe5 Kxf6 23. dxe6 Kxe5 24. Qd4# {R.E.Dixon won section B of
the Club Championship last year.} 1-0

