1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 g6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. e4 d6 6. f4 O-O 7. Nf3 e6 8. Be2 exd5
9. exd5 Na6 10. O-O Nc7 11. h3 a6 12. a4 b6 13. Bd3 Rb8 14. g4 h6 {I can't
prevent ......b5 and therefore decide to move quickly on the KS.} 15. Qc2 b5
16. g5 $6 ({Probably} 16. axb5 {first is better giving the Rook more scope.})
16... bxc4 17. Bxc4 Bxh3 $6 18. gxf6 Bxf6 ({Not} 18... Qxf6 19. Ne4) 19. Re1
Qd7 20. Qh2 {[58'] About best.} Bg7 {[41'] To support the h-Pawn and take the
sting out of Ne4.} ({If} 20... Qg4+ 21. Kf2 Bh4+ 22. Nxh4 Qxh4+ 23. Qg3 {etc.})
21. Ra2 $2 {Leads to trouble. I think this is about the crucial stage. Black
now gets on top and keeps the innitiative till the end. I wasn't happy about
my play here. I intended Ne4 & b3.} Rb4 {Putting a damper on my plans.} 22. Bf1
Bg4 23. Qg2 {So as to subsequently protect d5 & b3 rather than 23.Qg3 which
does not.} Rfb8 24. Be2 g5 {[67']} 25. Nh2 {[99'] After much thought and
getting a bit short of time.} ({If} 25. Ne5 dxe5 26. Bxg4 f5 $19) (25. fxg5 Bh3
$3) 25... Bxe2 26. fxg5 $6 {So as to "save" a Pawn.} hxg5 27. Rxe2 g4 {I'm in
a nasty mess here mainly due to the pressure on b2 and my useless Rook. I was
also short of time.} 28. Bg5 Be5 29. Re4 f5 30. Rxb4 Rxb4 31. Ra1 {[113']} Qg7
32. Qd2 Rd4 {A big rush now.} 33. Qc1 Qh7 34. Qc2 Qh3 35. Qg2 Qxg2+ 36. Kxg2
Nxd5 37. Be3 $4 Rd3 $4 {Time scrambling.} 38. Nxd5 Rxd5 39. Nf1 $2 Bxb2 40. Rb1
(40. Rb1 Bc3 {A possible continuation.} 41. Rb6 a5 42. Bf4 Be5 43. Bxe5 dxe5
44. Rb5 Kf7 45. Rxa5 Kf6 46. Ra8 c4 47. a5 c3 48. Rc8 Rxa5 49. Rxc3 Ra2+ 50.
Kg1 Kg5 51. Rc5 {etc. Black has good winning chances.}) 40... Bc3 {Time called.
Adjudicated Lost. Not at my best, and rather spoiled by the time scramble.} 0-1

