1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 g5 4. h4 g4 5. Ng5 h6 6. Nxf7 Kxf7 {These moves
came "out of the hat". We were handicapped equally so by toss of a coin it was
decided that he should give me the handicap.i.e.he had choice of colour but
had to mate me by move 54. he chose White.} 7. d4 h5 {Doubtful.} (7... Nf6 $142
) 8. Bxf4 d6 9. Nc3 Nc6 10. Bc4+ Ke8 11. g3 Bg7 12. Be3 Nf6 13. a3 Qe7 14. Qd3
Na5 $2 ({I think something like} 14... Bd7 15. Z0 {and} Kd8 16. Z0 Kc8 {
might be best.}) 15. Ba2 a6 16. O-O-O Nc6 $6 {Just asking for it!} 17. e5 {
Naturally.} dxe5 {What else?} 18. Qg6+ Kf8 $3 (18... Kd8 {is suicide. By going
to f8 the King escapes.}) 19. dxe5 Nxe5 {Now White "sees" a straightforward
win. Black had seen slightly further!} ({ot} 19... Qxe5 $4 20. Qf7#) 20. Rd8+
$2 {Apparently murderous.} (20. Qg5 $142) 20... Qxd8 21. Bc5+ Qd6 $1 {Now
White notices that after "winning" my Queen, his Queen can only go to g5 where
it is lost to ......Bh6} 22. Bxd6+ cxd6 23. Qg5 Bh6 24. Rf1 Nf3 25. Kd1 Bxg5
26. hxg5 Nh7 27. g6 Nhg5 28. Ne2 Be6 0-1

