1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 cxd4 6. axb4 dxc3 7. Qg4 Ne7 8.
Qxg7 Rg8 9. Qxh7 cxb2 $6 {A bit doubtful.} ({In the lancashire v Yorkshire
match last year I played....} 9... Qc7) 10. Bxb2 Qb6 $6 {Again doubtful.} 11.
b5 $1 {Of considerable nuisance value.} Nd7 12. f4 Nf8 ({Not fearing} 12...
Qe3+ 13. Ne2 Z0 {when the threat of} 14. Bd4 {is rather embarassing for Black.}
) 13. Qd3 {[10']} Nf5 {The Knight has little future here. Black is in a bad
way.} 14. g3 Bd7 15. Nf3 Qe3+ {Transposing from a rotten middlegame to a
rotten endgame.} 16. Qxe3 Nxe3 17. Bd3 Nc4 $2 {Black might do better to
mobilise some more pieces. He now proceeds to lose another Pawn.} 18. Bd4 b6
19. Bxc4 dxc4 20. Bxb6 Bxb5 21. Rxa7 Rxa7 {[31']} 22. Bxa7 {[18']} Bc6 23. Kf2
Ng6 24. Rb1 Kf8 25. Rb8+ Kg7 26. Rxg8+ Kxg8 27. Nd2 c3 {This Pawn is doomed.}
28. Nc4 {[22']} Be4 29. Ne3 Ne7 30. Ke2 Nd5 31. Nxd5 exd5 32. Kd1 Kg7 33. Bd4
Kg6 34. Bxc3 Kf5 35. Be1 Kg4 36. h4 Kf3 37. Kd2 Kg4 38. c3 Kf3 39. Kd1 Bg6 40.
Kd2 Be4 {Black seems to have made progress but when one is three Pawns down
thre is little hope.} 41. h5 {To draw away the King.} Kg4 42. h6 Kh5 43. Ke3
Kxh6 44. c4 Kg6 ({If} 44... Bh7 45. c5 {etc.}) 45. Kd4 Kf5 46. cxd5 {Reverend
Calvert was assistant Curate of St John’s, Preston, in charge of Christ
Church (1963-70). He died 5 March 2019 aged 91.} 1-0

