{[#] Odds of QKnight.} 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 d6 4. d4 Bg4 5. Bxf4 Nf6 6.
Bc4 d5 $6 {By way of mitigation for what follows it should be pointed out that
the game was played under very adverse conditions (e.g.Backgound music)} 7.
exd5 Qe7+ $2 {Black plays hopelessly throughout which boosted my
over-confidence and speeded up my play. It was virtually a skittles game.} 8.
Kf1 Qb4 9. Qe2+ Be7 10. Re1 {Threatening 11.c3} b5 11. Bxb5+ c6 12. dxc6 Nd5
13. Bxb8 O-O 14. c3 Qa5 15. c7 {I'd completely ceased to bother here.} Bd6 $2
16. Bc6 Raxb8 17. cxb8=Q Bxb8 18. Qb5 Qxb5+ 19. Bxb5 Be6 20. Ng5 Nc7 21. Nxe6
$4 {Without a thought and quite oblivious , but I'd given up calculating.}
fxe6+ 22. Ke2 Nxb5 23. h3 Bg3 24. Ref1 Nd6 25. Rxf8+ Kxf8 26. Kd3 {I
stillexpected an easy win.} Nf5 27. Rf1 g6 28. Rf3 Ke7 29. c4 a5 30. c5 Bc7 31.
Kc4 Kd7 $2 32. g4 Ne7 33. Rf7 h6 34. Rh7 Bf4 35. Kb5 Bd2 36. Kb6 Ke8 37. Rh8+
Kd7 38. Rh7 Ke8 39. c6 Nd5+ 40. Kb7 Bf4 41. c7 Bxc7 42. Rxc7 Nxc7 43. Kxc7 Ke7
44. Kb6 Kd6 45. Kxa5 Kd5 46. b4 Kxd4 47. b5 Kd5 48. b6 Kc6 49. Ka6 e5 50. b7
Kc7 51. Ka7 e4 52. b8=Q+ {Terrible. I just played it like a high speed
skittles game. maybe it was in keeping with the event.} 1-0

