1. d4 e6 2. c4 f5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e3 d5 5. Bd3 c6 6. Nge2 Bd6 7. Qc2 ({If now} 7.
O-O {I intended} Bxh2+ $1) 7... g6 {so as to be able to answer PxP with ePxP}
8. f3 O-O 9. Bd2 Na6 10. a3 dxc4 11. Bxc4 b5 $6 {Leaving the c-Pawn backwards
but securing possibilities on the QS.} 12. Bd3 Qe7 13. b4 {Fixing the c-Pawn
and preventing a later b4.} e5 14. O-O $2 {Probably the losing move.} ({
Correct was} 14. e4) 14... e4 $1 15. fxe4 Bxh2+ $1 16. Kh1 ({If} 16. Kxh2 Ng4+
17. Kg1 (17. Kg3 Qg5) 17... Qh4 18. Rf4 (18. Rfb1 Qh2+ 19. Kf1 fxe4+) 18... g5
19. Rf3 Qh2+ 20. Kf1 Qh1+ 21. Ng1 Nh2+ 22. Ke2 Nxf3 {and now} 23. Kxf3 (23.
gxf3 Qg2+ 24. Kd1 Qxg1+) (23. Nxf3 Qxa1) 23... fxe4+) 16... Ng4 17. Nf4 {
Loses a piece but what else is there.} (17. g3 Bxg3 $1 18. Nxg3 Qh4+) (17. Rf3
Qh4 18. Rh3 Nf2+ 19. Kxh2 Nxh3 20. gxh3 fxe4 21. Bxe4 Qxh3+) 17... Bxf4 18. Be1
({If now} 18. Rxf4 Qh4+ 19. Kg1 Qh2+ 20. Kf1 Qh1+ 21. Ke2 Qxg2+ 22. Kd1 Qg1+
23. Bf1 Nxe3+) 18... Nxe3 19. Qe2 Nxf1 20. Qxf1 fxe4 {White decides to plod on
for a while but it gets worse.} 21. Qe2 e3 22. Qf3 Qg7 (22... Qg7 {Threatening}
23. Z0 Qh6+ 24. Kg1 Bh2+ 25. Kh1 Bg3+) 23. Bg3 Bxg3 24. Qxg3 Qxd4 25. Bxg6 hxg6
26. Qxg6+ Qg7 27. Qxc6 Bb7 28. Qe6+ Rf7 29. Nd5 {The oly alternative was
Resigns.} Qxa1+ 0-1

