1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nf6 {I've only played against this once before (v John G
Collins Thames Valley Easter Cogress Rd 2 13\4\63) & I couldn't remember much
about the openig.} 3. e5 Nd5 4. Nc3 e6 5. Nxd5 exd5 6. d4 Nc6 7. dxc5 Bxc5 8.
Qxd5 Qb6 ({J.G.C. played} 8... d6) 9. Qd2 ({I considered} 9. Bc4 Bxf2+ 10. Kd1
O-O 11. Ng5 Nd8 12. Rf1) 9... d6 10. Bd3 ({Black regains the Pawn as...} 10.
exd6 {is too dangerous for White.}) 10... Nxe5 ({I would have been more
worried by} 10... Bg4) 11. Nxe5 dxe5 12. O-O O-O {[7'] Black was playing very
quickly and obviously knew the opening better than I did.} 13. Kh1 {[26']} Be6
14. f4 f6 15. b3 exf4 16. Qxf4 Bd4 17. Rb1 Be5 18. Qh4 g6 {White is getting on
top.} 19. Bf4 ({I also considered...} 19. Ba3) ({...and} 19. Bh6) 19... Bxf4
20. Rxf4 Kg7 21. Re1 Rae8 22. Rb4 Qc7 23. Rbe4 ({I alaso considered} 23. Bb5
Re7 24. Rbe4) {Black now offered a draw which I declined whereupon he played.}
23... Bd7 $4 (23... Bf7 {leaves White some innitiative but not enough to win.})
24. Re7+ Rxe7 25. Rxe7+ 1-0

