{Opponent grade 202} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Bd3 b6 $2 {Rather too
infelexible. I intended playingthis line from the start and played it
regardless. It doesn't turn out well in this line.} 5. exd5 exd5 6. Nf3 Nf6 7.
O-O O-O 8. Ne5 {I wasn't too happy now.} Bxc3 9. bxc3 c5 10. Ba3 {Doesn't turn
out particularly well.} Qc7 11. Qf3 Nc6 12. Rfe1 Re8 13. Nxc6 Bg4 14. Qg3 Qxc6
15. f3 Bh5 16. dxc5 bxc5 17. Qf2 c4 18. Bf5 Rxe1+ 19. Rxe1 Re8 20. Rxe8+ Qxe8 {
I felt that I'd just about equalised here. White has two Bishops but slightly
weaker Pawns.} 21. Bc5 Qe5 $2 {Rather too ambitious.} (21... a6 {is sounder.})
22. Qg3 {I'd missed this. If I exchange I'm left with a very bad ending.} Qe2
23. Qb8+ Ne8 {Now I get tied up and am probably in a lost position.} 24. h3 a6
25. f4 {To prevent ......Qe5+ after his Queen has moved.} Bg6 26. Bd7 f6 27. f5
Bf7 28. Bd6 g5 {Trying to break out.} 29. Be6 Kg7 30. Bxf7 Qd1+ {To gaurd the
d-Pawn but it turns out just the same.} 31. Kh2 Kxf7 32. Qb7+ Kg8 33. Bc5 Qe2 {
I view of the threat 34.Qe7 I have to give up the d-Pawn anyway.} 34. Qxd5+ Kg7
35. Qd7+ Kg8 36. Qd5+ Kg7 37. Qd7+ Kg8 38. Qe7 Qxe7 39. Bxe7 Kf7 40. Bb4 Nc7 {
Time was called and after some discussion I resigned. I think 24......Qe5 may
have been the losing move. Lancaster lost the match 4 - 2.} 1-0

