1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 3. d3 Nc6 4. Bg5 Nf6 5. exf5 {White wasn't too happy in
this opening.} d5 6. Nc3 Bxf5 {I was thiking of castling QS.} 7. Bxf6 ({
I don't like this move for White. Better} 7. Qd2 Z0 8. O-O-O) 7... gxf6 8. d4 {
To free his Bishop but leaving Black several reasonable moves.} Bb4 {After
some thought. Alternatives are......} (8... e4) (8... Nxd4) (8... exd4) 9. Bb5
e4 10. Qe2 $6 ({I had expected} 10. Nh4 Be6 {with a better game. continuation.
Black now ends up with 2B v 2N, a strong centre and 2 open files.}) 10... O-O {
Forcing his reply.} 11. Bxc6 bxc6 12. Nh4 Be6 13. O-O {It was difficult to
find a reasonable move here. Black must have a won game.} f5 14. Qh5 Qf6 15.
Rae1 $6 {Deciding that if he is to get anywhere he must attack. White intends
Re3-g3-etc} Qxd4 16. Re3 {Rather a waste of time as it turns out.} ({Possible
was} 16. Ng6 Rf7 {etc.}) 16... f4 17. Qg5+ Kh8 18. Rd1 Qf6 (18... Qxd1+ {
Might win.}) 19. Qxf6+ Rxf6 20. Ree1 Rh6 21. g3 Rg8 22. Ng2 fxg3 23. fxg3 $2 {
Hastens the end} Bc5+ 24. Kh1 Rxg3 25. Nf4 Bg4 26. Rd2 Bf3+ 27. Ng2 Rgh3 {
0 Lancaster won the match 6 -} 0-1

