{[#] Odds of f-Pawn and two moves.} 1. d4 Z0 2. c4 {easier to play at at these
odds than e4 & d4} Nf6 3. Nc3 d6 4. e3 {Very timid} g6 5. Be2 Bg7 6. h3 O-O 7.
Nf3 Bf5 8. Ng5 $6 h6 9. e4 Bc8 10. Nf3 Nbd7 11. Nh4 $6 {White does an awful
lot of Knight manoeuvering in this game.} Qe8 12. Qd3 ({If} 12. Nb5 Nxe4 13.
Nxc7 Qf7) 12... e5 {From now on Black is on top.} 13. d5 $2 {Blocking off the
centre and leaving Black free to attack on the KS.} Nc5 14. Qe3 a5 15. O-O Bd7
16. b3 Nh7 17. Ba3 b6 ({Not} 17... Na6 $2 18. c5 $1) 18. Qg3 g5 19. Nf3 Nf6 20.
Nd2 Na6 21. Nd1 {Waste of time.} Qg6 22. Bf3 (22. Bd3 Nh5 23. Qe3 Nf4) 22... h5
23. h4 g4 24. Nc3 Kh7 25. Be2 Bh6 26. Rad1 Kg7 ({Not} 26... Bxd2 27. Rxd2 Nxe4
$4 28. Nxe4 Qxe4 29. Bd3) 27. Bd3 $4 {Still thinking about defence of the
e-Pawn he blunders.} Bf4 {Not a single capture made. In the 1/4 final I beat S.
Metcalfe, giving him a Knight in a rather poor game. In the 1/2 final I lost
in about 70 moves to P.Nolan , giving him a Knight start.} 0-1

