1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 d6 4. Bc4 h6 {The first time I had played this line.
I wasn't too familiar with it.} 5. b3 {Played in a flash. White knew this line
well and this move had been recommended by M.J.Basman.} Be7 $1 {A surprise to
White. I threaten either 6......Bh4+ or 6......Bf6, in either case with a good
game.} 6. Qe2 {Discouraging the Bishop check by Black.} Bg4 7. Bb2 $6 {A
trifle over-confident perhaps.} ({I now expected} 7. O-O Bf6 {etc.}) 7... Bh4+
8. Kd1 $2 ({I expected} 8. Kf1 {in view of the follow up d4.}) 8... Bf6 9. d4
Nc6 10. c3 {White was decidedly unhappy now.} ({In view of his King position} 
10. e5 {is not possible.}) 10... Nge7 {I had thoughts of castling QS.} 11. Nbd2
O-O 12. Kc2 Re8 {Threatening 13......Nf5 14......Ne3+} 13. Qf2 Ng6 ({After
some thought I played the text. I considered} 13... g5 {but didn't like} 14. h4
) 14. Rae1 Na5 {I was doubtful about this.} 15. Bd3 Rc8 16. g3 c5 17. c4 $2 {
White was very short of time and had to rush to move 20. This is very doubtful.
} ({Possibly best was.} 17. d5 {which gives me e5 but leaves my Knight on a5
offside.}) 17... Nc6 $1 18. gxf4 $2 {White had no time to think.} (18. a3 {
was marginally better.}) 18... Nb4+ 19. Kc3 {Horrible but necessary} Qa5 20.
Qg3 {White has made it on the clock but has no hope.} Bxf3 21. Nxf3 ({Not} 21.
Qxf3 $4 cxd4#) 21... cxd4+ 22. Kd2 ({If} 22. Nxd4 Bh4) 22... Nxd3+ 23. Kxd3
Qxa2 24. Bxd4 Qxb3+ 25. Kd2 Rxc4 0-1

