1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 3. Nxe5 Qf6 4. Nc4 fxe4 5. Nc3 {White played these moves
instantaneously. I'd beaten him with this opening last year and began to
wonder if he'd prepared something meanwhile.} Qf7 6. Ne3 {Preventing 6......d5
& intending 7.Bc4 but it isn't so good as it looks at first sight.} Nf6 7. Bc4
Qg6 8. O-O c6 {White now realises that Black isn't too badly placed.} 9. Re1 d5
10. Nexd5 $5 {Almost a forced sacrifice.} cxd5 11. Nxd5 Bd6 12. Nxf6+ gxf6 13.
d3 Bh3 {Skating on thin ice but possibly best. The e-Pawn had to go.} 14. Rxe4+
Be5 15. Qf3 Bd7 {Only just. White threatened 16.RxB+ ; 17.Qxb7} 16. d4 Bc6 17.
d5 Bd7 18. Bf4 Bf5 {Again about the only move.} 19. Rxe5+ $6 fxe5 20. Bxe5 Be4
$2 21. Qh3 {Threatening 21.BxR ; 21.Qc8+} Bf5 22. Qb3 {Making it easier for
Black} ({After} 22. Qe3 {I'd have been in trouble.}) 22... Rg8 23. g3 Qb6 24.
Qxb6 axb6 25. Re1 Kd7 26. Bb5+ Kc8 27. a4 Bd7 28. c4 Re8 29. b3 Na6 30. f4 Nc5
31. b4 $2 {One move past the time control he gives it away. Now it's easy for
Black.} Nd3 32. Re3 Nxb4 33. Rb3 Bxb5 34. cxb5 Nxd5 35. Rd3 Rd8 36. Rd4 Ne3 37.
Re4 Rd1+ 38. Kf2 Ng4+ 39. Ke2 Rd5 40. Bc3 Kd7 41. h3 Nh6 42. g4 Re8 43. Rxe8
Kxe8 44. f5 Nf7 45. h4 h5 46. g5 Rxf5 47. g6 Ne5 48. g7 Kf7 49. Ke3 Rf3+ 50.
Kd4 Rd3+ 51. Kxe5 Rxc3 52. Kd6 Kxg7 0-1

