1. f4 {Played mainly for surprise value.} Nf6 2. Nf3 b6 3. d3 {Forcing him to
block the long diagonal with ......d5 in order to prevent e4.} Bb7 4. e4 e6 5.
e5 Nd5 6. a3 $1 {Denying b4 to his minor pieces.} g6 7. d4 Bg7 8. Bd3 Ne7 9.
O-O O-O 10. g4 {Preventing 10......Nf5 and intending a KS advance.} d5 ({
10.......d5 surprised me. Why not} 10... c5) 11. Qe1 {Envisaging Nh4 & f5} Ba6
12. Bxa6 Nxa6 13. Qe2 {A change of strategy. I decided to try and exploit my
general positional plus.} Qc8 14. Be3 c5 15. Nc3 {With thoughts of Nb5---d6}
cxd4 16. Nxd4 Nc7 {Rather passive.} (16... Nc5 $142) 17. Rf3 Qd7 18. g5 {
Preventing 18......f6 and intending a straightforward KS attack with; Rh3,
Qf2---h4} Nf5 19. Nxf5 exf5 20. Qf2 h5 {Desperate stuff in view of Rh3 & Qh4.}
21. gxh6 Bxh6 22. Qh4 Kg7 23. Qf6+ Kh7 24. Rh3 Rh8 ({and not} 24... Qd8 $4 25.
Qg5 $1) 25. Rd1 Qe6 {This secures respite from the direct attack but his
position remains hopeless. The d-Pawn is the immediate target.} 26. Qg5 Kg7 27.
Qg2 Rad8 28. Ne2 {With all sorts of nasty threats.} Kf8 $4 {In a very poor
position Black blunders. He saw his mistake immediately} 29. Rxh6 1-0

