{I needed to win to score 100%, S.S. neede to win to come second.} 1. c4 e5 2.
Nc3 f5 3. f4 $6 {One of Mr.S's little excentricities and rather a bad move.}
exf4 4. d4 $2 Qh4+ 5. Kd2 Nf6 6. Nf3 Qh6 7. Qe1 Ne4+ 8. Kd1 Bb4 9. e3 fxe3 10.
Bxe3 Qe6 11. Kc2 O-O 12. d5 Qe7 13. Bd4 Na6 14. Qh4 Qxh4 15. Nxh4 Nxc3 16. bxc3
Be7 17. Nf3 Nc5 $2 {Not the best.} 18. Re1 {Forcing ......Bd6 or Ne5 or Black
is likely to lose a Pawn.} Ne4 19. Bd3 d6 {Preventing the immediate win of a
Pawn.} 20. Rhf1 {There seems little point in this.} ({I expected} 20. Kb2 {
threatening 21.BxN etc.}) 20... Bf6 21. Re2 Bd7 22. Bxf6 Rxf6 23. Nd4 Nc5 24.
Re7 {White wastes a lot of time with Rook moves.} Kf8 25. Re2 Nxd3 26. Kxd3 Re8
27. Rb2 b6 28. Rbf2 Re5 29. g4 $2 {Gives Black a relatively easy endgame with
an extra KS Pawn and White's King cut off.} fxg4 30. Rxf6+ gxf6 31. Rxf6+ Kg7
32. Rf4 h5 33. Kc2 {Where's he going?} Kg6 34. Kb3 Bf5 35. Rf2 a6 36. Rg2 Re3
37. Rf2 Bd7 38. Kc2 h4 39. Kd2 Re5 40. Ne2 Bf5 41. Rg2 b5 42. Nf4+ Kg5 43. Nd3
Bxd3 44. Kxd3 bxc4+ 45. Kxc4 Re3 46. Kd4 Rf3 ({Not} 46... Kf4 $4 47. Rxg4+) 47.
c4 Kf4 48. Re2 g3 49. Re4+ Kf5 50. hxg3 (50. Rxh4 g2 {Threatens mate.}) 50...
hxg3 51. Re8 g2 52. Rf8+ Kg4 53. Rg8+ Kh3 54. Ke4 Rf1 55. Rh8+ Kg3 56. Rg8+ Kf2
57. Rg7 g1=Q 58. Rxc7 Qg4+ 59. Kd3 Qf3+ 60. Kc2 Re1 61. c5 Re2+ 62. Kb1 Qh1# {
Lancaster Club Championship 1971-72 1st Collins 10 2nd Turner 8 3rd Lawrence 7.
5 4th= Owen,Szalanczi 6.5 6th Lenartowicz 4.5 7th Russell 3.5 8th Muranyi 3
10= Wilkinson,Barry 1.5} 0-1

