1. f4 d5 2. Nf3 c5 3. g3 Nc6 4. Bg2 g6 5. O-O Bg7 6. c3 Nh6 {Rather artificial.
Black wants to force ......e5 as soon as possible.} 7. d3 O-O 8. Qc2 e5 $2 {
Black realised his mistake immediately. The position of his h-Knight results
in losing a Pawn.} 9. fxe5 Ng4 {About the best.} 10. d4 cxd4 11. cxd4 Qb6 {
Black has some positional compensation for his Pawn.} 12. e3 Bf5 13. Qb3 {
After much thought.} ({If} 13. Qd1 {or 13.Qe2, then} Nb4 {can be a nuisance.})
13... Nb4 14. Ne1 $1 {A useful move covering c2 & d3 also attacking d5.} Rac8 (
{If say.....} 14... Nd3 {then} 15. Qxb6 axb6 16. Rxf5 Nxe1 17. Rf1 {is good
for White as the d-Pawn falls.}) 15. Na3 {An interesting position but it's
Black who has all the problems. I particular his d-pawn is very weak.} Bc2 $6 {
Leads to a hopeless endgame.} (15... Be6 $142) 16. Naxc2 Nxc2 17. Qxb6 axb6 18.
Nxc2 Rxc2 19. h3 ({If} 19. Bxd5 Nxh2) 19... Nh6 20. Bxd5 Nf5 21. Be4 ({If} 21.
Bxb7 Nxg3 {is a nuisance.}) 21... Re2 {Loses the exchange but the alternatives
were no better.} 22. Bd3 Nxg3 23. Bxe2 Nxe2+ 24. Kf2 Nxc1 25. Raxc1 Ra8 26. a3
Re8 27. Rc7 f6 28. exf6 Bxf6 29. Rfc1 Bg5 30. R1c3 Rf8+ 31. Ke2 Bf6 32. Rc8
Rxc8 33. Rxc8+ Kf7 34. Rc7+ Ke6 35. Rxh7 Kd5 36. Rxb7 Kc6 37. Rf7 Bh8 38. Kd3
g5 39. e4 b5 40. e5 Kd5 41. Rh7 Bxe5 42. dxe5 1-0

