{Time control 40 moves in 2 hrs [Opp Grade 191]} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4
4. e5 Qd7 5. Nf3 b6 6. Bd3 Bb7 7. O-O Nc6 8. Ne2 {[22'] White intends to storm
the QS and leave my KBishop embarassed.} O-O-O {[3']} 9. c3 Bf8 ({I also
considered} 9... Be7 10. Z0 {and} g5 {sacrificing the Pawn for an open file.})
10. b4 f5 {White will, of course, make faster progress on the QS than Black on
the KS, but I hoped to contain his attack.} 11. a4 h6 12. a5 g5 {I felt I
could defend a2 if the a-file opens.} 13. axb6 ({Naturally not} 13. a6 {
more or less blocking the QS. However White may have done better to firstly
mobilise behind his Pawns.}) 13... cxb6 14. Bb5 Kb8 15. Qa4 Nge7 {White has no
immediate threats so I manoeuvre the Knight to c8 defending a2 & b6.} 16. Nd2 {
[55'] White's move may have intended c5 which gives my e7 Knight my d5 square
hence I move my Queen ( before my Knight c8)} Qc7 {[22']} 17. Nb3 Nc8 18. Bd2
N6e7 {Again eyeing d5 if he plays c4 . Also with thoughts on the QS. e.g.
f4-f5 & Nf5.} 19. Rfc1 {Now c5 is coming and I don't have time for a slow KS
build up. Something definite is neede on the QS. Hence.......} Bc6 20. c4 {
Exchanges favour Black.} dxc4 {[38'] Better than the Bishop exchange as it
ensures d5 for the Knight.} 21. Nc5 $5 {After much thought other lines give
Black at leat equality as his d & b Pawns are weak in an endgame.} bxc5 {
[47'] Forced. a6 & e6 were threatened.} 22. bxc5 Bxb5 {More or less forced in
view of 23.Ba5} 23. Rcb1 ({On} 23. Qxb5+ {I intended} Qb7 24. Qxc4 Qd5 {etc.})
23... Ka8 24. Rxb5 Nc6 {A useful move, covering important squares.} 25. Qxc4
Bg7 $1 {In wasn't sure about this. 26......BxP is now threatened and the Rooks
are connected . If I can move the Knight (c8) and play......Rb8 I should be
safe.} ({but......} 25... Nxe5 $6 26. Qxe6 {is good for White.}) 26. Bc3 {
Unpinning the d-Pawn. White was now getting short of time.} ({Not} 26. Qxe6
Nxd4) 26... Qd7 27. Qa4 {Threatens nothing. Black can force .......Rb8} ({
I expected} 27. Rab1 N8e7 28. Rb7 Qc8 29. Qa4 Rd7 {Blac seems Ok.}) 27... N8e7
28. Kf1 {With < 10' White is lost for a continuation. This is equivalent to
resigning.} Rb8 29. Rab1 Rxb5 30. Rxb5 Rb8 31. Ke1 {White had no hope. After
this another Pawn goes leaving him in a hopeless position, also with no time
on the clock.} Rxb5 32. Qxb5 Nxe5 {4 A good win with a new variation. I was
very satisfied with my play. Lancaster lost the match 2 -} 0-1

