1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 g6 4. O-O Bg7 5. d3 e5 6. Nbd2 Ne7 7. e4 O-O 8. exd5
Nxd5 9. Nc4 Nc6 10. Re1 Bg4 11. h3 Bxf3 12. Bxf3 Rc8 13. Ne3 {White wastes
time with his Knight manoeuvres.} Nc7 14. Bd2 Ne6 15. Nc4 b5 16. Ne3 Kh8 {
[16'] Intending ......f5} 17. Rb1 {[40']} f5 {[18'] Black is well on top now.}
18. Kh2 Ned4 19. Bg2 f4 20. Nf1 f3 $6 {Overdoing it. I was trying to win too
quickly. The Pawn becomes rather a liability.} 21. Bh1 g5 $2 {Played very
quickly. Overconfidence.} 22. Be3 g4 $6 23. c3 Ne2 24. hxg4 Qf6 25. Bxf3 Nf4 $4
{Going right off the rails. I just don't get enough compensation for the piece.
} (25... Qxf3 $142) (25... Nxg3 $142) 26. gxf4 Qh4+ 27. Kg2 exf4 28. Bxc5 Rf6
$2 (28... Rfd8 $142) 29. Nd2 Rf7 30. Rh1 Qd8 31. Ne4 Rd7 32. d4 Ne5 33. Qe2 Ng6
34. g5 Rc6 35. Rh5 Re6 36. Rbh1 h6 37. Bg4 f3+ 38. Qxf3 ({Not of course} 38.
Kxf3 $4) 38... Ne5 39. dxe5 Rd3 40. Be3 Rxe5 41. gxh6 {A.Gardner played for
the University. Rather a foolhardy attack and sacrifice. I should have won the
game with steadier play at about moves 20 - 25.} 1-0

