1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. g3 Nbd7 5. Bg2 Bb4+ 6. Bd2 Qe7 7. cxd5 $2 {
I'm doubtful about this. It seems to be the start of my troubles, giving Black
play on the KS.} exd5 8. O-O (8. Nc3 {May be better.}) 8... Bxd2 9. Qxd2 ({
I didn't like} 9. Nbxd2 {but the Queen isn't happy on d2.}) 9... O-O 10. Nc3 {
[10']} c6 {[33']} 11. e3 {I was already unhappy with the position. Black has
an easy build up on the KS whereas it will take some time for White to gat any
play going on the QS.} Ne4 12. Qc2 Re8 13. Nxe4 $2 {Againg doubtful. Black's
Pawn on e4 proves more of a nuisacnce than I'd expected.} dxe4 14. Nd2 Nf6 ({If
} 14... f5 {I hd intended.} 15. Qc4+ {followed by 16.b4}) 15. Rac1 Bg4 16. Rfe1
Rad8 17. Nc4 {After much thought.} (17. f4 {is a bit desperate}) ({I spent a
time examining} 17. Nxe4 {however Black does well with....} Nxe4 18. f3 Nf6 $1
19. fxg4 Nxg4 {etc.}) 17... c5 18. dxc5 Qxc5 19. Na3 $6 {Hoping to manoeuvre
the Knight to d4.} ({I didn't like} 19. Nd2) ({but possibly} 19. Bf1 {was best.
}) 19... Qh5 20. Qc7 {I couldn't find a move I was happy with.} Bf3 21. Rc5 $6
{This should lose outright but it may have been beyound saving.} Nd5 $1 {
With a subtle point which I miss.} 22. Qxb7 Bxg2 23. Kxg2 Qf3+ $2 {
Unfortunately Black misses it too.} (23... Nxe3+ $1) 24. Kh3 {Black was
expecting an easy win despite being a bit short of time.} ({And not} 24. Kg1 $4
Nxe3 {and if} 25. Rxe3 (25. fxe3 Rd2) 25... Rd1+) 24... Rd6 25. Rc6 {The only
move, but maybe good enough.} Qh5+ {Black decides to gain time on the clock
with a few checks.} 26. Kg2 Qf3+ 27. Kh3 Qh5+ 28. Kg2 Qf3+ {4 Black
miscalculates, not realising that he is repeating moves once too often. I now
declared my next move 29.Kh3 and claimed a draw. We were unable to find a
clear win for Black at the end. White seemed to survive in all lines.
Lancaster lost the match 2 -} 1/2-1/2

