1. c4 g6 2. d4 e6 {Illogical.} 3. e4 Bg7 4. Nc3 a6 5. f4 d6 6. Nf3 Ne7 7. Bd3
Nbc6 ({Surely} 7... c5 {is necessary}) 8. Be3 Bd7 9. O-O f5 {Action at last.}
10. a3 e5 11. d5 Nd4 {[25']} 12. fxe5 {[12']} dxe5 {[30']} 13. b4 f4 $2 (13...
Nxf3+ $142 14. gxf3 fxe4 {Now he loses the d-Pawn.}) 14. Bxd4 exd4 15. Ne2 O-O
{[41']} 16. Ra2 {[16']} Bg4 17. h3 Bxf3 18. Rxf3 Be5 19. Bb1 {[21']} c6 20.
Nxd4 cxd5 21. exd5 Nxd5 $6 {Complete despair} 22. cxd5 Qxd5 (22... Qxd5 23. Rd2
{If} Qd7 (23... Z0 {threatening} 24. Ba2) 24. Ba2+ Kh8 25. Ne6 {Hence reisgns.}
) 23. Rd2 {Rather a dissapionting game for the final. The second year running
winning the "Silver Knight" "The Final of the lancaster & Morecambe League
Individual Title was played earlier this week at the odd fellows' hall between
Dr. R.A.Collins (University & Lancaster) and the Rev John Calvert (Morecambe &
Lancaster). Dr. Collins opened with an English which the Rev J Calvert
attempted to meet with a Pirc-Robatsch system. Establicsing a broad centre the
White pieces denied all maneouverability to the opposition. In attempt at
freedom the Rev Calvert sacrificed a piece but to no avail, leaving Dr Collins
to retain his hold on the title" Lancaster Gaurdian 12/05/72} 1-0

