{Time limit 36 moves in 2hrs} 1. c4 c5 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. O-O
Nf6 6. Nc3 O-O 7. e3 {I wasn't too keen on this but wanted to break the
symmetry.} d6 8. d4 Bg4 9. h3 Bd7 10. d5 Na5 11. Qe2 Ne8 12. e4 a6 13. a4 Nb3
14. Ra3 Nxc1 15. Rxc1 e5 {After much thought. It leaves his d-Pawn and d5 weak.
} 16. dxe6 Bxe6 17. Rd1 Qf6 18. Ne1 h5 19. Nc2 Rd8 20. Ne3 Nc7 21. Rb3 Bc8 22.
Rd3 {Intending doubling on the d-file with the Queen behind the Rook. Also 23.
Rb6 to pressure the d-Pawn.} Qg5 23. Ncd5 Nxd5 24. Nxd5 Bd4 25. h4 Qe5 26. Kh2
Kg7 {To prevent subsequent Knight forks.} 27. f4 Qe8 28. f5 $5 Bxf5 29. Rxb7
Bc8 $2 ({Rather better seems.} 29... Be6) 30. Re7 Qxa4 31. Rxd4 {Hoping for
something on the Black squares.} cxd4 32. Qd3 Rg8 $4 {Black loses his head.} ({
If say} 32... Be6 {then I can't see anything better than a draw for White by}
33. Qxd4+ Kh6 34. Qe3+ Kh7 35. Nf6+ Kg7 36. Nxh5+ {etc.}) 33. Qxd4+ Kf8 34.
Rxf7+ $1 {A neat finish.} 1-0

