{Time limit 36 moves in 2hrs} 1. d4 f5 {[10']} 2. e4 fxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f3 exf3
5. Nxf3 e6 6. Bd3 Bb4 7. O-O c5 8. Ne2 {Leaves Black with a passed e-Pawn.}
cxd4 9. Nexd4 Nc6 10. c3 Bc5 11. Kh1 d6 12. Qe1 e5 13. Bg5 Qe7 {With the
thought of castling QS.} 14. Nf5 Bxf5 15. Bxf5 O-O 16. Qh4 h6 ({Not} 16... g6
$2 17. Bxg6 hxg6 18. Nd2 {etc.}) 17. Bd2 Qf7 18. Qh3 Qh5 19. Nh4 Ne7 20. Be6+ {
[65']} Kh7 {[88']avoiding Knight checks, better than 20......Kh8} 21. Rae1 g5 {
The end of White's attack.} 22. Nf5 ({If} 22. Qd3+ e4 23. Rxe4 Nxe4 24. Qxe4+
Kg7 {etc.}) 22... Qxh3 23. gxh3 Nxf5 24. Bxf5+ Kg7 25. Bc2 Nd5 26. Kg2 Rxf1 27.
Rxf1 Be3 28. Be1 {Loses another Pawn but the endgame is lost anyway.} Bc1 29.
Kh1 Bxb2 30. Be4 Nxc3 31. Bxc3 Bxc3 32. Rb1 Rb8 33. Rxb7+ Rxb7 34. Bxb7 Kf6 35.
Kg2 Ke6 36. Bc8+ Kd5 37. Bb7+ Kd4 {Four of my five opponents were prizewinners.
1st= M.Brigden; T.Skulason; P.Littewood; D.G.Ellison 4/5 5th R.A.Collins 3.5/5
6th= J.A.Foster; G.Homer; R.Pomfret; B.Thebault; A.willis 3/5 22 competed} 0-1

