{Time limit 20mph} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 3. d3 {Very passive.} Nc6 4. exf5 d5 5.
b3 Bxf5 6. Bb2 Bb4+ 7. Nbd2 {[8']} ({naturally} 7. Nc3 {loses a piece.}) 7...
Qe7 {[6']} 8. a3 Bd6 9. c4 $6 {[13] A rather deperate looking attempt to
create some room!} d4 $1 {[13'] Best I think. The e-Pawn is not weak and White
is kept cramped with his (b2) Bishop out of play.} 10. Qe2 Nf6 {I hadn't yet
decided which side to castle.} 11. g3 O-O 12. Bg2 a5 {Fixing his QS to some
extent.} 13. O-O Rae8 14. Rfe1 {I didn't like this for White leaving his
f-Pawn weak.} Qd7 {After much thought. I was expecting White to play Ne4
hereabouts.} 15. Kh1 {Leaving f2 even weaker.} Ng4 {Threatening 16......Bxd3
winning the Queen, and also intending to manoeuvre one of the Rooks to h6.} 16.
Rf1 Re6 17. Ng1 $2 {Giving Black a nice combination.} Nxh2 $1 {[45']} 18. Rfe1
{[32']} ({Neither} 18. Kxh2) ({or} 18. Bxc6 {are playable.}) 18... Rh6 {[45']}
19. Nh3 Bxh3 20. f3 Bxg2+ 21. Kxg2 Qh3+ 22. Kg1 Nxf3+ 23. Kf2 Nxd2+ 24. Qf3
Qh2# {A neat attack.} 0-1

