{Time limit 20mph} 1. e4 e5 2. Bc4 Nc6 3. Nf3 Bc5 4. d3 d6 5. c3 {If White
intends d4 then d3 was a wasted move.} Nf6 6. Bg5 h6 7. Bh4 g5 8. Bg3 Bg4 9.
Nbd2 Qd7 10. h3 Be6 11. Bxe6 fxe6 (11... Qxe6 12. Qe2 a6 13. Nb3 Bb6 14. d4
exd4 15. Nfxd4) 12. Qe2 a6 {Both waiting for the other side to castle one way
or the other.} 13. Nb3 Bb6 14. d4 exd4 15. Nfxd4 {This surprised me. I was
much more concerned about......} ({.......} 15. cxd4) 15... e5 {I wasn't too
worried about his Knight going to f5.} 16. Nf5 O-O-O 17. O-O-O Rdf8 {Threat 18.
.....Nxe4} 18. f3 Nh5 19. Bh2 Kb8 20. g4 ({If} 20. Bg1 Rxf5 $1) 20... Nf4 21.
Bxf4 exf4 22. h4 Ne5 23. h5 $2 {Closes the KS leaving Black the innitiative on
the QS. Better was to open the h-file.} a5 24. Rd5 a4 25. Nbd4 Rf6 26. Nb5 Bc5
27. Rhd1 {Threat 28.RxB or 28.RxN} Qc6 28. Nbd4 {Black threatend 28......NxP}
Qb6 29. Nc2 Qa7 30. Kb1 c6 31. R5d2 Kc7 ({I also considered} 31... b5 32. Nxd6
Rd8 33. Nxb5 Rxd2 34. Qxd2) 32. Ncd4 Rg8 $2 {To prevent 33.Ng7; 34.Ne6+ The
game was adjourned. White sealed and announced he was playing on with the sole
intention of getting a draw. (No comment!)} 33. Ne7 $1 {The game resumed 17/11/
72 [sealed move] I'd missed this completely.} Rgf8 34. Nd5+ Kd7 35. Nxf6+ Rxf6
36. Nf5 Nf7 37. Ng7 b5 $4 {Rubbish.} 38. e5 Re6 39. Nxe6 Kxe6 40. exd6+ Be3 41.
d7 1-0

