{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. d4 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. g3 g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. Nc3
O-O 6. Nf3 c6 7. O-O d6 8. Re1 Qc7 9. Bf4 {The Bishop tends to be a traget for
advancing Pawns here.} h6 10. c5 {[16']} g5 {[7'] These evening matches tend
to be played at a rate of knots.} 11. cxd6 exd6 12. Qb3+ Kh8 13. Bd2 d5 {
[9'] After the game White expressed doubts about this as he gets e5 & c5.
However, Black blocks the long diagonal, leaves the e-Pawn backward, secures
e4 and prevents d5.} 14. Rac1 Be6 {Rather a problem here. 15.Nxd5 was
threatened and there was no good square for the Queen} 15. Ne5 Rd8 16. f4 g4
17. Rc2 Qb6 {Forcing the exchange of Queens as the Pawn structure will give
Black much the better prospects.} 18. Qxb6 axb6 19. b3 Bf8 20. Ng6+ {Doubtful.
His Knight is better than my Bishop} Kg7 21. Nxf8 Kxf8 22. Na4 Nbd7 23. Bb4+
Kf7 24. Rec1 Ra6 25. Be1 {[63']} Rda8 {[33']} 26. Bf1 {White was beginning to
get short of time.} b5 27. Nc3 Ne4 28. Nxe4 $2 ({Short of time he loses two
Pawns. Better was} 28. Ra1 {and Black has nothing definite.}) 28... dxe4 29.
Ra1 Bxb3 30. Rcc1 {[74']} Rxa2 {[37']} 31. Rxa2 Rxa2 32. Rb1 Bc4 {5 Lancaster
lost the match 2 -} 0-1

