{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. c4 c5 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. O-O e5
6. d3 Nge7 7. Nc3 d6 ({I was expecting Black to play} 7... f5 {fairly quickly})
8. Bg5 h6 9. Bxe7 Nxe7 10. Rb1 {Aiming to mobilise on the QS before Black gets
going on the KS} O-O 11. b4 Rb8 {[30']} 12. Nd2 {[30']} b6 13. Qa4 a6 14. bxc5
dxc5 15. Nd5 $2 {[35'] Completely overlooking his 16th move. I thought for a
long while and then deciding time was short made a "hurried" move without
going through all the variations. Black gets right on top now.} Nxd5 16. Bxd5
b5 {[56']} 17. Qc2 {[60']} (17. cxb5 {Isn't good enough.}) 17... b4 {[59']} 18.
Qa4 {[62']} Qc7 {[62']} 19. Nb3 {[80'] Black's QS pawns were very strong and I
was rather unhappy here.} Bf6 20. Qa5 Qxa5 {[75']} 21. Nxa5 {[83']} Bd7 22. Kg2
{I want to play on the KS by f4 and this prvents ........Bh3 and .......Bd4+ 
(after f4)} Rfc8 ({I was expecting} 22... Be7 $2 {when} 23. Nc6 {forces off
his white sq Bishop.}) 23. Bb7 $4 {Ridiculous.} Rc7 $4 ({Completey missing} 
23... Rxb7 24. Nxb7 Bc6+) 24. Bd5 {[91'] Somewhat relieved. I'd seen my
mistake as soon as I'd let go of the Bishop.} Bd8 25. e4 {Still intending f4}
Rcc8 $2 {Losing his innitiative.} 26. Nb7 Bb6 27. Nd6 Rf8 28. f4 {[97']
Apparently much to Black's surprise.} exf4 {[95'] He offered a draw here
despite time shortage and the knowledge I was playing badly I decided......}
29. Rxf4 Be6 {A ridiculous game. I seem to be right off form this season.}
1/2-1/2

