1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Nc3 Ne4 8. d5
$6 ({M.C.O. gives} 8. Qc2 {In the text Black gets a lot of play against my
doubled c-Pawns.}) 8... Nxc3 9. bxc3 Bf6 10. Ba3 d6 11. Qd2 e5 12. e4 Nd7 13.
Rfd1 {so as to be able to defend the c-Pawn with Bf1} a5 14. Rab1 ({Best may
be action on the KS with} 14. Ne1 Z0 {followed by} 15. f4) 14... Ba6 15. Bf1
Qe7 16. Qc2 {All too slow Black gets the innitiative on the KS.} g6 17. h3 Kh8
18. Bd3 Rae8 19. Kg2 Bc8 20. Re1 Bg7 21. g4 Bh6 22. Bc1 Bxc1 23. Qxc1 Nc5 24.
Qe3 f5 25. Nh2 {About the only move} fxe4 26. Bxe4 Nxe4 27. Qxe4 Rf4 28. Qd3
Ref8 ({I was much more worried about} 28... e4 $1 {Now I can hold it together
with my next move.}) 29. f3 Ba6 30. Re4 Rxe4 {Time was no called. Lancaster
lost the match 1.5 - 5.5} 1/2-1/2

