{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 10'} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2
Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Nc3 Ne4 {As 3 days ago but with colours reversed.} 8. Qc2
Nxc3 9. bxc3 {[10'] M.C.O. gives only 9.QxN. The doubled Pawns prove a problem.
} f5 {[2']} 10. Re1 {[13']} d6 {[4']} 11. Nd2 $6 {since he never gets round to
e4 this move is open to question. His KS is left very weak.} Bxg2 12. Kxg2 e5
13. dxe5 {[9']} dxe5 {[13']} 14. Nf3 {[23']} Nc6 {[14']} 15. Rd1 Qe8 16. e3 g5
{White isn't making any constructive progress so Black can advance at his
leisure.} 17. h3 {[37']} Qf7 {[20']} 18. e4 {[49'] After some thought White
decides on positive action.} g4 {[23'] Breaking open the KS.} 19. hxg4 fxg4 20.
Nh2 (20. Ng5 {Was playable and possibly better.}) 20... Bc5 {Now f2 looks a
bit unhappy.} 21. Nxg4 Qf3+ 22. Kh3 h5 23. Nh2 {h2 again. I had expected...} (
23. Nh6+ Kh8 {and maybe} 24. Nf5) 23... Qf7 $1 {The best I think. Black
threatens 24......Qxc4 and in time Rxf2} 24. Qd2 $2 {Loses quickly} (24. Be3 {
White gets a terrible endgame.}) (24. f3 {Could be best.}) 24... Qe6+ 25. g4 ({
If} 25. Kg2 Rxf2+ {etc}) 25... hxg4+ 26. Nxg4 Rf3+ 27. Kh4 Be7+ {A good win
with my first Q.Indian for a number of years. Match result - 7 all} 0-1

