{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 c6 5. e3
Bg7 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Bd3 dxc4 8. Bxc4 b5 $6 {Leaving his c-Pawn backward. He
loses the game on c6 subsequently!} 9. Bd3 a6 10. Rc1 Bb7 {[27']} 11. b4 {[10']
} a5 12. a3 Nbd7 13. O-O Nb6 14. Nxb5 $6 {Making it interesting} Nfd5 {Best}
15. Nc3 Nxf4 16. exf4 Bxd4 17. Be4 {Still aiming at c6} Bg7 18. b5 Rc8 19. Qb3
Ba8 20. Rfd1 Qc7 21. bxc6 (21. Nd5 Nxd5 22. Bxd5 Qb6 {is not as good.}) 21...
Bxc6 22. Ne2 $1 {Renewing the pin and with another threat.} Qb7 $2 {Loses the
exchange} ({Correct was} 22... Ba4 $1) 23. Rxc6 $1 {The pin wins it} Rxc6 24.
Nfd4 {The other point behind 22Ne2! Black must give up both Rooks for Bishop
and Knight.} a4 {[68']} 25. Qb1 {[68']} Bxd4 26. Nxd4 Qc7 $2 {Short of time
this leaves hima piece down.} 27. Nxc6 Nc4 28. Qb4 Nd6 29. Bf3 Rc8 30. Qxa4 Nf5
31. g3 h5 32. Qb4 Kg7 33. Qe4 e6 34. Qe5+ Qxe5 35. fxe5 Ra8 36. Ra1 Ra4 37. Nb4
Ra5 38. a4 Nd4 39. Bd1 Rxe5 40. a5 Re1+ 41. Kg2 Nb3 {Black hopes to end up
with R&N v Q&N but he must lose one of his minor pieces.} 42. a6 Nxa1 43. a7
Rxd1 44. a8=Q Nb3 {Immobilises the Knight} ({If} 44... Rb1 45. Qa3) 45. Qa4 Rb1
46. Qa2 {5 Lc Gambit lost 2 -} 1-0

