{Time limit 20mph} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. e4 Nxe5 5. f4 Ng6 (5...
Nec6 {is more usual.}) 6. Be3 ({I also considered.} 6. a3) 6... Bb4+ 7. Nc3
Bxc3+ {He took this instantaneously. I felt he was probably playing for a draw.
} 8. bxc3 {I wasn't happy about the Pawns.} d6 9. Bd3 Nd7 10. Nf3 b6 11. Nd4 {
I was still in two minds which side to castle so this move marks time and
makes use of a few holes in the Black set-up.} Bb7 12. Nf5 O-O ({I was more
concerned about} 12... Nh4 {but Black hadn't even considered it apparently.})
13. h4 Nc5 14. h5 Nxd3+ {Again he moved instantaneously.} 15. Qxd3 Ne7 16. Ng3
h6 17. O-O-O $2 (17. f5 $1 {Best. Denying him mhis next move. I was in the
wrong frame of mind here. I felt I was on top and that he was only playing for
a draw, so I relaxed.}) 17... f5 $1 18. Nxf5 $2 {Played without dueconcern or
consideration. I felt that Black's last move was semi desperate attempt to
break out.} Nxf5 19. exf5 Qf6 ({Expecting} 19... Bxg2 20. Rhg1 {etc. However
while Black was thinking I noticed 19......Qf6. I then woke up rather late and
started thinking.}) 20. Rhg1 {I was convinced that I was now lost.} Qxf5 21.
Qf1 {After exchange of Queens my Pawns are very poor.} Qxh5 22. g4 Qa5 23. Kb2
d5 $4 {Turning a probable win into a probable loss. This move serves no useful
purpose and gives White all the chances.} ({Best} 23... b5 24. cxb5 a6) 24. g5
{Not possible before because of 24......PxP; 25.Rxp QxR!} h5 25. Qh3 Rae8 26.
g6 $1 ({Not} 26. Bd4 $4 Re2+) 26... dxc4 27. Rg5 Rf5 28. Rxf5 {A close thing
after adopting the wrong psychological approach.} 1-0

