{Time limit 20mph} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 Qd7 5. a3 Bf8 {11 As per
M.C.O.} 6. Be3 b6 7. Bd3 Bb7 8. f4 Nc6 9. Nf3 O-O-O 10. b4 {[20']} f5 {[7']}
11. Qe2 Be7 12. O-O Nh6 13. Rfb1 Nf7 {[12'] The battle lines are drawn.} 14.
Bb5 h6 15. a4 {Forcing definitive QS action by Black.} a6 16. Bxa6 Bxb4 {
Now 17......Ba5 will hold White up for some time.} 17. Bd2 g5 {Taking
advantage of a certain lack of solidity in White's position.} 18. Bxb7+ Kxb7
19. Qb5 Ba5 {[30']} 20. Ne1 {[55'] An odd move leaving the d-Pawn and the
Bishop undefended. Was White intending 21.Nd3; 22.Nc5+?} Ka7 {[33']
Threatening 21......Nxd4} 21. Qd3 gxf4 {Making a little KS headway.} 22. Nb5+
Kb7 23. Bxa5 Nxa5 24. Nf3 {[70']} Rhg8 {[39']} 25. Nd2 Ng5 26. Nb3 {Rather
critical. White now threatens 27.NxN; 27.Nc5+ both of whichare murderous.} Nxb3
27. Qxb3 {Now a couple of moves allows White a probable decisive breakthrough
so.......} f3 $1 28. g3 ({If now} 28. gxf3 Nxf3+ 29. Kf2 Nd2) (28. a5 Nh3+ 29.
Kf1 fxg2+ 30. Ke2 g1=Q) ({White's best was} 28. Nd6+ $3 Kb8 29. a5 {but Black
wins after} Nh3+ 30. Kf1 fxg2+ 31. Ke2 g1=Q) 28... Ne4 {Threatening 29......Nd2
} 29. Qb4 $2 Nxg3 $1 30. hxg3 {Loses, but what else?} Rxg3+ 31. Kf2 Rg2+ 32.
Ke3 f4+ 33. Kxf3 ({If} 33. Kd3 Qh7+) 33... Qg7 {A god game.} 0-1

