1. c4 f5 2. d4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. g3 d5 5. Bg2 c6 6. b3 Be7 7. Nf3 O-O 8. O-O Qe8
9. Bf4 Qh5 10. Rb1 {Building up for a QS push.} Ne4 11. Qc1 Nd7 12. b4 g5 ({
If now} 12... dxc4 {then} 13. Nxe4 {makes a mess of his Pawns.}) (12... Nxc3
13. Qxc3 g5 {May be better.}) 13. Nxe4 gxf4 14. Nc3 fxg3 15. hxg3 a6 ({I had
expected} 15... f4 {when White would have to decide whether to risk} 16. gxf4
$6) 16. b5 {In prerference to the more solid 16.a3} axb5 17. cxb5 c5 $6 {
Opens up the postion somewhat.} 18. dxc5 Bxc5 19. Ng5 $6 {In preference to the
more solid 19.e6} Rf6 20. Nxe6 {Hoping to profit from the open lines after ....
...RxN Bxd5} Rh6 $6 {The attack on the h-file doesn't turn out to be that
dangerous.} 21. Rd1 $6 ({Simply} 21. Qg5+ {winning a Pawn overall may have
been best.}) 21... Nf6 $6 {Doesn't tirn out as well as the line in the
previous note.} ({Black's best now seems to be} 21... Qh2+ 22. Kf1 Rxe6 {
When White is left to find good moves. Best for White then is} 23. Nxd5 {
with various threats} (23. Bxd5 $4 Qxf2#)) 22. Nxc5 f4 {Wins back the piece
but leaves him two Pawns adrift.} 23. Qxf4 Qh2+ 24. Kf1 Bh3 {Threatening 25....
..Qh1#} 25. Ke1 ({Naturally} 25. Qf3) ({or} 25. Bxh3 {prevent mate.}) 25...
Bxg2 26. Rb4 {A useful move with later threats of Rh4 in the offing.} Re8 (
26... Rf8 {might cause White more trouble but} 27. Ne6 {then is quite good.})
27. Nd7 {Another useful move ensuring maintenance of the innitiative. Black
now sealed his next move.} Nxd7 {[Play resumed 23/3/73] The only move} (27...
Re6 {Fails against} 28. Qb8+ Kg7 (28... Ne8 29. Rg4+ Kh8 (29... Kf7 30. Qf4+
Ke7 31. Ne5 Nd6 32. Rg8 {etc.}) 30. Qf4) 29. Qf8+ Kg6 30. Nxf6 Rxf6 31. Qg8+
Kh5 (31... Kf5 32. Rf4+ Ke5 33. Rxd5+ $1) 32. Rh4+) 28. Qg4+ Kh8 29. Qxd7 Qh5
$1 {By far the best. Anything elas seems a dead loss for Black. I my very
limited analysis I had not seen this move. Black, however, had put a lot of
time in on this position.} 30. Rh4 {Leads to a difficult game} ({Black later
suggested.} 30. Qc7) 30... Qe5 {Nasty. The night can't move, nor can the Queen
defend it, 31.Rd4 is no good.} 31. Rd3 $1 {Seems the only move.} Rxh4 32. gxh4
Rg8 33. Re3 $4 ({Correct is} 33. f3 {I'd considered this but rejected it for
some reason e.g.} Bxf3 34. Rxf3 Rg1+ 35. Kd2 Qd4+ 36. Kc2 {and wins}) 33... Be4
34. Kf1 $1 {Again the only move. Black offered a DRAW which I accepted. Fuzzy
thinking in the second session.} 1/2-1/2

