1. d4 d6 2. e4 e5 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. Bc4 exd4 5. Nxd4 Ne5 $2 6. Bb3 Be7 7. O-O Nf6
8. Nc3 O-O 9. h3 a6 10. Be3 (10. a4 $142) 10... b5 11. Qe2 $4 {Completely
overlooking the threat.} c5 12. Ndxb5 ({Afterwards Black suggested I could
have saved the piece with} 12. f4 {but after} cxd4 13. fxe5 dxe5 $1 {still
wins the piece.}) 12... axb5 13. Nxb5 Ba6 14. Rfd1 (14. Rad1 $142) 14... Qb6
15. c4 Rfc8 16. f4 Ng6 17. Nc3 Bb7 18. Bc1 Rd8 19. g4 h6 20. Bc2 Qc6 21. Kh2 {
Positionally White stands better. possibly best was to sit tight rather than
aim for a KS "do-or-die" assault.} Qc7 22. Kh1 ({Either} 22. Nb5) ({or} 22. Kg1
{may be better.}) 22... Nh7 23. Rg1 $2 Bf6 24. Rg3 $2 Re8 {The pins on pins
are getting rather nasty.} 25. Bd2 (25. f5 {is answered by} d5 $1) 25... Bxc3
26. Rxc3 Qe7 27. f5 {What else? There are holes everywhere.} Ne5 28. b3 {
Leads to an immediate loss, but what else?} Nc6 29. Be3 Qe5 30. Qd2 Nd4 31. Bf4
Bxe4+ 32. Kh2 Nf3+ 33. Rxf3 Qxa1 {My worst game of the season & the 3rd time
this season that I've overlooked simple tactical threats and lost. (lack of
practice?)} 0-1

