1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 3. Nxe5 Qf6 4. d4 d6 5. Nc4 fxe4 6. Nc3 Bf5 {The first time
I've tried this.} (6... Qg6 $142) 7. Ne3 c6 8. Nxf5 Qxf5 9. d5 {Best} Nf6 10.
Bc4 b5 {The match was rather a skittles affair with no clocks, constant
interruption, and lasting barely more than an hour, due to other ceremonials,
buffet supper. Hence play is rather in the lightning spirit.} 11. Bb3 b4 12.
Ne2 cxd5 (12... c5 {May be best.}) 13. Nd4 Qd7 $2 {A mistake in an awkward
position.} 14. Bg5 {Nasty. I now spent some time thinking, for the only time
in the game.} a5 {Awkward. The d-Pawn must go.} 15. a4 $2 {Odd.} ({Why not} 15.
Bxf6 gxf6 16. Bxd5 Ra6 17. Qh5+ {etc.}) 15... Be7 16. Bxf6 Bxf6 17. Bxd5 Ra6
18. O-O Qa7 19. c3 Qc5 20. Nb5 Nd7 21. Rc1 Nb6 22. Bxe4 O-O 23. Qxd6 Qxd6 24.
Nxd6 bxc3 25. bxc3 Rd8 {We now adjournedfor the, buffet, prize givibg etc. The
position is probably drawn as Black gets a pawn back. However, on resuming,
White seemed to have lost the thread of the position.} 26. Rfd1 {Doubtful} (26.
Nb7 $142) 26... Nxa4 27. c4 $4 {Completely overlooking the Knight.} Raxd6 28.
Bd5+ Kf8 29. Rb1 $4 {White had gone right of the rails now.} Nc3 {Lancaster
won the match.} 0-1

