1. d4 f5 2. e3 Nf6 3. Bd3 g6 4. Nd2 Bg7 5. f4 O-O 6. c3 b6 {Only 2 hours was
available for the match so it was necessary to play very fast to try and get a
result. It was therefore rather a skittle game and includes some rather
doubtful moves.} 7. Ngf3 Bb7 8. O-O d6 (8... a6 {was probably more prudent.})
9. Ng5 Bd5 10. c4 Bf7 11. Nxf7 {[10']} Rxf7 {[6'] Note the speed of play!} 12.
Qf3 Nbd7 13. Rb1 e5 $1 {Securing at least equality.} 14. Bc2 e4 15. Qe2 c5 {
Intending a KS advance after d5.} 16. b4 {[29']} Ng4 {[14'] Hoping that at
this rate of play he might miss the threat of 17......Nxe3} 17. bxc5 {[34']}
dxc5 {[14']} 18. Nb3 a5 {[15']} 19. dxc5 bxc5 20. Rd1 {[40']} Qc7 {[19']} 21.
h3 Ngf6 22. Bb2 a4 23. Nd2 h6 24. g4 {[40'] Getting moving on the KS before I
do.} Kh7 {[26']} 25. Qg2 a3 26. Ba1 Rb8 {After some thought.} ({If say} 26...
Ne8 27. gxf5 gxf5 28. Nxe4 $1) 27. Rxb8 Qxb8 28. Nb1 Nxg4 {With not much time
left this offered some prespects.} 29. hxg4 Bxa1 30. Nxa3 Bg7 ({If} 30... Qb2 {
(say)} 31. Nb5 Qxa2 32. Nd6) 31. Nb5 Bf8 32. a4 Qb6 33. Qh3 (33. Qh3 Qe6 {[=]}
34. gxf5 gxf5 35. Bb3 Rg7+ 36. Kh2 Qf6 {etc.}) 33... Qe6 {Time was called here
and we agreed a draw. I felt I had the best chances at the end. 2 hours isn't
long enough for a serious game. The Jamboree was won by Lancaster Delta. At
the league Prize giving I was awarded the Silver Bishop for the most
merritorious performnce in the league (7.5/8)} 1/2-1/2

