{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. d4 {[15'] I arrived late.} Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5
e6 4. Nc3 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. e4 g6 7. f4 Bg7 8. Bb5+ Nfd7 {[1']} 9. Bd3 {[16']}
O-O {[12']} 10. Nf3 Re8 11. O-O Na6 12. Nd2 Nc7 13. Qf3 a6 14. a4 Rb8 15. a5 b5
16. axb6 Nxb6 (16... Nxb6 {Threatening......} 17. Z0 Nbxd5 $1 18. exd5 Bd4+ 19.
Kh1 Re3) 17. Kh1 $1 Bb7 18. f5 {Leaves a hole on e5 but White is much stronger
on the KS.} Nd7 19. Nc4 Ne5 20. Nxe5 Bxe5 21. f6 Bc8 22. Ra2 {Protecting the
b-pawn so the Bishop can move.} Nb5 23. Nxb5 axb5 24. Qf2 {[50'] With the
threat of Qh4, Bg5, & Qh6} Bd4 {[1hr 17'] After much thought.} 25. Qh4 {[58']}
Re5 26. g4 Qe8 $6 {After another long think. I now thought for a long time
over 27.Qh6 or Bf4} 27. Qh6 {In view of the variations below I played for a
clear win of the exchange. 27.Qh6 wins the exchange but not the game. Best may
have been say, 27h3 defending the g-Pawn as White doesn't have to rush.} (27.
Bf4 Rxe4 28. Bxd6 Rxg4 29. Qh6 Bxf6 ({or} 29... Rb6 {wins Bishop for two Pawns
but it's unclear.}) 30. Rxf6 Qe1+ 31. Rf1 {wins}) (27. h3 $142) 27... Qf8 28.
Qxf8+ Kxf8 29. Bf4 {Wins the exchange as the Rook can't move.} Bxg4 30. Bxe5
Bxe5 31. Bxb5 g5 32. Kg2 h6 33. b3 Kg8 34. Bc4 Bh5 {What to do? His Bishops
are strong my Pawns are weak.} 35. Rf5 (35. Rf5 {Hoping for....} Bg6 $2 36.
Rxe5 $1 dxe5 37. Kf3 Rb6 38. Ra6 Rxa6 39. Bxa6 Kf8 40. Bb5 $18) 35... Bd4 {
Having none of it} 36. Rf1 Bg6 {An interesting game. (Played at Leeds Y.M.C.A.)
On 18/3/73 I scored 5.5 - 4.5 v Cheshire in a lightning match (all play all v
10 opponents)} 1/2-1/2

