1. b4 e6 2. Bb2 Bxb4 $4 {Losing before getting into second gear.} 3. Bxg7 Qg5 {
Black has a faint hope of losing only the exchange and a pawn.} 4. Bxh8 f6 5.
Nf3 Qg6 6. c3 Bd6 $2 (6... Be7 $142) 7. Qa4 h6 8. e4 Qh7 9. Bxf6 Nxf6 10. e5
Bxe5 11. Nxe5 Qe4+ {11.......Resigns is playable. Why exchange Queens when a
Rook down?} 12. Qxe4 Nxe4 13. d4 d6 14. Ng4 e5 15. Nxh6 exd4 16. cxd4 Bd7 17.
Bd3 Nf6 18. Nc3 Nc6 19. d5 Nb4 20. O-O-O O-O-O 21. Bf5 Rf8 22. Be6 Bxe6 23.
dxe6 Re8 24. Rhe1 c5 25. Rxd6 Kc7 26. Nb5+ Kb8 27. e7 a6 28. Rd8+ {P.Seery won
in both the two previous rounds by default, otherwise he would hardly have
reached the 1/4 finals.} 1-0

