1. e4 e5 2. Bc4 Nf6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nf3 Bc5 5. Bg5 {A bit doubtful} h6 6. Bh4 g5
7. Bg3 Nc6 8. Ne5 {This results in a simplification which leaves Black a clear
Pawn up.} Nxe5 9. Bxe5 Qe7 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 {Threat of 11.......d3} 11. Bd3 d6 12.
Nd2 Be6 13. a3 a5 {Neither of us was willing to commit ourselves to castle on
either side} 14. Qe2 c6 15. h3 Kd7 16. Nf3 b5 (16... Rhe8 $142) 17. e5 Qg7 {
White now made a remark "if one is to die, it's best to die gloriously" and
flamboyantly played........} 18. Bxb5 $4 {Black was winning but desperate
measures were hardly called for} cxb5 19. Qxb5+ Kc7 20. O-O Rhb8 21. Qd3 dxe5
22. b4 Bb6 23. b5 $6 Qg6 24. Qe2 (24. Qxg6 fxg6 25. Nxe5 Kd6 26. Nxg6 Bc4 {etc}
) 24... f6 25. Rfc1 Kb7 26. Nd2 g4 27. Ne4 {Desperation} gxh3 28. g3 Rd8 29.
Nd2 d3 30. cxd3 Qxg3+ {This game was almost a skittles match played under
adverse conditions, no Claock, and my opponent arriving 55' late. Morecambe B
won 6 - 1 (!)} 0-1

