{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3
cxd4 6. axb4 dxc3 7. Qg4 g6 $2 {Leads to a very poor game. If Black is oing to
play this variation he must be willing to let the g-Pawn go.} ({Alternatively.
} 7... Kf8) 8. bxc3 Nc6 9. Nf3 Nge7 10. Bg5 Qc7 {Nasty bu he can't prevent 11.
Bf6} 11. Bf6 Rg8 12. Bb5 Nf5 $2 {Doubtful. Now his King and Rook (g) are left
immobile.} ({He must try for} 12... Bd7 13. Z0 O-O-O) 13. Nd4 $1 {Eliminating
his (f) Knight and straightening out my Pawns.} Nfxd4 (13... Bd7 $142) 14. cxd4
Qb6 15. Bxc6+ Qxc6 16. O-O Bd7 ({He can hardly risk...} 16... Qxc2 17. Rfc1 {
etc.}) 17. Qh3 {[17']} h5 {[24']} 18. c3 b6 19. Ra3 {Intending to double on
the a-file.} a5 $6 {Opening up the QS but he is virtually a Rook down.} 20. Qe3
{With thoughts of invading via h6 & h7 if nothing happens on the QS.} axb4 {
[28'] He's commited now, but the opening of the position proves fatal.} 21.
cxb4 {[23']} Rc8 22. Ra7 Rc7 23. Qa3 {Threatening 24.b5 winning the Queen.} b5
24. Qa5 Rc8 25. h4 {Discouraging ......g5 and eliminating back-rank mate
threats.} Qc4 {[42']} 26. Bg5 $1 {[35'] Now 27.Rc1 is threatened and Black may
as well resign.} Qxd4 {[46'] What else?} 27. Rc7 {[40']} ({Not} 27. Rxd7 $2
Kxd7 28. Qxb5+ Rc6 {& draws. White was threatening mate in 2 on d8.}) 27... Rb8
{[49']} 28. Rfc1 {[43'] The end. Black decides to play it out for a few moves.}
Qc4 29. R1xc4 dxc4 30. Qa7 Rd8 31. Qc5 f6 32. exf6 Rg7 33. fxg7 Kf7 34. Rxd7+
Kg8 35. Rxd8+ {4 Lancaster lost the match 3 -} 1-0

