{Time limit 24mph} 1. d4 f5 2. e4 fxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f3 exf3 5. Nxf3 e6 6. Bg5
Be7 7. Qd2 d5 $6 {I don't like this. It leaves a hole at e5 and his e-Pawn is
weak.} 8. O-O-O Nc6 ({I had been more concerned about..} 8... c5) 9. Re1 a6 10.
h4 ({If} 10. Bd3 Nb4 {is a nuisance.}) 10... h6 $6 {This time leaving a hole
on g6.} 11. Bf4 Bd6 12. Bd3 Ne7 13. Be5 {Maintaining my hold on e5 and keeping
him cramped.} O-O 14. Bxf6 {Initiating a KS advance.} Rxf6 15. Ne5 {Still
blocking his e-Pawn and preventing 15.......Bf4} Nf5 {Trying to get some
air-space but White is too far up in development.} 16. Bxf5 Rxf5 17. g4 Rf8 18.
g5 Bxe5 {Trying to eliminate my attacking pieces.} 19. Rxe5 h5 {Trying to keep
it blocked but to no avail.} 20. g6 {Putting the squeeze on.} Rf5 ({If} 20...
Rf6 21. Qg5) 21. Rxf5 exf5 22. Qe2 {Putting Black in a quandry.} c6 ({If} 22...
Qf6 23. Nxd5) 23. Qxh5 Be6 24. Re1 Qf6 25. Na4 $1 {aiming for c5 is possible
as Black has no perpetual check after 25.......Qxd4?} ({Not} 25. Ne2 f4 $1)
25... Re8 (25... Qxd4 $2 26. Rxe6 Qf4+ 27. Kd1 Qd4+ 28. Ke2 Qc4+ 29. Ke1 $1
Qb4+ 30. Nc3 $18) 26. Nc5 b6 27. Nd7 $3 {Rather a surprise for Black. A crowd
of spectators now gathered in time for....Resigns.} ({Black decides he has a
draw after} 27. Nxe6) ({or} 27. Nxa6 {However the Knight was headed elseqhere.}
) 1-0

