{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3
cxd4 6. Qxd4 Nc6 7. Bb5 Bxc3+ 8. Qxc3 {[3']} Nge7 {[4']} 9. Ne2 {[8']} Bd7 {
[4'] Deviating from outr last game where I played 9.......Qc7. On refelction I
prefer......} ({....} 9... Qc7) 10. Bxc6 Bxc6 11. O-O Nf5 12. Nd4 {White
happily simplifies down. For my part I was happy to draw as I would have White
in the replay.} Nxd4 13. Qxd4 Qc7 14. f4 Bb5 {[15']} 15. Rf2 {[25']} g6 {
[18'] Preventing 16.f5. The holes left are not too serious as I wasn't
contemplating KS castling.} 16. Be3 b6 17. Qb4 Qc4 18. Qxc4 {[47']} Bxc4 {[27']
} 19. b3 Ba6 20. c4 $6 {Possibly White felt that he had to make an effort to
win rather than let it drag out as a draw with a replay with the Black pieces.
This move gives up a Pawn for open lines. White must have thought I couldn't
possibly hold onto the Pawn anyway.} dxc4 21. bxc4 Bxc4 22. Rc2 b5 ({If} 22...
Bd5 23. Rc7 {gives him good play.}) 23. Bc5 ({If} 23. a4 a6 {hold for Black.
The move played has the disadvantage of blocking the c-file for White. it
prevents castling but the King isn't going that way.}) 23... Kd7 $1 {Linking
the Rooks and preparing for the endgame.} 24. a4 Rhc8 {[52']} 25. Be3 {[67]
Keeping the d-file open.} a6 {[53']} 26. axb5 {[72']} axb5 27. Rac1 Kc6 28. Rd2
{[57' 30s]} Rd8 {[60']} 29. Rcd1 Rxd2 30. Rxd2 Ra1+ $2 {Probably not the best.
The exchange of Rooks which I force leads to a draw. I should probably have
kept Rooks on.} 31. Kf2 Ra2 32. Ke1 Rxd2 33. Kxd2 b4 {It's a dead draw but we
manoeuvered about a bit.} 34. Bd4 Kd5 35. Ke3 h5 36. g3 Bf1 37. Bb2 Kc4 38. Kd2
Bg2 39. Kc2 Be4+ 40. Kd2 Bf5 41. Ba1 Kc5 42. Ke3 Kd5 43. Bb2 Kc6 44. Bd4 Kb5
45. Kd2 b3 46. Ke3 ({and not} 46. Kc1 $2 Kc4 47. Bb2 Kd3 48. Kd1 Bg4+ {etc.})
46... Kb4 47. Bb2 Kc4 48. Bd4 1/2-1/2

