1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. Qg4 Ne7 6. a3 Qa5 $6 {Making it
interesting.} 7. axb4 $6 ({The alternative was.} 7. Bd2) 7... Qxa1 8. Kd1 Bd7 {
Else 9.Nb5; 10.Nd6+} 9. bxc5 Nf5 10. Bd3 h5 11. Qf4 {At this stage I was on
holiday and arrived back to find a pile of games waiting. I foolishly tried to
catch the post with all the games, and without looking at the games properly I
chose all my moves. Thus......} a6 $4 (11... g6 {is OK.}) 12. Bxf5 exf5 13.
Nxd5 Bc6 ({If} 13... Ra7 14. e6 {wins}) (13... Qa5 14. Nb6 Ra7 15. e6 {wins}) (
13... O-O {and I'll be murdered on the KS.}) 14. Nc7+ {Not enough time spent
on the moves. One must expect bad losses if moves are often played without
even setting the board up.} 1-0

