1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 Bd7 $2 {Loses a Pawn.} 6. Bxf6
Bxf6 7. cxd5 exd5 8. Nxd5 O-O 9. Nf3 Re8 10. Bc4 Be6 11. Qb3 b6 12. Rc1 Nc6 13.
Nxf6+ {Deciding to sacrifice the Queen for a variety of material.} Qxf6 14. d5
Na5 15. dxe6 Nxb3 16. exf7+ Kf8 17. fxe8=Q+ Rxe8 18. axb3 $1 Qxb2 19. O-O a6 $2
{Black now manages to lose his only hope, his QS Pawns.} 20. Bxa6 Qxb3 21. Rxc7
{Now he's in real bother as I can easily hold the b-Pawn, and I get all sorts
of chances in the middle.} Qa3 {I threatened 22.Bc4+ winning the Queen.} 22.
Bc4 Rb8 $2 (22... Qc3 $142) 23. Rf7+ Ke8 24. Rxg7 Rd8 25. Bb5+ Kf8 26. Rxh7 Qd6
27. Rh8+ Kg7 28. Rxd8 Qxd8 29. Nd4 Kf6 30. Rc1 Qa8 31. Rc6+ Ke5 {I think he
was hoping to get his King in a stalemate position then sacrifice his Queen.}
32. Rxb6 Qa2 33. h4 Kd5 34. h5 Ke5 35. h6 Kd5 36. Bc6+ {so as to be able to
play 37.h7 next move.} Ke5 37. h7 Qa8 {Still trying for a stalemate!} 38. f4+
Kf6 39. Bxa8+ Kg7 40. Be4 {Easy but interesting.} 1-0

