Bxg6 hxg6 9. Bf4 e6 10. Qe2 Nd5 11. Bd2 Bd6 12. O-O-O Qb6 13. a3 $6 {Weakening
the Qs rather.} c5 14. Bg5 ({If} 14. c4 {then} Nf4 ({and not} 14... N5f6 15. d5
) ({or} 14... Ne7 15. d5)) 14... cxd4 {With various ideas on the QS.} 15. Nxd4
Bc5 16. Nb3 {Threatening 17.RxN} (16. c3 Bxa3 17. bxa3 Nxc3 18. Qb2 Qa5 $1 19.
Rd2 Rc8) 16... N7f6 ({If} 16... Ne7 17. Ne4) 17. Ne4 Be7 18. Bxf6 gxf6 19. Rhe1
$6 {Interesting. He gives up a Pawn to open and gain control of the h-file.}
Rxh2 20. Rh1 Rxh1 21. Rxh1 O-O-O 22. Rh7 {Attacking the f-Pawn but he doesn't
gat a spare move to take it.} f5 23. Qc4+ Kb8 24. Nec5 Qc7 25. Kb1 ({Not} 25.
Rxf7 $4 Bg5+) 25... Ka8 {Threatening 26......b6} 26. Qb5 a6 27. Qc4 {Suicide.
he is lost but......} ({......} 27. Nxa6 {offers some chances.}) 27... b5 {
Not a bad game with a different opening to my usual repertoire.} 0-1

