1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 d5 5. exd5 Na5 6. Bb5+ c6 7. dxc6 bxc6 8.
Qf3 {I hadn't seen this before. Without consulting M.C.O. I sent back........}
e4 $2 {Makes it very interesting but not to be recommended in a correspondence
match. I was playing too casually.} 9. Nxe4 Qe7 10. Bd3 {I had missed this on
move 8! I'm sure I wouldn't have missed it over the board but had not bothered
to set up the pieces on that move..} Bg4 11. Qf4 Qe6 12. O-O Nd5 13. Qg3 f5 {
I et enough play to maybe justify my 8th move were it "over the board"} 14. Re1
({If} 14. Nec3 {then} Bd6 {and if} 15. f4 ({or} 15. Qh4 g5 $1 16. Qxg5 Rg8)
15... Nxf4 $1 16. Rxf4 g5) 14... Kd8 ({The alternative was....} 14... O-O-O 15.
Ba6+ Nb7 16. h3) 15. f3 Bh5 $1 {After much thought and the only move worth
playing.} 16. Ng5 ({If} 16. Qh4+ Be7 17. Qxh5 $4 Nf4 {wins the Queen.}) 16...
Qd7 17. Ne6+ Kc8 18. Bxf5 {Help!} Bg6 {I might as well resign.} 19. Nxf8 Qxf5
20. Nxg6 hxg6 21. Qg4 Qxg4 22. fxg4 Nb4 23. Na3 Nc4 24. Re6 Kd7 25. Rxg6 Nxa3
26. Rxg7+ Kd6 27. bxa3 Nxc2 28. Rb1 Rhe8 29. d4 Nxd4 30. Bf4+ Kd5 31. Rd7+ Ke4
32. Re1+ Kxf4 33. Rxd4+ Kg5 34. Rc1 Re6 35. Rc5+ Kg6 36. Ra4 Rf8 {Threatening
mate no less!} 37. h4 Rf7 38. Ra6 Rc7 39. Rca5 Ree7 40. Rd5 Re6 {No Reply!} 0-1

