1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 g6 5. c4 Bg7 6. Be3 Nf6 7. Nc3 Ng4 8.
Qxg4 Nxd4 9. Qd1 e5 10. Bd3 O-O 11. O-O d6 12. Qd2 {Following Geller v Barczay
Sousse IZ 1967 [M.C.O.11 P 173 Col 110]} f5 {Aggressive.} ({Geller v Barczay
went....} 12... Be6 13. Rfd1 Qh4 14. Ne2 Nxe2+ 15. Qxe2 $16) 13. Bxd4 exd4 14.
Nd5 f4 15. f3 ({If now} 15. Nxf4 Bh6 16. g3 Bxf4 17. gxf4 Qh4 $17) 15... Be5
16. Rac1 Be6 17. b4 b6 18. Rc2 Rc8 19. Rfc1 Kh8 {So as after exchanges
resulting from c5, to able to capture on d5 without Bc4 pinning anything.} 20.
Qf2 {A bit lost for a plan.} Rf7 {Negates his previous move.} 21. c5 dxc5 22.
bxc5 Bxd5 23. exd5 Rfc7 24. cxb6 Rxc2 25. Rxc2 Rc3 26. b7 Qxd5 $2 ({Correct was
} 26... Rxd3 27. Qe2 Re3 $1 (27... Rc3 $4 28. Qxe5+ $18)) 27. Qe2 Rxc2 28. Bxc2
Kg7 29. Qe4 Qc5 30. Kh1 Kf6 31. h4 Qc3 $4 32. Qxe5+ {No reply!} (32. Qxe5+ {
it might have gone} Kxe5 33. b8=Q+ Ke6 {seems best} 34. Bb3+ Kf5 35. Qb5+ Kf6
36. Qg5+ Kg7 37. Qxf4 {and say} d3 38. Qf7+ Kh6 39. Qf4+ Kh5 40. Qc4 $18) *

