{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 d6 5. Nc3
Nf6 6. Bc4 e6 7. Be3 g6 (7... Be7 {May be better.}) 8. f3 Bg7 9. Qd2 O-O 10.
O-O-O d5 {Sfter much thought. White threatened to win the d-Pawn.} 11. exd5
Nxd5 12. Nxd5 exd5 {[18']} 13. Bb3 {[20']} Be6 {[28']} 14. h4 {The most
aggressive course.} Na5 {[29']} 15. h5 {[29']} Nxb3+ {[34']} 16. axb3 {[30']}
Qf6 17. g4 {After some consideration. I wasn't too happy about weakening the
f-Pawn. The move played prevents 17......Bf5and allows the Queen to go to h2.}
Rfe8 18. c3 Rac8 19. Rh3 {[53'] Again after much thought. The Rook gaurds the
f-Pawn allowing the Knight to move. Also the possibility of doubling or
trebling on the h-file.} Qe7 {[63']} 20. hxg6 {[55']} fxg6 $6 {[65'] The
obvious move but leading to the loss of the d-Pawn.} 21. Bg5 {[58']} Qc5 {[77']
} 22. Nxe6 Rxe6 {[82'] What did he spend 5' thining about?} 23. Qxd5 {[63']}
Qxd5 24. Rxd5 Rec6 {[87'] This proves to be a poor file for his Rooks} 25. f4 {
[66']} Rc5 26. Rd7 R5c7 27. Rhd3 a6 28. Bd8 $1 {A very useful move restricting
his Rooks.} Rxd7 29. Rxd7 b5 30. Bc7 h6 31. c4 Bf8 32. Kd2 {[86']} Bb4+ {[105']
} 33. Kd3 {[86']} Re8 {[106']} 34. Bd6 {[90']} bxc4+ 35. bxc4 Re1 $4 {Short of
time he blunders. White had a straighforward win though, the c-Pawn marching
through .} (35... Re1 $4 36. Bxb4 {If} Rd1+ 37. Bd2) 36. Bxb4 1-0

