{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. Nf3 d5 3. exd5 exd5 4. d4 Bd6 5. Nc3
c6 6. a3 {I couldn't see the point of this.} Bg4 7. Be2 Nd7 8. Qd3 Ne7 9. Qe3 {
Rather artificial manoeuvering.} O-O 10. Ne5 Bxe2 11. Nxe2 Nb6 12. b3 Qc7 13.
Nf3 {White is making no progress and Black has gained the initiative.} Rfe8 14.
Qd3 Ng6 15. g3 Re7 {Control of the e-file secures Black a lasting advantage.}
16. h4 $6 {Aggressive but rather risky with his King in the centre.} Rae8 {
Rather embarassing for White.} 17. Be3 {As good as anything. There is no good
move.} Bxg3 $1 {Taking advantage of the e-file pressure.} 18. Kf1 Nf4 19. Bxf4
Bxf4 20. Re1 Re4 $6 {OK as it turns out but I hadn't realised the strength of
his reply.} 21. Ng5 {Threatening 22.f3. My reply is forced.} Bxg5 22. hxg5 f5 {
The only move White still threatened f3} 23. gxf6 ({The alternative was} 23. f3
) 23... gxf6 24. Kg2 Qg7+ 25. Kf1 Kh8 26. Rg1 Qh6 27. Qf3 Nc8 28. Rg4 Rxg4 29.
Qxg4 Nd6 30. Ng3 Rxe1+ 31. Kxe1 Qc1+ {My object is to collect another Pawn
then exchange Queens.} 32. Ke2 Qxc2+ 33. Kf3 Qd1+ 34. Ne2 Qd3+ 35. Kg2 Qg6 36.
Kg3 $2 Ne4+ 37. Kf4 Qxg4+ 38. Kxg4 Nxf2+ 39. Kf5 Ne4 40. Nf4 Kg7 41. Ne6+ Kf7
42. Nd8+ Ke7 43. Nxb7 Nd6+ 44. Nxd6 Kxd6 45. Kxf6 c5 {I was now lying in 3rd= 
(out of 134) behind Ely and P.Littlewood.} 0-1

