{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Nxd5 4. Nf3 Bg4 5. Be2
e6 6. O-O Be7 7. Ne5 Bxe2 8. Qxe2 c6 9. c4 Nf6 10. Be3 O-O 11. Nc3 {White has
won the opening.} Nbd7 {[31']} 12. Rad1 {[33']} Nb6 {[36']} 13. f4 {[36']} Qc7
{[44']} 14. b3 {[49'] Supporting the c-Pawn; but I was already using up a lot
of time. I was worried that Black can now play 14.......a4-a5} Rad8 {[47']} 15.
Ng4 {[51']} Nxg4 16. Qxg4 Nd7 {[50']} 17. Qf3 {[59'] I feel I missed the best
line around here.} Nf6 {[55']} 18. Ne4 {[61']} Nxe4 {[66']} 19. Qxe4 Bf6 20. g4
{[74']} g6 {[70']} 21. Qf3 Rd7 22. f5 exf5 23. gxf5 Bg7 $6 24. f6 $6 {
Naturally, but it leadsto problems.} Bh8 25. Rf2 $2 {My problem is that the e
& f Pawns need protection. I would like to manoeuvre the Bishop to e5. I
didn't play 25.Bf4 because of 25......Qa5 attacking the a-pawn. However this
was probably best.} (25. Bf4 Qa5 26. Be5 Qxa2 27. Ra1 {etc. After Blacks reply
to 25.Rf2 I was in a quandry.}) 25... Re8 {As time was short I played a 'safe'
move.} 26. Bg5 $2 {[90'] Missing his 28th move.} ({If now} 26. Bf4 Qd8 {
and I can't play} 27. Be5 {because of} Rxe5) 26... Qd8 27. Re2 $2 {Still
missing his 28th} Rxe2 28. Qxe2 h6 29. Bxh6 Bxf6 30. Be3 Bxd4 31. Rxd4 Rxd4 32.
Bxd4 Qxd4+ {[90']} 33. Kg2 {[102']} Qd7 34. Kh1 f5 35. Kg2 Kf7 36. Kh1 Qe7 37.
Qf2 b6 38. Qd2 g5 39. Kg1 Kg6 {[106']} 40. Kf2 {[114']} Qe6 41. Kf1 c5 42. Qd8
f4 43. h4 $2 {Rushing still with only minutes left.} Qh3+ 44. Kg1 Qxh4 45. Qe8+
Kf5 46. Qf8+ Ke5 47. Qe7+ Kd4 48. Qd6+ Ke3 49. Qe6+ Kf3 (49... Kf3 $4 50. Qd5+
Kg3 $4 51. Qg2#) 50. Qd5+ {Here the controller stopped play! (see above
variation) Adjudicated lost. Fuzzy thinking around moves 25 - 27 and a time
rush error on move 43.} 0-1

