{Time limit 1hr each} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 Qb6 6. Bd3
Bd7 7. O-O cxd4 8. cxd4 Nxd4 9. Nxd4 Qxd4 10. Nc3 a6 {[30s] Having played this
variation a few weeks ago at Preston I gained a big time advantage out of the
opening: important in a "1hr for all your moves" game.} 11. Be3 $2 {[10']
Doubtful.} (11. Re1 $142) 11... Qxe5 {[1']} 12. Re1 {[13']} Qd6 {[6']} ({Not} 
12... Qb8 $2 13. Nxd5) (12... Bb4 {Was an alternative.}) 13. Bd4 {[16'] Best}
Bc6 {[8']} 14. Rc1 Nf6 {[9']} 15. Na4 $2 {[34'] Starting to get well behind on
time he tries to start some action.} Qb4 $1 {[14'] White had missed this.} 16.
Nb6 $6 {[42']} (16. Bxf6 {Was the alternative.}) 16... Rd8 {[15']} 17. Bxf6 {
[51']} gxf6 {[16'] Simply in terms of time he hasn't a hope.} 18. Qh5 {
Threatening 19.Rxe6+} Ke7 $1 {[24'] Simplest} 19. Bg6 {[57'] Desperation now.
He must lose on time.} fxg6 20. Qh3 e5 {[29']} 21. Qg3 Bg7 {[31']} 22. Qe3 d4 {
White lost on time.} 0-1

