1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7. d5 e6 8. Be2 a6
9. O-O exd5 10. exd5 Re8 11. Bd3 Bg4 {Eliminating his Bishop but giving me
play on the KS} 12. h3 Bxf3 13. Qxf3 Nbd7 14. g4 Qc7 15. h4 $2 {Rather
overestimating my position.} (15. a4 $142) 15... b5 $1 {Securing good play for
Black on the QS.} 16. g5 Nh5 17. Kh2 $2 ({If} 17. cxb5 c4 18. Be4 axb5 {
is good for Black.}) (17. Kg2 $142) 17... bxc4 18. Bxc4 Re7 19. Bd2 Qb7 20. b3
Rae8 21. Rae1 $2 {Leads to problems.} Rxe1 22. Rxe1 Rxe1 23. Bxe1 Nb6 $2 {
I now realised that Black could have played...} (23... Nxf4 24. Bg3 Bxc3 {
Fortunately he missed it too.}) 24. Qe4 Kf8 25. Ne2 f5 26. Qe6 Nxc4 27. bxc4
Qe7 28. Qxe7+ {Uninspiring stuff. rather poor play by both of us. [The match
was played at Altrincham Grammar School]} 1/2-1/2

