1. d4 f5 2. f4 {Unusual, but possibly leading to a sort of Stonewall set-up.}
b6 3. e3 Bb7 4. Nd2 Nf6 5. Ngf3 e6 6. Bd3 d6 7. Qe2 Be7 8. Bc4 Nd5 9. a3 Bh4+
10. g3 {Weakening the long diagonal.} ({Alternatively} 10. Nxh4 Qxh4+ 11. Qf2
$2 Nxe3 $1) 10... Bf6 11. Bb5+ ({Rather better seems.} 11. e4) 11... c6 12. Bd3
Nd7 13. Nc4 Qe7 14. Ng5 $6 {Leads to trouble. 14.e5 was still best.} c5 {
Taking advantage of opening the long diagonal.} 15. e4 Nc7 {Leaving him rather
delicately placed in the centre.} 16. O-O $2 {Now he's lost.} ({Rather better
was} 16. dxc5 {but Black would still hope to win.}) 16... Bxd4+ 17. Kh1 d5 18.
Ne5 Nxe5 $6 {Possibly a mistake opening the f-file. I simply assumed that I
would win easily after winning his QBishop.} 19. fxe5 c4 $2 (19... dxe4 {
would be safest. However, I now became overconfident and began to play too
rapidly - my usual problem.}) 20. exf5 {Now I'm in a bit of bother but still
didn't realise it, playing my next move very quickly.} cxd3 $4 {After which
I'm probably lost.} (20... O-O-O {is possibly best.}) 21. Qh5+ {I now started
worrying.} Kd7 22. fxe6+ Kc6 23. c3 Bxe5 ({It's possible that} 23... Bxc3 {
was best here.}) 24. Rf7 ({I had expected} 24. Nf7 Bf6) 24... Qe8 25. c4 Kc5 {
I couldn't find a better move.} ({Neither} 25... dxc4) ({nor} 25... Nxe6 {
are any good.}) ({maybe} 25... Rd8) 26. Ne4+ {Again best.} Kd4 {With very
little hope left.} 27. Be3+ (27. b3 {5 is mate in}) 27... Kxe3 28. Qxe5 dxe4 {
Much the same as resigning, I felt.} 29. Qf4+ $4 {Missing a mate in two. Here
I offered a draw and he agreed. White must surely have a win. Exit Black much
relieved. Horrific!! Inefficient use of the clock at the crucial part of the
game. I must try to tae my time better.} (29. Re1+ Kd2 30. Qc3#) (29. Qf4+ Kd4
30. Qd6+ (30. Qxc7 Rd8 31. Qxb7 Qxe6 32. Re7 Qf5 33. Qxa7 Rd6 {Added by Dick
years later with Fritz. -0.46!}) 30... Nd5 31. Rxb7 ({or} 31. cxd5)) 1/2-1/2

