{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Nxd5 4. Nf3 Bg4 5.
Be2 e6 6. O-O Be7 7. h3 {varying from my game v Bennet a few weeks ago where I
played 7.Ne5} Bf5 8. a3 O-O 9. c4 Nf6 10. Be3 Nbd7 11. Nc3 Ne4 12. Nxe4 Bxe4
13. Nd2 Bg6 ({Not} 13... Bc6 {impeding his c-Pawn.}) 14. f4 c5 15. Nb3 ({If} 
15. d5 exd5 16. f5 d4) 15... cxd4 16. Bxd4 Be4 17. Bf3 Bxf3 18. Qxf3 Qc7 19.
Rac1 Bf6 20. Kh1 Bxd4 21. Nxd4 Rad8 (21... Rfd8 $142) 22. Qe3 e5 $6 {Leading
to problems.} 23. Nb5 exf4 24. Qxa7 Qc6 25. Qf2 Nc5 26. Qf3 Qxf3 27. Rxf3 Rd2
28. b4 Nd3 29. Rcf1 $2 {Throwing away a probable win by cramping the other
Rook.} (29. Rb1 $142) 29... g5 30. Nc3 $2 (30. Rb1 {Was still on.}) 30... Ne5
31. R3f2 Rxf2 32. Rxf2 Nxc4 33. Ne4 h6 34. a4 f5 35. Nc5 b6 36. Nd7 Rd8 {
At this stage all the other games had finished with Lancaster leading 3.5 - 2.
5. Thus Black had to win to draw the match.} 37. Rc2 Ne3 38. Rc7 {Threatening
to draw by 39.Nf6+} Nd5 39. Rb7 g4 40. hxg4 fxg4 41. Kh2 h5 42. a5 bxa5 43.
bxa5 Rc8 44. Rb8 {Draws!} Rxb8 45. Nxb8 Kf7 46. a6 Nb6 47. a7 Ke6 48. Nc6 {
Adjourned. The game resumed on 14/11/73} Kf5 {[Sealed]} 49. Nd4+ Ke4 50. Ne6
Kf5 ({He can't win. e.g.} 50... f3 51. Ng5+ Ke3 52. Nxf3 $1) 51. Nd4+ Kg5 52.
Ne6+ {3 Lancaster won the match 4 -} 1/2-1/2

