{Time limit 20mph} 1. f4 {Hoping to surprise him as I know he would have been
preparing defences. My other problem was that I started this game assuming
that my arranged game with G.Leigh would not continue, however, Mr.Leigh
declined to resign so I was playing two games simultaneously!} d5 2. Nf3 c5 3.
g3 Nc6 4. Bg2 g6 5. O-O Bg7 6. d3 Nf6 7. Nbd2 $2 {A very doubtful move leading
to trouble. Had I not been jumping backwards and forwards from one table to
the other I doubt whether I would have played this.} Ng4 8. Nb3 $6 {Another
doubtful move.} (8. Nb1 $142) 8... Qb6 {Very strong, threatening to win the
night.} 9. c4 dxc4 10. dxc4 Be6 {Now I'm in dire straights. However, Mr.Leigh
resigned here so now I could concentrate on this game! was it too late?} 11. h3
Rd8 12. Qe1 ({If} 12. Qc2 Nb4 13. Qb1 {may be just playable but I didn't like
it.}) 12... Nh6 13. Qf2 {As my c-Pawn is indefensible I attack his} Bd4 $2 {
Much to my satisfaction. I can now solve most of my problems.} ({I was much
more worried about.} 13... Bxc4) 14. Nfxd4 Nxd4 ({Not} 14... cxd4 15. c5) 15.
Nxd4 cxd4 ({If} 15... Rxd4 16. b3 Z0 17. Be3) 16. b3 {Now his d-Pawn gives him
problems.} Nf5 17. Rd1 O-O $2 {Now he'll have trouble saving the d-Pawn. Maybe
best was the imediate...} ({....} 17... Ne3) 18. Rd3 Rd7 19. g4 Ne3 {
Appraoching the time control with only a few mins left he decides to give up a
Pawn in the hope that he will get compensation by controlling the d-file. In
any effect the d-pawn is lost after...} ({...} 19... Ng7 20. Bb2 {followed by..
..} Z0 21. Rad1) ({If} 19... Nh6 $2 20. f5) 20. Bxe3 dxe3 21. Qxe3 Qxe3+ 22.
Rxe3 Rfd8 23. Be4 {So as to close the d-file with 24.Bd3} f5 24. Bd3 Kf7 25.
Rg3 Rd4 26. Rf1 Bc8 27. Rff3 b6 28. gxf5 Bxf5 29. Bxf5 gxf5 30. Rd3 Kf6 31.
Rgf3 e5 32. fxe5+ Kxe5 33. Kf2 R8d7 34. Rfe3+ Kf6 35. Kf3 h6 {[1hr 35'] The
game was now adjourned. I sealed.} 36. Rxd4 {[1hr 15'] The game resumed 30/11/
73} Rxd4 {I thought} 37. Re8 {gave a better chance as...} ({During the
adjournment I looked at.} 37. Rd3 {He can't reply} Rxd3+ ({However} 37... Rh4
38. Kg3 Re4 39. e3 {and I can make no progress as Black can tie up the QS by...
.} a5 $1) 38. exd3 Ke5 {as} 39. b4 {wins}) 37... Rd2 38. a4 Rb2 39. Re3 {
and Black's Rook is out of play.} Rd2 40. Rd3 Rb2 (40... Rxd3+ 41. exd3 Ke5 42.
b4 {wins}) 41. e4 {Eliminating my e-Pawn which is a bit of a liability.} fxe4+
42. Kxe4 Ke6 {To prevent 43.Kd5} 43. Kd4 Rf2 44. Rg3 Rf4+ 45. Kc3 Kf7 46. Kb4
Rf5 {Preventing 47.Kb5 so a new plan is needed.} 47. Kc3 Rf4 48. b4 Rh4 49. a5
bxa5 {I would have preffered not to have given White a passed Pawn had I been
Black.} 50. bxa5 a6 51. Rd3 Ke7 52. Kb3 Re4 {[2hrs 25']} 53. Kb4 {[1hr 50']}
Re5 54. Rd4 (54. c5 {is very loosening.}) 54... Rh5 {[2hrs 35'] [1hr 54']} 55.
h4 Re5 56. Rd5 $1 {Slow forward progress!} Re6 {[2hrs 39'] A good post for the
Rook defending along the 3rd rank.} ({If now} 56... Rxd5 $2 57. cxd5 Kd6 58.
Kc4 h5 59. Kd4 Kd7 60. Kc5 Kc7 61. d6+ Kd7 62. Kd5 Kd8 63. Kc6 Kc8 64. Kb6 {
wins!}) 57. Kc3 {[2hrs 9'] The alternatives offer little.} (57. Kc5) (57. c5)
57... Rg6 58. h5 Rf6 {[2hrs 45']} 59. Kd3 {[2hrs 16']} Ke6 {[2hrs 53']} 60. Kd4
{[2hrs 18']} Ke7 {[2hrs 58']} 61. Kc5 {The difference c.f.move 57 is that
after Black's reply I have gained a move.} Re6 62. Rf5 $1 {This and the next
two moves seem the best way to make progress.} Kd7 63. Rf7+ Ke8 64. Rh7 $1 {
Confining his King to the back rank and keeping an eye on his h-Pawn and
threatening to force the c-Pawn through.} Kd8 ({If} 64... Re5+ 65. Kb6 Rxh5 66.
c5 $1 {wins}) 65. Kd5 Rf6 66. Ke5 Rc6 67. c5 $1 {Still pushing forwards.} Kc8 (
{If} 67... Rxc5+ $4 68. Kd6 {wins.}) 68. Rh8+ Kc7 69. Kd5 Rf6 ({If} 69... Kb7
70. Rb8+) 70. Rh7+ Kb8 71. c6 {Adjourned. White has a win in all variations 
[He sealed.]} Rf1 {The game resumed 1/12/73} ({If} 71... Rf5+ 72. Kd6 Rf6+ 73.
Kc5 Rf5+ 74. Kb6 {etc}) 72. Rxh6 Rd1+ 73. Kc5 Rb1 74. Rh7 Ka8 {Black's hope is
to stalemate his King and commit suicide with his Rook.} 75. Rh8+ {With
thoughts of 75......Ka7 76.c7} Ka7 76. Rh7+ ({I now realised that} 76. c7 {
is no good} Rc1+ 77. Kd6 {and now not} Rxc7 $4 ({but} 77... Rc6+ $3 78. Kd7
Rxc7+ {and draws. So.....a change of plan.}) 78. Ra8+ {and wins.}) 76... Ka8
77. h6 Rb5+ 78. Kd6 Rb1 79. Rd7 {My King wants to escape the checks by hiding
behind the Rook!} Rd1+ 80. Kc7 Rh1 81. h7 Ka7 ({I thought he might try.} 81...
Rh6 {hoping for} 82. Rd8+ Ka7 83. h8=Q $4 Rxh8 84. Rxh8 {Stalemate.}) 82. Kd8+
Ka8 83. c7 Rc1 84. h8=Q (84. c8=Q+ Rxc8+ $1) 84... Rxc7 85. Kxc7+ {A very good
game. Total time ~7hrs} 1-0

