{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. d4 Nf6 2. e3 c5 3. c3 d6 4. dxc5 dxc5 5.
Qxd8+ {White was obviously playing for a draw from the start.} Kxd8 6. Bc4 {
[4']} e6 {[4']} 7. Nf3 Bd6 8. Nbd2 a6 9. Bb3 (9. a4 $142 {White seemed
frightened of advancing anything. Possibly because my record against him is 7/
7.}) 9... b5 {[5']} 10. c4 Bb7 11. Bc2 Nbd7 12. b3 Ke7 13. Bb2 {[11']} h6 {
[12']} 14. Bd3 Rhb8 15. O-O Bc6 16. Rfe1 {I felt that his best move was 16.e4
17.e5. My next move prevents this.} Ng4 17. h3 {[15'] White was playing very
quickly, presumably assuming that he just had to swap off pieces for his half
point.} (17. Bxg7 Rg8 {is clearly good for Black.}) 17... Nge5 {[19']} 18. Nxe5
Bxe5 (18... Nxe5 {I didn't like} 19. Be4) 19. Bxe5 Nxe5 20. Bf1 $2 {Doubtful.}
(20. Be4 $142) 20... Rd8 21. Rad1 Nd3 22. Bxd3 Rxd3 23. Nf3 Be4 $1 {Keeping
the initiative.} 24. Rxd3 ({If} 24. Ne5 Rxd1 25. Rxd1 Kf6) 24... Bxd3 25. Rd1
bxc4 $1 {Seems to win} 26. bxc4 {Accepting the loss of a Pawn. I expected
something like.....} ({......} 26. Ne5 Bc2 27. Rd7+ Ke8 28. Rxf7 cxb3 29. axb3
Bxb3 30. Rxg7 Kf8 {etc. and Black should win.}) 26... Bxc4 27. Rd2 {[25']} Bd5
{[50'] He was still playing twice as fast as me.} 28. Ne5 Ra7 {White looked at
the board and in a flash played.} 29. Rxd5 $4 {Leading to a hopeless endgame.}
exd5 30. Nc6+ Kd7 31. Nxa7 Kc7 {Now he saw it!} 32. f4 f5 33. g4 fxg4 34. hxg4
Kb7 35. Kf1 Kxa7 36. Ke2 Kb6 37. Kd3 Kb5 38. Kc3 {[35']} Ka4 {[59']} 39. Kb2
Kb4 40. a3+ Kc4 41. Kc2 a5 42. f5 a4 {It takes two to make a draw!} 0-1

