{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. d4 e6 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nc3 Bb4 {I don't know why
I played this as I'm better versed in the Modern Benoni} 4. a3 Bxc3+ 5. bxc3 c5
({I wasn't well versed in this opening and} 5... d5 {is more usual.}) 6. f3 ({
M.C.O.11 gives only} 6. e3) 6... Qa5 (6... d5 {may be sounder}) 7. Bd2 d6 8. e4
e5 {I was already feeling a bit lost. Also having gone to bed at 3 a.m. last
night I kept "falling asleep."} 9. Bd3 Qc7 10. Ne2 Nc6 11. Be3 cxd4 $6 {
Hoping to simplify but it just opens up the position for his bishops.} 12. cxd4
exd4 13. Nxd4 Nxd4 14. Bxd4 Qe7 {Not a good square for the Queen as it turns
out.} 15. O-O O-O 16. Re1 Be6 17. Rc1 {Threatening 18.c5. Things are very
difficult for Black now.} Nd7 18. f4 Nc5 ({Possibly better is} 18... f6 {
but I was worried about} 19. Qh5) 19. Bb1 b6 $2 {Probably wasting a valuable
move.} 20. Re3 Rad8 $4 {Fuzzy thinking. I saw what as coming too late.} 21. f5
Bc8 22. f6 Qb7 23. Qh5 {A good game by White but helped by me paying the
penalty of being too tired to concentrate (lack of sleep and travelling). I
don't even know why I played an opening I didn't know in a county match.} 1-0

