{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. d4 Nf6 {[50'] After 50' the top board of the
other team had not arrived. The only reserve was already playing a tournament
game. However, he voluntered to play the two games simultaneously with 50' on
his clock in this one!} 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7. d5
e6 8. Be2 Na6 9. O-O Ne8 $6 {His previous move suggested that he would try to
force his QS Pawns up. This move intends .......f5. Inconsistent.} 10. Be3 {
Intending to answer 11.......PxP with 12.cxd instead of my usual exd} exd5 11.
cxd5 Nec7 {A bit awkward.} 12. h3 f5 $6 {Really stirring it up. I now get
passed Pawns in the middle} 13. e5 dxe5 14. fxe5 {Beautiful!} f4 $6 {Again
doubtful the Pawn is left very weak.} 15. Bf2 Re8 16. d6 Ne6 17. Bc4 $1 {
This proves to be very strong. Moves on the theme of.......} ({.....} 17. Bxa6
bxa6 18. Qd5 {are not too good.}) 17... Bd7 $2 {It was rather important to
unpin the Knight.} 18. Qd2 {Intending to put Rooks on d1 & e1} Bc6 $2 {Now
he's had it but a good move is hard to find here! He may be lost anyway.} 19.
Qxf4 Bxf3 (19... Kh8 $142) 20. Qxf3 Kh8 {[88']} ({If} 20... Bxe5 21. Rae1 {
Wins a piece.}) 21. Qxb7 {[53']} Nb4 22. d7 $1 {Most efficient} Re7 23. Bxe6
Rb8 {An interjection which has no effect on the result.} 24. Qxa7 Rxe6 25. Bh4
(25. Rad1 Z0 26. Qxb8 $140 {is also strong}) 25... Nc6 ({If} 25... Ra6 26. Qxb8
) 26. Bxd8 Nxa7 27. Bc7 {A violent game! Lancaster won 5 - 1 [The match was at
Manchester]} 1-0

