1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 cxd5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Bf4 e6 7. e3 a6 8. Bd3
Be7 9. O-O O-O 10. a3 b5 11. b4 Nh5 $2 {A miscalculation.} 12. Ne5 $1 {wins a
Pawn.} ({I suspect that he had only considered} 12. Bxh7+ Kxh7 13. Ng5+ Bxg5
14. Qxh5+ Bh6 {wins}) 12... Nxe5 (12... Nxf4 13. Nxc6 {Wins a piece. We now
adjourned for tea (!)}) 13. Bxh7+ Kxh7 14. Qxh5+ Kg8 15. Bxe5 $2 (15. Qxe5 {
followed by} Z0 16. Qc7 {seems better.}) 15... Bd7 16. Qe2 {I couldn't see
much in a KS advance and I was concerned about 16......a5} Qb6 17. Rfd1 ({
I fancied} 17. e4 f6 18. Bf4 {and my d-Pawn is en prise. However I should have
contested the c-file.}) 17... Rfc8 18. Qb2 Rc4 {Again threatening ....a5. I
realised I had been playing too casually.} 19. Rac1 {Played without confidence.
} (19. Rdc1 $142) 19... a5 {[80']} 20. Na2 {[80']} axb4 21. Nxb4 {I felt I may
be lost here.} Bxb4 {This surprised (and pleased) me} (21... Qa5 {Outting
pressure on the a-Pawn seems better.}) 22. axb4 {Mediocre stuff. The match was
played at Preston Masonic Temple} 1/2-1/2

