{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5.
Nc3 Qc7 6. Be2 {I didn't remember much about this variation so I decided to
play solidly.} (6. g3 {is an alternative.}) 6... Nf6 7. Bf3 $6 {After much
thought} ({I now considered} 7. Bg5 {I didn't fancy saccing my e-Pawn and I
didn't particularly fancy doubled c-Pawns.}) ({I considered} 7. O-O Bb4 8. Qd3
{as in M.C.O. Vol 11 p185 col 169 but didn't like it.}) 7... d6 (7... Bb4 {
I intended to answer with} 8. Nde2 $6) 8. O-O Be7 9. Be3 Bd7 (9... Nbd7 $142)
10. a4 Nc6 11. Nxc6 Bxc6 12. a5 Nd7 13. Na4 Bxa4 ({On} 13... Bb5 14. Be2) 14.
Rxa4 Ne5 15. Be2 Rc8 16. f4 {Gaining the innitiative.} Nc6 ({If} 16... Qc6 17.
fxe5 $1 Qxa4 18. exd6 {etc}) 17. Bb6 Qb8 18. f5 {Gives him e5 but opens lines
for my pieces.} exf5 ({Not} 18... O-O $2 19. fxe6 fxe6 20. Bg4) 19. Rxf5 O-O
20. Rd5 {I was starting to get short of time here. This move puts pressure on
the d-pawn and prevents 20......Bd8} Ne5 21. c3 Rc6 22. Bd4 Rd8 23. Bg4 {
Moving quickly now.} Nxg4 24. Qxg4 g6 25. Rh5 Qc8 26. Qxc8 {With little time I
simplify.} ({If} 26. Qg3 Qe6 {attacks the e-Pawn.}) 26... Rcxc8 27. Rd5 Bg5 $4
28. Rxg5 {He blundered in my time rush.} 1-0

