{Time limit 20mph} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 f5 3. Bg2 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bc5 5. e3 Nc6 6. a3 a5
7. Qa4 Ra6 {White's last move had a certain nuisance value. Both....} (7... d6)
({and} 7... b6 {were discouraged and b4 was a possibility for White. However
a6 is not a good square for the Rook.}) 8. Nge2 O-O 9. Qd1 {The Queen was no
longer much use on a4 and is needed to support d4. Alao b3 does now not cut
off the Queen.} e4 10. d4 {A positive move is neede in view of 10......Ne5,
and possibly ......b6} exd3 11. Qxd3 d6 ({If} 11... Ne5 12. Qc2 {and he can't
take the c-Pawn.}) 12. b3 Ne5 13. Qc2 c6 $2 {[35'] Not a good move. The d-Pawn
is left weak.} 14. O-O {[20']} Nfg4 $2 {Apparently trying to weaen my KS, but
not worth the loss of time.} 15. h3 Nf6 16. Bb2 Qe8 17. Rad1 {Strating to
pressurise his d-Pawn. White is making steady progress. Black's manoeuvres are
too slow.} Qh5 $2 {Very risky. He doesn't realise how weak he is in the middle.
} 18. Nf4 Qh6 19. Na4 {Suddenly White's position opens up.} g5 $6 {Hopeful of
a KS attack, possibly at the cost of s Pawn.} 20. Nxc5 {[36'] Black suddenly
noticed his flag was rising. Although he had ~3' left he seemed to panic. and
quickly played.} Ra8 $4 {[57'] fatal he had to lose a pawn but now a couple of
pieces go as well.} 21. Rxd6 {[40'] The best way.} gxf4 22. Bxe5 fxe3 23. Qc3 {
Wins the Knight.} f4 24. fxe3 Bxh3 25. Rxf4 Rad8 26. Rfxf6 Qh5 {Black plays on
out of inertia.} 27. Bf3 Qg5 28. Ne4 Qg7 29. Rxf8+ Qxf8 30. Rxd8 Qxd8 31. Qd4
Qe7 32. Nf6+ Kf7 33. Bh5+ Ke6 34. Ne4 Qf8 35. Nc5+ Kf5 1-0

