1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 Ne7 5. Qg4 Nf5 6. a3 Ba5 7. Bd3 (7. Nf3 {
May be more precise as Black can now equalise with...} h5 8. Qf4 Qh4) 7... g6
$2 {The rot sets in.} 8. Bg5 Qd7 9. Bf6 h5 10. Qf4 {[6']} Rh7 $2 (10... Rg8
$142) 11. Nf3 {Simply threatening to win the exchange by 12.BxN and 13.Ng5} c5
{He has to take positive action.} 12. Bxf5 ({I didn't fancy} 12. dxc5 {becuase
of} d4) 12... cxd4 13. Nxd4 exf5 14. b4 Bd8 15. O-O {Simply building on my
suoerior position and development to win.} a6 $2 {Waste of a move.} 16. Rfe1
Kf8 {Loses outright but there seems no good move.} 17. e6 fxe6 {Resigns is the
alternative.} 18. Nxe6+ Kf7 19. Bxd8 Qxe6 20. Rxe6 Bxe6 21. Qg5 Nc6 22. Qf6+
Ke8 23. Qxg6+ Kxd8 24. Qxh7 1-0

