{Time limit 20mph} 1. d4 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. e3 g6 4. Nd2 Bg7 5. Ngf3 O-O 6. Be2 d6
7. Rb1 a5 8. a4 $2 {Leaves a hole on b4.} Nc6 9. Nb3 Qe8 {Intending .....e5}
10. d5 Nd8 (10... Nb4 {is too loose. I was quite happy with the Knight on d8})
11. Ng5 $2 {Results in the manoeuvering of the Knight to f4, but at the cost
of 3 moves.} h6 12. Nh3 b6 ({I had thoughts of} 12... g5 {and} 13. Z0 f4 {
but the text move is more solid.}) 13. Bd2 {Offering his a-Pawn.} Qxa4 14. Bc3
e5 {I felt well on top here.} 15. dxe6 Bxe6 16. Nd4 {Offering an exchange of
Queens when a Pawn down and with the inferior position. However, he was
apparently hoping to get an attac on the KS. I felt that he overestimated his
position.} Qxd1+ 17. Rxd1 Bd7 18. Bf3 Rb8 19. Nf4 Kh7 20. h4 {Active play.} Re8
21. Kd2 Nf7 22. Rh3 $6 {Intending 23.Rg3 but leads to trouble.} g5 $1 {
Positive action improving the position of my night onf7.} 23. hxg5 Nxg5 {
Leaving him in a quandry because of my hold on e4.} 24. Rh2 Nfe4+ 25. Kc2 Nxf2
({Also good was} 25... Nxc3 26. bxc3 {with a won game for Black.}) 26. Rf1 Ng4
27. Bxg4 fxg4 28. Nd5 Rf8 {It was necessary to counter the f-file.} 29. Rhh1 c6
30. Ne7 Rxf1 31. Rxf1 Ne4 $6 (31... Re8 {May be more solid. The text is a
little risky.}) 32. Rf7 $1 Nxc3 {Forced in view of the threat of 33.RxB+} 33.
Ndf5 Bxf5+ 34. Nxf5 Rg8 35. bxc3 Kg6 36. Nxd6 Rd8 37. Rb7 $2 ({He can save the
piece by} 37. Nb7 {although Black would still win after} Re8) 37... Rxd6 38.
Rxb6 {White plays on hoping for something to turn up and susequently hoping
for a stalemate.} Kf5 39. Rb7 Bf6 40. Ra7 Ke4 41. Rxa5 Kxe3 42. Rf5 Rd2+ 43.
Kb3 Rd6 44. Rf1 h5 45. c5 Ke2 46. Rf5 Re6 47. Rxh5 Kf2 48. Rh6 Kxg2 49. c4 g3
50. Rh5 Bd4 51. Rg5 Bf2 52. Rh5 Kg1 53. Rh3 g2 54. Ka4 Kf1 55. Rc3 g1=Q 56. Kb3
Re3 57. Kb4 Be1 58. Kb3 Rxc3+ 59. Ka4 Qd4 ({Not} 59... Qxc5 $4 {Stalemate.})
60. Ka5 Qxc5+ 61. Ka6 Qb4 0-1

