1. d4 f5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. c4 g6 4. e3 Bg7 5. Bd3 O-O 6. O-O d6 7. Bc2 {[7']} h6 8.
Nc3 c6 {[1']} 9. b3 Qc7 10. h3 $6 {Unnecessary and weakening the KS.} e5 {[4']}
11. d5 $6 {Blacking the centre and leaving me free to work up an attack on the
KS} c5 12. Bd2 a6 13. Ne2 {White was now stuck for a constructive plan and
moves tp and fro whilst Black builds up on the KS.} Qf7 14. Rc1 g5 15. Nh2 f4 {
Leaves a few holes but prevents 16.f4} 16. Nc3 Kh8 {Intending to double Rooks
on the g-file.} 17. Ne4 {Just the move I wanted as I was stuck for a good way
to develop my Knight.} Nxe4 18. Bxe4 Nd7 19. Bf3 Nf6 20. Re1 Bd7 21. Nf1 h5 22.
Nh2 Bh6 23. Rc3 Rg8 24. e4 Kh7 {To protect the Bishop in the event of Pawn
swaps.} 25. Be2 Rg7 ({Not} 25... Nxe4 $4 26. Bd3) 26. Bf3 ({I expected} 26. f3)
26... Rag8 27. Qe2 $4 {Still aimlessly manoeuvering he blunders.} g4 28. hxg4
hxg4 29. Bxg4 Nxg4 30. Nxg4 Rxg4 {Rather a cavalry charge.} 0-1

