{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. d4 g6 2. e4 Bg7 3. f4 c5 4. d5 d6 5. c4 Nf6
6. Nc3 O-O 7. Nf3 a6 8. a4 e6 9. Bd3 {After my game at south Manchester
earlier this season, I decided to recapture with my c-Pawn.} exd5 10. cxd5 Qb6
11. a5 Qc7 (11... Qb4 12. Ra4 {Resigns}) 12. O-O b5 {Gets his Queen back on b6
but doesn't really help much.} 13. axb6 Qxb6 14. Kh1 {safest} Ng4 $5 {Active
but leading to loss of time or a pawn. Black's poor development doesn't
justify this move.} 15. h3 {Black threatened 15......c4 and 16.......Nf2+} c4 {
Pressing but 15......Nf6 may be more prudent.} (15... Nf6) 16. hxg4 cxd3 17. f5
$1 {Black had overlooked this which wins a pawn and starts a KS initiative.} ({
Also good was} 17. Qxd3) 17... gxf5 18. gxf5 a5 {Temporarily saving the d-pawn.
} 19. Ng5 f6 20. Ne6 Bxe6 21. dxe6 {Better than fxe6 as my Knight gets d5 now.}
Qd4 {Doesn't achieve much} 22. Rf3 Re8 23. Rxd3 Qf2 24. Nd5 Nc6 25. Bf4 $1 {
Best} ({If} 25. Nc7 Ne5) 25... Rab8 26. b3 Nb4 27. Rf3 Qb2 28. Rb1 Qc2 ({Not} 
28... Qa2 29. Nc3 Qa3 $4 30. Bc1) 29. Qxc2 Nxc2 30. Bxd6 Rb7 31. e5 $1 {
The most effiecient way} Nd4 32. Nxf6+ Bxf6 33. exf6 Nxf3 34. f7+ Rxf7 35.
exf7+ Kxf7 36. gxf3 Kf6 37. Ra1 Re3 38. Kg2 Rxb3 39. Rxa5 Rb7 40. Kg3 Rg7+ 41.
Kf4 Rg1 42. Be5+ Kf7 43. Ra7+ Kg8 44. f6 {A good game. Colin Jex's first defat
of the season [Skein were the Lancaster University staff team captained by W.
Faibairn]} 1-0

