{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 {Obviously the "in" move
this season.} c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Be3 {I hadn't met this before.} Qb6 6. Qd2 cxd4
7. cxd4 Bb4 8. Nc3 Nge7 9. Nf3 Bd7 10. Be2 Rc8 11. O-O Bxc3 {Intending to
leave him a weak Pawnon c3.} 12. bxc3 Na5 13. Rab1 Qc7 14. Qb2 $6 {After the
game White said that he intended 14.Rfc1 and 15.Qb2 but played the moves in
the wrong order. As it turns out the text move is OK.} Qxc3 $5 {Very risky. It
turns out much worse than I expected.} 15. Qxc3 Rxc3 16. Bd2 Ra3 17. Bxa5 Rxa5
18. Rxb7 Rxa2 $5 {Underestimating his next move.} (18... Nc6 {may have been
safer.}) 19. Rc1 $1 Kd8 {After much thought.} 20. Ng5 Rf8 21. Nxh7 Rh8 22. Ng5
Rf8 23. Bh5 $2 {So as to create a hole at f6 for the Knight.} (23. Kf1 {
Seems best.}) 23... g6 24. Bd1 Nc6 25. Nh7 Rh8 26. Nf6 Bc8 27. Rxf7 $5 {
Winning a Pawn but probably throwing away his winning chances.} Ne7 $1 {
Cutting off the Rook.} 28. h3 Ra6 29. Bg4 Rc6 30. Ra1 a6 31. Rb1 Rc7 {The
Black position holds together well now.} 32. Rb6 Nf5 33. Bxf5 $2 {Steady
defence pays off! White makes a mistake overlooking my 35th move.} Rxf7 34.
Rd6+ $2 Ke7 ({If} 34... Kc7 35. Ne8+) 35. Bxg6 Rxf6 36. exf6+ Kxd6 37. g4 Rh6
38. Bc2 ({If} 38. f7 Ke7 39. Bh5 Rxh5 $1) 38... Rxf6 39. g5 Rf4 40. Kg2 Rxd4
41. Kg3 e5 42. f3 Ke7 43. h4 Kf7 44. h5 Kg7 45. h6+ Kh8 46. Bg6 Be6 {3 A good
defensive effort. The match result was 3 -} 0-1

