{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. c4 f5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. g3 g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. d4
O-O 6. Nh3 {A good line for White.} c6 7. Nf4 Na6 ({I feel something better is
needed here. Maybe} 7... e5 8. dxe5 Ng4) 8. O-O Nc7 ({maybe} 8... d5 {is
possible.}) 9. d5 {very strong.} cxd5 {More or less forced. I didn't like....}
({...} 9... e5 10. d6 Nce8 11. Nd3) 10. cxd5 d6 ({Again I didn't like.} 10...
e5 11. d6 Nce8 12. Nd3) 11. h4 Bd7 12. Re1 b5 $5 {Trying for QS play but
rather risky.} 13. Be3 Ng4 14. Bd4 Bxd4 (14... Ne5 {Might be better.}) 15. Qxd4
Nf6 $2 {A bad mistake wasting time. The Knight should stay where it is to
retain the option of going to f6 or e5. A slack move.} 16. e4 $1 {Threatening
a murderous breathrough on the KS.} Ng4 {Back again to try to keep the e-file
closed.} 17. Rad1 {Consolodating.} a6 {So as to be able to move the Rook.} 18.
Nd3 Rb8 (18... Rc8 $142 {as it turns out.}) 19. b4 Ne8 {After a lot of thought
and getting short of time. I could nearly win his Queen by.....} ({..........} 
19... e5 20. dxe6 Nxe6 21. Qxd6 Rb6 22. Qd5 Nf6 {but she escapes to} 23. Qb3)
20. e5 Rc8 {With little time left.} 21. Ne2 {Else I get a draw.} Rc4 22. Qb2
dxe5 {Loses pretty quickly, but sitting tight and allowing e6 is the only
alternative.} 23. Nxe5 Nxe5 24. Qxe5 Nd6 {With seconds left now.} 25. Nd4 Rxb4
{No time to think} (25... Rxd4 {is the only hope.}) 26. Nc6 Bxc6 27. dxc6 Qc8
28. Bd5+ Nf7 29. Qxe7 a5 30. c7 {and my Flag fell. Skating on too thin ice.
There may have been a way out around move 32 if I'd had more time on the clock.
} 1-0

