1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 {For the first time with White this season. With this
last game to play K.L. was half a point behind me therefore he needed a win I
only needed a draw.} c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 Qb6 6. Be2 {As in Glazer v R.A.C. a
few wees back.} Nge7 7. O-O {After this move I suddenly realised he could win
a Pawn. I was still playing at lightning speed.} cxd4 8. cxd4 Nf5 9. Be3 {
I was fairly happy to give up the b-Pawn.} Qxb2 {Needing a win he grabs the
Pawn.} 10. Nbd2 Qa3 $2 {The Queen never gets back into it from here. He could
have tried for another Pawn by....} ({...} 10... Nxe3 11. fxe3 Qc3 {White
could then have gone mad with} 12. e4 Qe3+ 13. Kh1 dxe4 14. Nxe4 $6 Qxe4 15.
Ng5) 11. Nb3 Nxe3 {Not a good move as it opens the f-file up for White.} 12.
fxe3 Be7 13. Bd3 O-O 14. Qe2 f5 15. exf6 Bxf6 16. Ne5 $1 {Best with various
threats.} ({If} 16. g4 g6 17. Z0 Bg7) 16... Nxe5 17. dxe5 Bg5 18. e4 $1 {
Opening up the position all to White's advantage.} dxe4 ({would possibly foil
White the best.} 18... d4) 19. Qxe4 {I felt that it must be a win now.} g6 20.
h4 Bh6 21. h5 Rf5 {His best chance.} 22. hxg6 hxg6 23. Qd4 $1 {Most accurate,
creating threats on the back rank.} ({Not to be recommended was} 23. Qh4 $2
Be3+ 24. Kh1 Rh5) 23... Rg5 24. Qd8+ Kg7 25. Qe8 Rf5 {Vainly hoping to salvage
something by blocking the f-file.} 26. Bxf5 gxf5 27. Rf3 f4 {Prevents 28.Rg3+,
but allows....} 28. Rc1 Qf8 29. Rc7+ Kh8 30. Qg6 {Rather burning his fingers
on the b-Pawn. Lancaster Club Championship 1973-74 1st Collins.................
.......8.5 2nd=Turner, Lenartowicz.....7 4th Fisher.........................5.
5 5th Lawrence....................5 6th Russell........................4.5 7th
Bland..........................3 8th Wilkinson.....................2.5 9th
Dixon...........................2 10th Leigh...........................0} 1-0

