{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 moves per 15'} 1. e4 e6 2. Nf3 d5 3. Nc3
dxe4 ({M.C.O. 11 gives} 3... d4) 4. Nxe4 Nf6 $5 {Much too risky.} 5. Nxf6+ gxf6
6. d4 c5 (6... b6 {may be more solid.}) 7. Be3 cxd4 8. Nxd4 e5 $2 {Probably
the losing move.} 9. Nb5 Qa5+ {After much thought although it gives up a Pawn.}
10. Qd2 Qxd2+ 11. Kxd2 Na6 12. Nxa7 Bf5 13. Bb5+ Bd7 14. Bxd7+ Kxd7 15. Rhd1
Nb4 16. a3 Nd5 17. Ke2 Ke6 18. Nb5 Rc8 {19.RxN was threatened} 19. Rac1 Nxe3
20. fxe3 ({Not} 20. Kxe3 $4 Bh6+) 20... Rg8 21. g3 f5 22. c4 Rg4 23. b3 h5 24.
Rd5 h4 25. Kf3 Be7 26. Rg1 hxg3 27. hxg3 Rh8 28. Nc7+ Kf6 29. Rb5 Rh2 {
Threatening mate.} 30. Rg2 Rxg2 31. Kxg2 Bxa3 32. Rxb7 Bc5 {The game was
adjourned.} 33. Rb5 {[Sealed move] The game resumed 6/11/74} ({I had expected.
} 33. Nd5+) 33... Bd6 34. Ne8+ Ke7 35. Nxd6 Kxd6 36. Kf3 Rg8 37. b4 Re8 38.
Rb6+ Kd7 39. c5 Kc7 40. Rf6 Re7 41. b5 ({Not} 41. Rxf5 Kc6) 41... f4 42. gxf4
exf4 43. Kxf4 Kb8 44. b6 Kb7 45. e4 Ka6 $2 {Loses straight off.} 46. Rc6 Kb7 {
Loses immediately but there was nothing else.} 47. Rc7+ Rxc7 48. bxc7 Kxc7 49.
Ke5 ({My faint hope was that he would inadvertenly play} 49. Kf5) 49... Kc6 50.
Kd4 Kc7 51. Kd5 Kd7 52. c6+ {A poor opening. I'm not yet back in form. My only
hope on adjournment was to be able to sacrifice Bishop for two Pawns.} 1-0

