{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 d5 {[3']} 4. Qa4 dxe4 {
[43'] 40 minutes over this!} (4... Bd7 $142) (4... Nf6 $142) 5. Nxe5 Qd5 {[47']
} 6. Nxc6 bxc6 7. d4 {[14']} ({M.C.O. 11 gives} 7. Bc4 {I prefer my move.})
7... Be6 {[56']} ({If} 7... exd3 8. Bxd3 {and neither the Bishop or rhe g-Pawn
can be taken.}) 8. Be3 {[15']} Nf6 {[61']} 9. c4 {[20']} Qd7 {[66']} 10. Nc3
Be7 {[74']} 11. Qc2 {I felt the Queen had served its purpose on a4. I still
wasn't sure which side I was going to castle.} Bf5 {[17']} 12. Be2 O-O 13. h3 {
[25']} Bb4 {[97'] Considering how much time he had left he was still playing
very slowly.} 14. O-O-O {[29']} Qe7 {[104'] He now had 16' for 26 moves.} 15.
g4 {[31']} Bg6 {[103']} 16. a3 {A little weakening but I felt in view of his
piece placing and time position , he shouldn't get much QS play.} Bxc3 17. Qxc3
Rab8 18. h4 {[33'] I was playing fairly quickly in order to keep him at it.} h6
{[110']} 19. h5 {[40']} Bh7 20. Rhg1 {I wanted to keep the possibility of Rd2
if he doubles against the b-Pawn.} Nd7 21. g5 {Played quickly but a little
impetuous. His next move proves more troublesome than I expected.} Nb6 {
The threat of 22.......Na4 is a nuisance.} 22. g6 Na4 {Played instantaneously.}
(22... fxg6 $142) 23. gxh7+ Kh8 (23... Kxh7 {May be better, but he had no time
to think now.}) 24. Qa5 Rxb2 {Desperate stuff now.} 25. Qxa4 Rfb8 {banking on
a last hope attack.} (25... Rxe2 26. Rd2 {Simply leaves him a Bishop down.})
26. Bxh6 Ra2 ({If} 26... gxh6 27. Rg8+ {Wins a Rook.}) 27. Bxg7+ Kxh7 28. Qa5 (
28. Qa5 {Threatens....} Z0 29. Qf5+ Kg8 30. Bf6+) 28... Rb5 29. cxb5 Rxa3 30.
Qa6 Qb4 (30... Rxa6 31. bxa6 {is hopeless.}) 31. Qxa3 Qxa3+ 32. Kd2 Qb4+ 33.
Ke3 {Black lost on time. Interesting, but he had no hope in such time trouble.
P.Griffiths is a member of Whitehaven C.C.} 1-0

