{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5.
Nc3 Qc7 6. Bd3 Nc6 7. Nde2 {[7'] Not mentioned in Moiseevs book on this
opening.} b5 {[2']} 8. a3 Bc5 9. O-O Bb7 10. Ng3 {[11'] I don't like this. The
Knight has no prospects here.} Nge7 {[5']} 11. Nce2 h5 {[6'] I was playing
very fast. The match got off to a very slow start as the initial venue had to
be changed. I had to finish within 2hrs hence it was a rather lightning effort.
} 12. Nf4 {[14'] Risky} h4 {[8']} 13. Ngh5 O-O-O {[10']} 14. c3 {He can hardly
take the g-Pawn but this is very passive.} Bd6 {[12']} 15. Qg4 {[33'] Now he's
in trouble although his position was very difficult.} ({Maybe} 15. Be2 {
was best}) 15... Ne5 {[13']} 16. Qh3 g5 {[14'] wins a piece.} 17. Be2 {[38']}
gxf4 {[16']} 18. Bxf4 Bxe4 {[18']} 19. Bxe5 Bxe5 20. Qxh4 d5 21. f4 Nf5 22. Qf2
Bd6 23. b4 Rdg8 24. Bf3 $2 Rxh5 25. Bxe4 dxe4 26. a4 e3 27. Qf3 Qb7 28. axb5
Qxf3 29. Rxf3 {[49']} axb5 {[28']} 30. h3 Nh4 31. Rxe3 Nxg2 32. Re4 Rxh3 33.
Rd4 Ne3+ 34. Kf2 Rg2+ {2 Lancaster won 4 -} 1-0

