{Time limit 40mph} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 4. d4 exd4 5. e5 Ne4 6. Qc2 {
Suggested by Jaenisch but 6.Qe2 seems better.} (6. Qe2 $142) 6... d5 7. cxd4
Bg4 8. Bb5 Bb4+ 9. Bd2 O-O 10. Bxb4 Nxb4 11. Qb3 Bxf3 $6 {Really stirring it.
He gets three Pawns and a lot of play for the Knight.} 12. gxf3 Qh4 13. Rf1 $8
Ng5 14. Qxb4 Nxf3+ 15. Kd1 Nxd4 16. Nc3 Qh5+ 17. Ne2 Nxb5 18. Qxb5 Qxe5 19. Rc1
{Willing to let the h-Pawn go in order to get some play.} c6 20. Qb3 Rfe8 21.
Rc2 d4 22. Qd3 c5 23. Ng3 b6 24. b3 g6 {Leads to problems} 25. Re2 (25. f4 {
is possible but leaves a hole on e3.}) 25... Qf4 26. Rfe1 Kf8 27. h3 {
Preventing a check on g4 in some variations.} Rad8 {The Rook appears to be
badly placed but it is not apparent at this stage.} 28. h4 $6 {Deciding to get
on with it, sacrificing the pawn to open the h-file or else by playing h5.}
Rxe2 29. Qxe2 Qxh4 {Accepting the challenge and also defending the Rook.} 30.
Qe5 Kg8 31. f3 $3 {A hard move to find. I want to play the Knight to e4-f6 but
the Black Queen can check on h5, so I prevent the check.} (31. Ne4 Qh5+) 31...
Qh3 {After much thought} 32. Ne4 $1 {Anyway} Qxf3+ {Black is lost.} 33. Kc1 Qf5
34. Nf6+ Kh8 35. Rh1 $1 {Leaving Black without a move.} Kg7 ({If} 35... h5 36.
Rxh5+ $1) 36. Rxh7+ Kf8 37. Rh8+ {3 A good game with a neat finish. The game
was played at M.J.Conroys' home. The match was a tie 3 -} 1-0

