{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. d3 e5 5. Nbd2
Be6 6. e4 d4 7. O-O f6 8. Ne1 g5 {Skating on thin ice.} 9. Bh3 Bf7 10. f4 h5
11. fxg5 fxg5 12. Bf5 Nh6 13. Ng2 Bg7 14. Qe2 Nxf5 15. exf5 {[55']} Bd5 {
[24'] I felt fairly happy here.} 16. Ne4 Bxe4 17. Qxe4 Bf6 {He offered me a
draw here.} 18. Bd2 Qd7 19. h3 Rd8 (19... O-O-O {is too risky.}) 20. Kh2 Kf8
21. a3 Rh7 22. Rf2 Qd6 23. Ne1 Kg8 {I didn't like having the King and Queen on
the same diagonal if he plays b4.} 24. Nf3 Qe7 {Doubtful.} (24... Rg7 $142) 25.
h4 $1 g4 (25... gxh4 {After this he gets the g-file.}) 26. Ng5 Rh8 27. Qe2 Rd7
28. Raf1 Nd8 {I have to find the right moves here.} 29. Kg2 Nf7 30. Ne4 Qe8 $1
{Only just. He threatens Bg5} 31. Qd1 ({If} 31. Bg5 {I can capture without
losing to f6.}) 31... Rc7 {The c-Pawn needs protection now.} 32. Qc1 Nd6 {
Again, only just good enough.} 33. Ng5 Rc6 34. Ne6 Qe7 35. Bg5 Nf7 36. Re2 c4
37. dxc4 Rxc4 38. Qd2 b6 39. Qd3 b5 40. Qd2 Rc8 {Adjudicated.[Komodo 9.1 gives
White as clearly better] White threatens 41.Nxd4 if he first prevents the
Queen check on the long diagonal. This match was played along with Lancaster
II (1.5) v Manchester II (4.5). Both matches were played at St. Joseph's Hall
which was situated on Aldrens Lane next to St. Joseph's primrary School.} 1-0

