{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. e3
e5 6. Nge2 d6 7. O-O Nbd7 8. Rb1 a5 9. a3 c6 10. b4 Nb6 {An unusual square for
the Knight in this opening but O.K. I think in this position.} 11. d3 {White
was already taking a lot of time.} axb4 {I would rather have the a-file than
the b-file.} 12. axb4 Qe7 13. b5 c5 {More or less forced but White gives up
his innitiative.} 14. Qb3 Bf5 15. e4 {White was getting short of time now.} Be6
16. f4 {The most active move.} exf4 17. Nxf4 {He appeared to have intended to
take with the Pawn but short of time felt this to be safer.} Ng4 18. Nce2 {
To prevent 18.......Bd4+} g5 $6 {I don't think I'd play this normally, but he
was so short of time I wanted to mix it.} 19. Nxe6 fxe6 20. h3 Rxf1+ 21. Bxf1
Ne5 22. Bg2 Qf7 23. Be3 {Short of time he finds the best moves.} (23. Bxg5 {
is suicide.}) 23... Qh5 24. g4 Qg6 25. Ng3 Rf8 26. Rf1 Rxf1+ 27. Kxf1 Qf7+ 28.
Kg1 Nf3+ 29. Kh1 Ne1 30. Qd1 Nxg2 1/2-1/2

