{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 moves per 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. c4 Qc7 ({Probably better is Kan's} 5... Nf6 {attacking the
e-Pawn. White now avoids playing Nc3 till I've commited my King Bishop
elsewhere}) 6. Bd3 Nc6 7. Nf3 Nf6 8. O-O Bc5 $5 {Doesn't turn out too well as
White gets a tempo out of b4.} 9. Nc3 d6 10. a3 Bd7 11. b4 Ba7 12. Bb2 Nd4 {
Relieving the pressure a little.} 13. Nxd4 Bxd4 14. Qd2 ({I thought he might
try} 14. Nd5 {or 14.Nb5}) 14... Bc6 15. Ne2 Bxb2 16. Qxb2 O-O {After some
consideration of......} ({......} 16... Nxe4 17. Qxg7 O-O-O {I felt I had to
play safe.}) 17. f3 {Keeping me pinned down.} b6 18. Rfd1 Bd7 {To answer 7.b5
with ......a5} 19. Rd2 Rfc8 20. Rc1 h6 {Something of a waiting move.} 21. Kh1 (
21. b5 $2 Qc5+ {Wins the a-Pawn.}) 21... a5 $1 {Easing the pressure on the
e-Pawn} 22. b5 {Opening a file would not favour White.} Qc5 23. Ra1 Rab8 24.
Nc3 Rd8 $2 {Turns out badly.} 25. Bf1 Be8 {After much thought. If......} ({
......} 25... Bc8 26. Na4 Qc7 27. e5 $1) 26. Na4 Qc7 27. Qd4 Rd7 28. Qf2 Kf8 {
To help in th defence.} 29. Qg3 (29. g4 $142) (29. Qe3 $142) (29. f4 $142)
29... e5 {More or less forced but not too bad.} 30. h4 {Allows me to
centralise my Knight.} Nh5 31. Qf2 Nf4 32. Nc3 Ne6 33. Nd5 {[1hr 14']
Adjourned. I now sealed} Qc5 {The game was resumed on 7/3/75. I now rather
expected another 40 moves ending in a draw. It turns out a little better than
that.} 34. Qe3 Qxe3 35. Nxe3 Nd4 36. Nf5 $2 {The wrong strategy. I gain the
innitiative in the centre as I can play .......d5once his e-Pawn is gone.} Nxf5
37. exf5 Ke7 38. Kg1 f6 {Now his weak c-Pawn becomes the target.} 39. Kf2 {
[1hr 28']} Bf7 {[1hr 28'] Now ......d5 is coming and White is in trouble.} 40.
Rc1 Rc8 41. Rdc2 Rdc7 42. Bd3 {There seems nothing better.} d5 43. cxd5 ({If} 
43. c5 {either} Rxc5 ({or} 43... bxc5 44. b6 Rc6 {seems OK for Black.})) 43...
Rxc2+ 44. Rxc2 Rxc2+ 45. Bxc2 Bxd5 46. Ke3 Kd6 47. g4 {After a long think. He
loses his QS Pawns in any event.} Kc5 48. a4 Kb4 49. f4 exf4+ 50. Kxf4 Bb3 51.
Bxb3 Kxb3 52. g5 Kxa4 53. gxh6 gxh6 54. Kg4 Kxb5 55. Kh5 a4 56. Kxh6 a3 57. h5
a2 58. Kg7 a1=Q 59. h6 Qa7+ 60. Kg8 ({If} 60. Kxf6 Qh7) 60... Kc5 61. h7 Qxh7+
62. Kxh7 Kd5 0-1

