{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5.
Nc3 Qc7 6. a3 {Not considered in Moiseev's book.} Nc6 {[0']} 7. f4 {[15']} b5 {
[6']} 8. g3 Bb7 9. Bg2 {[23']} Rc8 {[11'] Something of a waiting move to see
what he does.} 10. O-O $4 {[35'] Disaster. He apparently was concerned about ..
.....N-a5-c4 and considered 10.Nb3 for a long time, didn't like it so played
10.Castles without giving any thought to it.} (10. Nb3) 10... Nxd4 {[11']} 11.
Be3 {[36']} Nc6 {[12']} 12. e5 {[38']} (12. f5 {Seems a better chance of a
last-ditch attack. Now some exchanges can be forced .}) 12... Na5 13. Bxb7 Qxb7
14. f5 Nc4 15. Bd4 Bc5 {Developing a KS piece at last.} 16. fxe6 dxe6 {[22']}
17. Bxc5 Rxc5 18. Qd4 {[56']} Rc7 {[26'] Much better than 18.......Rc8 in view
of 19.Ne4-d6+} 19. Ne4 {[62']} Qa7 {[27']} 20. c3 {[70'] Getting short of time.
} Nh6 {[30']} 21. Rad1 {[72']} O-O ({Not} 21... Ne3 $4 22. Qd8#) 22. Nd6 {[73']
} Ne3 23. Qxa7 {[1hr 14' 30s]} Rxa7 24. Rd3 Nxf1 25. Kxf1 Ng4 {White rsigned
as hs flag fell} 0-1

