1. Nf3 d5 2. c3 c5 3. g3 Nc6 4. Qb3 c4 {As the program isn't very
sophisticated I adopt simple tactical threats to push it around.} 5. Qa4 Bd7 6.
a3 $2 Nd4 7. Qd1 Nb3 8. Ra2 Ba4 9. Ne5 Nc5 10. b3 Bxb3 11. Rc2 Bxc2 12. Qxc2
Nb3 13. Bb2 Qd6 14. Nf3 e5 15. Nh4 Rc8 16. a4 d4 17. cxd4 exd4 18. Qe4+ Ne7 19.
Qxb7 Rb8 20. Qb5+ $4 Rxb5 21. axb5 Qd5 22. e4 Qxe4+ 23. Kd1 Qxh1 24. Bxd4 Qxf1+
25. Kc2 {I now intended....25......Qc1# but typed 1813 (f1-c1) instead of 1613
(f1-c1).The computer Happily moved a non-existent piece and played....} Z0 26.
Bxg7 $4 Qc1# {I got it right this time.} 0-1

