{Time limit 24 mph} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. Nc3 a6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 Qc7 6. g3
Nc6 7. Nf3 Bb4 8. Bd2 Nf6 9. Bd3 {It's not clear why he played 6.g3} d6 10. a3
Bxc3 {In view of his weakened KS I change my plans and go for .......e5 and my
Q Bishop to the KS} 11. Bxc3 e5 {The hole on d5 is no great problem.} 12. Nh4
Be6 13. f4 Bg4 14. Be2 Be6 15. f5 $5 Bd7 {White has gained a few tempi but has
weakened his position, especially his e-Pawn.} 16. Bf3 g5 {Immediate positive
counterplay.} 17. Ng2 g4 18. Bxg4 Nxe4 {I felt that I was going to win now.}
19. Qd3 Nxc3 20. Qxc3 Rc8 21. Ne3 Ne7 {Better than 21.......Nd5 as 22.Nd5 by
White is prevented also the d-Pawn is more easily supported.} 22. Qxc7 Rxc7 23.
c3 Bc6 24. Rf1 h5 25. Bf3 f6 26. O-O-O Rd7 27. Bxc6 bxc6 28. Nc4 d5 29. Ne3 {
He can't find a plan.} Nc8 30. Rfe1 Nd6 31. g4 hxg4 32. Nxg4 Kf7 ({I thought
for a while about} 32... Rg7 33. Nxf6+ Ke7 34. Nxd5+ cxd5 35. Rxd5 {but didn't
like it.}) 33. Rf1 Rh4 34. Ne3 Rxh2 35. Nxd5 $5 {Desperation} (35. Rh1 $142)
35... cxd5 36. Rxd5 Ke7 37. Rfd1 Rd8 38. c4 Rhh8 39. Rc5 Rc8 40. Rxc8 Rxc8 41.
b3 Nxf5 42. Kb2 Ne3 43. Rd3 Nxc4+ 44. bxc4 Rxc4 45. Kb3 Rc6 46. Kb4 e4 47. Rd4
e3 {[K.Lenartowicz came second in Prelim D with 3.5/6]} 0-1

