{Time limit 24 mph} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Be3 Qc7 6. Bd3
Nf6 7. O-O Be7 8. Nd2 {Allowing my reply which equalises.} (8. Nc3 $142) 8...
d5 9. f4 $5 {Possibly premature. He gets into trouble now.} dxe4 10. Nxe4 Nd5
11. Bd2 {Giving up a Pawn.} (11. Bf2 {May have been playable as it is risky
for Black to capture the f-Pawn.}) 11... Qb6 12. c3 {[32']} Nc6 {[10']} 13. Be1
$2 {Surprised by the turn of events he blunders.} ({Best was} 13. Qb3 Qa7 14.
Kh1 {with some compensation for the Pawn.}) 13... Ne3 14. Qd2 Nxf1 15. Kxf1
Nxd4 16. cxd4 {[39']} Bd7 {[20']} (16... Qxd4 {Would be amusing (for White)})
17. Bf2 Qb4 18. Nc3 {White doesn't want to allow exchanges.} Rc8 19. Re1 Kf8 {
I didn't want to leave the King on e8.} (19... O-O {is too risky e.g.} 20. Re5)
20. Qe2 Bf6 21. a3 Qd6 22. Ne4 Qxf4 {White's position starts to look desperate}
23. Kg1 {Short of time} Rc1 24. Bg3 Bxd4+ 25. Kh1 Qe3 {Threatening 26.......
Qg1+} 26. Bd6+ $1 {A last chance.} Ke8 (26... Kg8 $4 27. Nf6+) 27. Qxe3 {
He rattles off a few more moves.} Bxe3 28. Rxc1 Bxc1 29. b4 Bxa3 30. Nc5 Bxb4
31. Nxb7 Bxd6 32. Nxd6+ Ke7 {[R.Newton was 1st in prelim E with 6/7]} 0-1

