{Time limit 24 mph} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d3 Nc6 4. g3 b5 {More aggressive
than in our game earlier this season.} 5. Bg2 Bb7 6. O-O d6 7. Re1 Be7 {
I considered fianchettoing the Bishop but this seems more solid.} 8. Nbd2 Qc7
9. Qe2 a6 {Defending the b-Pawn in view of d4 later on.} 10. c3 Bf6 {
Preventing d4 for the time being.} 11. Nf1 h6 {I didn't particularly trade off
the Bishop, hence ....h6 to prevent Bg5} 12. Ne3 g6 13. Ng4 Bg7 14. e5 {
White decides on some more direct action on the KS at the expense of giving
Black more central control.} d5 15. h4 {[31']} Nge7 {[15'] I was playing
rather fast; this tends to happen in these club games.} 16. Bf4 {Threatening
17.Nf6+ and I can't capture.} Qd8 ({If} 16... Qd7 17. Qe3 {Threatens both h &
c Pawns. Also the Black Queen is more vulnerable to attack by the White
Knights.}) 17. Nf6+ Kf8 (17... Bxf6 18. exf6 Ng8 19. Qe3 {Seems to give White
a variety of possibilities and leaves Black cramped.}) 18. g4 d4 {Aiming for
counterplay in the centre particularly with the Knights.} 19. h5 g5 20. Nxg5 $6
{The most enterprising line. If he simply retreated the Bishop Black would
probably win a Pawn.} Bxf6 ({I didn't particularly like} 20... hxg5 21. Bxg5 {
when White has a lot of pressure on the KS.}) 21. Nxe6+ $5 {This surprised me.}
({I was thinking in terms of} 21. exf6 hxg5 22. fxe7+ Qxe7 23. Be5 f6) 21...
fxe6 22. exf6 Nd5 23. Be5 Kf7 {A bit of a time rush here.} ({If} 23... dxc3 24.
f7) 24. Qe4 Nxe5 25. Qxe5 Qxf6 $5 {Doubtful.} ({Probably best is.} 25... Qd7 {
defending the Bishop and e-Pawn and if} 26. Qe4 Rag8) 26. c4 bxc4 27. dxc4 {
I now felt that my passed Pawn ought to give me a won endgame.} Qxe5 28. Rxe5
Kf6 $1 29. Rae1 ({Forcing} 29. Ree1 Nb4 30. Bxb7 Ra7 31. Z0 Nc2 {White goes a
different way.}) 29... Ne3 $1 30. Rxe6+ Kxe6 31. Bxb7 Rab8 32. Bd5+ Kd6 33.
fxe3 Rhe8 {Forcing e4 and leaving me with a winning d-Pawn.} 34. e4 Rxb2 35.
Rf1 d3 36. Rf6+ Ke5 37. Rf5+ Kd4 38. Rf4 d2 39. e5+ Kxe5 0-1

