{Time limit 24 mph} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 f5 {The Ponziani counter Attack.
Mentioned in Ponziani's book in 1782.} 4. d4 {The usual continuation.} fxe4 5.
Nxe5 Qf6 (5... Nf6 {is the alternative.}) 6. Nxc6 ({Larobok recommended.} 6.
Ng4) 6... bxc6 {Harding gives this as best.} (6... Qxc6 7. Qh5+) 7. c4 {
"Preventing" 7........d4 and allowing the Knight the c3 square.} d5 $2 {
Played without much consideration.} 8. cxd5 cxd5 9. Qh5+ Qf7 10. Bb5+ Ke7 11.
Qxf7+ {I felt that this was the simplest, but possibly......} ({........} 11.
Qe5+ Kd8 12. Bc6 {is stronger.}) 11... Kxf7 12. Bc6 Rb8 13. Bxd5+ Be6 14. Bxe4
$5 {Rather too casual. I underestimated his coming counterplay. Possibly best
is either.......} ({..........} 14. Nc3) ({.......or else} 14. Bxe6+ Kxe6 15.
Nc3) 14... Nf6 15. Bf3 {Doesn't turn out too well, but it's difficult to see
how the d-Pawn can be defended.} c5 $1 {getting things moving in the centre as
quickly as possible.} ({Alternatively he can win the d-Pawn by.} 15... Rb4) 16.
dxc5 {I still didn't realise how far ahead in development he was.} ({Maybe} 16.
d5 $1 {would be best.}) 16... Bxc5 17. O-O Bd4 {Ouch!} 18. Nc3 Rhc8 19. Nd1 {
I wasn't happy now.} Bxa2 $4 {A bad miscalculation losing a piece.} 20. Bf4 Bc4
21. Bxb8 Bxf1 22. Bxa7 Rd8 23. Bxd4 {Too casual on my part. Lancaster Club
Championship 1974-75 Collins 7 Seery 4.5 Lawrence 4 Newton 3.5 Crosby,
Suchacki 3 Russell 2.5 Turner, Fisher 1.5 Lenartowicz 0.5} 1-0

