1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 g6 {A fairly modern line not mentioned
in M.C.O.} 5. Bc4 Bg7 6. c3 {A good move, to which I couldn't find a good
reply.} Nf6 {Accepting a Bishop on h6.} ({If} 6... Nd7 7. Qb3 e6 8. Nd6+) 7.
Nxf6+ Bxf6 (7... exf6 {May well be better.}) 8. Bh6 Qb6 9. Qd2 Bf5 10. Ne2 Be4
{Intending to bring the Bishop to d5. I didn't mind Nb3-then NxB; However he
would be under no obligation to capture.} 11. O-O Nd7 12. Rfe1 Bd5 13. Bxd5
cxd5 14. Nf4 Qb5 15. a4 Qc4 16. a5 Nf8 {A good move in a position that was
becoming difficult. If White moves his Knight 17........Ne6 is very solid.} 17.
b3 Qc6 18. Rac1 Qd6 19. Qe2 a6 20. Qf3 {It looks bad now with White about to
break through.} O-O-O $1 {The best chance White was running short of time.} 21.
Bxf8 {I was pleased to see this. I was worried about Bishop pins after a later
.......Kb8. White was simply trying to reach the time control now and was
possibly playing for a draw.} Rhxf8 22. Nd3 Kb8 23. Ne5 ({I'd have preffered.} 
23. Nf4) 23... Bxe5 24. dxe5 Qc7 25. b4 Qc4 26. Qe3 e6 27. Red1 h5 28. Qd4 Qxd4
(28... Rc8 {Was possibly more promising.}) 29. cxd4 Rc8 30. Rc5 1/2-1/2

