{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 24 mph} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4.
Nxd4 a6 5. Bd3 Qc7 6. c4 Nc6 7. Nb3 {After some thought.} Nf6 8. O-O Be7 {
After my experiences in the 1/4 final I decided to revert to a Scheveningen
set-up} 9. Nc3 {[13']} d6 {[5']} 10. Be3 Ne5 {Securing Bishop for Knight.} 11.
Rc1 Nxd3 ({Not} 11... Nxc4 $2 12. Bxc4 Qxc4 13. Nd5) 12. Qxd3 Bd7 {Amongst
other things this prevents 13.Na4-b6} 13. Bf4 Nh5 {Forcing the Bishop to
retreat thus easing pressure on the d-Pawn.} 14. Bd2 {[27']} Rc8 {[19']} 15.
Ne2 Nf6 16. Rfd1 {[31']} Bc6 {[24']} 17. f3 {[32']} O-O {[29']} 18. Ned4 {
[47'] After 15' thought he gives up the idea of putting pressure on my d-Pawn.}
({If} 18. Bb4 $2 Rfd8 19. c5 e5 {etc.}) 18... Ba4 {[35']} 19. Qc3 {[54']} Nd7 {
[42'] Black improves his position while White meanders.} 20. Qb4 {[60']} Bxb3 {
[46'] More solid than 20........Nc5} 21. axb3 {[65'] This allows me to force
Queens off.} Qc5 22. Qxc5 ({Obviously not} 22. Qc3 $4 e5) 22... dxc5 23. Ne2
Rfd8 24. Bf4 Kf8 25. Rd3 Bf6 26. Rcd1 {[71'] White was short of time.} Ke8 {
[61']} 27. R1d2 Ne5 {Black is on top now.} 28. Rxd8+ Rxd8 29. Rxd8+ Kxd8 30.
Bxe5 $2 {Played with seconde to spare but he is left with a lost endgame.
However, Black was well on top.} Bxe5 {[65']} 31. Nc3 {[76']} Kc7 {White now
though for 18'} 32. Kf2 {[94']} Kb6 {Black threatens to march down the QS and
win.} 33. g3 {White must waste a move to save his h-Pawn.} Ka5 34. Na2 {
White decides to give up a Pawn to keep the White King out.} Bxb2 35. Ke3 b5
36. Kd3 {[98']} b4 $1 {[75'] Now it's won. White's Knight is trapped , the
Black King will go to the KS the White King must follow and the Black a-pawn
advances.} 37. f4 Kb6 38. Kc2 Ba3 {Keeping the Knight trapped. White can
hardly exchange it.} 39. e5 Kc6 40. Kd3 Kd7 41. g4 Ke7 42. g5 {Whites only
hope is to block the KS to stop the Black King getting through.} f6 43. h4 fxe5
44. fxe5 Bb2 $1 {And wins. The King must gaurd the e-Pawn. The a-Pawn will
advance win the Knight and the Queen} 45. Ke4 a5 {Since White can do nothing
it might be more accurate to fix the White Pawns on Black squares by.......} ({
........} 45... g6 {On the other hand it may prolong the game by one move.})
46. h5 {[1hr 55']} Kd7 {[1hr 31'] Playing it absolutely safe.} ({In fact} 46...
a4 {wins without trouble.}) 47. Kd3 {He might just as well lose actively than
passively. He could save a Pawn by playing......} ({..........} 47. g6 {
first but it's all the same in the long run.}) 47... Bxe5 48. Nc1 Bf4 49. Ne2
Bxg5 50. Ng3 {[1hr 59']} Be7 {[1hr 35']} 51. Ke4 Bd6 {My best win for some
time, to retain the local area title against a 200+ rated player.} 0-1

