1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Nc3 Qc7 6. Be3 Bb4 7. Bd2 Nc6 8.
Nxc6 bxc6 9. Qg4 g6 ({Probably} 9... Bf8 {was better. However, I had been at a
conference in Manchester all day, had been ill and was very tired. I knew that
I was playing badly.}) 10. Bd3 d5 11. e5 $5 {Opening a few lines but rather
doubtful.} Qxe5+ 12. Be2 Qd6 13. a3 Bc5 14. Na4 Ba7 15. Qh4 e5 16. Bh6 Nxh6 17.
Qxh6 Qf6 18. O-O e4 19. b4 $2 Bb8 $2 {As I let go of the piece I realised my
mistake.} ({Correct is} 19... Bxf2+ 20. Kh1 (20. Rxf2 Qxa1+) 20... e3 21. Qxe3+
Bxe3 22. Rxf6 Bd4) 20. Qe3 {Else 20.......Bf4 wins the Queen} Bf4 $2 (20... Ba7
$142 {Preventing infiltration on the QS.}) 21. Qb6 O-O 22. Nc5 Qg5 23. Kh1 Be5
24. Rad1 Qf6 25. f4 Bd4 $2 {One mistake follows another.} 26. Nxe4 $1 Bxb6 27.
Nxf6+ Kg7 28. Ng4 f6 29. Bf3 Re8 30. h3 Bf5 $2 {I was half asleep. The
blunders are quite obvious.} 31. c4 h5 32. Nf2 Bxf2 33. Rxf2 dxc4 34. Bxc6 Rad8
35. Rc1 Re3 {Just about surviving.} 36. Rxc4 Rxa3 37. b5 axb5 38. Bxb5 h4 {
He offered a draw here.} (38... Ra1+ $142) {The game was adjourned. He sealed.}
39. Rc1 {The game resumed 7/5/75} Kh6 40. Be2 $4 {Never say die! Now I have a
forced win.} Ra2 41. Kg1 Rdd2 42. Kf1 Bd3 43. Re1 f5 $22 44. g4 hxg3 45. Rg2
Rxe2 46. Rgxe2 Rxe2 47. Rxe2 g2+ 48. Kxg2 Bxe2 49. Kg3 Kh5 50. Kg2 Kh4 51. Kf2
Ba6 52. Kg2 Bb7+ 53. Kh2 Be4 {A nice finish after playing the first session in
a dream.} 0-1

