{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 4. d4 d5 5. Bb5
exd4 6. e5 Ne4 7. Nxd4 Bd7 {Black seemed familiar with this line and played
the opening very quickly} 8. Bf4 $5 {After some thought.} ({Harding's book
considers only} 8. Bxc6 {which is probably best.}) ({Unfortunately} 8. e6 fxe6
9. Bxc6 bxc6 10. Qh5+ g6 11. Qe5 {fails to} Qf6) 8... Nxd4 9. Bxd7+ Qxd7 10.
cxd4 ({naturally not} 10. Qxd4 Bc5) 10... Qf5 ({I was much more concerned
about.} 10... Bb4+) 11. Qa4+ c6 12. Be3 Be7 13. O-O O-O 14. Nc3 ({Less risky
was.} 14. Nd2) 14... Nxc3 15. bxc3 b5 {His best chance is QS action.} 16. Qb3
a5 17. Rfc1 Rfb8 18. Qc2 Qxc2 19. Rxc2 a4 {To prevent 20.a4 which I wasn't
keen on playing anyway.} 20. Kf1 Rc8 21. Rb1 Rab8 22. Rd2 Kf8 23. Ke2 Ba3 {
To prevent 24.Rb2} 24. f4 {Hoping for KS counterplay. Black decides he can't
allow that.} c5 25. dxc5 {Forced.} Bxc5 26. Rxd5 (26. Bd4) 26... Bxe3 27. Kxe3
Rxc3+ 28. Rd3 ({If} 28. Ke2 Rbc8 29. Rb2 a3) 28... Rc2 29. Rd2 Rc3+ 30. Rd3 Rc2
{My8th & 14th moves were rather doubtful. The match was played at The
University of Aston. [P.B.Cook won the Hastings Premier B Tournament 1956- 57 
(7/9)]} 1-0

