{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs 30' then 16 moves per hour} 1. c4 f5 2. d4 Nf6 3.
d5 {He plays this with a great flourish.} g6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. g3 O-O 6. Bg2 e5 7.
dxe6 dxe6 8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. f4 $5 {Played to prevent .......e5. However I can
force this move and his own e-Pawn is left backward.} ({I was more concerned
about} 9. Nb5 {and if} Na6 {possibly} 10. Be3 {attacking the a-pawn. I was
therefore intending} Ne8) 9... c6 10. Nf3 Nbd7 {Intending ...e5 also the
knight may well go to b6 or c5.} 11. O-O Re8 ({If} 11... e5 12. fxe5 Ng4 13. e6
{is a nuisance. White now realised he could not prevent ...e5 and that his own
e-Pawn is backward. he obviously decided that something positive was needed,
and after 30' played...}) 12. e4 $5 {Leads to all sorts of trouble.} fxe4 {
Better than 12........NxP} (12... Nxe4) 13. Ng5 e3 $1 {A useful move the Pawn
stays there for 8 moves.} 14. Nf3 {After 25' thought} ({If} 14. Bxe3 Ng4 15.
Bc1 (15. Bf2 Nxf2 16. Kxf2 Bd4+ 17. Ke1 {Is unhealthy for White.}) (15. Bd2
Bd4+ 16. Kh1 Nf2+ 17. Kg1 Ne4+ {Wins a Piece}) 15... Bd4+ 16. Kh1 Nf2+ 17. Kg1
Nd1+ 18. Kh1 Nxc3) 14... Nb6 {Better than 14.......e5.} 15. Ne5 {[1hr 17']} ({
He can't play} 15. b3) (15. c5) (15. Nd4 {are both bad for him}) 15... Nfd7 $1
{Winning material as he has too much under attack. Also the threatened 16.Nxc6
is prevented.} 16. Ne4 Nxe5 17. fxe5 ({I was expecting.} 17. Nd6) 17... Bxe5
18. Nf6+ Bxf6 19. Rxf6 Nxc4 20. b3 Nb6 21. Bxe3 {The Pawn falls at last.} Nd5
22. Bxd5 ({A touch of desperation. Better was} 22. Rf3 {when} Nxe3 {loses the
e-Pawn} 23. Rxe3) 22... exd5 23. Bh6 Bf5 {A good game against the Lancashire
II match Captain.} 0-1

