{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs 30' then 16 moves per hour} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6
3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 g6 5. Nc3 Bg7 6. Be3 Nf6 7. Nxc6 bxc6 8. e5 Nd5 9. Nxd5 cxd5
10. Bd4 {After much thought.} ({I wasn't too familiar with this line and felt
that} 10. Qxd5 {was too risky However M.C.O.11 col 102 gives} Rb8 {and both}
11. Bc4 (11. Bxa7 {as satisfactory}) ({I was considering} 11. O-O-O $5)) 10...
O-O 11. Be2 d6 12. exd6 Qxd6 13. Bxg7 Kxg7 14. O-O {The trouble with all this
is that I lack space and mobility and my QS Pawns are rather weak.} e6 15. Qd4+
Kg8 16. Rfd1 ({I considered} 16. c4 {but didn't like} Qb4 17. a3 Qa4 18. Rfd1
Ba6) 16... Ba6 17. Bxa6 Qxa6 18. Rd3 {With thoughts of a KS attack.} Rac8 19.
Ra3 Qe2 20. Rc3 e5 {After much thought.} 21. Qxd5 Rxc3 (21... Rcd8 22. Qf3) ({
If} 21... Rfd8 22. Rxc8) 22. bxc3 Rc8 {I completely overestimated my position
here. Black has the better of it but I mistakenly felt that I had the
initiative.} 23. Qd1 Qc4 24. Qe1 {I felt that when he captured the c-Pawn the
Queen exchange followed by Rc1 would be good for me. Unfortunately I am so
tied down that he can pick his moment having first brought his King up.} Rc5 {
[1hr 37']} 25. Qd2 $2 {[1hr 40']} Rd5 ({I was more concerned about} 25... Qb5
26. Z0 Qb2) 26. Qe1 (26. Qd1 a5 27. h3 (27. a4 $142) 27... a4 28. a3 Rxd1+) ({
Not} 26. Qe3 $2 Qxa2 $1) 26... a5 27. a3 (27. a4 $142) 27... a4 28. h3 Rc5 29.
Qd2 Kg7 30. Qe1 Kf6 31. g3 h5 32. h4 Qxc3 $1 {The correct moment.} 33. Qxc3 (
33. Qd1 {may have offered more hope.}) 33... Rxc3 34. Ra2 Kf5 35. Kf1 Ke4 36.
Ke2 Kd4 37. Kd2 Rf3 38. Ke2 e4 39. Ke1 Kc3 40. Ke2 f6 41. Kf1 e3 {Incorrect
assessment of the position early on; trying to play for a win when my opponent
held the initiative. [A.P.Wernitz won the Tournament with 9/11]} 0-1

