{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs 30' then 16 moves per hour} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6
3. Nc3 {I felt he would know more about the Petroff Defence than I.} Nc6 4. Bc4
{A dubious line.} Nxe4 5. Nxe4 ({I intended to answer} 5. Bxf7+ {but spent 15'
deciding it was no good.}) 5... d5 6. Bd3 {I wasn't too happy about this
either. I was particularly concerned with 6......f5} dxe4 7. Bxe4 Bd6 8. Bxc6+
$5 {Giving up Bishop for Knight to get a better endgame, but the open lines
favour Black.} bxc6 9. d4 e4 (9... exd4 {seems good for Black.}) 10. Ne5 Bb7 $2
{A mistake leading to trouble.} 11. Qg4 O-O ({It's difficult to find a good
move here. Not good enough is} 11... Bb4+ 12. c3 Qxd4 13. Qxg7 Bxc3+ 14. bxc3
Qxc3+ 15. Bd2 Qxa1+ 16. Ke2 {and wins.}) 12. Bh6 Qf6 13. Bg5 Qe6 {Now his
pawns are mangled.} ({I thought} 13... h5 {was best.}) 14. Qxe6 fxe6 15. Nd7
Rf5 16. Be3 e5 17. dxe5 Bxe5 18. Nxe5 Rxe5 {He offered a draw here (Hopefully!)
} 19. O-O-O {[62']} Kf7 {[1hr 29']} 20. Rd7+ Re7 21. Rhd1 Bc8 {[1hr 40']} 22.
Rd8 {[1hr 11']} a5 {[1hr 53']} 23. Rh8 {[1hr 15']} Re8 24. Rxh7 Bf5 25. Rh4 ({
Not} 25. Rh5 $4 Bg4) 25... Rad8 26. Rxd8 Rxd8 {[2hr 7']} 27. Bd2 {[1hr 27'] So
as to be able to play Rh5 if needed.} a4 28. Rf4 Ke6 29. g4 Bg6 {[1hr 19']} 30.
Bc3 ({Not} 30. h4 Ke5 {Threatening 31......RxB}) 30... Rh8 $2 {Getting short
of time he blunders.} 31. Bxg7 {[1hr 35']} Rxh2 32. Rf6+ Ke7 33. Rxg6 Kf7 {
[2hr 25']} 34. Rxc6 {Wins but with unnecessary difficulty.} (34. Rh6 {is
easier. With 34.Rxc6 I felt I'd have no great problems with my extra Pawns.})
34... Kxg7 35. Rxc7+ Kf6 36. Rc8 Kg5 37. Rf8 Kxg4 38. a3 (38. b3 {is answered
by} a3 39. Z0 Rh1+ 40. Kd2 Ra1) 38... Rh3 39. Kd2 Rh1 40. Ke2 $2 {Getting
tired I relax.} ({Correct was my original intention} 40. Kc3 {and if} Rc1 ({
I was worried about} 40... Rf1 {threatening 41......e6 but I always have a
check to get the Rook out of the way.}) 41. b4) 40... Rc1 {He just made the
time control.} 41. Rc8 Rb1 42. Rb8 Rc1 43. c3 Kf4 44. Rf8+ {To push the Black
King back so I can get my King to e3.} Ke5 45. Kd2 ({It may now be my only
hope of a win if Black plays correctly is} 45. Rd8 {and if} Rc2+ 46. Rd2 {
but I can't find a clear win after} Rc1 {. Fortunately he goes wrong.}) 45...
Rf1 46. Ke2 Rb1 $2 {Now it's lost} ({Correct was} 46... Rc1 {repeating the
position of two moves back.}) 47. Rb8 Kf4 ({If} 47... Rc1 48. Rb5+ $2 ({so} 48.
Rb4 Rc2+ {can be answered by} 49. Ke3) 48... Kf4 49. Rb4 {with the Black Rook
able to give perpetual check}) 48. Rb4 Rc1 49. f3 {Winning both Black Pawns.}
Rc2+ 50. Kd1 Rh2 51. fxe4 Ke3 52. Kc1 Kd3 {Threatening mate.} 53. Rd4+ Ke3 54.
Kb1 Rh1+ 55. Ka2 Re1 56. Rxa4 Kd3 57. Kb3 {A lot of ups and downs. I was
rather too complacent after about move 20 and relaxed too much in the endgame.}
1-0

