{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs 30' then 16 moves per hour} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 {
Must be in vogue at the moment.} 3. Nc3 Bb4 {[1']} 4. Nd5 Nxd5 {[10']} 5. exd5
O-O 6. c3 Ba5 (6... Bc5 {seems better.}) 7. d4 exd4 8. Nxd4 d6 9. Be3 Nd7 10.
Be2 Re8 {[35']} 11. O-O {[21']} h6 {[43']} 12. Bd3 Nf6 13. Qf3 {He said
afterwards that he was very unhappy here.} Ng4 14. Rae1 Bd7 15. Bf4 Qf6 16. h3
{[55'] I felt that I would get a good endgame but there may be better here.} ({
Maybe} 16. Ne6) 16... Ne5 {[1hr 22']} (16... g5 {is not as good.}) 17. Bxe5
Rxe5 18. Qxf6 gxf6 19. f4 $5 {The endgame is not so good as I had expected.} ({
I had originally intended} 19. Nf3 {but saw} Rxd5 20. Be4 Rh5 21. b4 Bb6 22.
Bxb7 Rb8 23. Be4 Bb5 $1) 19... Rxe1 20. Rxe1 Bb6 21. Re7 Rd8 22. Kf1 Bxd4 23.
cxd4 Kf8 24. Re2 Re8 25. Rc2 {I still felt that I had the edge.} c6 26. Kf2 (
26. dxc6 {simply activates his Bishop.}) 26... cxd5 27. Rc3 Rc8 28. Rb3 Rc7 29.
Ke2 {The King goes to d2 to prevent Rook infiltration.} Ke7 30. Kd2 {[1hr 36']}
a6 {[1hr 57']} 31. Bc2 $2 ({Not best. I wanted to attack his front d-Pawn and
if} 31. Be2 Bf5 $1 {However, the text may possibly lead to a lost ending.})
31... Rxc2+ 32. Kxc2 Ba4 33. Kd3 Bxb3 34. axb3 Kd7 35. Ke3 (35. Ke3 f5 36. Kf3
Kc6 ({Fritz gives -0.72 [Dick's notes years later]} 36... Ke6 37. Ke3 Ke7 38.
Kd3 h5 39. Ke3 Kf6 40. b4 Ke7 41. Kf3 f6 42. Kg3 Kf7 43. b3 b6 44. Kh4 Kg6 45.
Kg3 Kg7) 37. Kg3 Kb5 38. Kh4 Kb4 39. Kh5 Kxb3 40. Kxh6 Kxb2 41. Kg7 a5 42. h4
a4 43. h5 a3 44. h6 a2 45. h7 a1=Q 46. h8=Q b5 {and it is difficult to stop
his b-Pawn.}) 35... f5 {[2hr 26'] Getting short of time he now offered me a
draw. I accepted as he may have a win. I feel I should have made more of my
superior opening.} 1/2-1/2

