Nf3 e6 4. g3 b6 5. Bg2 Bb7 6. O-O Be7 7. Nc3 O-O {[1']} 8. d5 {[20'] A sharp
line.} Bb4 {[9'] A better move than it looks at first sight.} 9. Ne1 {[50']} ({
He spent 30' examining various lines of the} 9. dxe6 dxe6 10. Ng5 {type but
didn't like them.}) 9... Bxc3 {[15']} 10. bxc3 {[50']} e5 11. c5 {[60']
Doesn't turn out as well as he'd hoped.} e4 ({If} 11... bxc5 12. Qb3) 12. c4 ({
Possibly} 12. cxb6 {first was better as I am able to hang onto my extra Pawn.})
12... bxc5 13. Rb1 Ba6 14. Qa4 Qc8 {15.RxN was threatened.} 15. f3 d6 {[42']}
16. Bb2 {[1hr 26']} ({If} 16. fxe4 {simply} fxe4 {is good for me. I would have
threats of moves like .......Qe8 as the Queen exchange would lose his c-Pawn.})
(16. Bg5 {seems better than 16.Bb2 as the Bishop would be on a better diagonal.
}) 16... exf3 {[45'] Taking advantage of his last move.} 17. Bxf3 ({Now} 17.
Nxf3 Ne4 {ties his Knight down.}) 17... Nbd7 18. Nd3 $2 {Loses another Pawn.} (
18. Rc1 {Is rather better although Black is still well on top.}) 18... Nb6 {
[49']} 19. Qc2 {[1hr 49']} Bxc4 20. Bxf6 Bxd3 ({If} 20... Rxf6 21. Nf4 Z0 22.
Ne6) 21. Qxd3 Rxf6 22. e4 f4 {[65']} 23. Qe2 {[2hr 4']} fxg3 24. hxg3 Qh3 25.
Bg2 {Giving up another Pawn for the faint hope of an attack.} Rxf1+ 26. Rxf1
Qxg3 27. Rf3 Qg6 ({If} 27... Qe5 28. Qf1 Qe7 {(Intending Rf8)} 29. Bh3 {
is good for White.}) 28. Qf2 Nd7 29. Rg3 Qf6 30. Rf3 Qa1+ 31. Kh2 Qe5+ 32. Kh1
Rb8 33. Qf1 {[2hr 18']} Nf6 {[1hr 40']} 34. Rf5 Qb2 35. e5 {A last try} dxe5
36. Rxf6 gxf6 37. Qxf6 Qc1+ 38. Bf1 Qf4 39. Qe6+ Kh8 40. d6 Qxf1+ {I last
played against this opponent at Bognor Regis in 1963} 0-1

