{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs 30' then 16 moves per hour} 1. Nf3 f5 {I felt
that an IM would be well up on most openings, and that I would do best to
stick to the system I'd played earlier in the tournament.} 2. d4 Nf6 3. g3 b6
4. Bg2 Bb7 5. O-O e6 6. c4 Be7 7. Nc3 O-O 8. d5 {[7'] I was fairly happy with
this having been in this position in my last game but one.} Bb4 {[7']} 9. Nd4 {
[14'] P.Dean had thought for 30' and played 9.Ne1. Rellstab's move is much
better.} Bxc3 {[11']} 10. bxc3 {[14']} exd5 {[22'] White threatened simply PxP.
} (10... Qe7 {is prevented by} 11. d6) (10... Qc8 {is very passive}) ({If} 
10... e5 11. Nxf5) 11. Bg5 {[21'] As I had expected} ({If} 11. Nxf5 Ne4) 11...
h6 {[32']} 12. Bxf6 {[22']} Rxf6 {[34']} ({If} 12... Qxf6 {then} 13. Nb5 {
is a nuisance. Also after 12.Rxf6 the Rook isn't badly placed on f6.}) 13. cxd5
Na6 14. Qc2 Qf8 15. e3 ({I felt he might try} 15. e4 {but he didn't like} f4)
15... Nc5 16. Rad1 a5 ({If} 16... Re8 17. Nb5) 17. Nb3 {[35']} Rd8 {[59']} (
17... Nxb3 {unites his Pawns and may allow him to break open the QS. I played
the Rook to d8 rather than e8 because of the possibility of}) (17... Re8 18.
Nxc5 Qxc5 19. Qa4 {attacking the d-Pawn.}) 18. Rd4 Ba6 19. Rfd1 {[42']} Nb7 {
[75']} 20. Bf1 {This surprised me. He felt that my Bishop was quite strong but
simply 20.c4 was simpler.} (20. c4) 20... Bxf1 21. Kxf1 Nd6 22. c4 {[48']} Ne4
{[1hr 25']} 23. Nd2 {[50'] Again he felt that my Knight was too strong.} Nxd2+
{[1hr 32']} (23... Ng5 24. Kg2 Z0 25. h4 {gets me nowhere.}) (23... Nc5 {
was an alternative.}) 24. R1xd2 d6 {Else 25.c5} 25. Kg2 {[52']} Re8 {[1hr 35']}
26. Re2 Rf7 27. Red2 {[59']} Rfe7 {[1hr 50'] He now asked me if I was played
for a win. I felt it was drawn so draw agreed. A solid draw against a titled
player. L.Rellstab had an Elo of 2265 (203 BCF)} 1/2-1/2

