{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nc3 Nc6 4. Bb5 {
Deviating from my doubtful line 4.Bc4 v D.G.Ellison B.C.F. Maj Open 8/87/75}
Bb4 5. O-O d6 $5 {Interesting. Not given in M.C.O.11} ({More usual is} 5... O-O
) 6. Nd5 Bc5 7. d4 exd4 8. Nxd4 Bd7 9. Nb3 ({Tarrasch best games p.290 gives} 
9. Nf5 $1) 9... Ne5 10. Bxd7+ Nfxd7 11. Nxc5 Nxc5 12. f4 {Black wasn't looking
too happy.} Nc6 {Better than.....} ({....} 12... Ned7 13. Qg4) 13. f5 (13. Qg4
Qd7 14. Qxg7 O-O-O {is good for Black.}) 13... Qd7 14. Bg5 Ne5 15. Bf6 $5 {
Looks good but is probably premature. I should have defended the e-Pawn first.}
Nxe4 16. Bxg7 Rg8 {I now ran short of time trying to find a good continuation.}
17. Nf6+ (17. f6 {is it clear.}) 17... Nxf6 18. Bxf6 Qc6 19. Qe2 Kd7 20. Bxe5 {
Lancaster lost the match 2 - 4 "A disappointing result"} 1/2-1/2

