{Time limit 24 mph} 1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 e6 {Amove which he lives to
regret. I decided now that if I could exchange my front d-Pawn for his c-pawn
then the Pawn on e6 is misplaced.} 4. Bb5+ c6 5. dxc6 Nxc6 6. c3 {The most
solid line.} Bd7 7. Nf3 Be7 {[11'] Rather passive c.f.7.......Bd6} 8. O-O {[8']
} O-O {[12']} 9. Re1 Re8 10. Nbd2 a6 11. Bd3 b5 {[23']} 12. a3 {[14']} Bd6 $5 {
Leads to trouble.} (12... Nd5 13. Z0 Bf6 {may offer more.}) 13. Ne4 Nxe4 ({If} 
13... Bc7 14. Bg5 {Puts on the pressure, but now Black's KS looks bad.}) 14.
Rxe4 {My intentions are clear.} Ne7 {Trying to prop up the KS} 15. Rh4 Nf5 (
15... Ng6 {Would be answered the same way.}) 16. Rxh7 $1 {I could hardly play
anything else in this position.} Kxh7 17. Ng5+ (17. g4 {is too slow.}) 17...
Kg8 ({If} 17... Kg6 18. Qg4) 18. Qh5 Nh6 19. Nh7 $3 {0.75/0 This was the move
I had to see before sacrificing the Rook. [many years later with Fritz Dick
looked at the game again] After 19.Nh7 Fritz gives Black better} f5 {Trying to
block linesbut it's no use.} ({Fritz gave} 19... Nf5 20. Ng5 Qf6 21. Qh7+ Kf8
22. Ne4 Qg6 23. Qxg6 fxg6 24. g4 Bc7 25. Nc5 Bc6 26. gxf5 exf5 27. Bd2 Bd6) ({
One line I considered was} 19... g6 20. Qxh6 Bf8 21. Qh3 {and if} e5 22. Qxd7
$1) 20. Bxh6 gxh6 21. Qg6+ Kh8 22. Qxh6 (22. Nf6 {is more precise}) 22... Kg8 (
{Black could now prolong the game by} 22... Bf8 {but misses it} 23. Nxf8+ Kg8
24. Nh7 Re7 25. Nf6+ Kf7 26. Bxf5 exf5 27. Nxd7 Rxd7 ({else if} 27... Qxd7 {
he loses a Rook}) 28. Re1 {I feel White should win.}) 23. Qg6+ Kh8 24. Nf6 Qe7
25. Qh6+ Qh7 26. Qxh7# {A very pleasing win.} 1-0

