{Time limit 36 moves in 1hr 30' (then adjudication)} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3
Nf6 4. cxd5 cxd5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Bf4 Bf5 7. e3 e6 8. Bb5 $5 {Trying too hard. I
felt at the time that this was inferior to 8.Bd3 but wanted to break the
symmetry. The is too loose an attitude against this class of opponent, However.
............} Bd6 9. Bxd6 Qxd6 10. O-O O-O 11. a3 ({I felt that this defeat
was psychologically self-inflicted. I knew that the "correct" move was} 11. Bd3
{but automatically shrank from} Bxd3 12. Qxd3 {which leaves a symmetrical
position with Black to move!}) 11... Rac8 12. Bxc6 {Needless to say 12.Bd3 is
better.} Qxc6 {[22']} 13. Ne5 {[38']} Qa6 {[26']} 14. g4 {I have no way of
countering the c-file so counterplay is needed.} Bg6 {[30']} 15. f3 {[46']} Rc7
16. h4 Nd7 17. Nxg6 {[61']} ({I considered} 17. Nxd7 Rxd7 18. e4) 17... hxg6
18. Rc1 $2 {I rather lost the thread around here.} Rfc8 19. Qd2 $2 {Played
under the misapprehension that I could reply to 19.......Nb6 with 20.b3 Qxa3
21.Nb5} Nb6 {[45']} 20. Rf2 {[75']} ({I now realised in the above line...} 20.
b3 Qxa3 21. Nb5 {that Black could play...} Qxc1 22. Rxc1 Rxc1+ 23. Qxc1 (23.
Kg2 R1c2 24. Qxc2 Rxc2+) 23... Rxc1+) 20... Nc4 21. Qe1 Qb6 22. Na4 Qb3 23. Nc5
{[35']} Qxe3 24. Qxe3 Nxe3 25. Re1 Nc4 26. h5 {With no time left and
adjudication looming desperate measures are called for.} gxh5 27. gxh5 Nd6 28.
h6 gxh6 29. Nxe6 fxe6 30. Rxe6 Rg7+ 31. Kh1 Nf5 32. Rf6 Rf8 33. Re6 Nxd4 34.
Rxh6 Rxf3 {0 White lost on time. K.L lost 6 -} 0-1

