{Time limit 20 mph} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Nc3 Qc7 6. Be3
Nf6 7. a3 b5 8. Bd3 Bb7 9. f3 {[9']} d6 {[5']} 10. Qd2 Be7 11. O-O {[12']} Nbd7
12. Rad1 Rc8 13. Nb3 O-O 14. Rfe1 Rfd8 15. Qf2 {Preventing 15.......Ne5 which
I intended.} Nc5 16. Nxc5 dxc5 17. Be2 {White begins to meander a bit and
Black gets on top.} Bd6 18. g3 {[24']} h5 {[24']} ({I was vaguely looking at
lines like} 18... b4 19. axb4 cxb4 20. Bb6 Qxb6 21. Qxb6 Bc5+ 22. Qxc5 Rxc5 {
which unfortunately end in} 23. Rxd8+ {Thus 18......h5 gives the King an
escape and might lesd to .....h4 later.}) 19. Bd3 Qc6 20. Rd2 $2 {He minces
round for too long and loses a Pawn.} Be5 21. Nb1 c4 22. Bf1 c3 23. bxc3 Bxc3
24. Nxc3 Qxc3 25. Rxd8+ Rxd8 26. Bc5 Rd2 27. Bb4 Rxf2 28. Bxc3 Rxf3 {After
much thought} 29. Bb4 {Threatening to win the exchange.} Ng4 30. Bd3 Ne5 31.
Rd1 Nxd3 32. cxd3 g5 33. Rd2 Kg7 34. Bc3+ Kg6 35. Kg2 $2 ({I thought that he
might try} 35. Rf2 {hoping for} Rxd3 36. Rf6+ {with chances. I would have
replied as in the game with.....}) {......} 35... Bxe4 36. Bb4 Rxd3+ 37. Kf2
Rxd2+ 38. Bxd2 Kf5 39. Ke3 Bc2 40. h3 e5 41. Bc3 Ke6 42. Bb2 f5 {I would have
resigned. It can't be much fun for White. However.......} 43. Bc3 f4+ 44. gxf4
gxf4+ 45. Kf3 Kf5 46. Bd2 e4+ 47. Ke2 Bd3+ 48. Ke1 e3 49. Bc1 Ke4 {White lost
as he appeared to have no clear plan after initial development.} 0-1

