{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 Qb6 5. Nf3 Bd7
6. Be2 Bb5 {I studied this line a couple of years ago but couldn't remember
much about it.} 7. O-O Bxe2 8. Qxe2 Qa6 9. Qxa6 ({He was expecting} 9. Qd1)
9... Nxa6 10. Be3 Rc8 11. Nbd2 c4 {After some thought, Black must now aim for
an advance on the b-file, so action on the other wing seems best.} 12. Ne1 Ne7
13. f4 f5 {Unwilling to let me force open the f-file.} 14. exf6 gxf6 15. Nef3
Nf5 16. Bf2 Bd6 17. Nh4 {I felt that this would open the position and give me
winning chances but Black gets enough counterplay on the e-file.} Bxf4 18. Nxf5
exf5 19. Rae1+ Kd7 20. Be3 Bxe3+ 21. Rxe3 Rce8 22. Rxe8 Rxe8 23. Rxf5 Re2 24.
Rf2 Re1+ 25. Nf1 Ke6 26. g4 Nc7 27. Kg2 Ne8 28. Ng3 Nd6 29. Kh3 Ne4 30. Nxe4
Rxe4 31. Kh4 b5 32. a3 a5 {He offered a draw here.} 33. Kh5 b4 34. axb4 axb4
35. h4 1/2-1/2

