{Time limit 24 mph} 1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. Nc3 Nb6 4. d4 e6 5. a3 d6 6. Qg4
dxe5 7. dxe5 g6 8. Bd3 Nc6 9. Nf3 Bg7 10. Bg5 f5 11. Qh4 Qd7 12. O-O-O Qf7 13.
Bb5 Bd7 14. Bf6 $5 {This was my first game after 3 weeks of flu. Both I and my
play were a bit shaky.} h6 ({Rather better seems} 14... Bxf6 15. exf6 O-O-O ({
Not} 15... O-O $4 16. Ng5)) 15. Bxg7 Qxg7 16. Qf4 O-O-O 17. h4 a6 18. Bxc6 {
After much thought} ({I wanted to play} 18. Ba4 {then Bb3 but} Nxa4 {wins my
e-Pawn.}) 18... Bxc6 19. Nd4 Bd5 20. Qg3 Qf7 21. Nxd5 Rxd5 22. Ne2 Nd7 {
Now I acquire a passed Pawn.} 23. Rxd5 exd5 24. f4 Rg8 25. Qe3 Nb6 26. b3 $2 {
Weakening. My play is rather poor around here, still out of form and feeling
unwell.} Qe7 27. Kb2 c5 28. c3 Rd8 29. Ka2 Kc7 30. Rd1 Kb8 31. g3 Na8 32. Qf3
Nc7 33. b4 $2 Qe6 34. Kb2 Qc6 35. Qe3 Ne6 36. bxc5 $2 {I think I must have
been half asleep around here.} Qb5+ 37. Ka1 Qa4 38. Qc1 Nxc5 39. Nd4 {How did
my position get this bad?} Nb3+ {I was pleased with this it eases the tension.}
40. Nxb3 Qxb3 41. Rd3 Rc8 42. Qb2 Qc4 43. Re3 Qf1+ 44. Qb1 Qf2 45. Qd3 Qg1+ 46.
Kb2 Rc5 47. Re2 Rb5+ 48. Ka2 Qc5 {The game was adjourned here.} 49. Qd4 {
[Sealed move] The game was resumed 15/12/75} Qe7 $2 {Seems to lose. As does....
..} ({......} 49... Qxd4 50. cxd4 Kc7 51. e6 Kd8 52. e7+ Ke8 53. Re6) ({.....or
} 49... Qc4+ 50. Qxc4 dxc4 51. e6) ({.....or} 49... Kc7 50. e6 Kd8 51. e7+ Ke8
52. Qh8+) ({Correct is} 49... Ra5 $1 50. Qb4 ({Dick analysed with Fritz years
later.} 50. Qxc5 Rxc5 51. e6 Rc8 52. e7 Re8 53. Kb2 Kc7 54. Re6 h5 55. Kb3 Kd7
56. Rxg6 Rxe7 57. Rh6 Re3 58. Rxh5 $14) 50... Rb5 51. Qxc5 Rxc5 {and now I
wanted to play} 52. Kb2 (52. h5 gxh5 53. Kb2 Rc6 54. e6 Rc8 55. e7 Re8 56. Re5
Kc7 57. Rxd5 Rxe7 58. Rxf5 Re3 59. Rxh5 Rxg3 60. Rxh6 Rg4 {which seems drawn.})
52... Kc7 (52... h5) 53. h5 $1 gxh5 54. Rh2 {and wins but Black could play
instead 52.......h5! Therefore 52.h5}) 50. Rb2 ({Not} 50. e6 Rc5 51. Re5 b6 $1
52. Rxd5 $2 Qxe6) 50... Rxb2+ ({If} 50... Rc5 51. Rb6) 51. Kxb2 Qd7 52. Qc5 Qd8
53. e6 {Seems more active than marching my King around to win his d-Pawn.} Qc7
{Else 54.e7} 54. Qxd5 Qb6+ 55. Ka2 Qf2+ 56. Kb3 Qb6+ 57. Ka4 Qc7 58. c4 b5+ {
The best chance.} 59. cxb5 Qc2+ 60. Kb4 ({Not} 60. Ka5 Qc3+ 61. Kxa6 $4 Qxa3+
62. Kb6 Qa7+ 63. Kc6 Qc7#) 60... Qb2+ 61. Qb3 Qd4+ 62. Ka5 Qd8+ 63. Kxa6 Qc8+
64. Ka5 Qc7+ 65. Kb4 Qd6+ 66. Kc3 Qc5+ 67. Kd3 Qd6+ 68. Ke2 Qd4 69. Qe3 Qc4+
70. Kf2 Qa2+ 71. Qe2 {Solid play in the second session.} 1-0

