{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs.} 1. f4 e5 2. fxe5 d6 3. exd6 Bxd6 4. Nf3 g5 5.
d4 g4 6. Ng5 f5 7. e4 h6 8. e5 {[5']} Be7 {[25'] All "book" but he was more
familiar with it than I was.} 9. Nh3 gxh3 10. Qh5+ Kf8 11. Bc4 Qe8 {Apparently
out of date.} ({M.C.O. gives} 11... Rh7) 12. Qxh3 Qc6 ({Possibly} 12... Qg6 {
would be better}) 13. Bd3 Qg6 14. O-O Nc6 {I can't save the f-Pawn.} 15. c3 {
[30']} Kg7 {[50']} 16. Bf4 {[43'] This surprised me. he declines the Pawn for
development.} (16. Rxf5 {is interesting.}) 16... Bg5 17. Qe3 {[54']} Nge7 {
[63']} 18. c4 {White tries to mobilise his central pawns.} Bxf4 19. Rxf4 Nb4 {
[75']} 20. Nc3 {[62']} c6 21. Raf1 Be6 22. R1f3 Kf8 ({If} 22... Kh7 {the
h-Pawn is very weak.}) 23. Ne4 {Looks good but Black keeps playing actively.}
Nxd3 24. Qxd3 Rg8 25. Rg3 Qf7 26. Rxg8+ Qxg8 27. Nd6 Qg5 28. Rf1 b6 {The
presence of the clock was becoming apparent to us both here.} 29. b3 Kg7 30. g3
Rf8 {It was all a bit of a rush to move 40 now.} 31. Qf3 Qg4 32. Kg2 Qxf3+ 33.
Kxf3 Kg6 34. Ke3 Rd8 35. Rd1 Kg5 36. Kf3 Rf8 37. h4+ Kg6 38. Ke3 Rd8 39. Kf4
Rf8 40. Rd2 (40. Rd2 Rd8 {White's Knight is immobile his Rook must stay on the
d-file (else .......Nc8) so..} 41. Rd1 {say} Kh5 42. Rd2 (42. Kf3 Ng6 43. Ke3
Bd7 44. Nf7 Rf8 45. Nd6 Kg4 46. b4 c5 47. bxc5 bxc5 48. Rg1 Rb8 49. Nf7 cxd4+
$17 {0.90/0 Dick & Fritz}) 42... Ng6+ (42... Rf8 43. Rf2 Ng6+ 44. Ke3 Kg4 45.
Rf3 f4+ 46. gxf4 Nxf4 {wins}) 43. Kf3 (43. Ke3 $1) 43... c5 $1 {wins}) 40...
Rd8 {Adjudicated. Won for Black. The match depended on this result. Cumbria
won 8.5 - 7.5} 0-1

