1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bc4 e6 7. Bb3 Be7 8. Be3
e5 {A little inconsistent.} 9. Nf5 Bxf5 10. exf5 Nbd7 11. Nd5 Nc5 12. Bc4 b5
13. Nxf6+ Bxf6 14. Bd5 Rc8 15. O-O O-O 16. c3 Qe7 17. Qd2 Kh8 18. Rae1 g6 19.
Qc2 Qd7 20. f4 $1 {Leads toanadvantageous endgame for White.} Qxf5 21. Qxf5
gxf5 22. fxe5 Bxe5 23. Bh6 Bg7 24. Bxg7+ Kxg7 25. Rxf5 Nd3 26. Re2 (26. Re7 {
is too risky.}) 26... Rc7 27. Rd2 Ne5 28. Bb3 Rc6 29. Rf4 f6 30. Rh4 h6 {
Here the game was adjourned. I sealed 31.a4. The game resumed on 9/1/76} 31. a4
bxa4 32. Bxa4 Rb6 33. Rhd4 Rfb8 34. b3 Rd8 35. c4 {The advance of the c-Pawn
decides it} Nf7 36. c5 Rbb8 37. cxd6 Rb6 38. d7 Ne5 39. Rd6 Rxd6 40. Rxd6 Kf7
41. Rxa6 Ke7 42. Ra7 Rb8 43. d8=Q+ Kxd8 44. Rh7 Rb4 45. Rxh6 Ke7 46. Rh3 Rd4 {
Black now manages to drag the game out but it's never really in doubt.} 47. Re3
Kf7 48. h3 Rd1+ 49. Kh2 Rd2 50. Bb5 Rb2 51. Re2 Rb1 ({If} 51... Rxb3 52. Rxe5
Rxh3+ 53. Kxh3 ({Not} 53. gxh3 $4 {when the queening square is the wrong
colour.})) 52. Re3 Rb2 53. Rc3 Kg6 54. Bc4 Kg5 55. Kg3 f5 56. h4+ Kf6 57. Bd5
Rd2 58. Bf3 Rd4 59. Kh3 Rb4 60. g3 Rd4 61. Kg2 Rd2+ 62. Kf1 Rb2 63. Bd1 Rd2 64.
Ke1 Rg2 65. Be2 Rg1+ 66. Bf1 Ng4 67. Ke2 Nh2 68. Bh3 {Black managed to get his
Knight stuck.} Rb1 69. Ke3 Re1+ 70. Kd4 Re4+ 71. Kc5 Re5+ 72. Kb4 Re4+ 73. Ka5
f4 74. gxf4 1-0

