{Time limit 20 mph} 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. d4 O-O 5. g3 d6 6. Bg2
Nbd7 7. O-O e5 8. Rb1 {Leaves the Rook vulnerable to .......Bf4, and not
necessary at this stage anyway.} Re8 9. e3 a5 10. a3 c6 11. b4 Nb6 12. Qb3 $2 {
lands him in trouble} (12. dxe5 $142 dxe5 13. Qxd8 Rxd8 14. Nxe5) 12... Bf5 13.
Rb2 Bd3 14. bxa5 Nxc4 15. Rd1 Nxb2 16. Bxb2 e4 ({Not} 16... Ba6 17. dxe5) 17.
Ne1 Ba6 18. Qb6 d5 19. Bh3 Bf8 20. Na4 Bb5 21. Qxd8 Rexd8 22. Nc5 Bxc5 {
I relaxed a little too much around here and White gets a lot of play.} 23. dxc5
Ne8 24. Bc3 f5 25. Nc2 Nc7 26. Nd4 Ba6 27. Bf1 Kf7 28. Rb1 Rab8 29. Rb6 Bxf1
30. Kxf1 Rdc8 31. Rb1 Ne6 {Doubtful.} 32. Nxe6 Kxe6 33. h4 Rc7 $2 {An
oversight. I saw my mistake straight away. (playing too fast)} 34. a6 Ra8 35.
axb7 $2 ({Correct was} 35. Ba5 Rf7 36. axb7 Rb8 37. Rb6 $1) 35... Rb8 36. Ba5
Rcxb7 37. Rxb7 Rxb7 38. Bb6 d4 39. exd4 Kd5 40. a4 Rb8 41. a5 Ra8 42. Ke1 Kxd4
43. Ke2 h6 44. Kd2 g5 45. hxg5 hxg5 46. Ke2 f4 47. gxf4 gxf4 48. Kd2 e3+ 49.
Ke2 f3+ {Fairly typical of the "fast" evening games (i.e. games with a
reasonable mph but where one has to play fast to try and finish the game in
one evening)} 0-1

