{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 g6 4. d4 Bg7 5. Bg5 f6
({Not relishing} 5... Nge7 6. d5 Nb8 7. d6) 6. Be3 d6 7. Bc4 Nh6 8. h3 Qe7 9.
Nbd2 Nf7 {[19']} 10. Qe2 {[35']} O-O {[20']} 11. O-O-O Bd7 12. dxe5 {Although
I get an attractive looking position it may have been better to attack on the
KS} dxe5 {[30']} 13. Nb3 {[46']} b6 {[34']} 14. Bd5 {[50']} a5 15. Qc4 {[58']}
Qe8 ({Too risky is} 15... a4 16. Na1 Na5 17. Qxc7) 16. Rd2 $2 {This and te
next move but one are strategically wrong. I should attack on the KS.} a4 17.
Na1 Kh8 18. Rhd1 (18. Nc2 $142) 18... Nd6 19. Qe2 a3 $1 {[59'] Now I'm in
trouble whatever I do.} 20. b3 {[68'] The c-Pawn is left fearfully weak.} f5 {
[59'] Threatening to open the long diagonal.} 21. exf5 {[1hr 22']} (21. Bxb6 {
isn't good enough.}) 21... gxf5 {[68']} 22. g3 {[1hr 28']} Ra5 {Now I am
probably lost.} 23. b4 Nd4 $1 {Breaking open the position in a decisive manner.
I had also run short of time.} 24. cxd4 {Short of time I was unable to analyse
it properly so I took this way and hoped for the best.} Rxd5 {[1hr 20']} 25.
dxe5 (25. Nb3) (25. Nc2 {both were possibly better. I was rushing
unnecessarily and should have taken more time here.}) 25... Bb5 {Black has
threats everywhere.} 26. Qe1 Rxd2 27. Bxd2 Qc6+ 28. Nc2 Qxf3 29. exd6 Be2 30.
dxc7 Bxd1 31. Qxd1 Bb2+ {Incorrect strategy in the early middle game and poor
use of time nearer the end. Lancaster lost the match. The score in Dicks book
was 4 - 1 to Bolton with 1 game left to be decided on board 5 Kazim
Lenartowitz v Nighel Short!! Jeff had an ELO rating of 2405.} 0-1

