{Time limit 40 moves in 2 hrs} 1. b3 Nf6 2. Bb2 g6 3. d4 Bg7 4. c4 O-O 5. g3 d6
6. Bg2 c6 7. Nf3 Bg4 {Intending to swap off Bishop for Knight.} 8. O-O Nbd7 $6
{As it turns out I should have taken the Knight to fulfil my original
intention.} 9. Nfd2 {Leaving my Bishop very embarassed.} d5 10. f3 {[18']} Be6
{[20']} 11. Na3 c5 12. e3 Rc8 13. Rc1 a6 14. Qe2 dxc4 15. bxc4 cxd4 16. exd4 h5
17. Nc2 Nh7 $2 {Too casual.} 18. Ba3 {[45'] Threat 19.d5} Re8 {[37']} 19. d5
Bf5 20. Ne3 {Rather awkward but I have a saving move.} Qa5 {White threatened
21.g4} (20... Z0 21. g4 Nb6 {or f8} 22. Nxf5 {isn't too good.}) 21. Nxf5 Qxa3
22. Nxg7 Kxg7 23. Ne4 f5 $6 24. Nf2 Nhf6 25. g4 hxg4 ({I wanted to play} 25...
Nxd5 {but} 26. Qd2 {is too good for White}) 26. fxg4 fxg4 27. Nxg4 b5 {Setting
him a few problems.} 28. Rf3 $4 {One of those days.} ({Correct is} 28. Ne5 $1)
28... Qxc1+ 29. Rf1 Qxc4 30. Qe6 Qxg4 {K.Wells was Cumberland County Champion
in 1963.} 0-1

