1. d4 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nc3 e6 4. g3 Be7 5. Bg2 O-O 6. e3 h6 {Adopting a 'wait
and see policy'.} 7. Nge2 d6 8. O-O a6 9. b4 Qe8 $5 {The problem with this
type of game. Against a G.M. I would play 9.......e5 with a good game. However
the Queens may come off and I MUST beat this opponent so I play a 2nd best
move to stop it becoming drawish. Objectively I should still play 9......e5.} (
9... e5) 10. Nf4 g5 {and this is too loosening.} 11. Nd3 c6 12. Qb3 Kg7 13. Bb2
Nbd7 {My position is pretty rotten.} 14. e4 {I was more concerned about........
} (14. d5) 14... fxe4 15. Nxe4 Nxe4 16. Bxe4 Nf6 17. Bg2 Qg6 18. Rae1 Bd7 {
I wasn't happy.} 19. d5 $2 (19. c5 $142) 19... cxd5 20. cxd5 e5 21. Nxe5 $5 (
21. Bxe5 {wins a pawn as} dxe5 22. Nxe5 {is too dangerous for Black.}) 21...
dxe5 22. Bxe5 Bb5 23. Be4 (23. d6 {first was better.}) 23... Qf7 24. Bd3 Bxd3
25. Qxd3 Bxb4 26. Rb1 Bc5 27. Rb2 Kg8 28. d6 Nd7 29. Rxb7 $2 {Getting it over
with.} Nxe5 30. Rxf7 Nxd3 31. Rxf8+ Rxf8 32. d7 Rd8 0-1

