{Time limit36 moves in 1hr 30'} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 Nc6 3. Nf3 e6 {Following my new
policy of writing my moves down before playing them I wrote down 3......d6
here but then preffered the text move.} 4. Nc3 a6 5. a4 {I seem to have him
worried already.} d5 {Expecting to end up with an isolated Pawn but with good
piece play. I also considered......} ({........} 5... Qa5 6. Z0 {followed by}
b5) 6. exd5 exd5 7. d4 Nf6 8. Be3 cxd4 9. Bxd4 Nxd4 10. Qxd4 Be7 11. O-O-O {
Risky but attacking the d-Pawn.} O-O {Willing to give up the d-pawn for active
play.} 12. Bd3 {Deciding that the d-Pawn was too hot.} ({If} 12. Nxd5 Nxd5 13.
Qxd5 Qb6 ({or} 13... Qc7 {with good play.})) 12... Qc7 13. Rhe1 ({If} 13. Nxd5
Nxd5 14. Qxd5 Qxf4+ 15. Kb1 Qxa4 {However his Queen is getting a little
cramped.}) 13... Rd8 ({If} 13... Bc5 {he is forced to play} 14. Nxd5) 14. Rxe7
$5 {He seemed to have decided that something spectacular was needed else I was
getting on top.} Qxe7 15. Re1 Qd6 16. Re5 b6 17. f5 $2 {I dodn't like this.}
Bb7 18. g4 {[56']} Nd7 {[1hr 16']} 19. Ne4 {Desperation.} Qf8 20. f6 (20. f6
Nxe5 21. Neg5 Nxd3+ $2 22. Qxd3 g6 23. Nxh7 Kxh7 $2 (23... Qh6+ $1) 24. Ng5+
Kg8 25. Qh3) 20... Nxe5 {As I had to make 16 moves in 13 minutes he might have
tried for something like 21.N4-g5 A good effort. The match was played at
Ambleside Library.} 0-1

