{Time limit 48 moves in 2 hrs.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5.
Nc3 g6 6. Bc4 Bg7 7. Bb3 O-O 8. f3 Nc6 9. Be3 Bd7 10. Qd2 Ne5 {[5']} 11. O-O-O
{[7']} Rc8 {[5']} 12. h4 $2 {The start of much rubbish in this and the next
few games, but I was already feeling unwell and I hope these games are not
typical of my play.} h5 13. Bh6 Nc4 {[10']} 14. Bxc4 Rxc4 15. Bxg7 Kxg7 {[10']}
16. Rhe1 {[36']} Qa5 {[11']} 17. Kb1 {[50']} Rfc8 18. Nce2 {[60']} Qxd2 19.
Rxd2 b5 {[36']} 20. a3 $2 {Doubtful.} a5 21. c3 b4 22. cxb4 axb4 23. b3 R4c7
24. a4 $2 {[1hr 16'] Completely oblivious to what was coming, But I was
half-dead by now and rather past caring.} e5 {[46']} 25. Nc2 {[1hr 13']} d5 $1
{[47'] Ouch!} 26. Nc1 {[1hr 21']} dxe4 27. fxe4 Bc6 28. Nxb4 Bxe4+ 29. Kb2 Bf5
30. Ne2 {No doubt there were some better moves around here.} Rb7 {[59']} 31.
Na2 {[1hr 40']} Ne4 {Wins the exchange} 32. Rdd1 Nf2 33. Rd2 Nd3+ 34. Rxd3 Bxd3
35. Nec3 e4 36. Nxe4 {Without thought and beyond caring.} Re7 37. Nac3 Rce8 {
Amongst my other troubles were the poor lighting and the freezing cold. The
Congress was held at Norbreck Castle Hotel, Blackpool.} 0-1

