{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 g6 5.
Bd3 Bg7 6. c3 {Hardly necessary.} Nc6 7. Be3 Nf6 8. f3 O-O 9. Nd2 Bd7 10. O-O
a6 11. Rc1 Ne5 12. Be2 {[32']} d5 {[12']} 13. c4 dxe4 14. Nxe4 Nxe4 15. fxe4 h5
16. h3 Nc6 17. Nxc6 {[48']} Bxc6 {[20']} 18. Qc2 Qa5 19. b3 Rad8 20. Rfd1 Qe5
21. Bf3 Qc7 22. Qf2 Qe5 23. Qc2 f5 24. Rxd8 Rxd8 25. Bb6 Rd7 26. Re1 Bh6 27.
Bf2 Rd2 28. Qb1 fxe4 29. Bxe4 Qf6 30. Bf3 {[1hr 14']} Bxf3 {[51']} 31. gxf3
Qxf3 32. Qxg6+ Bg7 33. Qg2 Qxg2+ 34. Kxg2 Bd4 35. Rf1 Rxa2 36. Kg3 h4+ $2 {
Over elaborating. A rubbish move. Exchanging wins easily.} 37. Kf3 Bxf2 38.
Rxf2 Ra3 39. Rb2 Ra1 40. Kg4 Rg1+ 41. Kxh4 Kf7 42. Re2 Kf6 43. Re3 {The game
was adjourned. The game resumed 29/3/76. I sealed:} Rg7 {I felt that I had
winning chances still.} 44. Rg3 {As expected.} Rh7+ 45. Kg4 Ke5 46. h4 ({
I felt his best hope was} 46. Kf3) 46... Kd4 47. h5 e5 48. Rh3 (48. Kg5 {
isn't good enough.}) 48... e4 49. h6 e3 50. Kf3 Kd3 51. Rh5 ({If} 51. Rh2 e2) (
{If} 51. Kf4 Kd2) 51... Rf7+ 52. Kg4 e2 53. Rd5+ Ke4 {This game won the Club
Championship with one game to go - careless stuff on move 36, however. D.J.
Barr was 1975 Champion.} 0-1

