1. e4 Nc6 2. Nf3 e5 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Qh4 5. Nc3 {M.C.O. 11 gives both 5......
Nf3 and 5.....Nb5 as better than this.} Bb4 6. Qd3 {Again M.C.O. gives 6.Nb5}
Nf6 ({Possibly} 6... Bxc3+ {is best.}) 7. Bd2 Bxc3 8. Bxc3 Ne5 ({I didn't like
} 8... Qxe4+ 9. Qxe4+ Nxe4 10. Nb5 {However I don't like 8.....Ne5 either.}) 9.
Qe3 O-O $5 {Makes it interesting.} 10. Nf5 Qxe4 11. Bxe5 $5 ({If} 11. Qxe4 Nxe4
12. Bxe5 Re8) ({However} 11. Ne7+ Kh8 12. Qxe4 Nxe4 13. Bxe5 Re8 14. Bxc7 {
may be best.}) 11... Qxf5 12. Bxf6 $2 (12. Bd3 $142) 12... Qxf6 13. Be2 d5 (
13... Qxb2 {is rather risky.}) 14. c3 Bg4 15. O-O $2 {Played instantly. Having
seen one little trap he looks no further.} Rfe8 16. Qd2 $2 ({Relatively best
was.} 16. Qxe8+) 16... Rxe2 17. Qxd5 Rxb2 18. f3 Bh3 19. Rf2 Rxf2 20. Kxf2 Qb6+
21. Kf1 Bxg2+ 22. Kxg2 Qb2+ 23. Kg3 Qxa1 24. Qxb7 Re8 25. Qxc7 Qg1+ 26. Kh3 h6
27. Qd7 Re5 28. Qd8+ Kh7 29. Qh4 g6 {Kirkby Lonsdale Club Ch RAC 7/7 Barr 5
Kneale 5 Colton 3 Yoxall 2.5 White 2 Nadin 2 France 1.5} 0-1

