{Time limit 20 moves per hour.} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nc3 {As earlier this
season.} Nc6 4. Bb5 Bb4 5. O-O O-O {[14']} 6. d3 {[3']} d6 7. Bg5 Bg4 {[23'] M.
C.O. 11 gives this a '?'. I had a feeling that it was wrong but couldn't
remember the correct continuation.} 8. Bxf6 {[12']} ({The line which I
couldn't remember was} 8. Nd5 Nd4 9. Nxb4 Nxb5 10. Nd5 Nd4 11. Qd2 c6 12. Nxf6+
gxf6 13. Bh4 Bxf3 14. Qh6) 8... gxf6 {[32']} 9. Ne2 Bxf3 10. gxf3 Ne7 11. f4 {
[21']} c6 12. Ba4 f5 13. c3 Ba5 {Completely symmetrical. In general the
symmetry is unlikely to favour Black.} 14. Qd2 Kh8 {[45']} 15. Kh1 {[30']} fxe4
({I was amazed that he didn't play.} 15... Qd7) 16. dxe4 d5 {A bit risky,
especially as he was running short of time.} 17. exd5 exf4 18. Qd4+ f6 19. Nxf4
Qd6 20. Ne6 Rf7 21. Ng5 ({I rather fancied} 21. dxc6 Qxe6 22. cxb7 Rb8 23. Bb3
{However....} Qc6+) 21... Rff8 22. Ne4 Qxd5 23. Qxd5 Nxd5 24. Nd6 b5 ({
Alternatively} 24... Rab8 25. Nxb7 Rxb7 26. Bxc6 Rxb2 {etc}) 25. Bb3 Nf4 26.
Rad1 Bc7 $2 {Fatal. Possibly he realised it as he offered a draw here.} ({
He had to get some room for his King e.g.} 26... f5) 27. Nf7+ Kg7 (27... Rxf7 {
Relatively better.}) 28. Rg1+ Ng6 29. Rd7 Bb6 30. Ng5+ {My 5th title in 6
years. "Dr. R.A.Collins of Lancaster won the Lancaster and Morecambe Chess
league individual level when he defaeted P.T.Seery of Lancaster in the final.
This is his third consecutive win and his fifth win in six seasons" Lancaster
Gaurdian 7/5/76} 1-0

