{Time limit 20 moves per hour.} 1. f4 e5 2. fxe5 d6 3. exd6 Bxd6 4. Nf3 g5 5.
d4 g4 6. Ng5 f5 7. e4 h6 {[9']} 8. e5 Be7 9. Nh3 {All as in Turnock v Collins 
[28/2/76]} Bh4+ $2 {After some thought and not particularly good. I felt that
Black must take the Knight to justify his whole opening policy.} 10. g3 {[4']}
Qd5 {I didn't like this either} 11. Nf2 Bg5 12. Nc3 Qa5 13. Bxg5 {[9']} hxg5 {
[39']} 14. Qd2 {[10'] I felt that I probably had a won game now.} Nc6 {[46']}
15. O-O-O {[12']} Nce7 {[52']} 16. Bb5+ {To make him block the long white
diagonal.} c6 17. Bc4 Nd5 {[56'] A Pawn had to go anyway and this seems best.}
18. Nxd5 {[18']} ({On reflection I rather prefer} 18. Bxd5 cxd5 19. Qxg5) 18...
Qxd2+ 19. Rxd2 cxd5 20. Bxd5 Ne7 21. c4 {Probably OK.} Nxd5 22. cxd5 Bd7 23.
Rc2 {[25']} Ke7 24. Nd3 {Doesn't turn out too well.} b6 25. Kd2 $2 {Starting
to dither I missed Black's reply or rather the strength of it.} Raf8 $1 {
Excellent!} 26. Ke3 $2 {Seems to lose but it's difficult to find a good move.
Maybe 26.e6 or 26.R2c1} (26. Rc7 {Looks good but} f4 27. gxf4 g3 {is horrible})
26... f4+ {White seems to be lost.} 27. gxf4 {What else?} Rh3+ 28. Kd2 Bf5 29.
d6+ {My only hope.} ({If} 29. Nf2 Rf3 {wins a piece.}) 29... Ke6 $2 {Salvation!
} ({After} 29... Kd8 {White could resign...almost.}) 30. d5+ Kxd5 31. Nb4+ Ke6
32. Rc7 {Threatening mate.} Be4 33. Rf1 {The h-Pawn has to go.} Rxh2+ 34. Ke3
Bf3 ({Not} 34... Rxb2 35. Re7+ Kf5 36. fxg5+) 35. Re7+ Kf5 36. fxg5 Kxg5 ({If} 
36... Rxb2 {I had considered} 37. d7 Z0 {threatening} 38. Rf7+) 37. Nd3 Re2+
38. Kd4 Re4+ 39. Kc3 b5 ({If} 39... Rc8+ 40. Rc7) 40. d7 Rd8 41. Re1 Rc4+ 42.
Kd2 Rd4 43. e6 Rh8 44. Re5+ Kg6 45. Ke3 Rc4 46. Re8 Rh7 47. Nf4+ Kg7 48. d8=Q {
This was the deciding game in the Club Championship. One or two errors but an
exciting game.} 1-0

