{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs then 10' for the rest} 1. e4 c6 2. Nf3 d5 3. Nc3
dxe4 {Having studied Keene's cassette on the 5.......gxN line I hoped to
transpose.} 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Nxf6+ gxf6 6. Bc4 Bf5 7. d3 Qc7 8. Qe2 Nd7 9. h3 Bg6
10. Be3 e6 11. O-O-O b5 12. Bb3 a5 13. a3 a4 14. Ba2 b4 15. axb4 Bxb4 16. c3
Be7 17. Kd2 {Getting worried.} Rd8 18. Ke1 Nb6 19. Kf1 {A pity he can't castle.
} Nd5 20. g3 a3 21. Bxd5 Rxd5 22. b4 O-O 23. Kg2 Ra8 24. d4 Qb7 25. Kh2 a2 26.
Ra1 Qa6 27. Qxa6 Rxa6 28. Nd2 Rd8 29. Rhe1 Bd6 30. f4 Rda8 31. Nc4 Bc7 32. Red1
Bc2 33. Rd2 Bb3 34. Nb2 Bd6 35. Kg2 Ra3 36. Kf2 Bd5 37. Nd1 Be4 38. Rb2 Bb1 39.
Ke2 Kg7 40. Kd2 {White was short of time.} Kg6 41. Ke2 e5 42. b5 {A touch of
desperation here.} Rb8 43. b6 exd4 44. Bxd4 c5 45. Be3 Ra6 46. c4 Raxb6 47.
Rxb6 Rxb6 48. Nc3 Rb2+ {The clock was now stopped and 10' added to eachgiving
him 11' and me 21'. He claimed that he knew nothing of the 10' rule despitr
ample documentation. We continued and he kept grumbling and reading the rules.}
49. Kf3 f5 {Threatening ......Be7-f6. White continued to complain and after 5'
played (deliberately?)} 50. Na4 $2 Be4# {A pleasing game for my first trial
with this line.} 0-1

