{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs then 10' for the rest} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 Nc6 3. Nf3
e6 4. Nc3 d5 5. e5 {Leads to a poor game.} (5. exd5 $142 exd5 6. Bb5) 5... Nge7
6. d4 Nf5 {I was already unhappy. What do I do about the d-Pawn?} 7. Bb5 Bd7 8.
Bxc6 Bxc6 {That didn't help much.} 9. Qd3 {Hoping to be able to play Be3.} Qb6
{No chance! What now? I decided to give up the d-Pawn, hopefullyonly
temporarily, to block the centre.} 10. g4 {Trying to force him to exchange
Knights so that .....Ne3 won't occur later.} cxd4 $5 {Surprise!} (10... Nxd4
$142) 11. gxf5 ({I spent some time considering} 11. Nxd5 {but was unhappy about
} Qa5+ ({In view of the following variations Black would probably play.} 11...
Bxd5) 12. Kf2 Bb5 {as after} (12... Nh6 13. Rg1 O-O-O 14. Nxd4 Rxd5 15. Be3 Bc5
16. Qc3 Bxd4 17. Bxd4 Qd8 18. Rad1 Qh4+ 19. Qg3 Nxg4+ {[Dick & Fritz]}) 13. Qd1
{Black wins a piece by} ({However, White has the resource} 13. Nc7+ $1 {
winning a piece}) 13... Nh6) (11. Ne2 Bb5 12. Qd2 Bxe2 13. Kxe2 Ne3 14. Qxd4
Nxc2 15. Qa4+ Qc6 16. Qxc6+ bxc6 17. Rb1 h5 18. g5 Bc5 {[Dick & Fritz]}) 11...
dxc3 12. bxc3 (12. fxe6 {is just too reckless.}) 12... Bc5 13. fxe6 Bf2+ 14.
Kd1 fxe6 15. Nd4 Bxd4 16. Qxd4 Qxd4+ {Here he offered a draw which I accepted.}
1/2-1/2

