6. Bh4 g5 7. Bf2 Bb4 8. exf5 (8. e5 {Seems better, but he was playing like
lightning.}) 8... exf5 9. Qe2+ Kf7 10. O-O-O Bxc3 11. bxc3 Qd6 12. Kb2 Nc6 13.
c4 Qb4+ 14. Ka1 Qc3+ 15. Kb1 Nb4 16. cxd5 {Threatening to exchange everything
off by 17.Qc4. However, he was playing so fast that I that I thought that I
might be able to tempt him into an obvious error.} Qa3 17. Qc4 b5 $1 18. Qb3 ({
If} 18. Qxc7+ Bd7) 18... Qxb3+ 19. cxb3 Nbxd5 20. Bxb5 $4 {As I'd hoped he
took the Pawn instantaneously} Nc3+ 21. Kb2 {Losing not just a Bishop but two
Rooks as well.} Nxd1+ {He obviously hadn't adjusted to "40 - minute" play and
played the whole thing like a "10 - second" game} 1-0

