{Time limit 40' for all moves} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 4. d4 d6 5. Bc4
Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. h3 Nxe4 8. Bd5 Bf5 {He felt doubtful about this afterwards
and the Bishop may have a better home on a6 after the exchanges.} 9. Re1 Nf6
10. Bxc6 bxc6 11. dxe5 dxe5 12. Qxd8 Rfxd8 13. Nxe5 Bc5 {Black gets good play
for the Pawn.} 14. b4 {Hoping to push him off that diagonal (15......Ne4 is
threatened) also trying to free my QS.} Bd6 15. Nxc6 Re8 16. Be3 $5 (16. Bd2
$142) 16... Nd5 17. Bd2 Rxe1+ 18. Bxe1 Bd7 19. Nd4 a5 $5 {Behind on the clock
he decides that active play is best. However, White gets a passed Pawn.} 20.
bxa5 Rxa5 21. c4 Ra4 22. cxd5 Rxd4 23. Nc3 Be5 24. a4 $1 Bc8 {Intending to go
to a6 to Blockade the Pawn.} (24... Rc4 {is answered by} 25. a5 $1) 25. Rb1 {
Black has back rank weaknesses as well.} c6 {Giving up another pawn.} 26. dxc6
Rc4 27. Nd5 {White has all the play now.} Kf8 28. Bb4+ Ke8 29. Re1 f6 30. f4
Rd4 31. fxe5 Rxd5 32. exf6+ Kf7 33. fxg7 Kxg7 34. Re7+ Kg6 35. Re8 Ba6 {
Loses the Bishop but it was hopeless anyway.} 36. c7 Rd1+ 37. Kh2 Rc1 38. Re6+
{A good result against the Cumbria top-board.} 1-0

