{Time limit 40' for all moves} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3
Nc6 6. cxd5 Nxd5 7. Bc4 Nf6 8. Nge2 e6 9. O-O Be7 10. Bf4 a6 11. a3 O-O 12. Rc1
b5 13. Ba2 Bb7 14. Qd2 b4 {Probably premature.} 15. axb4 Bxb4 16. Bb1 Na5 $5
17. Qd3 {Rather a nuisance.} g6 18. Bg5 Be7 19. Rfe1 Rb8 {Either.....} (19...
Rc8) ({or} 19... Nd5 {were preferable}) 20. Nf4 Nd5 21. Nxe6 $1 {Possibly
unsound but at this rate of play Black is in trouble.} fxe6 22. Rxe6 Rf5 23.
Bxe7 Nxe7 24. Rce1 Nec6 25. Ne4 Bc8 26. Rd6 Qf8 27. Qc3 Qf7 {Threats along the
diagonals are ominous. I couldn't find a good move.} 28. d5 Ne5 {Help!} 29.
Rd8+ Kg7 30. Nd6 {Crunch! The Queen is lost. After much frantic thought I
decide on 30......Nf3+ 31.gxN Rg5+. I picked up the Knightto play ......Nf3+
and realised my King was en-prise (King captures were allowed in this
tournament) ....so Resigns. A good attack by White. I was pushing too hard
early on and left too many weaknesses.} 1-0

