6. Nc3 Bb4 7. Qc2 O-O 8. O-O Bxc3 9. Qxc3 Ne4 10. Qc2 Nc6 11. a3 a5 12. d5 exd5
13. cxd5 {[9']} Ne7 14. Nd2 Nd6 $5 (14... Nxd2 $142 15. Qxd2 d6 {With pressure
against his d-pawn}) 15. Nc4 Ne4 {Deciding to transpose into the previous
variation if the White Knight goes back to d2.} 16. Bf4 Bxd5 ({I wasn't too
keen on} 16... Nxd5 17. Bxe4 fxe4 18. Qxe4 Nxf4 19. Qxb7 Nxe2+ {as my Knight
is rather out on a limb.}) 17. Ne3 Bc6 18. Rfd1 $2 ({I had expected} 18. Nxf5 {
which seems to regain his Pawn with a fair position.}) 18... Ng6 $1 {Taking
advantage of his Bishop's placement.} 19. Bxe4 fxe4 20. Qc4+ Kh8 21. Nd5 ({
I expected} 21. Ng2) 21... Bxd5 22. Qxd5 Nxf4 23. gxf4 Rxf4 24. Qxd7 Qg5+ 25.
Kf1 Rxf2+ $1 26. Kxf2 Rf8+ ({Not} 26... e3+ 27. Kf3 {and the King escapes}) 27.
Ke1 e3 {A neat finish.} 0-1

