1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bc4 e6 4. c3 a6 5. d4 b5 6. Be2 Bb7 7. Nbd2 Nf6 8. Bd3
Be7 9. O-O Nbd7 {I wasn't happy about castling as e5 would give him a big KS
attack.} (9... O-O 10. e5) 10. a4 bxa4 11. Rxa4 O-O {At this stage I
remembered my game against Phil Seery in the Individual final a couple of
years ago. I might be able to hit at the Rook with .....Qc6 later on} 12. Qe2
Qc8 {White has knidly left his Rook undefended.} 13. e5 Nd5 {Threatening 14....
.Nf4} 14. exd6 (14. Ne4 $142) 14... Bxd6 15. Ng5 ({Again} 15. Ne4) 15... N7f6
16. Nde4 Be7 17. c4 $2 {Starting to go wrong. In some lines this simply loses
the d-Pawn.} Nxe4 18. Nxe4 ({If} 18. Bxe4 Nb6 {and maybe} 19. Bxb7 Qxb7 20. Ra3
Bxg5 21. dxc5) 18... Nb4 19. dxc5 $2 {11 Missing the threat I've been trying
to engineer since move} ({About his only move was} 19. f3 {answered probably by
} cxd4) 19... Nxd3 20. Qxd3 Qc6 21. Ra3 (21. Nc3 Qxg2#) 21... Qxe4 22. Qxe4 {
White carries on but I have plenty of time.} Bxe4 23. Rg3 Bxc5 24. Rd1 Rfd8 25.
Rxd8+ $2 {Loses a piece.} Rxd8 26. h3 Rd1+ 27. Kh2 Rxc1 28. b3 Bd6 1-0

