{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr} 1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 c6 4. Bg5 e6 {Leads to
a cramped position.} 5. Qd2 Nbd7 6. Nf3 (6. f4 {Was given consideration.}) 6...
Qc7 7. O-O-O h6 8. Be3 Be7 9. h3 O-O $2 {Risky} 10. g4 e5 $2 {It's difficult
to find a good move but this does nothing to stem the tide.} 11. g5 hxg5 12.
Bxg5 Re8 {There seem to be no good moves} 13. Rg1 Nh5 14. Bc4 Ndf6 15. Bh6 g6 {
Not really a mistake as White has so many threats...} ({....if say} 15... Be6
16. Bxg7 Nxg7 17. Qh6 Bf8 18. Qxf6 Bxc4 19. Rxg7+ Bxg7 20. Rg1) 16. Rxg6+ Kh8
17. Bg7+ {Short ans sweet! On the same evening I beat P.J.Colton in the same
competition.} 1-0

