1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Nc3 Nc6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 a6 6. Bc4 Nf6 7. Bg5 g6 $5 8.
Bxf6 exf6 9. Qd2 Bg7 (9... Be7 $142) 10. O-O-O Qc7 {Losing a pawn but possibly
he had no choice.} 11. Nxc6 Qxc6 12. Qxd6 Qxd6 13. Rxd6 O-O 14. Nd5 b5 15. Bb3
Bb7 16. Ne7+ Kh8 17. Bd5 Bxd5 18. Nxd5 Rfd8 19. Rxd8+ Rxd8 20. f4 $5 f5 21. Re1
fxe4 22. Nc7 ({I now noticed that} 22. Rxe4 {is answered by} Bxb2+ {so he had
to change plans.}) 22... f5 23. Nxa6 Ra8 24. Nb4 Bf8 25. Nc6 ({Help! If} 25. a3
Bxb4 26. axb4 Ra1+ 27. Kd2 Rxe1 28. Kxe1 Kg7 {and if say} 29. c4 Kf6 $1 {Draws}
) 25... Rxa2 26. Kb1 Ra6 27. Nd4 b4 28. Nb3 Rd6 29. Re2 h5 $2 {Weakens his
g-Pawn if my Knight reaches e5.} 30. g3 Kg8 31. Nd2 Rd4 32. Ka2 Kf7 33. Kb3 Ke6
34. Nf3 Kd7 $4 35. Nxd4 {Fortunately one can rely on this type of error
cropping up to save the day inthese very fast games where the clock rules.} 1-0

