{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5.
Nxf6+ gxf6 6. Ne2 Bg4 {I'm not sure whether I'd repeat this.} 7. f3 $6 {
Looks odd but turns out surprisingly well.} Bf5 8. Be3 Nd7 9. Qd2 e6 $2 {
I gave this little thought. I underestimated the strenght of his KS Pawn push.}
({Maybe better would be} 9... h5) ({or} 9... Bg6) 10. g4 Bg6 11. h4 h5 12. Nf4
{Suddenly things look black for Black.} Bd6 13. Nxg6 fxg6 (13... Bg3+ 14. Kd1
fxg6 15. f4 {Traps my Bishop.}) 14. Bd3 f5 {The best chance but the position
may be lost.} 15. gxf5 gxf5 16. O-O-O Qf6 17. Bg5 Qf7 {The d-Pawn is too hot.}
18. Bc4 Nf8 ({If} 18... Nb6 19. Bxe6) 19. Rhe1 Kd7 $2 {Missing his reply} ({
Possibly} 19... Be7 {is the only move.}) 20. Bxe6+ $1 {I had superficially
examined this but it came as a big surprise.} Nxe6 21. d5 Nxg5 ({If say} 21...
Nd4 22. dxc6+ Nxc6 23. Qxd6+ Kc8 24. Re7 Nxe7 25. Qd7+ Kb8 26. Bf4#) 22. dxc6+
Kc8 23. Qxd6 Qc7 24. cxb7+ Qxb7 25. hxg5 Qc7 26. Qe6+ {I think that I played
too quickly and superficially. The match was played at the Royal Hotel Kirkby
Lonsdale.} 1-0

