{Time limit 36 moves in 1hr 30'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. d4 cxd4 5.
Nxd4 a6 6. Bc4 e5 7. Nf3 Be7 8. h3 Nbd7 9. Be3 {Doesn't turn out too well.} (9.
Bg5 $142) 9... O-O 10. O-O Qc7 11. Bb3 b5 {My e-Pawn is looking a bit weak} 12.
Nd5 Nxd5 13. Bxd5 Rb8 14. Qd3 Nf6 15. Ne1 Nxd5 16. Qxd5 Be6 17. Qd2 Qc6 18. f3
f5 19. exf5 Rxf5 20. Nd3 Rd8 21. Rad1 Qb7 22. Qa5 {Threatening 23.Nc5} Bc4 23.
b3 Bxd3 24. cxd3 Rff8 25. Qd2 d5 26. Rc1 Rc8 27. Rxc8 Rxc8 28. Rc1 b4 29. Rc2
$2 {Lack of concentration. I had relaxed here and was wondering vaguely why he
was putting Pawns on black squares.} d4 30. Bf2 (30. Bg5 $142) 30... Rc3 {
Crunch!} 31. Rxc3 bxc3 32. Qc2 Qb4 33. Kf1 Qa3 34. Ke2 Qb2 35. Kd1 Qa1+ 36. Ke2
Qb2 {He picked up the Queen, put it on h1, held on and retrived it to b2 in
view of the time control.} (36... Qb2 37. Kd1 {[Adj 0-1]} Qa1+ 38. Ke2 Qh1 39.
b4 (39. g3 Qxh3 40. b4 Qe6 41. a3 Kf7 42. Kf1 Bg5 43. Kg2 Kg6 44. Qd1 Qc6 {
[-2.65 Fritz]}) 39... Qxg2 40. Qa4) 37. Kd1 {Time was called. Adjudicated won
for White but it's ot clear and a number of us were unable to find a definite
win for Black. My problem at the moment is losing concentration. Too many
games maybe.} 0-1

