1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Bd3 Bg6 5. f4 e6 6. Nf3 c5 {Black gets an
improved French Defence out of this.} 7. c3 Nc6 8. Bxg6 hxg6 9. Be3 Rc8 10.
Nbd2 {Declining the c-Pawn.} b6 11. Ng5 {Designed to prevent 11......f6 which
I wasn't intending anyway.} Nh6 12. g4 Be7 13. Nh3 cxd4 14. cxd4 $2 {He
probably didn't give this much thought but it's suicidal.} Nb4 15. Kf2 Nc2 16.
Rb1 ({Now if} 16. Rc1 Nxe3 17. Kxe3 Rxc1 18. Qxc1 Nxg4+) 16... Bh4+ ({I also
considered} 16... Nxe3 17. Kxe3 Nf5+ 18. gxf5 Rxh3+) 17. Kf3 (17. Ke2 {is a
little better}) 17... Nxg4 {Naturally.} 18. Nf1 Be1 $1 {Piling on the pressure
the threat is 19......RxN} 19. Ng1 Qh4 20. Qe2 ({The threat amongst other
things} 20. Z0 Ngxe3 21. Nxe3 Qf2+ {etc.}) 20... Ngxe3 {With various threats
including mate on g4 and the Knight fork on d4. White has no move} 21. h3 {
At least preventing 21......Qg4# ...but does not prevent} Qh5# {Violent stuff!
I also beat Brian Burton in the same tournament.} 0-1

