{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. d4 f5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. g3 b6 4. Bg2 Bb7 5. c4 e6
6. O-O Be7 7. b3 ({I have normally faced} 7. Nc3 {in this position.}) 7... O-O
8. Ba3 {There is some reason to suppose that White's hopes were no higher than
a draw. He certainly gets on advanatage from this.} Bxa3 ({Afterwards I felt
that} 8... d6 {might have been preferable as} 9. Ng5 {is no problem.}) 9. Nxa3
a6 {Played reluctantly....} ({....but} 9... Qe7 10. Nb5 {is a nuisance.}) 10.
Nc2 Qe7 11. Nce1 d6 12. Nd2 {The other Bishops go but his KS white squares
prove, at the end, to be a fatal weakness.} Bxg2 13. Nxg2 Nc6 14. e3 Nd8 {
Possibly too slow aiming for h6. Maybe......} ({....} 14... e5 {is better.})
15. Qc2 Nf7 (15... Nf7 {Discouraging} 16. e4 {in view of the exchanges} fxe4
17. Nxe4 Nxe4 18. Qxe4 {followed by} Ng5) 16. f4 {Deciding to block it up.} d5
{After much thought.} 17. Nh4 {This gives me a chance to create some play.} ({
After} 17. c5 {it is hard to see how I can make appreciable progress against
an opponent playing for a draw.}) 17... c5 18. Nhf3 Rac8 19. Rac1 Nd6 20. Ne5
g6 {To give the option of capturing on d5 with the e-Pawn if necessary.} 21.
Ndf3 Qb7 22. Qe2 a5 23. a4 Nfe4 24. Nd2 Rfd8 25. Rfd1 Nxd2 {If I were to play
25.....Qe7 the position would be symetrical apart from my Knight being one
square foreward. Getting short of time I felt that I had to try to create some
winning chances.} 26. Rxd2 dxc4 27. bxc4 Ne4 28. Rdd1 cxd4 29. exd4 Rd6 30. Qe3
Rcd8 31. Nf3 Nc5 {I had 12' left he had 19'.} (31... Qd7 {is probably better
but I was hurrying now.}) 32. Ng5 h6 33. Re1 {I saw a glimmer of hope now.}
hxg5 34. dxc5 gxf4 35. gxf4 ({Not} 35. Qxf4 $4 Rd2) 35... bxc5 36. Rb1 (36.
Qxc5 $4 Rd2) 36... Qc6 37. Rb5 {Apparently regaining his Pawn.} Rd1 38. Rxa5 $4
{For 37 moves I haven't had a look in, but with me in time trouble he commits
a suicidal Pawn grab.} (38. Rxa5 R8d2 {In view of my time trouble 4' left [for
10 more moves] he might have tried.} 39. Ra8+ {as} Qxa8 {gets him a draw} ({
However I was ready with} 39... Kf7 $1 40. Ra7+ Ke8 41. Ra8+ Kd7 42. Ra7+ Kc8
43. Ra8+ Kb7)) 38... R8d2 {Perseverance pays off, for 3hr30' I thought that
I'd be going home with only half a point.} 0-1

