{48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 Nf6 2. Nc3 d5 3. e5 d4 4. Nce2 {I've been waiting
some time tp play this line having seen it in one of Tal's games.} Ng8 {
After some thought} ({If} 4... Nfd7 5. e6) ({but} 4... Ng4 {is possible.}) 5.
Nf3 Nc6 6. h3 {I felt I had time for this as 6.......Bg4 would be a nuisance.}
Bf5 (6... f5 {is worth considering.}) 7. d3 {[5']} e6 8. g4 Bg6 9. Bg2 ({Maybe
} 9. a3 {was worth a move.}) 9... Bb4+ 10. Bd2 {[10']} Bxd2+ 11. Qxd2 h6 12. a3
{[12']} ({If} 12. Qf4 {to win the d-Pawn then} Nb4) 12... Nge7 13. Nf4 Qd7 14.
c4 $5 {Risky. The opening of lines favours Black to some extent. c4 controls
d5 if he doesn't take, but I underestimated his QS chances after exchanging.}
dxc3 15. bxc3 Na5 16. Rb1 Rd8 17. Nxg6 Nxg6 18. d4 b6 {Black won't castle till
I do.} 19. O-O O-O 20. Qc1 {I was intending h4-h5 & g5 to open up his KS.} Qe7
21. Re1 c5 22. dxc5 $5 {Again underestimating Black's resources.} Qxc5 {
Now I couldn't find a good move. Black threatens both 23.....Nc4 23......Rd3}
23. Bf1 Nc4 24. Bxc4 Qxc4 25. Rb4 Qd3 26. Kg2 Qd5 {Threatening 27.......Nh4+.
He offered a draw here.} 27. Kg3 Qc5 28. Rd4 {I didn't particularly like the
reply 28.....Rd5, but in view of his offered draw I expected him to swop.} Rxd4
(28... Rd5) 29. cxd4 Qc8 30. h4 {[66'] I still fancied a KS attack.} Ne7 {
[1hr 31']} 31. Qd2 Qd7 32. h5 Rc8 33. Rc1 Rxc1 34. Qxc1 Qc6 35. Qxc6 Nxc6 36.
Kf4 {I felt that my greater command of space and advanced King gave me the
better practical chances.} Ne7 {Black decides that d5 is the square for his
Knight. Maybe so.} 37. Ke4 Nd5 38. Nd2 Kf8 39. Nc4 a5 {There seems no reason
to weaken his b-Pawn unless forced to do so.} 40. Nd6 Ke7 41. Nb5 {To prevent
41......Nc3+} Kd7 42. f4 Ke7 43. g5 hxg5 {Now he may be lost.} ({Simply} 43...
Kd7) ({or} 43... Kf8 {was OK. Mow I will be able to threaten a h-Pawn advance.}
) 44. fxg5 Kf8 {He was short of time as well.} ({If} 44... Kd7 $2 45. h6) 45.
Nd6 Ne7 46. Kd3 {Simply heading for the QS Pawns.} Kg8 47. Kc4 Nd5 48. Kb5 {
he had little time now and no good move.} f5 {With the QS Pawns doomed he is
forced into desperate measures.} ({I had expected.} 48... Nf4) 49. gxf6 gxf6
50. exf6 Nxf6 51. Kxb6 Nxh5 52. Kxa5 Nf4 53. Kb5 Nd5 54. a4 Nc7+ 55. Kb4 Nd5+
56. Kc5 Kf8 57. a5 Ke7 58. Nc8+ Kd8 59. Nb6 Nc7 60. Kc6 Na6 61. Kb7 Nb4 62. a6
Nxa6 63. Kxa6 Kc7 64. Kb5 Kd6 65. Kc4 Kc6 66. Na4 Kd6 67. Nc3 Kc6 68. Ne4 Kd7
69. Nc5+ Kd6 70. Nxe6 Kxe6 71. Kc5 Ke7 72. Kc6 Kd8 73. Kd6 {Perseverance! K.L.
lost3.5 - 2.5 [R.A.C. 1, Jex 0.5, Kneale 0, White 0, Barr 0.5, Plucknett 0.5] 
[The match was played at the Sun Hotel Kirkby Lonsdale]} 1-0

