{Time limit 48 moves in 2 hours} 1. f4 e5 2. fxe5 d6 3. exd6 Bxd6 4. Nf3 g5 5.
g3 h5 $5 6. d4 g4 7. Nh4 Be7 8. Ng2 h4 {Maybe I was taking this a little
lightly.} 9. Bf4 Bf5 10. Nc3 hxg3 11. Bxg3 Nf6 12. Ne3 Be4 13. Bg2 Bxg2 14.
Nxg2 Nh5 15. Qd3 Nxg3 16. Qxg3 Qxd4 17. Qxc7 Bd6 $5 {Going mad! I got a little
carried away here.} 18. Qc8+ Ke7 19. Qxb7+ Kf8 20. Ne4 {Preventing the
threatened 20......Bg3+ Now what? I cast around.} Rxh2 21. Rf1 (21. Rxh2 {
is a draw.}) 21... Qb4+ {There was nothing else.} 22. Qxb4 Bxb4+ 23. Kf2 f5 $2
{This was really bad. A casual move - I just pushed the Pawn forward' Sheer
laziness.} 24. Kg1 Rh5 25. Ne3 Kg8 26. Rxf5 Rxf5 27. Nxf5 Nc6 28. Nh6+ Kg7 29.
Nxg4 Re8 30. Ngf2 Ba5 31. Rd1 Bb6 32. Kf1 Nd4 33. c3 Nf5 34. Rd7+ Kg6 35. Ke1
Ne3 36. Nd6 $2 Rf8 37. Nde4 Ng2+ {Wins a piece} 38. Kf1 Ne3+ 39. Ke1 Ng2+ 40.
Kf1 Ne3+ {I offered a draw. He looked at the other games and declined.} 41. Kg1
Ng4 42. Rd6+ Kh5 43. Rxb6 axb6 44. Kf1 Ra8 $2 {Rubbish. Laziness again.
Correct is.......} (44... Ne3+ {then} 45. Ke1 (45. Kg1 Ra8) 45... Ra8) 45. Nxg4
Kxg4 46. a3 Kf4 47. Nf2 Rd8 48. Ke1 Ke3 {Adjudiated a win for White. Exiting
early on but sheer casual laziness afterwards. The match was played at R.A.F.A.
Penrith} 1-0

