{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs then 12 moves in 30'} 1. c4 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2
Bg7 4. Nc3 O-O 5. d4 d6 6. Nf3 c5 7. dxc5 Qa5 {[25'] After much thought.} ({
M.C.O. 11 gives} 7... dxc5 8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. Be3 Na6 {as equal but Black doesn't
fancy t so he gives up a Pawn.}) 8. cxd6 exd6 $2 (8... Ne4 {isn't good enough..
...}) ({....but} 8... Rd8 9. O-O Rxd6 {Seems much better. After the text he is
stuck with a weak d-Pawn.}) 9. O-O Nc6 10. Bd2 {Threatening 11.Nd5 or b5
followed by 12.Bc3!} Qh5 {Black decides to attack.} 11. Ng5 $5 ({Maybe} 11. Nb5
{is more solid, but I felt that I may be able to embarass his Queen.}) 11...
Ne5 {[49']} ({Not, for example} 11... Ng4 $4 12. h3 Nf6 13. Bf3) 12. b3 {[38']}
h6 {[54']} 13. Nf3 {[40']} Nfg4 14. h3 {Forced.} Nxf3+ 15. exf3 Ne5 {[61']} 16.
f4 {[51']} Bg4 $1 {His best chance.} (16... Qxd1 {would leave him a lost end
game.}) 17. Qb1 {After much thought} Nf3+ 18. Bxf3 Bxf3 19. Qd3 {[1hr 13']} g5
{[1hr 16']} 20. fxg5 hxg5 21. Qf5 {A good sqaure for the Queen.} Rae8 22. Rae1
Re5 23. Rxe5 Bxe5 24. Rc1 f6 25. Nd5 {[1hr 25']} Kg7 {Black banks on the
h-file.} 26. Nc7 Rh8 27. Ne6+ Kg8 ({If} 27... Kf7 28. Nxg5+) 28. c5 {
Remarkably Black isn't threatening anything. The White h-Pawn is immune, so I
open up the c-file.} dxc5 29. Rxc5 Bc6 {To stop the Rook penetrating. However,
it allows a neat finish.} 30. Rxe5 {Black can resign.} Qd1+ 31. Re1 Qxd2 32.
Qg6# {A good game.} 1-0

