{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. Bd3 c5
6. c3 Nc6 7. Ne2 Qb6 8. Nf3 cxd4 9. cxd4 Bb4+ 10. Bd2 Bxd2+ 11. Qxd2 Qb4 {
Black played all this very quickly and gave the impression he was playing for
a draw.} 12. a3 ({Keres-Flores Buenos Aires 1939 went} 12. Rc1 Qxd2+ 13. Kxd2
$16 {which seems better than my line.}) 12... Qxd2+ 13. Nxd2 ({If} 13. Kxd2 Na5
{is good for Black.}) 13... O-O {After much thought.} 14. Rc1 f6 {Also after a
long think.} 15. f4 Nb6 16. Nb3 Na4 17. Rc2 a6 {Better than......} ({....} 
17... Bd7 18. Bb5 Nb6 19. Nc5) 18. Nd2 Bd7 19. b3 Nb6 20. Nf3 f5 21. h3 Na5 22.
Nd2 Rac8 23. Rc5 Nc6 24. Kf2 Na7 25. Rhc1 Bc6 26. Nf3 Nb5 27. Ng5 Nd7 28. R5c2
Rfe8 29. a4 Nc7 30. b4 {I felt that I had good prospects of a win but a
gradual strangulation policy (possibly with a KS advance) might take another
40 moves and Black only neede to play to move 40. I therefore felt obliged to
do something positive, even if it did seem premature.} Nb6 31. b5 {Hoping that
something would turn up, especially as he was in time trouble.} axb5 32. axb5
Nxb5 33. Rb2 Nc4 34. Bxc4 dxc4 35. Rxc4 Nc7 36. Rc5 h6 37. Nf3 Nd5 38. Nd2 Ra8
39. Nc4 Reb8 40. Na5 Ne7 ({With seconds to spare he avoids} 40... b6 $4) 41.
Nxc6 {Rather frustrating, playing only 40 moves against an opponent who wants
a draw. Lancaster lost 4 - 2 (Collins 0.5, Jex 1, Lawrence 0, Seery 0.5,
Turner 0, Crosby 0) The match was played at Carlisle.} 1/2-1/2

