{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O
f6 6. d4 Bg4 7. dxe5 ({I knew about} 7. c3 {from Fisher's book (p.346) but
wasn't too happy about what to play after 10......QKt3}) 7... Qxd1 8. Rxd1 fxe5
9. Be3 ({Fischer - Smyslov 1967 went} 9. Rd3 {which Fischer gives a !}) 9...
Nf6 10. h3 Bxf3 11. gxf3 Bd6 12. Nd2 O-O-O 13. Nc4 g5 $6 {Banking on a KS
assault to compensate for the d-file.} 14. Rd3 Rhg8 {After a long think.} 15.
Rad1 h5 16. Nxd6+ cxd6 17. Rxd6 Rdf8 {A good move. Now it was my turn to think.
} 18. Kh2 {I couldn't find a move that I was happy with.} ({If} 18. Re6 g4 19.
hxg4 hxg4 20. Rxe5 gxf3+ 21. Kf1 (21. Kh1 $4) 21... Ng4) 18... g4 19. Rg1 {
[1hr 14']} Ne8 ({If} 19... gxh3 20. Rxf6) ({or} 19... gxf3 20. Rxf6) 20. Re6
Rxf3 21. hxg4 hxg4 22. Rg3 (22. Rxe5 $142) 22... Kd7 23. Rxe5 Nf6 {Seems to
win his Pawn back.} 24. Kg2 ({If} 24. Rf5 Rxg3) 24... Kd6 {[1hr 17']} 25. Ra5 {
[1hr 34']} Rxg3+ {[1hr 19']} 26. fxg3 Nxe4 {I declined a draw here but his
Knight gets a good post at d5 and is then as good as the Bishop.} 27. Bf4+ Kd7
28. Re5 Nf6 29. c4 b5 30. cxb5 axb5 31. Be3 Ra8 32. a3 Ra4 33. Rf5 {[1hr 54']}
Nd5 {Black declined a draw here.} 34. Bg5 Ke6 35. Rf2 Rc4 36. Bh6 Nf6 37. Re2+
Kd5 38. Rd2+ Ke4 39. Re2+ Kd3 40. Rd2+ Ke4 {It seems that he always had
compensation for the Pawn. Cumbria had a bad result. [Toothill (D), Everett (0)
, Collins (D), Ian Wells (0), Mellor (0), Billsborough (0), etc]} 1/2-1/2

