{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. f4 e5 2. fxe5 d6 3. Nf3 {White
chickens-out.} dxe5 4. e4 Bc5 5. b3 Bg4 6. Bb2 ({Horrific would be.} 6. Be2)
6... Nd7 7. d4 $6 {White said afterwards he felt obliged to do something
definite.} exd4 8. Bxd4 Bxf3 9. gxf3 Qh4+ 10. Ke2 O-O-O {White had missed this
when playing 7.d4?!} 11. c3 Ngf6 12. Qe1 Qh6 (12... Qh5 $142) 13. Qf2 Qh5 14.
Nd2 Rhe8 15. Kd3 Nd5 {I spent a lot of time on this.} 16. Kc2 {Best. The
Knight can't be taken, nor the Bishop.} Nf4 ({I had intended} 16... Nxc3 {and}
17. Kxc3 ({or} 17. Bxc5 Nxc5 18. Kxc3 Qe5+ 19. Kc2 Qxa1 20. Bh3+) 17... Bxd4+
18. Qxd4 Nb6 19. Qf2 Qe5+ 20. Kc2 Qxa1 {However} 21. Bh3+ {Kills it for me. So,
after much thought leaving me short of time 16......Nf4}) 17. Rd1 ({Now if} 17.
Bxc5 Nxc5 {controls d3}) 17... Re6 {Doubtful, but starting to rush. White was
also short of time and the rest was a scramble.} 18. Nc4 Bf8 19. Qg3 Ng6 20.
Kb2 $5 Rxe4 $6 {Is this safe?} 21. Bh3 {Help!} Re2+ 22. Kb1 Qh4 23. Bxa7 Qxg3
24. hxg3 b5 $1 25. Bxd7+ Rxd7 26. Rxd7 Kxd7 27. Na5 Re6 28. Bd4 c5 29. Bf2 Kc7
30. Kb2 $4 {With seconds to go he blunders} ({Black should have won even after
} 30. a3 Z0 {to play} 31. b4 {defending the Knight.}) 30... Re2+ {Exciting.}
0-1

