{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. Nc3 d5 3. g3 d4 4. Nce2 e5 5. d3 Bg4
6. Bg2 Bd6 7. f3 Be6 8. Nh3 f6 {White's opening is rather artificial and
Black's position very solid.} 9. f4 h6 10. O-O c5 11. c3 {After much thought.}
({He didn't fancy} 11. fxe5) ({or} 11. f5) 11... Nc6 12. Bd2 Qd7 13. Nf2 Nge7
14. Kh1 g5 {White obviously wasn't happy with the opening.} 15. f5 Bf7 16. a3
a5 17. a4 Ra6 18. Ng1 Rb6 19. Qc1 Ra6 20. h4 {White decided that he must take
some posiive action.} Nc8 21. Ngh3 Nb6 22. c4 {Sealing most of the QS so I
change direction.} Nd8 23. Ng4 Be7 ({If} 23... Qe7 24. Nxh6) 24. Nxh6 $5 Rxh6
25. hxg5 fxg5 26. Bxg5 Bxg5 27. Qxg5 Rh5 28. Qg7 Qd6 29. g4 Rh4 30. g5 Nd7 31.
g6 $5 {Wins back a piece for two Pawns, but leaves Black the better game.} ({
Mybe it was better to maintain the tension by} 31. Kg1) ({or} 31. Kh2 Z0 32.
Kg3) ({or} 31. Rf2 {doubling Rooks.}) 31... Bxg6 ({Not} 31... Bg8 32. f6) 32.
fxg6 ({If} 32. Qg8+ {simply} Qf8) 32... Qxg6 33. Qxg6+ Rxg6 34. b3 $2 {Short
of time he made a quick move.} (34. Rf3 $142 {but Black is on top anyway after}
Ne6 {with the threat of.....} 35. Z0 Ng5) 34... Rg3 35. Rad1 Rhxh3+ 36. Bxh3
Rxh3+ 37. Kg2 Rh7 38. Rf5 Ne6 39. Kf3 Nf4 40. Kg4 (40. Kg4 Rh2 {e.g.} (40...
Ng2 $1) 41. Rxf4 ({Dick & Fritz looked at} 41. Kg3 Rh6 42. Kf3 Ke7 43. Rg5 Rb6
44. Rg7+ Ke6 45. Rb1 Nxd3 46. Rg8 Rb4 47. Re8+ Kd6 48. Rh8 Nf6) 41... exf4 42.
Kxf4 Rf2+ {etc.}) 40... Rh2 {O.K. but 40......Ng2 wins otright. Time was
called and White resigned. A good result. I am the only cumbria player on the
top 7 boards to have won in 3 matches. [today: Toothill (L), R.A.C. (W),
Everett (L), I.Wells (L), Billsborough (L), K.Wells (L)]} 0-1

