{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 {[1']} 3. Bg2 c6 {[15']} 4.
Qa4 $5 Bc5 {[30'] My unusual 4th move at least gained me some time on the
clock.} (4... Na6 $142 5. Z0 Nc5) 5. e3 {Now his Bishop will be embarassed.}
Qe7 6. a3 O-O {[33']} 7. b4 Bb6 {[33']} 8. Nc3 {[19']} a5 {[45']} 9. b5 Rd8 10.
Nge2 d5 {[55']} 11. bxc6 bxc6 12. cxd5 {[29']} cxd5 {[63']} 13. Qb3 {Forced.}
Qe6 14. Rb1 Bc7 {[1hr 16']} 15. Nb5 {[37'] I felt that I had to try to keep
the innintiative.} Na6 16. d4 {[41']} Bd7 {[1hr 27'] Threatening to start
exchanging so I must do something positive.} 17. Nxc7 Nxc7 18. dxe5 {[48'] My
aim was to leave him with a weak d-Pawn.} Qxe5 19. Bb2 Qd6 {[1hr 30']} 20. Bxf6
{[60'] After some thought. I decided that this may be the most active.} Qxf6
21. Qc3 {After much consideration of 21.Qb6 or 21.Qb7.} ({Not} 21. Bxd5 $4 Nxd5
22. Qxd5 Bc6) 21... Qxc3+ 22. Nxc3 {I was relying on his time shortage and
weak d-Pawn now.} Rab8 {[1hr 41']} 23. O-O {[1hr 11']} ({I wanted to play} 23.
Kd2 {but it's too risky.}) 23... Nb5 {[1hr 47']} 24. Nxb5 {[1hr 14']} Rxb5 25.
Rfd1 {It's difficult for Black now.} Rxb1 {There's little chance.} 26. Rxb1 Bc6
{He had about 5' left for 23 moves I felt that he may try.....} ({.....} 26...
Be8 27. Rd1 Bc6 28. Rc1 {etc.}) 27. Rb6 Rc8 $2 {Played in a flash but again 27.
.....Be8makes it harder for White who has to march his King round. After the
text White has a killer.} 28. Bh3 {That shook him.} f5 29. Bxf5 Rc7 30. Kf1 Bb7
31. Ke2 g6 32. Bb1 Bc8 33. Kd2 Rc5 34. Ba2 Bf5 35. Bb3 Be4 36. a4 Kg7 37. Rb7+
{To push his King further from my passed b-Pawn which is due to appera.} Kh6 {
Giving up the h-Pawn is no better.} 38. Rb5 Rxb5 39. axb5 {Black exceeded the
time limit. In any event he was hopelessly lost. Black had little chance after
using so much time early on. Results: 1st D.Everett 5/5 2nd R.A.C 4/5 3rd R.H.
Mellor 4/5 I was 2nd on sum of opponents scores and won a £3 Book token. Ken
Wells came 4th= with 3.5/5 Ian Wells came 6th= with 3/5} 1-0

