{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e3 c5 2. f4 Nc6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. b3 g6 5. Bb2 Bg7
6. Bb5 O-O 7. O-O d6 8. Bxc6 bxc6 9. d3 Rb8 10. Nbd2 d5 $5 {I wasn't too happy
about letting him have e5 but I wanted to make some more central progress.} 11.
Be5 {Attacks the Rook but 11.Ne5 is more appropriate.} (11. Ne5) 11... Ra8 12.
Qe1 {He offered a draw here!} Qb6 13. c4 Rd8 14. Qh4 Bf5 {Best I think;
actively counteracting his KS pressure.} 15. Ng5 Bxd3 16. Bxf6 exf6 17. Qxh7+ {
White is commited to this but has a lot en prise.} Kf8 18. f5 {Clearly he must
keep his attack going.} Bxf5 (18... gxf5 {is uninviting.}) (18... fxg5 {
is suicidal after} 19. f6) (18... Bxf1 {is very risky.}) 19. e4 dxe4 20. Ngxe4
Qc7 ({If} 20... Bxe4 21. Nxe4 f5 22. Ng5 {saves the Rook.}) 21. Qh4 Qe5 22.
Rae1 {[1hr 26'] He offered another draw here.} Rd4 {[1hr 35']} 23. Rf2 $2 {
Leads to immediate trouble.} Bxe4 24. Rxe4 Rxe4 25. Nxe4 f5 26. Ng3 {Forced.}
Qd4 27. Qg5 Qa1+ 28. Rf1 Qxa2 29. Re1 Bd4+ 30. Kh1 Qf2 31. Qe7+ Kg7 32. Rf1 Qe3
33. Qd7 Rh8 {Short of time, White runs out of moves, 34.......QxN is
threatened. He tries.......} 34. Nxf5+ gxf5 35. Qxf5 Qe6 36. Qg4+ {In the rush
it goes, but it hardly matters} Qxg4 {A fair start [The Congress was played at
Norbreck Castle Hotel.]} 0-1

