{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 {[10'] Arriving late I found that I'd got
the draw I wanted against the 2nd highest graded player in the counrty.} c5 2.
Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Bd3 {A bit of a doubtful line.} Nc6 6. Nb3 d5
{Black has equalised} 7. exd5 Nxd5 8. O-O Ndb4 9. Nc3 $2 {Possibly the losing
move. I felt that the isolated Queen Pawn would not be a problem, but events
prove otherwise.} ({Possibly} 9. Be2 {was best}) 9... Nxd3 10. Qxd3 Qxd3 11.
cxd3 Be7 12. Be3 O-O 13. Rfd1 Nb4 {Possibly I shold have prevented this by 13.
a3} 14. Bc5 ({Now} 14. a3 Nc2 15. Rac1 Nxe3 {Gives two Bishops v two Knights})
14... Bxc5 15. Nxc5 b6 16. Nb3 Rd8 17. d4 Ba6 18. Rd2 {I wasn't happy about
this but coldn't find a good line.} Bc4 19. Nc1 Rd7 20. b3 Ba6 21. N1e2 Rc8 22.
f3 {Hoping to bring the King across} Kf8 {Black makes slow but steady progress}
23. Rad1 Rdc7 24. a3 Bxe2 25. Nxe2 Nc2 26. a4 Ne3 27. Rb1 g5 28. Kf2 Nd5 29. g3
Ke7 ({If} 29... Rc2 30. Rb2) 30. Ke1 h5 31. Kf2 {hanging direction in view of
his KS intentions.} f5 32. f4 {Maybe this is wrong but I was starting to get
short of time.} g4 {An open g-file might offer White counterplay.} 33. Rbb2 Kd6
34. Ke1 Nc3 35. Rdc2 {I was having to rush now.} Kd5 36. Rd2 Ne4 37. Rd1 h4 ({
I was expecting} 37... Rc2 {and if} 38. Rbb1 Nc3 39. Nxc3+ R8xc3 {and White's
Pawns fall.}) 38. gxh4 {No time for thought but I hoped to mix it in the time
rush.} Rh8 39. Ng3 Rxh4 40. Nxe4 Kxe4 41. Re2+ Kxf4 42. Rxe6 Rxh2 43. Re2 Rh1+
44. Kd2 Rxd1+ 45. Kxd1 Rd7 46. Rd2 Ke4 47. Re2+ Kd3 ({Even short of time I
could hope for him to play} 47... Kxd4) 48. Rf2 Rxd4 {The d-Pawn falls at last.
Having made the time control and not being able to play 49.Rxf5, I resigned.
Technical efficiency by Black} 0-1

