{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O
Bg4 6. h3 h5 7. d3 Bxf3 ({In round 1, against this opponent, Fred Turner had
played.} 7... Qf6) 8. Qxf3 f6 {The start of going off the rails.} 9. Qg3 g5 $6
{Going mad; Offering the g-Pawn for an attack which isn't on as I am unable to
develop any pieces properly.} 10. Bxg5 Qd4 11. Be3 $1 ({I expected} 11. Bc1
O-O-O) 11... Qxb2 {I wasn't too happy about this.} 12. Qg6+ Kd8 13. Nd2 Qa3 14.
Nc4 {Now I saw what I'd missed.} Qe7 15. f4 {White either overlooks 15.Na5 or
prefers this.} (15. Na5 Kc8 16. Bc5 $1 {I could find no good line so intended.}
Qd8) 15... exf4 (15... Qg7 {is no good.}) 16. Bxf4 Qe6 17. Qg3 Bc5+ 18. Kh1 Ne7
{After agonies, I was sure I was lost.} 19. Bxc7+ Ke8 20. Qf3 Bd4 21. Nb6 Ra7 {
Looks horrid but .......} ({...........} 21... Bxb6 {surely loses so, by the
text, I looked to confuse the issue.}) 22. c3 $1 Be5 23. Bxe5 fxe5 24. Qe3 {
Black could resign.} Rg8 {The only hope is an attack.} 25. Nd5 Nxd5 26. Qxa7
Nf4 27. Qb8+ Kd7 28. Qxb7+ Kd6 {Threats of 29......Rxg2 or ........Nxg2 made
White think.} 29. Rxf4 {After all he's two Pawns up.} exf4 30. Qb4+ Kd7 31.
Qd4+ Kc7 32. Qf2 Qe5 33. Qa7+ Kd6 34. Qd4+ $5 {Is this best?} Qxd4 35. cxd4 Rg3
36. Rd1 f3 37. gxf3 Rxf3 {Can White win?} 38. Kg2 Re3 39. Rd2 h4 40. Kh2 a5 41.
e5+ $5 {Desperation.} Kd5 42. Rc2 Kxd4 43. Rxc6 Rxe5 44. Rc4+ Kxd3 45. Rxh4
Re2+ 46. Kg3 Rxa2 {What a let-off!} 1/2-1/2

