1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. Qg4 Kf8 $4 {Not having played the
Winawer for a long time I chickened out of the sharp line.......} (5... Ne7 {
however White would have answered with} 6. Nge2) 6. dxc5 Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 Qc7 8.
Nf3 Qxc5 9. Rb1 {Threatening 10.Rb3 followed by 11.Ba3} h5 $5 {Possibly too
weakening.} 10. Qf4 Ne7 11. Bd3 Nbc6 12. O-O Nd8 {Needless to say I was none
too happy about the opening.} 13. Rb5 Qxc3 14. Bb2 Qc7 15. Ba3 Kg8 16. c4 {
Looks good opening lines but isn't too bad for Black.} dxc4 17. Bxc4 Ng6 18.
Qe4 Qc6 19. Qd4 Qd7 20. Qe3 b6 21. Rb2 Bb7 22. Rd2 Qa4 23. Rfd1 {Awkward for
Black.} Bd5 {Giving back the Pawn.} ({White suggested} 23... Bxf3 24. Qxf3 Nc6
{but it looks very fragile.}) 24. Bxd5 exd5 25. Rd4 Qe8 26. Rxd5 Ne6 27. Ng5
Rd8 28. Nxe6 Rxd5 29. Rxd5 Qxe6 {I offered a draw here feeling that I was out
of the wood. However.......} 30. Qf3 $1 {A terrible move to meet whan you are
short of time. I could find no good reply.} f6 ({If} 30... Qe8 31. Qd1) ({If} 
30... Rh6 31. Bc1) ({Fritz gives (0.46)} 30... Qg4 31. Qd3 h4 32. h3 Qe6 33.
Qf3 Qe8 34. Qd1 Kh7 35. Qh5+ Kg8 36. Qg5 Kh7 37. Rd4 b5 38. Qf5 Kg8 39. Bd6 Qe6
) 31. h3 Kf7 32. exf6 gxf6 {No time to think} 33. Bb2 Ne7 34. Rxh5 Rxh5 35.
Qxh5+ Kf8 36. Qh8+ Kf7 37. Qh7+ Kf8 38. Ba3 Qe1+ {Time was called. I resigned.
Cumbria did badly [4.5 - 11.5] R.A.C. (L), Toothill (L), Everett (L), Lamping 
(W), Cloudsdale (L)} 1-0

