{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 {I don't play this now in
important games. I had won the competition anyway.} 3. Bc4 {The first time
that I've faced this.} b5 4. Bb3 {Best I think.} d6 5. d4 {This too seems best.
} Be7 {embarking on a precarious course.} 6. dxe5 fxe4 {I'm more or less
commited now.} 7. exd6 exf3 $5 {Not recommended for an important game.} 8. Qxf3
Qxd6 9. Qxa8 {I had spent ages considering all this White simply took the Rook
after 30 seconds thought.} c6 {Threatening 10.....Qc7 & 11.....Bb7} 10. Qxa7 c5
11. c4 Nc6 12. Qa8 Qe6+ 13. Be3 {Now things started to look worse.....} Nd8 ({
...if} 13... bxc4 14. Bxc4) ({...or} 13... b4 14. Ba4) 14. cxb5 c4 15. Ba4 Bb7
16. b6+ Kf7 17. Qa5 g6 ({If} 17... Nh6 18. Qh5+) 18. O-O $2 {Better than I
could have hoped for.} Qe4 19. f3 Qxe3+ 20. Kh1 Bd6 21. Nc3 $2 {White is
losing the thread} Qf4 22. Kg1 ({Possibly better is} 22. g3) 22... Qxh2+ 23.
Kf2 Bg3+ 24. Ke3 Bf4+ 25. Kd4 Ne7 26. Kxc4 Ne6 27. Bd7 Ra8 28. Qb4 Bd6 29.
Bxe6+ (29. Bxe6+ Kxe6 {White lost on time. Anyway we continued casually with}
30. Rfe1+ ({Fritz & Dick examine} 30. Qb3 Ba6+ 31. Nb5 Rc8+ 32. Kd3+ Kf6 33.
Rfc1 Nc6 34. Rxc6 Rxc6 35. Qa4 Qxg2 36. Qd4+ Be5 37. Qd8+ Kf5) 30... Kf6 31.
Qb3 Ba6+ 32. Nb5 Qf4+ 33. Re4 Qd2 34. Qc3+ Qxc3+ 35. bxc3 Rc8+ 36. Kb3 Bxb5 {
Black won easily.}) 29... Kxe6 {White lost on time. All very unsound but
exciting. One can afford to play these lines in games which don't matter.} 0-1

