{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 moves per 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 {I was expecting to play Ian Wells and had prepared
this. Fortunately his father also plays the Dragon.} g6 {Allows a Maroczy Bind.
} 6. c4 Bg7 7. Be3 O-O 8. Be2 Nc6 9. Qd2 Bd7 {[9']} 10. Nc3 {[7']} Qb8 11. O-O
{[9']} Rc8 12. Rac1 a6 13. Rfd1 ({If} 13. a4 Na5) 13... Be8 ({Evidently not
liking} 13... Nxd4 14. Bxd4 b5) 14. Nc2 {[30']} Ne5 {[29']} 15. Nb4 {[33'] The
most active.} e6 {Weakens the d-Pawn, but not to be recommended was......} ({
.......} 15... Nxc4 16. Bxc4 Rxc4 17. Nbd5 Nxd5 18. Nxd5 Rxc1 19. Rxc1 Qd8 20.
Bb6 Qd7 21. Rc7) 16. b3 Bf8 {[41']} 17. Nc2 {[45']} b5 $5 {Striking for
freedom but it costs a pawn.} 18. Bg5 Bg7 19. f4 Neg4 {A Pawn must go.} 20.
Bxf6 Nxf6 21. Qxd6 Qa7+ 22. Qd4 bxc4 23. Qxa7 Rxa7 24. Bxc4 Nh5 {The Knight
necer really gets back into play from here.} 25. Ne2 Bc6 {[59']} 26. e5 {[57']}
Bf8 27. a4 $5 {To prevent 27.....Bb5} (27. g3 $142) 27... Bxa4 28. Ncd4 {
[65'] Threatening 29.bxB and 29.Nxe6} ({I realised} 28. Ra1 {is answered by}
Rxc4) 28... Bb5 $5 ({Why not?} 28... Bd7) 29. Nxb5 axb5 30. Bxb5 Rxc1 31. Rxc1
Rb7 {We played on quickly now-it is a problem getting these evening matches
finished in one go.} 32. Ba4 ({If} 32. Bc4 Bc5+ 33. Kf1 Be3) 32... Rb4 33. Rc4
({If} 33. g3 g5) 33... Rxc4 34. bxc4 Bc5+ 35. Kf1 Be3 36. g3 h6 37. Kg2 f5 38.
Kf3 Bc5 39. Be8 Kh7 ({If} 39... Kg7 40. h3 {Threatens to win the Knight.}) 40.
Nc3 Ng7 {[1hr 20']} 41. Bd7 $5 {[1hr 21']} ({My first thought was} 41. Bf7 {
which paralyses Black; but I was worried my Bishop would also be stuck. 41.Bf7
would have been quicker though.}) 41... Kg8 42. Na4 Ba7 43. c5 Kf8 44. c6 Ke7
45. Nc3 Ne8 $5 {Loses but it's difficult to find an alternative.} 46. Nb5 Bb6
47. Bxe8 Kxe8 48. Nd6+ {Much glum brooding by Black now.} Kd8 ({If} 48... Kf8
49. Ke2 $1 {and I just march the King to the QS.}) 49. Nf7+ Kc7 ({It's just
possible that} 49... Ke7 50. Nxh6 Kf8 {Offers more hope.}) 50. Nxh6 Kxc6 51.
Nf7 Kd5 52. h4 ({Not} 52. Nh8 g5) 52... Kc6 53. Nh8 g5 54. hxg5 Kd7 55. g6 {
A good game for one of these rather rapid evening games.} 1-0

