{Time limit 24 moves per hr} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 {
He watched my game v Webb at Blackpool [Lancs Open Rd2 9/3/77]} 5. Nc3 Bb4 6.
Bd3 $5 (6. e5) (6. Ndb5 {are both more usual.}) 6... Nc6 7. Nde2 d5 8. O-O h6 (
{Not caring for} 8... d4) 9. exd5 exd5 (9... Bxc3 10. dxc6) (9... Nxd5 10. Ne4)
10. Nb5 a6 ({If} 10... Bc5 11. Bf4) 11. Nbd4 O-O 12. h3 Re8 13. Be3 Ne5 14. c3
Bf8 15. Bf4 ({If say} 15. Bf5 Nc4) 15... Nxd3 ({I felt that} 15... Nc4 {
was stronger}) 16. Qxd3 Bd6 17. Rfe1 Be6 18. Rad1 Bxf4 19. Nxe6 Bh2+ 20. Kxh2
fxe6 21. Nf4 Qd6 22. g3 b5 23. a3 Rad8 24. Ng6 e5 25. Nh4 e4 26. Qd4 Qe5 27.
Ng2 g5 {Possibly rather weakening.} 28. Ne3 {He offered a draw here.} h5 29.
Kg2 Qxd4 {Possibly losing patience.} 30. Rxd4 Re7 31. Red1 Red7 32. a4 Kf7 33.
axb5 axb5 34. Rb4 Rb8 35. Nc2 Rc7 $2 {Rather a waste of a move.} 36. Nd4 Rcb7
37. Ra1 Ne8 38. Ra6 Rb6 ({If} 38... Nc7 39. Rh6 Kg7 40. Rd6 {Ties him up.}) 39.
Rxb6 Rxb6 40. Rxb5 Rxb5 41. Nxb5 Ke7 42. Kf1 Nd6 $2 {Giving up; He looked
dejected and seemed unwillingto fight a rear-gaurd action.} 43. Nxd6 Kxd6 44.
Ke2 Kc5 45. b3 1-0

