{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. a3 {After some
thought.} Bxc3+ 5. bxc3 dxe4 6. Qg4 Nf6 7. Qxg7 Rg8 8. Qh6 Rg6 ({
Fischer-Kovacevic Zagreb 1970 went} 8... Nbd7) ({The older line is} 8... c5) 9.
Qh4 $5 ({Everyone gives.} 9. Qe3) 9... Qd5 10. Ne2 {One disadvantage of 8.....
Rg6 is 11.Nf4 is threatened.} e5 {I felt that I had equalised.} 11. Bd2 {
Again after much thought.} Nbd7 {The most solid.} ({White intends} 11... Z0 12.
c4 {and is} Qxc4 13. Nf4) 12. c4 Qe6 13. d5 Qb6 {Better than....} ({....} 13...
Qg4) 14. Nc3 $2 {Leads to disaster.} Qd4 $1 {Now he is in trouble. After ages,
leaving himself short of time, he played} 15. Rd1 $6 ({Apparently he didn't
like} 15. Qh3 Ng4 16. Qg3 Ndf6 17. Z0 {Threatening} Nh5 {and I can see little
hope for White.}) 15... e3 {Wins a piece.} 16. Qxd4 exd4 {A pleasant position
to be in.} 17. Nb5 exd2+ 18. Rxd2 Kd8 19. Nxd4 Nc5 20. g3 Nfe4 21. Re2 Nd6 22.
Nb3 Nxb3 {I didn't particularly want to straighten out his Pawns but this
seems to offer least counterplay.} 23. cxb3 Bg4 24. Re3 Rg8 ({If} 24... Kd7 25.
f3 Bf5 26. g4 {etc.}) 25. Bd3 Nf5 ({If} 25... Bf5 26. Bxf5 Nxf5 27. Rf3) 26.
Bxf5 ({If} 26. Re5 Nd4) 26... Bxf5 27. Kd2 Kd7 28. Re5 Bg6 29. f4 Rae8 30. Rhe1
f6 31. Re6 Rxe6 32. Rxe6 f5 33. c5 Re8 34. Rxe8 ({I was half expecting} 34. Re5
{but White who was getting short of time wasn't willing to spend time working
it out. In fact after} Rxe5 35. fxe5 c6 {White is stuck for a good move.})
34... Bxe8 35. Kd3 Ke7 36. Kd4 Kf6 37. h3 {Possibly it was better not to put a
Pawn in a white square} ({However, Black an manoeuvre the Bishop to b3 forcing
d6.} 37. Kc4 Bh5 38. Kd4 Bd1 39. Kc3 Bf3 40. Kd4 Be4 41. b4 Bb1 42. Kc4 Ba2+
43. Kd4 Bb3 {and maybe} 44. b5 Ba4 45. c6 bxc6 46. bxc6 Ke7 47. Ke5 Bc2 48. Kd4
Kd6 {and White wins. If White pushes his KS Pawns during any stage of this
Black simply marks time with the Bishop.}) 37... Bd7 38. b4 Bb5 {Threatening
39.....Bf1 followed by the previous line. White was very short of time now.
The rest was rather a scramble for White.} 39. g4 h6 {Now he will have to open
up the KS in view of 40....Bf1} 40. d6 {A spot of time rush desperation now.}
cxd6 41. cxd6 Bd7 42. g5+ {It's hopeless now.} hxg5 43. fxg5+ Kxg5 44. Ke5 f4
45. Ke4 Bxh3 46. Kf3 Bd7 {A good result} 0-1

