{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 moves per 15'} 1. d4 e6 2. e4 d5 3. Nc3
Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. Bd2 {[1']} a6 {[5'] More usual are....} (5... Ne7) (5... Nc6)
6. a3 {[17']} Bxc3 7. Bxc3 Nc6 8. dxc5 {[25'] Doesn't turn out too well.} d4 9.
Bd2 Nxe5 10. Bf4 Qd5 11. Qe2 {More or less forced.} Nd7 ({Maybe} 11... Nc6 {
is more accurate.}) 12. b4 Ngf6 13. Nf3 Ne4 ({Alan Potts felt that} 13... e5 {
would win! I was unsure and played safely.}) 14. Qc4 Qf5 15. Bg3 Nxg3 16. hxg3
Ne5 $2 {Sloppy too casual. I had originally intended....} ({....} 16... Qe4+
17. Be2 Ne5 18. Nxe5 Qxe5 {Threatening 19......d3 I don't Know why I played
the text.}) 17. Qxd4 Nxf3+ 18. gxf3 Bd7 {After much thoght.} ({If} 18... Qxf3
19. Qxg7 {and there is no good line for Black. I missed one point (below) but
there seems no good move for Black anyway.}) 19. Bd3 $1 Qg5 ({I realised that} 
19... Qxf3 {is answered by} 20. Be4) 20. f4 Qd5 21. Qxd5 exd5 {The position is
pretty hopeless for Black and the d-Pawn must go.} 22. Kd2 h6 23. Rae1+ Kd8 24.
Re5 Bc6 25. Rhe1 Re8 26. Rxe8+ Bxe8 27. Kc3 Rc8 28. Kd4 Bc6 29. Bf5 Rc7 30. Bh3
f6 31. Be6 Re7 32. Re3 g5 {My only hope is either counterplay on the KS or
elimination of all the KS Pawns} 33. fxg5 fxg5 34. g4 Rh7 35. Bxd5 Bxd5 36.
Kxd5 h5 37. gxh5 Rxh5 38. Ke5 Rh8 39. Rf3 g4 {The sealed move and the best
chance. The game resumed 5/5/77 Ifelt sure he would play 40.Rf7} 40. Rd3+ $2 {
Played with very little thought, this achieves nothing.} ({If} 40. Rg3 Rh2) ({
or} 40. Rf4 Rg8) ({However after} 40. Rf7 {I must be lost} Rh3 41. Rxb7 Rxa3
42. Ra7 Rc3 43. Rxa6 Rxc2 44. Rb6) 40... Kc7 41. Kf4 Rf8+ 42. Kg3 Rf5 {With
ideas of .......a5} 43. Rd4 Rf3+ 44. Kg2 Rxa3 45. Rxg4 Rc3 {He now thought for
ages, could find no good line, and seemed to accept that he had gone wrong.}
46. Rd4 {To cut the King off from the f-file} Rxc2 47. Kg3 a5 48. bxa5 Rxc5 49.
Ra4 Kd6 50. f4 Ke6 51. Kg4 Kf6 52. Ra1 Rb5 53. Ra2 Rd5 54. a6 bxa6 55. Rxa6+
Kf7 56. Kf3 Rd4 57. Ke3 Rb4 58. Rd6 Ke7 59. Rd4 {Giving up} Rxd4 60. Kxd4 Kf6
61. Ke4 {A successful rear gaurd action.} 1/2-1/2

