{Time limit 65' each for all moves} 1. d4 e6 2. g3 {Prior to this game Bob
Newton had a string of good results with this line.} c5 3. c3 d5 4. Bg2 f5 {
One needs to play actively in these fast games.} 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Bf4 Nf6 7. Ne5
$2 {He should continue his development.} Qb6 {Taking the innitiative.} 8. Qb3
$2 {Missing my 10th move.} cxd4 9. Qxb6 $2 (9. Nxc6 $142) 9... axb6 10. Nxc6
dxc3 {Winning a pawn.} 11. Nxc3 {[10']} bxc6 {[5']} 12. O-O Ba6 13. Bc7 $2 {
Again, he should eliminate the weaknesses (e.g.the e-Pawn) first.} Nd7 14. Rfe1
g5 15. Rac1 $4 {Overlooking the point of my last move.} Ra7 {He could resign
now.} 16. f4 Rxc7 17. fxg5 {[25']} Be7 {[12']} 18. h4 Bc5+ 19. e3 Ne5 20. Rcd1
Nc4 21. Na4 Bxe3+ 22. Kh2 (22. Kf1 Nd2# {Would save him a lot of worrying. As
it is it goes from bad to worse.}) 22... d4 23. b3 Ne5 {Threatening 24......
Ng4+ 25.Kh1 Nf2+} 24. Kh3 Nd3 25. Rxe3 dxe3 {[17'] Resigns. Enough is Enough.
Rather a disaster for White. 27th May 1977 Lancaster Chess Club Lightning. 1st
R.A.C 12.5/13 [I beat: B.Burton,F.Turner, F.Ward, W.K.Wells, P.T.Seery, A.C.
Kearns, H.Kearns, A.Fawcett, C.Fisher, M.Donaghay, J.V.Davies, L.Bland. I drew
with Ian Wells in the last round. I won a £2 book token. 2nd Ian Wells11.5/13
Drew with me and lost to H.Kearns. Prize £1 book token} 0-1

