Fischer v Gligoric, Havana 1966.} Bd6 ({Gligoric played.} 7... exd4) 8. h3 Bh5
9. Nbd2 Ne7 10. Nc4 {[11'] Threatening the e-Pawn.} Bf7 {[22']} 11. Qe2 Ng6 12.
Rd1 Qe7 13. Na5 {I couldn't find anything to do with my Bishop} Rb8 14. Nb3 O-O
15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Nxe5 ({If} 16. Nfd4 Bc4) 16... Qxe5 17. g3 Bh5 {He offered a
draw. I declined and played} 18. Qc4+ Bf7 19. Qe2 ({If} 19. Qd4 Qh5 {is too
good for Black.}) 19... Bh5 20. Qc4+ {There's nothing better.} Bf7 21. Qe2 {
I failed to find a good plan.} 1/2-1/2

