3. Nd2 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. f4 c5 6. c3 Nc6 7. Ndf3 Qa5 ({White was playing very
fast so I decided to vary from} 7... Qb6) 8. Kf2 f6 {[9']} 9. g3 {[5']} f5 10.
a3 {[7']} c4 {[14']} 11. h3 Be7 12. g4 Nf8 13. Ne2 {[22']} Bd7 {[21']} 14. Ng3
Qd8 15. Bg2 Na5 16. Nd2 {To prevent 16.....Nb3 but his f-pawn is deserted} Ng6
17. Ke3 Nh4 18. Bf1 g5 19. Nh5 ({Black had threatened} 19. Z0 gxf4+ 20. Kxf4 $4
Bg5#) 19... gxf4+ 20. Kf2 Bg5 21. Nf3 Nxf3 22. Qxf3 Nb3 23. Rb1 Nxc1 24. Rxc1
Qb6 25. Rb1 O-O-O 26. Be2 {White marks time. Black will open up the KS with
good winning prospects.} Ba4 27. Bd1 {He can hardly allow 27......Bc2, 28......
Be4} Bxd1 28. Rhxd1 {[59']} Rdf8 {[63']} 29. Rd2 fxg4 30. hxg4 a5 {White can
do notjing. His Knight is useless, so I fix the QS before transferring the
Queen to the KS.} 31. Rh1 Qc7 32. Rb1 a4 33. Rdd1 {[1hr 11']} Qf7 {[67'] White
thought for a while then apparently decided to give up the exchange in the
hope of activating his Knight.} 34. Re1 Bh4+ 35. Kg2 Bxe1 36. Rxe1 Qg6 37. Nf6
h5 38. Kf2 hxg4 39. Nxg4 ({If} 39. Qxg4 Rxf6) 39... Rfg8 40. Rg1 Rh2+ {A fair
game.} 0-1

