{Time limit 40 moves in 1hr 30' then 30' for the rest of the game.} 1. e4 e6 2.
c4 c5 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 a6 6. Be2 Nf6 7. Nxc6 bxc6 8. Qc2 d5 {
I felt that this probably equalised.} 9. exd5 cxd5 10. O-O Bb7 11. Qa4+ Qd7 12.
Qxd7+ Nxd7 13. Bf3 $2 {With very little thought he gets a poor endgame.} Ne5
14. cxd5 Nxf3+ 15. gxf3 Bxd5 16. Kg2 Be7 17. Nc3 Bc4 18. Re1 O-O 19. b3 Bd3 ({
Neither} 19... Bb4) ({nor} 19... Bf6 {seem better.}) 20. Bb2 Bf6 21. Na4 Bxb2
22. Nxb2 Bb5 23. Rac1 Rac8 24. Rxc8 Rxc8 25. Rd1 Kf8 26. Rd2 {[28']} Ke7 {[39']
} 27. Nd1 Rc5 28. h4 {He can't let his King get stuck on the h-file.} f5 29. f4
{Else 29.....f4 constricts him.} Bc6+ 30. Kg3 h6 31. f3 {He offered a draw
here.} Rd5 {I'm not sure about this.....} ({.....possibly} 31... Rc1 {is
better.}) 32. Rxd5 ({I was expecting} 32. Rc2) 32... Bxd5 33. Kf2 Bc6 34. Ke3
Kf6 35. Nb2 Kg6 36. Kf2 Kf6 37. Nc4 g5 38. hxg5+ hxg5 39. Kg3 Bd5 40. fxg5+ {
[59']} Kxg5 {[1hr 14']} 41. f4+ Kf6 42. Ne5 {The game is probably drawn but I
felt that I should give him the opportunity to go wrong.} Ke7 43. Nd3 Kd6 44.
Kf2 Be4 45. Nb2 Bb1 46. a3 Bc2 47. b4 Bb3 48. Nd3 Kd5 49. Ke3 Bc4 {I could see
no line offering winning chances here. White plays 50.Nc5 here and I can't
protect both a & e-Pawns and also manoeuvre the King to the QS. However, White
thought for a long time and played.} 50. Ne5 (50. Nc5) 50... Bb5 51. Nf3 $2 {
This seems to lose.} (51. Nd3 {Seems to draw}) 51... Kc4 52. Nd4 Bd7 53. Nf3
Kb3 54. Ne5 Bb5 55. Nd3 Kxa3 56. Nc5 {A bit late} Bc4 57. Kd4 Kxb4 58. Nb7 Bd5
59. Nc5 a5 60. Nd3+ Kb5 61. Kc3 a4 62. Kb2 Be4 63. Ne5 {T e a-Pawn is on the
wrong colour to Queen so the White f-Pawn must be captured. If the Kingmarches
to e4 then White defends the Pawn by Ng6. Therefore the Bishop must be posted
on e8to prevent this. So,....} Bc6 ({After} 63... Kb4 64. Ka1 a3 65. Ka2 Bd5+
66. Ka1 Kc3 67. Kb1 Kd4 68. Ng6 Ke3 69. Kc2 Bc6 70. Kb3 Be8 71. Ne5 Kxf4 {
-3.72/0}) 64. Ka3 Be8 65. Nf3 Kc4 66. Ng5 Bd7 67. Nf7 Kd4 68. Ne5 Be8 69. Nf3+
Ke3 70. Ng5 Bd7 71. Nh3 Kf3 72. Kb4 Kg3 {Score for the Tournament 4/6 Level
with Kurajica (!), Pritchett, Franklin, Basman, P.Littlewood, etc. Bellin
scored 3! Ian Wells woon the U-14 prize with 3.5. The time limit was rather
fast and I deliberately played quickly in some games. I also tried to play
soundly, hence 4 draws. A good effort.} 0-1

