{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+
6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 Qc7 8. Qxg7 Rg8 9. Qxh7 cxd4 10. Ne2 Nbc6 11. f4 dxc3 12.
Nxc3 a6 13. Qd3 Bd7 {[26']} 14. Rb1 {[15']} Na5 15. h4 Nf5 16. Rh3 Bc6 ({
Rather better is} 16... O-O-O {as played by Ulhmann here in several games.})
17. h5 O-O-O 18. h6 Rg6 19. h7 Rh8 20. Ne2 Bb5 $6 {Underestimating his reply
and maybe getting rather carried away with QS operations.} ({Possibly} 20...
Rg7 {is best.}) 21. Rxb5 $1 {Seems best.} axb5 22. Nc3 Qc4 $5 {This too maybe
wrong.} ({Maybe} 22... Nc4 {is best.}) 23. Nxb5 {Now I was a bit stuck.} Qxd3
24. Bxd3 Nc4 {After much thought.} ({Maybe} 24... Kd7 {is best.}) 25. Nd6+ {
I knew that I'd gone wrong now.} Ncxd6 26. exd6 Rg7 27. g4 ({If} 27. Bb2 Rhxh7)
27... Rgxh7 {The only hope.} 28. Rxh7 Rxh7 29. gxf5 Rh1+ 30. Kd2 Kd7 31. Bb2
Kxd6 32. f6 {I was short of time. White has a straightforward win.} Kc5 33. Be5
d4 {Missing his reply but I was lost anyway.} 34. Bg6 $1 Rh2+ 35. Kc1 Kc4 36.
Bxf7 Kc3 37. Kb1 Rh1+ 38. Ka2 Rh2 39. Bg6 {Black lost on time. Slack thinking
in the middlegame. The match was played at Fulwood.} 1-0

