Nc3 e5 6. Ndb5 d6 7. Nd5 {Not really recommended but I had played this in The
Bank of Dublin so felt that I could gain time in the opening..} Nxd5 8. exd5
Nb8 9. c4 Bd7 {I don't like this.} 10. Nc3 Be7 11. Be2 O-O 12. O-O Na6 13. Kh1
Nc7 $2 {Now he gets very cramped.} (13... f5 $142) 14. f4 {Threatening 15.fxe.
I also considered....} ({....} 14. c5) 14... Ne8 15. f5 {Keeping him tied down.
} Nf6 {[35']} 16. g4 {[13']} h6 17. Be3 Nh7 18. Qd2 Bg5 19. Bxg5 Qxg5 $2 {
Loses the d-Pawn.} (19... Nxg5 $142 20. Kg2 Z0 {Intending} 21. h4 Nh7 {When I
can follow up with} 22. Ne4) 20. Qxg5 Nxg5 21. h4 Nh3 22. Ne4 Nf4 23. Bf3 {
[29']} b5 {[66'] Black was getting a little short of time.} 24. b3 bxc4 25.
bxc4 Rab8 26. Nxd6 {Black won't have time to utilise the 7th rank.} Rb2 27. c5
Ba4 {Very little time now.} 28. c6 Rc2 {With no time left he had to move.} ({
Now} 28... Rfb8 29. c7) 29. Bd1 {Black lost on time. Lancaster A won 7 - 0 
[Collins, Ward, Seery, M.Kearns, Fisher, Fawcett, Tebatt]} 1-0

