1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. Bd3 c5 6. c3 Nc6 7. Ne2 cxd4 8. cxd4
Qb6 9. Nf3 Bb4+ {Not as good as the immediate....} ({......} 9... f6) 10. Kf1
f6 11. Nf4 Ne7 $2 {After a lot of thought and the start of the trouble.} (11...
O-O {is no good after} 12. Nxe6 Re8 13. Bf5 Ndxe5 14. dxe5) ({I didn't fancy
risking} 11... fxe5 {However,Rotariu v Diaconescu Romania 1960 then went} 12.
Nxe6 Nf6 13. Nxg7+ Kf8 14. Bh6 {Winning, so it seems that 10......f6 was wrong.
The game may be lost for Black after that.}) 12. a3 fxe5 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. dxe5
Bc5 15. Qh5+ Kf8 ({After} 15... Kd8 16. Qf7) 16. Bxh7 Bd7 17. Ng6+ Nxg6 18.
Qf3+ Nf4 {To make him block the Queen Bishop path with his Queen.} 19. Qxf4+
Ke8 20. Bg6+ Kd8 21. b4 Be7 22. Be3 Qa6+ 23. Kg1 Rf8 {Again after much
deliberation and probably not the best.} ({I didn't like} 23... Rh4 24. Qg3
Rxb4 {Which leaves me weak(er) on the KS}) ({Maybe} 23... Rc8) ({or} 23... Qc4
{is best}) 24. Qg3 Qc4 25. Rc1 Qe2 $5 ({Probably]} 25... Qh4 {is best}) 26. h3
Bb5 $4 {Completely losing the thread} 27. Rc2 {Caught in the opening again - I
shall have to spend more time on them.} 1-0

