1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. c5 b6 7. b4 Nc6 $2 {
This gets him into a terrible mess.} ({Best seems} 7... Be7) 8. Bb5 Bd7 ({If} 
8... Qc7 9. Bf4 $1) 9. Bxc6 Bxc6 10. b5 Bd7 ({Despearate measures such as} 
10... Bxb5 11. Nxb5 bxc5 {would probably be followed by} 12. Qa4 {12........
Resigns.}) 11. c6 Bc8 12. Rb1 {Prevents 12......Bb4 and allowing 12......a6
hich could be answered by 13.a4} Bd6 13. Nf3 {As Black's only hope is to force
.......e5.} ({I considered} 13. f4 {but felt that it was unnecessary.}) 13...
O-O 14. Bg5 h6 {He doesn't have a great deal of choice.} 15. Bh4 g5 {Weakening
his KS but he must try something.} 16. Bg3 {In view of my superior position I
didn't give much thought to sacrificing on g5.} Ne8 ({He didn't like} 16... Ne4
17. Nxe4 dxe4 18. Nd2 f5 19. Bxd6 Qxd6 20. Nc4 {Followed by 21.Ne5}) 17. Bxd6
Qxd6 ({I was expecting something like} 17... Nxd6 18. h4 g4 19. Ne5 f5 20. f3
g3 21. Qd2 Kg7 22. Rb3) 18. Ne5 Kg7 {Presumably to play 19......Rh8. I was
expecting....} ({......} 18... f6) (18... Kg7 19. Qd3 {[Resigns] The
continuation I was hoping for was.....} Qe7 ({Maybe} 19... f5 20. g4 Nf6 21. f3
Rh8 22. h4 {Breaks through. Black is effectively his Queen Bishop & Rook down.}
) {(say)} 20. h4 Rh8 21. hxg5 hxg5 (21... Qxg5) 22. Rxh8 Kxh8 23. Kd2 Nf6 {
(say)} 24. Rh1+ Kg8 25. Qh3) 19. Qd3 {Prevents 19.......f6 and threatens to
open the KS by 20.h4 After some thought and to my surprise he resigned. To
beat a 206 graded player in 19 moves has to be a goos result.} 1-0

