cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 g6 $2 6. c4 Nc6 7. Be3 Bg7 8. Qd2 O-O 9. Nc3 Bd7 10. Be2
Rc8 11. Rc1 a6 {[16']} 12. O-O {[7']} Ne5 13. b3 e6 {[28']} 14. Rfd1 Ne8 15.
Nc2 Nc6 (15... Z0 {Threatening} 16. f4 Nc6 17. e5) 16. Na4 {Squeezing the
Black position.} Nb8 17. Nb6 Rc6 {[43']} 18. c5 {Now Black has to find
something quickly.} Bb2 {At least this surprised me.} 19. Rb1 Qf6 {More or
less obligatory after his last move. Now he threatens to get some freedom
after 20.......Qc3} 20. Rxb2 $1 {Whilst this traps his Queen it does not
obtain a material advantage but lead to a won position because of the
passivity of the Black pieces.} Qxb2 21. Bd4 Qxa2 22. Ra1 Qxb3 23. Bc4 Qxb6 24.
cxb6 Rxc4 25. Ne3 {Black is very weak on the Black squares.} Rc6 26. e5 Bc8 27.
Ng4 d5 28. Rc1 Nd7 29. Bb2 f5 30. exf6 Nexf6 31. Rxc6 bxc6 32. Ba3 c5 33. Qe3
Nxb6 34. Qxc5 Nbd7 ({If} 34... Nfd7 35. Qe7 Z0 36. Nh6+ {etc.}) 35. Nxf6+ Rxf6
36. Qxc8+ Nf8 37. Bxf8 Rxf8 38. Qxe6+ Kg7 39. Qxa6 Rf5 40. Qd6 Kh6 41. Kf2 Kg5
42. g4 Rf6 43. h4+ Kh6 44. Qxf6 d4 45. Qf8# 1-0

