{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+
6. bxc3 Qc7 7. Nf3 Ne7 8. Bd3 $2 b6 9. a4 Ba6 10. O-O Bxd3 ({Not} 10... O-O $4
11. Bxh7+ Kxh7 12. Ng5+ Kg8 13. Qh5 Rc8 14. Qxf7+ Kh8 15. Nxe6) 11. Qxd3 h6 12.
Ba3 Nd7 13. Rfb1 O-O 14. Nd2 Ng6 15. g3 Rfc8 16. Ra2 cxd4 {After much thought.}
17. cxd4 Qc3 18. Qxc3 Rxc3 19. Bb4 {[49']} Rc6 {[69']} 20. a5 {[50']} b5 {
[1hr 20']} 21. Kf1 {[51']} a6 22. Ke2 Rac8 23. Kd3 R6c7 {Black was looking a
bit lost now. I felt that Ihad good winning chances by exchanging Rooks and
penetrating on the QS.Unfortunately my old problem, overconfidence, led me to
start playing too quickly.} 24. Rb3 h5 25. Rc3 $5 {Completely overlooking his
reply. I played this move very quickly. 25.f4 is best. The reply now came
almost instantaneously.} (25. f4 $142) 25... Ngxe5+ $5 {Rather a shock. My
first instinct was that I had blundered and lost but as I took stock of the
situation a light apperared.} 26. dxe5 Nxe5+ 27. Ke3 $1 {Now he gets a shock.}
Ng4+ (27... Rxc3+ 28. Bxc3 Rxc3+ 29. Kd4 {wins a piece.}) (27... d4+ 28. Kxd4
Nf3+ 29. Rxf3) 28. Kd4 Rxc3 29. Bxc3 Nxf2 30. Bb4 Ng4 31. h4 Nf6 32. c3 Ng4 33.
Ra1 f6 34. Re1 Kf7 35. Re2 Nh6 36. Rg2 Nf5+ 37. Kd3 e5 38. Ke2 g6 39. Nb3 Rc6
40. Bc5 Nh6 41. Kd2 {Time was called. Adjudicated drawn. P.J.Brooks had a
junior grade of 190 ~ 180 The match was played at The Catholic Club Winkley
Square Preston} 1/2-1/2

