{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 24 moves per hr} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 {I completely forgot I played this line against him
last September.} e5 6. Nb3 d5 7. exd5 Qxd5 8. Bd2 ({An improvement on} 8. Qxd5)
8... Nc6 9. Nc3 Qd8 10. Bb5 Bd7 11. Qe2 Qc7 12. O-O-O {[7']} O-O-O {[25']} 13.
Bg5 {[10']} Be7 {[38']} 14. Kb1 {[16']} ({I didn't like} 14. Rhe1 Nd5 15. Nxd5
Bxg5+) 14... Rhe8 {[42']} 15. Rhe1 h6 {[51']} 16. Bh4 {[20']} g5 17. Bg3 Bd6 {
[53']} 18. Bc4 Nd4 {[55'] Much the best move.} 19. Qf1 {[29']} Ne6 {A bit
cramping. I expected the Knight trade. I now felt that I could try to force
the issue.} (19... Nxb3) 20. Rxd6 $1 Qxd6 21. Bxe5 ({Not} 21. Rxe5 $2 Nf4)
21... Qe7 22. Qf2 Nc7 {Short of time he finds the best move.} 23. Re2 Bc6 24.
Qxa7 Nfd5 $2 {Short of time he sheds a piece.} 25. Bxd5 Bxd5 26. Bxc7 Qxc7 27.
Rxe8 Rxe8 28. Nxd5 Re1+ 29. Nc1 Qd6 30. Qa8+ Kd7 (30... Qb8 {is very risky
after} 31. Qa5) (30... Kd7 31. Qxb7+ {Black resigns. A continuation} Ke6 32.
Nc7+ Kf5 33. Ne8 Qg6 {To defend the f-Pawn. White must win.}) 31. Qxb7+ {
Having made the time control he resigned. A fair game for this competition. On
9/1/78 I beat P.A.Leigh in the same competition.} 1-0

