h5 7. d3 Qf6 8. Be3 Bxf3 9. Qxf3 {[3']} Qxf3 {[7']} 10. gxf3 {[3']} Bd6 {[11']}
11. Nc3 Ne7 12. Ne2 Ng6 13. Rad1 O-O-O 14. Kh1 c5 15. Rg1 Rd7 {[26']} 16. b3 {
[34']} b6 {[32']} 17. Rg2 {[44']} Kb7 {[37']} 18. Bg5 {[50']} Rg8 {[56']} 19.
Rdg1 Rf8 {[65']} 20. Bc1 {[64']} Rh8 {[1hr 10']} 21. Bg5 {[68']I felt that we
were getting nowhere so I offered a draw here. He thought it over for nearly
20' before deciding to continue. Perhaps I should have been more careful and
looked for possible counterplay. Maybe....} ({......} 21. a4 {and} Z0 22. Nc3 {
activating the Knight.}) 21... Be7 {[1hr 29']} 22. f4 {[1hr 19']} (22. Bxe7 {
Maybe this is safest}) 22... Bxg5 23. fxg5 (23. Rxg5 {Might be playable.})
23... b5 {Now .....c5 is coming} 24. Rg3 $2 ({Possibly} 24. f4 exf4 25. Rf2 {
is most active}) 24... Rhd8 25. f4 {[1hr 37'] Thus my last move was wasted}
exf4 {[1hr 37']} 26. Rf3 c4 27. bxc4 bxc4 28. Rb1+ $2 {I regretted this
straight away.means that .......Rd1 will be check in some lines.} Kc8 29. d4 {
Now shortage of time steps in.} Re7 30. e5 f6 31. gxf6 gxf6 32. Rg1 {So my
28th was wrong.} Nf8 33. Nxf4 fxe5 34. dxe5 Rxe5 35. Ra3 $2 Rf5 36. Ng6 Nxg6
37. Rxg6 Rf2 38. Rc3 Rd1+ 39. Rg1 Rdd2 40. Rg8+ (40. Rg8+ Kb7 41. Rxc4 Rxc2 42.
Rb4+ Kc6 {etc.}) 40... Kb7 {Having survived the time scramble, I resigned. An
opening that doesn't suit my style, some imprecise moves, and time shortage.}
0-1

