Nf6 6. Bd3 Nc6 7. Nb3 Qc7 8. O-O d6 9. Nc3 Be7 10. Be3 Ne5 11. Rc1 Bd7 (11...
Nxc4 $4 12. Bxc4 Qxc4 13. Nd5 {is obviousley suicidal for Black.}) 12. Be2 Bc6
{Not a very good square for the Bishop.} 13. f3 O-O 14. Nd4 Rab8 {Another not
very useful move.} 15. Qd2 Qd7 16. Rfd1 Rfd8 17. b4 Qe8 {[48'] The threat was
18.b5} 18. b5 {[41']} Bd7 {[50']} 19. Nb3 Rdc8 20. Qd4 Qd8 $2 {Cramped he
overlooks the reply.} 21. c5 {Pretty murderous.} Ne8 ({Not} 21... axb5 22. cxd6
Nc6 23. dxe7 $1) 22. cxd6 Bxd6 {[1hr 24']} (22... Bf6 {Might just offer a
little hope.}) 23. f4 {[60']} Qf6 24. fxe5 Bxe5 25. Qxd7 Qh4 ({If} 25... Rd8 {
I had originally intended} 26. Nd5 {but} Qh4 {is a nuisance}) 26. g3 Bxg3 27.
hxg3 Qxg3+ 28. Kf1 Qxe3 {There is no perpetual} 29. Qd3 Qh6 30. Qf3 axb5 31.
Nxb5 Rxc1 32. Rxc1 Ra8 33. Nc7 $6 {Possibly unnecessary risk taking.} Rc8 34.
Qg3 (34. Nxe8 Rxc1+ 35. Nxc1 Qxc1+ 36. Kg2 Qc6 $1) 34... Nf6 35. Bf3 Qe3 36.
Kg2 {With a little trap.} Nxe4 {Short of time he falls in} 37. Nxe6 {An
absolute crusher. With no time left he scrambled out a few moves.} Qg1+ 38.
Kxg1 Rxc1+ 39. Nxc1 Nxg3 40. Nd4 $1 {Winning the b-Pawn because of the threat
of 41.Kg2} f5 41. Bxb7 g5 42. a4 f4 43. a5 g4 44. a6 f3 45. a7 {An exciting
game! The match was played at the Newby Bridge Hotel} 1-0

