{[#] Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 moves per 15'} 15... Nxd4 {[17']}
16. Bb4 Bd7 17. Rfd1 {Threat 18.Bxh7} Rc8 18. Ra2 Nc6 19. Bd6 a6 {I wanted to
play the Knight to d8-f7 and .....Bc6} ({If} 19... Nd8 20. Bb5 {is a nuisance.}
) 20. c4 $5 {I had assumed that he couldn't play this, and it seems wrong.}
dxc4 21. Bxc4 Nxe5 $1 {White had assumed I couldn't play this.} 22. Bxe5 Rxc4
23. Rad2 {Looks good, but, quite, simply......} Bxa4 24. Rd8+ Kf7 25. Rxh8 Bxd1
26. Rxh7 Rg4 {Unfortunately the Rook gets a bit stuck on the KS.} 27. Kf1 Bb3 (
{Maybe} 27... Bc2 {then transferring the Rook to the QS would have been a
better plan.}) 28. f3 Kg8 29. Rh5 Rg6 30. g4 Bd5 31. Ke2 Rh6 $2 {Otherwise
White plays32.g5 It seems the last few moves formed a wrong plan for Black.}
32. Rxh6 gxh6 33. Ke3 Kf7 34. f4 Kg6 {it seems drawn as he can force off the
h-Pawn if I move my King away.} 35. Kd4 Bf3 36. h3 h5 37. gxh5+ Kxh5 38. Kc5
Bg2 39. Kb6 Kh4 40. Ka5 Kxh3 41. Bc7 Kg4 42. Be5 Kf5 43. Bc7 Ke4 44. Bd6 Kd5
45. Be5 Kc5 46. Bc7 Bc6 47. Bb6+ Kc4 48. Bc7 b5 49. Bd6 Bb7 50. Bb4 {I missed
my chance somewhere around moves 27-28.} 1/2-1/2

