{Time limit 1hr 10' for all moves} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 g6 5.
Nxc6 dxc6 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 {He played all this very quickly and seemed to be
playing for a draw.} 7. Bc4 Ke8 8. Bd2 Bg7 9. Bc3 Bxc3+ 10. Nxc3 Nf6 11. O-O b5
{[7'] Hoping to create some play.} 12. Bd3 {[12']} e5 13. f4 Be6 14. b4 {[13']}
(14. fxe5 Nd7 {is good for Black but the text move leaves him with a weak Pawn
on thr QS.}) 14... Ke7 {[12']} 15. a4 {I felt that his chances lay on the KS.}
a6 16. axb5 axb5 17. f5 gxf5 18. exf5 Bd5 19. Rae1 $2 {It must be wrong to
give up the a-file.} Kd6 {[15'] Playing fast still in view of the time limit.}
20. Be4 Bc4 21. Rf2 Ra3 {Getting on top.} 22. Nb1 Ra1 23. Rd2+ Kc7 24. Bd3 Rd8
25. Rdd1 Bxd3 26. cxd3 Nd5 27. Rxe5 Nxb4 28. Re7+ Rd7 29. Rxd7+ Kxd7 30. Kf2
Ke7 {Threatening 31......Nxe2+} 31. Ke2 {It is difficult to see anything
better.} Nd5 {Threatening 32......RxN} 32. Nd2 $4 {Worried about the clock he
blunders White is probbly lost but can make a fight of it.} ({If} 32. Kd2 Ra2+
$19) (32. Kf2 Kf6 33. g4 Kg5 34. Kf3 Nb4 {etc. White fights on a little.})
32... Nc3+ {Kirkby Lonsdale won the Jamboree which was played at Storeys
Social Club Lancaster} 0-1

