{Time limit 20 in 1hr} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Bc4 c5 4. c3 cxd4 5. cxd4 Nc6 6.
Ne2 e5 {I don't think that this can be best.} 7. d5 Na5 8. Bd3 {Threatening 9.
b4} b6 9. Nbc3 Nf6 10. Bd2 d6 11. Rc1 Nb7 12. f3 O-O 13. O-O Bd7 14. Be3 Ne8 {
Black's only counterplay is via .......f5} 15. g4 f5 16. exf5 gxf5 17. Qc2 Qc8
(17... fxg4 {is dangerous for him.}) 18. h3 h6 19. Qd2 f4 20. Bf2 Qd8 21. b4
Nf6 22. Ba6 {I can tie him up a bit on the QS now.} Qb8 23. Rc2 Nd8 24. Rfc1
Nf7 25. Bh4 ({If} 25. Ne4 Nxe4 26. fxe4 Ng5) 25... Ng5 26. Bxg5 hxg5 27. Qd3
Qd8 28. Ne4 {After much thought. 28.Qg6 is probably O.K. but I felt I had the
better position anyway and didn't want to take risks.} (28. Qg6) 28... Nxe4 29.
Qxe4 Qf6 30. Rc7 Rf7 31. Bd3 Qh6 32. Kg2 a5 33. b5 $5 {This may well be wrong
as he blocks the position now.} Bf6 34. a4 Bd8 35. R7c2 {I was in a time rush
now.} Kg7 36. Rh1 {My flag actually fell somewhere around here but the clock
was faulty and I hadn't nreached the hour mark.} Rf8 37. Nc1 Rh8 38. Ne2 Qf6 {
Adjourned! We now had to vacate the room! We stopped without a sealed move
being made. I now felt that the position was drawn. With te correct play Black
can prevent me breaking through. I decided I might have a chance if he simply
tried to draw by, say, moving his Queen from f6 to h6. See variation below.}
39. Rhc1 {The game commenced 17/11/78} (39. Rhc1 Qh6 40. Ng1 Qf6 41. Rc3 Qh6 $2
42. Rc7 $1 Bxc7 43. Rxc7 Rhd8 44. Qf5 Qf6 45. Rxd7+ Rxd7 46. Qxd7+ Kf8 47. Bf5
$1 Qd8 {(say)} 48. Ne2 Qxd7 49. Bxd7 {Wins}) 39... Rh6 40. Ng1 Kf8 41. Rc3 Qh8
42. Qe2 Rf6 43. Be4 Qg7 44. Qf2 {With thoughts of h4.} Qf7 45. Ne2 Qg7 46. Rh1
Rh6 47. Nc1 Qf6 48. Nd3 Rb8 49. Qc2 Qf7 50. Qc1 Qf6 51. Qa3 Ke7 52. Re1 Qh8 53.
Nf2 ({I now thougght for a long tme about} 53. Bf5 Bxf5 54. Rxe5+ Kd7 55. Rxf5
Rxh3 {but it's all too risky.}) 53... Qf6 54. Bd3 Qh8 55. Rc2 Kf8 56. Kg1 {
I now had thought of marching my King to the QS and forcing my h-Pawn up.} Ra8
57. Bf1 {Deciding instead to have another go with the Knight.} Qg7 58. Ne4 Qe7
59. Rec1 Rb8 60. Nf2 Qf7 61. Qb3 Qe7 62. Re1 Ra8 63. Nd3 Rb8 64. Nc1 Bc8 65.
Ne2 Qf7 {Adjourned. Without a sealed move. A whole session with no captures
and no Pawn moves; the last Pawn move being 31 moves ago. Is there any hope? I
decided that the only hope was to get my Bishop to f5 even though I would
split my Pawns up. Can it be achieved? The game resumed 28/11/78} 66. Nc3 Bd7 (
66... Bb7 {Makes it much harder for me.}) 67. Ne4 {I couldn't have played this
with his Bishop on b7.} Qe7 68. Nf2 Qf7 69. Bd3 Ra8 70. Be4 Rb8 71. Qd3 Rf6 {
He realises he must stop Bf5} 72. Rec1 Be8 $2 {At last! A Moments carelessness
after all that time throws it away.} 73. Rc8 {Now he gets squeezed to death}
Rxc8 {A piece exchanged!} 74. Rxc8 Qe7 75. Bf5 Rh6 76. Kg2 Bf7 77. Qc4 Be8 {
Else I play 78.Qc6 threatening the b-Pawn or Qa8} 78. Ra8 {Threatening 79.Qc8
winning the Bishop.} Bd7 79. Bxd7 Qxd7 80. Qc6 Ke7 {Preventing 81.Qxb7} 81. Ne4
Rg6 82. Rb8 Bc7 83. Rb7 Qxc6 84. bxc6 Kd8 85. Nc3 Rg7 86. Nb5 Kc8 {Loses
quickly.......} ({......but if} 86... Re7 87. h4 gxh4 88. Kh3 {Wins as in a
note below.}) (86... Kc8 {I reasoned thus. Obviously I can play...} 87. Nxd6+ {
but possibly he can be a nuisance after} (87. Rxc7+ Rxc7 88. Nxc7 Kxc7 89. h4
gxh4 ({However suposing he doesn't take my h-Pawn then I queen on g8 one move
before he does on b1} 89... b5 90. hxg5 b4 91. g6 b3 92. g7 b2 93. g8=Q b1=Q
94. Qg7+ Kb6 95. Qb7+) 90. g5 b5 91. g6 b4 92. g7 b3 93. g8=Q b2 94. Qh7+ {wins
}) (87. h4 {forces} gxh4 {or 88.h5}) 87... Bxd6 88. Rxg7 b5 {e.g.} 89. axb5 Bc7
{cuts my Rook off. No doubt I could get round this but there is a quicker way.}
) 87. Nxd6+ {and he immediately resigned. Nearly 8 hours of attrition. Never
say die!} 1-0

