{Time limit 20 moves in 1hr} 1. d4 b6 2. Nf3 Bb7 3. e3 e6 4. Bd3 f5 5. Nbd2 Nf6
6. c3 Be7 7. Qc2 {White has adopted a passive set-up but now decides to force
e4.} c5 8. e4 g6 9. b3 Nc6 10. Bb2 Rc8 {Threatening 11.......cxd} 11. Qb1 {
White seems to have a solid position but is mated in another 10 moves. I felt
now that by opening up the position I would have an advantage on the black
squares.} cxd4 12. Nxd4 ({Mot caring for} 12. cxd4 Nb4) 12... Nxd4 13. cxd4
fxe4 14. Nxe4 Nxe4 ({I considered} 14... Bb4+ 15. Nd2 {but} Bxg2 16. Rg1 {
is good for White.}) 15. Bxe4 Bb4+ 16. Ke2 (16. Kf1 {is possibly better
although with the King's Rook trapped and the open lines Black has much the
better of it. White probably expected now...} Ba6+ {however} 17. Bd3) 16... Qg5
$1 17. Rd1 {Probably best.} ({If} 17. Bxb7 Qd2+ {and} 18. Kf1 ({or} 18. Kf3
Rf8+ 19. Ke4 (19. Kg4) (19. Kg3 {both are much the same}) 19... Rf4+ 20. Ke5
Ke7 21. Z0 {any White move} d6#) 18... Rc2 19. Qe1 Qxe1+ 20. Rxe1 Rxb2 $19) ({
If} 17. Kf1 Qd2 {etc}) 17... Qg4+ 18. Ke3 ({If} 18. Bf3 Ba6+ {Wins the exchange
}) 18... d5 19. Bd3 ({If} 19. Bf3 Qg5+ 20. Ke2 Ba6+) 19... O-O 20. h3 {Short
of time he loses quickly but no less severly than say.....} ({.....} 20. f3
Qxg2 21. Rf1 Qd2#) 20... Qf4+ 21. Ke2 Qxf2# {Very neat. A Pleasing win.} 0-1

