{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nc6 5.
Nf3 Be7 6. Bd3 Nf6 7. c3 b6 8. Qa4 $2 {Rather a waste of a move.} Bb7 9. Qc2 a6
10. Bf4 {Doesn't achieve much} Nd5 11. Bd2 Nf6 {Black has given me my wasted
move back.} 12. O-O-O Nxe4 ({I thought he might go for} 12... Qd7 {followed by.
..} 13. Z0 O-O-O) 13. Bxe4 f5 $5 {Creating a nasty weakness on e6.} 14. Bd3 g6
15. Rhe1 Qd6 16. Bc4 Nd8 17. Ng5 {After much thought. I wasn't overly happy
about it.} Bd5 18. Bb3 b5 {One of several moves which puzzled me. (along with
his 9th & 14th)} 19. Re5 O-O {Best.} ({If} 19... Bf6 20. Bxd5) 20. Rde1 ({
I wanted to play} 20. Nxe6 Bxe6 21. Bxe6+ Nxe6 22. Qb3 Rf6 23. Rde1 Kf7 {
but then I'm stuck.}) 20... Bxg5 {He has to do something in view of his e-Pawn.
} 21. Bxg5 Nf7 22. Bxd5 Nxg5 $2 {Short of time he makes it easy for me.} ({
Correct is} 22... Nxe5 23. Bxa8 Nf7) 23. Bxa8 Rxa8 24. h4 Nf7 25. Rxe6 Qf4+ 26.
Kb1 Qxh4 27. Re7 c6 28. Qb3 Rf8 29. a3 Qxf2 30. R1e2 Qg1+ 31. Ka2 c5 32. Qd5 c4
33. Re1 Qf2 34. Rxf7 {After a number of preparatory moves.} Rxf7 35. Re7 {
A bit of a skittles game as so often in these evening matches.} 1-0

