{Time limit 20 moves per hr} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 {[0']}
5. f3 {[0']} Nc6 {[11'] He said afterwards that he was quite happy to play
against a Maroczy Bind.} 6. c4 {[4']} g6 {[19']} 7. Be3 {[5']} Bg7 {[19']} 8.
Qd2 {[5']} Bd7 {[23']} 9. Nc3 {[5']} Rc8 {[24']} 10. Be2 {[5']} Ne5 11. b3 Qa5
{[32']} 12. Rc1 {[9']} O-O {[34']} 13. O-O {[9']} Rfe8 14. Rfd1 a6 15. g4 Kh8 {
[44']} 16. Kg2 {[18']} e6 17. g5 Ng8 18. h4 Ne7 19. h5 gxh5 20. Rh1 h4 {
[59'] The last few moves were a bit of a rush for him.} 21. Rxh4 {[34']} N5g6
22. Rh5 {Eyeing his Queen.} Nf8 {Black sets up a solid KS defence.} 23. f4 Neg6
{[1hr 22']} 24. Qd3 {[41']} Kg8 25. Bd2 Red8 26. Kg3 {f4 was a bit vulnerable.}
({If} 26. Nd5 Qxd5 $1) 26... Qc5 27. Nf3 Rc6 28. Nd1 Qa3 {[1hr 47']} 29. Rc2 {
[65'] The sealed move White's advantage is primrarliy the cramped state of
some of Black's pieces. I felt that my best bet might be in the endgame. On
the dy of the resumption I had been ill all week and felt bad, should I offer
a draw? I decided to play on and take it staedily. Also he was short of time.
The game resumed on 26/1/79} b5 {As expected} 30. Bc1 ({If} 30. Ne3 e5 $1 {
hence the text}) 30... bxc4 31. Bxa3 cxd3 32. Bxd3 Rxc2 33. Bxc2 {[65'] As per
plan.} Bc6 34. Rh2 d5 35. Rd2 Nd7 36. e5 {Keeping him cramped.} Bf8 {I felt
that he would try to draw by exchanging everything.} 37. Bxf8 Kxf8 38. Nd4 Bb7
39. Bxg6 $1 {I now felt that if I now played Rc2 he would exchange Rooks and
that I could winwith a good Knight v bad Bishop.} fxg6 40. Rc2 Rc8 {Most
obliging although he hadn't much choice.} 41. Rxc8+ Bxc8 {[1hr 18']} 42. Kf3 {
[1hr 26']} Ke8 {[2hr 11']} 43. Ke3 {[1hr 27']} Kd8 {[2hr 16']} 44. Nc6+ {
[1hr 27']} Kc7 45. Ne7 {[1hr 27'] Black is suffering from a bad Bishop, a weak
e-Pawn less space and a potential passe White b-Pawn} Nb6 {[2hr 24']} 46. Kd4 {
[1hr 28']} Bd7 47. Nf2 Nc8 $5 {Seem doubtful as his remaining piece is no
match for my Knight.} 48. Nxc8 Bxc8 49. Kc5 Bd7 50. b4 Bb5 51. Ng4 Kd7 {
[2hr 37']} ({Not} 51... Bc4 $2 52. Nh6) 52. a3 {[1hr 41']} Ke7 53. Ne3 Kd7 {
[2hr 41']} 54. Nc2 {[1hr 43']} Kc7 55. Nd4 Bd7 56. Ne2 Bb5 57. Nc3 Be8 58. a4
Bc6 59. b5 {[1hr 50']} axb5 {[2hr 55']} 60. axb5 Bb7 $5 {After this he loses
quickly} ({I had expected} 60... Be8 {and then} 61. Ne2 Bd7 62. Nd4 Be8 63. b6+
Kb7 64. Kd6 Kxb6 65. Ke7 Kc5 {best} 66. Nb3+ Kb4 67. Nd2 Kc3 68. Nf3 Bb5 {
B moves} 69. Kxe6 {and White should win}) 61. b6+ Kb8 62. Nb5 Bc8 63. Nd6 Bd7
64. Nb5 Be8 65. Nd6 Ba4 66. f5 exf5 67. e6 f4 68. Nb5 f3 69. e7 Bxb5 70. Kxb5 {
A good win. I was now at the half way stage the only player with a 100% score.}
1-0

