{Time limit 42 moves in 1hr 45'} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 e6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. Nc3 a6 5. g3
d5 6. Bg2 Nf6 7. e5 Nd7 8. a4 {We now have a French Defense type of position
but a poor variation for White.} Qc7 9. O-O Be7 10. b3 b6 11. Bb2 Bb7 {I still
hadn't decided which side to castle.} 12. Kh1 h5 13. h4 g6 14. d4 {I anything
this favours Black.} cxd4 15. Nxd4 Nxd4 16. Qxd4 Rc8 17. Rae1 $2 {I don't
understand this, it loses the exchange} Bc5 18. Qd3 Bb4 19. Nxd5 $6 {He tries
this for tactical chances, in view of.......} ({........} 19. Re3 d4 20. Qxd4
Bc5) ({or} 19. Rf3 d4) 19... Bxd5 (19... exd5 20. e6) 20. Bxd5 Nc5 $1 {He
missed this. Now he has Queen, Rook & Bishop en-prise, the Knight covers e6 &
a6 and I get a bit of room round the King.} (20... exd5 21. e6 {is unpleasant.}
) 21. Qe3 Bxe1 22. Rxe1 exd5 {A Rook down he now has to try desperado tactics.}
23. e6 Rh7 ({Not} 23... O-O $2 24. Qd4) 24. exf7+ ({If} 24. e7 f5 25. Bf6 Ne4 {
etc.}) 24... Kxf7 25. f5 Ne4 {A useful move.} 26. Qd4 Qc6 {I thought he had
run out of moves.} 27. fxg6+ (27. Z0 {I threaten} Nxg3+ 28. Kg1 (28. Kh2 Qxc2+)
(28. Kg2 Qxc2+) 28... Qc5) 27... Kxg6 28. Rxe4 dxe4 29. Qe5 Rhc7 {Best I think,
eliminating possibilities of forks and covering the first 3 ranks.} 30. Qg5+ (
30. Qg5+ Kh7 {Resigns. If} 31. Qxh5+ Qh6 32. Qf5+ Qg6 {and he has no checks}) (
{Had he played} 30. g4 e3+ 31. Kg1 Qf3 $1 32. gxh5+ (32. Qg5+ Kf7 33. Qxh5+ Ke6
34. Qg6+ Ke7 35. Qg7+ Ke8 36. Qg6+) 32... Kh7) 30... Kh7 {The match was played
at the Ullswater Centre Penrith.} 0-1

