6. h4 c6 7. Be2 Be6 8. exf5 Bxf5 9. g4 {White decides on a KS Pawn storm.
However, as Black hasn't castled yet White may be simply left with weak Pawns.}
Be6 10. Bxf6 Bxf6 11. g5 Be7 12. Bh5+ g6 13. Bf3 Na6 14. h5 {Possibly he
should complete his development first his g-Pawn is left weak.} Kd7 {
Connecting the back rank and heading for the QS.} 15. Bg4 Bxg4 16. Qxg4+ Kc7
17. Ne4 {defending the g-pawn bit asking for ....d4} Nb4 18. Qe2 Rc8 ({Not} 
18... Bxg5 19. hxg6 hxg6 20. Rxh8 Qxh8 21. Nxg5) 19. a3 Na6 20. Nf3 {[34']} Kb8
{[36']} 21. O-O-O $2 {Putting the King on the wrong file and diagonal.} d5 22.
Nf6 (22. Ned2 {was safer}) 22... Bxf6 23. gxf6 Qxf6 24. Qxe5+ Qxe5 25. Nxe5
Rce8 26. Nf7 Rhf8 27. hxg6 hxg6 28. Nd6 {Losing outright.} Re6 0-1

