{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 per 15'} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. c4 d6 4.
Nc3 e5 5. dxe5 dxe5 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 7. Bg5+ f6 8. Be3 Be6 {After much thought. I
had expected.......} ({.....} 8... c6) 9. O-O-O+ Nd7 10. Bd3 Ne7 11. Nge2 c6
12. h3 Kc7 13. Kb1 {[17']} Nc8 {[45']} 14. Rc1 {[19']} Bf8 {[50']} 15. Rhd1 {
[20/]} Bf7 {[58']} ({If} 15... Bc5 16. Nd5+) 16. a3 Ncb6 17. Na2 Bc5 18. b4
Bxe3 19. fxe3 {The doubled Pawns are no real problem.} a5 $5 {Rather risky as
he was now very short of time.} 20. c5 Nc8 21. b5 Kd8 22. a4 Ke7 23. Bc4 Bxc4
24. Rxc4 Rd8 25. Nec1 cxb5 26. axb5 Na7 {He was rushing here.} 27. Nc3 Rac8 28.
Nb3 a4 $2 ({Maybe} 28... b6) 29. Rxa4 Nxc5 30. Nxc5 Rxc5 {Black makes the time
control but had missed my next move.} 31. Nd5+ Rdxd5 32. Rxd5 Rxd5 33. exd5
Nxb5 {So Black has a pawn for the exchange and should win another.} 34. Kc2 Kd6
35. e4 f5 36. exf5 gxf5 37. Rh4 Kxd5 38. Rxh7 Nd4+ 39. Kd1 b5 40. h4 Ke6 41. h5
Kf6 42. h6 Kg6 43. Re7 Kxh6 44. Rxe5 Kg5 45. Rd5 Ne6 46. Rxb5 Nf4 47. Rb8 Nd5
48. Ke2 Kf4 49. Kf2 Kg4 50. Rg8+ Kf4 51. g3+ {The later play might be easier
without this.} Ke5 52. Kf3 Ke6 53. Rg6+ Ke5 54. Ra6 {[68'] The game was
adjourned here. I felt that this is a win for White. I must sacrifice the Rook
for Knight & Pawn at the appropriate moment. I must manoeuvre my King to g5 or
g6 initially. However, I did not spend enough time on it to find a clear win.
The position to reach is: White King on g6, Pawn on g3, Rook on a6; Black King
one6, Knight on e4, Pawn on f5. I couldn't see a clear win but 1.Rf3 Nd6 2.
Re3+ Ne4 3.g4! and wins} Nf6 {[1hr 33'] Sealed move. The game resumed on 8/2/79
} 55. Ra4 ({Fritz gives} 55. Ra5+ {2.18/0} Nd5 56. Ke2 Kd4 57. Ra4+ Ke5 58. Kd3
Nc7 59. Ra5+ Kf6 60. Kd4 Ne6+ 61. Ke3 Kg5 62. Ra4 Kf6 63. Ra6 Kf7) 55... Nd5
56. Ra5 Ke6 57. Ke2 {An initial sortie in the wrong direction.} Nc7 58. Ke3 Kf6
59. Kd4 Ne6+ 60. Kd5 Nc7+ 61. Kd6 {[1hr 15']} Ne8+ {[2hr]} 62. Kd5 {I'd got
the message now.} Nc7+ 63. Kd4 Ne6+ 64. Ke3 Kg5 65. Re5 Kf6 66. Rd5 Kg5 67. Kf3
Kf6 68. Kg2 Kg6 69. Rd6 Kf6 70. Kh3 Ke5 71. Ra6 {[1hr 26']} Ng5+ {[2hr 30']}
72. Kh4 Nf3+ 73. Kh5 Nd4 74. Kg6 $2 (74. Ra4 {Would lead to the winning
position.}) 74... f4 75. g4 f3 76. g5 Ke4 77. Kh5 {Rubbish. I saw the right
line and played the moves in the wrong order.} ({Correct is} 77. Rf6 Ne2 78.
Kh5 Nf4+ 79. Kg4) 77... f2 78. Ra1 Nf3 79. Rf1 Nxg5 {Rather poor. Apart from
the mental lapse on move 77, my adjournment analysis wasn't sufficiently
thorough.} 1/2-1/2

