{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5.
Be3 {Doesn't turn out too well.} Qb6 6. b3 Nc6 7. c3 Nge7 8. Nc2 O-O 9. b4 Bxe3
10. Nxe3 f5 {Maybe premature.} 11. Nc4 Qd8 12. b5 {[23']} Na5 {[15']} (12...
Nb8 {is possibly better.}) 13. Nxa5 Qxa5 14. Qd6 Rf7 15. f3 fxe4 16. fxe4 Ng6
17. g3 Qa4 ({I wanted to play} 17... b6 {but} 18. a4 {traps my Queen.}) 18. Bd3
b6 19. Nd2 a6 $5 ({Maybe best is} 19... Bb7 {and if} 20. Qc7 d5) 20. Ke2 axb5
21. Rhf1 Qa3 22. Qxb6 {Dangerous.} Qxc3 23. Rac1 Qb4 $4 {Rubbish. I realised
immediately that I should have played 23......Qa3. Fortunately White replied
quickly.} (23... Qa3 $142 {if} 24. Rxf7 {then} Qxc1) 24. Qd8+ $2 ({Correct is} 
24. Rxf7 Kxf7 25. Qd8 $18) 24... Rf8 25. Rxf8+ Qxf8 26. Qxf8+ Kxf8 27. Bxb5 Ke7
28. a4 Ba6 29. Rb1 Ne5 30. h3 Nc6 31. Ke3 h6 32. Nc4 Kd8 33. Nb6 Ra7 34. Rd1
Nb8 35. Kd4 Rb7 36. Kc5 Ke7 37. Nc8+ Kd8 38. Nd6 Rc7+ 39. Kb6 {I think he felt
that he had won a piece here.} Rc3 40. Bxa6 Rc6+ 41. Kb5 Nxa6 42. Nf7+ Kc8 ({
Not} 42... Kc7 43. Rxd7+) 43. Rd6 Nc7+ 44. Ka5 Rc4 {Adjourned. He offered a
draw next day which I accepted. He had sealed 45.Rd3 A rather flawed piece of
work.} 1/2-1/2

