{Time limit 20 moves per hr} 1. d4 b6 2. e4 e6 3. g3 {In a conventional Q.
IndianWhite generally fianchettos his Bishop. However, having a Pawn on e4
rather than a Knight on f3 gives White immediate problems.} Bb7 4. Bg2 f5 {
He looked worried now.} 5. d5 Nf6 6. Bg5 Bc5 7. Nh3 {Unnecessarily putting the
Knight off-side. I wasn't actually threatening 7.......Bxf2+} fxe4 8. dxe6 {
Clearly best} h6 (8... dxe6 {is hardly attractive.}) ({I also considered} 8...
a5) 9. exd7+ Nbxd7 10. Be3 Bxe3 ({Also OK is} 10... Qe7) 11. fxe3 Ne5 12. Nc3 {
Probably best.} Qe7 13. Nf2 {It's difficult to find good moves for White.} Rd8
14. Qe2 Nf3+ 15. Bxf3 exf3 16. Qc4 (16. Qb5+ c6 {and he certainly can't defend
his e-Pawn.}) 16... Qxe3+ 17. Kf1 Rd2 18. Ncd1 ({If} 18. Qa4+ b5 19. Qxb5+ c6)
18... Qe2+ {Short and sweet} 0-1

