{Time limit 26 moves in 1hr 30'} 1. e4 e5 2. Bc4 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. d3 h6 5. Be3
Bb4 6. a3 ({If} 6. Nge2 {then maybe} Ng4) 6... Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 d5 {This seems to
equalise for Black.} 8. exd5 Nxd5 9. Qf3 $5 {Overexhuberent. I shouldn't do
this sort of thing against strong opposition.} Be6 10. Bd2 ({I had originally
intended} 10. Rb1 {....but didn't like} Nxe3 11. Bxe6 Nxc2+ 12. Kd2 fxe6 13.
Qh5+ Kd7 14. Kxc2 b6) 10... O-O {I was unhappy now. .....f5 is coming. I
considered 11.g4 but it's too rash.} 11. Ne2 (11. g4) 11... f5 12. Ng3 {
I wasn't sure where my King should go.} Qd7 13. h3 {Although he wasn't
threatening to win my Queen (13......f4 etc.) I felt that 13.h3 was most solid.
} Rae8 (13... f4 14. Ne4 Bg4 15. Nc5) 14. O-O-O {My position is horrible with
the centre liable to open I move my King, and take my chances on the QS.} Qd6
15. Kb2 b5 {Black switches his attack.} 16. Bb3 a5 {I felt that it was almost
resignable.} 17. Ra1 {[60'] Black now spent a long time deciding how to break
through.} Nb6 $2 {[59'] After this Black is no doubt still on top but I get a
ray of hope.} 18. Nxf5 $1 {Winning a pawn, and more important, getting the
Knight onto a good square.} Qd7 19. g4 Na4+ 20. Kc1 Bxb3 ({I think that} 20...
Kh8 {unpinning the Bishop and threatening 21......g6 is better.}) 21. cxb3 Nc5
22. Kc2 Rd8 23. Rhd1 Qe6 (23... Nxd3 $2 24. Qxc6 $1 Qxc6 25. Ne7+) 24. Rab1 Kh8
25. Be3 {White is suddenly recovering. Also Black was short of time and wanted
to keep the attack going so.........} Rd5 $2 (25... Nb7 26. Qe2 {and White is
OK.}) 26. c4 {With ony ~10' I didn't have time to analyse this properly.
However, I felt that if I was going to try to win I had to play this. Also
Black was down to a few minutes.} bxc4 27. bxc4 {Quite a crowd gathered now.}
Rxd3 ({If} 27... Nd4+ 28. Nxd4 Rxf3 29. Nxe6 $18) 28. Rxd3 {With hardly any
time left Black tries.....} e4 ({When considering 26.c4 I had seen} 28... Nxd3
29. Kxd3 e4+ 30. Qxe4 Rd8+ 31. Nd4 Ne5+ {and felt that I was OK eg} 32. Ke2
Qxc4+ 33. Kd1 Qf1+ 34. Kd2 Nc4+ 35. Kc3) 29. Bxc5 $1 {I grab as much as I can
for the Queen.} ({I now saw straight away that say} 29. Qh1 exd3+ 30. Kd2 Qxc4
{is probably won for Black,}) 29... exf3 ({If} 29... exd3+ {simply} 30. Qxd3) (
29... Qxc4+ 30. Rc3 Qa4+ 31. Rbb3) 30. Bxf8 Qxc4+ 31. Rc3 ({I had long enough
to decide that} 31. Kd2 Qa2+ 32. Kc1 Qc4+ {is a draw.}) 31... Qe2+ 32. Kc1 ({
With no time to think I couldn't risk} 32. Kb3 a4+) 32... Qe1+ ({I expected
him to play but having to move very fast he decided to keep checking me. In
fact} 32... Qxf2 33. Rxc6 {seems Ok for me.}) 33. Kb2 Qd2+ {Maybe he could
take the f-Pawn here.} 34. Rc2 Qd5 35. Bxg7+ Kh7 36. Bc3 {with about 1' to
spare.} Qb5+ {With seconds to spare. The game was stopped here. Black resigned.
Not one of my best games but one of my best-ever results. Quite a recovery
from the position after about 16 moves. J.Toothill had the CM title.} (36...
Qb5+ {It's a fairly straight-forward win.e.g.} 37. Ka1 Qc5 38. Rb7 Qxa3+ 39.
Kb1 Qc5 {say} 40. Rxc7+ Kg8 (40... Kg6 41. Rg7#) 41. Rxc6 {etc.}) 1-0

