{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 per 15'} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. e3 Nc6
4. Nf3 d6 5. d3 g6 6. Be2 Bg7 7. a3 a5 8. Qc2 O-O 9. O-O Ne8 10. Rb1 f5 {
I was fairly happy with the outcome of the opening.} 11. b4 h6 {A bit slow
maybe.} 12. c5 Ne7 13. cxd6 cxd6 14. Qb3+ Kh8 15. Rd1 Nc7 16. bxa5 Rxa5 17. Bd2
Ra7 18. Rdc1 Nc6 19. Ne1 g5 20. a4 f4 21. Nb5 Be6 22. Qd1 Nxb5 23. axb5 Ne7 24.
b6 Ra6 25. d4 fxe3 {A small diversion.} 26. Bxe3 ({If} 26. fxe3 {his d-Pawn is
weak.}) 26... Ra2 27. Rc2 Rxc2 28. Nxc2 {A bit of a rush here.} Nd5 29. Qd2
Nxe3 30. Qxe3 (30. fxe3 {is more solid.}) 30... Bf5 {Rather awkward for him
now and he loses a Pawn.} 31. Bd3 exd4 32. Nxd4 Bxd3 33. Qxd3 Qf6 34. Nf3 g4
35. Nd2 Qxf2+ 36. Kh1 Re8 37. Rf1 Re1 38. Rxe1 Qxe1+ 39. Nf1 Qf2 40. Qb5 d5 41.
Qe8+ Kh7 42. Qb5 d4 43. Qd3+ Kh8 44. Qb5 {The game was adjourned.} d3 $1 {
Rhe sealed move and much the best. The game resumed on 16/3/79} 45. Qe8+ {
Forced} ({White seems to be lost.e.g.} 45. Qxd3 $4 Bd4) ({or} 45. Qb1 d2 46.
Qd3 Bd4) 45... Qf8 46. Qe1 Qf4 47. Nd2 (47. Ng3 Qe5 48. Z0 Qa1 {forces Queens
off.}) (47. Qb1 d2 48. Qd1 Bc3 49. Qe2 Qd6 50. Qd1 h5 {etc.}) (47. Qd1 Qd4 48.
Qe1 (48. Nd2 Qe3 {Threatens 49......Bc3} 49. Nf1 (49. Nb1 Bb2) 49... Qe2) 48...
Qe5 49. Qb1 (49. Qc1 Qc3 50. Qd1 Qc2 51. Qe1 Qe2 52. Qc1 Kh7 53. Qb1 Bb2 {
as in the main line.}) 49... Qe2 50. Qc1 (50. Ng3 Qc2 51. Qe1 d2) 50... Kh7 51.
Qb1 Bb2 52. Kg1 Kg7 53. Kh1 Kh8 54. Z0 d2) {I had disposed of this line fairly
early in my analyasis, but, with another game in play I couldn't quite recall
the details [I now had a very heavy schedule of games to play so very
foolishly I agreed to play on simultaneously with playing my C.C.game with Tom
Hayes Idiocy!]. Without much thought I played......} 47... Qe5 48. Qc1 Qa1 $2 {
I neede to make a move to reach the time control and with my other clock going
rushed into 48.......Qa1? Leads to a fairly quick draw.} ({If} 48... Qe3 {
he checks on c8 & c4}) ({If} 48... Qd4 49. Qc8+ Kh7 50. Qf5+) (48... Qc3 $142
49. Qe1 Qa1 50. Nb1 Qe5) ({or} 48... Bf8 $142) 49. Nb1 Kh7 $2 {Another half
thought out move. I seemed to be winning a piece in my other game.} (49... Qd4
$142) 50. Qf1 {Draws} Qd4 51. Qf5+ Kg8 52. Qe6+ {Now my attempt to avoid the
draw is very dangerous. Additionally it appeared that we had lost the match
anyway and my other game, critical to winning the club championship was
getting involved. I came to my senses and - Draw agreed. A pity after good
play in the first session, but one can't expect to play well in two simul
games of this type.} 1/2-1/2

