{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. d4 e6 2. e3 {He has a tendencey to play
stodgy stonewall type set-ups} c5 3. c3 Nf6 4. Bd3 b6 5. Nf3 Bb7 6. O-O Qc7 {
Threatening 7......Ng4 which will force the weakening g3.} 7. h3 Be7 8. Nbd2
Nc6 9. e4 {[6']} d6 {[6']} 10. a3 a5 11. Re1 Rd8 12. Qc2 h6 {This game was in
some ways difficult as I could not motivate myself. I have a 100% score
against K.L. He plays quickly and as a result makes tactical errors. I found
myself unwilling to spend a long time on my moves as I expected a mistake
sooner or later from him.} 13. Nf1 g5 {Additionaly, I felt that I would take
liberties.} 14. e5 Nd7 15. Qe2 (15. exd6 Bxd6 {is good for Black.}) 15... cxd4
16. cxd4 $2 {[19'] and here is the first mistake. White loses a Pawn as his
Queen is trying to defend e5 & d3} dxe5 {[13'] He sighed here!} 17. dxe5 Ndxe5
18. Nxe5 Nxe5 19. Bb5+ {Best.} Nd7 ({If} 19... Nc6 {it may get pinned by an
eventual Rc1}) 20. Be3 {White's position is quite good. He threatens 21.Rc1
also Rd1 or Bd4 and the b-Pawn may have to be abandoned.} O-O 21. Qh5 Kg7 22.
Bd4+ (22. Rac1 {looks better.}) 22... Bf6 23. Bxd7 $2 {Definitely wrong.} Bxd4
24. Ba4 Bxf2+ 25. Kxf2 Qf4+ 26. Kg1 Qxa4 27. Qe2 Qd4+ 28. Kh1 Qd3 29. Qe5+ Kh7
30. Ng3 Qd5 31. Qe2 Qd2 32. Rac1 Qxe2 33. Rxe2 Rd3 34. Rc7 {[40']} Bd5 {[58']}
35. Ne4 Kg6 36. Kh2 Bxe4 37. Rxe4 Rd2 38. b4 axb4 39. Rxb4 Ra8 40. Rxb6 Rxa3
41. Rb1 Raa2 42. Rg1 h5 0-1

