{Time limit 20 moves per hr} 1. d4 b6 2. e4 Bb7 3. Nc3 e6 4. Nf3 Bb4 5. Bd3 Ne7
6. Qe2 d5 7. Bd2 c5 (7... O-O {is possibly more solid.}) 8. Bb5+ Bc6 9. exd5
exd5 ({If} 9... Nxd5 10. Ne5 {is a nuisance}) 10. O-O O-O 11. Bxc6 Nbxc6 12.
Nd1 Bxd2 13. Qxd2 Nf5 14. dxc5 ({If} 14. c3 cxd4 15. Nxd4 Ncxd4 16. cxd4 Qf6)
14... bxc5 15. Ne3 {Forcing an exchange of Knights. I began to wonder if he
was playing for a draw - if so, not a good policy in a K.O.with the White
pieces, as he would have Black in a replay.} Nxe3 16. Qxe3 d4 17. Qe4 Qd7 18.
Ng5 g6 19. f4 {[42'] A bit of aggression - maybe I will get some chances.} Rfe8
({Not} 19... f5 $2 20. Qe6+ {winning the c-Pawn.}) 20. Qd3 Rab8 21. Ne4 $2 {
White gets ambituos but makes a tactical error. This threatens a Knight
forkand the c-Pawn but allows a nasty pin.} Qf5 {Suddenly White is in trouble.}
22. Rae1 Re6 {Now he had a long think. 23.......Rbe8 is threatened winning the
Knight. He can't simply move it as he loses at least the b-Pawn.} 23. Qa6 {
I was half expecting this. At least it's active but puts the Queen offside and
immediately loses the b-Pawn.} Rxb2 24. Qc8+ {This doesn't help much.} Kg7 25.
h3 Rxe4 (25... Z0 {hoping to get in} 26. g4 Qd5 27. f5 Z0 28. f6+) 26. Qxc6
Rxe1 27. Rxe1 Qxc2 28. Rf1 Rb1 29. Qd6 Rxf1+ 30. Kxf1 Qb1+ 31. Kf2 Qxa2+ 32.
Kg3 Qe6 33. Qxc5 Qe3+ 34. Kh2 Qxf4+ 35. Kh1 a6 36. Qc4 Qf6 37. Qa4 Qd6 38. Qa1
f6 39. Qb1 d3 40. Qb7+ Kh6 {A good solid win relying on superior technique
rather than pyrotechnics. (see S.Webb "Chess for Tigers")} 0-1

