{Time limit 20 moves per hr} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 e5 5. Nb3 {
A wiwn in this game meant that I must come at least equal first in the
championhsip, so I play carefully.} a6 6. a4 h6 {All a bit slow.} 7. Be3 Nf6 8.
Bc4 {Black's move order has allowed me to ignore the attack on the e-Pawn.} d6
9. O-O Be7 10. a5 {Tying him down a bit.} Be6 11. Bd5 ({Now if} 11. Bxe6 fxe6 {
and he can't play...} 12. Z0 Ng4) 11... O-O 12. Nc3 {[13']} Nd7 {[18']} 13. f4
exf4 (13... Nc5 {May be playable.}) 14. Bxf4 Nf6 15. Qd2 Bxd5 {Black tries to
free his position by exchanging.} 16. exd5 Nb8 ({I was expecting} 16... Ne5)
17. Nd4 Re8 $2 {Not realising the danger. Now he gets wiped out.} 18. Bxh6 gxh6
{No doubt he could prolong matters by declining the sacrifice. However, I
think that he had decided to call my bluff, probably missing my 21st move.} 19.
Qxh6 Ng4 {He was threatened with both 20.Nf5 & 20.Rf3-g3+} ({If} 19... Nh7 20.
Rxf7 $1) 20. Qh5 Ne5 {Defending f7, or is he?} 21. Rxf7 $1 Nxf7 22. Ne6 {
Winning the Queen in view of the mating threat.} Bf6 23. Qg6+ ({Black hoped for
} 23. Nxd8 $2 Rxd8 {With R, N & B for Q and 3Ps}) 23... Kh8 24. Nxd8 Bd4+ 25.
Kh1 Rxd8 26. Qxf7 Nd7 27. Ne4 Ne5 28. Qh5+ Kg7 29. Ng5 {A neat sacrificial
attack.} 1-0

