{Time limit 20 moves per hr} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. e5 Nc6 5. c3 d4 6.
Bd3 {Rather odd.} Qb6 7. Na3 Bd7 8. O-O $5 dxc3 9. Nc4 Qc7 ({I considered} 9...
cxb2 10. Nxb6 bxa1=Q 11. Nxa8 Kd8 {but it wasn't very clear. I only needed
half a point to be outright winner so played it safe.}) 10. dxc3 b5 11. Ne3 c4
12. Bc2 Bc5 {I began to get a bit overconfident around here.} 13. Qe2 Rb8 $2
14. b4 Bb6 ({Maybe} 14... Bf8 {is best.}) 15. Kh1 Nge7 $2 (15... h6 {Would
save a lot of trouble.}) 16. a4 a6 17. Ng5 {Going to e4 & d6} Na7 $5 {Now the
Black squared Bishop goes.} 18. a5 Bxe3 19. Bxe3 Nd5 20. Bd2 Nc8 $4 {Rubbish.
I still didn't realise that I was in touble.} 21. Qh5 {Now I know that I was
lost. After much thought all I could find was.} Rf8 ({I had vagually looked at
this and thought} 21... Bc6 {was O.K. but} 22. Nxe6) 22. Qxh7 Bc6 23. Qxg7 Nce7
24. Ne4 Rg8 25. Qh7 Rd8 26. Rf2 Kf8 27. Re1 Ng6 {Threatening 28......Rh8} 28.
Qh6+ Ke8 29. Nd6+ Rxd6 30. exd6 Qxd6 31. Bxg6 Rxg6 32. Qh8+ Kd7 {Here the game
was adjourned and White sealed his move. I spent very little time on it as 33.
f5 is quite obvious and an absolute killer.} 33. Qe5 $2 {Not so good (The game
resumed 1/5/79.)} (33. f5) 33... f5 34. Kg1 Nf6 {I have a bit of hope now.} 35.
Qxd6+ Kxd6 36. g3 Ng4 37. Be3 {White decided that my Knight was too strong.}
Nxf2 38. Kxf2 Rh6 39. h4 Ke7 40. Bd4 Rg6 41. Be5 Kf7 42. Re3 Rg8 43. Kg1 Kg6
44. Kh2 Kh5 {Now it's drawn and unfortunately I relaxed again.} 45. Kh3 Bd5 {
I offered a draw here.} 46. Bf6 Rf8 47. Bd4 Rg8 {Ridiculous lack of
concentration.} (47... Be4 {draws easily but I felt that it didn't really
matter what I played.}) 48. Re5 Kg6 {After much thought.} ({If} 48... Rg6 49.
Bc5 Rg7 50. Bf8 Rg8 51. Be7 {followed by} Z0 52. Bg5 {and} Z0 53. g4+) 49. g4
fxg4+ 50. Kxg4 Kf7+ 51. Rg5 {[2hr 19']} Be4 {[2hr 47']} 52. Kg3 Bg6 53. Be5 Rd8
54. h5 Rd3+ 55. Kh4 Bf5 56. Rg7+ Kf8 57. Kg5 Rg3+ 58. Kh6 {Short of time I
couldn't decide whether the exchange of Rooks was better.} Rh3 (58... Rxg7) 59.
Ra7 Bg4 60. Kg5 Bxh5 61. Rxa6 Bf3 62. Rxe6 Rg3+ 63. Kf6 Bh5 64. f5 Rg7 65. Bd6+
Kg8 66. Re7 Rg2 67. a6 Ra2 68. a7 Ra6 69. Ke5 Bf3 70. f6 Bh5 71. Rg7+ Kh8 72.
Bc5 Bf3 73. Kf5 Be4+ 74. Ke5 {If he takes the Bishop my Rook goes suicidal.} (
74. Kxe4 Rxa7 (74... Re6+ 75. Kf3 Re3+ 76. Kf4 Rf3+ 77. Ke5 Re3+) 75. Bxa7)
74... Bd5 75. f7 {Very unsatisfactory. Overconfidence to start with then slack
play later. This allowed Phil Seery to tie =1st with me.} 1-0

