{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 d6 5. Bxc6+
bxc6 6. d4 exd4 7. Nxd4 c5 8. Ne2 {After some thought. I felt that the Knight
might go to g3-f5 or h5 or else go to d5 via f4.} Nf6 9. Nbc3 Be7 10. Nf4 O-O
11. b3 {Doesn't turn out too well I should really castle.} Bb7 12. f3 Re8 13.
Bb2 c6 {Now he can force ......d5} 14. O-O d5 15. Re1 $2 {I didn't realise the
trouble that I was getting into.} (15. exd5 {is nasty but a little better}) ({
Maybe the best line is something like.} 15. e5) 15... Bd6 {The Knight proves
to be awkwardly placed.} 16. Qd2 Qc7 17. Nce2 {Now I'm all tied up.} dxe4 {
Now I knew that I was lost. Without much hope I tried......} 18. Bxf6 gxf6 $2 (
18... e3 $1 {wins fairly comfortably.}) 19. Nh5 {Suddenly the bad Knight is a
good Knight.} e3 {Too late.} 20. Nxf6+ Kh8 $2 {A second error.} 21. Qd3 Kg7 22.
Nxe8+ Rxe8 23. Ng3 c4 {Black resigned before I could reply. A scrappy win P.
Dickinson had the Candidate Expert title (C.X.) Which was awarded for a player
graded 175 or over for two consecutive seasons. If the grade fell below 17 the
title was lost.} 1-0

