{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. g3 f5 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. d3 Be7
6. Rb1 O-O 7. Nf3 a5 8. a3 Kh8 9. O-O d6 10. b4 axb4 11. axb4 Qe8 12. b5 Nd8
13. c5 {White decides on active play immediately.} Bd7 14. Qb3 Be6 15. Qc2 Nd5
16. Ng5 {After a lot of thought.} Nxc3 17. Qxc3 Bd7 {I had originally intended
17......Bb8 but felt d7 was the better square.} 18. cxd6 cxd6 19. b6 Bf6 20. e4
$5 {This hands the innitiative over to Black} Bxg5 21. Bxg5 Ne6 22. Bd2 f4 23.
gxf4 Rc8 24. Qb2 Nxf4 25. Bxf4 Rxf4 26. Rbc1 {I now searched for a long while
for a clear winning line but couldn't find one.} Rxc1 27. Qxc1 Bc6 {After much
thought. I didn't like this but there seemed nothing definite on the KS his
Queen threatened to penetrate to c7 and my back rank is weak.} 28. f3 {[1hr
33']} h6 {[1hr 32']} (28... Qd8 $142) 29. d4 Qd8 30. Qb2 d5 $5 {Active lay
seemed best.} 31. dxe5 ({If} 31. exd5 Qxd5 32. dxe5 Qc5+ 33. Kh1 Rb4) 31...
dxe4 32. fxe4 Rxf1+ 33. Kxf1 Qd3+ 34. Kf2 Bxe4 35. Bxe4 Qxe4 36. Qb5 Qf4+ 37.
Kg2 Qe4+ 38. Kg3 Qe3+ 39. Kg2 Qe4+ {Here I offered adraw but he was deaf and
didn't hear me!} 40. Kg3 Qe3+ {Now he claimed a draw with} 41. Kg2 {A
reasonable game. [P.C.Hoad had the CX ttle]} 1/2-1/2

