{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. Bd3 c5
6. c3 Nc6 7. Ne2 cxd4 8. cxd4 Nb6 {The Leningrad system.} 9. O-O Nb4 {It's not
clear that this achieves much.} 10. Bb1 a5 11. a3 Nc6 {[4']} 12. Nf3 (12. f4
$142) 12... Be7 13. Re1 Bd7 14. Ng3 {With the nuisance threat of Nh5. However,
I wasn't really sure what to do with this position.} g6 15. Bd3 a4 16. Be3 Na5
17. Nd2 Rc8 18. Rc1 Rxc1 19. Qxc1 Qc8 20. Qb1 Nbc4 21. Nxc4 Nxc4 22. Bxc4 Qxc4
23. Rc1 Qa6 24. Rc3 Bb5 {After a lot of thought.} 25. Rc8+ {Else 25......Bc4}
Bd8 26. Bg5 Kd7 27. Qc1 Bc4 {I had felt from the start that Black was playing
for a draw.} 28. Rxd8+ Rxd8 29. Bxd8 Kxd8 30. Qh6 {About the only hope of
playing for a win.} Ke7 31. Qxh7 Qb6 32. Qh4+ Ke8 33. Qh8+ {Gaining time on
the clock.} Ke7 34. h4 $5 Qxb2 35. Qf6+ Ke8 36. Qh8+ Ke7 37. h5 gxh5 38. Nxh5
Qxa3 39. Nf6 {Threatening mate in 1 but he has perpetual check. Unfortunately
I don't have time to prevent it. e.g.....} (39. g3 Qa1+ 40. Kh2 Qxd4 {etc.})
39... Qc1+ 40. Kh2 Qf4+ 41. Kh1 Qc1+ 42. Kh2 Qf4+ 43. Kg1 1/2-1/2

