1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. O-O d6 6. b3 Nbd7 7. Bb2 c5 8. Nbd2
Rb8 9. e4 b6 10. Re1 cxd4 11. Bxd4 {White seems determined to force e4} Bb7 12.
e5 {After a long think and leading to a very drawn position. I don't think he
was hoping for more.} (12. c4 $142) 12... dxe5 13. Nxe5 Bxg2 14. Kxg2 Nxe5 15.
Bxe5 Qd5+ {This wouldn't have been possible hd he played 12.c4} 16. Nf3 Rbd8
17. Qxd5 {Here he offered a draw and there seemed little point in playing on.
Drawn. Lack of ambition on the part of the Lancashire Chess Association
President.[D.Lees had the CX title] A mediocre tournament for me.} 1/2-1/2

