{Time limit 40' each for all moves} 1. d4 e6 2. c4 b6 3. Nc3 Bb7 4. e4 Bb4 5.
Bd3 f5 6. exf5 $4 {Asso often in these 40' tournaments, aand especially in the
first round, players set off at lightning speed. Here he starts much too
quickly and blunders horifically. He carries on hoping something might turn up.
} Bxg2 7. Qh5+ {[5'] He started to think for a while, but it's a bit too late.}
Kf8 {[4']} 8. fxe6 dxe6 9. Nf3 Bxh1 10. Bg5 Qe8 11. Qg4 h6 12. Bf4 Nf6 13. Qh3
Nc6 14. O-O-O Bxf3 15. Qxf3 Nxd4 16. Qe3 Nf5 17. Qe5 $4 {Playing quickly again
in the hope of 'Randomising' the game he blunders again. What follows is
hardly worth bothering with.} Bd6 18. Qe2 Bxf4+ 19. Kc2 $2 Nd4+ 20. Kb1 Nxe2
21. Nxe2 e5 22. Re1 Qd7 23. Rd1 Rd8 24. Nc3 Qh3 25. Bg6 Rxd1+ 26. Nxd1 Qf1 27.
Kc2 Qxc4+ 28. Nc3 Nd5 29. Bd3 Nb4+ 30. Kd1 Qxd3+ 31. Ke1 Nc2# {I could hardly
have hoped for an easier start. He simply played much too fast. 30 players now
had 1/1} 0-1

