{Time limit 40' each for all moves} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 Bb4 $5 {As with
my last opponent he played rather fast. I have sneaking suspicion , that
intendidng to play the Winawer, he whipped out his Bishop to b4 before
realising that my Knight was on d2 not c3?} 4. c3 Ba5 {e7 looks better} 5. b4
Bb6 6. a4 c6 {[2']} 7. Qg4 {[1']} g6 8. e5 Nh6 9. Qh3 Nf5 10. Ngf3 {[2']} ({Not
} 10. g4 Nh4 ({or} 10... Qh4)) 10... a5 {[7']} 11. g4 {[3']} Ng7 {[10']} 12.
Nb3 {[4']} h6 13. Bg5 {[5']} Qd7 14. Bf6 Kf8 {[15']} 15. Bd3 {[8']} Rh7 16. Qg3
Ne8 17. h4 Bc7 $4 {Black decides to pin my e-Pawn, threatening to win a piece.}
({There were now various lines like} 17... Nxf6 18. exf6 Rh8 {(say)} 19. bxa5
Bxa5 $4 20. Nxa5 Rxa5 21. Qxb8) {There is one slight drawback however} 18. Nc5
{I thought that he might now resign with all the pieces on the board. However,
people rarely give in too early in these 40' games as "anything can happen" in
a time-rush.} Nxf6 19. Nxd7+ Nfxd7 20. h5 Kg7 21. hxg6 fxg6 22. Qh4 Kf7 $2 23.
Ng5+ {About 14 players had 2/2} 1-0

