{Time limit 40' each for all moves} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 g6
5. c4 Bg7 6. Nb3 Nf6 7. Nc3 O-O 8. Be2 d6 9. Be3 Bd7 10. O-O Rc8 11. f3 Ne5 {
The problem with playing this line gainst the Accelerated Dragon is that the
c-Pawn is hard to defend.} 12. Nd2 Be6 13. b3 Qa5 14. Rc1 Nfd7 15. Ndb1 {
16.f4 is now threatened.} ({Unfortunately} 15. f4 Nc6 16. f5 {doesn't win a
piece as the c3Knight is en-prise.}) 15... Nc6 16. Bd2 Qb6+ 17. Kh1 a6 18. h3
Bd4 19. Bh6 {A doubtful move.} Rfe8 20. f4 $2 {A poor move leaving the Bishop
on h6 stranded.} Be3 21. Na4 Qd4 (21... Qa7 $142 {e.g.} 22. Rc2 Nd4) 22. Qxd4
Bxd4 $4 {Forgetting about the threat.} 23. f5 gxf5 24. exf5 {There were now
Myself A.Graham (who had beaten John Toothill) and Ralph Mellor on 4/4} 1-0

