{Time limit 40' each for all moves.} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 c5 4. exd5 exd5
5. Bb5+ Bd7 6. Bd3 $5 {I'm not sure why I decided against 6.Qe2+ possibly I
was worried that it was a bit drawish. However, at the beginning of this round
it looked as if a draw would be good enough as, even if Nick harris beat Ralph
Mellor I would have a better sum-of-opponents score. I decided to play solidly
if possible and see how it went.} Nf6 7. dxc5 Bxc5 8. Nb3 Bd6 9. Bg5 {I
started to realise that I wasn't playing it very well.} (9. Be3 $142) 9... O-O
10. Ne2 {I have to block the e-file although the Knight would be better of f3.}
Nc6 11. c3 {I started to use up time around here.} (11. O-O $2 Bxh2+ $1) 11...
Ne5 12. Qd2 Nxd3+ 13. Qxd3 Bc6 14. O-O-O Be7 15. Nf4 Ng4 16. Bxe7 Qxe7 17. Qg3
Nf6 18. Nd4 {Threatening to win immediately with 19.Nf5} Qd7 19. f3 Rfe8 20.
Qg5 h6 21. Qg3 Rac8 22. Nd3 Ba4 23. Rde1 Ne4 $1 {I was starting to worry about
being behind on the clock, this move didn't help matters.} 24. fxe4 dxe4 25.
Kb1 exd3 26. Qxd3 Rxe1+ 27. Rxe1 Bc6 28. g3 Qd5 29. Qf1 Qh5 30. Qe2 {I now
stopped scoring.} Qg6+ 31. Ka1 Re8 32. Qd2 Rd8 33. Re3 Qd6 34. a3 Re8 35. Qe2
Rd8 {We manoeuvred around for a few moves and the following position was
reached. I was now well down on time so I played........} 36. Nxc6 {and
offered a draw. He accepted immediately rather to my surprise as he could win
the tournament if he beat me. I now went off to get an up to date 'SO scores'
for myself and Nick harris, whose game with Ralph mellor was very complicated.
To my horror I found that my previous opponens were doing badly in the last
round whereas his were doing welland he could end up with a SOS of 1pt above
me. 15' later Ralph won to secure second place for himself and leave me 1st. I
won £20. There was a 4-way tie for 2nd placeon 5pts with Ralph Mellor taking
the prize on SOS. My best tournament result for a long while.} 1/2-1/2

[Event "Friendly Match"]
[Site "Kirkby Lonsdale"]
