{Time limit 20 mph} 1. Nf3 d5 2. d4 c5 3. e3 Nc6 4. Bb5 Bg4 5. Bxc6+ {No doubt
he was playing for a draw.} bxc6 6. O-O e6 7. h3 Bh5 8. c3 {[3']} Qc7 {[3']} 9.
Nbd2 Bd6 10. Re1 Nf6 11. Qc2 Bg6 {To prevent e4.} 12. Qd1 {[9']} O-O {[8']} 13.
b3 Qa5 14. Bb2 Bh5 15. Qc1 cxd4 16. cxd4 Rac8 17. Bc3 {[16']} Qa6 {[17']} 18.
b4 {As usual I was having trouble motivating myself against a weak opponent
and the game was progressing very fast. I decided that I must transfer my
Queen over to the KS and attack there.} Qd3 19. a3 {[19']} Ne4 {[29']} 20. Nxe4
Qxe4 21. Nd2 {Suddenly his KSis a bit short of defenders.} Qh4 22. e4 f6 23.
Re3 {He suddenly becomes more aggresive but his position is rather shaky.} e5
24. g4 {A touch of desperation now.} ({If} 24. exd5 exd4 {Forks Rook & Bishop.}
) ({or} 24. dxe5 fxe5 {Threatens 25......Qxf2+, and 24......d4}) 24... Bg6 25.
Nf3 $2 {His position was difficult but this loses a Pawn and leaves him with a
bad game.} Qxh3 26. Nxe5 Qh4 27. Nxg6 Qxg4+ 28. Kf1 Qxg6 29. Qd1 $2 dxe4 30. d5
Bf4 31. Re2 {His position just collapses.} Qf5 32. Rc2 cxd5 33. Bd4 Qh3+ 34.
Ke2 Rxc2+ 35. Qxc2 Rc8 36. Qb3 $2 {saves a few moves} Qxb3 0-1

