{Time limit 42 moves in 1hr 45' then 15' to finish.} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5
Nd4 4. Bc4 {I didn't know much about this defence so preferred not to play the
more usual......} ({.....} 4. Nxd4) 4... Bc5 5. O-O d6 6. h3 Be6 7. b3 Bxc4 8.
bxc4 Nxf3+ 9. Qxf3 Qf6 {Black was playing very quickly and quite plainly for a
draw.} 10. Qb3 Rb8 11. Nc3 Ne7 12. Na4 O-O 13. Bb2 Nc6 14. Nxc5 {[22']} dxc5 {
[10']} 15. f4 Nd4 16. Bxd4 cxd4 17. fxe5 Qxe5 18. d3 g6 19. Rf3 {[41']} c5 {
[14']} 20. Qa4 {[42']} a6 {[15']} 21. Qd7 Qe6 22. Qc7 Qc8 ({Not} 22... Qc6 $2
23. Rxf7 $1) 23. Qe7 b6 24. Raf1 Rb7 25. Qf6 Qd7 26. Rb1 Qe6 27. Qg5 {[65']} f6
{[28']} 28. Qc1 {[69']} a5 29. Qf4 Qe5 30. Qg4 Kh8 31. Rbf1 {Threatening32.Rxf6
} Rbf7 32. h4 {I was getting a bit frustrated. Black is hoping only for a draw
and will do nothing, so I have to create some play. I was also well behind on
time and started to play quickly.} a4 33. Qh3 h5 34. g4 Qe6 35. Rf4 Kh7 36. Qg2
b5 $2 {At last a mistake.} 37. cxb5 Qxa2 38. gxh5 gxh5 39. Rf5 $4 {Horrendous.
I was playing very quickly and simply overlooked his reply. I should have
slowed up when I realised I was winning.} Rg7 {What to do? I decided to rush
on as i felt he could easily go wrong.} 40. Rxh5+ Kg8 41. Rg5 fxg5 42. Rxf8+
Kxf8 43. h5 {I carried on at breakneck speed. My opponent, with bags of time,
did likewise!} Qb1+ 44. Kh2 Qxb5 45. h6 Qb8+ 46. Kh1 Rh7 47. Qxg5 {Obviously a
fairly critical position but he replied quickly.} Qc7 48. Qf6+ Qf7 {Still
playing quickly.} ({Easiest is} 48... Rf7 49. Qh8+ Ke7 50. h7 {what else?} Qg3)
49. Qd8+ Qe8 50. Qf6+ Rf7 51. Qh8+ Ke7 52. Qe5+ Kd8 53. Qb8+ Kd7 (53... Ke7 {
-3.24/0} 54. Qe5+ Kd7 55. Qd5+ Kc7 56. Qxc5+ Kb7 57. Qd5+ Kb8 58. Qd6+ Rc7 59.
Qb6+ Rb7 60. Qd6+ Kc8 61. Kg2 a3 62. Qa6 Qe7 63. Qa8+ Kc7 64. h7 Qxh7 65. Qa5+
Kd7 66. Qxa3 Qg6+ 67. Kf2 Rc7 68. Qb3 Ke7 69. Qb2 Qd6 70. Kf3 Qc5 71. Qb8 Qxc2
72. Kf4 Qh2+ {ect Examined by Dick & Fritz}) 54. Qb7+ (54. Qb7+ {after} Kd6 55.
Qd5+ Kc7 56. Qxc5+ Kb8 57. Qb6+ Ka8 58. Qa6+ Ra7 {59.Resigns}) 54... Kd8 {
He now said "It's drawn isn't it?" and stretched out his hand: so DRAWN! He
got his draw! A terrible game.} 1/2-1/2

