{Time limit 42 moves in 1hr 45' then 15' to finish.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5. Be3 Qb6 6. b3 ({During the lunch break I had played this
line in a quick game against Ian Wells (who was on the next board to me during
this round) Ian had played} 6. Nc3 {and I had ventured} Qxb2 $5 {I got
annihilated after} ({I suggested} 6... a6 {Ian suggested} 7. Na4 {but after}
Qa5+ 8. c3 ({maybe he has to play} 8. Nc3) 8... Be7 9. Bd3 b5 {He loses a piece
}) 7. Ncb5) 6... Nc6 7. c3 Nge7 8. Be2 ({Stan Foulkes played} 8. Nc2 {against
me earlier this year, which seems to be better.}) 8... d5 9. Bf3 e5 10. Nxc6 $2
{Unsound. I suspect that he didn't see either my 12th or 13th move.} ({I
expected} 10. Nc2 {when I intended} dxe4 11. Bxe4 f5) 10... Bxe3 11. O-O bxc6 (
11... Bxf2+ 12. Rxf2 bxc6 13. exd5 {is O.K. for White}) 12. fxe3 dxe4 13. Be2
Nd5 $1 ({After} 13... Qxe3+ 14. Kh1 {Black has 2 extra but doubled Pawns and a
very loose position. After the text move White is really in trouble.}) 14. Qc1
{[40']} Nxe3 {[21']} 15. Rf2 Bg4 16. Bc4 {There is rather a lack of good moves.
Maybe best is............} ({...........} 16. Bf1 {but then} Rd8 {is very
strong.}) 16... Nxc4 (16... Nd1 17. Bxf7+ Ke7 {White has no good move}) 17.
bxc4 Rd8 {White could resign.} 18. Nd2 {Finishing things a bit quicker than....
..} (18. Na3 e3 19. Rb2 Rd1+ 20. Qxd1 Qxb2 21. Qc1 Qf2+ 22. Kh1 O-O {etc.})
18... e3 19. Qe1 exf2+ {Short and sweet!} 0-1

