{Time limit 42 moves in 1hr 45' then 15' to finish.} 1. e4 d6 {An experiment
for me.} 2. d4 g6 3. Be3 Bg7 4. c4 c5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Qd2 Nf6 7. Nc3 {I suddenly
realised I'd got myself into the Black side of a Maroczy bind v Dragon, which
I wasn't happy about.} cxd4 8. Nxd4 Ng4 9. Nxc6 bxc6 10. Bg5 ({I was expecting.
} 10. Bd4) 10... Qa5 11. h3 Ne5 12. f4 Nd7 13. Be2 Rb8 14. Rd1 $4 {Threatening
15.Bxe7, a vision that makes him overlook my threat. He was clearly very
muddled as he explained that he had intended 15.Bxe7 but overlooks the fact
that after 15.....KxB 16.Qxd6+ Ke8 my Queen's Rook is defended no doubt he
casually intended. 16.Nd5+} (14. O-O Qb6+ 15. Kh1 Qxb2) (14. Rd1 $4 Z0 15. Bxe7
Kxe7 16. Qxd6+ Ke8) 14... Rxb2 {Instant collapse. Quite a success for my first
Pirc Defense. R.Tomlinson won the 130-160 grading prize with 4/5} 0-1

