{Time limit 42 moves in 1hr 45' then 15' to finish.} 1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. Nc3
Nxc3 4. bxc3 d5 5. d4 Bf5 6. Ba3 e6 7. Bxf8 Kxf8 8. g4 $5 {Pushing too hard.}
Bg6 ({Rather better seems} 8... Be4 9. Nf3 (9. f3 {is answered by} Qh4+)) 9. h4
h5 10. g5 {[11']} Bf5 {[30']} 11. Bh3 Bxh3 12. Nxh3 g6 13. Nf4 Kg7 14. Qd3 Qe7
15. O-O Nd7 16. c4 {[30']} c6 {[51']} 17. cxd5 cxd5 18. c4 dxc4 19. Qxc4 Nb6
20. Qb3 Rhd8 21. Rfd1 Nd5 22. Nd3 Rdc8 23. Rac1 b6 24. Nb2 {[42']} Rc7 {[64']}
25. Rxc7 Qxc7 26. Nc4 Qb7 27. Nd6 Qa6 $2 {Laving f7 weak.} 28. Qf3 Rf8 29. Rc1
$2 {Too impetuous again, trying to rush it. Black gets enough play to draw now.
} ({Best seems} 29. a3 $1 {and then Rc1 Black defends by} Qa4 30. Rc1 Qd7 {
but at least White can keep trying.}) 29... Qxa2 30. Rc8 Qb1+ {Correct
allowing the Queen to retreat to e4 or f5.} 31. Kg2 {is g2 any better?} Rxc8
32. Qxf7+ Kh8 33. Nxc8 Qe4+ {Here he offered a draw which I accepted. After
this round Dave Everett & Ian Wells had 4/5 and 8 of us had 3/5.} 1/2-1/2

