{Time limit 42 moves in 1hr 45' then 15' to finish.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 {I beat him with this line a couple of years ago.} e5 6.
Nb3 Be7 (6... d5 $142) 7. c4 O-O 8. Be3 Be6 9. Nc3 Nbd7 10. Nc1 Rc8 11. b3 Qa5
12. Qd2 b5 $2 {Apparently a complete oversight. I can't take with the Pawn,
but it didn't occur to him that I could take with the Knight!} 13. Nxb5 Qxd2+
14. Bxd2 a6 15. Nc3 Bd8 16. Bd3 Bb6 17. N1e2 {[16']} Ne8 {[30']} 18. Rd1 {
Starting to eye his d-Pawn.} Nc7 19. Ng3 g6 20. Bb1 {[31']} Kg7 {[40'] I
threatened 21.Bh6} 21. Na4 Ba7 22. h3 {With thoughts of f4.} ({Neither} 22. Bb4
) ({or} 22. Ba5 {quite work.}) 22... Rfd8 23. Ke2 {[50']} Nc5 {[52']} 24. Nc3
f6 25. Be3 Bb8 26. Kf2 {[52']} Ne8 {[66']} 27. Rd2 Kf8 28. Rhd1 Ke7 29. Nge2 {
Slowly rearranging. I intended something like Nc1 followed by BxN excahnge
Rooks and Nd3 & Na4 winning his c-Pawn. Black tries to create some play.} f5 $2
{Overlooking the loss of a Pawn.} 30. Bg5+ Nf6 31. exf5 gxf5 32. Bxf5 Bxf5 33.
Nd5+ Ke6 34. Bxf6 Rf8 35. Bg5 $5 Bxh3 {[1hr 14']} 36. Kg1 {[1hr 10']} Rg8 $2 (
36... Bf5 $142) 37. Nef4+ exf4 38. Nxf4+ {[1hr 16']} Kd7 (38... Kf5 $4 39. Rd5#
) 39. Nxh3 Rg6 40. Bf4 Rcg8 41. b4 Na4 42. c5 {[1hr 18']} Nc3 {[1hr 26']
Fifteen minutes were now added to the time remaining for the rest of the game.}
43. Rc1 Na4 (43... Rxg2+ {is no good}) 44. Rc4 Rc8 45. Rcd4 Rc6 46. R4d3 {
Threatening 47.Ra3 winning the Knight.} Nxc5 47. bxc5 Rxc5 48. Rb2 Ba7 49. Kf1
Kc6 {Putting a quick end to it.} 50. Be3 {I now had to wait for the S.O.S. to
be calculated to see if I'd got 3rd prize-I had. Results 1st Dave Everett 4.5
£50 2nd I.D.Wells 4.5 ----£30 3rd R.A.C. 4----------£20 45 competed A fair
tournament and my second £20 prize in a few weeks.} 1-0

