bxc6 6. d4 exd4 7. Nxd4 c5 8. Nf3 ({Against P.Dickinson recently I played} 8.
Ne2) 8... g6 {A bit of a nuisance this.} 9. Bd2 Bg7 10. Bc3 f6 11. O-O {[25']}
Ne7 {[11']} 12. Re1 O-O 13. b3 {[36']} Bb7 {[17'] My e-Pawn is weak. I felt
uneasy about my position and started to use a lot of time.} 14. Nbd2 Qd7 15.
Bb2 Rae8 16. c4 Nc6 {[23']} 17. Nf1 {[57']} Nd8 18. Qc2 $2 {[62'] Loses,
initially the e-Pawn, and then the game. I should have noticed the strength of
his reply.} (18. Ng3 $142) 18... f5 $1 {I saw the problem now.} 19. Bxg7 {
[1hr 16']} (19. exf5 {is a shambles.}) 19... Qxg7 {[41']} 20. Rad1 {[1hr 22']}
({If} 20. Ng3 {(or g5 or d2)} fxe4 21. Nxe4 Bxe4 22. Rxe4 Rxe4 23. Qxe4 Qxa1+)
20... fxe4 {Now my position collapses.} 21. N3d2 Qf7 22. Nb1 Ne6 23. Nc3 {
[1hr 37']} Nd4 24. Qd2 Re5 25. Ng3 Rfe8 26. Rc1 Qd7 {[54']} 27. Kh1 {[1hr 49']}
Qg4 28. Nd1 Nf5 29. Nxf5 gxf5 30. Ne3 {[1hr 55']} Qg5 31. g3 {[1hr 58']} R8e6 {
[68']} 32. Kg1 f4 33. Ng2 e3 34. fxe3 fxg3 35. Nf4 gxh2+ {White lost on time.
Colin Crouch had a FIDE rating of 2330 and was a Candidate Expert (CX)} 0-1

