d4 d5 {[5']} 5. Bb5 {[37']} a6 $5 {[12'] Doubtful.} ({P.B.Cook played} 5...
exd4 {against me a few years ago.}) 6. Bxc6+ bxc6 7. Nxe5 Nxe4 {[13']} 8. O-O {
[44']} ({Naturally not} 8. Nxc6 $4 Qf6) ({However, I was worried about} 8. Qf3
{e.g.} Be6 9. Nxc6) 8... Bd7 {[21']} 9. f3 Nd6 10. Re1 {[58']} Be7 {[25']} 11.
Qe2 Nc8 {Black's position is quite solid and White runs outof ideas.} 12. Bg5 {
[1hr 10']} f6 {[31']} 13. Nxd7 Qxd7 14. Bf4 Kf7 15. Nd2 c5 16. dxc5 Bxc5+ 17.
Kh1 Bd6 18. Bxd6 Nxd6 19. Qd3 {Tying down both Rooks.} Qb5 20. Qxb5 $2 {
[1hr 25'] leaving Black the betterendgame. Better seems.....} (20. Qd4 Nf5 21.
Qf4) 20... axb5 {[41']} 21. Nb3 Rhe8 22. a3 {Black threatened to exchange
Rooks and win the a-Pawn or if.......} (22. Nd4 Rxa2 $1) 22... Nc4 {[58']} 23.
Nd4 Rxe1+ 24. Rxe1 Nxb2 25. Nxb5 c6 26. Nd6+ {[1hr 46']} Kg6 {[67']} 27. Ra1
Na4 28. c4 d4 29. Kg1 Rb8 30. Rd1 {[1hr 50'] White was getting short of time.}
Nc3 {[1hr 18']} 31. Ra1 f5 ({If} 31... d3 32. Ne4) 32. c5 d3 33. Nc4 Na4 $4 {
Rubbish! He had only a short time left so, very foolishly, I tried to rush him,
and blundered myself.} 34. Ne5+ Kg5 35. Nxd3 Rb3 36. Nb4 Nxc5 37. Nxc6 Na4 38.
Nd4 Rb2 39. Kf1 Kf6 40. Ne2 g5 {Here the match ended and he offered a draw.
Accepted! [J.F.Turnock CX]} 1/2-1/2

