{Time liimit 20mph [I had a bye in Rd1]} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 Qxd5 4. Nc3
Qd8 5. Bc4 e6 6. Be3 {I was half asleep when this game was played and maybe
this move is not precise. The Bishop may be more useful elsewhere} Nf6 7. a3
Nbd7 8. Nf3 Nb6 {[7']} 9. Bb3 {[6']} Nbd5 10. O-O Bd6 11. Bg5 h6 {[11']} 12.
Bh4 {[10']} g5 {[18'] Rather weakening.} 13. Bg3 {[10']} Bxg3 14. fxg3 $6 {
Simply playing too quickly. I had my usual "lack of motivation" problem with
an opponent who I had scores 100% over the last decade. The move may not, in
fact, be too bad as Black is left with a rotten position in return for the
exchange.} Ne3 15. Qe2 Nxf1 {[21']} 16. Rxf1 {[14'] I decided to play a bit
more slowly now.} O-O 17. Qe5 (17. Nxg5 hxg5 (17... Qxd4+) 18. Qe5 {etc might
be worth trying for.}) 17... Nd7 18. Qe3 {[17']} Nf6 19. Ne5 Nd5 20. Qe4 f5 21.
Qd3 Kg7 22. Ne2 Nf6 23. c3 Qd6 {[43']} 24. Bc2 {[38']} Bd7 {[45'] I got the
impression that he didn't really know what to do around here.} 25. g4 Ne4 26.
Qe3 Qd5 27. c4 Qd6 28. c5 Qe7 (28... Qd5 $4 29. Bb3) 29. Rf3 {[42']} Rad8 {
[56']} 30. h4 Bc8 ({If} 30... gxh4 31. Nf4) 31. h5 Rf6 32. Ng6 Qf7 33. Ne5 Qe7
34. Ng6 Qf7 35. Ne5 {Here he asked me if I was repeating moves. I said I was.
Drawn. Rubbish! The first time that I've dropped half a point against KL.}
1/2-1/2

