{Time limit 20/hr} 1. d4 Nf6 2. e3 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. b3 O-O 5. Bb2 d6 6. Nbd2 a5
7. a3 Nbd7 8. c4 Nh5 9. Bd3 {[5']} (9. Be2 $142) 9... c5 {[7']} 10. Ng5 $5 {
It is typical of KL that he goes for minor tactical threats, in this case 11.
Nxh7. It is much sounder to castle.} e5 {Gaining the initiative and winning a
Pawn.} 11. Nge4 ({After} 11. Nxh7 Re8 {his Knight is stuck.}) ({If} 11. Ngf3
exd4 {and he can hardly open up the e-file.}) 11... exd4 12. O-O {[15']} Ne5
13. Be2 dxe3 14. fxe3 {Better than.....} ({.....} 14. Bxe5 exd2) 14... Nf6 15.
Nxf6+ Bxf6 16. Ne4 Nf3+ 17. Bxf3 Bxb2 18. Rb1 Be5 19. Qd5 {[30'] I didn't see
the point of this.} Qe7 {[29']} 20. Rbd1 Be6 21. Qd3 Rad8 22. Nf2 Bf5 23. e4
Bc8 24. Be2 Bb2 {Hoping to force 2.a4 fixing the QS. It's bluff really as I
wouldn't be very likely to take the Bishop off it's good diagonal.} 25. Bg4 f5
26. exf5 Bxf5 27. Bxf5 Rxf5 28. Ng4 Bd4+ 29. Kh1 Rxf1+ 30. Rxf1 {[49']} Rf8 {
[46']} 31. Rxf8+ Qxf8 {All of the exchanges have left White a Pawn down with a
bad position. The Bishop is much better than the Knight and he is vulnerable
on the back rank. For some reason he didn't seem to realise what problems he
had and blunders in his attempt to exchange further.} 32. Qf3 $4 {Loses
outright.} Qe7 {Kl now let out a big sigh and announced to all that I'd missed.
......} ({.......} 32... Qxf3 33. gxf3 h5 {winning the knight. However he
slowly realised that he is lost anyway. The Knight is still stuck. He tries to
rescue it.}) 33. h3 {A quicker way to lose than.....} ({........} 33. Qf1 h5
34. Nf2 Qf6 35. Kg1 Qf4 36. Z0 Qe3 37. Z0 Qxb3 {etc.}) 33... Qe1+ 34. Kh2 Bg1+
0-1

