{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 per 15'} 1. d4 e6 2. c4 b6 3. e4 Bb7 4.
Bd3 f5 $5 5. exf5 {Played by Browne v Miles. I had seen the game some time ago
but had forgotten about it.} Bb4+ 6. Kf1 Nf6 7. fxe6 dxe6 8. a3 Be7 9. Nf3 Nc6
(9... O-O $142) 10. Nc3 O-O {[15']} 11. Bg5 {[30']} h6 {[16']} 12. h4 {[32']
Rather a surprise. I now had a long think.} Qe8 {[30'] Taking the Bishop must
lose. The text threatens ......PxB, ....Qh5, ....Rd8} 13. Qe2 {[39']} Qd7 {
[36'] I can't see anything better although I'm sure that I should now be lost.}
14. Bxf6 $2 {[52'] After a long think.} (14. d5 $1 {which I expected , puts me
in terrible trouble.}) 14... Bxf6 {[37']} 15. Qe4 {[54'] Now I can equalise.}
Nxd4 {[44']} 16. Qxb7 Nxf3 17. Qxf3 Bxc3 18. Qe4 Bd4 {He declined the offer of
a draw here.} 19. Qh7+ Kf7 {[51']} 20. Re1 {[61']} Ke7 {He hadn't realised
that I could play this.} 21. Re2 ({If} 21. Bf5 {then either} Rxf5 ({or} 21...
Be5 22. Rxe5 Rxf5) 22. Qxf5 Rf8) 21... Qd6 22. Qg6 {[1hr 10']} Rf7 {[52']} 23.
h5 Raf8 {I suddenly felt that I was on top, especially as White had little
time left.} 24. f3 Qc6 $5 {Getting a bit carried away with ideas of 25.......
Rxf3+} 25. Rh4 Rxf3+ $5 {Rushing on as he had little time left. This may just
be sound but leaves me with a very difficult game.} 26. gxf3 Qxf3+ 27. Ke1 Bf2+
28. Kd2 Bxh4 29. Qxe6+ Kd8 30. Re4 Bg5+ {I suddenly found that I was in
trouble.} 31. Kc2 {Time ticked on and suddenly I'm in time trouble. Hence......
....} c5 $2 ({I had originally intended} 31... Qf2+ 32. Kb3 Qc5 {but after} 33.
Re5 {I'm stuck.}) (31... Qf6 {is best}) 32. Qd6+ {Getting carried away with 
(unsound) enthusiasm; also trying to rush my opponent - as usual, rebounding.}
1-0

