{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3
a6 6. c4 Qc7 7. Be3 e6 8. Nc3 {[5']} Nc6 {[5']} 9. Qd2 Bd7 10. Be2 {[6']} Rc8
11. Rc1 ({Threat} 11. Z0 Na5 12. b3 b5) 11... Be7 12. O-O {[8']} O-O {[10']}
13. Rfd1 Rfd8 (13... Qb8 $142) 14. Nd5 {Making life interesting} ({If} 14. Ncb5
{then he can play} Qb8) 14... exd5 15. cxd5 Nxd4 ({If} 15... Qa5 16. Nxc6 {
leaves me a Pawn up.} (16. dxc6 {his a-Pawn goes.}) (16. Qxa5 Nxa5 17. b4)) 16.
Rxc7 Nxe2+ 17. Qxe2 Rxc7 18. Bb6 Rcc8 19. Bxd8 Bxd8 {The smoke clears I have
Q+P for BBN} 20. Qd2 {Black apparently decided that this was to allow 21.Rc1,
but he missed the other threat.} Be8 $2 {This probably loses the game as I now
win 2 Pawns. he was expecting 21.Rc1 Ba5} 21. Qb4 (21. Rc1 Ba5) 21... Rc5 {
If the d-Pawn goes he's in trouble.} 22. Qxb7 Rb5 23. Qxa6 Bb6+ 24. Kh1 {
He now had a very long think.} Bc5 {[66'] Hanging onto the d-Pawn at the
expense of leaving two united passed Pawns.} ({When playing 21.....Rc5 he
probably intended} 24... Rxb2 {but} 25. Qa3 {wins the d-Pawn}) 25. b3 {[44']}
Bd7 26. g4 {Putting the squeeze on and giving my King a bit of room.} h6 27.
Qa8+ Kh7 28. h4 {With possibilities of opening the h-file for my Rook.} Rb4 {
He said he'd been getting desperate here. A sacrifice was obviously coming.}
29. Qd8 Nxe4 30. fxe4 Bxg4 31. Rc1 $1 Bf3+ 32. Kh2 Rxe4 (32... Bxe4 33. Rc4)
33. Rxc5 $1 dxc5 34. Kg3 Bg4 35. d6 Rd4 (35... c4 $142) 36. Qc7 Be6 37. a4 c4
38. bxc4 {A pleasing win. I've not played with Q v BBN in a serious game
before.} 1-0

