{Time limit 20mph} 1. d4 b6 2. e4 Bb7 3. Nd2 e6 4. Ngf3 c5 5. c3 cxd4 6. cxd4
Bb4 7. Bd3 Nf6 8. O-O Nc6 {I was a little unhappy with the opening.} 9. Re1 Be7
{I didn't fancy castling, the Bishop is out on a limb and the e-file could
open.} 10. a3 d6 11. b4 Rc8 12. Bb2 Kf8 {Looks rather odd, but it removes the
King form the e-file and the a4-e8 diagonal and protects the g-Pawn.} 13. Rc1 {
[17']} d5 {[35'] I felt that I had to do something positive.} 14. e5 Nh5 15.
Rc3 {Probably better is 15.g3 preventing .....Nf4. White has no need to rush
his c-file build up.} Nf4 16. Qc2 {Played instantaneously.} g5 {Trying for KS
play ......g4 is threatened also the King can go to g7 to get the Rook into
play.} 17. Rc1 {[34']} Kg7 {[56'] getting short of time, also I had a sudden
fear that the time limit was 24 rather than 20mph.} 18. Nf1 {[50'] after 16'
thought and rather a surprise.} ({I was expecting} 18. b5 Na5 19. Rxc8 Qxc8 20.
Qxc8 Rxc8 21. Rxc8 Bxc8 22. Bc2 {but this is rather oversimplifying.}) 18...
Qd7 $4 {Short of time, and unsure of how many moves I had to play I blunder
horribly. I realised imediatly.} 19. Bb5 {White was also short of time but
this is easy to find.} g4 20. Bxc6 $4 {White's time shortage saves me; He
plays the moves in the wrong order.} ({After} 20. Ne1 {Black has no move e.g.}
a6 21. Bxc6 Bxc6 22. Rxc6 Ne2+ 23. Qxe2 Rxc6 24. Qxg4+ {etc}) 20... Bxc6 21.
Ne1 {[68']} ({and not} 21. Rxc6 $4 Ne2+ 22. Qxe2 gxf3) 21... Ba4 22. Qd2 Bg5
23. Ne3 h5 24. Nd3 Rxc3 25. Rxc3 Rc8 ({Maybe} 25... Nxd3 {offers more}) 26.
Nxf4 {Again played instantaneously} Bxf4 27. Nf5+ exf5 28. Qxf4 {1 When
playing 24.........Rxc3 I had intended 28.....Kg6. However I now realised that
29.Bc1 threatens mate in} Rxc3 29. Bxc3 $2 {Again instantaneous} (29. Qg5+ {
seems to offer more}) 29... Qc6 30. Bd2 Qg6 31. Qe3 Bb5 {I felt that the game
may now be drawn but that such chances as they were were mine. Apparently
White felt that he stood better and that I had no chances (a fact demonstarted
to be untrue)} 32. Qc3 {I don't think that White can risk QS sorties} h4 33.
Qe3 h3 {Hoping to create something.} 34. g3 {I don't like this, better seems
to be..................} (34. gxh3 gxh3+ 35. Qg3) 34... Kf8 {Improving my
King's position (heading for the QS should the Queens come off) and getting
out of the firing line.} 35. f3 {White was getting short of time again.} Ke8
36. Kf2 f4 $6 {With White short of time I decided to force it. Fortunately he
had to move quickly and...} 37. Qxf4 $4 ({I wasn't sure what I'd do after} 37.
gxf4 {e.g.} g3+ ({or} 37... gxf3 38. Qxf3 Qb1 {say}) ({or} 37... Qb1)) 37...
Qd3 {I though that I would win on time but he managed.....} 38. fxg4 Qf1+ {
.....before his flag fell. Rather a flawed masterpiece governed by the clock. 
[The game was played at Bare]} 0-1

