{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 per 15'} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 d6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4.
Nc3 Nf6 5. Be2 O-O 6. O-O {[1']} Bg4 {Probably better than 6.......Nbd7 which
I played last week.} 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Bxf3 Nc6 9. Be3 e5 {[6']} 10. d5 {[6']} Ne7
{[6']} 11. g4 {[9'] A bit loosening but intending to prevent .....f5 e.g.11....
.Nd7 12.g5 He now had a long think.} c6 {[28']} (11... Nd7 12. g5) 12. g5 Ne8
13. Bg4 {[11'] I was managing to play fairly quickly, as after the last game,
I felt that it was important not to get in time trouble at 6 per 15'} Nc7 {
[35']} 14. Qd2 {[17']} c5 {[43']} 15. a4 {[18']} f6 {[52']} 16. gxf6 Bxf6 17.
Bh6 {[20']} Bg7 18. Bxg7 Kxg7 {[52']} 19. f4 exf4 {[56']} 20. Rxf4 Ng8 21. Raf1
Qe7 {[60']} 22. Nb5 {[35'] So as to remove his Knight covering e6, also
possibly to get a check on c3.} Nxb5 23. axb5 Rxf4 {Black was getting short of
time.} 24. Rxf4 Rf8 ({Not} 24... Qg5 $4 25. Rf7+ Kh6 26. Rxh7+) 25. Qc3+ {[38']
} Kh6 {Played almost immediately.} ({I had expected} 25... Nf6 26. Be6 Z0 {
followed by} 27. e5) 26. Rxf8 Qxf8 27. Qe3+ ({I considered also} 27. Qd2+ Kg7
28. e5 dxe5 29. d6 Nf6 30. d7 Qd8 31. Be6 {etc}) 27... Kg7 28. e5 dxe5 29.
Qxe5+ Qf6 30. Qc7+ Kh6 31. Qxc5 {[51']} Qxb2 {[1hr 24']} 32. Qf8+ Kg5 {Black
decides to sacrifice a piece for a perpetual in view of.......} ({..........} 
32... Qg7 33. Qf4+ g5 {etc}) 33. Qxg8 Qc1+ 34. Kf2 Qd2+ 35. Kf3 Qf4+ 36. Ke2
Qe4+ 37. Kd2 Qd4+ 38. Ke1 Qe3+ 39. Kf1 Qc1+ ({Easier is} 39... Qf4+) 40. Ke2
Qxc2+ 41. Ke3 Qc3+ 42. Ke4 Qe1+ 43. Kd4 Qf2+ 44. Ke4 Qe1+ 45. Kd3 Qf1+ 46. Kd4
Qf2+ {Lancaster won the match. My play was a little sounder of late.} 1/2-1/2

