{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 {[1']} 4. d4 exd4 {
[9'] I was quite pleased he spent a while thinking about this.} 5. e5 Ne4 6.
cxd4 ({Jaenisch recommended} 6. Qc2 Nc5 7. cxd4) ({Hardings book prefers.} 6.
Qe2) 6... Bb4+ 7. Bd2 ({Janetschek v Bukenstrom Leipzig 1960 preffered} 7. Nbd2
) 7... Nxd2 8. Nbxd2 O-O {[14']} 9. a3 {[8']} Bxd2+ 10. Qxd2 {[8']} d6 {
I decided at this stage that I hadn't played the best line. It will take 2
moves to get the King off the e-file and the e-Pawn is a bit weak.} 11. Bb5 {
[19'] I wasn't very happy with this and was expecting something like 11.......
Bd7} dxe5 {[29']} (11... Bd7 12. Bxc6 Bxc6 13. d5 Bb5 14. Nd4 (14. O-O-O) 14...
Ba6 15. e6 {may have put Blackoff this line.}) 12. Bxc6 {[27']} bxc6 {[29']}
13. dxe5 Bg4 14. Qc3 Qd5 15. O-O ({If} 15. Rd1 Qe4+) 15... Rad8 16. Rac1 Rfe8 {
[46']} 17. Rfe1 {[55'] I was fairly happy with the position now.} h6 {Giving
up a Pawn, although it was awkward to defend it. Black obviously expects that
the disruption of my KS will compensate.} 18. Qxc6 Bxf3 19. gxf3 Qd2 {I
suspect that he missed my next move.} 20. Rcd1 Qg5+ {Black still hoped to win.}
(20... Qxd1 21. Qxe8+ {seems drawn}) 21. Kf1 {I didn't want to get caught in
the corner.} Qf4 {Probably best.} 22. Rxd8 {Deciding to accept another Pawn.} (
{I also considered} 22. e6) 22... Rxd8 {[61']} 23. Qxc7 {[1hr 25']} Re8 24. Qc6
Rb8 ({If} 24... Rxe5 25. Rxe5 Qxe5 26. Qa8+ Kh7 27. Qe4+ $18) 25. e6 fxe6 ({If
} 25... Rxb2 26. e7) 26. Qxe6+ Kh8 {[1hr 11']} 27. Qg6 {[1hr 40'] He offered a
draw here which I declined. This move surprised him.} ({I had originally
intended} 27. Qe5 {but 27.Qg6 is much stronger.}) 27... Qa4 $2 {Flustered
possibly , by my refusal of the draw he goes wrong.} ({Correct is} 27... Qxf3 {
which draws, but he was worried about} 28. Re8+ Rxe8 29. Qxe8+ {etc However my
King can't hide as in the actual game . Now he's lost.}) 28. Re7 Rg8 ({If} 
28... Qd4 29. Re8+ Rxe8 30. Qxe8+ Kh7 31. Qe4+ $18) 29. Kg2 a5 30. Qe4 {
[1hr 47'] Apart from a mild time shortage I was fairly confident.} Qb5 31. Qe5
{Preventing the check on the g-file, keeping g7 under attack and defending the
b-Pawn.} Qd3 32. Re6 $1 {Covering g6 and threatening mate. hence the b-Pawn is
mobilised.} Qd2 33. b4 {Pretty decisive.} axb4 34. axb4 {[1hr 50']} Kh7 {
To activate the Rook.} 35. b5 Rf8 36. Qe3 $1 {[1hr 54'] Awkward fpr Black as
the Queen can't go to c2, b4, or d5 and has to take up a passive position on
d7.} Qd7 37. Qe4+ Kg8 38. b6 Rb8 39. Qc4 $1 {Finding the best moves even
though short of time.} Qf7 40. Qc7 {Decides it. Black is completely lost but
rattled off a dozen moves at great speed. I took it rather more slowly.} Qxc7 (
{If} 40... Qxe6 41. Qxb8+ Kh7 42. b7 Qg6+ 43. Qg3) 41. bxc7 Rc8 {I could
simply have stopped now as adjudication was soon due, but felt that I should
continue.} 42. Rc6 Kf7 43. Kg3 Ke7 44. Kg4 Kd7 45. Rc2 g6 46. f4 Kd6 47. f5 h5+
48. Kg5 gxf5 49. Kxf5 Kd7 50. Kg5 Rg8+ 51. Kxh5 Kc8 {A major triumph! I felt
that I played very well. This was my 3rd county win in a row and I was the
only Cumbrian 1st team winner today.} 1-0

