1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. c3 {Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} Nf6 5.
O-O d6 {Allows White to push on the QS.} 6. a4 a5 7. d4 exd4 8. cxd4 Ba7 9. Nc3
Bg4 $5 {Allowing White to "mix it"} 10. Qb3 O-O 11. Qxb7 $5 {Rather risky but
I felt that I could take risks against this opponent.} Nb4 {Leaving my Queen a
bit short of squares.} 12. e5 {[11']} Bxf3 13. Qxf3 Nd7 14. exd6 Nc2 {Black
decides that he can mix it as well.} 15. dxc7 Qxc7 16. Bxf7+ {Making it
interesting.} Kh8 ({If} 16... Rxf7 17. Qxa8+ Rf8 18. Qd5+) 17. Nd5 Qc6 18. Qh5
{The threat is 19.Ne7 then 20.Ng6(or mate) Black thought very briefly but was
unable to restrain himself.} Nxa1 $2 {It had to be.} (18... Nf6 19. Nxf6 Qxf6
20. Bd5 {and then} Rad8 $4 (20... Nxa1 21. Bxa8 Rxa8 22. Bg5 Qxd4 {and now} 23.
Rxa1 $2 ({so} 23. Be3 Qxb2 24. Bxa7 {is good for White}) 23... Qxf2+ 24. Kh1
Rf8 25. h3 Bb8 {is good for Black}) 21. Be4 g6 22. Qxa5 Nxa1 23. Bg5 {etc}) 19.
Ne7 {The threat of 20.Ng6+ seals it} Rxf7 20. Nxc6 {On the way to the 1/4
final I beat H.F.White, A.J. Leigh and A.Hagthornthwaite} 1-0

