{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. d4 b6 2. e3 Bb7 3. Nf3 e6 4. b3 f5 5. Bb2
Nf6 6. Bd3 d6 7. Nbd2 Be7 8. Qe2 Nc6 9. a3 O-O 10. O-O a5 11. c4 g6 {As so
often in these evening league matches the game started off very fast. My
strategy, as usual v KL when I am Black, is to wait for him to "over-commit+/=
himself.} 12. e4 {Possibly his aRook should be developed first.} Nh5 13. Qe3
Bf6 14. Rab1 Re8 {Discouraging the opening of the e-file. Black may have
equalised certainly White now thought for a while and with an air of not being
able to fine anything better played...........} 15. e5 $5 {Relieving the
tension in the centre and allowing Black a lot of play.} dxe5 16. dxe5 Be7 17.
g3 g5 $1 {He was looking a bit dejected so I decided to pressure him.} 18. g4
$2 {Desperate measures} (18. h3 $2 Nxg3 $1) (18. Ne1 {Seems better}) 18... Nf4
({Not} 18... fxg4 $2 19. Qe4) 19. gxf5 ({If} 19. Bc2 Bc5 20. Qe1 fxg4 {wins a
piece.}) 19... Qxd3 20. f6 $5 {Possibly missing my reply.} Qf5 {2 Theratening
mate in} 21. Kh1 Bc5 22. Qe1 Rad8 23. Nxg5 {Assuming that I won't take it.
However...} (23. Z0 {Threatening} Rxd2 24. Qxd2 Nxe5 {etc}) 23... Qxg5 24. Rg1
Nxe5+ 25. Ne4 (25. Ne4 Ng4 26. f3 Bxe4 27. Qxe4 Nf2#) 25... Ng4 0-1

