{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 d6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. Nf3
Bg4 6. e5 $5 {No doubt premature, but in these evening games against an
opponent who one expects to beat easily, it is tempting to go in for early
tactical lines.} dxe5 7. Bxf7+ Kf8 8. dxe5 {After some thought. I couldn't
find anything better.} Qxd1+ 9. Nxd1 Bxf3 10. gxf3 Kxf7 11. exf6 exf6 12. Bf4
Re8+ 13. Ne3 {[14']} c6 {[24']} 14. O-O-O {[15']} b5 15. Rd3 a5 {[35']} 16.
Rhd1 {[20']} Ra7 17. a4 {[28']} Rae7 {[45']} 18. axb5 cxb5 19. Rd6 {[38']
Awkward for Black. The threat is 20.Rb6} Re6 $2 {Losing 1 or 2 Pawns.} 20. Rxe6
Kxe6 21. Rd6+ Kf7 22. Rb6 Nd7 23. Rb7 {[41'] A useful intermediate move
forcing the King onto the e-file.} Ke6 24. Rxb5 a4 25. Ra5 f5 26. Rxa4 Ne5 27.
Ra6+ Kf7 28. Ra7+ Kg8 29. b4 $2 {Trying to rush things. I overlooked his 30th
move.} Nxf3 30. Rb7 {Again doubtful. I intended 31.Rb8} Bc3 {[1hr 12'] very
awkward. He threatens 31......Ra8 forcing 32.Rb8+ then my b-Pawn goes.} 31. Kd1
g5 {[1hr 26']} 32. Rb8 Rxb8 33. Bxb8 Bxb4 34. Nxf5 Kf7 35. Ke2 Ng1+ 36. Kd3 Bc5
37. Nd4 Kg6 38. Kc4 Bxd4 $2 {Black now has a complete mental storm, forgetting
about my Bishop.} 39. Kxd4 Nf3+ 40. Kd5 Nxh2 $4 41. Bxh2 {I beat David Barr in
the Semi-Final.} 1-0

