{Time limit 50 moves in 2hrs 15'} 1. e4 b6 {[13']} 2. d4 {[2']} Bb7 3. Bd3 {
[4']} e6 {[14']} 4. c4 {[6']} Nc6 {[22']} ({If} 4... f5 5. exf5 {as in
Cunningham - Collins (L, M & D Lge 4/12/79) & Browne v Miles (Interpolis 78)})
5. Nf3 Nb4 {Is this worth the wasted tempi?} 6. O-O Ne7 {[30']} 7. Nc3 {[12']}
Nxd3 {[31']} 8. Qxd3 Ng6 {[36']} 9. Re1 {Preventing 9......d5} Bb4 10. Bd2 {
I wasn't sure about this.} O-O 11. d5 {[21'] Else he frees his game with 11....
..e5} e5 {[48']} 12. g3 {Depriving the Knight of squares but weakening the
white squares somewhat. I also considered...........} ({........} 12. h4) 12...
d6 {[51']} 13. a3 Bxc3 {[51']} 14. Qxc3 {[35'] I had thoughts of b4 & c5, but
now 14......f5 looks good for Black.} h6 {[1hr 12'] 21 mins thought to play
this; I was much more concerned about......} ({......} 14... f5) 15. g4 {
[38'] Preventing ......f5 is the first priority.} Bc8 {[1hr 22'] he was using
up a lot of time.} 16. h3 h5 {[1hr 25']} 17. Nh2 Qh4 {[1hr 40'] Another 15' on
this.} 18. Qf3 {[47']} Nf4 $5 {[1hr 44'] This doesn't turn out too well as I'm
able to pen the e-file by e5.} 19. Bxf4 exf4 20. Qxf4 Qxh3 21. Re3 Qh4 22. e5
$1 {[59'] Now I gain the initiative.} hxg4 {[1hr 51']} 23. exd6 cxd6 {[1hr 55']
Black now had 20 mins for 27 moves.} 24. Qxd6 {[61'] [1hr 56'] Black has to
move quickly and decides that his best chance is to attack.} f5 25. Rae1 f4 {
[1hr 57']} 26. Re8 Qf6 27. Rxf8+ {[1hr 14']} Qxf8 28. Qxf8+ Kxf8 29. Re4 g5 {
[1hr 58']} 30. Re5 g3 {[2hr 1']} 31. fxg3 fxg3 32. Nf1 g4 33. d6 {[1hr 25']
Possibly this is wrong as the Pawn is now weak but Black gets cramped.} Ba6 {
[2hr 5']} 34. Re4 {[1hr 25']} g2 {[2hr 10'] He now had mins for 16 moves.} 35.
Rf4+ ({Not} 35. Kxg2 $4 Bb7) 35... Ke8 36. Ne3 Kd7 37. Rf6 Rg8 {Either 37......
Re8 or 37......Rh8 are better, but he was moving very fast now. I would
probably have replied with 38.Nf5} (37... Re8 38. Nf5) (37... Rh8 38. Nf5) 38.
b4 Rg5 {Black was rapidly running out of time. This move prevents 39.c5} 39.
Kxg2 {Simplest.} g3 40. Rf7+ Kxd6 41. Rxa7 Bc8 42. Rh7 ({Not} 42. Nf1 $2 Bh3+ {
with some chances.}) 42... Bd7 43. Rh6+ Kc7 {he was moving like lightning now.}
44. Nd5+ Kd8 45. Rh8+ Be8 (45... Be8 46. Nf6 {[Time] Fritz gives} Ke7 (46...
Re5 47. Kxg3 Ke7 48. Nxe8 Re4 49. Rh4) 47. Nxe8 Rg4 48. Nc7 Rxc4 49. Nd5+ Ke6
50. Nxb6) 46. Nf6 {Black lost on time. It is remarkable that he should have
taken so long over some of his moves.} 1-0

