{Time limit 0 moves in 2hrs 15'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 d6 5.
Bxc6+ bxc6 6. d3 {Rather a passive line.} f5 7. exf5 Bxf5 8. O-O Nf6 9. Nbd2
Be7 10. b3 {Not a terribly good idea as the Bishop is misplaced on the long
diagonal. However, he was already in the position of being short of good moves.
} O-O 11. Bb2 Nd5 {I got the feeling about here that I was going to win.} 12.
Nc4 $2 {A wasted move} Bg4 13. Ncd2 Qd7 {I was in 2 minds whether to play this
line or 13.......Qe8. I felt that this move prevented 14.h3 However.....} 14.
h3 $2 {Just asking for it!} Bxh3 15. gxh3 Qxh3 {Threatening 16......Nf4 and
mate on g2.} 16. Nh2 Rf6 {It's possible that when playing 14.h3? he had
overlooked this obvious move, Counting only on 16.......Nf4 17.Qf3} 17. Kh1 Rh6
18. Ndf3 Rf8 {Winning back the piece.} 19. Bc1 Rh5 20. Rg1 Rxf3 21. Rg2 Nf4 22.
Bxf4 Rxf4 23. Qg1 Qf3 {Rather limiting his options.} 24. Qd1 Qxd1+ 25. Rxd1 {
[56']} Rfh4 {[40']} 26. Rd2 {Now I can exchange off into a simple endgame.} ({
but if} 26. Rdg1 Bg5 27. Z0 Bf4 {wins easily.}) 26... Bg5 27. Re2 Bf4 28. f3
Kf7 29. Kg1 Bxh2+ 30. Rxh2 Rxh2 31. Rxh2 Rxh2 32. Kxh2 Kf6 33. Kg3 Kf5 34. b4
c5 35. bxc5 dxc5 36. a3 g5 37. a4 h5 38. a5 h4+ 39. Kf2 Kf4 40. c3 h3 41. c4 h2
42. Kg2 h1=Q+ 43. Kxh1 Kxf3 {Fairly drastic punishment of a passive opening.}
0-1

