} 5. dxe5 {[17'] 12' thought, then the Queen swap. I guessed that this meant
that he would play for a draw as usual.} dxe5 {[5']} 6. Qxd8+ {[18']} Kxd8 {
[5']} 7. Nf3 {[20']} e4 {[15']} 8. Nd4 {[26']} c6 {[16']} 9. a3 a5 {[17']} 10.
Na4 {[35']} c5 {[24']} 11. Nb5 Ra6 12. b3 Bd7 13. Bb2 Kc8 14. Nac3 {[45']} Be7
15. Be2 {[45']} Nc6 {[44']} 16. O-O {[49']} Na7 {[46']} 17. Rac1 Kb8 18. Rfd1
Re6 19. Nd5 {[56'30s]} Nxd5 $2 {[57'] Short of time I go wrong.} ({Maybe} 19...
Ne8 {is best.}) 20. Nxa7 Kxa7 21. Rxd5 Bc8 22. Bxg7 Rg8 23. Bc3 Reg6 24. g3 b6
25. Rcd1 Kb8 26. Be5+ Ka8 27. Bh5 Rg5 28. Be2 Be6 29. R5d2 Rd8 30. f4 Rgg8 31.
Kf2 Rc8 32. Rg1 Rcd8 33. Rxd8+ Rxd8 34. Rd1 Rxd1 35. Bxd1 a4 36. Ke1 Kb7 37.
Kd2 axb3 38. Bxb3 b5 39. Kc2 Kb6 {Adjourned. I thought the game drawn and
hardly bothered to look at it.} 40. cxb5 {[Sealed Move] The game resumed on 8/
4/80} c4 41. Ba4 Bxa3 $2 (41... Ka5 $142 42. b6 Kxb6) 42. Bd4+ $1 Kb7 ({If} 
42... Bc5 43. Kc3 {Leaves Black a bit stuck.}) 43. Kc3 Be7 44. b6 Bd8 45. Bb5
Bxb6 46. Bxb6 Kxb6 47. Bxc4 Bxc4 $2 48. Kxc4 Kc6 49. Kd4 Kd6 50. h3 h5 51. h4 {
After 51.g4 it's drawn [RAC 1980] My 2nd ever loss in this competition. A
common problem after beating an opponent repeatedly year after year, it is
difficult to motivate oneself and play well - hence a sloppy game.} 1-0

