{Time limit 40' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 d3 5. Bxd3 Bc5
6. O-O d6 7. a4 a5 8. Na3 Bg4 9. Be2 Nf6 10. Qc2 h6 11. Nc4 O-O 12. Ne3 Bh5 13.
Nf5 Re8 14. Ng3 Bg6 15. Bd3 Qd7 16. Nh4 Ne5 17. Nxg6 Nxg6 18. Kh1 Ne5 19. Bd2
Qg4 $5 20. f3 Qh4 21. Be2 {[16']} Nh7 {[22']} 22. Nf5 Qd8 23. b4 Bb6 24. f4 Ng6
25. Bh5 Nh4 26. Nxh4 Qxh4 27. Bf3 {[23']} Qe7 {[25']} 28. Rae1 Qd7 29. b5 Rad8
30. c4 Nf6 31. Bc3 Qe6 32. Qd3 Nd7 33. Bb2 Kh8 34. Qc3 f6 35. Bh5 Rf8 36. Qg3
Nc5 {White spent a long time looking for a clear line and was now in some time
trouble. I had about 15' left.} 37. e5 {He has to do something definite.} dxe5
38. fxe5 f5 $1 {About the only move White now looked a bit frantic and with
very little time left tried:} 39. Rd1 $2 Rxd1 40. Bxd1 (40. Rxd1 Ne4 {etc.})
40... Ne4 {The remaining moves were played at lightning speed.} 41. Qf4 g5 42.
Qc1 Nf2+ 43. Rxf2 Bxf2 44. Bb3 Rd8 45. Qc2 Bc5 {His Flag fell a few seconds
later. In round 5 I blost a wild game against Prof.J.T.Farrand and in round 6
had an easy win (37 moves in 12') v P.Craven.} 0-1

