1. d4 f5 2. Nc3 g6 3. e4 fxe4 4. Nxe4 Bg7 5. Nf3 d6 6. Bd3 Nc6 7. c3 Bg4 8. h3
Bxf3 9. Qxf3 e5 $5 {I had decided to play it very sharply but this is going a
bit too far. In view of the limited time available and White's solid position
I open myself up to all sorts of cross-fire.} 10. Ng5 Qe7 $2 (10... Qf6 $142)
11. d5 {Not having played in a simul for about 15 years (on the receiving end)
I had forgotten how quickly the other player appears, requiring an instant
move. Later (too late) in this game I 'prepared' a reply quickly then thought
about it. In the present position I soon realised .......Nd8 is instantly
fatal, so ......Nb8 has to be played. I then started to considering 11......
Na5 12.b4 e5 etc. When he reappeared. Caught in mid thought I played..........}
Na5 $2 {The Knight must eventually be lost, not to mention problems on the KS.}
12. Bb5+ {At this point I decided that this would be the first game to finish.}
Kd8 13. Nf7+ Kc8 14. Nxh8 a6 15. Be2 Bxh8 16. b4 e4 {The Knight must go so I
will be a Rook adrift. However, anything can happen in a simul so I carried on.
} 17. Qg4+ Kb8 18. Bd2 Nf6 19. Qh4 Qe5 20. bxa5 Nxd5 21. O-O Ka7 22. c4 e3 23.
Bxe3+ Nxe3 24. fxe3 Qxe3+ 25. Qf2 Qxf2+ 26. Kxf2 Bd4+ 27. Kg3 Be5+ 28. Kf3 Bxa1
29. Rxa1 Rf8+ 30. Ke3 Rf5 31. Bd3 Rxa5 32. a4 c6 33. Kd2 b5 34. cxb5 cxb5 35.
Kc3 bxa4 36. Kb4 Rd5 37. Bc4 Rd4 $2 38. Kc3 Rf4 39. Rxa4 d5 40. Bb3 Rf5 41. Rd4
Kb6 42. Rxd5 Rf2 43. Rd2 Rf6 44. Bd5 Kc5 45. Bf3 a5 46. Rd5+ Kb6 47. Rd7 h6 48.
Rb7+ Ka6 49. Rb2 Rf4 50. Re2 Rf6 51. Re8 Ka7 52. Kd4 a4 $2 53. Ra8+ Kb6 54.
Rxa4 Rf4+ 55. Be4 g5 56. Ke3 Rf6 57. Rc4 h5 58. Rc2 g4 59. h4 Kb5 60. Rf2 Rh6
61. Rf5+ Kc4 62. Kf4 Kd4 63. Bb1 Rb6 64. Rxh5 Rxb1 65. Kxg4 Ke4 66. Rh8 Ke5 67.
Rf8 Rb4+ 68. Kg3 Rb3+ 69. Rf3 Rb2 70. h5 Rb4 71. Kh3 Rb6 72. Kh4 Rb2 73. g4 Rb4
74. h6 Rb1 75. Kg5 Rh1 76. Kg6 Rh4 77. g5 Rh1 78. h7 Rh2 79. Kg7 {2 RDK won 20
and drew} 1-0

