{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3
d6 6. Be2 g6 7. O-O Bg7 {[1']} 8. Be3 Bd7 {[8']} 9. f3 {[9']} Qb6 $6 {[28'] At
the time of this game I was contemplating giving up playing (lack of time &
enthusiasm). I didn't really want to play in this match and would have been
happy with a quick draw. However, Black has other ideas......this move loses.}
10. Nf5 {[32'] There isn't a great deal of choice if........} ({.........} 10.
Qd2 Nxe4 11. Na4 {isn't particularly good.}) 10... Qxb2 {[31']} 11. Nxg7+ {
[37']} Kf8 {[31']} 12. Qd2 $1 {[39']} (12. Bh6 Qxc3 {was what I initially
planned when looking at my options on move 10. The text leads to a won game.})
12... Kxg7 {[45']} 13. Bh6+ Kg8 14. Rfb1 Qa3 15. Rxb7 {With a Rook out of play,
his King stuck a White Rook on the 7th and White controlling the open file.
One feels that White should win!} Qc5+ 16. Kh1 {[46']} Be6 {[64'] Black has no
good move.} 17. Rab1 {[48']} Nd8 18. Rxe7 $1 {[61']} Rc8 {[77']} ({If} 18... d5
19. Nxd5 Bxd5 {Forced} 20. Qxd5 $1 Qxe7 (20... Qxd5) (20... Nxd5 21. Re8+ Qf8
22. Rxf8#)) 19. Qf4 {Threatening 20.QxN and since 19......QxN is no defence
Black has no move.} Bf5 (19... Z0 20. Qxf6 Qxc3 21. Qxc3 Rxc3 22. Re8#) 20. Nd5
{A good result. My first win on top board for the County. The match was played
at Lancaster Royal Grammar School.} 1-0

