{Time limit 4o moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 d3 5. Qxd3
d6 6. Be2 Nf6 {[2']} 7. O-O {[4']} Be7 {[11']} 8. Nd4 {[5']} d5 $2 {[19']
Possibly the major mistake. I felt that this would ensure equality but
probably it just opens up the position with my King still in the centre and
with White ahead in development.} 9. exd5 Nxd4 {[20']} 10. cxd4 {[9']} Nxd5 11.
Nc3 O-O 12. Bf3 Nb4 $5 13. Qd1 c6 14. a3 Na6 15. d5 cxd5 {[58']} 16. Nxd5 Bd6 {
[59']} 17. b4 {[47']} Nc7 {[65']} 18. Bb2 Rb8 19. Re1 {[58']} Ne6 {[1hr 19']}
20. Qd3 {[67']} Ng5 {[1hr 31']} 21. Rad1 {[1hr 14']} Nxf3+ {[1hr 38' 30s]} 22.
Qxf3 {[1hr 14']} Kh8 {[1hr 48'] Out of practice I was taking much too long.}
23. Nf6 {[1hr 20']} Qb6 {[1hr 54']} 24. Qh5 h6 25. Nd5 Qc6 26. Qxh6+ {Not
having looked a Chess Board for nearly 2 months, I was persuaded to play in
this. Not a particularly surprising result, therefore.} 1-0

