{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. f4 d5 4. fxe5 Nxe4 5.
Nf3 Bg4 ({MCO 11 gives} 5... Be7) 6. d4 Bb4 {White was already feeling
uncomfortable.} 7. Qd3 ({If} 7. Bd2 Nxd2 8. Qxd2 Bxf3 {etc.}) 7... Nc6 {
Threatening 8.......Bxf3 again.} 8. Be2 Bxf3 {Maybe not the best.} 9. Bxf3 O-O
10. Bf4 (10. Be3 {Strengthening the d-Pawn is better.}) 10... Kh8 {Preparing
to push the f-Pawn.} 11. a3 $2 {Doubtful as the Bishop can go back to b6.} Ba5
12. O-O Bb6 (12... Nxd4 13. Qxd4 Bb6) 13. Be3 Nxc3 14. Qxc3 $2 {Loses a Pawn.}
Nxe5 $1 {This surprised him. The result is that he makes a second, fatal,
mistake.} 15. Bxd5 $4 {He should just accept the loss of a Pawn. After, say 15.
Rad1 he is reasonably placed with KS attacking chances.} Ng4 {He'd missed this.
I thought that he might resign now.} 16. Bxb7 Rb8 (16... Nxe3 {Might be easier.
}) 17. Rf4 Nxe3 18. Qxe3 Rxb7 19. c3 c6 20. Qe4 Qd5 21. Qc2 Re7 22. Raf1 Kg8
23. Rh4 f5 24. Rhf4 g6 25. g4 {He was short of time now.} Rfe8 26. R4f2 c5 27.
gxf5 gxf5 28. Rg2+ {He overran his time somwhere here but the pointer [on the
clock] was bent so that the flag didn't fall until 45'' late, which allowed
him to "reach" the time control.} Kh8 29. Rxf5 cxd4 30. Kh1 ({If} 30. Rxd5 d3+)
30... Re1+ 0-1

