10. Qd2 {[5']} Rc8 11. f3 {[15'] I wasn't happy with this but was in the mood
to play it solidly.} Nh5 {[21'] Doesn't achieve much.} 12. Rfd1 {[20']} Nxd4 {
[27'] Rather a surprise.} 13. Bxd4 Bxd4+ 14. Qxd4 Nf4 {[32']} 15. Bf1 {[33']}
Rc5 16. Rd2 Qc8 {[52']} ({I had expected} 16... Qb6) 17. Kh2 {[36']} Rh5 $5 {
[62'] Rather doubtful.} 18. Nd5 {[46']} Nxd5 19. exd5 e6 {A touch of
desperation here, giving up a Pawn to get the Rook back into play.} 20. dxe6
Bxe6 21. Qxd6 Rc5 {[67']} 22. c3 {[45']} Rc6 23. Qd4 Qc7+ {[67']} 24. Kh1 Qa5
25. a3 Qg5 {[1hr 12'] Black was short of time (3' for 5m)} 26. Rad1 Bb3 27. Re1
Be6 28. f4 Qa5 29. Re5 Qc7 $2 {Giving up another pawn in the time rush.} 30.
Qxa7 Bc4 {Black now "gives up" and obligingly swaps pieces off.} 31. Bxc4 Rxc4
32. Qe3 b6 33. Rd4 Rxd4 34. Qxd4 Rd8 35. Rd5 Rxd5 36. Qxd5 Qxf4 37. Qd8+ Kg7
38. Qd4+ Qxd4 39. cxd4 Kf6 40. a4 Ke6 41. b4 {One week ago I lost to this
opponent: being told that I needed to win a drawn position to save the match:
however I had played in a vey lack-lustre style.} 1-0

