d6 6. e4 g6 7. f4 Bg7 8. Bb5+ Nfd7 9. Bd3 O-O 10. Nf3 a6 11. a4 Qa5 {This
surprised me.} 12. Bd2 Qc7 {[7'] Threatening .....c4 and .....Nc5} 13. Qb3 {
[7']} Nf6 {[25'] A long think he was clearly unhappy.} 14. O-O {[11']} Nbd7 {
[37']} 15. Be3 $2 {[16'] I wanted to play Nd2 but overlooked the strength of
his reply.} ({Better} 15. Be1 {or c1}) 15... Ng4 16. Bc1 $2 {[20'] Out of
practice I overlook the reply.} ({Also bad is} 16. Rfe1 $2 Nxe3 17. Rxe3 Bd4)
16... c4 $1 {Ouch!} 17. Qxc4 Qb6+ 18. Kh1 Nf2+ 19. Rxf2 Qxf2 20. b4 $4 {
A second error: fatal this time. I wanted to cut off his c5 retreat. I felt
that it was unlikely that he would now play ......Nb6 as Qb3 would threaten to
win his Queen with Ra2} Nb6 21. Qb3 $4 (21. Qa2 {is the only move.}) 21... Bh3
{Ouch again! Out of practice - missing tactical points.} 0-1

