1. d4 f5 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Bg5 O-O 6. Bxf6 $2 Bxf6 7. h4 {
He had obviously decided that attacking playwas best, but he was playing very
slowly.} h6 8. Qc2 d6 9. g3 ({I had ecpected} 9. g4) 9... c6 10. h5 {[18']} g5
{[4']} 11. g4 Bg7 12. gxf5 Bxf5 13. Qb3 Qc7 14. d5 Kh8 15. Bh3 $6 {Giving up a
piece but opening up the KS. O.K. for a 40' game.} g4 16. Bxg4 Bxg4 17. Nh4 {
[31']} Bxh5 {[10'] Rather risky} 18. Qc2 Qb6 19. Ne4 Nd7 20. O-O-O cxd5 21.
Rxd5 Ne5 22. b3 Rac8 23. e3 {maybe threatening 23.f4. He had very little time
left now} Bf7 24. Ng5 $1 {His best chance with 1' left} Bg8 (24... hxg5 $4 {
2 allows mate in}) 25. Ng6+ Nxg6 26. Qxg6 Rf6 {White lost on time On the same
evening I beat Alan Bowers in the first round of the League Level (Silver
Knight). On 12/11/82 I beat J.Baldwin in the 40' tournament.} 0-1

