{Time limit 45 moves in 2hrs then 15' for the rest of the game.} 1. e4 c5 2.
Nf3 e6 3. e5 {Played after much thought. I couldn't remember when I last
played someone graded 70. He seemed fairly lost from the start.} d5 4. c3 Qa5
5. Bd3 {[15']} Nc6 {[3']} 6. O-O Nge7 7. Ng5 $2 Nxe5 8. Bxh7 {[21'] Just
asking for trouble.} Qc7 {[10'] Eyeing h2.} 9. f4 {[30']} N5c6 {[14']} 10. f5
$6 {Pressing on but it can only hasten the end.} Nxf5 {He now picked up the f5
Knight and was obviously going to take it with the Bishop, when he noticed h2.
After balancing the Knight in mid air for a minute he played.} 11. Rxf5 exf5
12. Qf3 {[43']} Qe7 {[18']} 13. d3 {[50'] He carried on for some time now
presumably because no-one else was anywhere near finishing.} Qe1+ 14. Qf1 Qxf1+
15. Kxf1 Be7 16. Bxf5 Bxf5 17. Ke2 {[60']} Rxh2 {[21']} 18. Be3 Bxg5 19. Bxg5
Rxg2+ 20. Ke3 Rxg5 21. Kf4 Rg1 22. Kxf5 Kf8 23. Kf4 Re8 24. Kf3 Rf1+ 25. Kg2
Rf5 26. Nd2 Re2+ {[27']} 27. Kg1 Rxd2 28. Rf1 Rg5+ 29. Kh1 Rxd3 30. Rg1 Rh3# {
In subsequent rounds Mr.Gunn played much better (scoring points!) and there
were comments that he was grossly undergraded!} 0-1

