{Time limit 45 moves in 2hrs then 15' for the rest of the game.} 1. e4 c5 2.
Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Qxd4 {I had been intending to play this for a couple of
years. Having hardly played for the last 6 months, this was probably not the
time to try it.} a6 5. Be3 Nf6 6. Nc3 e6 7. h3 Be7 8. Be2 b5 9. a3 Bb7 10. O-O
{[28']} O-O {[18'] I wasn't happy here. I decided that positive action was
needed.} 11. e5 {[39']} Nc6 12. Qf4 {[41']} dxe5 {[25']} 13. Nxe5 Bd6 14. Nxc6
Bxc6 15. Qh4 {[49']} Qc7 {[33']} 16. Bd3 {maybe I should have contested the
d-file.} Be7 17. Rfe1 Rfd8 18. Bd4 $2 {[67'] 18.Bf4 seems better. I had
completely overlooked his reply!} (18. Bf4 $142) 18... Ne4 {[63']} 19. Qh5 {
[1hr 16']} Rxd4 20. Nxe4 h6 21. Re3 Rad8 22. Rae1 {[1hr 23']} Qb7 23. Qe2 {
[1hr 37'] I was getting a bit short of time now.} Qd7 {[1hr 19']} 24. Ng3 $2 {
losing the thread of it.} Bg5 25. Re5 Bf4 26. Rh5 {[1hr 46']} (26. Nh5 $142)
26... Qb7 27. Ne4 $4 {Suddenly realising that I had 9' for 18 moves I
pannicked. I saw the mistake immediatly (so did he!) 27.Qf1 is best.} (27. Qf1
$142) 27... Bxe4 0-1

