{Time limit 45 moves in 2hrs then 15' for the rest of the game.} 1. e4 e5 2.
Nf3 f5 3. Nxe5 Qf6 4. Nc4 fxe4 5. Nc3 Qf7 6. d4 Nf6 $5 {Maybe....} (6... d5) ({
or} 6... Bb4 {are best here.}) 7. Ne5 Qe6 8. Bg5 {With the nast threat of 9.
BxN & 10.Bc4. Without too much thought I deceided I could prevent this with.}
Bb4 $2 {A difficult situation.} ({Best may be} 8... d6 {eg} 9. Bc4 Qf5) 9. Bc4
$1 d5 10. Bxf6 {Help!} O-O {Seems best} 11. Be7 {Another Bishop move out of
the blue!} Bxc3+ 12. bxc3 Re8 (12... Qxe7 13. Bxd5+ Be6 14. Bxe4 {Simply loses
two Pawns.}) 13. Bxd5 Qxd5 14. Bh4 {[40']} Nc6 {[27']} 15. Bg3 Nxe5 16. Bxe5
Qc4 {I was fairly happy here. Although a pawn down I am better developed and
White can't castle and is weak on the white squares.} 17. Qd2 Bf5 18. g4 $5 {
A shade reckless. White oversetimates his position.} Bg6 19. h4 Rad8 20. Qe3 {
[62']} Rf8 {[51']} 21. Rh3 Rf3 22. Rxf3 exf3 23. Qxf3 Bxc2 {The exchanges have
brought my Bishop into play.} 24. Rc1 {[1hr 21']} Rf8 25. Qe2 Bd3 26. Qb2 $2 {
Hoping to exchange Queens with 27.Qb3 but missing my reply.} Qd5 {Threatening
27.......Qe5+ and 27......Qh1+. White has no answer.} 27. Qb4 Qe4+ {A good
"last round" game. I won a bottle of Whisky for 7th place (a good result in a
field of 2 International Masters and about 20 +200 rated players)} 0-1

