{Time limit 30 movwa in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5.
Nc3 d6 6. Be2 Be7 7. O-O O-O 8. Be3 Nc6 9. Qd2 e5 10. Nb3 a5 11. Rad1 {He had
played quickly out of here but expected 11.a4. He now thought for quite a
while.} Be6 12. f3 {[10']} a4 {[21']} 13. Nc1 {[10']} Na5 $5 {[31'] Risky} 14.
Nxa4 {[15']} Nc4 {[46'] 15' thought, changing his mind.} 15. Bxc4 {[15']} Rxa4
{[48']} ({He had originally intended} 15... Bxc4 16. Nb6 Bxf1 17. Nxa8 Bxg2 18.
Qxg2 Qxa8 {but, quiite rightly, decided that it was good for White. The text
is also better for White.}) 16. Bd5 {[18']} Nxd5 {[52']} 17. exd5 Bf5 {[53']}
18. b3 {[19']} Ra6 19. c4 Qd7 20. a4 {Satbilising the QS prior to KS action.
Black was a long way down on time.} Bd8 {[62']} 21. Ne2 {[25']} Bb6 {[67']} 22.
Rc1 Rc8 23. Nc3 {[26']} Ba5 24. Qf2 Bb4 25. h4 Bg6 26. f4 {Black is in big
trouble; short of time, his pieces are largely out of play on the QS.} e4 $2 {
Opens the long diagonal Bd4 will be strong.} 27. f5 Bxc3 {[1hr 14']} 28. Rxc3
Bh5 29. f6 {Not a nice move to meet when you've only seconds left.} g6 30. Qf4
Re8 {An instantaneous reply, defending the e-Pawn but missing the main threat.}
31. Qh6 {A straightforward win.} 1-0

