{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 c6 2. c4 {[3']} d5 {[5']} 3. exd5 {[3']}
cxd5 4. cxd5 {[4']} Qxd5 5. Nc3 Qa5 {Nigel said he hadn't analysed this. 5.....
.Qd6 or 5......Qd8 are normal.} 6. d4 Nf6 7. Nf3 e6 8. Bd3 {[7']} Be7 {[14']}
9. O-O Bd7 $2 ({I wasn't happy with this. Nigel felt that} 9... O-O {was best})
10. Re1 Nc6 11. a3 {[15']} a6 {[30'] Being so out of practice I was thinking
slowly.} 12. Bd2 {[24']} Qd8 {[41']} 13. Bc2 {[27']} Rc8 14. Bg5 {[29']} O-O {
[56']} 15. Qd3 g6 16. Bh6 Re8 {[59']} 17. Bb3 {[39']} Na5 {[69']} 18. Ba2 b5
19. Ne5 Nc6 20. Nxf7 {This surprised me. I had looked at it and thought it
didn't get him anywhere.} Kxf7 21. d5 Bf8 (21... Kg8) (21... Bc5 {were
alternatives}) 22. Bxf8 {[45']} Kxf8 {[1hr 32']} 23. dxc6 {[45']} Rxc6 {
[1hr 39']} 24. Rad1 {[47']} Qc7 {[1hr 43']} 25. Ne4 {[52']} Nxe4 26. Qxe4 ({If
} 26. Rxe4 Rc1) 26... Bc8 {[1hr 48'] Time was getting a little short now.} 27.
h4 {[59']} Rd6 $2 {[1hr 51'] There may be something better.} 28. Qf4+ Ke7 {
[1hr 51']} 29. h5 Qc5 {[1hr 56']} 30. Rxd6 Qxd6 31. Qh6 gxh5 {[1hr 57']} 32.
Qxh7+ Kd8 33. Qxh5 Bd7 {[1hr 58'] Else 34,Rd1 wins the Queen.} 34. Rd1 {
[1hr 10']} Qc6 35. Qg5+ Re7 ({If} 35... Kc8 36. Rc1) 36. Bb1 Qc4 {[1hr 59']}
37. Qf6 Qc6 38. Bg6 {Help!} Qc5 39. b4 {and my flag fell. Having to play board
1 for the county against an International Master, for my second game in 6
months, was possibly asking rather a lot! [Scored as Board 3, the top two
boards were used for the N.Champs]} 1-0

