{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. c4 Nf6 2. d4 c5 3. d5 b5 {Not having played
for 2 and a half years I had been persuaded to play, against my better
judgement. I was rather surprised to be on Bd1. My "rustiness" can be gauged
from the fact that when he played this I couldn't remember what the opening
was called! I continued rather slowly.} 4. cxb5 a6 5. bxa6 Bxa6 {I had no idea
what the main lines were.} 6. Nc3 g6 7. e4 Bxf1 8. Kxf1 d6 9. Nge2 {[10']} Bg7
{[3']} 10. h4 {This surprised him.} O-O {[4']} 11. Rh3 {[18']} Nbd7 {[9']} 12.
Qc2 {[24']} Nb6 {[11']} 13. Kg1 {[27']} e6 {[14']} 14. dxe6 {[34']} fxe6 {[14']
} 15. Nf4 {[41']} Ng4 {[34']} 16. Qe2 {[63']} ({I just didn't feel confident
enough to play.} 16. Nxe6) 16... Nxf2 {[55']} 17. Rf3 Ng4 {[58']} 18. g3 {
[1hr 26']} Bd4+ 19. Kg2 Qd7 {[65']} 20. Qb5 {[1hr 36']} Qb7 {[1hr 11'] I now
started to panic as the clock passed 100'. I felt that I had to speed up - the
result, Naturally, a huge blunder.} 21. Qd3 $4 {[1hr 43'] I realised as I let
go.} Ne5 {After such a long lay off my main problem was bound to be time. I
resolved not to play again until I could get back into it properly.} 1-0

