{Time limit 24 in 1hr +15' allegro} 1. d4 f5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 g6 4. c4 Bg7 5.
Nc3 O-O 6. e4 fxe4 7. Nxe4 c6 8. Ne2 d6 9. O-O {I was quite happy with the
opening as i can get my QBishop out and have fair scope for ....e5 etc} Nxe4
10. Bxe4 Bg4 {A useful move he now had a long think.} 11. f3 {[25']} Bf5 {[12']
} 12. Be3 {[33']} Nd7 {[15']} 13. Qc2 {[42'] I prefer 13.Qd2 or 13.Qb3} e5 {
[23']} 14. Rad1 {[41']} Qe7 15. dxe5 {[48']} Nxe5 {[31'] Threatening 16......
Nxf3} 16. Bxf5 {Forced} Rxf5 17. Bf4 {[54']} Re8 {[38']} 18. Nd4 Rf7 19. Kg2 a6
{I intended to prevent Nb5 after ......c5} 20. h4 c5 21. Nb3 b5 22. cxb5 (22.
Nd2 $142) 22... axb5 23. Nd2 {[59']} c4 {[53']} ({An alternative is} 23... d5
24. Nb3 Nc4 {Threatens 25......RxB}) 24. Ne4 Rxf4 ({Maybe} 24... Nd3 {is
better as I can hang onto the exchange if he plays} 25. Rxd3) 25. gxf4 {[59']}
Nd3 {[55']} 26. Rxd3 {seems best} cxd3 27. Qxd3 Rd8 {Suddenly White has the
better of it. However, he had very little time left. I felt that pudhing the
d-pawn was the best bet.} 28. Ng5 $5 (28. Rf2 {may be best}) 28... Rf8 29. Rf2
{Suddenly it's better for Black as the f-pawn goes and the Bishop goes to e5}
Rxf4 30. Re2 Be5 {Now White was running out of time.} 31. Qd5+ Kh8 32. Nf7+ $4
{Throwing it away in the time rush.} (32. Rc2 $142 {when Black must play} Rf8 {
however Black then has the better of it.}) 32... Rxf7 {Quite an interesting
game. My third successive game where a mistake in time shortage has decided it.
} 0-1

