[4']} Bf5 {[9']} 10. Nd4 {[9']} Bg6 11. c3 Bd6 12. O-O O-O {[12']} 13. N2f3 {
[14']} Nbd7 {[13']} 14. Be3 Rfe8 15. Rc1 b5 {[17']} 16. Nh4 {[23']} Be4 {[22']}
17. Qd2 Ne5 18. b3 {[36']} Rac8 {[29'] Threatening 19......Ba3 winning the
c-Pawn.} 19. f3 Bg6 20. f4 Ned7 21. Nxg6 ({Much more interesting is} 21. f5 $5
{which is very complicated.e.g.} Bh5 22. g4 Ne4 23. Qd1 Bh2+ 24. Kh1 Ng3+ {etc}
) 21... Ne4 $1 ({If} 21... hxg6 22. Bf3 {covers e4.}) 22. Qd1 {[45']} hxg6 {
[36'] I was noe hoping to shift his f-pawn by ......g5. However.....} 23. f5 $4
{An "attacking" move but the roof falls in!} Bh2+ {Winning a rook.} 24. Kh1
Ng3+ 25. Kxh2 Nxf1+ 26. Kg1 Nxe3 27. fxg6 fxg6 28. Bf3 Nf6 29. Qd2 Re5 {
The inaugural match for the University staff team-a 6-0 win. (RAC, Nick Young,
Walter Fairbairn, Mark Ainsworth, John Brooke, Harold White)} 0-1

