{Time limit 35 moves in 1hr 15' then 15' allegro} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6
4. Ba4 Nf6 5. Qe2 Be7 6. c3 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. h3 Na5 9. Bc2 c5 10. O-O {[0']} O-O
{[12']} 11. Rd1 Qc7 12. d4 Bd7 13. dxe5 dxe5 {[18']} 14. Nbd2 {[5']} h6 15. Nf1
Be6 16. b3 {[12']} c4 {[26']} 17. b4 Nc6 18. a4 Qb7 19. a5 Rad8 20. Bd2 Rd7 21.
Ng3 Rfd8 22. Nh4 {[18']} Bf8 {[42']} 23. Nhf5 Ne7 24. Ne3 Ng6 25. Ng4 $5 {
Black now gets a Pawn but at the expense of a semi open h-file.} Nxg4 26. hxg4
Bxg4 27. f3 Be6 28. Nh5 Kh8 29. Kf2 Qa7+ 30. Be3 ({Not} 30. Qe3 $4 Rxd2+) 30...
Qb7 31. Rh1 Rd6 32. Rag1 {[33']} Be7 {[1hr 10']} 33. g3 Kg8 34. f4 Bc8 35. Nxg7
$5 Kxg7 {I thought that I was probably lost.} 36. Qh5 Rd2+ {I must play
actively.} 37. Kf3 {Is there anything better?} Rxc2 {I suddenly felt better.
This takes the Bishop away from the defence of the e-Pawn.} 38. Qxh6+ Kg8 39.
f5 {After some thought. He clearly thought that he had lost his way. This
allows 39......Bxf5 which seems to win. However, he had completely missed......
} Qxe4+ $1 {Beautiful!} 40. Kxe4 Bb7# {One rarely gets a chance of that kind
of finish.} 0-1

