{90' all moves} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. Qc2 c6
7. e3 Nbd7 8. Bd3 h6 9. Bxf6 Nxf6 10. Nge2 Bd6 11. h3 {[3']} Be6 {[6']
Aggressive but leaves the e-Pawn weak.} 12. f4 Qe7 {[10']} 13. O-O-O {[12']} a6
{[14']} 14. Kb1 {[15']} Rc8 {[23']} 15. Rhe1 c5 16. f5 {[26'] Blocks the
diagonal.} Bd7 {[29']} 17. dxc5 {[29']} Rxc5 18. Nd4 O-O 19. Nb3 Ba4 20. g4 Re8
{Threat 21....d4 winning a piece.} 21. Re2 {[52']} Rcc8 {[45']} 22. Rg1 b5 23.
Qd1 {[62']} Bxb3 {[60']} 24. Qxb3 Qe5 {[67']} 25. h4 b4 26. Nd1 Nd7 {The
threat of 27......Nc4 defends th a-Pawn.} 27. Nf2 Nc5 28. Qd1 Nxd3 29. Qxd3 a5
30. g5 hxg5 31. Rxg5 {Doubtful.} (31. hxg5 {is more solid.}) 31... Be7 32. Rg1
Bxh4 {We were both very short of time now.} 33. f6 $2 {A degree of panic here.}
(33. Ng4 $142) 33... Qxf6 34. Qxd5 Bxf2 35. Rf1 {He won't get the chance to
re-take the Bishop.} Red8 $1 {White is fatally weak on the back rank . All of
this was in a big rush.} 36. Qg2 Qf5+ 37. e4 Qd7 38. a3 Qd3+ 39. Ka1 Qxe2 40.
Qxf2 Rd1+ 41. Ka2 Qc4+ 42. b3 Qc1 {White lost on time.} 0-1

