{75' each for all moves} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Nf3 e6 4. Bb5 {The start of
his troubles.} Nd4 5. O-O a6 6. Be2 b5 7. Nb1 {[10'] A courageous decision.}
Bb7 {[5']} 8. Nxd4 cxd4 9. Bf3 Bc5 10. c3 Ne7 11. b4 Bb6 12. Bb2 Nc6 13. e5 {
Probably not a good idea.} Qc7 14. Bxc6 $2 {Probably the losing move, removing
his one developed piece.} Qxc6 15. Qg4 (15. Qf3 {Might be best, horrible
though it is.}) 15... h5 {He now thought for 20'} 16. Qg3 ({If} 16. Qxg7 O-O-O
17. cxd4 Kb8 18. Rc1 Qd5 19. Nc3 Qxd4 {and White runs out of moves}) 16... Rh6
$1 {White can resign.} 17. f3 dxc3+ 18. Kh1 Rg6 (18... cxb2 {is more precise
but it makes little difference.}) 19. Qh4 cxb2 20. Nc3 bxa1=Q 21. Rxa1 Rxg2 {
Rubbing salt in the wound. This aesthetically more pleasing than} (21... Qxf3)
22. Qxh5 Qxf3 23. Qh8+ Ke7 24. h4 Rg5+ {A bit of a blood bath.} 0-1

