Ne2 Qb6 8. Nf3 Be7 9. O-O Nf8 10. Re1 Bd7 11. Qc2 $2 Rc8 12. Qd1 cxd4 13. cxd4
{[12']} Nb4 {[9']} 14. Nc3 Nxd3 15. Qxd3 Ng6 16. Bd2 O-O 17. Qe2 a6 18. a3 Qb3
19. Bg5 Bxg5 20. Nxg5 h6 21. Nf3 Rc7 22. Rac1 Rfc8 23. Qc2 Qxc2 24. Rxc2 Nf4
25. Re3 b5 26. g3 Nh3+ 27. Kg2 Ng5 28. Nxg5 hxg5 29. b4 a5 30. bxa5 Ra8 31. Rb2
Rxa5 32. Rb3 Rc5 33. Rd3 f6 34. f4 gxf4 35. gxf4 Kf7 {Getting relatively short
of time, I offered a draw here. He declined almost immediately.} 36. Kf3 Rc8
37. Rd2 Rh8 38. Kg3 Rh6 {He had twice as much time left as I had.} 39. Rdb2
Rg6+ 40. Kf3 Rg1 41. Nxb5 Bxb5 42. Rxb5 {He offered a draw here. I knew I was
better but had much less time left. I asked Walter (F) how the other games
were going (4 Bds). We hadwon on 1 and were level/winning on 3 & 4 - so I
agreed a draw. Board 4 then lost a won endgame and board 3 drew when the
exchange up! We won on board count.} 1/2-1/2

