{30' each game} 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. d3 e5 5. Nbd2 f5 6. e4 fxe4 7.
dxe4 d4 8. O-O Nf6 9. h3 Be7 10. Qe2 O-O 11. Nc4 {[4']} Qc7 {[3']} 12. Nh2 b5
13. Nd2 a6 14. f4 {I started to feel a bit apprehensive here.} Bd6 15. f5 Bb7 {
Maybe drastic action such as ......g5 is needed} 16. g4 Nb4 17. g5 Ne8 18. Ndf3
Qf7 {I was at a loss now.} 19. a3 Nc6 20. Nh4 Qe7 21. Qh5 g6 22. fxg6 Rxf1+ 23.
Nxf1 hxg6 24. Qxg6+ Qg7 25. Qe6+ Qf7 26. Qxf7+ Kxf7 27. g6+ Kg7 28. Ng3 Ne7 29.
Nh5+ Kh8 30. Bg5 Bc8 31. Rf1 {Help! I am hopelessly lost.} Be6 32. Rf8+ Ng8 33.
Rf2 Ra7 34. Nf5 Be7 {We were both getting short of time so all this was being
played very quickly.} 35. Nxe7 Nxe7 36. Rf8+ Bg8 37. Rxe8 Nxg6 38. Nf6 Ne7 {
In time trouble, still just managing to hold on.} 39. Nxg8 Nxg8 40. h4 Kh7 {
The only reason for continuing is that we were both very short of time and
anything can happen in the final scramble} 41. Bh3 Kg7 42. Bf5 c4 43. h5 a5 44.
h6+ $2 {In the rush giving the Pawn away but it shouldn't affect the result.}
Nxh6 45. Bxh6+ Kxh6 46. Rxe5 b4 47. Re6+ Kg7 48. Rd6 $4 {Losing. He is
preventing 48......Rd7 and ......d3. however 48.Rb6! would win.} ({With the
Rook on b6 he could play 49.axb axb} 48. Rb6 $1 c3 49. axb4 cxb2 (49... axb4
50. Rxb4) 50. bxa5) 48... c3 49. bxc3 {With the Rook on b6 he could play 49.
axb axb} bxa3 50. Rg6+ Kf8 51. Rf6+ Kg8 52. Rg6+ Rg7 53. e5 a2 54. e6 a1=Q+ 55.
Kg2 Qa4 {White lost on time. An amazing recovery!} 0-1

