{1hr 30' for all moves} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. Nf3 Bc5 5. e3 Nc6 6.
a3 a5 7. b3 O-O 8. Bb2 Re8 9. Be2 ({Here I considered} 9. Bd3 Ngxe5 (9... h6
$142) 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Bxh7+ Kxh7 12. Qh5+ Kg8 13. Bxe5 {Threatening 14.Bxg7
Black can avoid this by 9......h6}) 9... Ngxe5 10. Nbd2 d6 11. Nxe5 Nxe5 12.
Nf3 Bg4 13. O-O {[4'] I was reasonably happy with the outcome of the opening,
especially as I could remember little about the Budapest Defence.} Re6 $2 {
Loses a Pawn.} 14. Nxe5 Bxe2 15. Nxf7 Kxf7 16. Qxe2 Kg8 17. Rad1 Qh4 18. Rd5 $5
{Active play but the Rook gets pushed away.} Rh6 19. h3 Rf8 20. a4 {So as to
free the Bishop. However, I was unsure if I really had time for this. Black
now gets some pressure.} c6 21. Rdd1 Rg6 22. Kh2 d5 23. Be5 Qg5 24. Bg3 Bd6 25.
cxd5 {Best.} ({If} 25. Qg4 Qxg4 26. hxg4 Rh6+ 27. Kg1 Bxg3) ({Or} 25. Qe1 $2
Bxg3+ 26. fxg3 Rxf1) 25... Bxg3+ 26. fxg3 Qxg3+ 27. Kh1 Rxf1+ 28. Qxf1 ({If} 
28. Rxf1 {simply} cxd5) 28... cxd5 29. Rxd5 h6 ({If} 29... Rf6 30. Qc4 {
is hard to meet.}) 30. Qe2 Rc6 31. Rd8+ Kh7 32. Qd2 Rf6 33. Kg1 Rg6 (33... Re6
{may be better....but} 34. Rd7 {is best.}) 34. Re8 $1 {Black was getting short
of time so I set a little trap into which he falls.This move gaurds the e-Pawn
and frees the Queen.} Qxh3 $2 35. Qd5 Rg4 ({If} 35... h5 36. Qg8+ Kh6 37. Qh8+
Kg5 38. gxh3) 36. Qf5+ {This won the match for us on board count.} 1-0

