{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bc4 Bc5 5. O-O d6 6. h3 Be6
7. d3 Qd7 8. Qe2 O-O-O 9. a3 h6 10. b4 {Unaware of the threat to the h-Pawn.}
Nd4 11. Nxd4 $2 (11. Qd1 $142) 11... Bxd4 12. Bb2 Bxh3 13. Bb5 {He can't take
the Bishopbut I don't see the point of this unless it is to provoke a target
for a QS attack.} c6 14. Bc4 Bg4 15. Qd2 h5 16. b5 c5 17. b6 a6 18. Rab1 Rh6
19. Nd5 Nxd5 20. Bxd5 Rg6 21. Bxd4 $2 {Completely missing the threat.} Bf3 22.
Bxe5 Rxg2+ 23. Kh1 Qh3+ {After 24.Bh2 I have the choice of 5 mates in 1.
Probably 24......Rd6+ is the most attractive} 0-1

