{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 Be7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. c5 $2 {
In these quick games one tries to vary things, but this is not good.} Nbd7 7.
O-O c6 8. Nc3 b6 9. cxb6 axb6 10. Qc2 Bb7 11. Bf4 Ra5 12. a3 Qa8 13. Ne5 Nxe5
14. Bxe5 Nd7 15. Bf4 Bf6 16. Rfd1 Rc8 17. e4 {The only way to get some play.}
c5 18. e5 Be7 19. Bf1 {I now had 10' left he had 17'} cxd4 20. Rxd4 Rac5 21.
Qd2 b5 $5 22. Bxb5 Nb6 {Giving up a pawn to activate his Knight, but doesn't
achieve much.} 23. Bg5 {I now have attacking chances on the KS.} Bxg5 24. Qxg5
Rxc3 $6 {His time was getting short and he "goes for it" but it isn't sound.}
25. bxc3 Rxc3 26. Qe7 {Threat 27.Be8} Bc6 27. Rf4 Qf8 28. Qxf8+ {Easy now,
especially as he was running out of time. The rest was a mad rush for him.}
Kxf8 29. Bxc6 Rxc6 30. a4 Rc2 31. a5 Nd7 32. a6 Rc8 33. a7 Ra8 34. Rb4 Ke8 35.
f4 Kd8 36. Kf2 Kc8 37. Rc1+ Kd8 38. Rb7 {Threat 39.Rcb7} Rc8 39. Rxc8+ Kxc8 40.
Rxd7 ({In the rush simply overlooking} 40. a8=Q+) 40... Kxd7 41. a8=Q f6 42.
Ke3 g5 43. exf6 gxf4+ 44. Kxf4 e5+ 45. Kxe5 h5 46. f7 h4 47. f8=R hxg3 48. Qb7#
{S.Taylor 0.5 - 0 RAC 1 - 1 W.Fairbairn 0.5 - 0 B.Jolly 1 - 0.5 Uni Staff won
4.5 - 3.5} 1-0

