{30' each/game} 1. e4 d5 2. e5 {He plays this defence regularly so I try to
switch to a French.} c5 3. c3 Nc6 4. d4 $2 {Loses a Pawn as this is not a
French defence as he heasn't played .....e6} cxd4 5. cxd4 Qb6 {A problem now.}
6. Nc3 ({Not having played ......e6 he can answer....} 6. Nf3 {with} Bg4) 6...
Qxd4 7. Qxd4 $5 {Going into a losing line. At this speed of play, not
surprising.} ({Clearly} 7. Nxd5 Qxe5+ {is good for Black.}) 7... Nxd4 8. Nxd5
$5 (8. Bd3 {is maybe objectively better.}) 8... Nc2+ 9. Kd1 Nxa1 10. Nc7+ Kd8
11. Nxa8 Bf5 {Only now did I realise that he could xtract his Knight and I
can't} 12. Be3 (12. e6 Bxe6 {was the alternative.}) 12... b6 13. Nf3 Nc2 14. e6
Nxe3+ 15. fxe3 Bxe6 16. Bb5 {My chances lie in the fast time limit and faster
development.} Bd5 17. Ne5 Kc8 18. Ke2 Kb7 19. Rd1 {I was happy now.} Nf6 20.
Rxd5 Nxd5 21. Bc6+ Kb8 22. Bxd5 {For the first time I felt like I might win.}
e6 23. Bf3 Bc5 24. Nxf7 Rf8 25. Ng5 Rxf3 $6 {Short of time he panics and is
left with a hopeless endgame.} 26. gxf3 Kxa8 27. Nxe6 Bd6 28. h3 Be5 29. b3 h6
30. f4 Bf6 31. e4 Bb2 32. Kf3 Kb7 33. Kg4 Kc6 34. Kf5 Kd6 35. e5+ Ke7 36. Nxg7
Kf7 37. Nh5 a5 38. Ng3 b5 39. Ne4 b4 40. Nd6+ Ke7 41. Nc4 {I stopped recording,
I won the a-pawn with ~5' on the clock had plenty of time to force the central
Pawns through. [There were 2 30' games in the Jamboree.] In the 2nd game very
short of time , I left a Rook en prise. However we won the trophy.} 1-0

