{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. e3 e6 3. Bd3 c5 4. c3 d5 5. Nd2 Nc6 6. f4 Bd6 7.
Ngf3 Qc7 8. Ne5 c4 9. Bc2 b5 10. O-O a5 11. g4 Nd7 12. g5 Bb7 13. Ndf3 Nb6 14.
Nxc6 Bxc6 15. Ne5 {[17']} g6 {[14']} 16. Ng4 O-O-O 17. Bd2 Be7 18. Ne5 Rdf8 19.
Qg4 Kb7 20. Rae1 Nc8 21. Nxc6 Qxc6 22. e4 Re8 23. exd5 exd5 24. Qf3 (24. f5 {
Looks the most active for White.}) 24... f5 25. Re5 Bd6 $1 {It was all a big
rush now, especially for White. However, he sees the problem.} 26. Ree1 ({Not} 
26. Qxd5 $4 Qxd5 27. Rxd5 Kc6 {and the Rook is stuck.}) ({or} 26. Rxd5 Kb6 $1 (
{Not} 26... Ne7 $2 27. Rxb5+) 27. Z0 Ne7 {is coming.}) 26... Bc7 27. Rxe8 Rxe8
28. Re1 Rxe1+ 29. Bxe1 {He offered a draw here.} Nd6 {Now he was rushing
desperately.} 30. b3 $2 Ne4 31. Kf1 {The remaining moves approximate what
happened as I didn't record the the moves in the time rush.} Qd6 32. Bg3 Kc6
33. bxc4 bxc4 34. Kg2 Qa3 35. Bb1 Qb2+ 36. Kh3 Qxb1 {and he resigned soon
after.} 0-1

