{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. g3 d6 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. d3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7.
Qd2 Ng4 8. f4 Nxe3 9. Qxe3 Bg4 10. h3 Bd7 11. Nf3 Qa5 12. Qd2 e6 13. O-O O-O
14. Kh2 a6 15. Nh4 b5 16. f5 Bf6 {After a long think, again leaving him short
of time.} 17. Qf4 e5 {In the short time available I was trying to work out the
consequences of....} ({....} 17... g5 {e.g.} 18. Qxd6 Rad8 ({Fritz gives} 18...
Bxc3 19. Ng6 hxg6 20. bxc3 Rac8 21. fxg6 Qc7 22. gxf7+ Rxf7 23. Qxc5 Ne5) 19.
fxe6 Be8 20. exf7+ Rxf7 21. Qe6) 18. Qe3 Bxh4 ({Maybe} 18... g5 {is possible})
19. gxh4 f6 {He was rushing now} 20. fxg6 hxg6 21. Qh6 Ne7 (21... Kf7 {may
hold out longer.}) 22. Nd5 Rae8 23. Nxf6+ {2 S.J.Taylor 0.5 - 1 RAC 1 - 1 W.
Fairbairn 0.5 - 0.5 B.Jolly 1 - 0.5 We won the math 6 -} 1-0

