{30' each/game} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Bg5 $2 h6 5. Bh4 Qb6 6. b3 e6 7.
Nf3 $2 Bb4+ 8. Nbd2 ({If} 8. c3 Bxb1) 8... Bc3 9. Rb1 Bxd4 10. Nxd4 Qxd4 11.
Bg3 Nd7 12. Nf3 {He has to lose another Pawn unless he is willing to play 12.f4
} (12. f4 Qe3+ 13. Be2 {which is horrid.}) 12... Qc3+ 13. Qd2 Qxc2 14. Qxc2
Bxc2 15. Rc1 Bg6 16. Be2 Ne7 17. Bf4 $2 Bh5 18. O-O $2 (18. Bg3 {is the only
way to hold the e-Pawn.}) 18... g5 19. Be3 ({If} 19. Bg3 Ng6) 19... Bxf3 20.
Bxf3 Nxe5 21. Be2 Nf5 22. Bc5 Kd7 23. Rfe1 {[8']} b6 {[9']} 24. Ba3 Ng6 25. g3
Nd4 26. Bd1 Rhg8 27. Bb2 Nb5 28. Be2 Nd6 29. Bd3 c5 30. Rc2 d4 31. Bc1 Ne7 32.
g4 Rac8 33. h3 Nd5 34. Bd2 Rge8 35. f3 f5 36. Kg2 fxg4 {Exchanging my first
Pawn!} 37. hxg4 Rf8 38. Rcc1 Nf4+ 39. Bxf4 Rxf4 40. Rh1 Rcf8 41. Rcf1 R4f6 42.
Rh3 Nf7 43. Be4 Ne5 44. Rhh1 Kd6 {We were rushing now.} 45. Bb7 R8f7 46. Be4
Rf4 47. Ba8 ({White avoids} 47. Rxh6 Nxg4) 47... R4f6 48. Be4 b5 49. Kg3 c4 50.
bxc4 Nxc4 51. Rh2 Ne3 52. Rb1 Rc7 53. Rd2 e5 54. Bd3 {He was almost out of
time now.} a6 55. Re1 Rc3 56. Rb1 Kc5 57. Be4 b4 58. Bd3 a5 59. Kf2 $2 Nxg4+
60. Kg3 Ne3 61. Be4 a4 62. Bd3 b3 63. Be4 Nc4 64. Rf2 Kb4 65. axb3 axb3 66. Kg2
b2 67. Re2 Ka3 68. Bd5 Ne3+ 69. Kf2 Nxd5 70. Rexb2 Rcxf3+ 71. Ke2 Nc3+ 72. Kd2
Nxb1+ {and White's flag fell.} 0-1

