1. e4 e5 2. d4 exd4 3. c3 dxc3 {Not the sort of opening one wants to face in a
30' event.} 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. Nxc3 Bb4 6. Bd2 d6 7. a3 Bxc3 (7... Bc5 $142) 8. Bxc3
Nf6 9. Bd3 Bg4 10. O-O Ne5 11. Be2 Qe7 12. Nxe5 Bxe2 13. Qxe2 dxe5 14. Bb4 {
I wasn't happy here and used up some time.} c5 {Seems the best but Black's
position is shaky.} 15. Qb5+ Nd7 16. Rad1 ({I had expected} 16. Bc3 {then if}
b6 (16... O-O-O $13) 17. Qc6 Rd8 18. Rad1 {is difficult for Black.}) 16...
O-O-O 17. Rc1 {White has lost a move compared with the last note, as the
Bishop will have to move at some stage.} b6 18. a4 Kb7 19. Bxc5 $4 {Needing to
move quickly he blunders.} Nxc5 20. a5 Qd6 21. axb6 axb6 22. b4 Nb3 {Now the
Knight will plant on d4.} 23. Rc2 $2 Nd4 24. Rd1 $2 {he was rushing now but
had given up.} Nxb5 25. Rxd6 Rxd6 0-1

