1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. g3 d6 4. Bg2 g6 5. d3 Bg7 6. Nf3 O-O 7. O-O c6 8. b4 $5
Bf5 ({I was slightly concerned about} 8... e4 9. Ne1 {etc.}) 9. e4 Bg4 10. Qb3
Qc8 11. Rb1 Na6 12. Be3 Bh3 13. Rfc1 Bxg2 14. Kxg2 {[11']} Nc7 {[20']} 15. a4
Ng4 16. Bd2 Ne6 17. h3 Nf6 18. Be3 {I was happy about how the opening had gone.
} Nd7 19. Ne2 Kh8 {I felt that Black didn't have a plan.} 20. c5 {This opens
the b-file and stops him playing ......c5.} dxc5 21. bxc5 Rb8 22. Qc4 Qd8 23.
Nd2 Qe7 24. f4 Bh6 25. Nf1 {[49']} exf4 {[46']} 26. Nxf4 Nxf4+ 27. Bxf4 Bxf4
28. gxf4 Qf6 $2 {Probably the losing move. I can now force the Queens off and
he gets a rotten endgame.} ({I had expected} 28... Qh4 29. Qd4+ Nf6 30. Qe3)
29. Qc3 Rfd8 30. Ne3 Qxc3 31. Rxc3 Nf6 {My pressure on b7 and the Knight going
to d6 give me a huge advantage.} 32. Nc4 Nh5 33. Nd6 Rd7 34. Kf3 Ng7 35. Rcb3
Ne6 36. Rxb7 Rbxb7 37. Rxb7 Nxc5 38. Nxf7+ Kg7 39. Rxd7 Nxd7 40. Nd8 c5 41. e5
Kf8 42. Ke4 Ke8 43. Nb7 Ke7 {[1hr 10']} 44. a5 {[1hr 10']} h6 45. Kd5 h5 46.
Nxc5 Nb8 {He could resign but with very little time left he knocks out a few
more moves:-"Never resign in a time rush"!} 47. d4 h4 48. Ke4 Nc6 49. a6 Nd8
50. d5 Nf7 51. d6+ Nxd6+ 52. exd6+ Kxd6 53. Nd3 Kc7 54. Ne5 Kb6 55. Nxg6 Kxa6
56. f5 Kb7 57. f6 {The best game I've played for a while. Lancaster A won 3 -
1 RAC............1 A.Fawcett....0.5 W.Fairbairn..1 B.Standen....0.5} 1-0

