1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Bd3 Bg6 5. f4 e6 6. Nf3 c5 7. Bxg6 hxg6 8. c3 {
[6']} Nc6 {[1']} 9. Be3 cxd4 10. cxd4 Qb6 11. O-O {[11'] I am unlikely to take
the b-Pawn.} Nge7 {[3']} 12. Nbd2 {[14'] He was taking a lot of time.} Nf5 $2 {
Probably wrong as it is inviting g4} 13. Bf2 Be7 14. Nb3 O-O $5 {Walking into
a big attack.} 15. g4 {[17']} Nh6 {[6']} 16. Ng5 Qd8 17. Be3 Qd7 {[8']
Intending ......f6} 18. Nc5 Qc8 19. Nh3 b6 20. Nd3 Qa6 {Still not realising
the strenght of his coming attack.} ({Maybe} 20... f5 {is necessary.}) 21. Ndf2
Rac8 22. f5 $1 exf5 23. Bxh6 gxh6 ({Is} 23... fxg4 {better?}) 24. gxf5 f6 25.
Qg4 g5 26. Qh5 Rf7 27. Ng4 {I had been well ahead on time but had used most of
it up now. The position is terrible.} Kf8 {The only hope is to run away.} 28.
Qxh6+ Ke8 29. exf6 {Help. Something active is needed.} Qd3 30. Rae1 Qxd4+ 31.
Kh1 Qxg4 32. fxe7 Nxe7 33. Qh8+ ({A big rush by both of us} 33. f6 {looks
possible.}) 33... Kd7 34. Qe5 Rc2 {Threatens mate.} 35. Qe6+ Kd8 36. Qd6+ (36.
Qd6+ Kc8 {0-1 The final position is very complex. Not what you want in a rapid
game. It looks good for White e.g.} 37. Qe6+ ({Fritz gives} 37. Rf2 Rc6 38. Qa3
Nxf5 39. Qa6+ Kd8 40. Qd3 Rc5 41. Rg2 Qc4 42. Qxc4 Rxc4 43. Nxg5 Re7 44. Ne6+
Kd7 45. Nf8+ Kd6) ({or} 37. Nf2 Qxf5 38. Rxe7 Rxe7 39. Qxe7 Rxf2 40. Qe8+ Kc7
41. Rc1+ Rc2 42. Rxc2+ Qxc2 43. Qe5+ Kc8 44. Qxd5 Qb1+ 45. Kg2 Qxb2+) 37... Kd8
38. Nf2 Qf3+ 39. Kg1 {and White threatens the Rook on f7 which must continue
to protect the Knight. Maybe} Ke8 40. Rc1 Qe2) 36... Kc8 {White's flag fell. I
had 60'' left.} 0-1

