{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. c4 c5 4. Nc3 cxd4 5. Nxd4 Nc6 6.
Nxc6 bxc6 7. e3 Bc5 8. g3 O-O 9. Bg2 d5 10. O-O Ba6 11. Re1 ({If} 11. b3 dxc4
12. Bxc6 Rc8 {is good for Black.}) 11... Bxc4 12. Qa4 Qb6 13. b3 Bb5 14. Nxb5
cxb5 15. Qf4 Bd6 16. Qd4 {Now I get the c-file.} Qxd4 17. exd4 Bb4 18. Re2 Bc3
19. Bb2 Bxb2 20. Rxb2 Rac8 21. a4 b4 22. Bf1 a5 23. Rd1 Rc3 24. Bd3 Rfc8 25.
Kg2 g6 26. Ba6 R8c7 27. Bd3 Kg7 28. h3 Nd7 29. h4 Nb8 30. g4 Rc1 31. Rb1 $2 {
Loses the b-Pawn} Rxd1 32. Rxd1 Rc3 33. Rd2 Rxb3 34. f4 Rc3 35. Rd1 Nc6 36. h5
{Leaving the d-Pawn in the hope of creating something on the KS} Nxd4 37. hxg6
hxg6 38. Bb1 Nc2 39. Rh1 b3 40. Kf2 Rc4 41. Ke2 {White seemed to have decided
that his only hope was to engineer a stalemate situation in the final time
rush.} Rxa4 42. Kd2 Rxf4 43. Kc1 Rxg4 {Six passed Pawns!} 44. Kb2 a4 45. Rh3
Rc4 46. Rg3 e5 47. Rg2 Rb4 48. Bxc2 bxc2+ 49. Ka2 c1=R ({I could play} 49...
c1=Q {but after} 50. Rxg6+ {my King gets persued all over the place.} Kf8 51.
Rg8+ Ke7 52. Re8+ Kf6 53. Re6+ Kg5 54. Rg6+ Kh5 {and wins}) 50. Rg3 Rcb1 51.
Rg2 d4 52. Rf2 d3 53. Rd2 e4 54. Rg2 e3 55. Rh2 R1b3 56. Rb2 Rxb2+ 57. Ka1 {
Hoping for 57......e2 or 57......d2} R2b3 {1 To my great disappointment I
wanted him to play: 58.Ka2 then I could play 58......Kh8 with mate in} 0-1

