{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Bc4 a6 4. a4 d6 5. d3 Nf6
6. f4 Nbd7 7. Nf3 Qc7 8. O-O Be7 {[3']} 9. Qe2 {[7']} O-O 10. h3 b6 11. g4 Bb7
12. g5 {Else he can play ......d5} Nh5 {Leads to a more interesting position
than 12......Ne8. The fork threatened on g3 and threat to f4 give him some
pressure.} 13. Qf2 d5 $5 {I had thought that he couldn't play this. It
certainly gives him some play, but the pressure which my c4 Bishop exerts will
win the game.} 14. exd5 Nxf4 15. Bxf4 ({If} 15. Qh2 e5 {is OK for Black.})
15... Qxf4 16. dxe6 {I was a little concerned opening the f-file for his Rook
but it seems OK.} Bxf3 ({I had been calculating lines like} 16... fxe6 17.
Bxe6+ Kh8 18. Bxd7 (18. Bd5 Bxd5 19. Nxd5 Qd6 20. Nxe7 Qxe7 21. Rae1) 18...
Qxf3) 17. Qxf3 Qxg5+ 18. Qg2 Qxg2+ 19. Kxg2 Ne5 20. Nd5 Ra7 21. exf7+ Nxf7 22.
Nxb6 g6 {Trying to disentangle the pin, but he doesn't get time.} 23. Rae1 a5
24. Nc8 $1 {very neat the pin wins it.} Rxc8 25. Rxf7 1-0

