{1hr 15' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 b6 3. g3 Bb7 4. Bg2 e6 5. Bg5 h6 6. Bxf6
Qxf6 7. c3 d5 8. Ne5 Bd6 9. Qa4+ c6 10. Nd3 O-O 11. Nd2 Ba6 {Preventing 12.e4}
12. Nb4 Bb5 13. Qb3 a5 14. Nd3 ({Naturally not} 14. a4 $4 axb4) 14... Nd7 15.
c4 $2 {Loses the d-Pawn.} dxc4 16. Nxc4 Qxd4 17. Nxd6 Qxd6 18. Rd1 Ra7 {
Getting the Rook off the long diagonal and allowing 19.Nf4 (say) to be
answered by 19......Qb4+} 19. O-O Qc7 20. Qc2 c5 21. Rfe1 {White would do
better to try and take control of the d-file by doubling Rooks.} Bc6 22. f3 {
This leaves him with a dead Bishop.} Rd8 23. Qc3 Raa8 24. Bh3 Nf6 25. Nf4 Rxd1
26. Rxd1 Rd8 27. Rd3 Rxd3 28. Qxd3 Qd7 29. Qxd7 Nxd7 30. Kf2 Ne5 31. Nd3 Nd7
32. Bf1 Kf8 {He was now getting short of time. I had ~ 30'. The rest of the
game was played quite fast.} 33. Ke3 Ke7 34. Kd2 Kd6 35. Kc3 e5 36. e4 Bb5 37.
b3 g5 38. g4 Nb8 39. a4 Ba6 40. Be2 Nc6 41. Bd1 Nd4 42. Kd2 f6 43. h3 {Now he
willhave to worry about my Bishop going to f1 at some stage.} Ne6 44. Be2 ({
The threat was} 44. Z0 Bxd3 45. Kxd3 Nf4+) 44... Kc6 45. Kc3 {He was having to
move very fast now.} b5 46. Kb2 Nd4 47. Nc1 Nxe2 {White lost on time.} 0-1

