{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Bc4 Nc6 4. Nf3 Nge7 5. Qe2 {
Preventing 5......d5 but the Queen is misplaced here.} (5. d4 $142) 5... a6 6.
a4 g6 7. d3 Bg7 8. Be3 d6 9. O-O O-O 10. Ba2 Nd4 11. Qd1 Nec6 12. Bxd4 cxd4 13.
Ne2 e5 14. h3 Be6 15. Bxe6 fxe6 16. Qd2 d5 17. exd5 exd5 18. c3 dxc3 19. Nxc3
Kh8 20. Rab1 {I felt that I had to create some space and play for my pieces.}
Qd7 21. b4 Rad8 22. b5 axb5 23. Rxb5 {I felt a bit happier now. Black now had
a long think having played quickly up to here.} Rxf3 $5 {I haadn't considered
this.} 24. Rxd5 ({If} 24. gxf3 Qxh3 $13 {However, I didn't have to take the
Rook.}) 24... Rxd3 25. Qxd3 Qc8 26. Rxd8+ Nxd8 27. Rd1 Nc6 28. Qd7 Qa8 {
Black has to retreat and it is fairly straightfoward for White.} 29. Rb1 Na5
30. Nd5 e4 31. Nc7 Qg8 ({Not} 31... Qf8 32. Ne6) 32. Ne6 Bf6 33. Rc1 Nc6 34.
Qxb7 Ne7 ({If} 34... Qxe6 35. Rxc6 {wins immediately}) 35. Qxe4 Qb8 36. Qf4 Qb2
37. Qc4 Qb6 38. Qc8+ Ng8 39. Qc4 Ne7 40. Nf4 {I just need to consolidate, keep
f2 protected and push the a-Pawn.} Bh4 41. g3 {He can't take on g3 because ot
the check on c3, now he has no good square for the Bishop.} Bg5 42. Qc5 {
We won the match 3 - 1 (WDDW)} 1-0

