{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 d6 3. f4 e5 4. f5 Nf6 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Bc4 h6
7. d3 a6 8. a4 Bd7 9. Be3 Na5 10. h3 Nxc4 11. dxc4 Be7 12. g4 {[7']} Qb6 {[15']
} 13. Qd3 O-O-O ({Naturally not} 13... Qxb2 $4 14. Rb1 Qa3 15. Bc1) 14. O-O g6
15. fxg6 fxg6 16. Nh4 {[16']} Rdg8 17. Rxf6 $2 {Horrific! I assumed 18.Nd5 Qc6.
I realised my error immediately after playing the move. This error is quite
inexplicable.} Bxf6 18. Nf3 {I felt that I was now lost. Black will come
crashing down the KS unless I can create some instant mayhem on the other side
of the board.} ({I assumed that after} 18. Nd5 Qc6 {he had to play or Qc7})
18... Be6 19. b4 Qc7 20. b5 a5 21. b6 {The best hope. If he plays .....b6 I
must be lost.} Qxb6 {Clearly he felt he had to take this or I play 22.Nb5 then
pick up the a-Pawn. however, I now have attacking chances} 22. Rb1 Qd8 23. Nb5
Be7 24. Na7+ Kc7 {Forced, but now he's in trouble.} 25. Qb3 Qa8 26. Qb6+ {
Suddenly I have at least a draw.} Kd7 27. Qb5+ Kc7 28. Qxa5+ Kd7 29. Qb5+ Kc7
30. Bxc5 $1 dxc5 ({He can probably hang on with say} 30... Rh7 {it is
difficult to see a winning line here for Black.}) 31. Qb6+ Kd7 32. Nxe5+ Ke8
33. Qxe6 Rg7 $8 34. Nxg6 Rhg8 ({If} 34... Rhh7 {then} 35. Nxe7 Rxe7 36. Qg8+) (
34... Rxg6 {Simply leaves him a lost endgame.}) 35. Nxe7 Qxa7 36. Nxg8+ Kd8 37.
Rd1+ 1-0

