{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. e3 b6 4. Nf3 Bb7 5. Bd3 c5 6. O-O Be7
7. Nc3 Na6 8. a3 O-O 9. Rb1 Rc8 10. Na2 d5 11. b4 $2 {Loses the c-Pawn} cxd4
12. exd4 dxc4 13. b5 $6 {Doubtful.} ({although after} 13. Be2 {Black can
support the c-Pawn and has control of e4 & d5}) ({If} 13. Bc2 Bxf3 14. Qxf3
Qxd4) 13... cxd3 14. bxa6 Bxa6 15. Nb4 $2 {Loses the exchange} Bxb4 16. axb4 d2
17. Nxd2 Bxf1 18. Nxf1 Rc4 19. Be3 {[23']} Nd5 {[13']} 20. b5 Qc7 21. Nd2 Nc3
22. Qb3 Nxb1 23. Nxc4 Rc8 24. Qxb1 Qxc4 25. g3 h6 26. Qe4 {Is he heading for
b7 and the a-Pawn? If so it will shorten the game considerably.} Qxb5 27. Qb7
Qc6 28. Qxa7 Ra8 0-1

