{1hr 30' each game} 1. d4 d5 2. e4 dxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f3 Bf5 {I had looked at
this earlier in the day and found a good line. However, I couldn't remember
what it was!} 5. Bc4 ({I have a feeling that} 5. fxe4 {is better, then if} Nxe4
({or} 5... Bxe4 6. Nxe4 Nxe4 7. Be3 Z0 {&} 8. Qf3) 6. Nxe4 Bxe4 7. Be3 Z0 {then
} 8. Qg4 Z0 {&} 9. O-O-O) 5... a6 6. Be3 e6 7. a3 Be7 8. h4 $6 {Waste of time}
(8. fxe4 $142) 8... h6 9. Qd2 (9. fxe4 $142) 9... c5 $6 {Gives me a Pawn but
the Queens come off.} 10. d5 $6 ({I suspect that} 10. dxc5 {is objectively
better.}) 10... Bd6 {I hadn't expected this but it works out quite well.} 11.
O-O-O b5 12. Ba2 {[18']} ({I considered} 12. Nxb5 axb5 13. Bxb5+ Ke7 {but
protects the Bishop}) ({also} 12. dxe6 bxc4 13. exf7+ (13. Qxd6 Qxd6 14. Rxd6
Bxe6 15. fxe4 {may be best}) 13... Ke7 {holds}) (12. Bb3 {may be better}) 12...
e5 $1 {I had missed this. Now I am worse.} 13. Nge2 Qd7 14. Ng3 b4 15. Ncxe4
Nxe4 16. Nxe4 Bxe4 17. fxe4 bxa3 18. bxa3 Qa4 19. Qd3 Nd7 20. Kd2 {I have to
get the Rooks accross and get the King to a safer area.} Nb6 21. Ke2 c4 $2 {
This seems to lose a Pawn.} 22. Qc3 Qb5 23. Bxb6 ({If} 23. Rb1 Na4 {is good
for Black.}) 23... Qxb6 24. Qxc4 O-O {I was happier now but, with opposite
coloured Bishops and the heavy pieces on, I felt it was going to be a long
hard slog.} 25. a4 Qc5 $6 {I'm sure Black would do better with the Queens on.}
26. Qxc5 Bxc5 27. Rb1 a5 28. Rb5 Rfd8 $4 {Getting behind on time he plays too
quickly and having worked out a series of moves plays the last move in the
sequence instead of the first. The rest is just a quick bash.} 29. Rxc5 Kf8 30.
Rb1 Ke7 31. Rb7+ Ke8 32. d6 Rxd6 33. Rxe5+ Kf8 34. Rxf7+ 1-0

