{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Bc4 Nc6 4. f4 Nd4 5. d3 a6 6. a4 Nh6 7.
Nf3 Be7 8. O-O O-O $5 ({I now considered} 8... f5 {but didn't want to spend
too long analysing, so played safe.}) 9. h3 ({Something like} 9. f5 Ng4 10. h3
Nf6 11. e5 Ne8 12. Nxd4 cxd4 13. Ne4 Qc7 14. f6 {must be good for White}) 9...
f5 {[7']} 10. Be3 {[4']} Qb6 11. a5 Qa7 ({At the fast time limit not willing
to risk.} 11... Qxb2 12. Na4 Qb4 13. Nb6 Rb8 14. Ra4 Qc3 15. Ne1 Z0 16. Bd2 {
etc}) 12. Ra4 b5 ({Playing 12.Ra4 with the bright idea of....} 12... Z0 13.
Nxd4 cxd4 14. Bxd4 {so as to answer} Qxd4+ {with 15.Bxe6+. There is a smal
flaw in this!}) 13. axb6 Qxb6 14. Nxd4 $5 {As I played this I realised that ...
..Qxd4 in the above line is check!} cxd4 15. Bf2 Bc5 16. Ne2 Bb7 17. Ng3 Qxb2 {
Having declined to take the Pawn on move 11, which was possibly OK, he now
takes it and loses the game. He missed my 20th move.} 18. Bb3 {Wins the Queen.}
fxe4 19. Ra2 Qc3 20. Be1 exd3 21. Bxc3 dxc3+ 22. Kh2 d2 {With relatively
little time left for both of us it is worth playing on.} 23. f5 {As so often
in this opening line the white squared Bishop proves very strong.} Bd5 24. Ra5
Bd6 ({If} 24... Bb4 25. Rxd5) ({or} 24... Bxb3 25. Rxc5 {wins the c-Pawn}) 25.
Rxd5 Bxg3+ 26. Kxg3 exd5 (26... Nxf5+ 27. Rdxf5 {Loses the Knight}) 27. Bxd5+
Kh8 28. Bxa8 Rxa8 29. f6 gxf6 30. Rxf6 Ng8 31. Rf3 Re8 ({If} 31... Rc8 32. Qa1)
32. Rxc3 Nf6 33. Rd3 Re1 34. Qf3 {Having avoided the Knight forks it is easy
now.} Ne4+ 35. Kh2 h6 36. Rxd7 1-0

