{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 d6 3. f4 e5 4. f5 Nf6 5. Bc4 Nc6 6. d3 Nd4 7.
Be3 a6 8. a4 Be7 9. Nf3 Nxf3+ {Better to leave the Knight on d4.} 10. Qxf3 Bd7
11. g4 Qa5 12. Ke2 O-O-O {Giving up the Pawn: a fair decision in a 30' game.}
13. Bxf7 Rdf8 14. Bc4 h5 {Turns out badly.} 15. g5 Ng4 $2 {Now the Knight gets
stuck with no retreat.} 16. Nd5 Qd8 ({Avoiding} 16... Bd8 $4 17. Bd2 {Winning
the Queen.}) ({If} 16... Nxe3 17. Nxe7+ Kd8 18. Ng6 Nxc4 {and then not} 19.
Nxh8 ({Instead White plays} 19. dxc4 {and the Black Rooks are still forked.})
19... Qd2+ {With various possibilities which might prove difficult in a
rapidplay game e.g.} 20. Kf1 Ne3+ 21. Kg1 Rxf5 22. exf5 Bc6 23. Qg3 Nxf5 {etc})
17. Nxe7+ Qxe7 18. Bd2 {Wins the Knight.} Qd8 19. h3 Nf6 20. gxf6 Qxf6 21. Rag1
Bxa4 22. b3 Bxb3 {Desperation. If 23.BxB he pushes the a-Pawn.} 23. cxb3 Qe7
24. Qg3 Rh7 25. Qg6 Qc7 26. Qxh7 {Dick won the 30' Championship} 1-0

