{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. c5 Nc6 6. Bb5
Bd7 7. Nf3 g6 8. Nc3 Bg7 9. O-O O-O 10. Bxc6 Bxc6 11. b4 a6 12. Bb2 Qc7 13. Re1
e6 14. Qe2 {[35'] He spent a long time on this} Rfd8 {[16']} 15. Rad1 {[36']}
b6 {[29'] I wasn't happy here. I decided that to get some play I had to open
the b-file.} 16. Qe5 {[46'] Not very useful.} Qb7 {[30']} ({Not} 16... Qxe5 $2
17. Nxe5) 17. Qe2 Rab8 18. Bc1 {[60']} bxc5 19. bxc5 Ne4 {I felt I had some
play now.} 20. Nxe4 dxe4 21. Ng5 Bxd4 22. Bf4 {This works out well for White}
Rbc8 23. Bd6 {[69']} h6 $5 (23... Bb5 {looks better. It threatens the Queen
and ..........Bxc5 The Pawn can't be defended by the Queen from c2 due to RxB
so} 24. Qxe4 (24. Qc2 Rxd6 25. cxd6 Rxc2) 24... Qxe4 25. Nxe4 e5 26. Z0 {
threatening} f5 {which looks OK.}) 24. Rxd4 hxg5 25. Qe3 {He offered a draw
here. We had won the match so I decided to continue as I felt I was better.
However, the KS is weaker than I realised.} f6 26. Rdd1 Qb2 {This gets me
nowhere as the Queen needs to defend the 2nd rank.} 27. Re2 {[1hr 12']} Qb5 {
[51']} 28. Ree1 Bd5 $2 {Losing it I overlooked the reply.} (28... Kf7 $142) 29.
Be7 {Now I've had it.} Re8 30. Bxf6 Kf7 31. Qxg5 Qxc5 32. Be5 Rg8 33. Rc1 Qe7
34. Qf4+ {[After studying the ECF grading database I think Arnside were
playing "double point" matches as they were when I (Sean Parker) joined the
league in 2007]} 1-0

