{Time limit 40 moves in 1hr 30' then 30' allegro} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nc3
Nc6 4. Bb5 Bb4 5. O-O O-O 6. d3 d6 7. h3 Qe7 {This allows a nuisance pin on g5
and forces the exchange on c3 in view of Nd5} 8. Bg5 Bxc3 9. bxc3 Nd8 10. Rb1 (
10. d4 {Looks better e.g.} exd4 11. cxd4 {now if} Qxe4 $6 {then} 12. Bxf6 gxf6
13. Bd3 {must be good for White}) 10... c6 11. Bc4 Be6 ({I was concerned about
} 11... b5 12. Bb3 a5) 12. Bb3 Bxb3 13. Rxb3 Rb8 14. Nd2 Ne6 15. Be3 b6 16. f4
exf4 17. Bxf4 Nxf4 ({Again, I had been concerned about} 17... Nc5 {e.g.} 18.
Rb1 ({However, I can possibly risk} 18. Rb4 a5 19. Rd4 {inview of the threat
to the d-Pawn and Bg5}) 18... Na4) 18. Rxf4 d5 19. Qf3 Rfd8 {This weakens f7}
20. Rb1 dxe4 21. Nxe4 Nxe4 22. Rxe4 Qc5+ 23. d4 Qd5 24. Rb3 {After a lot of
thought. I considered both 24.Rbe1 & 24.Rf1 . Both are very risky with the
a-Pawn going.} (24. Rbe1 Qxa2 25. Re7 Rf8 {Seems to hold.}) (24. Rf1 Re8 {
Seems OK}) 24... Qd7 {After this I get some pressure} ({I had expected} 24...
Re8 {when the ending after} 25. Rxe8+ Rxe8 26. Qxd5 cxd5 27. Kf2 {may be good
for White}) 25. c4 {[62']} Re8 {[60']} 26. Rbe3 Kf8 27. Kf2 g6 $2 {With time
getting on he plays quickly and commits suicide.} 28. Qf6 Kg8 29. Re7 Rxe7 30.
Rxe7 Qf5+ 31. Qxf5 gxf5 32. Rxa7 b5 33. Rc7 Rb6 34. cxb5 cxb5 35. Rc5 Kf8 36.
Rxf5 Ke7 37. Ke3 b4 (37... Re6+ 38. Re5 {wins}) ({If} 37... Ke6 38. Rh5) 38.
Kd3 {Lancaster won 3 - 2 Collins 1; Fawcett 0.5; Fisher 0.5; Bland 0.5;
Cornish 0.5} 1-0

