{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Bc4 a6 4. a4 Nc6 5. f4 Nge7 6. e5 d5
7. exd6 Qxd6 8. d3 Nf5 9. Nf3 Be7 10. Ne4 Qc7 11. O-O Bd7 12. c3 O-O 13. Qe2 {
I considered 13.g4 but felt that it was too loose.} Na5 14. Ne5 Nxc4 {[30']}
15. dxc4 {[16']} Bc6 16. Ng3 {Around here I started to feel that it wasn't
going well. Maybe 16.g4 is playable.} Nxg3 17. hxg3 Rad8 {[40']} 18. Be3 {[20']
} b6 {I assumed that this was to support c5. however, it also allows .....Qb7
with pressure on the long diagonal.} 19. b3 $2 {To defend a4 so the aRook can
move. However, I didn't consider his reply.} (19. Nxc6 $142) 19... Be4 {
This is awkward for me. 20......Bd3 is threatened.} 20. Rad1 Qb7 {I am
starting to get tied up. Also ......f6 of .......Bf6 is coming.} 21. Qf2 {
After a long think, hoping for some QS play.} f6 22. Nf3 Bf5 23. b4 {[52']
Trying for some play.} Qc7 {[67'] He now offered a draw. We had won one game
and seemed to be at least level in the other two. My position is not good so I
agreed. [The match was a tie,Uni Staff won the match on board count]} 1/2-1/2

