{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 {I have seen him play the
Marshall so I steer clear of the Ruy Lopez.} Nf6 4. d4 exd4 5. e5 Ng8 6. cxd4
d5 7. Bb5 Bb4+ 8. Nc3 Bg4 9. h3 Bh5 10. O-O Nge7 11. Bg5 Bxc3 12. bxc3 O-O 13.
g4 Bg6 {[22']} 14. Bd3 {[10']} Qc8 15. Nh4 Bxd3 16. Qxd3 Ng6 17. Nf5 {Now
there is the possibility of Nxg7 at some stage.} Nd8 18. Qf3 Ne6 19. Bd2 $2 ({
Correct is} 19. Be3) 19... Qd8 20. Qg3 {[33']} Ng5 {[52']} 21. f3 Ne6 22. h4 {
[35']} Ne7 {[60']} 23. f4 c5 {The best chance of some play} 24. Nd6 $2 ({
Better to admit that 19.Bd2? was wrong and play} 24. Be3 {Then e.g.} cxd4 25.
cxd4 Nc6 26. Rad1 {followed by} Z0 27. Nd6 Z0 28. f5) 24... cxd4 25. f5 Nc5 26.
cxd4 Ne4 27. Nxe4 dxe4 28. Qe3 $2 (28. Be3 $142 Nc6 29. Rad1) 28... Nc6 29.
Qxe4 ({I realised that it had gone wrong. The d & h Pawns are attacked. If} 29.
Bc3 Qxh4 {and I can't play} 30. Qxe4 {as} Qg3+ {wins the Bishop.}) 29... Qxd4+
30. Qxd4 Nxd4 31. Rab1 b6 32. Bb4 (32. Kf2 {May be best, preventing Knight
forks. Time was now short and the play becomes rapid and scrappy.}) 32... Rfe8
33. Bd6 Rac8 {I was worried now. I can't contest the c-file because of the
Knight fork on e2.} 34. Rf2 Rc4 35. Kh2 $2 (35. Kg2 {Looks better in view of
the possible Knight fork.}) 35... Rec8 ({I had expected} 35... Nc6 {which
seems to win a pawn.}) 36. Kg3 Rc3+ 37. Kg2 Rc2 38. Rb2 Rxf2+ 39. Rxf2 a6 40.
Rd2 Nb5 41. Bb4 a5 42. Be7 h6 43. Rd8+ Rxd8 44. Bxd8 Nc3 {All of this was
played fast.} 45. Bxb6 Nxa2 (45... a4 {looks better}) 46. Bxa5 Kf8 $2 ({
He has to play} 46... Nc1) 47. Kf3 $2 {Going too fast I overlook the same
thing.} Ke8 $2 48. Ke4 $2 Kd7 $2 49. Bd2 {Noticing at last that the Knight can
be trapped. Now it's all over.} Ke7 50. g5 hxg5 51. Bxg5+ f6 52. Bd2 Kd7 53.
e6+ Ke7 54. Kf4 Ke8 55. Kg4 Ke7 56. Kh5 Ke8 57. Kg6 Kf8 58. h5 Ke8 59. Kxg7 {
Dick won the Lancaster Club Championship.} 1-0

