{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. e6 {Worth a try
in a quickplay game and justified by the fact that he spent 3' on his reply.}
fxe6 6. h3 Nge5 7. e4 Be7 8. Nxe5 Nxe5 9. Qh5+ Nf7 10. Nc3 O-O 11. Be3 g6 12.
Qd1 Bf6 13. Qc2 c6 14. O-O-O Qc7 15. Kb1 e5 {It isn't clear what this achieves.
As he can't force ......d5 he should go for a QS advance.} 16. h4 {Beginning a
KS attack but also preventing him putting a piece on g5.} d6 17. Be2 Bd7 18. g4
a6 19. g5 Bg7 20. h5 b5 $2 {Banking all on a QS attack. Now the King's Bishop
is buried. He was starting to get short of time here.} 21. h6 Bh8 22. b3 ({
I can play} 22. cxb5 axb5 23. Nxb5 {but it gives him attacking lines and is
too risky in a quickplay game.}) 22... Qc8 23. c5 dxc5 24. Bxc5 Re8 25. Be3 Be6
26. Rd2 a5 27. Rc1 a4 28. b4 Rd8 {He was rushing now.} 29. Nd1 Rxd2 30. Bxd2
Bc4 $2 {Playing very fast he goes to pieces 30......Nd8 is better though White
is still on top.} (30... Nd8 $142) 31. Bxc4 bxc4 32. Qxc4 Ra6 33. b5 {With no
time left he now played 33.......Nd6. I pointed out this left him in check so
he resigned.} (33. b5 {now if} Rb6 34. Ba5 Rxb5+ 35. Qxb5) 1-0

