{30' each/game.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 b6 3. Nbd2 Bb7 4. e3 e6 5. Bd3 c5 6. c3 d5 7.
O-O Nbd7 8. Qa4 c4 9. Be2 ({Not} 9. Bc2 {when} Qc7 {threatens} 10. Z0 Bc6 11.
Qa6 Nb8) 9... Qc7 10. Ne5 Bd6 11. Ndf3 O-O 12. Nxd7 Nxd7 13. Qc2 f5 14. g3 Nf6
15. Ng5 Qe7 16. f4 h6 17. Nf3 Ne4 18. Nh4 {[11']} Qf7 {[6']} 19. Qd1 g5 20. Bh5
Qg7 21. fxg5 {This seems very risky, opening up the lines of attack along the
g-file and also for my black sq Bishop.} Qxg5 22. Ng6 Rf6 {After some thought.}
({Either} 22... Nxg3 {or 22......Bxg3 looks possible . Maybe} 23. Rf2 {I just
didn't have time to work it all out., so play safe} ({or} 23. Nxf8)) ({However,
if} 22... Bxg3 {maybe simply} 23. Kh1) 23. Nf4 Kh7 24. Qf3 Rg8 25. Kh1 Bc8 26.
b3 $2 {Short of time White feels that he has to do something positive. However,
the thing that he absolutely must not do is open up the long White diagonal.}
Qg7 27. bxc4 $2 dxc4 28. Rb1 $2 Bb7 29. Kg1 Nxc3 0-1

