{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. c3 d6 5. d4 exd4 6. cxd4
Bb6 7. h3 h6 8. Nc3 Nf6 9. O-O O-O {I really couldn't remember anything about
how to play against the Guicco Piano} 10. Re1 Ne7 {Trying to force .....d5} 11.
Be3 d5 12. e5 Nh7 13. Bd3 Bf5 14. Nh4 Bxd3 15. Qxd3 Qd7 16. a4 c6 17. a5 Bc7
18. b4 g5 {I started to get more ambitious here.} 19. Nf3 f5 20. exf6 Rxf6 {
Possiblt starting to get ambitious. I had ideas of ......Rxf3 and doubling
Rooks. However, it is probably better to bring the h7 Knight back into play.}
21. Ne5 Qe6 $2 (21... Qf5 {looks much better. However, I had necer lost to
Andrew and didn't want to go into a drawish line. My pieces are now very
restricted.}) 22. Na4 b6 23. Bd2 Qd6 (23... Qf5 $142) 24. Rac1 Nf8 $2 {Not
realising the mess I'm in, my pieces are overloaded 24......Re8 defending the
Knight may be best.} 25. b5 cxb5 26. Qxb5 a6 27. Qd3 Qd8 $2 {This loses it.
The alternatives are probably best.} (27... bxa5) (27... b5) 28. Ng4 Rg6 29.
axb6 Bxb6 {Only now did I realise the problem.} 30. Nxb6 Rxb6 {I can't take
with the Queen as the Knight is loose.} 31. Ba5 Neg6 {Hoping he might try
something "clever" like 32.Rb1?} 32. Nxh6+ Kg7 33. Ng4 Nf4 34. Qf5 Rf6 35.
Qxg5+ 1-0

