{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. Bc4 a6 5. a4 Nf6 6. e5 $2
{Horribly out of practice I completely overlook the e-Pawn is indefensible
after 6......Ng4.} Ng4 ({I had got obsessed with} 6... d5 7. exf6 dxc4 {etc.})
7. Qe2 Qc7 8. O-O {All I can do is hope my lead in development will count for
something.} Ncxe5 {Threatens 9......Nxf3+ with mate on h2.} 9. Nxe5 Nxe5 10. d3
{[24']} Bd6 ({I had expected} 10... d5 {which buries my Bishop.}) 11. f4 Nxc4 {
I was happy with this. My Bishop was a worse piece than the Knight.} 12. dxc4
O-O 13. Be3 b6 14. Ne4 Bb7 15. Nxd6 Qxd6 16. Qf2 Qc6 17. a5 {[50']} d6 {[50']}
18. axb6 a5 {I'm not sure why he played this.} 19. Qg3 {Threat 20.f5} f5 20.
Bd2 Rf6 21. Rf2 Rg6 22. Qh3 Qxb6 23. Bc3 Qc6 24. Rxa5 Rxa5 25. Bxa5 Qa4 26. Qc3
Qa1+ 27. Qe1 Qxb2 28. Bc3 Qb6 29. Qd1 Qc6 {He was getting a little short of
time now.} 30. Qd2 Qe4 31. Re2 Qxc4 32. Qxd6 {I offered a draw here as there
seems no other reasonable outcome.} Qxe2 33. Qd8+ Kf7 34. Qd7+ Kf8 35. Qd8+
1/2-1/2

