{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. f4 e6 4. Bc4 a6 5. a4 g6 6. Nf3 Bg7 7.
O-O Nd4 8. d3 Ne7 9. e5 Nef5 10. g4 Nxf3+ 11. Qxf3 Nd4 12. Qf2 d5 $2 {The
thematic move but his c-Pawn is weak and I have pressure on the black squares.}
13. exd6 Qxd6 14. Ne4 {[6']} Qe7 {[5']} 15. c3 {Wins the c-Pawn.} Nc6 16. Qxc5
Qxc5+ ({If} 16... Qh4 17. Nf2 {and the Black Queen is out of play.}) 17. Nxc5
b6 18. Ne4 O-O 19. Be3 Rb8 {[10']} 20. Nd6 {[8']} b5 {Loses another Pawn but
he was under pressure. White threatened 21.Nxc8 and 22.Bxa6} 21. axb5 axb5 22.
Bxb5 Ne7 23. Ba7 Ra8 24. d4 Rd8 25. Nxc8 Rdxc8 26. Bc5 Nd5 27. Rxa8 Rxa8 28.
Bc6 Ra2 29. Bxd5 exd5 30. Ba3 Bf8 31. Bxf8 Kxf8 32. Rb1 {32.Rf2 might be
better, leaving the Rook more scope} Ke7 33. Kf2 Kd6 34. Kf3 Kc6 35. g5 Kb5 36.
f5 Kc4 37. Kf4 Kb3 38. fxg6 fxg6 39. Ke5 Kc2 ({More chance is offered by
activating the Rook e.g.} 39... Ra5 {However, White plays} 40. Rf1 Kxb2 41. Rf7
Kxc3 42. Rxh7) 40. Rf1 Rxb2 {Giving up.} 41. Rf2+ Kxc3 42. Rxb2 Kxb2 43. Kxd5
1-0

