{30' each/game} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. c3 d6 4. Bc4 Nc6 ({In these fast games
there is always the possibility of something like.} 4... c5 $2 5. dxc5) 5. h3
Bd7 6. Bg5 Bf6 {If he has to play this he has clearly gone wrong already.} 7.
Be3 e5 8. d5 Nce7 9. Bd3 {After a (relatively) long think. If he plays 9......
c5 I want to be able to play 10.c4 to maintain a bind.} Bg7 10. g4 f5 $2 {
10......c6 looks better he gets in a mess now.} 11. gxf5 Nf6 ({Not liking} 
11... gxf5 12. Qh5+ Ng6 13. exf5 Nf6 {etc}) 12. Bg5 Rf8 13. fxg6 hxg6 14. Nd2
Nh5 15. Qc2 Nf4 16. Bxf4 exf4 (16... Rxf4 {Leaves him with more space.}) 17.
O-O-O g5 18. Ngf3 Ng6 $2 {Proves fatal.} (18... Ng8 {Looks better}) 19. e5 $1
Nxe5 ({The alternative} 19... Nh8 {allows} 20. e6 {and is too horrible to
contemplate especially with <15' left.}) 20. Bg6+ Nxg6 ({The alternative is} 
20... Ke7 21. Nxg5 {then maybe} Rf6 22. Rhe1 Qg8 23. Ndf3 {etc.}) 21. Qxg6+ Rf7
22. Nxg5 Qf6 23. Rde1+ Kd8 ({If} 23... Kf8 24. Nh7+) 24. Nxf7+ Kc8 25. Qxf6
Bxf6 1-0

