{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs then 30' allegro} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5
4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Be3 Be6 $5 {Rather odd.} 7. c5 g6 8. Be2 Bg7 9. Nf3 O-O
10. O-O a6 11. a4 Ne4 12. Qc1 Qa5 13. Rd1 f5 {[26'] Leaves a few holes.} 14.
Bd3 {[25']} Qd8 15. Ne2 {[32']} Bd7 16. Nf4 e6 17. Ne2 Qe8 (17... e5 {Is more
interesting}) 18. Ne1 Nf6 19. f4 {Putting an end to ......e5} Ne4 20. Nf3 Nb4
21. b3 Nc6 22. Rb1 Nb4 {He seems stuck for a plan.} 23. Qa3 Nxd3 24. Rxd3 a5
25. Ne5 {[62']} Bc6 {[61']} 26. Qc1 Qc8 {He offered a draw here. Five draws
would win the match on the basis of lower grading.} 27. Nc3 Nxc3 28. Rxc3 Bxe5
$2 {Having had his draw offer turned down he starts swapping off. However,
this may be the fatal error, leaving his KS black squares very weak.} 29. dxe5
Rd8 30. Bd4 Qc7 31. Qe1 Qe7 32. Bf2 {Threatening not simply 33.Bh4 but then 34.
Bf6 and a KS advance.} Rdc8 33. Rbc1 Kf7 34. Rh3 h5 35. Bh4 Qd7 36. Bf6 Rg8 37.
Qh4 Ke8 38. Qg3 Qf7 39. Rc3 Kd7 40. Qe3 Ke8 41. Rh4 Qd7 42. Rd3 Qf7 43. h3 Kd7
44. Kf1 Qf8 45. g4 Qf7 46. Qe2 fxg4 47. hxg4 Rh8 {A last hope. However, he
should probably have tried to swap Rook for Bishop on f6 at an earlier stage.}
48. Bxh8 Qxf4+ {If he can get a couple of Pawns for the exchange he might hang
on for a bit.} 49. Qf3 Qc1+ 50. Rd1 {Match Result RAC--------1 A.Fawcett-1 C.
Fisher---0.5 B.Cornish--0.5 B.Standen-0.5} 1-0

