{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. d3 h6 {It
didn't occur to me that he would grab the e-Pawn.} 6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. Nxe5 Bd6 (
7... Bc5 $142) 8. Nf3 Bg4 9. h3 Bxf3 10. Qxf3 Qd7 11. Bf4 O-O-O 12. O-O {[3']}
Bc5 {[9']} 13. Nd2 Nh7 {Intending a KS advance} 14. Nb3 Bd6 15. Qg3 f5 16. Bxd6
cxd6 17. exf5 Qxf5 18. Qg4 {[13'] I began to suspect that he wanted a draw.
This would not be a major problem for me as I would be White in the replay.
However, I would rather win this one.} Qxg4 {[14']} 19. hxg4 Nf6 20. f3 Rde8
21. Rfe1 Kd7 22. Nd4 g6 23. Kf2 Rhf8 {Threat 24......Nxg4} 24. Rxe8 Rxe8 25.
Re1 Rxe1 26. Kxe1 Nd5 {I was happy now. My Knight is better than his and he
has Pawn weaknesses.} 27. a3 $2 {Loses a Pawn.} (27. Kd2 $142) 27... c5 28. Ne2
Ne3 29. Nf4 g5 30. Nh5 Ke6 31. Ng7+ Kf6 32. Ne8+ $2 {Now the Knight gets stuck
here.} Ke5 33. g3 Nxc2+ 34. Kd2 Nd4 35. Ke3 $2 Ne6 {Now his Knight can't move.}
36. f4+ {A touch of desperation now.} gxf4+ 37. gxf4+ Nxf4 38. Nxd6 $4 {
He was now playing very fast and ends it quickly.} Nd5+ 39. Kf3 Kxd6 40. Ke4 b5
41. Kf5 Ne3+ 42. Kf4 Nxg4 0-1

