{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5. Nb3 ({I was
going to answer} 5. Nxc6 {with} Qf6) 5... Bb6 6. a4 Qh4 7. Qe2 ({I had expected
} 7. Qf3 {when} Ne5 8. Qe2 {is unclear}) 7... a6 8. Nc3 d6 9. a5 Bg4 10. Qd2
Ba7 11. g3 Qh5 12. Bg2 O-O-O 13. Nd5 Nf6 14. Nf4 Qe5 15. Nd3 Qe7 16. Qf4 Be6
17. O-O $2 {Loses a Pawn. Black's position was better with the White Knights
rather limited and the Black Bishops active.} Bxb3 18. cxb3 Nd4 19. Kh1 Nxb3
20. Ra4 Nxc1 21. Rxc1 Rhe8 22. Bh3+ {Pointless. I was going to move the King
to b8 anyway.} Kb8 23. Bg2 Nd7 24. Rac4 c6 25. b4 Ne5 26. Nxe5 dxe5 27. Qf3 Rd4
28. Qe2 {He was rushing now.} Rxc4 29. Qxc4 Rd8 30. Kg1 Qf6 31. Qc2 Qd6 32. Bf1
{White lost on time. Black wins the f-Pawn after 32......Qd2} 0-1

