{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 d6 2. d4 g6 3. f4 Bg7 4. c3 Nf6 5. Bd3 O-O 6. Nf3 c5
7. O-O Nc6 $2 {Wastes 2 moves. 7......Bg4 looks better} 8. d5 Nb8 {[8'] 8......
Na5 leaves his Knightvulnerable to an attack by b4.} 9. h3 {[3']} Bd7 10. a4
Ne8 11. Be3 Qc8 12. Nbd2 e5 {[17']} 13. f5 {Seems like a decent Pawn sacrifice.
I spent a while thinking about it. He replied in about 15''.} Nf6 ({If} 13...
gxf5 14. exf5 ({However, after} 14. g4 {he is in danger of being pushed off
the board.}) 14... Bxf5 15. Bxf5 Qxf5 16. Ng5 Qg6 17. Rf3 {White has good
attacking chances.}) 14. g4 h6 15. Qe1 Nh7 16. h4 gxf5 {Deciding that he must
do something.} 17. gxf5 f6 18. Qg3 Kh8 19. h5 Ng5 {[33']} 20. Nh4 {[17']} Be8
21. Ng6+ Bxg6 22. hxg6 {Now his h-Pawn is doomed.} Kg8 23. Kg2 Rd8 24. Rh1 Kf8
25. Rh5 Nd7 26. Rah1 Ke7 27. Nf3 Rh8 28. Nh2 Qf8 29. Ng4 Re8 30. c4 {Since he
can't prevent the win of the h-Pawn I tidy up the QS first.} a5 31. Qh4 Kd8 32.
Nxh6 Rxh6 33. Rxh6 Bxh6 34. Qxh6 {[35']} Qg8 35. Bxg5 fxg5 36. Qxg5+ Kc7 37.
Be2 {He was actually in the process of putting his Rook en-prise on e7 when he
realised and decided to resign. The two passed Pawns win easily.} 1-0

