{1hr 30' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. g3 Bb4 4. Bg2 O-O 5. a3 Bxc3 6. bxc3
d6 7. Qb3 (7. Rb1 {is probably better leaving the Queen other options.}) 7...
Nc6 8. d3 Na5 9. Qa4 c6 10. Bg5 Bd7 {[11']} 11. e3 {[7']} c5 12. Bxf6 Bxa4 13.
Bxd8 Raxd8 14. Ne2 b6 15. Rb1 $4 {Horrific. I was playing too quickly and had
not wanted to play at all. To make matters worse I had considered his reply.}
Bc2 16. Kd2 {The alternative is to lose the d3 & c4 Pawns with an awkward
position.} Bxb1 17. Rxb1 Rd7 18. Kc2 Re7 19. Bd5 g6 20. Ng1 Kg7 21. Nh3 h6 22.
Kd2 g5 23. f3 {Clearly he wants to open up the position. I bide my time.} f5
24. Nf2 {Preventing .....g4 or .....e4 and ...f4 gives me e4 for my Knight.}
Nb7 25. Rg1 Nd8 26. Rg2 Ne6 27. Ke2 Nc7 28. Bc6 Ne8 29. e4 f4 (29... fxe4 30.
Nxe4 {gives me a good square for the Knight.}) 30. Bd5 Nf6 31. Rg1 fxg3 {
Now my Knight can go to e3 & f5.} 32. hxg3 Nh5 {This doesn't achieve anything.}
33. Ng4 Nf6 34. Ne3 Nxd5 35. cxd5 Rd7 36. Nf5+ Kg6 37. c4 Rxf5 {He gets the
extra Pawn but it doesn't count for mutch.} 38. exf5+ Kxf5 39. Rh1 Kg6 40. g4
Rf7 41. a4 Rf6 42. Ke3 Kg7 43. Rh5 1-0

