{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. a4 Bc5 6. c3
Nc6 7. Be3 Nf6 $4 {Horrific! With other things on my mind I was just going
through the motions. I realised as soon as I let go of the Knight.} 8. Nxc6 Qb6
9. Bxc5 Qxc5 10. Nd4 Nxe4 11. Bd3 Nf6 ({I briefly considered} 11... Nxf2 12.
Kxf2 e5 13. Re1 O-O {but} 14. b4 Qa7 15. Rxe5 {Kills it}) 12. Nd2 Qd5 13. N2f3
{My only hope is to mobilise my pieces quickly create some space and the
opportunity for some tactical play.} e5 14. Qe2 O-O 15. Nf5 Qc5 16. Be4 $2 {
Just asking for me to play 16......d5} d5 17. Bc2 g6 18. Ng3 Bg4 19. Qd2 Bxf3
20. gxf3 Rac8 21. Bd1 Rfd8 22. O-O Qc6 23. Qe2 Qd6 24. Re1 Qb6 {The e-Pawn is
immune.} 25. Qc2 Nd7 26. Qb3 Qc6 27. Qb4 Qf6 {Lol has a tendency to take hot
Pawns. I couldn't believe that he would take the b-Pawn but I thought I would
give him the chance.} 28. Qxb7 $4 {Incredible! This loses a whole Rook.} Nc5
29. Qb4 ({If} 29. Qa7 Rd7 {and the Queen is trapped.}) 29... Nd3 30. Qb3 Nxe1
31. Kf1 Nxf3 32. Bxf3 Qxf3 33. Qd1 $2 {It has to be best to keep the Queens on.
Also his Rook is now buried.} Qxd1+ 34. Rxd1 Rc4 35. Ra1 Rb8 36. Ra2 f5 37. Ke2
Kf7 38. Nf1 Ke6 39. Ne3 Rh4 40. Nf1 Rc8 41. Kd2 Rf4 42. Ke2 Rcc4 43. Ra3 {
White resigned before I could reply.} 0-1

