{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Bc4 d6 4. d3 Nf6 5. f4 e5 {Weakens
the White squares.} 6. f5 Be7 7. Be3 Nc6 8. Qd2 Bd7 9. O-O-O Na5 10. Nd5 $2
Nxc4 $2 ({As I played 10.Nd5? I suddenly realised he could play......} 10...
Nxe4 11. dxe4 Nxc4 12. Qc3 Nxe3 {and I can't play} 13. Qxe3 {because of} ({
So I have to play} 13. Nxe3 {and after} Bg5 14. Nf3 Bxe3+ 15. Qxe3 Bc6 {
and Black is on top. however, he missed all this.})) 11. Nxf6+ Bxf6 12. dxc4
Bc6 13. Qd3 Qc7 14. Ne2 a6 15. Nc3 O-O $5 {Dangerous.} (15... O-O-O $142) 16.
g4 Be7 17. h4 b5 18. g5 {Winning a Pawn is just too risky.} b4 (18... bxc4 {
Opening lines seems better.}) 19. Nd5 Bxd5 20. Qxd5 Rfd8 21. Rhg1 {[22']} g6 {
[30']} 22. f6 Bf8 23. h5 Kh8 24. Rh1 Ra7 $2 {Loses the c-Pawn.} 25. hxg6 fxg6
26. Bxc5 Rb7 27. Be3 Rc8 28. b3 a5 29. Kb1 Ra8 30. Rh2 Qf7 ({I was hoping for
something like.} 30... a4 31. Rdh1 axb3 32. Rxh7+ Qxh7 33. Rxh7+ Rxh7 34. Qxa8
{I now tryvarious things before sorting out the correct breakthrough.}) 31.
Rhd2 {[33']} Qc7 {[51'] He offered a draw here.} 32. Rh2 {Hoping that he still
may try 32......a4} Rd8 33. Rdh1 Rd7 34. Qe6 Rf7 35. Qe8 {Threat 36.Rxh7+} Rb8
36. Qe6 Rb7 37. Qd5 Rd7 38. Rd1 Rf7 39. Rhd2 Rd7 $2 {Allows an immediate
breakthrough.} 40. c5 Rd8 ({If} 40... Rb5 41. cxd6 Rxd5 42. dxc7 Rxd2 43. Rxd2
Rxc7 44. Bb6) 41. Qe6 Qd7 {He can't save the d-Pawn and will probably lose the
e-Pawn as well. However, now it is easy for White.} 42. Qxd7 Rbxd7 43. c6 (43.
cxd6 Bxd6 44. Bc5 {the text is easier}) 43... Rf7 44. c7 Ra8 45. Bb6 Rd7 46.
Bxa5 Rc8 47. Bxb4 Rcxc7 48. Bxd6 Bxd6 49. Rxd6 Rxd6 50. Rxd6 Rc8 51. Rd7 Rf8
52. a4 1-0

