{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Bd3 e5 6. dxe5 {
Still hopelessly rusty on openings I try to "play it safe". However, this
makes it relatively easy for Black.} dxe5 7. Nf3 Bg4 8. h3 Bxf3 9. Qxf3 Nc6 10.
O-O Nd4 11. Qd1 O-O 12. Bg5 Ne6 13. Bxf6 Bxf6 14. Nd5 c6 15. Nxf6+ Qxf6 16. Qe2
{After much thought. I wasn't happy with the position.} Rfd8 17. Rfd1 Rd4 {
[14']} 18. Qe3 $2 {[51'] This seems wrong. I need to keep the Knight out of f4
so g3 seems best. After the text the Bishop will become pinned.} (18. g3 $142)
18... Rad8 {[15']} 19. f3 $2 {[58'] This definately seals it.} (19. g3 {
now allows} Ng5) 19... Nf4 {Bishop moves 20........Qg5 threatens mate on g2
and the Queen has nowhere to go.} 0-1

