{Played without clocks.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Nf3 Nc6 6.
Bd3 Bc5 7. O-O Nge7 8. c3 d5 9. b4 Bd6 10. Nbd2 O-O 11. Nb3 b5 12. a4 bxa4 13.
Rxa4 Qb6 14. Be3 Qc7 15. g3 dxe4 16. Bxe4 Bb7 17. Qc2 g6 18. Bd2 Rfd8 19. Re1
f5 20. Bxc6 ({I was expecting something like} 20. Bd3 Nxb4 21. cxb4 Qxc2 22.
Bxc2 Bxf3 23. Rxe6 Bd5 24. Re1 Rac8) 20... Bxc6 21. Nbd4 Bxa4 22. Qxa4 Qd7 23.
Qb3 Bb8 24. Nxe6 Qd5 25. Ned4 ({I had expected} 25. c4 Qd3 26. Qa4 {when I may
have nothing better than.} Qd7) 25... Qxb3 26. Nxb3 Bd6 27. c4 Nc6 28. c5 Bf8
29. Re6 Rxd2 {The most active.} (29... Rac8 {Hands the initiative to White})
30. Nfxd2 Nxb4 31. c6 Rc8 32. Nd4 Bc5 33. N2b3 Bxd4 34. Nxd4 Kf7 {Her c-Pawn
is a weakness and ties down his pieces.} 35. Rd6 Rc7 36. Kf1 a5 $2 {This trows
it away.} (36... Ke7 $142 37. Re6+ Kd8 38. Rf6 ({If} 38. Ke1 Re7 {forces the
Rooks off and wins the c-Pawn.}) 38... Re7 {blocks off the White King} 39. Z0
Kc7 {looks good fo Black.}) 37. Ke2 a4 38. Kd2 a3 39. Rd7+ Rxd7 40. cxd7 Ke7
41. d8=Q+ Kxd8 42. Kc3 a2 43. Nb3 Nd5+ 44. Kb2 Nf6 45. f3 a1=Q+ 46. Kxa1 Nd5
47. Kb2 Ke7 {Galina is from Ukraine} 1/2-1/2

