{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Bc5 4. d3 {In the Cornish style
i.e. rather passive blocking in the King Bishop.} (4. Nxe5 {is not the sort of
line he likes.}) 4... d6 5. h3 h6 6. Be2 f5 {Seizing the initiative.} 7. Be3
Nf6 {after some thought.} (7... Bxe3 8. fxe3 fxe4 9. Nxe4 d5 {also looks good.}
) 8. Bxc5 dxc5 9. Qd2 f4 {Constricting him} 10. O-O-O Be6 11. g3 g5 12. gxf4
gxf4 13. Rdg1 {Interestingly, the g-file plays little part in subsequent
proceedings.} Qe7 14. Ne1 {In order to swop off his Bishop.} ({I had expected} 
14. Rg6 O-O-O 15. Nh4) (14. Nh4 Nxe4 {is risky}) 14... O-O-O 15. Bg4 Rhg8 16.
Bxe6+ Qxe6 17. Nf3 Nd4 18. Qd1 ({If} 18. Nxd4 Rxg1+ 19. Rxg1 cxd4 20. Nd1 Qxh3)
18... Rxg1 19. Nxg1 b5 20. Kb1 b4 21. Nce2 Nb5 22. Nf3 $2 {Missing the reply}
Nxe4 23. Qf1 {Again after some thought.} Nf6 ({If} 23... Ng5 24. Nxg5 hxg5 25.
Qg2 {threatens the g-Pawn and at some time Qa8+. If then} Rg8 26. Rg1 {
threatens 27.h4}) 24. Nd2 e4 25. Nc1 ({The alternative was} 25. Nxf4) 25...
exd3 26. Nxd3 {Loses a piece.} ({If} 26. cxd3 c4 {he can't play} 27. dxc4 Rxd2
28. cxb5 {because of} Qe4+ 29. Ka1 Qc2) 26... c4 27. Nxf4 Qf5 28. Qxc4 Rxd2 29.
Qxb4 Qxc2+ 30. Ka1 Rd1+ 0-1

