{30' each/game} 1. d4 f5 2. g4 {Somewhere in the back of my mind I could
rmember this - but none of the variations. Colin has played it a number of
times.} fxg4 3. h3 d6 4. Qd3 Nf6 5. Bg2 {Is this best?} (5. e4 Z0 6. e5) (5.
Bg5) 5... c6 6. hxg4 Bxg4 7. Nf3 Qd7 8. Ng5 Bf5 9. e4 Bg6 10. Bh3 Qc7 11. Ne6 {
This looks good but he can't sustain a piece here and to some extent it gets
in the way. Also his e-Pawn is under attack and in 2 moves his b-Pawn.} Qa5+
12. Bd2 Qb6 13. f3 Qxb2 14. Bc3 Qc1+ 15. Qd1 Qxd1+ 16. Kxd1 Na6 {I felt that I
was now a solid 2 Pawns up and can shift the piece on e6.} 17. Na3 ({If} 17.
Bf1 {simply} Bf7) 17... Bf7 18. Rb1 Bxe6 19. Bxe6 Nc7 20. Bh3 b6 21. Bd2 Kf7
22. Bd7 $4 {Being blind and playing on a braile set, Colin has to tell me his
moves. Here, I queried his move but he resignedly repeated.........Bd7, having
realised his mistake.Easy to make in a quick game, especially for an unsighted
player.} Nxd7 0-1

