{30' each/game} 1. c4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 c5 4. d5 d6 5. e4 Nd7 6. f4 Nh6 7.
Bd3 O-O 8. Nge2 a6 9. O-O f5 10. Ng3 fxe4 11. Ngxe4 Nf5 12. a4 Nf6 13. Ra3 Nd4
14. h3 Nh5 15. Ng5 {Threat 16.Nxh7} Ng3 16. Re1 Ngf5 17. Ne2 Nxe2+ 18. Rxe2 Nd4
{The 8th consecutive Knight move.} 19. Re1 {[12']} Re8 {[25'] Black has only
5' left. I only need to sit tight to win on time.} 20. Kh1 e5 21. Be4 {Playing
it quickly (so as to hurry him) and just holiding it together to minimise his
play. The text allows the a3 Rook access to the KS.} ({I was considering
something like} 21. Nxh7 Kxh7 22. Qh5+ Kg8 23. Bxg6 Re7 24. f5 {Threatening 25.
Bg5. However, I wasn't willing to spend time working all this out.}) 21... Bf5
22. Rae3 $4 {Again played very (too) quickly. As I let go of the Rook I
realised the f-pawn was loose.} exf4 23. Bxf5 {Pretty well forced.} Rxe3 24.
Rxe3 {This has all gone horribly wrong. However, Black was desperately short
of time so I was still fairly confident.} fxe3 25. Be6+ Nxe6 26. Nxe6 Qf6 27.
Bxe3 {The rest was at "high speed" Black had very little time. I had ~15' but
didn't want to give him time to think.} Qxb2 28. Qg4 {I must prevent 28......
Qa1 forcing the Queens off.} b5 29. cxb5 axb5 30. Nxg7 Qxg7 31. axb5 Ra1+ {
Better to leave the Rook on the back rank. The check achieves nothing.} 32. Kh2
Qe5+ 33. Bf4 Qxd5 (33... Qe1 {Might offer hpe of a perpetual check.}) 34. Qc8+
Kg7 35. Qd7+ Qf7 $2 ({After} 35... Kg8 {it is a draw. However, Black had to
move instantaneously. Now it is probably still probably a draw but he would
have to find the moves instantaneously.}) 36. Bh6+ {Blacks flag fell.} (36.
Bh6+ Kg8 $4 (36... Kf6 37. Qxd6+ Kf5 ({Not} 37... Qe6 38. Bg7+) 38. Qxc5+ Ke6 {
is probably a draw. Black has to be careful.e.g.} 39. Qc6+ Ke5 $2 (39... Kf5 $2
40. g4+ Ke5 41. Qc3+) (39... Ke7 40. Bg5+ Kf8 41. Qd6+ Kg8 {is a draw}) 40.
Qc3+) 37. Qd8+ Qf8 38. Qxf8#) 1-0

