{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bd3 {Presumably for surprise value in
this quick game. However, the plan of c3,Bc2,d4 is too slow and he never
manages to play d4.} e5 4. c3 Nf6 5. Bc2 d5 6. exd5 Qxd5 7. O-O Bg4 8. Ba4 $2 {
Loses a piece.} e4 9. Re1 O-O-O 10. Bxc6 (10. h3 Bh5 11. g4 exf3 12. gxh5 Qg5+
13. Kh1 Qg2#) 10... Qxc6 $2 {Played instantly and without thought.} 11. Ne5
Bxd1 {I felt my control of the d-file and the difficulty White will have
developing the QS might mean that I was still winning.} 12. Nxc6 Rd3 $2 {
Unnecessarily giving away a pawn.} (12... bxc6 $142) 13. Nxa7+ Kb8 14. Nc6+
bxc6 15. Rxd1 Nd5 {White is a Pawn up and a passed pawn but is in a terrible
tangle.} 16. Na3 Be7 17. Nc2 Nb6 18. b3 Rhd8 19. Ne1 R3d7 20. a4 Bf6 21. Bb2 {
Something had to go.} ({If} 21. a5 Bxc3) 21... Rxd2 22. Rxd2 Rxd2 23. Rb1 Nd5
24. Kf1 Nxc3 25. Bxc3 Bxc3 26. Rc1 Bd4 27. Rc2 Rd1 28. Ke2 Rb1 29. f3 Rxb3 30.
fxe4 Re3+ 31. Kd1 Rxe4 32. Nf3 h6 33. a5 Kb7 34. Nd2 Rf4 35. Nb3 Rf1+ 36. Kd2
Rf2+ 37. Kd1 Rxc2 38. Kxc2 Bg1 39. h3 Ka6 40. Kd3 Kb5 41. a6 Kxa6 42. Kc4 Kb6
43. Nd2 Kc7 44. Nf3 Be3 45. g4 Kd6 46. Nh4 g6 47. Nf3 Ke6 48. Kd3 Bf2 49. Kc4
h5 50. gxh5 gxh5 51. Ng5+ Kf5 52. Nxf7 Kf4 53. Nh6 Kg3 54. Nf5+ Kxh3 55. Ng7 h4
56. Nf5 Kg4 57. Nh6+ Kf4 0-1

