{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. g3 c5 4. Bg2 d5 5. c3 Nc6 6. Bg5 h6 7.
Bf4 Bd6 8. Qd2 b6 9. O-O Bb7 10. Re1 cxd4 11. Bxd6 $2 {Loses a Pawn.} dxc3 12.
Nxc3 Qxd6 13. Nb5 Qe7 14. Rac1 O-O 15. Nfd4 Rfc8 16. Nc3 Qb4 17. Ndb5 a6 18. a3
Qe7 19. Nd4 b5 20. Bh3 Nxd4 {Now I get control of the c-file} 21. Qxd4 Rc4 22.
Qd2 Rac8 23. Bg2 b4 24. Nb1 a5 25. a4 Qc5 26. Rxc4 Qxc4 27. Rd1 Qc2 28. Qxc2
Rxc2 29. b3 Ba6 30. Bf3 Nd7 31. e4 Nf6 32. exd5 exd5 33. Kg2 Rb2 34. Nd2 Bb7
35. h4 Kf8 {White was now very short of time and rushing. I had 7'10''.
Foolishly I was moving fast so as not to give him time to think. With both
pkayers rushing it is equally likely either will make a mistake.} 36. g4 Ke7
37. Re1+ Kd7 38. Rd1 Kd6 $4 {And here is the mistake. I realised as I let go
of the piece. fortunately he was moving like lightning and deciding his moves
before I made mine, so I get away with it.} 39. Kg3 $4 Ke7 40. Re1+ Kf8 41. Rd1
Nd7 42. Kg2 Ne5 43. Kg3 Rc2 44. Kf4 {Rather surprising. Having to make an
instant move,he follows a series of "safe" moves with a King sortie.} f6 {
A quick "safe move by me.} ({I didn't have time to think about} 44... Nd3+ 45.
Ke3 Rc3 {etc}) 45. h5 Rc3 {Threatening to win a piece. he doesn't have time to
see it.} 46. Kg3 $2 (46. Be2 {Would save the piece but his King is left in a
dangerous position.}) 46... Nxf3 47. Nxf3 d4 48. Kg2 ({He only had seconds
left.} 48. Rxd4 Rxf3+ {is not much better for White.}) 48... Bxf3+ 49. Kf1 Bxd1
50. f4 Re3 51. g5 Bxh5 52. gxf6 gxf6 53. f5 Re2 54. Kg1 d3 0-1

