{2hr each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Bc5 {To get him out of the main lines as I
could remember nothing about the vienna.} 3. Bc4 d6 4. d3 Be6 {[9']} 5. Nf3
Bxc4 6. dxc4 h6 7. Qe2 Nf6 8. Bd2 a6 9. Rd1 Nc6 10. Na4 Qe7 ({If} 10... Ba7 11.
c5 {and my d-Pawn is effectively pinned.}) 11. O-O {[30']} Ba7 {[34']} 12. Kh1
O-O 13. b4 Qe8 14. Nb2 {[37']} Qe6 {[51']} 15. h3 {[40']} Rfb8 {[59'] I
thought about 15......b5 immediately but it isn't sound.} (15... b5) 16. Nh4 {
[49']} Nd4 {[62']} 17. Qd3 Nh5 {[1hr 12']} 18. Nf5 {[64']} Kh7 {[1hr 15']} 19.
f4 $2 {[68'] This leads him into all sorts of problems.} ({Correct is} 19. Kh2)
19... Nxf5 {He looked pleased about this presumably on account of. 20.exf5 Qd7
21.g4 etc.} 20. exf5 e4 $1 {[1hr 21'] Now he saw why he would have been better
with his King on h2. The White Queen, if it moves, must protect g3.} (20... Qd7
21. g4) 21. fxe6 {[1hr 24']} ({If} 21. Qc3 Qf6) (21. Qa3 Qe7 {threatens} 22. Z0
e3) 21... exd3 22. Kh2 dxc2 23. Rde1 ({If} 23. Rc1 fxe6 {and Black is a Pawn
up in a solid position. White decides that the c2 Pawn won't run away and goes
for control of the e-file.}) 23... fxe6 24. Rxe6 Re8 25. Rfe1 Rxe6 26. Rxe6 b5
{5 vs 3 on the QS.} 27. f5 Bd4 {Now he's in trouble and realises he should
have gone for the c-Pawn.} 28. Bc1 {[1hr 34']} Be5+ {[1hr 32']} 29. Rxe5 {
Desperation faced with the Knight manouevre f4-e2} dxe5 30. Nd3 Nf4 31. Nxe5 {
[1hr 43']} Ne2 {[1hr 34']} 32. Bd2 Rd8 0-1

