{2hr each/game} 1. c4 f5 2. d4 e6 3. g3 Nf6 4. Bg2 Bb4+ 5. Nc3 O-O 6. Qb3 Nc6
7. e3 Ne4 8. Nge2 Bxc3+ 9. bxc3 $5 {leads to problems with the c4 Pawn.} d6 10.
Qc2 Na5 {After much thought.} 11. Bxe4 ({If} 11. Qd3 {then} b6 12. Z0 Ba6)
11... fxe4 12. Qxe4 Qf6 13. O-O Nxc4 14. f4 {[51'] Pushing for a bit of room
round the King.} Rb8 {[38']} 15. Qd3 b5 16. a4 {[69'] To get some play.} a6 {
[41']} 17. axb5 axb5 18. Ba3 Ra8 19. Bb4 Bb7 20. Rxa8 Rxa8 {[44']} 21. e4 {
[1hr 28'] Trying to block out the Bishop but I wasn't happy.} Ra2 22. Re1 {
[1hr 38']} Qg6 23. Nc1 Rd2 {[60']} 24. Qf3 {[1hr 50'] 10' left.} Qe8 {[1hr 11']
} 25. Nb3 {Moving fast now.} Rb2 26. Na5 {[1hr 52']} Nd2 27. Qe3 Ba8 $5 28. c4
$5 Qh5 $2 {I expected 28......Bxe4 which is still threatened and I wondered if
27.......Ba8 meant that Black was going to mark timewhilst I lost on time, so
desperate measures are needed.} ({If} 28... Bxe4 29. Rd1 Nf3+ 30. Kf1 Nxh2+ 31.
Kg1 Nf3+ 32. Kf1 Ba8 $19) 29. Bxd2 {The horror scenario was that I, a piece up,
would not have time to win.} b4 30. d5 {Blocking the diagonal at last.} Qe8 31.
Nb3 Qa4 32. Nd4 Qa2 33. Nf3 {All my moves were in a rush now.} Rb3 34. Qf2 Rd3
35. Bxb4 $5 Qb3 $5 {Played instantaneously but 35........Qxf2+ would leave me
about 2' to win the endgame, probably not possible as he could sacrifice
pieces for promoted Pawns to use up time.} 36. Qa7 $1 {[1hr 58'] The only hope
i have to play for mate. I didn't have time to think about it.} Rxf3 37. Qxa8+
Kf7 38. dxe6+ Kxe6 ({If he had played} 38... Kf6 {I would have played} 39. e5+
{to interpose with the Queen after taking the Rook. However this was
unnecessary as I could have transposed into the game line.} (39. Qf8+ Kxe6 {
then he would be threatening 40.......Rxg3+ with perpetual.})) 39. Qe8+ Kf6 40.
e5+ Kf5 41. Qf7+ Kg4 42. Qe6+ Kh5 43. Qf5+ 1-0

