{2hr each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 {I hadn't
played the Dragon for over 30 years and could remember very little about it.
He was playing his moves very quickly so clearly I was going to be in trouble.}
6. Be3 Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 Nc6 9. Bc4 Bd7 10. O-O-O a6 {The first departure
from the Soltis line of the Yugoslav Attack.} ({Usual is} 10... Rc8) 11. h4 b5
$2 {[4'] My lack of knowledge of the variation becomes potentially fatal. I
considered 11.......h5 but only briefly.} 12. Bb3 {[3']} Na5 $2 {I could still
play ......h5} 13. Bh6 Nc4 14. Bxc4 bxc4 15. h5 {Now I'm in trouble.} Qb6 $2 (
15... Qa5 {is better as becomes apparent on move 19.}) 16. hxg6 fxg6 17. Bxg7
Kxg7 18. Qh6+ Kf7 19. Nd5 Qa5 20. Nxf6 Kxf6 21. g4 Rf7 22. Qf4+ Kg7 23. Rxh7+
Kxh7 24. Qxf7+ Kh6 25. Rh1+ Kg5 26. Ne2 {It was apparent from this
tournamentthat my ancient memories of opening theory need serious updating. I
had opening problems in all my games.} 1-0

