{Time limit 40 moves in 2hr then 30' for the rest} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 c5
4. Ngf3 {I couldn't remember much about the Tarrasch.} (4. exd5 {Is more
common.}) 4... Nc6 5. Bb5 cxd4 6. Nxd4 {[14']} Bd7 {[16']} 7. N4b3 Nf6 8. Qe2 {
[23']} Qb6 {[33']} 9. Bxc6 {[35']} Bxc6 10. e5 Ne4 11. f3 Nxd2 12. Bxd2 {[44']}
(12. Bxd2 Bb5 {I didn't like my position.e.g.} 13. Qf2 Qxf2+ 14. Kxf2 b6 {
and he is stronger on the c-file so I accepted.}) 12... Bb5 {[45'] Here he
offered a draw. On the other boards we were level on two and better on two. WE
won (on board count for the 4th match in a row). We won £200 and the trophy
for a year plus individual trophies. 1.R.A.C.-------0.5 2.A.Fawcett---1 3.C.
Fisher ----0.5 4.W.Fairbairn 0.5 5.B.Standen --0 The match was played at
Queniborough, near Leicester.} 1/2-1/2

