{1hr ' each/game} 1. e4 d6 2. d4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. Bc4 Nf6 5. Be3 e5 $2 {
Playing his first game for a While, Walter blunders before he has really got
going.} 6. dxe5 dxe5 7. Qxd8+ Kxd8 8. Bxf7 Ke7 9. Bb3 Nc6 10. Bc5+ Ke8 11. Nf3
(11. Nb5 Nxe4 12. Ba3 Kd8 13. Rd1+ Bd7 14. Bd5 a6 ({but} 14... Nf6 {Might be O.
K. for Black}) 15. Nxc7 {is O.K.}) 11... b6 (11... Ng4) 12. Ba3 Bf8 13. Ba4 Bd7
14. Bxf8 Rxf8 15. Bxc6 Bxc6 16. Nxe5 Bxe4 17. Nxe4 Nxe4 {[16']} 18. f3 {[17']}
Rf5 19. Nc6 Rc5 {Black tries to get some play for his Rook but it ends up
offside.} 20. Nd4 Nf6 21. O-O-O Kf7 22. Rhe1 Re8 23. Rxe8 Nxe8 {[21']} 24. f4 {
[25'] White's advantage is not so much the extra Pawn as a better Rook and
Knight.} Rc4 25. g3 Nd6 26. c3 Rc5 {The Rook could have got trapped after Kc2
& b4.} 27. Nf3 Kf6 28. Rd2 Ne4 29. Rd3 ({If} 29. Rd7 Nxc3) 29... Kf5 30. Ne5
Nf2 31. Rd7 h5 32. Rf7+ {[52']} Ke6 {[43']} 33. Rg7 Nh3 {Doesn't achieve much.}
({but} 33... Kf5 34. Rxg6 Rxe5 35. Rg5+ Kf6 36. Rxe5 Nd3+ 37. Kd2 Nxe5 38.
fxe5+ Kxe5 39. Ke3 $18) 34. Rxg6+ Kf5 35. Rh6 1-0

