{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs then 30' for the rest} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3
d6 4. d4 Be7 5. d5 Nb8 6. Bd3 {To prevent 6......f5} Nf6 7. h3 O-O {[6']} 8. c4
{[5']} Nbd7 9. Nc3 Nc5 10. Be3 Nxd3+ 11. Qxd3 Bd7 12. O-O (12. g4 {is maybe
better}) 12... Ne8 13. g4 {To prevent 13......f5} h5 14. Nh2 {[17']} g5 {
Active play by Black.} 15. Rfc1 {Vacating f1 for the Knight and, if Black
blocks the position with ......h4, preparing for QS play.} hxg4 16. hxg4 Kg7
17. f3 Rh8 18. Nf1 {[29']} Nf6 {[47']} 19. Ng3 {[36']} (19. Bxg5 {Seemed too
risky e.g.} Bxg4 20. fxg4 Nxg4 21. Bxe7 Qxe7 22. Qg3 Rag8 $3) 19... Nh7 {[62']}
20. Kg2 Nf8 21. Rh1 Ng6 22. Rxh8 Qxh8 23. Rh1 Nh4+ {This leaves the Knight
pinned and rather stranded.} 24. Kf2 Qh6 25. Qd2 Kg8 {Giving him the option of
playing ......Qf6 without the Knight fork.} 26. Nf5 Bxf5 27. exf5 a6 28. f6 $2
{Ridiculous.} ({After} 28. Ne4 {White is well on top. Black's Knight is
stranded and Whitw can begin operations on the QS.}) 28... Qxf6 ({I got
carried away with lines like} 28... Bxf6 29. Ne4 Be7 30. Nxg5 {etc. I
completely overlooked the fact that 28......Qf6 threatens f3!}) 29. Rh3 Qg6 30.
Ne4 f6 31. b4 b5 32. c5 Rc8 ({and not} 32... dxc5 $4 33. d6) 33. Rh1 {[1hr 16']
} Rf8 {[1hr 37'] Threatening 34......f5 which looks very good for Black. I was
initially stuck for an adequate response.} 34. Rg1 $1 {Much the best, aiming
at his weakness on g5} Qh6 35. Rh1 Qg6 36. Rg1 {Lancaster won 3-1 R.A.C.
-------- 0.5 A.Fawcett--- 0.5 B.Cornish -----1 B.Standen ----1 Creda are from
Stoke} 1/2-1/2

