{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 e6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. g3 g6 5. Bg2 Bg7 6. O-O
Nge7 7. d3 d5 8. e5 Nf5 9. Nc3 Bd7 10. Qe1 Ncd4 11. Qf2 Nxf3+ 12. Bxf3 Nd4 13.
Bd1 b6 14. h4 h5 15. Be3 Nf5 16. d4 cxd4 {I was quite relieved about this.} ({
I knew that he would be playing for a draw and I was worried about} 16... Nxe3
17. Qxe3 c4 {when I would be struggling to create chances.}) 17. Bxd4 Nxd4 18.
Qxd4 Bf8 19. Kh2 Bc5 20. Qd2 Qe7 21. Be2 {[19']} Bb4 {[23']} 22. Qd3 Bxc3 23.
Qxc3 Rc8 24. Qd2 Qc5 25. c3 Bb5 {He offered a draw here. I felt that I was
slightly worse but hoped that he might go wrong if he assumed that it was
"Dead Drawn".} 26. Rad1 Bxe2 27. Qxe2 O-O $2 {And here is the error.} (27...
Ke7 $142) 28. g4 Qe7 29. Kg3 {Defending the h-Pawn and half opening the h-file
for a Rook.} hxg4 30. Qxg4 {I now felt that I would win.} Rc4 {This serves no
purpose.} 31. Rh1 Kg7 32. h5 Rh8 33. hxg6 fxg6 (33... Rxh1 34. gxf7+ {is no
better.}) 34. Rxh8 Kxh8 35. Qxg6 Qg7 36. Qxg7+ Kxg7 37. Rd4 Rc7 (37... Rxd4 {
is a clear loss.}) 38. f5 exf5 39. Rxd5 1-0

