{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O b5 6. Bb3
Be7 7. Re1 O-O 8. h3 {Not happy about facing the Marshall.} d6 9. c3 Na5 10.
Bc2 c5 11. d4 cxd4 12. cxd4 Qc7 13. d5 h6 14. Bd2 Nc4 15. b3 Nxd2 16. Nbxd2 {
[7']} Bb7 {[14']} 17. Rc1 Qd7 18. Nf1 Nh7 {Intending ......f5} 19. g4 {[11']
The riskiest option. Alternatives were.} (19. Qd3) (19. Ne3) (19. Ng3 {The
text leaves black square weaknesses.}) 19... Ng5 20. Kg2 Nxf3 21. Qxf3 Rac8 22.
Bd3 Bg5 23. Ne3 {[17']} Bf4 {[24']} 24. Qe2 Qe7 25. Nf5 Qf6 ({Not} 25... Qg5 $2
26. h4) 26. Ne3 Qg5 {Aggresive but he is deseerting the QS.} 27. a4 bxa4 28.
bxa4 a5 29. Rxc8 Rxc8 30. Nf5 Qf6 31. Ba6 Bxa6 32. Qxa6 Rd8 33. Qxa5 g6 34. Ne3
h5 35. Qc3 Qg5 36. f3 Kg7 37. Nf1 Rh8 38. Qd3 Qh4 39. Rb1 hxg4 40. fxg4 Qg5 41.
a5 Ra8 42. a6 Qd8 43. Ra1 Qb6 44. Ra2 Qc5 {[67']} 45. Nh2 {[1hr 11']} Qc1 {
[1hr 12']} 46. Nf3 Qc5 47. Ne1 Qc1 48. Qe2 Qc3 49. Nd3 Bg5 50. Nb2 Bf4 51. Nc4
$4 {After my careful manoeuvering I start to move fast as the time gets short 
(we were both short of time) 51.Nc4?? loses.} ({Correct is} 51. Qd3) 51... Qg3+
52. Kf1 Qxh3+ 53. Qg2 Qd3+ 54. Qe2 {Here he offered a draw which I immediately
accepted as I suspected that it is lost.} (54. Qe2 {Black can win by} Qb1+ 55.
Kf2 Rh8 56. Ne3 Rh2+ 57. Ng2 Qh1 58. Kf3 Rh3+ 59. Kf2 Bg3+ 60. Kf3 Be1# {
Whether he could find this in the time left is another matter. However, in the
line above 56......Bxe3 also wins and this is easier to find. A lucky escape! 
[Arnside only played 5 games in this season all double pointers]}) 1/2-1/2

