{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 d5 4. Qa4 Qd6 5. exd5 ({Harding's
book gives} 5. d4) 5... Qxd5 6. Bc4 Qd6 ({If} 6... Qe4+ 7. Kd1 {Theatening
both 8.Bxf7+ and 8.Re1}) 7. O-O Be7 8. d4 Bd7 $2 {Black is in a difficult
opening for a quickplay game where one isn't familiar with the opening. 8......
..Bd7 makes life awkward for him.} 9. Qb3 Na5 ({If} 9... exd4 10. Bxf7+ Kf8 11.
Bxg8 Rxg8 12. Nxd4 Nxd4 13. cxd4 Qxd4 14. Qxb7 {is good for White.}) 10. Bxf7+
Kf8 11. Qd5 Qxd5 12. Bxd5 exd4 13. Nxd4 Nf6 14. Ne6+ Bxe6 15. Bxe6 Nc6 {[17']}
16. Bf4 {[6']} Nd8 17. Bb3 c6 18. Nd2 Nf7 19. Nf3 Bd6 20. Bxd6+ Nxd6 21. Rad1
Nf7 22. Nd4 Nd8 23. Rfe1 a5 $5 {With not much time left he decides to lash out
down his QS. However, he surely has to activate his King Rook e.g. 23......h5}
(23... h5) 24. a4 b5 $5 25. axb5 cxb5 26. Nxb5 Rb8 27. f3 {As the Knight is
immune I prevent back rank problems and take e4 and g4 away from the Black
Knight.} Nf7 28. Bxf7 Kxf7 29. c4 Kg6 30. b3 Rhe8 {It looks better to keep
both Rooks on.} 31. Rxe8 Rxe8 32. Kf2 Rc8 33. g4 Ra8 34. Kg3 a4 35. bxa4 Rxa4
36. Rc1 Rb4 37. Nd6 Nd7 38. Rc3 Nc5 39. h4 Na4 40. Rc2 1-0

