{1r 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. f4 d5 4. e5 Nc6 5. Nf3 Nh6 6. d3 Be7
7. g3 {7.a4 which I considered may be prefferable.} b5 8. Bg2 b4 9. Ne2 O-O 10.
O-O Bb7 11. h3 Nf5 12. g4 Nh4 13. Nxh4 Bxh4 {I was hoping that this Bishop
would simply be left out of play.} 14. Kh2 {As it turns out 14.Kh1 would be
better.} (14. Kh1 $142) 14... f6 15. d4 fxe5 16. dxe5 {The problem here is
that the e-Pawn is weak if he can undermine it with ......g5} Ne7 17. c3 bxc3
18. bxc3 Qc7 19. Qc2 {In view of what follows, possibly 19.g5 (ugly though it
looks) would be best, threatening the Knight manouevre g1-f3 or Qh5.} (19. g5
$142 Z0 20. Ng1 Z0 21. Nf3 (21. Qh5)) 19... Rad8 20. Rb1 {My other problem is
that ......Ba6 is threatened. I considered 20.Qa4 which may be best.} (20. Qa4
$142) 20... Ba6 21. Rf3 {I wasn't happy about this especially as ......g5 was
coming.} g5 22. Kh1 Ng6 {I felt that I might be lost now.} 23. Be3 {To bring
the other Rook to the f-file should I get the chance.} Bxe2 24. Qxe2 gxf4 25.
Bd2 Rb8 26. Rff1 Rxb1 27. Rxb1 Rb8 28. Rxb8+ Qxb8 29. Qa6 {I have to try to
get some play.} Qb6 30. Qc8+ Kf7 31. Qd7+ Be7 32. Bxd5 {I felt that this was
my only chance.} exd5 33. Qf5+ Kg7 34. e6 Bf6 35. Bxf4 $5 ({The last few moves
were played in a rush and I missed} 35. g5 Qd8 36. gxf6+ Qxf6 37. Qxd5 Qe7 {
which looks O.K. for White.}) 35... Nxf4 36. g5 Qxe6 37. gxf6+ Qxf6 38. Qg4+
Kh6 39. Qf3 Qg5 {Now he can play ......Qg2+ leaving him an easily won endgame.
However, he only had about 1' left whereaa I had about 10', so I played on
quickly. The game lasted another 2' during which 61 individual moves were made.
} 40. Kh2 Qg2+ 41. Qxg2 Nxg2 42. Kxg2 Kg5 43. Kg3 h5 44. Kf3 d4 45. cxd4 cxd4
46. Ke4 Kh4 47. Kxd4 Kxh3 48. Kc5 Kg3 49. Kc6 h4 50. Kb7 a5 $2 {A mistake
because pushing the a-Pawn serves no purpose but uses up his time.} 51. Kb6 a4
52. Kb5 a3 53. Kb4 h3 54. Kxa3 h2 55. Kb4 h1=Q 56. a4 Qa8 57. Kb5 Kf4 58. a5
Ke5 59. Kb6 Kd6 60. a6 Kd7 61. Kb5 Kc7 62. Ka5 Kc6 63. Kb4 Qxa6 64. Kc3 Qa4 65.
Kd3 Kd5 66. Ke3 Ke5 67. Kd3 Qb3+ 68. Kd2 Ke4 69. Ke2 Qb2+ 70. Kd1 {At this
point I noticed his flag had fallen. As I have only a King it is a draw. He
can mate in 2 if he hadn't wasted moves pushing the a-Pawn he would have won.}
1/2-1/2

