[WhiteTeamCountry "ENG"]
[BlackTeamCountry "ENG"]

{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 e6 2. Nf3 d5 3. e3 c5 4. b3 Nc6 5. Bb2 Nf6 6. Bd3 Bd6
7. O-O O-O 8. Nbd2 b6 9. Ne5 Bb7 10. f4 Nb4 11. Be2 Rc8 12. c3 Nc6 13. Ndf3 Ne4
14. Nxc6 Bxc6 15. Ne5 Bb7 16. Bd3 f5 {I wasn't particularly happy with all
this.} 17. Nf3 ({If} 17. Rc1 cxd4 18. cxd4 {The position would be completely
symetrical (with Black to move)}) 17... Qe7 18. Rc1 c4 19. Bxe4 fxe4 20. Ng5 {
he has thoughts of a KS attack so keeps the Knight on that side.} h6 21. Nh3
Ba6 22. b4 Bb7 23. Rc2 Bc6 24. Rcf2 Bd7 25. Qh5 {Probably intending g4 - but
not possible as the Queen is short of squares.} Qf7 26. Qh4 Be7 27. Qg3 $2 {
Missing the threat.} Qh5 {Now he had a long think - although he has little
choice in his next move.} 28. f5 Bh4 29. Nf4 {This was a surprise.} ({I had
expected} 29. Qd6 {and something like} Bxf2+ 30. Rxf2 Qe8 31. Nf4 ({He has
toplay} 31. Qg3 {and after} Rxf5 {Black is the exchange and a Pawn up.}) 31...
Rc6 32. Qe5 Rxf5 $19) 29... Bxg3 30. Nxh5 Bxf2+ 31. Rxf2 Rxf5 32. Nf4 g5 33.
Ng6 Kg7 34. Rxf5 exf5 {Move 34 and I have 8 Pawns on 8 files still.} 35. Ne7 {
Appears to win a Pawn but leaves the Knight with problems.} (35. Ne5 $142)
35... Re8 36. Nxd5 Bc6 37. Nc7 Re7 {Now his Knight will be lost on a6 so he
decides to give the Pawn back.} 38. b5 Rxc7 39. bxc6 Rxc6 40. Ba3 Kf7 41. g3
Ke6 42. Bf8 Kd5 43. a3 h5 44. Be7 Rg6 45. Kf2 Ke6 46. Bb4 h4 47. gxh4 {making
it easy for Black.} ({If} 47. Bf8 hxg3+ 48. Kxg3 Rg8 49. Bh6 ({If} 49. Bb4 a5)
49... Kf6 {Wins the Bishop}) ({He has to play.} 47. Kg2 {Black then puts the
Rook on h7 (after exchanging Pawns and marches the King through the QS on the
white squares)}) 47... gxh4 48. a4 h3 49. a5 Rg2+ 50. Kf1 Rxh2 51. axb6 axb6
52. Bf8 Rc2 53. Kg1 Rxc3 54. Bg7 Rxe3 ({54.Be7 is not really a trap! Even if} 
54... b5 55. d5+ Kxd5 56. Bxc3 {Black still wins.}) 0-1

