{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 b6 2. e4 Bb7 3. Nc3 e6 4. Nf3 d5 $5 {Not good.} (4...
Bb4 $142) 5. exd5 Bxd5 $5 (5... exd5 {is better even though the long diagonal
is blocked.}) 6. Nxd5 Qxd5 {After this I end up behind in development and with
my back to the wall.} ({Again} 6... exd5 {seems better}) 7. Bd3 Nf6 8. O-O Be7
9. Re1 c6 {Concerned about c4 and d5.} 10. c4 Qd8 11. Bg5 Nbd7 12. Qc2 h6 13.
Bh4 O-O 14. Rad1 Rc8 15. a3 Nh5 16. Bxe7 Qxe7 17. g3 Nhf6 18. Qe2 Rfd8 19. Ne5
Qd6 20. Bc2 Qc7 21. b4 {[65']} (21. Nxf7 {Doesn't work.}) 21... c5 {[40']} 22.
Nxd7 Rxd7 23. dxc5 Rxd1 24. Rxd1 bxc5 25. Qd3 g6 ({Not} 25... cxb4 $4 26. axb4
{with a protected passed c-Pawn.} Qxc4 $4 27. Qd8+ $1) 26. b5 Kg7 27. h3 Qe5
28. Kg2 h5 29. f4 $2 {This seems to end any winning chances for White (based
on creating a passed QS Pawn) as the King is exposed to Queen checks.} Qc7 30.
Qf3 Qa5 31. a4 ({If} 31. Qb7 Rd8) 31... Rd8 32. Rxd8 Qxd8 33. Qe3 Qa5 34. Kf2 (
{If} 34. Qxc5 Qc3 35. Qf2 Qxc4 {is O.K. for Black.}) 34... Qc7 35. Be4 Qa5 36.
Bc2 Qc7 {White seems to have chances but with 5' to my 25' he was probably
right to take the draw.} (36... Qc7 37. Qe5 {Black can chose between} Qxe5 ({or
} 37... Qa5 38. Ke2 {and the White King marches to the QS. The Black Queen has
then to defend a7 and c5.}) 38. fxe5 Nd7 39. a5 Nxe5 40. b6 axb6 41. axb6 Nd7
42. b7 {and the Knight is tied to b8.}) 1/2-1/2

