{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. Nf3 d6 5. g3 O-O 6. Bg2
Nbd7 7. O-O e5 8. d5 (8. e4 {is more usual.}) 8... a5 9. Bg5 Nc5 10. a3 a4 11.
Nd2 h6 12. Bxf6 ({I considered} 12. Be3 {which looks better.}) 12... Qxf6 13.
e4 Qe7 14. Qe2 $2 (14. Qc2 {may be better. I lose the game in the end because
the Queen is undefended on e2}) 14... f5 15. f4 $2 {I didn't give this enough
thought. Now it all falls apart.} exf4 16. Rxf4 Bd4+ 17. Kh1 Bxc3 18. bxc3 Bd7
19. Raf1 fxe4 20. Nxe4 $5 {This definitely loses it.} ({I had intended} 20.
Rxf8+ {and I don't know why I took on e4}) 20... Rxf4 21. Rxf4 Bf5 {Now I've
had it. The Knight is pinned and he will play ........Re8 so I lose a piece.
The Queen has nowhere to go.} 22. Nf6+ {Afterwards he asked why I had played
this. He hadn't realised that he was winning a piece!} Qxf6 23. g4 {A few
quick moves now just in case he gets carried away.} Qe5 24. Qf2 Nd3 25. Qd4
Qxf4 0-1

