{30' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. d3 f5 5. Nf3 d6 6. Nc3 Nf6 7.
O-O O-O 8. Rb1 a5 9. Bg5 c6 10. e4 Na6 11. Qd2 Be6 12. b3 Qc7 13. Rfe1 Rae8 14.
Be3 Nc5 15. Ng5 {This leads to trouble} Bc8 16. Rbd1 h6 17. Nf3 fxe4 18. dxe4
Nfxe4 19. Nxe4 Nxe4 20. Qc1 {There is no good square for the Queen.} Bg4 21.
Bxh6 Nc5 22. Bxg7 Kxg7 23. Re3 {The alternative is to give up the exchange e.g.
23.Nh4 with a possible attack on my g-pawn.} e4 24. h3 (24. Rd4 {with hopes of
a KS attack might be better.}) 24... Bxf3 25. Bxf3 Rxf3 26. Rxf3 exf3 27. Qc3+
Kh7 28. Qxf3 Qe7 29. Rd4 Kg7 {We were both short of time now.} 30. Qc3 Qe1+ 31.
Qxe1 Rxe1+ 32. Kg2 Re6 {It was all abig rush now.} 33. Rd2 Kf6 34. Kf3 Ne4 35.
Rd4 Ng5+ 36. Kg4 Re4+ 37. Rxe4 Nxe4 38. Kf3 d5 39. Ke3 Ke5 40. f4+ Ke6 41. g4
b5 42. h4 Nf6 43. cxd5+ Nxd5+ (43... cxd5 {Seems to win more easily.}) 44. Kd4
Nxf4 45. Kc5 Kd7 46. Kb6 a4 {I realised here that it had all gone wrong.} 47.
bxa4 bxa4 48. Ka5 Kc7 49. Kxa4 Kb6 50. Kb4 c5+ 51. Kc4 Ng2 52. h5 g5 {I didn't
want to draw and although the position seemed unwinable he had 30'' left (I
had 60'') so I simply picked a line where a lot of moves would be required in
the hope that I would win on time.} ({If} 52... Ne3+ 53. Kd3 Nxg4 54. hxg6 {
it still seems to be a draw.}) 53. Kd3 Nf4+ 54. Kc4 Nxh5 $5 55. gxh5 {I didn't
want to repeat moves unless he claimed a draw. The text keeps the game going,
hopefully long enough for him to lose on time.} g4 56. h6 g3 57. h7 g2 58. h8=Q
g1=Q 59. Qf6+ Kc7 60. Qe7+ Kc8 {White now "played" 61.Qc5+ but his flag had
fallen. I had 36 seconds left.} 0-1

