{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. Nbd2 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. c3 O-O 6. Be2 Nbd7
7. O-O e5 8. Qc2 a5 9. Rd1 Qe7 10. b3 c5 11. dxe5 Nxe5 12. Nc4 $2 Nxc4 13. Bxc4
Qxe4 14. Bd3 Qc6 15. Re1 Bg4 16. Ng5 Rfe8 17. Bd2 d5 18. h3 Bd7 19. Nf3 Rxe1+
20. Rxe1 Re8 21. Ne5 Qc8 ({If} 21... Qd6 {or 21......Qc7} 22. Bf4) 22. a4 Bc6
23. c4 b6 24. Bg5 Nd7 25. Nf3 Rxe1+ 26. Nxe1 d4 27. Qe2 Ne5 28. Bf4 f6 (28...
Nxd3 {might be better but I was getting short of time and having to move
quickly.}) 29. g4 Kf7 30. Bxe5 fxe5 31. Nf3 Qc7 (31... Qe8 {Looks better
covering e5.}) 32. Ng5+ Kg8 33. f4 {Had I played 31......Qe8 I could now play
33......exf5} Qe7 34. Be4 Be8 {So as to beable to cover f7.} 35. Bd5+ Kh8 36.
Ne6 Bf7 $2 {I was having to play like lightning 36......exf4 may be playable.
After the text I'm in trouble.} 37. Nxg7 Bxd5 (37... Kxg7 $142) 38. cxd5 Kxg7
39. fxe5 {How did that happen? I am suddenly faced by killer passed Pawns with
less than a minute left I just had to find moves now. It became a mad panic
rush.} h5 40. gxh5 gxh5 41. Qg2+ Kf8 {I now gave up trying to record the moves.
I pushed my d-Pawn which he took but this allowed me to take his e-Pawn. He
then allowed a Queen exchange which my King captured his d-Pawn. His King went
for my h-Pawn and I created a passed QS pawn. He Queened the h-Pawn one move
to me queening my b-pawn and we agreed a draw. I had a few seconds left he had
3'} 1/2-1/2

