{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 exd5 4. Nf3 Bd6 {I was convinced
he was playing for a draw so I try to prevent symmetry. In view of his later
play my assumption may have been wrong.} 5. Nc3 Ne7 6. Bd3 Bg4 7. h3 Bh5 8. g4
Bg6 9. Bxg6 hxg6 10. Qd3 c6 11. Bd2 Nd7 12. O-O-O {[14']} b5 {[6']} 13. Rde1
Qc7 14. Ng5 {Prevents QS castling.} Kf8 15. Qf3 Nf6 16. h4 Qd7 17. Reg1 Rb8 {
Waiting for White to advance - playing the Rook to a protected square} 18. h5
$5 {Seems premature 18.Kh1 then 19.a3 first} gxh5 19. gxh5 Qf5 20. Qe2 Bf4 21.
Kb1 (21. Bxf4 Qxf4+ {Wins either the d or h-Pawns}) 21... Bxd2 22. Qxd2 Rxh5
23. Rxh5 Nxh5 24. Qe2 Nf4 25. Qe3 Re8 26. Qg3 Neg6 27. a3 ({He wants to play} 
27. Qh2 {but this loses to} Qxg5) 27... Kg8 {Allowing 28......Qf6 aiming at
the d-pawn by removing the fork on h7.} 28. Qh2 Qf6 29. Nf3 (29. Qh7+ {Gets
him nowhere.}) 29... Ne2 30. Nxe2 Qxf3 31. Ng3 {[1hr 13']} Qf4 {[55'] Pinning
the Knight and eyeing the d-Pawn.} 32. Rd1 Re2 {Now another Pawn falls.} 33.
Qh3 Rxf2 34. Qc8+ Nf8 35. Qh3 {[1hr 21']} Qh6 {[63'] |Forcing a Queen exchange.
} 36. Qg4 Qg6 {The threat to c2 forces him to exchange.} 37. Qxg6 Nxg6 38. Re1
Kf8 39. Nh1 Rf3 {Kills the Knight.} 40. Kc1 {[1hr 25']} Ne7 {[64']} 41. c3 g5
42. Rg1 g4 43. Ng3 f5 44. Nxf5 {Short of time this seems as good as anything.}
Rxf5 45. Rxg4 a5 46. b4 axb4 47. axb4 Rf2 48. Rg3 Kf7 49. Rd3 Kf6 50. Rd2 {
This makes it easy for me but his King was stuck on the first rank.} Rxd2 51.
Kxd2 Kf5 52. Ke3 Ng6 53. Kf3 Nh4+ 54. Ke3 Kg4 55. Kd3 Kf4 56. Kd2 Ke4 57. Kc2
Ke3 58. Kb3 Kd3 59. Kb2 Nf3 60. Kb3 Ng5 61. Kb2 Ne4 0-1

