{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 d5 5. Bg5 Nbd7 6. e3
h6 7. Bh4 O-O 8. a3 Bxc3+ 9. Qxc3 b6 $6 {I don't think that he gave this much
thought. He had a long think after my reply.} 10. cxd5 exd5 11. Qc6 Rb8 12. Rc1
Bb7 13. Qxc7 {This wins a Pawn but leaves me way down in development.} Qxc7 14.
Rxc7 Rfc8 15. Rxc8+ Rxc8 16. Kd1 Bc6 17. b3 {After much thought.} Ne4 18. f3 ({
Maybe} 18. Bd3 {is better}) 18... Nc3+ 19. Kc2 {This looks very risky but is O.
K.} a5 20. Ba6 {I offered a draw here as we seemed to be going for an opposite
coloured Bishop endgame.} Ra8 21. Kxc3 ({I considered} 21. Bd3 {which may be
better keeping the Bishop pair.}) 21... Rxa6 22. Ne2 a4 23. Rc1 $2 {I thought
for a long time trying to find a good line, then moved quickly as time was
getting on. I realised immediately that this leaves my Knight embarassed.} Bb5
24. Ng1 axb3 25. Kxb3 Bc4+ 26. Kb2 b5 27. Be1 Re6 28. Bd2 Nb6 29. Nh3 {Time
was getting short and I was having to hurry now.} g5 30. Nf2 f5 31. Re1 Kf7 32.
e4 $2 {With time short and no time to really analyze it I decide on action.} ({
Much better is to sit tight with} 32. Bb4 Z0 33. Nd1 ({or possibly} 33. g4))
32... fxe4 33. fxe4 dxe4 34. Nxe4 Bd5 35. Rf1+ Kg6 36. Nc3 Bxg2 37. Rf2 ({
No time to think. Much better is} 37. Rg1 Bc6 38. h4) 37... Bc6 38. d5 {
Trying to keep active. If I "stop playing" I lose on time.} Nxd5 39. Nxd5 Bxd5
40. Bb4 h5 41. Kc3 h4 42. Kd4 Bc6 43. Ba5 Kh5 44. Bc7 Kg4 45. Rd2 Bf3 46. Kc5 {
Moving like lightning I give the Bishop away. I kept going for a few moves
then resigned.} 0-1

