{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. Nc3 Bb7 5. g3 Bb4 6. Bg2
O-O 7. O-O d5 8. cxd5 exd5 9. Bg5 Bxc3 10. bxc3 h6 11. Bxf6 Qxf6 12. Qb3 {
This is where I started to use up time.} Nd7 13. Rfe1 {I spent a long time on
this.} Rfe8 14. Qa4 {25']} Qc6 15. Qxc6 Bxc6 16. Nd2 Nf6 17. e3 Rad8 18. Rec1 {
[35']} Bb7 {[11']} 19. Rab1 Re7 {Clearly ......c5 is to come so I must play
actively.} 20. c4 c5 {Else I push on to c5.} 21. dxc5 bxc5 ({If} 21... dxc4 $5
22. c6 (22. Bxb7 Rxd2 (22... Rxb7 $2 23. Nxc4 {is good for White}) 23. c6 {
is interesting}) 22... Bxc6 {isn't good for White}) 22. cxd5 Bxd5 23. Bxd5 Rxd5
24. Rb2 {A bit passive.} (24. Nb3 Rc7 25. Rc4 {may be better.}) 24... Red7 25.
Nb3 {Now the Pawn pushes on.} Rd1+ 26. Rxd1 Rxd1+ 27. Kg2 c4 28. Nd4 c3 29. Rc2
Ne4 30. Kf3 f5 31. Nxf5 Rd2 {[29']} 32. Rxd2 {[1hr 13'] With the huge time
differential I was having to think quickly.} ({If} 32. Nd4 Nxf2 33. Rxc3 Rxa2)
32... cxd2 33. Ke2 Kf7 ({If} 33... Nc3+ 34. Kxd2 Nxa2 35. Ne7+ Kf7 36. Nc6 a6
37. Kc2 Ke6 38. Kb2 Kd5 39. Kxa2 $18) 34. Nd4 ({I can't defend the a-Pawn. If} 
34. a3 Nc3+ 35. Kxd2 Nb5 {etc.}) 34... Kf6 {Now I can defend the a-Pawn.} 35.
Nc6 a6 36. Nb4 a5 37. Nc6 a4 38. Nb4 Nxf2 39. Kxd2 Ng4 40. Nd5+ Ke5 41. h3 Nf2
42. Nc3 a3 43. Nb5 Nxh3 44. Nxa3 Nf2 45. Ke2 Ne4 46. Kf3 Nc3 47. Nc4+ {I
offered a draw here. As I had less than 2' left he declined. I had been
rushing for the last few moves. I now had to "scramble". I have to eliminate
his pawns. If we just manoeuvre around I lose on time.} Kd5 48. Nd2 Nxa2 49.
Kf4 Nc3 50. e4+ Ke6 51. g4 g5+ 52. Kf3 Ke5 53. Ke3 Nd1+ 54. Ke2 Nc3+ 55. Ke3
Nb5 56. Nf3+ Kd6 57. Kd3 Nc7 58. Nd4 Ke5 59. Nf5 Kf4 60. Nxh6 Ne6 61. Nf7 Nc5+
62. Kd4 Nxe4 {At this point he said "yes it is drawn".} (62... Nxe4 {I intended
} 63. Nxg5 Nxg5 {on the grounds that he has insufficient material to win.
However it is possible to win. White King on g8, Pawn on g7 Black King on g6
Knight on f4 Then: 1.Kh8 Kh6 2.g8=B?? Ng6#!}) 1/2-1/2

