{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs then 30' for the rest} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5
{The first time that I have played this.} 4. cxb5 a6 5. Nc3 {This transposes
into the main line.} axb5 6. Nxb5 Ba6 {Unsure about the intricases of the
opening I stick to the main line.} ({However} 6... Qa5+ 7. Nc3 Bb7 {leaves his
d-Pawn in trouble. He can play} 8. Bd2 Qb6 9. e4 {which is O.K. for him so I
was probably right to stick to 6......Ba6}) 7. Nc3 g6 8. e3 {Why not 8.e4?}
Bxf1 9. Kxf1 Bg7 10. Nge2 O-O 11. e4 d6 12. f3 Nbd7 {[7']} 13. g4 {[20'] After
a long think he tries for KS play.} Qa5 {[15']} 14. h4 {[42'] After 22'
thought.} ({If} 14. g5 {I would have replied} Ne8) 14... Rfb8 {[18']} 15. Qc2 {
[50']} Qa6 {[26']} 16. Kg2 {[59']} Ne5 17. b3 {[67']} Nd3 {[32']} 18. Bg5 {
[1hr 12']} h6 {[41']} 19. Be3 Nd7 20. Rad1 Nb4 21. Qd2 {[1hr 17']} Kh7 {[53']}
22. a4 Ne5 23. Nb5 Qc8 {With thoughts of a possible ......Nxg4 at some stage.}
24. Nec3 {[1hr 37']} ({Not} 24. Ng3 $4 Rxb5 $1) 24... f5 $5 {[1hr 15'] it was
this or 24......c4. The text is more risky.} 25. exf5 {n[1hr 47']} gxf5 {
[1hr 15']} 26. g5 h5 27. Bf4 c4 $5 {Concentrating too much on creating play
and ignoring his chances of counterplay. Had I seen his 29th I would have
played 27......Kg6} (27... Kg6) 28. Bxe5 Bxe5 29. g6+ {I hadn't seen this
coming.} Kg7 (29... Kxg6 {Looks very risky.}) 30. bxc4 ({He can't risk} 30. Qg5
cxb3 {then} 31. Qxh5 ({or} 31. Qxe7+ Kxg6 32. Qg5+ Kf7 33. Qxh5+ Kf8 {and he
is in trouble on the QS.}) 31... Qh8) 30... Qxc4 {He was getting short of time
now and has to play quickly.} 31. Nd4 $2 {Probably the losing move though it
looks good at first sight. However, the threats of 32.Nxf5+ or 32.Ne6+ force
my reply and he goes into what probably is a lost endgame, not least because
he still had 9 moves to the time control and not much time left.} Bxd4 32.
Qxd4+ Qxd4 33. Rxd4 Nc2 34. Rd2 Ne3+ 35. Kf2 Nc4 36. Re2 Ne5 37. Rg1 {Having
to move fast he looks for "safe" moves.} ({If} 37. f4 {then} Nxg6 {eyes both
the h & f-pawns.}) 37... Rb3 38. Re3 $2 ({Still moving fast he sees that} 38.
Rc1 Nd3+) ({and} 38. Rc2 Rc8 {lose.}) ({and that if the Knight moves e.g.} 38.
Nd1 {then} Rxf3+ 39. Kg2 Ra3 40. Z0 R8xa4 {are all hopeless. So the text is
really no worse than everything else, his Pawns being so weak.}) 38... f4 39.
Rxe5 dxe5 40. Ne2 Rxa4 41. Rg5 Re3 42. Ng1 {or 42......Ra2 wins the Knight}
Ra2+ 43. Kf1 Rb3 44. Rxe5 Rb1+ 45. Re1 Rxe1+ 46. Kxe1 Kxg6 0-1

