{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 {[1']} 5. f4 c5 {
[8'] Surprising since he plays the K.I. regularly he didn't seem familiar with
the 4-Pawns.} 6. d5 O-O 7. Nf3 a6 8. a4 {[1']} e6 {[22']} 9. Be2 exd5 10. exd5
{[1']} Re8 {[31']} 11. O-O {[1']} Bg4 {[35]} ({More usual is} 11... Bf5) 12. h3
{[2']} Bf5 13. Nh4 {[12']} Ne4 {[45']} 14. Nxf5 {[16']} gxf5 ({If} 14... Nxc3
15. bxc3 {he has to continue} gxf5 ({in view of} 15... Bxc3 $2 16. Ra3 Bb4 17.
Rg3 {leaving White a piece up.})) 15. Nxe4 {The Knight is too strong to be
left on e4.} fxe4 16. Bg4 {[22'] The Bishop is almost untouchable on g4 & f5.
This prevents ......f5} Bd4+ 17. Kh1 Nd7 18. Ra3 Nf6 19. Bf5 Kh8 20. Be3 Bxe3
21. Rxe3 b5 {Trying for some counterplay. He is threatened with g4-g5 and Qh5}
22. b3 bxc4 23. bxc4 {b [33']} Rg8 {[1hr 14']} 24. g4 {Black is probably lost
now.} Rb8 ({If} 24... h6 {then simply} 25. h4 Z0 26. g5) 25. g5 Nd7 26. Qa1+
Rg7 {[1hr 23']} 27. h4 {[39']} h6 {As his flag started to rise he panics and
ends it quickly.} ({However, the only reasonable move} 27... f6 {loses to} 28.
Bxd7 Qxd7 29. Qxf6 {followed by} Z0 30. Rxe4 {etc}) 28. gxh6 Qxh4+ 29. Rh3 {
This was the last league match of the season and we won the match to take the
title.} 1-0

