{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Nf3 Bb4
7. Bd3 d5 8. Bd2 $2 {As in Cornish - Collins [Lancaster C.Ch 24/1/06] The rest
of the game is too horrific for comment.} (8. Bg5 {Looks best.}) 8... Bxc3 9.
Bxc3 dxe4 10. Nxe5 exd3 11. Nxd3 Qe7+ 12. Qe2 Qxe2+ 13. Kxe2 Nc6 14. Rhe1 O-O
15. Kf1 Nd5 16. Bd2 {[8']} Bf5 {[5']} 17. Re2 f6 18. Rae1 Kf7 19. h3 Rfe8 20.
a3 $2 Rxe2 21. Rxe2 $2 Nd4 22. Re1 Nxc2 23. Rc1 Bxd3+ {[8']} 24. Kg1 Re8 25.
Rd1 Be2 26. Rc1 Nd4 27. Kh1 $2 Nb3 28. Rb1 Nxd2 29. Rc1 Bh5 30. Kg1 Nf4 31.
Rc7+ Re7 32. Rc2 $2 Re1+ 33. Kh2 Nf1+ 34. Kh1 Ne3+ {And White having managed
to lose a 4th piece resigned. This win secured the Lancaster Quickplay
Championship. I had already won the Lancaster Club Championship.} 0-1

