{30' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 d6 3. g3 f5 4. d3 Nf6 5. Bg2 g6 6. Bd2 Bg7 7.
Qc2 O-O 8. Nd5 c6 9. Nxf6+ Bxf6 10. Bc3 a5 11. Nf3 Na6 12. O-O Nc7 13. Qd2 Ne6
14. b4 $2 axb4 15. Bb2 ({Realising too late that} 15. Bxb4 {is answered by} e4)
15... c5 16. a3 bxa3 17. Rxa3 Rxa3 18. Bxa3 Bd7 19. Bb2 Bc6 20. Ne1 Bxg2 21.
Nxg2 Nd4 22. Ne3 Bg5 23. Qd1 Qa5 {I'm not sure about this. 23......h5 - h4
might have been a better plan.} 24. h4 Bh6 25. Bxd4 exd4 26. Nd5 g5 {Both of
us were getting short of time now and the game speeds up. The text is a bit
loose.} 27. Qc1 Qd8 28. f4 gxf4 29. gxf4 Qxh4 30. Rf2 Kh8 31. Rh2 Rg8+ {
I hadn't realised that I was getting my King into a hole with weaknesses on f6
& h6} 32. Kh1 Qg3 33. Qf1 {Now I had to think hard with the Bishop attacked
and Nf6 threatened.} ({I had expected} 33. Nf6 Rg6) 33... Bg7 34. Rg2 Qh4+ 35.
Rh2 Qg4 36. Rg2 Qh5+ 37. Rh2 Qf7 38. Qh3 h6 39. Qh4 Kh7 40. Ne7 Re8 41. Nd5 Re6
{I noticed that his flag had fallen. According to a spectator it had fallen a
couple of moves earlier. I had about 90'' left.} 0-1

