{2hr each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7.
d5 b5 8. cxb5 a6 9. bxa6 {I felt that I might get a superior form of a Benko
Gambit.} ({Lalic - Zakic 1986 went} 9. a4 {with advantage to White.}) 9... Qa5
10. Bd2 Bxa6 11. Bxa6 Qxa6 12. Qe2 Nfd7 13. Qxa6 {[19']} Nxa6 {[12']} 14. Rb1 {
I wasn't entirely happy with this.} f5 {I hadn't expected this and suddenlr
realised how weak my d-Pawn has become} 15. Ng5 {This seemed to offer the best
chances} fxe4 16. Ne6 e3 {I hadn't expected this} ({After} 16... Bxc3 17. bxc3
Rfb8 18. Ke2 {My d-Pawn is vulnerable. If c4 then the c-Pawn can be put under
pressure.}) 17. Bxe3 Bxc3+ 18. bxc3 Rfb8 19. O-O $2 (19. Ke2 $142 {as the King
may be useful in the centre.}) 19... Nf6 20. c4 Nb4 21. f5 {The a-Pawn is a
goner so I try for some KS play.} Rxa2 22. fxg6 hxg6 {[32']} 23. Bg5 {[61']}
Kf7 24. Bxf6 exf6 {[37']} 25. Ng5+ {[1hr 11']} Kg7 26. Ne4 $2 (26. Ne6+ {
is a draw by repetition, but I was hoping for more. However, after his reply
he is better placed so I should have gone for the draw.}) 26... Re8 27. Nxf6 $4
{A complete brain storm! For some unaccountable reason I had it in my mind
that I had to protect f2 not g2, and that} Ree2 28. Rf3 ({From the previous
note I thought that} 28. Ng4 {was O.K. I don't understand what I was thinking
about.}) 28... Rxg2+ 29. Kf1 Rxh2 30. Ne8+ Kh6 31. Kg1 {[1hr 31']} Rh4 32. Nxd6
({Probably} 32. Rf2 Rxf2 33. Kxf2 Rxc4 34. Nxd6 {is better}) 32... Rah2 {[48']}
33. Rbb3 {[1hr 43']} Rh1+ 34. Kg2 Nc2 {Help. Knight forks everywhere.} 35. Rg3
R4h2+ 36. Kf3 Nd4+ 37. Kf4 {[1hr 48']} Nxb3 38. Rxb3 Rh5 39. Rb5 g5+ 40. Kg3
R5h3+ 41. Kg2 g4 42. Rxc5 Kg5 43. Rc8 R1h2+ 44. Kg1 g3 45. Ne4+ Kf4 46. d6 Rh1+
0-1

