{2hr each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Nb3 Bb4
7. Bd3 d5 8. exd5 Nxd5 9. Bd2 Nxc3 10. bxc3 Be7 {Although I have spoiled his
Pawns he is better developed and my KS looks a bit bare.} 11. O-O Nc6 12. Qe2
Be6 {I had thought of castling QS but after this move his reply causes me
problems.} 13. f4 Qc7 {I wasn't happy here.} 14. fxe5 {I was happier now} (14.
f5 {was what I had expected.}) 14... Qxe5 15. Qf2 Bxb3 ({Maybe I should have
tried} 15... O-O-O {Then if, for example, he tried to attack down the QS with}
16. a4 $2 {then} Bxb3 {is good e.g.} 17. Rfe1 Bc5 18. Be3 Bxe3 19. Rxe3 Qxc3)
16. Rae1 ({Even in the last round he is unlikely to overlook} 16. cxb3 $4 Bc5)
16... Qh5 17. axb3 O-O 18. Kh1 Bd6 19. Bf4 {Here he offered a draw. I have
played so badly in this tournament that I felt it best to accept.} 1/2-1/2

