1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 {I was going to play the Benko Gambit if I had had
the chance.} 4. cxb5 a6 5. bxa6 Bxa6 6. Nc3 g6 7. g3 d6 8. Bg2 Bg7 9. Nf3 O-O
10. O-O Ng4 11. Re1 Nd7 12. Qc2 Qa5 13. Bg5 Rfe8 14. Rab1 h6 15. Bd2 Reb8 16.
a3 Nge5 17. Nd1 {[40']} Qd8 {[37']} 18. Bc3 {[42'] This seems to neutralise
any long diagonal pressure that he might have hoped for.} Rb7 {[45']} 19. Nxe5
Nxe5 20. Ne3 Rab8 21. b4 {[57'] I wasn't entirely confident about this but
felt that I had to play actively.} Qc8 22. bxc5 {[64']} Qxc5 23. Rxb7 Rxb7 24.
Bb4 {Here we had drawn on Bd3 we were level on 4 and winning on 2, so I
offered a draw, which he accepted. We then lost on Bd4, which didn't matter if
we won on 2. However, this went downhill and their Bd2 accepted a draw offer
when in a winning position to win the match 2.5 - 1.5. Maybe I should have
played on and tried to make something off the a-pawn.} 1/2-1/2

