{1hr each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 c5 4. d5 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. Nc3 g6 7.
Bg5 h6 8. Bxf6 Qxf6 9. e3 Bg7 10. Be2 O-O {[9']} 11. O-O {[9']} Nd7 12. Rc1 {
[10']} Ne5 {[10']} 13. b3 {[16']} Bd7 14. Nd2 Qe7 15. Nc4 {[22']} f5 {[15']}
16. Nxe5 Qxe5 17. Qd2 Rab8 {[16']} 18. Bb5 {[22'] I was taking toolong and
Black was playing much faster.} Rf7 19. Bxd7 Rxd7 20. Rc2 Rf7 21. g3 {I didn't
have a good plan here and was worried about the time so I just tried to play
solidly but quickly.} b5 22. Ne2 g5 23. Rd1 Qe4 {[19']} 24. Nc3 {[41']} Bxc3
25. Qxc3 Qf3 26. Qd3 Re8 27. Re1 Rfe7 28. Rce2 {[48']} a6 29. Rd2 Qe4 {[29']}
30. Qc3 {[51'] It all opens up in a time scramble. I have better chances with
Queens on.} Re5 $5 31. f4 $1 {This seemed to offer the best chances, now Black
had a long think.} R5e7 ({Not} 31... gxf4 32. gxf4 R5e7 33. Rg2+) ({If} 31...
Rxd5 {I intended} 32. Qf6 Re6 33. Qd8+ Kg7 34. Rxd5 Qxd5 35. fxg5 {is O.K. for
White.}) 32. fxg5 Qe5 33. Qxe5 Rxe5 34. gxh6 Kh7 35. Kf2 {I offered a draw
here.} Kxh6 36. Kf3 a5 37. Rg2 {Gives up the d-Pawn but confines the King to
the h-file.} Rxd5 38. g4 fxg4+ 39. Rxg4 Rf8+ 40. Ke2 Rg5 41. Reg1 {To keep his
King on the h-file} Rxg4 42. Rxg4 d5 43. h4 Rf5 44. e4 {Eliminating one of my
isolatedPawns. We were both short of time now.} dxe4 45. Rxe4 Rh5 46. Re6+ Kg7
47. Ra6 Rxh4 48. Rxa5 b4 49. a3 bxa3 50. Rxa3 {4 We played a few more moves at
high speed then agreed a draw. The Champions [Lancaster A] won the match 5 -}
1/2-1/2

