{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Qc7 $5 6. Bg5
({Probably} 6. Ndb5 {is best but I was worried that he might know the line and
I didn't want to go into a sharp line in a quick game.}) 6... Bb4 7. Qf3 Bxc3+
8. bxc3 Qe5 9. Bxf6 gxf6 10. Bd3 Nc6 11. Ne2 a6 12. Qe3 {To play f4} Qg5 13.
Qh3 Ne5 $2 {This forces him to excahnge his relativel good Knight for my poor
Bishop, and straighten my Pawns.} 14. f4 Nxd3+ 15. cxd3 Qg6 16. Qf3 Rg8 {[14']}
17. g3 {[14']} e5 18. O-O d6 19. f5 Qg5 20. c4 h5 {[18']} 21. Nc3 {[18']} h4
22. Nd5 {Not concerned about losing the g-Pawn as the Knight is very strong.}
Kf8 23. Rab1 ({maybe} 23. Kg2 {is more solid.}) 23... hxg3 24. Qxg3 Qxg3+ 25.
hxg3 Rxg3+ 26. Kf2 Rxd3 {Apparently he is happy to be 2-Pawns up but his
position is awful.} 27. Rh1 Rd2+ 28. Ke3 Rg2 29. Rh8+ Rg8 30. Rxg8+ Kxg8 31.
Nxf6+ {Moving fast now but.....} ({.......maybe} 31. Rb6 {is better Black is
completely tied up.}) 31... Kg7 32. Ne8+ Kf8 33. Nxd6 b5 {A touch of
desperation here. He was very short of time.} (33... Ke7 {may be better but
then} 34. Rb6 {threatening} (34. Nxc8+ Rxc8 35. Rxb7+ {is probably not as good.
}) 34... Z0 35. f6+) 34. cxb5 axb5 35. Nxc8 Rxc8 36. Rxb5 Rc3+ 37. Kd2 Ra3 38.
Rxe5 (38. Rb2 {leaves me a bit tied up.}) 38... Rxa2+ 39. Ke3 Ra6 40. Kf4 f6
41. Rb5 {We were moving very fast now but I briefly considered.....} ({........
..............} 41. Re6 {then} Rxe6 42. fxe6 {and if} Ke7 $2 ({However, eben
short of time he might have found} 42... Ke8 $1 $11) 43. Kf5 $18) 41... Ra1 (
41... Ra4) 42. Rb7 Rf1+ 43. Ke3 Rd1 44. Rb4 Kf7 45. Ke2 Rd6 46. Rb3 {
Momentarily lost. I realised I neede the Rook on b1 to prevent him occupying
d1.} Rd4 47. Kf3 Rd1 48. Rb4 Rd6 $2 {he should leave the Rook on d1.} 49. Rb7+
Kf8 50. Rb1 $1 Ke7 (50... Ke7 51. Ke3 {[Time] If now say} Rd7 {or 51.Rd8 I
intended} 52. e5 fxe5 53. Ke4 {etc.(which is drawn [6 piece TB draw] but
difficult for him to find in a time scramble)}) 51. Ke3 {Black lost on time.}
1-0

