{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. f4 d6
7. Be3 Bd7 8. Qd2 Nxd4 9. Bxd4 Bc6 10. Bd3 Be7 11. O-O Qc7 12. Rad1 e5 $5 {
leaves a big hole on d5.} 13. Be3 Ng4 14. Bc4 Bf6 15. f5 Nxe3 16. Qxe3 {[14']}
h6 {[14']} 17. Bb5 Bg5 18. Qd3 Rd8 19. Kh1 O-O 20. Rf3 Bf6 {[18']} 21. Qe2 {
[19'] With thoughts of a KS attack. In the quickplay games I try to play 
(quick) solid moves which might cause my opponent to use up time thinking, but
also to not leave him any tactical chances, hence 19.Kh1} Qb6 22. Rg3 Bxb5 $2 {
This gifts me d5 for the Knight. He should sit tight as I have no immediate
prospects on the KS:-however, players feel they have to "do something" in
these quick games.} 23. Nxb5 a6 $2 {Wast of a move. The Knight is going to c3
and then d5 anyway.} 24. Nc3 Rd7 {The only move in view of 25.Nd5} 25. Nd5 Qd8
26. Qd2 {Switching to the QS} Kh8 (26... b5 {Gives him some space but he is
hit with} 27. Qxh6) 27. Qb4 {Now he's had it. He only had a couple of minutes
left and the d-Pawn will fall after Rdg3 (if not before).} Bg5 (27... b5 {
Looks best, but with time runnning out he decides to try for a bit of mayhem
hence 27......Bg5}) 28. Nb6 Bf4 ({With more time he might have tried} 28... Rc7
{when I have to play} 29. c3 {with a strong bind.}) 29. Nxd7 Bxg3 30. Nxf8 Qh4
31. h3 Qh5 {Threatening mate for the second move running!} 32. Qd2 Kg8 33. Nd7
Bf4 34. Qd3 Qh4 35. Nb6 Qf2 36. Nd5 1-0

