{60' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7.
d5 e6 8. Be2 exd5 9. exd5 Re8 10. O-O Ne4 {I hadn't played against this before.
} 11. Nxe4 Rxe4 12. Bd3 Re8 13. Qc2 Nd7 14. Bd2 Nf6 15. h3 {With the 60' limit
I was trying to play solid moves quickly. However 15.a4 may be more solid.} (
15. a4) 15... b5 {This makes it interesting. As is often the case in this
variation my d-Pawn is weak.} 16. cxb5 Nxd5 17. Be4 {This is a bit risky as
the Bishop can become weak.} Bf5 $2 {This is bad.} ({Correct is} 17... Bd7 18.
Qd3 ({If} 18. Qc4 Nb6) 18... Nb4 {After 17......Bf7? he is on the back foot.})
18. Bxf5 gxf5 {[19']} 19. Qxf5 {[16']} Ne3 20. Bxe3 Rxe3 21. Ng5 Qf6 22. Qxh7+
Kf8 {[25']} 23. Qh5 {[25']} Qg6 24. Qh4 Rae8 $2 {This loses immediately.} (
24... Bh6 {May be best.}) 25. f5 Qh6 26. Nh7+ 1-0

