{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. e3 b6 4. Nf3 Bb7 5. Bd3 e6 6. Nbd2 d5
7. Qc2 Nbd7 8. b3 Rc8 9. Bb2 $2 {He now ends up with a weak isolated c-Pawn.}
cxd4 10. Bxd4 dxc4 11. bxc4 {Forced in view of the pin.} Bd6 12. O-O {[14']}
Qe7 {[8'] Threatening e6-e5-e4} 13. e4 e5 14. Be3 O-O 15. Nb3 {[21']} Rc7 {[9']
} 16. Rac1 h6 {I can take my time in pressuring c4.} 17. Nfd2 {White has
thoughts of f4.} Rfc8 18. Qd1 a5 19. Rc2 ({If} 19. a4 {the Pawn is weak.})
19... Bb4 {Now I will be able to swop off the Knight on d2 at the right moment
to leave his e & c Pawns vulnerable.} 20. Qe2 Qe6 21. f4 {Trying for some
activity else .....a5 etc will win the c and or e pawns} a4 22. f5 {[32']} Qc6
{[32']} 23. Nd4 $5 {[45'] after 13' thought. I was wondering what he was
considering. His idea is that 23......exd4 24.Bf4 hits the Rook and if 24.....
Bd6 he gets a fork with e5. However, there is a flaw in his plan.} ({he sees
that} 23. Nc1 Bxd2 24. Qxd2 Nxe4 {etc is winning for Black so by 23.Nd4!?? he
wants to make the waters murky.}) ({Clearly} 23. c5 $2 axb3 24. cxb6 bxc2 25.
bxc7 c1=Q {wins for Black}) 23... exd4 24. Bf4 Bd6 25. g4 ({Now he sees the
problem} 25. e5 Bxe5 26. Bxe5 Nxe5 {and he can't play} 27. Qxe5 {becaue of}
Qxg2#) 25... Bxf4 26. Rxf4 Qd6 27. Qf2 Ne5 28. Bf1 Nfxg4 29. Qh4 Qf6 30. Qg3 ({
He can have 2 Knights for the Rook but after} 30. Rxg4 Nxg4 31. Qxg4 d3 32. Rc1
Qd4+ 33. Kh1 Qe3 {he is horribly tied up.}) 30... Ne3 31. Rb2 Nxf1 32. Kxf1
Nxc4 33. Nxc4 Rxc4 0-1

