{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Bc4 e6 3. Nc3 a6 4. a4 Nc6 5. Nf3 Qc7 6. d3 Nf6
7. Qe2 Nd4 8. Nxd4 cxd4 9. Nd1 Bd6 {This prevents 10.e5, 10.0-0 or 10.f4} 10.
g3 b6 11. Bg5 Bb7 12. c3 dxc3 13. Nxc3 Rc8 14. Bh4 {I wasn't sure why he
played this.} Bb4 15. Rb1 $2 {[37'] Missing the threat.} Nxe4 {[22']} 16. Rc1 {
[43']} (16. dxe4 {Will lose the Pawn as well.}) 16... Nxc3 {[32']} 17. bxc3
Bxc3+ 18. Rxc3 Bxh1 {He is now faced with the loss of a Bishop by 19......b5}
19. Ra3 $2 {A bit shell shocked he more or less gives up.} (19. Rc2 {allowing
20.Bb3 is better but after} Qc5 {Threatening 20......g5 he's in trouble.})
19... b5 20. axb5 axb5 21. Rc3 bxc4 22. d4 Qa5 23. Qd2 O-O 24. Be7 Rfe8 25. Bc5
Be4 26. Rxc4 Qxd2+ 27. Kxd2 d6 {White knocked out a few more moves before
resigning.} 0-1

