{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. Nc3 {[3']} axb5
6. Qd3 {[10']} Ba6 7. Qf3 d6 8. e4 {[14']} b4 {[6']} 9. Bxa6 Rxa6 10. Nd1 Nbd7
11. Qd3 Qb6 12. Nf3 g6 13. O-O Bg7 14. Ne3 O-O 15. Nc4 {This doesn't turn out
too well.} Qb5 16. Re1 $2 ({He should play unpinning the Knight, although after
} 16. Rd1 Rfa8 {Black is well on top.}) 16... b3 17. a3 Ra4 {[16']} 18. Nfd2
Nb6 19. Qe2 {Resigns is the alternative. He now plays on for a few moves in a
resigned fashionand, expectedly, blunders further.} ({If} 19. Ne5 c4) 19...
Nxc4 20. Nxc4 Qxc4 21. Qxc4 Rxc4 22. f3 Nd7 23. Rb1 Rc2 24. Rd1 Rb8 25. Rd2 c4
({I could also play} 25... Rxc1+ 26. Rxc1 Bh6 {immediately, but there is no
hurry and I can just play 25......c4 followed by N-c5-d3}) 26. Rf2 Bd4 0-1

