{1hr 30 each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. e4 dxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f3 exf3 5. Nxf3 e6 {
Very passive.} 6. Bc4 Bd6 (6... Be7 $142) 7. O-O O-O 8. Bg5 Nbd7 9. Qe1 {
Intending Qh4} h6 10. Bh4 Be7 11. Rd1 Nd5 {Giving back the Pawn to get some
freedom.} 12. Nxd5 Bxh4 13. Nxh4 exd5 14. Bxd5 Nf6 {[13']} 15. Bc4 {[11']} c6
16. Nf5 {[16']} Bxf5 17. Rxf5 Nd5 18. Qf2 Qd7 19. Qf3 {I assumed that this
forced 19......Rad8} Ne3 {The firt of three moments of surprise that I had in
this game. I had assumed that this wasn't possible but then he played it. It
only took a few moments to realise it is O.K. for White.} 20. Rxf7 Rxf7 21.
Qxe3 ({I think that he expected} 21. Bxf7+ Qxf7 22. Qxe3 Qxa2) 21... Re8 22.
Qf4 ({Second moment of horror. I nearly played} 22. Qb3 $4 {just noticing}
Qxd4+ {23.Resigns in time}) 22... Ref8 {[34']} (22... Re6 {is more interesting.
Now I can swap off all the major pieces into a won Pawn endgame}) 23. Rf1 {
[35']} b5 {I can choose when to swap off as he can't do anything. I assumed
that the text was messing up his Pawn structure so that it would be easier for
me in the endgame. However, he had another reason.} 24. Bb3 Qxd4+ $4 {The
third moment of horror but only for a couple of seconds! Black has had a
complete mental illusion 23.....b5 was to remove the Bishops defence of f1!}
25. Qxd4 {He went to play 25......Rxf1# when he realised that his Rook was
still pinned. A pity really but I had a won endgame after swapping off the
major pieces.} 1-0

