{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Bc4 a6 3. a3 e6 4. d3 b5 5. Ba2 Bb7 6. Nf3 d5 {
This opens the e-file, possibly to White's advantage.} 7. exd5 exd5 8. Qe2+ Be7
9. b4 {This leaves his Bishop on a2 stuck.} (9. O-O $142 Nf6 10. Bg5 Nbd7 {
and I may have to play ......Kf8}) 9... c4 10. dxc4 dxc4 11. Nc3 ({Still not
keen on} 11. O-O) 11... Nf6 12. O-O O-O 13. Re1 Re8 14. Be3 Nbd7 15. Rad1 {
[12']} Qc7 {[10']} 16. h3 {Else 16......Ng4} h6 17. Bb1 Qc6 {Pinning the Knight
} 18. Bd4 $2 Bxb4 19. axb4 ({The text is possibly no worse than.} 19. Qd2 Bxa3)
19... Rxe2 20. Rxe2 Nf8 21. Re3 Rd8 22. Kf1 {[40']} Ne6 {[28']} 23. Be5 Rxd1+
24. Nxd1 Nd5 25. Re1 Nxb4 26. Ne3 Nd5 27. Nf5 {Tying the d5Knight down.} f6 28.
Bf4 $4 {Presumably on the grounds that 28......Ndxf4 allows the fork on e7.
However, I just take with the other Knight.} Nexf4 29. Rd1 Qc7 30. Re1 Nc3 {
Simplifies it down to an easy ending a piece up.} 31. Re7 Qxe7 32. Nxe7+ Kf7
33. Nf5 Bxf3 34. gxf3 Nxb1 35. h4 Nd2+ 36. Ke1 Nxf3+ 37. Kd1 c3 38. Nd6+ Kg6
39. Ne4 b4 40. Ng3 a5 0-1

