{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Nf3
Bb4 7. Bd3 d5 8. Bd2 $2 {Amazingly he loses a piece as in Bland - Collins
Lancaster QP 21/4/06 & Bland Collins Lancaster QP 8/12/06} (8. Bg5 $142) 8...
Bxc3 9. Bxc3 dxe4 10. Nxe5 exd3 11. Nxd3 Qe7+ 12. Qe2 Qxe2+ 13. Kxe2 O-O 14.
Rhe1 Nd5 15. Bd2 Nc6 16. Kf1 Bf5 {The same position that we reached in both of
the above games! He played 17.Re2 in the first & 17.Bc3 in the 2nd. Now he
finds a third option.} 17. Rac1 {[14']} f6 {[5']} 18. Nc5 b6 19. Nb3 Kf7 20. f3
Rad8 21. a3 a5 22. h3 a4 23. Na1 {Buried till the end of the game.} Ne5 24. Bc3
$2 Nxc3 25. bxc3 Nc4 26. Re2 Nxa3 27. Kf2 {[32']} Rfe8 {[12']} 28. Rce1 Rxe2+
29. Rxe2 Rd1 30. Re1 Rxe1 31. Kxe1 Nxc2+ 0-1

