{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 {I was expecting a Ruy Lopez
and was hoping to play the Marshall.} Bc5 4. O-O d6 5. h3 Nf6 6. d3 h6 7. Nc3
Na5 {To break the symmetry and to gain a tempo on move 9.} 8. Re1 Nxc4 9. dxc4
Be6 10. b3 a6 11. Nd5 c6 {Expecting 12.Nxf6 opening a file to his King.} 12.
Nxf6+ gxf6 13. Qd3 {[14']} Qd7 {[12']} 14. Be3 Bxe3 15. Qxe3 O-O-O 16. Kh2 f5
17. exf5 Bxf5 18. c3 Kb8 19. Rad1 Qe6 {[37']} 20. Qb6 {[36'] results in some
"nuisance" value but the Queen is out of play here. The immediate threat is 21.
Nxe5} Qf6 21. Rd2 Rhg8 (21... Rhe8 {may be more accurate. Then I can answer 22.
c5 with 22......d5}) 22. c5 Qg6 ({I had spent some time looking at} 22... Rxg2+
23. Kxg2 Bxh3+ {etc. The problem is that his Queen is threatening the Rook on
d8 once the other Rook has gone.}) 23. Rg1 {[36']} Qf6 {[54'] Changing tack
and overdefending the d8-Rook} 24. Rgd1 d5 {[64'] I spent more time looking at
sacrificial lines here.} 25. Re2 {[44']} Rde8 {[68']} 26. Rde1 Bxh3 {Now it
works.} 27. Kxh3 Qf5+ 28. Kh2 Qh5+ 29. Kg1 Qxf3 30. g3 {[50']} e4 {[77']} ({
I realised here that time was getting short and I neede to speed up. I had
spent some time looking at} 30... Rxg3+ 31. fxg3 Qxg3+ {variations. The resy
of the game was played very quickly.}) 31. Re3 Qf5 32. Kg2 h5 33. Rh1 {[55']}
Qg4 {[78']} 34. Qb4 {Trying to get the Queen back into play.} f5 35. Rh4 $4 {
Playing quickly he blunders but ......f4 was coming anyway.} Qxh4 36. Qd4 f4
37. Re1 f3+ 0-1

