{Time limit 40moves in 2hr then30' allegro} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4.
Ba4 {[1']} Nf6 {[1']} 5. d4 {[6'] He plays this regularly but I know nothing
about it.} exd4 {[7']} 6. e5 {[10']} Ne4 {[12']} 7. O-O Nc5 {[19']x As per the
only line in MCO 14. This is Morphy - Lowenthal London 1858 [match Rd 14]
given as equal.} 8. Bxc6 dxc6 9. Nxd4 {[19']} Ne6 {[22']} 10. Be3 {[24']} Nxd4
11. Bxd4 Be6 12. Nc3 Be7 13. f4 {[33']} Qd7 {[32']} 14. Be3 {[35']} O-O-O {
[38']} 15. Qxd7+ Rxd7 16. f5 Bc4 17. Rf3 ({Not} 17. Rf4 Bg5) 17... Re8 {
There is no immediate advantage doubling on the d-file. The Rook eyes the
e-Pawn threatening 18......Bb4} 18. b3 {This came as a surprise.} Bb4 {[52']}
19. Bf2 {[75']} ({I had espected} 19. Bf4 {but he didn't like} Bc5+) 19... Red8
{[62']} 20. Bh4 ({Not} 20. bxc4 $2 Bxc3 21. Rxc3 Rd1+ 22. Be1 Rxa1 23. Kf2)
20... Bxc3 21. Rxc3 Rd1+ 22. Rxd1 Rxd1+ 23. Kf2 {Here he offered a draw. We
were winning on Bd1 & Bd3 and level on Bd4 so I accepted. We won the match 2.5
- 1.5} 1/2-1/2

