{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 d6 3. Nc3 g6 4. e4 Bg7 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3
Nbd7 $2 {Now he gets pushed all over the place} 7. e5 dxe5 8. dxe5 (8. fxe5 {
Would leave the e-Pawn weak after an eventual ......c5}) 8... Ng4 {The Knight
is vulnerable here.} (8... Ne8 $142) 9. Be2 {I considered 9.e6 but 9.Be2 is
more solid.} Nc5 {This Knight is also vulnerable.} 10. Nd4 Nh6 11. Be3 c6 $2 {
Gives up a Pawn but his position is difficult.} 12. O-O {Again more solid than.
........} ({................} 12. Nxc6 {which wins a pawn but helps Black with
his QS development.}) 12... Ne6 13. Nb3 Qxd1 (13... Nf5 $142) 14. Raxd1 Nf5 15.
Bc1 b6 $2 {This seals it, but finding a good move is difficult anyway.} 16. g4
Nh6 (16... Nh4 17. f5 Nc7 18. f6 exf6 19. exf6 Bh8 20. Bg5) 17. f5 Nc7 18. f6
Bxf6 {Accepting the inevitable as apiece is lost. Had the Knight gone to h4 on
move 16 then 18......exf6 19.exf6 Bh8 20.Bg5 would still have won a piece.} 19.
exf6 exf6 {Resignation} (19... Nxg4 20. fxe7 Re8 21. Rd8 Be6 22. Rfd1 {is
horrible for Black.}) 20. Bxh6 1-0

