{1hr 30' each/game} 1. Nf3 d5 2. d3 Nf6 3. Nbd2 c5 4. g3 Nc6 5. Bg2 e5 6. e4 {
[1']} d4 7. O-O Bg4 8. a3 Qd7 9. Qe1 {[4']} h6 {[5']} 10. Kh1 Bd6 11. Ng1 g5
12. Nc4 {White was playing very fast this move alows him to force f4.} Bc7 13.
f4 gxf4 14. gxf4 b5 {The best chance of some tactical play. My position is
rather loose especially the Knight on f6.} 15. Nxe5 ({The main alternative,
which I expected ,was} 15. fxe5 bxc4 16. exf6 cxd3 17. cxd3 Ne5 18. Qd2 Qd6 {
threatening ......Nc4. Then say} 19. Nf3 Bxf3 20. Bxf3 Nxd3 {allows} (20...
Qxf6 {seems O.K.}) 21. e5) 15... Nxe5 16. fxe5 Bxe5 {White had taken less than
12' so far. I felt a mistake would come unless he slowed down.} 17. h3 $2 {
[12'] And here it is. I felt for a moment this was good for White. Then I
noticed the hole on g3.} Nh5 {[31']} (17... Bh5 18. Qh4 $18) 18. Nf3 {The best
choice.} Bg3 $1 {Any variation where I don't take on f3 leaves the e5 Bishop
hanging. This solves the problem} 19. Qe2 (19. Qd2 {Looks better. Black can
play} Bxh3 {when} 20. Bxh3 ({If} 20. Kg1 Rg8 {etc.}) 20... Qxh3+ 21. Kg1 Rg8)
19... Bc7 20. Qf2 Ng3+ 21. Kg1 Bxf3 (21... Bxh3 {Could be better as it removes
the later threats on the long white diagonal (see next note)}) 22. Qxf3 Nxf1
23. Kxf1 ({I was concerned about} 23. e5 $1 {e.g.} Rb8 ({Black's only move may
be} 23... Qd8 $1 {but} 24. Qc6+ Kf8 25. Bxh6+ Kg8 26. Rxf1 {is looking good
for White.}) 24. Qf6 {Threatening the h8 Rook and 25.Bc6}) 23... Be5 24. Bf4 f6
25. Bxe5 fxe5 26. Qh5+ $2 {Now it's all over. He had to keep the Queens on.}
Qf7+ 27. Qxf7+ Kxf7 28. Ke2 Ke7 29. Rf1 Raf8 30. Bf3 Rhg8 31. h4 Rf4 32. h5 Rg3
33. b3 Kd6 34. b4 Kc6 35. Rf2 Kb6 36. Bh1 Rxf2+ 37. Kxf2 Rh3 0-1

