{1hr 30' wach/game.} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. cxd5 {Knowing little of
the Slav I didn't want to get into a sharp line.} cxd5 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bg5 (6.
Bf4 $142) 6... Ne4 7. Bf4 Nxc3 8. bxc3 g6 9. e3 Bg7 10. Bd3 O-O 11. O-O {[8']}
Be6 {[27'] Trying to prevent c4 so as to keep me with the backward Pawn.} 12.
Rb1 Na5 13. Qa4 {This doesn't turn out too well.} a6 14. e4 dxe4 15. Bxe4 Bc4
16. Rfc1 Bb5 17. Qb4 {The Queen is vulnerable here.} Rc8 18. Ne5 {After much
thought I wasn't happy with this. Probably 18.Nd2 is better} Bxe5 19. Bxe5 Rc4
20. Qb2 Ra4 21. Bf4 {Covering d2.} Nc4 22. Qb3 Ra3 {Here he offered a draw
which I accepted. Black stands better the a-Pawn is weak.} 1/2-1/2

