{1hr 30' ach/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Nf3 e6 4. a3 {There seems no point
in this.} d5 5. exd5 exd5 6. d4 Be6 7. Bb5 a6 8. Bxc6+ bxc6 9. h3 {There seems
no point in this either.} Nf6 10. O-O Be7 11. Re1 O-O 12. Be3 {[15']} Rb8 {[6']
} 13. Ne5 $5 ({Clearly} 13. dxc5 Rxb2 {is bad for White but 13.Ne5 is risky as
it weakens d4.}) 13... Qc8 14. b3 $2 {Loses a piece.} ({He had to play} 14.
dxc5 {although his Pawns are a mess after} Rxb2) 14... cxd4 {[8']} 15. Qxd4 c5
16. Qd2 {[27']} d4 {[10']} 17. Bxd4 cxd4 18. Qxd4 Rd8 19. Qe3 {[32']} Bc5 {
[11']} 20. Qf3 {Threatening 21.Nc6 then 22.Ne7+} Rd2 21. b4 $2 {He has no good
moves but this seems pointless.} (21. Nc6 {If} Rb7) 21... Bxf2+ 22. Kh1 Bxe1
23. Rxe1 Qb7 24. Qf1 Bxh3 25. Ne2 Rxc2 ({Not} 25... Rbd8 $2 26. Nf3) 26. Kh2
Qxg2+ 27. Qxg2 Bxg2 28. Kxg2 Re8 29. Kf3 Rxe5 30. a4 Rb2 31. b5 axb5 32. axb5
Rb3+ 33. Kf4 ({If} 33. Kf2 Ng4+ 34. Kf1 Rf3+ 35. Kg2 Rf2+) 33... Nd7 34. Rd1 {
Having played on a Rook down he might have hoped that, since we were playing
quickly, I might have overlooked the back rank mate after 34.Rc1 by playing
something involving moving the Knight. However I have mate in 2.} g5+ 35. Kg4
Nf6# 0-1

