{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 d5 4. Qa4 Bd7 {He played 4......Qd6
against me in the Club Rapid 27/1/06} 5. exd5 Nd4 6. Qd1 Nxf3+ 7. Qxf3 Bd6 8.
Bc4 Nf6 9. d3 h6 10. h3 Qe7 11. Be3 c6 12. Rg1 {I had to think about this} (12.
O-O {is risky as} cxd5 13. Bxd5 Nxd5 14. Qxd5 Bc6 {Leaves my KS bare}) 12...
cxd5 13. Bxd5 Nxd5 14. Qxd5 Bc6 15. Qc4 a6 16. Nd2 O-O 17. Ne4 Bxe4 18. dxe4
Rac8 19. Qe2 b5 20. a3 Bc5 21. g4 Bxe3 22. Qxe3 Rfd8 23. Ke2 Qc7 24. Rad1 Qc4+
25. Kf3 Qe6 26. Rd3 $2 {Playing fast I fail to notice that 26......Qf6+ will
cover d8 so I will lose the d-file.} Qf6+ {[17']} 27. Kg2 {[14']} Rxd3 28. Qxd3
Rd8 29. Qe2 Qd6 30. Rc1 {Given the chance I will play d4.} Qd2 31. Qxd2 Rxd2
32. Rb1 Kf8 33. b4 Ke7 ({On} 33... Rc2 {I intended} 34. Rb3 Ke7 35. a4 bxa4 36.
Ra3 {etc.}) 34. a4 Rd3 35. axb5 axb5 36. Rc1 Kd6 37. c4 {All this was played
fast. I had to create some chances.} bxc4 38. Rxc4 Rb3 {This looks drawn. I
have to give him the chance to go wrong.} 39. f3 g6 40. Kg3 f6 {He should have
brought his King back to defend the Pawns.} 41. h4 g5 $2 {And here is the
mistake! His h-Pawn will go.} 42. h5 Kd7 43. b5 $1 {This surprised him.} Rxb5
44. Ra4 Rb8 $2 {In the rush he misses 44......Rc5} (44... Rc5 $1) 45. Ra7+ Ke6
46. Rh7 Rg8 47. Rxh6 Kf7 {It looks better to preserve his Rook, but he is
still lost} 48. Rh7+ Rg7 49. Rxg7+ Kxg7 50. Kf2 Kh6 51. Ke2 Kg7 52. Kd3 Kh6 53.
Kc4 Kg7 54. Kd5 Kf7 55. Kd6 Kg7 56. Ke6 1-0

