{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 e5 $5 {I have never met this before. He said
afterwards that he felt he had to try something completely different.} 2. dxe5
Nc6 3. Nf3 Qe7 {I think you have to play this opening as a gambit with 3.....
d6. He now gets way behind on development.} 4. Nc3 ({An attempt to hang onto
the Pawn with} 4. Qd5 {seems to leave the Queen vulnerable.}) 4... Nxe5 5. e4
h6 {Seems unnecessary.} 6. Nd5 Nxf3+ 7. Qxf3 Qc5 {Throughout the game Black
has trouble finding good squares for his Queen.} 8. Be3 Qa5+ ({Naturally} 8...
Qxc2 $2 {spells disaster on c7.}) 9. c3 c6 10. Nf4 Nf6 {[16']} 11. Bd4 {[23']}
Qd8 {[26']} ({If} 11... Be7 12. Bc4 {vwhen} O-O $2 {meets} 13. Ng6) 12. Bc4 {
[24']} Qe7 13. O-O c5 ({If} 13... Nxe4 14. Bxf7+ Qxf7 15. Qxe4+ Kd8 16. Rfe1 Z0
17. Bb6+ $140) 14. Bxf6 Qxf6 15. e5 Qf5 ({If} 15... Qd8 16. Ng6) 16. g4 Qg5 17.
Bxf7+ Kd8 18. h4 {[40']} Qxe5 {[55']All three Queen moves meet the same reply.
Black could resign.} 19. Ng6 Qf6 20. Qxf6+ gxf6 21. Nxh8 d6 22. Rfe1 Bd7 23.
Ng6 {Afterwards we had a friendly game which I won by answering. 1.d4 with e5
2.dxe5 d6 3.e5xd6 Bxd6 etc} 1-0

