{30' each/game} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 e6 $2 4. c3 c5 5. a3 Qb6 6. f4 Nc6 7.
Nf3 Nge7 8. Be2 $2 Nf5 (8... cxd4 $142 9. cxd4 Nf5) 9. g4 Nfe7 10. b4 cxd4 11.
cxd4 g6 12. Be3 Bg7 13. Nc3 a6 14. Kf2 Bd7 15. Rc1 Rc8 16. Na4 Qd8 $2 17. Nc5
b5 $2 18. Nxa6 Qb6 19. Nc5 Rc7 20. Qd3 Na7 21. Rc2 O-O 22. Rhc1 Rd8 23. h4 f5
24. g5 Kf7 {Black is in a rotten position for a quick-play game as White can
decide to do and when.} 25. Nd2 Bc6 26. Ndb3 Rdc8 {16']} 27. Na5 {[16']} Bf8
28. Kg3 Ng8 29. Rh1 h5 30. gxh6 Nxh6 31. h5 Bg7 $2 32. hxg6+ Kxg6 33. Nxe6 Re7
34. Nxc6 Rxc6 35. Rxc6 Qxc6 36. Ng5 {Threatening 37.Bh5#} Bf8 37. Bh5+ Kg7 38.
Rc1 Qd7 39. Qc3 Kh8 40. Bf3 Bg7 41. Qc5 Ng4 42. Bd2 Bh6 43. Rh1 Kg7 44. Qxd5
Kg6 {At this point I suddenly realised that whilst he had almost run out of
time, so had I and the rest of the game was played at lightning speed.} 45.
Qxd7 Rxd7 46. Bxg4 fxg4 47. Be3 Nc6 48. Rd1 Rd5 49. Ne4 Bg7 50. Nc3 Rd8 {
At this point I gave up recording the moves. However, after another 25 moves
with the flags hovering and moving like lightning I managed to stalemate him
with Q,N and PPP vs K. This was the forst half point that B.C. had taken off
me. Uni Staff won 6.5 - 1.5} 1/2-1/2

