{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 c5 4. d5 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. Nc3 g6
7. Bg2 Bg7 8. Nf3 O-O {[1']} 9. O-O {[2']} Re8 10. a4 Na6 11. Re1 Nc7 12. Nd2
b6 13. Rb1 Rb8 14. b4 cxb4 15. Rxb4 Bb7 16. Qb3 Nd7 17. e4 {May not be best,
leaving a hole on d3. Also Black could force a draw by repetition.} Na6 18. Rb5
Nac5 (18... Nc7 {is a draw.}) 19. Qa3 Ba6 20. Rb1 Nd3 {I wasn't entirely happy
here. Black is threatening 21.......Qf6 hitting c3 and f2 so I want to be able
to reply 22.Nd1. Therefore, I have to put the Rook on f1 under the gaze of the
Bishop.} 21. Rf1 Nxc1 {I'd have left the Knight on d3.} 22. Rfxc1 Nc5 23. Nb5
Bh6 24. f4 Bxb5 25. axb5 Bg7 26. Rc4 Ra8 27. h3 a6 28. bxa6 Rxa6 {[37']} 29.
Qb4 {[55']} Ra4 30. Qxb6 Qxb6 31. Rxb6 Rxc4 32. Nxc4 Bd4+ 33. Kh2 Nxe4 {[57']}
34. Nxd6 {[65'] Leads to an opposite Bishop draw.} (34. Ra6 $142) 34... Bxb6 {
[67']} 35. Nxe8 Kf8 {Secures the draw.} 36. Bxe4 Kxe8 37. f5 Bc7 38. Kg2 Ke7
39. fxg6 hxg6 {[h1hr 11']} 40. h4 {[1hr 11']} Kf6 41. Kh3 Ke5 42. Bf3 f5 43. g4
fxg4+ 44. Kxg4 Bd8 45. Bg2 1/2-1/2

