{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 4. d4 Bd6 $5 {He was playing
lightning fast but gave this a bit more thought.} 5. d5 Ne7 6. Bd3 c6 7. c4 Ng6
8. O-O O-O 9. Nc3 Nf4 $4 {Still bashing out his moves instantaneously he
blunders.} 10. Bxf4 exf4 11. e5 Bc5 12. exf6 Qxf6 13. Ne4 Qe7 14. Nxc5 Qxc5 15.
Ng5 h6 16. Ne4 Qe7 17. d6 Qd8 18. c5 b6 19. b4 bxc5 20. bxc5 Qa5 {Allows a
quick finish.} 21. Nf6+ $1 Kh8 ({Clearly} 21... gxf6 22. Qg4+ Kh8 23. Qf5 {
mates}) 22. Qh5 Qc3 {Attacking both Bishop & Knight is his only hope . However,
it is to no avail.} 23. Qf5 g6 24. Qxf4 Kg7 25. Ng4 g5 26. Qf5 Rh8 27. Ne5 {
In the second game I got very short of time in a complex position and had to
stop scoring and play very fast. I won a Pawn but was left with opposite
coloured Bishops and a draw.} 1-0

