{2hr each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. cxd5 cxd5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Bf4 Ne4
7. e3 Nxc3 8. bxc3 g6 9. Bd3 Bg7 10. O-O O-O 11. h3 Re8 {Threatening 12......
e5 forcing 13.dxe5 when my c-Pawn is weak. I now had a long think.} 12. Bb5 {
The alternatives are not very good.} (12. e4) (12. c4) 12... Bd7 13. Qb3 a6 $2
{Not the best as after my reply the d & b Pawns are en prise} 14. Be2 {[25']}
e5 {[27']} ({After} 14... e6 {I can simply take the b-Pawn. I now take it
anyway after a bloodbath on e5.}) 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Nxe5 Bxe5 17. Bxe5 Rxe5 18.
Qxb7 {[34']} Rb8 {[47'] Deciding that the a-pawn is going anyway, getting some
play.} 19. Qxa6 {[36']} Rb2 20. Rab1 {[48'] Again after a long think. Now
Black decided that my Queen was overloaded, gaurding a2 & e2, so tries to
force the issue.} Re6 $5 21. Qxe6 {Better than..........} ({................} 
21. Rxb2 Rxa6 22. Bxa6 Qa5) 21... Bxe6 22. Rxb2 Qg5 23. Bg4 {Solving the
possible KS threat of a perpetual at the cost of a Pawn.} Bxg4 24. hxg4 Qxg4
25. Rb4 Qc8 26. Rc1 Qa6 27. a4 Kg7 28. e4 dxe4 29. Rxe4 h5 30. Rb4 Qa5 31. Ra1
h4 32. Rxh4 Qxc3 33. Rb1 Qa3 34. Rf4 {I have to try to combine attempts to
force the a-Pawn forward with threats against his King. The threat is 35.Rb7}
g5 35. Re4 Qd3 {[1hr 27']} 36. Reb4 Qa3 37. Rg4 Kg6 38. Rb5 Qc1+ 39. Kh2 Qc7+
40. g3 {[1hr 41']} Qc2 {Giving up the g-pawn to keep an attack on f2 & a4.
However 40......f6 looks better.} (40... f6 $142) 41. Rgxg5+ Kh6 42. Rh5+ Kg7
43. Rbg5+ Kf8 44. Rf5 {Now Black gets the a-Pawn but is lost on the KS} Qxa4
45. Rh7 Qc2 46. Rhxf7+ Kg8 47. Rf4 {[1hr 46']} Qc5 {[1hr 42']} 48. R7f5 Qc2 49.
Rg5+ 1-0

