{2hr each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. d4 cxd4 3. c3 d5 {This is a sharp line in the
Morra Gambit.} 4. exd5 Qxd5 5. cxd4 Nc6 6. Nf3 e6 ({M.C.O. gives} 6... e5) 7.
Nc3 Bb4 8. Bd2 Qd8 (8... Bxc3 {Gives him the 2 Bishops but may be better.}) 9.
Bb5 Nge7 10. Ne4 Bxd2+ 11. Qxd2 Qd5 12. Nc3 Qd6 13. O-O O-O 14. Bd3 Ng6 15. Be4
Bd7 {Probably the simple 15.......a6 is better.} 16. Rad1 {[37']} Rad8 {
[47'] After much thought. White threatens 17.d5 and after 17......exd5 18.Bxd5
threatens 19.Bxf7+ but maybe 18......Be6 is O.K. So maybe 16......a6 is again
best.} 17. Qg5 {[43']} Nce7 {[56']} 18. Qc5 {[51]} Qxc5 $2 {Leaves me in
difficulties.} (18... Qb8 {Looks horrid, but seems O.K. as I can follow with...
....} 19. Z0 Bc6 {which seems O.K.}) 19. dxc5 Bc6 20. Rd6 Bxe4 21. Nxe4 Nf5 {
I knew that I was in trouble here and White has a QS Pawn majority which he
will push.} 22. Rxd8 Rxd8 23. Rc1 Nf4 24. Kf1 Kf8 25. g3 Nd3 26. Rd1 {[64'] I
wasn't worried about the pin.} Rd5 {[1hr 30']} 27. Rd2 Ke8 {[1hr 37']} 28. g4
Nh6 29. Nd6+ Kd7 $4 {Getting short of time I blunder. However, White probably
has a won game although Black has chances.} 30. Rxd3 1-0

