{2hr each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7.
d5 e6 8. Be2 exd5 9. exd5 Re8 10. O-O Na6 11. h3 {The improvement on my game
with him a year ago.} Nc7 12. a4 a6 13. Bd3 Rb8 14. a5 b5 15. axb6 Rxb6 {[24']}
16. Qc2 {[10']} Re7 {[40']} 17. f5 Nce8 {A year ago he was able to play ......
Ng4 .....Ne5 as I hadn't played h3.} 18. g4 gxf5 19. Bxf5 Bxf5 20. Qxf5 {[31']}
Qd7 {[54']} 21. Qc2 Qb7 22. Nh4 Re5 23. Nf5 Rb4 24. Qd3 {[52']} Nd7 {[1hr 17']}
25. Bf4 $5 {[58'] Wins the exchange but the b-pawn goes and Black gets a lot
of play. Maybe I should have supported b2 first with 25.Rb1 and maybe Rf2 or
even 25.Nd125.} Rxb2 26. Nxg7 Kxg7 27. Bxe5+ Nxe5 28. Qe4 {I wasn't sure about
this.} ({maybe best is} 28. Qf5 {then if} Nxc4 $2 29. Qg5+ Kf8 30. Rad1 Qd7 31.
Ne4) 28... Qb3 29. Qe3 {I wanted to play Nd1-e3 but I gat mated.} Qxc4 30. Ne4
Qxd5 {[1hr 32']} 31. Rad1 {[1hr 37'] I was starting to get rather worried here
as I couldn't see a clear way through and he has a lot of Pawns.} Qa2 ({
He played} 31... Qa2 {and offered a draw here. I have to play} 32. Qg3 {
which is very passive} ({or} 32. Rf2) ({or} 32. Rd2 {He has too many pawns
after the Rook exchange so I accepted.})) 1/2-1/2

