{Time limit 40 moves in 1hr 40' then 20' allegro} 1. e4 c5 {My reward for
losing in Rd1 is a 216 opponent in rd2} 2. Nf3 a6 3. c4 Nc6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4
Nf6 6. Nc3 d6 ({M.C.O. gives} 6... e6) 7. Be2 e6 8. O-O Be7 9. Be3 Qc7 10. Rc1
Bd7 {The problem here is that I have (again!) got myself into a line that I
have never play and don't know.} 11. Kh1 Nxd4 12. Qxd4 Bc6 13. Rfd1 {[17']} O-O
{[15']} 14. f3 {[20']} Qd7 {[27'] Starting to use up time I was worried about
Nd5} 15. Qb6 Qd8 16. Rc2 {[37']} Qxb6 {[40']} (16... Nd7 $142) 17. Bxb6 Nd7 $2
{Loses the d-Pawn but I was stuck for ideas. I thought I might be able to play
18......f5 to get some play.} 18. Bc7 Ne5 19. Bxd6 Bxd6 20. Rxd6 g5 21. Kg1
Rfc8 22. b4 {[53']} Be8 {[61']} 23. c5 {[54']} a5 24. a3 axb4 25. axb4 Nc6 26.
Rb2 Ra3 27. Nb5 Ra4 28. Rdd2 Rxb4 29. Rxb4 Nxb4 30. Nd6 {Regaining the Pawn.}
Rb8 31. Rb2 Nc6 32. Rxb7 Rxb7 33. Nxb7 Nd4 {I was short of time and having to
play fast.} 34. Kf2 g4 35. Ke3 gxf3 36. gxf3 Nb3 $4 {The effect of having to
play fast.} ({I had intended} 36... e5 {but for some reason played 36......
Nb3? The Knight is now lost.}) 37. Bd1 Nxc5 38. Nxc5 Kg7 39. Ba4 Bxa4 40. Nxa4
Kg6 41. Nc5 Kg5 42. Nd7 h5 43. f4+ {Again getting short of time, as well as
getting the opening wrong.} 1-0

