{Time limit 40 moves in 1hr 40' then 20' allegro} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. b4 cxb4
4. a3 e6 5. Be2 d5 {This leads to a very open game. I had decided (after 2
losses) to throw cation to the winds in this game to make it interesting.} 6.
exd5 exd5 7. O-O Nf6 8. Re1 Be6 (8... Be7 {is "safer"}) 9. Ng5 Ne4 $5 {There
are clearly chances on the black squares so I "go for it"} 10. Nxe6 fxe6 11.
Bh5+ g6 12. Bb2 {White was making his moves very quickly and I was already
well behind on time.} Rg8 13. d3 bxa3 ({I spent ages trying to make} 13... Nxf2
{work but it doesn't.}) 14. Bd4 {[16'] Now moving the Knight allows 15.Rxe6+
and I am in big trouble. However, I have a resource.} Nc6 $1 15. dxe4 Nxd4 16.
Bg4 (16. Qxd4 {is answered by} Bg7 17. Qa4+ b5 {and the a1R goes}) 16... dxe4
17. Rxe4 Nf5 18. Qf3 {Probably better than......} ({.........} 18. Rxe6+ Kf7 {
I now spent a lot of time on my next move.}) 18... Qb6 19. Nc3 O-O-O $2 (19...
Kf7 {Looks better and if} 20. Bxf5 gxf5 21. Qh5+ Kg7) 20. Rb1 {I now realised
that b7 is a real problem. If 20......Qc6 21.Rc4 However, in a game of this
sort there is only one reply thus............} Qxb1+ {|_hat else?} 21. Nxb1 a2
22. Qc3+ Kb8 23. Qb2 (23. Na3 {Looks O.K. and if} Bb4 24. Qb2) 23... h5 {
It was probably better to keep the Bishop off the long diagonal.} 24. Bf3
axb1=Q+ 25. Qxb1 {I now had 5' to reach move 40 he had 70'.} Rg7 {At 20'' per
move I wasn't expecting to survive.} 26. c3 Re8 {3' left} 27. h3 Bc5 {2' left.}
28. Rc4 Rc7 {The error was bound to come at this speed. I realised as I moved
it that 28......Rc8 hangs on.} ({Later analysis with Fritz [+/- 1.59]} 28...
Rc8 29. Qe4 Rcc7 30. Qe5 Bd6 31. Qxe6 Rce7 32. Qc8+ Ka7 33. g3 Ref7 34. Bd5 Rf8
35. Qe6 Re7 36. Qxg6 Re1+) 29. Rxc5 1-0

