{Time limit 40 moves in 2hrs + 30' allegro} 1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 e6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. d4
cxd4 5. Nxd4 a6 6. Nxc6 bxc6 7. Bd3 Bb4 8. Bd2 Ne7 (8... Nf6 {is playable.}) 9.
O-O d5 10. a3 Bc5 {Prevents 11.f4} 11. Qh5 {Stopping me castling.} Ng6 12. exd5
({If} 12. e5 Qh4 13. Bxg6 hxg6 {is fine for Black.}) 12... cxd5 13. Rae1 {
Threatening 14.Nxd5} O-O 14. Kh1 {[44']} f5 $5 {[32'] leaving the e-Pawn weak
but gaining some space and blocking the b1-h7 diagonal, so freeing the Knight}
15. b4 {[58']} Bd6 16. f4 {[66'] Preventing ........Ne5} Rf7 {[48'] A "general
purpose" move. The Rook can move along the second rank, also f8 is freed for
the Knight.} 17. Ne2 {Threatening 18.c4} Rc7 ({If} 17... Qc7 18. Rc1) 18. Nd4 {
[1hr 14']} Qf6 {[1hr 10']} 19. c3 {[1hr 23']} Nf8 {[1hr 12']} 20. Re2 g6 21.
Qh3 {Big surprise. I had expected 21.Qf3 which prevents my reply. I would have
played 21......Bd7} (21. Qf3 Bd7) 21... e5 {Consider that I "must not lose"
and that we were doing O.K. on the lower boards I offered a draw here. he went
off to consult his match captain and to check all the other boards. After a
while he came back, sat down and started thinking. This went on for a while
till he suddenly realised that he only had 17' left to move 40, and accepted
the draw. It is very complicated with possible White sacrifices on f5. At the
end of the match with one game left it was tied 7.5 each. We needed to win the
last game or lose on board count. The position was drawn but the Herts player
went wrong in time trouble and lost. We won and each got a trophy.} 1/2-1/2

