Unusual.} Bb4 7. Bg5 Qb6 8. Bxf6 gxf6 9. Qd5 {I'm not sure why he played this.}
Bxc3+ 10. bxc3 d6 11. Qb3 Qc6 12. O-O-O {Very risky. Also the e-pawn is loose.}
Be6 13. Qb4 Ke7 14. f4 Rd8 15. c4 a5 {Taking the e-Pawn is unnecessarily risky.
} 16. Qb2 Ra6 17. Qb5 Qxe4 18. Nc3 {Loses at leat a Knight but his position is
hopeless anyway.} Qe3+ 19. Kb2 Rb6 20. fxe5 Rxb5+ 21. cxb5 dxe5 22. Rd3 Rxd3
23. Bxd3 f5 {Playing fast now I overlook his reply: but it doesn't affect
matters.} 24. Bxf5 Qc5 25. Bxh7 {He, in turn, overlooks the threat.} Qb4+ 26.
Kc1 Qxc3 27. h3 {He now seems to decide thathis only hope is that I might
stalemate him in the time rush. However, deliberatelygiving away ones pieces
alerts your opponent to this possibility.} Qa1+ 28. Kd2 Qxh1 29. b6 Qxg2+ 30.
Kc3 Qxh3+ 31. Kb2 Qxh7 32. a4 Nc6 33. c4 Nb4 34. c5 Qc2+ 35. Ka3 Qa2# 0-1

