{1hr 30' each/game} 1. Nf3 d5 2. d3 Nf6 3. g3 g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. O-O O-O 6. Nbd2
Na6 7. c3 c6 8. d4 Nc7 9. Re1 a5 10. e4 dxe4 11. Nxe4 Nxe4 12. Rxe4 Nd5 13. Bd2
Re8 14. Qc1 b5 $2 {Too casual. I was expecting to win easily so was not taking
enough care. This weakens the long diagonal and c4 is coming.} 15. Ne5 Ra6 $6 {
Another doubtful move in view of the coming c4.} 16. Bh6 Bh8 17. c4 bxc4 $2 {
Again played without enough care. Now the Rook on a6 is badly placed, the Pawn
on c6 is weak and f7 is eventually threatened.} (17... Nf6 $142) 18. Qxc4 Qb6 {
It could already be lost.} 19. Rc1 {Now I was stuck. If the Knight moves it's
mate on f7.} Bxe5 {Now the Black squares around the King are vulnerable.
Possibly best is to give up the c-pawn by 19......e6} (19... e6) ({Dick with
Fritz [+/- 0.77]} 19... Bb7 20. Qe2 Raa8 21. Rg4 Red8 22. Bf3 Bf6 23. Rc5 Qc7
24. Qe4 a4 25. Rc4 Ra7 26. Rc1) 20. Rxe5 Be6 ({If} 20... e6 {then} 21. Bxd5 {
and neither Pawn can recapture.}) 21. Qe2 Bd7 ({The threat was} 21... Z0 22.
Rxe6 fxe6) 22. Bxd5 cxd5 23. Rxe7 Rd8 {There is no saving move.} 24. Rxd7 {
[Arnside played all their games at home. These matches were for double points.
John Hornagold scored 4/5 his only loss to Glenn House (SP)]} 1-0

