{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. Nf3 e6 5. O-O h6 6. c4 Be7
7. Nc3 Bd7 8. c5 g5 9. b4 Ne4 10. Qb3 Nxc3 11. Qxc3 f5 {He is playing actively
but this buries his Knight} (11... a6 $142) 12. b5 Nb8 13. Rb1 Bf6 14. a4 g4
15. Ne1 c6 16. Bf4 h5 17. f3 {After much thought. I was worried about ....
h4-h3 and my Bishop has to go to h1. Also opening the f-file would sink me.} b6
18. Qe3 {Pinning the e-Pawn so both Bxd5 Rxd5 may become possible.} a6 $5 {
Making it interesting.} 19. Bxb8 Rxb8 20. bxc6 Bc8 21. fxg4 $2 {Awful! I
realised the mistake immediately and had to sitthere whilst he thought for
ages.} ({I started to consider} 21. Qf4 {then if} Ra8 ({So} 21... e5 22. dxe5
Bg5 23. c7 $3) 22. cxb6 {must win for White.} Bg5 23. Qe5 (23. Qc7 {seems to
win.} Qxc7 24. bxc7 Ke7 25. Rb8 Ra7) 23... Bf6 {I neede to retreat the Queen.
Hence 21.fxg4? Having forgotten that I had rejected this right at the start.})
21... Qc7 $2 ({I saw that after 21.fxg4} 21... bxc5 {threatens the b1R and
also 22......Bxd4. I would have to play.} 22. Nc2 {but after} Rxb1 23. Rxb1
cxd4 {Black is much beter placed than in the game.}) 22. Nc2 Qxc6 23. Nb4 Qxa4
(23... Qd7 {or c7,b7 then} 24. Nxd5) 24. Bxd5 Bxd4 $2 {Short of time he
overlooks that the Queen will attack h8.} 25. Qxd4 1-0

