Bb4 7. Bg5 Qc7 8. Qd3 d6 ({I spent some time considering} 8... Nxe4 {after} 9.
Qxe4 Bxc3+ 10. bxc3 ({Interesting is} 10. Kd1 Bxb2 11. Rb1 Bc3 12. Rb3 d6)
10... Qxc3+ 11. Ke2 Qxa1 12. Nxe5 {I was unsure how he might be able to
proceed after} O-O {It seems O.K. (having looked at it afterwards) but I felt
there was no point playing a risky variation against an opponent I should be
able to beat by straightforward means.}) 9. Bxf6 gxf6 10. a3 Bxc3+ 11. bxc3 Nd7
12. Qd2 Nc5 13. Qe3 $2 {Overlooking the threat.} ({After} 13. Bd3 Na4 14. c4
Be6 15. Qb4 Qc6 {followed by.....} 16. Z0 Rc8 {he is under pressure.}) 13...
Nxe4 14. Qxe4 Qxc3+ 15. Ke2 Qxa1 16. Qh4 Be6 {Getting the pieces developed.}
17. Qxf6 Kd7 18. Ng5 Qa2 19. Kd2 h6 20. Nf3 Qxa3 21. Bd3 Qb4+ 22. Ke2 {There
is no good square. Going to the back rank loses the Rook} ({If} 22. Ke3 Qf4+ {
leaves me a won endgame.}) 22... e4 0-1

