1. c4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. g3 O-O 5. Bg2 d6 6. O-O e5 7. d3 h6 8. b4 $5
{Making it interesting.} e4 9. Nd2 Ng4 ({The alternative was} 9... Nd5 10. cxd5
Bxc3 11. Rb1 exd3 12. exd3) 10. Ndb1 ({Clearly} 10. Bb2 e3 {is good for Black.}
) 10... exd3 11. exd3 Nc6 12. a3 Nge5 13. Ra2 Rb8 {To free the Bishop.} 14. Be3
a6 15. Ne2 Re8 16. Nf4 Bg4 17. Qb3 Nf3+ 18. Bxf3 Bxf3 19. Nd2 Bg4 20. h3 Bc8
21. Kh2 g5 22. Ng2 Qd7 23. g4 h5 24. Qd1 hxg4 25. hxg4 Qxg4 26. Qxg4 Bxg4 27.
f3 Bf5 28. Ne4 Be5+ 29. f4 gxf4 30. Bxf4 Bxf4+ {I felt that this would lead to
a goos endgame. Attempting to pressure my 2 Bishops may give him chances.} 31.
Rxf4 Bxe4 32. dxe4 Ne5 33. Ne3 Re6 34. Rg2+ Rg6 35. Nd5 Rxg2+ 36. Kxg2 c6 {
Seemed more solid than 36......Nxc4} 37. Ne3 Re8 38. Kf1 Re6 39. Ke2 Rh6 40.
Ng4 {This exchange leaves him poorly placed.} Nxg4 41. Rxg4+ Kf8 42. a4 (42.
Rg3 $142) 42... Rh3 43. b5 Rc3 44. e5 dxe5 45. Kd2 Ra3 46. bxa6 bxa6 47. c5 Ke7
48. Rb4 Ke6 49. Rb6 Kd5 50. Rxa6 Kxc5 51. Ra7 f5 52. a5 f4 53. Re7 Kd6 54. Ra7
e4 55. a6 e3+ 56. Ke2 Ra2+ 0-1

