{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Nf3
Bb4 7. Bd2 O-O (7... Bxc3 8. Bxc3 Nxe4 9. Bxe5 Qa5+ 10. Bc3 Nxc3 11. Qd2 O-O {
is an alternative.}) 8. Bd3 d5 $2 {Ridiculous. For the second time in a week I
realise that I can't play a particular move, analyze something else, then play
the unplayable move. I realised immediately.} 9. exd5 $2 {Losing a piece for
two Pawns.} ({Correct is} 9. Nxd5 {when} Bxd2+ 10. Qxd2 Nxd5 11. exd5 Qxd5 $4 {
loses the Queen.}) 9... Bxc3 10. Bxc3 e4 11. Bxf6 Qxf6 12. Bxe4 {[7']} Re8 {
[6']} 13. Qd3 Bf5 14. Nd2 Bxe4 15. Nxe4 Qg6 16. O-O Qxe4 17. Qxe4 {[12']} (17.
Qb3 $142) 17... Rxe4 {[12']} 18. b3 {With 2 Pawns for the Knight Black faces
some difficulties. Fortunately he gives away a pawn by playing very fast.} b5
19. Rfc1 Nd7 {[See Cornish-Collins League 10/1/06]} 20. c4 $2 bxc4 21. bxc4 Nb6
22. Rab1 Rxc4 23. d6 Rxc1+ 24. Rxc1 Kf8 25. Rc7 Rd8 26. Rc6 Rb8 27. h3 Ke8 28.
Rc7 Rd8 {I had been hoping to win the d-pawn without losing the a-pawn but
couldn't find a way.} (28... Rc8 29. d7+ {would be a nice wayto go wrong.}) 29.
Rc6 Nc8 30. d7+ Kxd7 31. Rxa6 Nd6 32. a4 Rc8 33. a5 Rc7 34. Ra8 Nb5 35. Rb8 Kc6
36. a6 Ra7 37. Rc8+ Kd7 38. Rb8 Nc7 39. Rf8 Ke7 40. Rb8 Nxa6 41. Rb6 Nc5 42.
Rb5 Ne6 43. Re5 Kf6 44. Re3 g5 45. Rf3+ Kg6 46. Kh2 Ra2 47. g3 h5 48. Kg2 g4
49. hxg4 hxg4 50. Rc3 Ng5 {I intended ....Nf3, ....Ra1,....Rg1#. This plan
contains a flaw which I hadn't considered at this stage.} 51. Rc6+ f6 52. Rc4
f5 53. Rf4 {I now saw the problem with ....Nf3 ...Ra1White is stalemated if he
can lose his Rook so I would be faced with a desperado. So 53......Ne4traps
his Rook but how do I then make progress? (probably moveing the King to e1)
However the actual move is easiest.} ({I had expected} 53. Rc6+ Kf7 54. Rc7+
Ke6 55. Rc6+ Kd5 {etc.}) 53... Nh3 54. Kf1 Nxf4 55. gxf4 g3 56. fxg3 Kh5 0-1

