7. Re1 O-O 8. h3 d6 9. c3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7 12. Nbd2 Bb7 13. Nf1 Rac8
14. d5 Nc4 15. Ng3 Rb8 {Not playing all this for a quarter of a century, I was
a bit rusty. I decided to relocate the Bishop on the c8-h3 diagonal.} 16. Nh2
Ne8 {[16'] I was expecting 17.h4 and can now reply 17......Bh4} 17. Qf3 {[30']}
Bc8 {[19']} 18. Ng4 {[37']} Bxg4 {I was concerned that Nh6+ might become an
option. Also the Knight was a better piece than the Bishop.} 19. Qxg4 Qc8 20.
Qe2 Qd8 {Intending 21......Bg5} 21. a4 {[63']} Nb6 {[38'] White threatened 22.
a5 when my Knight would be trapped.} 22. Be3 ({Clearly} 22. axb5 axb5 23. Qxb5
Nxd5 {is O.K. for Black.}) 22... Nc4 23. axb5 Nxe3 24. fxe3 $5 {Opening the
f-file is not going to help him and the Knight on g3 is left undefended.} Bh4
25. Qg4 ({Obviously not} 25. Qf2 Qg5) 25... Bxg3 26. Qxg3 axb5 27. Ra7 Ra8 {
Draw agreed. Black is better as White has a poor Bishop but should be O.K.
with correct play.} 1/2-1/2

