{30' each/game} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Be7 6. Nxf6+
Bxf6 7. Bxf6 Qxf6 8. Nf3 b6 9. Bb5+ c6 10. Bd3 Nd7 11. O-O {[3']} O-O {[1']}
12. Be4 Bb7 13. Re1 Rfe8 14. c3 e5 15. dxe5 Nxe5 16. Nxe5 Rxe5 17. Qd7 Rb8 18.
Qc7 Ree8 19. Rad1 Rec8 20. Qd7 Rd8 21. Qh3 h6 22. f3 ({My original plan was} 
22. Rd7 {but was afraid that} Re8 {pins the Bishop}) 22... Rxd1 23. Rxd1 Rd8
24. Re1 ({Now} 24. Rd7 {He can't play 24.......Rxd7 and has to go back to b8.}
Rxd7 (24... Rb8 {I then have} 25. Rxb7 $1) ({So} 24... Bc8 25. Rxd8+ Qxd8 {
and Black is O.K. So 24Rd7 doesn't work.}) 25. Qxd7 {and I was worried that}
Qf4 {might give him a perpetual check. However I'm threatening mate.}) 24...
Qd6 25. Qh4 f5 $5 {He spent some time on this, which left him short of time.} (
{I expected} 25... Qd2 26. Qf2 Qxf2+ 27. Kxf2 Rd2+ 28. Re2 Rxe2+ 29. Kxe2 $16)
26. Bc2 ({25......f5!? sets the simple "trap"} 26. Bxf5 $6 Qc5+ ({Maybe he was
going to answer with} 26... Ba6 {then after} 27. Z0 Qd2 28. Qf2 Qxf2+ 29. Kxf2
Rd2+ {and I can't play} 30. Re2) 27. Kh1 {which seems to leave Black simply a
Pawn down. however short of time myself I wasn't willing to risk anything.})
26... Ba6 27. Bb3+ Kh8 28. Qf2 Qd2 $2 {With very little time left he overlooks
my reply.} 29. Re8+ Kh7 30. Bg8+ {I'm not sure if I've ever played Bg8+ before.
} Kg6 ({If} 30... Kh8 31. Qxd2 Rxd2 32. Bc4+ {wins the Bishop.}) 31. Re6+ Kh5
32. Bf7+ {In the second game, playing much too quickly, I gave away my Queen
on move 10!} 1-0

