{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. a4 bxc4 ({Kasparov played} 
4... b4 {here but Pinski prefers the text.}) 5. Nc3 d6 6. e4 Ba6 7. Nf3 ({
Pinski gives} 7. f4 {as better here.}) 7... g6 8. Be3 Nbd7 9. h3 Bg7 10. Be2
O-O 11. O-O Rb8 12. Qd2 Rb4 13. a5 {[15']} Qc7 {[8']} 14. Bg5 Rfb8 15. Rfb1 Qb7
16. Ra2 Rb3 17. Bd1 {He played this almost instantly, but it forces the move
that I had intended} Rxc3 $1 {I felt that this had to be the right move!} 18.
Qxc3 Nxe4 19. Qc2 Nxg5 20. Nxg5 c3 21. Ne4 Ne5 {Preventing 22.Nxc3 because of
the threat 22......Bd3} 22. Be2 (22. Nxc3 $2 Bd3) 22... Bxe2 23. Qxe2 Qxd5 {
Threatening the Rook.} 24. Ra4 {Loses quickly.} ({If} 24. Nxc3 {White was
worried about.} Nf3+ 25. Qxf3 Qxf3 26. gxf3 Bxc3 {and White is fighting a lost
cause. So he decided to move the a2 Rook.}) ({If} 24. b3 Rxb3) ({or} 24. Ra3
cxb2 25. Rxb2 Rxb2 26. Qxb2 Qxe4 27. Qb8+ Bf8 28. Qxa7 Qe1+ 29. Kh2 Qxf2 {
followed by} 30. Z0 Bh6 31. Z0 Bf4+ {all hopeless for White.}) 24... Rxb2 25.
Rxb2 cxb2 26. Nd2 ({If} 26. Qxb2 Nf3+ {wins the Rook.}) ({If} 26. Nc3 Nf3+ 27.
Qxf3 Qxf3 28. gxf3 Bxc3 {Wins immediately.}) ({If} 26. Qc2 Qd3 27. Qxd3 Nxd3
28. Nd2 Bc3 29. Nb1 Bb4 {etc.}) 26... Qxd2 27. Qxd2 b1=Q+ {At last one of my
Pawns disappears.} 28. Kh2 Qb5 29. Re4 Qd3 30. Qe1 h5 31. f4 Nc6 32. Re3 Qb5
33. Rxe7 {Desperation.} Nxe7 34. Qxe7 Qb8 {Everything is defended so...........
Resigns} 0-1

