{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. c4 Bf5 $2 5. cxd5 Nb8 6.
e4 $2 {Horrific!} ({I considered} 6. Nc3 Z0 {then} 7. e4 {etc:checked it
decided it was best then played 6.e4!}) 6... Bxe4 7. Bxe4 Nxe4 8. Qf3 Nf6 9.
Nc3 c6 10. Nge2 {A pawn must go.} ({If} 10. dxc6 Nxc6 {the d-Pawn goes.}) 10...
cxd5 11. O-O Nc6 12. a3 h6 13. Kg2 {Turns out badly.} e6 14. g4 (14. Be3 $142)
14... Bd6 15. Re1 Nh7 16. Nb5 Bb8 17. Bf4 Ng5 18. Qe3 a6 19. Nbc3 Bd6 $2 20.
Nxd5 Bxf4 21. Ndxf4 O-O 22. Rad1 Ne7 23. Nc3 Nh7 24. Qf3 $2 {I was having one
of those days! Immediately after playing this I saw 24.d5} (24. d5) 24... Nf6
25. Nh3 Ned5 26. g5 $5 {Not good as he is able to exchange Queens.} hxg5 27.
Nxg5 Nxc3 28. bxc3 Qd5 29. Ne4 Nxe4 30. Rxe4 Rac8 31. Re3 Qxf3+ 32. Kxf3 Rc4
33. Rb1 b5 34. Ke2 g6 35. Rb4 Rfc8 36. Kd2 Kg7 {My weak Pawns give Black the
advantage.} 37. Rb1 Ra4 38. Rb3 Rac4 39. Rh3 Rd8 40. Kd3 e5 41. Rb4 Rxb4 {
Leaves him with a weak a-Pawn.} 42. axb4 exd4 43. cxd4 Kf6 44. Re3 Rc8 45. d5
Rc4 46. Re4 Rc1 47. Ke3 Rd1 48. Rd4 Rxd4 $2 {Hurrying, this loses. The rest
was a big rush.} 49. Kxd4 Ke7 50. Kc5 Kd7 51. Kb6 Kd6 52. Kxa6 Kxd5 53. Kxb5
Ke4 54. Kc4 Kf3 55. b5 Kxf2 56. b6 f5 57. b7 f4 58. b8=Q f3 59. Qg3+ Ke3 60.
Qxg6 f2 61. Qg3+ Ke2 62. Qg2 Ke1 63. h4 f1=Q+ 64. Qxf1+ Kxf1 65. h5 Kf2 66. h6
Kf3 67. h7 Kf4 68. h8=Q {Black now realized that I had sufficient time left so
resigned. Very poor overall, I dodn't know why I played so badly.} 1-0

