{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 c5 6. d5 a5 7. Nf3
Bg4 8. Be2 a4 9. O-O O-O 10. h3 Bd7 11. Be3 Na6 12. a3 Nh5 13. Kh2 f5 14. e5
dxe5 15. fxe5 f4 16. Bf2 Bf5 17. Bd3 Qc7 18. Re1 Bxd3 {[16']} 19. Qxd3 {[8']}
Rf5 20. e6 Raf8 21. Nxa4 g5 22. Nc3 Bxc3 23. Qxc3 Ng7 24. Re5 {Rather
underestimating his KS advance.} h5 25. Rae1 $6 {As it turns out things go
well after this. However, I had seen that I could lose a piece but then
started considering other options, realised that time was getting on and
"quickly" played this. In these quickplay games one needs to play "safe" moves
in this situation.} (25. Rxf5 Rxf5 26. Kh1 g4 27. Nh4 {Looks better.}) 25... g4
26. Bh4 gxf3 27. gxf3 Rxe5 28. Rxe5 Nf5 {Black was very short of time and has
opened up attacking prospects for White. His Knight on the a-file is trapped
on the QS so White is on top. He had to play the rest very fast.} 29. Bg5 Kh7
$2 {He must be lost now.} 30. Bxf4 Qd8 31. Qd3 Kg6 32. Re2 h4 33. Rg2+ Kf6 34.
Qe4 Ng3 35. Qe5+ Kg6 36. Qg5+ Kh7 37. Qxh4+ {Next move I would have had the
choice of 4 pieces to capture the Knight.} 1-0

