{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Bc4 Bb4+ ({If} 4... Bc5 {
M.C.O. gives a line} 5. c3 dxc3 6. Bxf7+ Kxf7 7. Qd5+ Kf8 8. Qxc5+ Qe7 {
My move prevents Qd5+ after 5.Bd2, but he can play a similar line with Qh5+})
5. Bd2 Bc5 6. Ng5 Nh6 7. Nxf7 Nxf7 8. Bxf7+ Kxf7 9. Qh5+ g6 10. Qxc5 d6 11. Qa3
Be6 12. Qg3 Qf6 13. c3 Rhe8 14. O-O Kg8 15. Na3 Qe5 16. Qd3 a6 17. f4 Qc5 ({If
} 17... Qf6 {or 17......Qg7} 18. f5 {is good for White.}) 18. Rf2 {I had
expected 18.Kh1 possibly he wanted to double Rooks on the f-file.} ({After
this he can't activate his Knight by} 18. b4 Qb6 19. Nc4 $2 {because of} Qb5)
18... d5 {I felt happy now as my pieces get more play.} 19. exd5 Qxd5 20. cxd4
Qxd4 21. Qc3 $2 {This just seems to lose a move.} Rad8 22. Qxd4 Rxd4 23. Bc3
Rd3 {Prevents him protecting his a-Pawn with 24.b3} 24. Re1 Kf7 25. Rfe2 Re7
26. Ra1 {[63'] Else his a-Pawn goes.} Red7 {[53']} 27. Kf2 Ne7 28. Nc2 Nd5 29.
Be5 ({If} 29. Nb4 Nxc3 30. Nxd3 Nxe2 31. Kxe2 Bc4 32. Rd1 Bxa2) 29... Nf6 30.
h3 c5 {A useful move, denying him b4 & d4 and allowing the dRook to move.} 31.
a3 Bc4 {He was getting short of time.} 32. Bxf6 Kxf6 33. Ne3 R3d4 34. Rc2 Rd2+
({If} 34... Rxf4+ 35. Kg3 Rdd4 36. Rac1 {didn't look good.}) 35. Rxd2 Rxd2+ 36.
Ke1 $2 {With his flag rising he had to rush and blunders. However, the
alternatives look good for Black.} (36. Kf3 Be2+ 37. Kg3 Rxb2) (36. Kg1 Bb3 37.
Rb1 h5) 36... Re2+ 0-1

