{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 Nf6 4. d4 d5 5. exd5 ({Steinitz
recommended} 5. Bb5 {but 5.exd is OK according to Hardings book.}) 5... Qxd5 6.
dxe5 $2 {Sloppy play which leaves me in trouble.} Qxd1+ 7. Kxd1 Ng4 8. Be3 ({If
} 8. Ke1 Bc5) 8... Ncxe5 9. Nxe5 Nxe5 10. Bf4 Bd6 11. Bb5+ Bd7 ({If} 11... c6
12. Re1) 12. Re1 {This leaves me awkwardly placed.} (12. Bxd7+ $142 Nxd7 ({
I [SP] would have played} 12... Kxd7) 13. Bxd6 cxd6 14. Re1+) 12... Bxb5 13.
Bxe5 O-O-O 14. Bxd6 Rxd6+ 15. Kc1 Rhd8 {I was not happy here.} 16. a4 Bc4 {
Threat 17......Bb3} 17. Ra3 Be6 18. a5 Bf5 19. Ra4 Bxb1 {I felt happier now. I
think that he should have harassed my KS Pawns.} 20. Kxb1 Rd1+ 21. Rxd1 Rxd1+
22. Kc2 Rd5 23. Rf4 f5 24. Rh4 h6 25. b4 Kd7 26. f3 Ke6 27. c4 Rd6 28. c5 Rd5 {
He offered a draw here. The position, of course, is a dead draw, but I battled
on for a bit.} 29. Rc4 g5 30. h3 c6 31. h4 Ke5 32. hxg5 hxg5 33. g4 fxg4 34.
Rxg4 Kf5 {I wanted to play 35.Re4 but he replies .....Re5. Afterwards he said
this would lose to a6 (which it doesn't) so he would have stayed on the d-file.
I was worried about him manoeuvering his Rook to h4, so offered a draw which
he accepted.} 1/2-1/2

