{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. g3 Nf6 4. Bg2 e6 5. Nf3 b6 6. O-O h6
7. Qc2 Nbd7 8. Bf4 Bb7 9. Nbd2 Rc8 10. Rac1 Be7 11. cxd5 exd5 ({If} 11... cxd5
$2 12. Bc7 O-O 13. Bxd8 Rxc2 14. Bxe7) 12. Qa4 a6 13. Rc2 O-O 14. Rfc1 c5 15.
dxc5 Bxc5 $2 {Probably the losing move} ({I had expected} 15... Nxc5 16. Qd4
Ne6 17. Qe5) 16. b4 Be7 17. Bc7 Qe8 18. Bh3 {He is getting squeezed in all
directions.} g5 19. Ne5 g4 {Giving up a pawn to buy some freedom.} 20. Nxg4
Nxg4 21. Bxg4 b5 22. Qb3 f5 23. Bf3 Qf7 24. h4 {To keep his Bishop off g5} Kh7
25. Qe3 Ra8 {The threat was 26.Qa7} ({If} 25... Bxb4 26. a3 Be7 27. Qa7 Ba8 28.
Qxa6 Bxa3 29. Ra1) 26. a3 Rg8 27. Kh2 Qf6 {Threatening 28......d4 which is a
nuisance} 28. Nb3 Bd6 29. Bxd6 Qxd6 30. Rc7 Rgb8 31. Qd3 Kg6 32. h5+ Kf6 33.
Nd4 Qe5 {Black has no good move.} 34. Rxd7 {It is relatively unusual to win a
game without moving the e-Pawn.} 1-0

