{1hr 30'each/game} 1. d4 e6 2. c4 f5 3. g3 Be7 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. O-O Nc6
7. Nc3 d6 8. a3 d5 9. c5 Bd7 10. b4 a5 $2 {Very odd.} 11. b5 Na7 12. a4 b6 13.
c6 Be8 14. Qc2 h6 15. Ne5 Nc8 16. f3 Nd6 17. Bb2 Nf7 {Playing too fast.} 18.
Ng6 Nd6 19. Nxf8 Bxf8 20. e4 {Trying to open it up but maybe 20.Rae1 first is
better.} Nc4 21. Nd1 Bg6 22. exf5 Bxf5 23. Qe2 h5 24. Ne3 Bb4 25. Nxc4 dxc4 26.
Qxc4 Nd5 {For a pawn he has activated some pieces.} 27. Qe2 Qf6 28. f4 Bg4 29.
Bf3 Bh3 30. Bxd5 $5 {Possibly wrong. This weakens the White squares around the
King and opens the e-file.} exd5 31. Rf2 Bg4 32. Qe5 $2 {Much too casual. 32.
Qd3 then 33.Ba3 or 33.Bc3} Qf7 {I realised that I had gone wrong now.} 33. Qe3
Re8 34. Qb3 Re4 35. Ba3 Be1 36. Rf1 Qe6 37. Qb1 Bd2 38. Qd3 Re2 {I am in
trouble now. Black threatens ......Bh3, ......Be3+ and ....Bg2#} 39. f5 $1 {
The most active response.} Qe8 (39... Qe3+ 40. Qxe3 Bxe3+ 41. Kh1 Bh3 42. Rg1
Bxf5 43. h4 Be4+ 44. Rg2 Bxg2+ 45. Kh2 Bf3+ 46. Kh3 Bg4#) 40. f6 gxf6 41. Rxf6
{We were both getting short of time now. I just had to check that 41......Re1+
doesn't work. Now Black has to find a move.} Be3+ (41... Re1+) (41... Bh3 42.
Rf8+ Qxf8 43. Bxf8 (43. Qxe2 Qh6 44. Qe8+ Kh7 (44... Kg7 $2 45. Bf8+) 45. Qe7+
Kh8 (45... Qg7 46. Qxg7+ {may be OK for White}) 46. Qd8+ Kh7 47. Qxc7+ {
and White has a passed pawn.}) 43... Be3+ 44. Qxe3 Rxe3 {and White doesn't
have a clear win.}) 42. Kh1 Qe4+ 43. Qxe4 dxe4 {Both down to a few minutes,
Black is still threatening mate in 3. I didn't want to give the exchange back
but I couldn't find another way to stop the mate. Sudddenly, I realised the
d-Pawn could win it.} 44. Rg6+ Kh7 45. Rxg4 hxg4 46. d5 Rc2 ({If} 46... Rd2 47.
Re1 Rd3 (47... Bf2 {say} 48. Rxe4 Z0 49. Rxg4) 48. d6 $18) 47. d6 cxd6 48. Bxd6
{Both playing fast now.} Bd4 49. Re1 e3 50. Bf4 e2 51. c7 Bf2 52. Rxe2 Rxe2 53.
c8=Q Re1+ 54. Kg2 Re2 55. Qf5+ 1-0

