{40 moves in 1hr 40' then 20' allegro} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Bg5 Bf5 4. e3 e6
5. Bd3 Bg6 6. f4 Be7 7. Bxf6 Bxf6 8. f5 $5 {Very odd. This leaves him with a
weak e-Pawn.} exf5 9. Qf3 c6 10. Bxf5 Qe7 {Threatening 10......Bxd4; 10......
Bg5; 10.......Bxf5} 11. Kd2 Bxd4 12. Nxd5 {Seems the most active but his King
gets caught in the cross-fire.} cxd5 13. Bxg6 Qb4+ 14. Ke2 hxg6 15. exd4 Qxd4 {
White's problem is not that he's lost a pawn, but that his King is stuck in
the middle.} 16. Qe3+ Qe4 17. Nf3 {[60'] 17.Qxd4 leaves me with a protected
passed Pawn.} Nc6 {[45']} 18. c3 O-O ({If} 18... O-O-O {I may get hit by Ng5
at some stage.}) 19. Kd2 Rad8 20. Rad1 ({As it turns out} 20. Rhd1 {would be
better.}) 20... Qg4 21. Qf2 d4 22. cxd4 Nxd4 23. Kc1 ({He has no good move. If
} 23. Nxd4 Rxd4+ 24. Kc1 Rc8+ {and the Rook on d1 is loose.}) 23... Rc8+ 24.
Kb1 Qe4+ 25. Ka1 Nc2+ {If his Queen wasn't on the second rank I'd have a
smothered mate.} 26. Kb1 Ne3+ 27. Ka1 Nxd1 28. Rxd1 Qc2 29. Qf1 Rfe8 30. Rb1
Qe2 31. Qg1 b6 32. Nd4 Qe3 33. Nb5 Qxg1 34. Rxg1 Re7 35. Rd1 Rce8 36. Rb1 a6
37. Nd6 Rd8 38. Nc4 b5 39. Na5 Re2 40. Nb3 Rxg2 41. Nc5 Rd6 42. Ne4 Rc6 43. Rd1
f5 44. Nc3 Kh7 45. Rh1 {Presumably White's continuing as I might walk into a
Knight fork. However, he needs to play a3 to stop the back rank threats.} ({If
} 45. Nd5 Rd2 $1 {wins the Knight.}) 45... g5 46. h3 f4 47. a3 Kg6 48. Nd5 Rcc2
49. h4 Rxb2 50. hxg5 Kxg5 51. Nc3 Rbc2 52. Nd5 Ra2+ 53. Kb1 Rgb2+ 54. Kc1 Ra1+
55. Kxb2 Rxh1 {Only 3 boards played in the match as only three Yorkshire
players arrived. We won on 1 & 2 and lost on 3.} 0-1

