{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. d3 b5 6. Bb3
Be7 7. c3 O-O 8. Nbd2 d6 9. h3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. Nf1 Re8 12. Ne3 Qc7 13. O-O
Bb7 {13......Be6 might be better or 13......g6 and ....Bf8-g7} 14. Nf5 Rad8 15.
Bg5 d5 16. Nxe7+ Qxe7 17. Qe2 Qd6 18. Rad1 d4 $2 (18... h6 $142) 19. cxd4 cxd4
20. Nh4 h6 $5 {I decided that he couldn't sacrifice on h6, but had failed to
notice that my Knight on a5 is vulnerable.} 21. Nf5 Qe6 {Still unaware of the
h6 sacrifice.} 22. Bxh6 gxh6 23. Qd2 Nh7 24. Qxa5 Nf8 {I wasn't too unhappy at
losing a Pawn as I now have prospects on the KS along the g-file. However I
knew that he would play Bb3 forcing my Queen to to move so 24.....Nf8 isso
that I can answer Qcy with .....Rd7.} 25. Bb3 Qg6 $2 {Missing his reply.} (
25... Qf6 $142 26. Qxd8 $1) 26. Qxd8 $1 Rxd8 {Against a strong opponent I
would have resigned. however against the Morecambe b-team I make (the correct)
decision to play on. I now played at blitz speed with nothing to lose and also
in the hope that he would speed up.} 27. Ne7+ Kg7 28. Nxg6 Nxg6 29. Rc1 Nf4 30.
Rc7 {With 30' on the clock he was playing at lightning speed taking a few
seconds over each move. I did the same.} Bc8 31. Rxf7+ Kg6 32. Rd1 a5 33. g3 $2
{Leaves the Bishop embarassed and the d-Pawn loose.} a4 34. gxf4 axb3 35. axb3
$4 {Played instantly.} ({Even after} 35. Ra7 bxa2 36. Rxa2 Bxh3 37. fxe5 Bg4 {
Black can fight on.}) 35... Kxf7 36. Kg2 Rg8+ 37. Kf3 Bxh3 {A lucky escape!}
0-1

