{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. Nf3 e6 4. Nc3 d5 5. dxc5 Bxc5 6. Bg5
Qb6 7. e3 Qxb2 8. Bxf6 gxf6 9. Qc1 Ba3 10. Qxb2 $2 {All this is horrific for
White.. He has to play 10.Ne2 [RAC]} (10. Ne2 $6 dxc4 11. Qxb2 Bxb2 12. Rb1 c3
$19 {[NJ]}) 10... Bxb2 11. Nxd5 exd5 12. Rd1 Bc3+ 13. Nd2 dxc4 {I now suffered
my usual failing, with White playing so badly , I continued in a blase manner 
[RAC]} 14. Bxc4 Be6 15. Bb5+ Nc6 16. O-O O-O-O (16... Bxd2 17. Rxd2 (17. Bxc6+
bxc6 18. Rxd2 Ke7) 17... Ke7 {all look safer [RAC]}) 17. Ne4 Rxd1 18. Rxd1 Be5
19. f4 Bc7 20. Nxf6 h6 21. Nd5 Bxd5 (21... Rd8 22. Bxc6 bxc6 23. Ne7+ Kb7 24.
Rb1+ Bb6 {Looks OK for Black.}) 22. Rxd5 Re8 23. Rd3 Bb6 24. Kf2 Re7 25. Rc3
Kc7 26. g4 a6 27. Be2 Kd8 $2 {The first mistake due to my casual play. I gave
this little thought.} 28. Bxa6 Nb4 29. Bb5 ({If} 29. Bc4 Rc7 {is awkward for
him.}) 29... Nxa2 30. Rd3+ Kc7 31. Kf3 Nb4 32. Rb3 Nc6 33. h4 Bd4 $4 {How
could I play this?? With hardly any thought I decide to bring the Bishop to
the KS (g7). I can't remember the last time I played this badly.[RAC] A
surprising error by Dick [NJ]} 34. Bxc6 $1 ({He must have expected this} 34.
exd4 $4 {[NJ]} Nxd4+ 35. Kg3 Nxb3 {Game over!!}) 34... bxc6 35. exd4 Re1 {
Can I get a draw? [RAC]} 36. h5 Rf1+ 37. Ke4 Kd6 38. Rc3 Re1+ 39. Kf5 Rd1 40.
Rc4 Rf1 41. g5 hxg5 42. Kxg5 Kd5 43. Rc5+ Kxd4 44. Rxc6 Ke4 45. Rf6 Rg1+ 46.
Kh6 Kd5 47. Rxf7 {[TB draw]} Ke6 {I was happier now.} 48. Rg7 Rf1 49. Rg6+ Kf7
50. Rg4 Kf6 51. Rg8 Kf7 1/2-1/2

