{30' rach/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. c3 Nf6 5. d4 exd4 6. cxd4
Bb4+ 7. Nc3 Nxe4 8. O-O Bxc3 9. bxc3 ({More usual is} 9. d5 Bf6 10. Re1 Ne7)
9... d5 10. Bd3 ({Steinitz - Lasker Wch 1896 (6)played} 10. Ba3 {but Black was
better.}) 10... O-O 11. Qc2 f5 12. h4 h6 $2 {This leaves a hole on g6 which
causes me problems.} 13. Bf4 Qe7 14. Rae1 Be6 15. Be5 Nxe5 {Probably would
have been better to develop the Queens Rook.} 16. Nxe5 Qe8 17. Re3 g6 18. Rh3
Kg7 19. Be2 c6 {White was playing fast and I was looking to play solid moves
quickly.} 20. h5 g5 21. g4 fxg4 $2 {Again playing quickly but this seems wrong.
} (21... Rf6 $142) 22. Bxg4 Rf6 (22... Bxg4 23. Nxg4 Qe6 24. f3 Nd6 25. Ne5 Nf7
(25... Qxh3 26. Qg6+ Kh8 27. Qxh6+ Kg8 28. Qg6+ $11 {(NJ]}) 26. Ng4 {[NJ]}) 23.
f3 Nd6 24. Qe2 Bxg4 {Again played quickly but 24......Rd8 or 24......Bf5 seem
more solid.} 25. fxg4 Rxf1+ 26. Qxf1 {I realised that I had gone wrong as his
Rook will get back into play whereas my a8 Rook is difficult to activate. Also
I have a problem on g6. However, I was now ahead on time and he was having to
play fast.} Nf7 27. Re3 Nxe5 28. Rxe5 Qd7 29. Rf5 $2 (29. Qe2 $1 {Leaves me in
big trouble. After 29.Rf5? I can activate my Rook.}) 29... Re8 30. Qf3 Re7 31.
Qd3 Qd6 32. Re5 Rxe5 33. dxe5 Qe6 34. Qf5 $2 {Having to move quickly this
loses outright.After the exchange of Queens my passed g-Pawn means that he
can't take his King to the QS..} ({Correct was} 34. Qe2 {when, bearing in mind
how little time he had left, he still had a chance.}) 34... Qxf5 35. gxf5 c5
36. e6 Kf6 37. Kf2 b5 38. Ke3 a5 {7 Pawns on the 5th rank.} 39. Kd3 g4 {
This game gave me 100% in the club quickplay (8/8)} 0-1

