{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. b6 Qxb6 (5... e6
{is the main alternative.}) 6. Nc3 g6 7. e4 d6 8. Be2 Bg7 9. Nf3 O-O 10. O-O
Bg4 {I am not sure I would play this again.} (10... Nbd7 {may be more solid.
Now White gets a pawn steamroller going.}) 11. Nd2 Bxe2 12. Qxe2 Nbd7 13. f4 {
[16']} Qb7 {[10']} 14. Nc4 Nb6 {[23']} 15. Nxb6 Qxb6 16. e5 dxe5 17. fxe5 Nd7
18. Bf4 Qb4 {I need to play actively. Rook moves don't achieve much.} 19. Kh1 (
19. Rad1 $142) 19... c4 $1 {The most active. The Queen now defends e7 (after
e6 and xchanges) and the Knight has a square on c5 with a possible leap to d3
possible.} 20. e6 Nc5 21. exf7+ Rxf7 22. Be5 Raf8 (22... Bxe5 23. Rxf7 Kxf7 24.
Qxe5 Nd7 25. Rf1+ Nf6 26. Ne4 {is just too risky for Black.}) 23. Rxf7 Rxf7 24.
Bxg7 Kxg7 1/2-1/2

