{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 c6 5. c5 g6 6. Nf3 Nbd7
7. O-O Bg7 8. Nc3 O-O 9. Bf4 a5 10. a3 b6 11. cxb6 {Leaving him with a weak
c-Pawn. Also if I don't play this he can block the QS with ......b5} Nxb6 12.
Ne5 Nh5 $5 {A surprise, giving up the c-Pawn.} 13. Nxc6 Qe8 14. Ne5 Nxf4 15.
gxf4 Ba6 16. Re1 Bxe5 {Also a surprise.} 17. fxe5 Qd7 18. Bf1 Rfc8 19. e3 Bxf1
20. Kxf1 Nc4 21. Na4 {Makes it interesting.} Qb5 22. Re2 Rab8 23. Kg1 Qb3 24.
Qxb3 Rxb3 25. Rc1 Rcb8 26. Rcc2 Kg7 {I felt that Black was playing for a draw
and may just sit tight. In that case my chances lay in e4 exd5. Nc3. However,
Black decides to bring his King into it.} 27. Kg2 {I had thoughts of marching
my King to c1 so as to free the Knight but now decided to see what he would do.
} f6 $2 28. exf6+ Kxf6 $2 29. e4 $2 {Both missing the threat.} h5 $2 {He
offered a draw here.} 30. exd5 exd5 31. Nc5 Rxb2 32. Nd7+ Kf7 33. Nxb8 Rxb8 34.
Rc3 a4 35. Rf3+ Kg8 36. Re7 Rb3 37. Rff7 Rxa3 38. Rg7+ Kf8 39. Ref7+ Ke8 40.
Ra7 1-0

