{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. b6 Qxb6 6. Nc3 g6
7. e4 d6 8. Be2 Bg7 9. Nf3 O-O 10. O-O a5 {Seery - Collins League 12/2/08 10...
...Bg4 didn't turn out too well.} 11. Nd2 Ba6 12. Nc4 Bxc4 (12... Qb7 {May be
more solid.}) 13. Bxc4 Qb4 {The Queen is vulnerable here.} (13... Na6 $142) 14.
Qe2 Nfd7 15. f4 Nb6 {This is a faulty plan the Queen gets stuck.} 16. Bb5 c4 {
Threatening to win the Bishop.} 17. a3 Qc5+ ({I considered} 17... Qb3 {but
it's risky}) 18. Be3 Qc7 19. Rac1 N8d7 20. Bc6 Rac8 21. Nb5 Qb8 {This position
lokked worse the longer I looked at it. Trying to get some play with ......
Rfd8, ......Na4, loses the Queen to Ba7. ......f5 leaves fatal weaknesses on
the white squares.} 22. Bxd7 {I was pleased about this White lets me out of
the bind. He should just consolidate.} Nxd7 23. Nd4 Rfe8 {The threat was 24.
Nc6 25.Nxe7+} 24. Rxc4 Rxc4 25. Qxc4 Qxb2 26. Qa4 Kf8 27. Nc6 Qc3 28. Ba7 $2 {
White was very short of time now and moving quickly. I now get a free move to
defend the a-Pawn. I still had about 30'} ({Correct is} 28. Bf2) 28... Ra8 29.
Bf2 Nc5 30. Bxc5 Qxc5+ 31. Kh1 Ra6 $2 {Very foolish. He was having to move
very fast so I was playing quickly to "rush him". I just didn't give this much
thought. The idea was to activate the Rook via b6.} 32. Nb8 Qa7 33. Nxa6 Qxa6
34. Rb1 Bf6 $2 ({Still playing fast I briefly considered} 34... Bb2 {which is
best. Now he can force the Queens off. There was no need for me to play so
fast as I had plenty of time.}) 35. Qb5 Qxb5 {The rest was a mad scramble.
White had almost no time left now. Could he win the game before his time ran
out?} 36. Rxb5 Bc3 37. Rb8+ Kg7 38. g3 Bd4 39. a4 h5 40. Kg2 Kf6 41. Kf3 Bg1
42. h3 Bc5 43. g4 hxg4+ 44. hxg4 e5 45. f5 gxf5 46. gxf5 Bd4 47. Ra8 Bc3 48.
Ra7 Bb4 49. Ke2 Bc3 50. Kd3 Be1 51. Kc4 Bd2 52. Kb5 {White lost on time.} 0-1

