{2hr each game} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Bd2 {Possibly because it's the
last round he plays a wild variation.} dxe4 5. Qg4 Qxd4 {MCO says murky
complications arise from 5......Qxd4 6.0-0-0 h5} ({MCO 14 gives} 5... Nf6 6.
Qxg7 Rg8 7. Qh6 Qxd4 ({or} 7... Nc6 {Keres - Botvinnik World Ch 17 Tourn 1948})
) 6. O-O-O f5 (6... h5) 7. Qh4 ({MCO gives} 7. Qg3 Bd6 8. Bf4 Bxf4+ 9. Qxf4 Qc5
10. f3 $13) 7... Be7 8. Qg3 Bd6 9. Qh4 Bd7 10. Nb5 Qf6 ({If} 10... Bxb5 11.
Bxb5+ c6 12. Bc3) 11. Nxd6+ cxd6 12. Qg3 Nc6 {Bc3 was still the threat} (12...
e5 {leaves the white squares weak. So I decided I had to let a Pawn go.}) 13.
Qxd6 {[37']} Qe7 {[39']} 14. Qc7 {[41']} Bc8 ({I thought about} 14... Nf6 15.
Qxb7 O-O) 15. Qg3 Nf6 16. Nh3 a6 {To prevent 17.Bb5 and to force the Bishop
off if he playes14.Bc4} 17. Bc4 b5 18. Bb3 Nd4 {The threat of 19......Ne2+
forces the exchange of Bishop for Knight.} 19. Rhe1 Nxb3+ 20. Qxb3 ({I had
expected} 20. axb3) 20... e5 {Preventing 21.Nf4 and allowing ......Be6} 21. Bb4
Qe6 22. Qg3 {The 4th time he has played Qg3} f4 {Playing actively but my King
is feeling the draught.} 23. Qxg7 Rg8 24. Qc7 {Simply threatening 25.Rd8#} Bd7
25. Rd6 Qf7 {Clearly I am skating on thin ice! he now thought for a long time.}
26. Rxf6 $5 ({I expected} 26. Red1 {when I can't play} Rc8 $2 {because of} ({
so may haveto go for} 26... Rxg2) ({or} 26... Nd5) 27. Qxc8+) 26... Qxf6 27.
Rxe4 Bxh3 $1 {He had overlooked this} 28. gxh3 {[1hr 28']} ({If} 28. Rxe5+ Be6
{and I am OK}) 28... Rg1+ {[1hr 21']} 29. Be1 {With the Bishop out of action
it is easier for me} ({If} 29. Kd2 Qd8+ {forces off Queens.}) 29... Rd8 {
Now it's won} 30. Rxe5+ Kf8 31. f3 {I was threatening ......f3 and ......Qf4+}
Qd6 32. Rf5+ Kg8 {170.04/0 I came 4th= Tournament grade} 0-1

