{40 in 1hr 40' then 20' allegro} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 d5 3. cxd5 Nxd5 4. g3 {
He may know this line well so I prefer not to go for the obvious 4.e4} c6 5.
Bg2 g6 6. Nf3 Bg7 7. O-O O-O 8. Nc3 Nd7 9. Nxd5 cxd5 10. Bf4 Nf6 {White has
"lost" a move. The position is symmetrical except that White is 2, rather than
1, move ahead.} 11. Qb3 Ne4 12. Rfc1 e6 {[25']} 13. Rc2 {[22']} Bf6 {[36']} 14.
Rac1 Nd6 15. e3 Nc4 16. h4 {Preventing ......g5 which could be a nuisance in
some lines.} Na5 17. Qc3 Nc6 18. Bf1 Qa5 $2 {After much thought and played
with an air of desperation. I had expected 18......a6. The move played loses a
pawn.} 19. Qxa5 Nxa5 20. Bd6 Re8 ({Clearly not} 20... Rd8 21. Bc7) 21. Bb5 Nc6
22. Bxc6 bxc6 23. Rxc6 {[28']} Bd7 {[60']} 24. Rc7 Rec8 25. Ne5 $5 {This may
be wrong and maybe I should keep the Knight on. I wasn't too worried about the
opposite coloured Bishops as there would still be a Rook on but the Knight may
have made a difference. Also, in view of this morning game, there was an
element of "don't lose" in my play.} Bxe5 26. Bxe5 Rxc7 27. Rxc7 Bb5 28. Bd6 h6
{[68']} 29. Kg2 {[68']} Be2 {[69']} 30. a4 {[1hr 20']} Kg7 31. a5 g5 32. hxg5
hxg5 33. f3 Kg6 34. Kf2 1/2-1/2

