{1hr 30' each game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 d5 {Apparently he has played this before.}
3. cxd5 Qxd5 4. Nc3 Qa5 {An experiment. He normally plays 4......Qd8} 5. Bd2
Qb6 6. e3 e6 {Now his c8 Bishop is a problem.} ({Naturally not} 6... Qxb2 $2 7.
Rb1 Qa3 8. Nb5) 7. Nf3 c5 $2 {Loses a pawn.} ({Again} 7... Qxb2 8. Rb1 Qa3 9.
Nb5 Qe7 10. Bb4 {is not to be recommended for Black.}) 8. Na4 Qc7 9. dxc5 Bxc5
$4 {Loses a piece.} 10. Rc1 Nbd7 11. b4 Ne4 12. Qc2 Nxd2 13. Nxd2 b6 14. bxc5
bxc5 15. Nxc5 Qd8 16. Bb5 O-O 17. Ndb3 Nb6 18. O-O Qe7 19. Bc6 Rb8 20. Rfd1 Rd8
21. Rxd8+ Qxd8 22. Rd1 Qe7 23. Qd3 {This clinched the 2007/08 Club Champioship
for me.} 1-0

