{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. g3 Be7 5. Bg2 dxc4 6. Qa4+
Qd7 7. Qxc4 b5 $5 {A surprise.} 8. Qc2 Bb7 9. O-O Be4 10. Qd1 a6 11. Bg5 Bb7 (
11... Z0 {Threat} 12. Bxf6 Bxf6 13. Ne5 Qd5 14. Nc3) 12. Nbd2 O-O 13. Rc1 Nd5
14. Bxe7 Qxe7 15. Qc2 Rc8 16. a3 Nd7 17. Nb3 N7b6 18. Qc5 Re8 19. e4 Nf6 20.
Nfd2 Rac8 21. Rc2 Ba8 22. Rfc1 Nc4 $5 {Black said that he felt he "had to do
something". However, this loses a Pawn. Had he done nothing I intended f3 and
Bf1} 23. Nxc4 bxc4 24. Qxc4 Bxe4 25. Bxe4 Nxe4 26. Qxa6 g6 27. Qc6 Nd6 28. Nc5
{This doesn't tuen out too well.} Nf5 29. Qe4 Qd6 30. Nb3 Qb6 31. Rc3 Red8 32.
Qc6 {Play was speeding up now.} Qxc6 33. Rxc6 Nxd4 34. Nxd4 Rxd4 35. Rxc7 Rxc7
36. Rxc7 Rd1+ 37. Kg2 Rd3 38. Rc1 $2 {Playing quickly - getting the Rook
behind the Pawns seems wrong.} ({With} 38. Rb7 {I can advance the Pawns and
eye his KS Pawns.}) 38... Rb3 39. Rb1 Kf8 40. Kf1 Ke7 41. Ke1 Kd6 42. Kd2 Kc5
43. Rc1+ Kb5 44. Rc2 e5 45. Kc1 f5 46. Rd2 e4 47. Kc2 Kc4 48. a4 {Now 49.Rd4+
is threatened.} Rb4 49. a5 (49. Rd7 $142 {The a Pawn can't be taken.} Rxa4 50.
b3+) 49... Rb5 50. Rd7 Rxa5 51. Rxh7 Rc5 52. Rd7 Rd5 $2 {Playing fast (he had
given p keeping score) he makes it easy for me. The rest was a scramble.} 53.
Rxd5 Kxd5 54. Kc3 Kc5 55. h4 Kd5 56. b4 e3 57. fxe3 Ke4 58. b5 Kxe3 59. b6 Kf3
60. b7 Kxg3 61. h5 gxh5 62. b8=Q+ Kg4 63. Qh2 h4 64. Kd3 f4 65. Ke2 f3+ 66. Kf2
Kh5 67. Kxf3 Kg5 68. Qf4+ Kh5 69. Qf5+ Kh6 70. Qg4 h3 71. Qxh3+ Kg6 72. Qe6+
Kg5 73. Qe5+ Kg6 74. Kg4 Kf7 75. Kg5 1-0

