{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. c4 c5 4. d5 b5 5. cxb5 a6 6. b6 Qxb6
7. Nc3 Bg7 8. e4 d6 9. Nd2 O-O 10. Nc4 Qc7 11. Be2 Nbd7 12. O-O Rb8 13. f4 Nb6
14. Ne3 Nfd7 15. Rb1 c4 {This is the best way to get some play. It also cramps
White somewhat.} 16. a4 Nc5 17. Qc2 ({If} 17. Nxc4 Nxc4 18. Bxc4 Nxe4 19. Nxe4
Qxc4 {is goodfor Black.}) 17... Nb3 18. Bd2 Bd7 {His a-Pawn is weak.} 19. a5 $5
Nxa5 20. f5 ({Possibly he had intended} 20. Nb5 {when he played 19.a5. However,
} Qc5 {is good for Black.}) 20... Nb3 21. Qd1 Qc5 22. Kh1 Qd4 {Forcing his
reply} 23. Bc1 Nxc1 24. Qxc1 Bh6 25. fxg6 $5 {A panic response} ({If} 25. Rf3
gxf5 26. exf5 Bxe3 27. Qxe3 Qxe3 28. Rxe3 Bxf5 {Wins for Black but White has
chances.}) 25... Qxe3 26. gxh7+ Kh8 27. Qxe3 Bxe3 28. Bh5 Bd4 29. Rxf7 Rxf7 30.
Bxf7 Kxh7 31. Ne2 Be5 {Covering the Knights squares} 32. Rf1 Na4 33. h4 Rxb2
34. Ng1 Bg4 {Covering the Knights squares} 0-1

