{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. Nc3 axb5 6. Bg5
b4 7. Bxf6 gxf6 8. Nb5 {This looks very risky but may be playable.} Qa5 9. e3
Ba6 10. a4 bxa3+ $5 {As it turns out this is probably wrong.} 11. Nc3 Qb4 (
11... Bxf1 {is met by} 12. Rxa3) 12. Rxa3 {The longer I looked at this the
worse things got.} Qb7 ({I wanted to play} 12... Bxf1 13. Rxa8 Bxg2 {but I now
saw} 14. Qa4 $1 {when I can't play} Qxa4 {because of} ({I would probably have
to play} 14... Qxb2 {but then} 15. Nb5 {and I am in trouble.}) 15. Rxb8#) 13.
Rb3 ({I was expecting} 13. Qa1 {which leaves me in trouble.}) 13... Qc8 14.
Bxa6 Nxa6 15. Nge2 Nb4 16. O-O Bg7 (16... d6 $142) 17. Qd2 (17. d6 $142) 17...
d6 18. e4 h5 ({If} 18... f5 19. Qg5) 19. f4 h4 20. Nd1 Bh6 21. Nf2 (21. Rh3 {
Looks good.}) 21... Rg8 22. Qd1 f5 23. e5 {This leaves the d-Pawn weak.} Qc7
24. Ra3 Rb8 25. Qa4+ Kf8 26. Qa7 $2 {Throws it away. He played this very
quickly.} Qxa7 27. Rxa7 Nxd5 {Suddenly White is in big trouble. A Pawn has
gone and he is threatened with ......Rxb2; ......Nxf4; ......Ne3} 28. exd6 exd6
29. Nd1 {Temporarily defending all the threats.} Kg7 30. Rf3 (30. g3 $142)
30... Rge8 31. Kf2 Re4 32. Ndc3 Nxc3 33. bxc3 Rb2 34. Re3 Bxf4 35. Rxe4 fxe4
36. g3 hxg3+ 37. hxg3 Bxg3+ 38. Ke3 Be5 39. Ra4 f5 40. Ra1 Kf6 (40... Rxe2+ {
also wins}) 41. Rh1 d5 42. Rh8 Rb7 43. Rd8 Ke6 44. Re8+ Re7 45. Rc8 Bd6 46.
Nf4+ Bxf4+ 47. Kxf4 d4 48. Rxc5 d3 49. Ke3 Rd7 50. Kd2 f4 51. Rc4 e3+ 52. Kd1
Ke5 {[Dick didn't play in the Rd3 match Lancaster A v Morecambe Knights]} 0-1

