{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5
e6 7. Qd2 Be7 8. O-O-O Nc6 9. f3 {Unusual but I knew little about the opening.}
Nxd4 10. Qxd4 b5 11. e5 $5 {This may be premature but Black gets pushed around
a bit.} dxe5 12. Qxe5 Qb6 13. Be3 Qb8 14. Qg5 O-O 15. Bf4 Qb7 16. Be5 Ne8 17.
Qg3 Bd7 18. Bd3 f6 19. Bd4 Rd8 ({I had expected} 19... e5) 20. Qf2 Bc6 21. Ne4
Bd5 {[45']} 22. Kb1 {[44']} Nd6 23. Nc3 Nc4 $2 {23......Bc6 looks better. Now
he won't have a good recapture on d5.} (23... Bc6 $142) 24. Nxd5 Qxd5 $5 (24...
exd5 {is better even though there are holes left on the White squares.}) 25.
Bb6 {After much thought. This results in a degree of panic on his part.} Kh8 $5
{A bit of a panic reaction.} ({After} 25... Nxb6 26. Qxb6 {I am threatening
both the a-pawn and 27.Bxf7+. Then if} Rd6 27. Qa7 {and he is still in trouble.
Apparently the threat of Bxh7+ mesmerised him so he gives up the exchange.})
26. Bxd8 {[58']} Rxd8 {[62']} 27. Qe2 Qc6 28. Qe4 Qxe4 29. Bxe4 Nd6 30. c3 f5 {
Abandons the e-Pawn but it is straightforward for White anyway. He was playing
very quickly now, presumably hoping that I might do the same.} 31. Bc2 Kg8 32.
Bb3 Kf7 33. Rhe1 Nc4 34. Rxd8 Bxd8 35. Rd1 Bf6 36. Bxc4 bxc4 37. Rd7+ Ke8 38.
Rc7 e5 39. Rxc4 a5 40. Kc2 g5 41. Rc5 e4 42. Rxf5 e3 43. Rxf6 1-0

