{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O Bg4 6. h3
Bh5 ({MCO 14 gives} 6... h5) 7. Nc3 ({I spent a while considering} 7. g4 Bg6 8.
Nxe5 {but} Qd4 9. Nxg6 hxg6 {is good for Black.}) 7... Bd6 8. d4 $2 {White was
playing for a draw but also playing quickly. This loses the d-Pawn but it is
very hard to defend.} Bxf3 (8... exd4 $142) 9. Qxf3 exd4 10. Ne2 Bc5 {I wanted
to play 10.......Be5 but it is hit by f4 at some stage.} 11. Rd1 Qf6 12. Qf4 {
I hadn't expected this and now had a long think.} Bd6 ({Clearly} 12... O-O-O
13. Qg4+ {and 14.Bg5 isn't on.}) 13. Qxf6 Nxf6 14. Nxd4 O-O-O 15. Bg5 (15. f3
$142) 15... Be5 16. c3 c5 17. Nf3 Rxd1+ 18. Rxd1 Nxe4 {Maintianing my Pawn
plus.} 19. Nxe5 Nxg5 20. f4 Re8 21. Re1 {Again, played very quickly.} f6 22.
Nd3 ({Echanging Knights} 22. fxg5 fxe5 {gives me a passed Pawn.}) 22... Rxe1+
23. Nxe1 Ne6 24. g3 {Again, almost instantaneous but it gives me a tempo for
my next move.} (24. f5 $142) 24... c4 {Taking d3 away from his Knight and
allowing my Knight c5.} 25. Kf2 {Again, played quickly but he should look to
the QS.} (25. b3 $142 {but Black still has the advantage.}) 25... Nc5 26. Ke3
Na4 27. b3 Nxc3 28. Kd4 Nxa2 29. Kxc4 Nc1 {Rd 1 was between the two Grammar
school teams. Everyone else had a bye.} 0-1

