{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 d5 {[As in Collins-Fairbairn Lancaster CC 07/
10/08]} 3. cxd5 Nxd5 {In the above game he played 3......Qxd5} 4. e4 Nb6 5. Be3
e6 6. Nc3 Bb4 7. a3 Bxc3+ 8. bxc3 N8d7 9. Bd3 e5 10. d5 Nf6 11. Ne2 Bd7 12. O-O
Nc8 {Black's position is awful.} 13. h3 Nd6 14. Qc2 O-O 15. c4 a6 {Black
doesn't have a decent move.} 16. f4 exf4 {What else?} 17. Bxf4 Nh5 18. e5 Nxf4
19. Rxf4 Bxh3 $2 ({It probably makes no difference what he does.} 19... Ne8 20.
Bxh7+ Kh8 21. Raf1) ({or} 19... Nc8 20. Bxh7+ Kh8 21. Raf1 Be8 22. e6 f6 23.
Rh4 {and he can resign.}) 20. exd6 Qg5 21. g3 cxd6 22. Bxh7+ Kh8 23. Rh4 {
Threatening both the Bishop and the discovered check. He lasted 23 moves as in
the game on 7/10/08.} 1-0

