7. Qd3 (7. Bc4 Nc6 8. O-O d6 9. Qd3 O-O 10. Nd5 Nxd5 $14) 7... O-O (7... d6 8.
Bd2 Nbd7 9. Qc4 Qb6 10. O-O-O Nc5 11. Na4 Nxa4 12. Qxb4 Qxb4 13. Bxb4 Nxe4 $15)
8. Bd2 Nc6 9. Nd5 Bxd2+ 10. Nxd2 d6 11. c3 ({Fritz prefers} 11. Nxf6+) 11...
Nxd5 12. Qxd5 Be6 13. Qd3 Qc7 14. Be2 Rad8 15. O-O f5 (15... d5) 16. Qh3 {
I wasn't expecting this.} ({Fritz gives} 16. exf5 Bxf5 17. Qd5+ Kh8 18. Rad1
Bg6 19. g3 Bf7 20. Qe4 d5) 16... Qd7 ({Fritz gives} 16... Rf6 17. exf5 Bxf5 18.
Qe3 d5 19. Rae1 Be6 20. Bd3 Qa5 21. a3 Qc7) 17. exf5 Bxf5 18. g4 $2 {Not good.}
(18. Qe3 $142 d5 19. Rac1 Qf7 20. Nb3 d4 21. cxd4 exd4 22. Qf4 d3 23. Bf3 Qf6)
18... Be6 (18... Bg6 19. Qe3 d5 20. f4 d4 21. cxd4 Qxd4 22. Qxd4 Rxd4 23. Nb3
Re4) 19. Ne4 Qe7 20. Rfd1 Rf4 21. Qg2 d5 22. Nd2 Rdf8 23. Rf1 e4 24. Rad1 Ne5
25. f3 e3 ({Both getting short of time I decided against spending time working
out} 25... exf3 {-3.66/0 as 25......e3 looked good. Fritz gives 25.exf3 as} 26.
Rxf3 Nxf3+ 27. Bxf3 d4 {etc}) 26. Nb3 Nc6 27. Nd4 {Played very quickly but
loses material.} Nxd4 28. Rxd4 Rxd4 29. cxd4 Qb4 30. g5 {With time running out
he decides to try for a attack.} Qxd4 31. b3 Qh4 {Threat 32......Bh3} 32. f4
Rd8 ({Playing fast we both overlook} 32... Rxf4) 33. Rf3 Qe1+ 34. Rf1 Qd2 35.
Rf3 d4 36. f5 {He ws just trying to find moves now with no time left.} Bd5 37.
Bc4 Qxg2+ (37... Bxc4 38. bxc4 e2) 38. Kxg2 Bxc4 39. bxc4 d3 40. Rxe3 d2 0-1

