{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Nf5
{I was well aware that 6.Ndb5 (0.52) was the correct move but wanted to "mix
it" with J.C. especially as I felt he would not be familiar with this.} (6.
Ndb5) 6... d6 7. Ne3 a6 8. Ned5 Be7 (8... Nxd5 9. Nxd5 Ne7 10. Bc4 {(0.64)}) 9.
Be3 Nd7 {The d-Pawn goes} ({Fritz prefers.} 9... Nxd5) 10. Qd2 h6 11. O-O-O b5
(11... Bg5 $142) 12. Nxe7 Qxe7 13. Qxd6 Qxd6 14. Rxd6 Nd8 (14... Bb7 $142) 15.
Nd5 Rb8 16. Be2 (16. Ba7 Rb7 17. Rxa6) 16... Ne6 17. Rd1 Ndc5 18. Nc7+ Ke7 19.
Nxe6 ({Fritz prefers} 19. R6d5) 19... Nxe6 20. R6d5 (20. c4 $142) 20... f6 21.
c4 bxc4 22. Bxc4 Re8 {Seems pointless.} 23. Ra5 (23. b3 $142) 23... Rd8 24.
Rxd8 Kxd8 25. Bxe6 Bxe6 26. Rxa6 Bf7 27. a3 {[57']} Rc8+ {[53']} 28. Kb1 {
Conscious of the clock I "play safe".} ({With time in mind I woudn't want to
play the Fritz line} 28. Kd2 Bb3 29. Ra7 Rc2+ 30. Kd3 Rc6 31. f3 Bc4+ 32. Kd2
Rd6+ 33. Ke1 Rd7 34. Rxd7+ Kxd7 35. a4) 28... Ke8 29. Rd6 {Again the "safe"
move rather than 29.Ra7} Rc4 30. f3 Ke7 31. Rd2 Rc6 32. b4 Ke8 {Marking time}
33. Kb2 Bg6 34. g4 h5 35. h3 Bf7 36. Bc5 (36. b5 $142) 36... h4 37. a4 g5 38.
a5 $2 {Makes life very difficult and although Fritz is still 2.20 in practice
it may be unwinnable.} ({Correct is} 38. Kc3 {keeping the Bishop out.}) 38...
Bc4 {Now my h-Pawn will be under threat.} 39. Rf2 Kf7 40. Ka3 Bb5 41. Kb3 Ke6
42. Kc3 Rc7 43. Rd2 Rd7 {He offered a draw here. With minutes left I thought
I'd blown it.} 44. Ra2 {The only winning chance but it's clearly drawn.} Rd3+
45. Kc2 Rxf3 46. a6 Rf2+ $4 {Short of time he blunders} ({Correct is} 46...
Rxh3 47. Ra5 (47. a7 {is a draw by perpetual.}) 47... Bc6 48. a7 Rh2+ 49. Kb3
Bxe4 50. Ra6+ Kf7 51. a8=Q Bxa8 52. Rxa8 {(0.07)}) 47. Bxf2 1-0

