{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O Bg4 6. h3
Bxf3 7. Qxf3 Bd6 8. Na3 Nf6 9. Nc4 O-O 10. d3 h6 11. b3 Nh7 12. Bb2 Ng5 13. Qg4
f6 14. Rae1 Qc8 15. Re2 b6 {To prevent Na5 which would be a niusance.} (15...
Qxg4 16. hxg4 Bc5 $11) 16. d4 exd4 17. Bxd4 Qxg4 18. hxg4 Ne6 (18... Rad8 $142)
19. Bxb6 {The sort of move one is likely to miss in a quickplay game.} cxb6 20.
Nxd6 Rfd8 21. Rd1 Kf8 22. Red2 Ra7 (22... Rd7 $142) 23. Nc4 Rxd2 24. Rxd2 b5 {
This is Fritz's preffered move.} 25. Ne3 Rc7 26. f3 g6 27. Kf2 Ke7 28. g3 Rc8
29. Ke2 Rc7 30. c3 {From 26......g6 to 30.c3 are all best according to Fritz.}
Ng7 (30... a5 {Fritz}) (30... Rd7 {Fritz}) 31. f4 h5 32. gxh5 Nxh5 33. Kf3 Rc8
$2 (33... Rd7 $142) 34. g4 Ng7 35. Nc2 Rh8 36. Kg3 c5 37. Rd5 Rc8 38. e5 Rc6
39. Ne3 b4 40. c4 Ne6 41. exf6+ Kxf6 42. Rd7 Nf8 43. Nd5+ Ke6 44. Re7+ Kd6 45.
Rf7 Rc8 46. Rf6+ Ne6 47. Rxg6 1-0

