{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 e6 2. e4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bb4+ {
Seems to simply lose a tempo} 6. c3 Be7 7. Bd3 Nf6 8. O-O b6 {Leaves holes on
the white squares} (8... Nd5 $142) 9. Qa4 Bd7 10. Qc2 Nxe4 11. Bxe4 f5 {
This is Fritz's choice but the e-Pawn is left weak.} 12. Bd3 O-O 13. Re1 Qe8
14. Bc4 (14. Bf4 {Fritz}) 14... Qg6 15. b4 {After much thought.} ({I wanted to
play} 15. d5 {Fritz gives} exd5 16. Bxd5+ Kh8 17. Bf4 Bd6 18. Bxd6 cxd6 19.
Rad1 {but it wasn't clear to me.}) (15. Qb3 {Looks good, but then} Na5 {
is a nuisance. 15.b4 is to prevent this.}) 15... a6 16. Qb3 Kh8 17. Bxe6 Bxe6
18. Rxe6 Rf6 19. Re2 Bd6 20. d5 Nb8 (20... Nd8 21. Bg5 Rf8 22. Rae1) 21. Bg5
Rf8 22. Rae1 Nd7 23. Qc4 Nf6 24. Re6 h6 {Now it all goes pear shaped. He was
very short of time - I had more but (as usual) foolishlt started to play
quickly.} 25. Bf4 $2 {I realised my error immediately. Despite being short of
time he finds the right reply.} ({Correct is} 25. Bxf6 Rxf6 26. h3 a5 27. Qc6
Rd8 28. bxa5 bxa5 29. Qb5) 25... Qg4 {Again played quickly.} 26. Ne5 ({I had
briefly considered} 26. Bxd6 Qxc4 27. Bxf8 Rxf8 28. Ne5 Qxc3 29. Ng6+ Kg8 30.
Nxf8 {but didn't like it so quickly played 26.Ne5}) 26... Nxd5 $2 {Short of
time he played this instantaneously} ({Correct is} 26... Bxe5 27. R1xe5 g5 28.
Rxf6 Qd1+ 29. Qf1 Qxf1+ 30. Kxf1 Rxf6 31. Be3 Kg7 32. f4 Kg6 33. Re7) 27. Qxd5
$2 {I instantly saw that he can't play 27.......Qxf4 because of 28.Ng6+, so I
win a piece...............} ({..............completely overlooking} 27. Nxg4)
27... Rad8 {Moving instantaneously he misses it as well. I'd seen it now} 28.
Nxg4 1-0

