{2hr each/game} 1. d4 f5 2. Bg5 g6 3. c4 Bg7 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. g3 d6 7.
Bg2 h6 8. Bxf6 Bxf6 9. Qd2 Bg7 10. O-O c6 11. Rac1 Qe8 12. e3 {Playing solid.
12.d5 is Fritz's choice.} Nd7 13. d5 c5 14. b3 g5 15. Ne1 a6 16. a4 Qg6 17. Nd3
Ne5 18. f4 Nxd3 19. Qxd3 Bd7 20. e4 Rf7 (20... gxf4 21. gxf4 fxe4 22. Nxe4 Qg4
23. Rf3 Rxf4 24. Rg3 $17) 21. Ne2 b5 22. axb5 (22. cxb5 {Fritz}) 22... axb5 23.
Qe3 gxf4 24. Rxf4 Be5 25. Rff1 b4 26. Kh1 Raf8 27. Nf4 Qg5 28. h4 Qg4 29. Bh3
Bxf4 30. gxf4 Qxh4 31. Rg1+ {I thought that I was lost now. However, he was
very short of time so I hoped I could get something from the g-file.} Kh7 32.
Rg3 (32. Qg3 Qh5 33. Qh2 Qf3+ 34. Qg2 Qxf4 35. Rcf1 Qh4 36. exf5 $15) 32...
fxe4 33. Qxe4+ Bf5 34. Qg2 Bxh3 35. Rxh3 Qxf4 36. Rg1 Qf6 37. Rg3 Ra8 {He was
moving very fast.} 38. Kh2 Qh4+ 39. Rh3 Qf4+ ({He misses.} 39... Qf2) 40. Kh1
Qf6 41. Rg3 Qh4+ 42. Rh3 Qf6 {I was trying to work out whether I could claim a
draw by 43.Rg3. When he suddenly said "Do you want a draw?" I accepted. Black
is better.} 1/2-1/2

