{440 moves in 1hr 40' then 20' allegro} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Bc4 d6 4. Nf3 Nd7
5. c3 h6 6. O-O e6 {I decided to play the Hippo even though I have barely
glanced at the book I havee bought on it.} 7. Na3 b6 8. Nc2 Bb7 9. d5 e5 10.
Nb4 Ne7 11. Be3 O-O 12. Re1 a5 13. Nc2 f5 14. exf5 Nxf5 {Maybe I should play
these "less solid" moves more. However, I wanted to play safe in the 1st round.
} (14... gxf5 $142) 15. Qd2 Nf6 16. Rad1 Kh8 ({If} 16... Qe7 17. Nxe5) 17. h3
Bc8 {I decided to bring the Bishop into play on the KS.} (17... b5 $142 18.
Bxb5 Nxd5) 18. Nh2 g5 19. Qe2 Bd7 20. Bc1 Be8 21. Ne3 Bg6 {I played this
without too much thought and didn't consider Fritz's preference for............
..} (21... Bh5) ({or} 21... Nh4) 22. Bd3 Nxe3 23. Bxe3 Qe8 24. Ng4 Kh7 25.
Nxf6+ Bxf6 26. b4 Qf7 {Threatens 27......e4} 27. Bxg6+ Qxg6 28. Qc4 Qg7 29. b5
Rae8 30. Qe4+ Qg6 31. Bd2 Qxe4 {Here I offered a draw which he accepted
instantaneously. I probably played too conservatively in this game (trying to
get half a point on the board) and missed better moves 17......b5 and
recapturing with the g-Pawn on move 14.} 1/2-1/2

