{40 moves in 1hr 40' then 20' allegro} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 e6 4. Nc3 exd5
5. cxd5 d6 6. e4 g6 7. Bd3 Bg7 8. h3 O-O 9. Nf3 a6 10. a4 Nbd7 11. O-O Nh5 12.
Qc2 Ne5 13. Nxe5 Bxe5 14. Ne2 g5 {This came as a surprise.} 15. g4 $2 {I was
unnecessarily worried about 15......g4} Nf4 16. Bxf4 {I felt that my Knight
might be more useful than his Bishop in this position.} gxf4 17. f3 Qb6 18. Qc4
{I wasn't expecting him to take the b-Pawn.} Qxb2 19. Rab1 b5 {After a long
think.} (19... Qd2 $142 20. Rb6 Ra7 21. Rfb1 Qe3+ 22. Kg2 h5 {However, this
looks very risky for a human player}) 20. axb5 axb5 21. Qxb5 Qd2 22. Qb3 {
22......Ba6 was threatened.} Ra2 23. Bc4 Ra7 {Here he offered a draw which I
accepted.} 1/2-1/2

