{30' each/game} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. Nc3 e6 5. Bd3 Nd7 6. O-O b6 7.
Bg5 {varying from our game on 23/10/09} Ne7 8. Qd2 h6 9. Bh4 g5 10. Bg3 Bb7 ({
Fritz prefers} 10... g4 11. Z0 {then} Bxd4 {In a quickplay game I wanted to
keep it tight.}) 11. d5 e5 12. h4 Ng6 13. hxg5 hxg5 14. Qxg5 {In a quickplay
game this is risky} Bf6 15. Qe3 Qe7 16. Bb5 O-O-O 17. Bxd7+ Qxd7 18. Ng5 $2
Rdg8 19. Nh3 Ba6 $2 ({Correct is} 19... Rxh3 {I was thinking about this but in
a fast game wasn't willing to spend time on this.}) 20. Ne2 Kb7 {With time
getting on I was in "make safe moves quickly" mode.} 21. b3 Bxe2 22. Qxe2 Nh4
23. Qc4 $2 {Loses straight off.} Kb8 $2 {However, wanting to move fast, and
prevent an exchange of Queens, I miss the immediate win. Immediately after
moving (and thinking in his time) I saw the move.} ({of course} 23... Nf3+) 24.
Qd3 Nxg2 25. Kxg2 Qxh3+ 26. Kf3 Bh4 {Again, a "quick move"} ({Correct is} 26...
Qh5+ 27. Kg2 Qh2+ 28. Kf3 Rh3 29. Rg1 Bh4 30. Raf1 Kb7 31. Rg2 Bxg3 32. Rxh2
Bxh2+ 33. Ke2 Rxd3) 27. Rh1 {Played in seconds.} ({If} 27. Ke2 Bxg3 28. Rg1
Qg4+) ({or} 27. Rg1 Qg4+ 28. Kg2 f5 29. Qf3 Qf4 30. exf5 Bxg3 31. Qxf4 Bxf4+)
27... Rxg3+ 28. fxg3 Qxg3+ 29. Ke2 Qg2+ 0-1

