{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 f5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Bf4 g6 4. Nc3 c6 5. e3 Bg7 6. Be2
O-O 7. h3 d6 8. O-O b5 9. a3 a5 $2 {My big problem at the moment playing too
casually.} 10. d5 c5 (10... Qb6 $142 11. dxc6 Nxc6 12. Bxb5 Ba6 13. a4 Nb4) 11.
Bxb5 Qb6 12. Rb1 Ne4 13. Ng5 (13. Bd3) 13... Nf6 {I was simply playing badly
today.} (13... Bxc3 $142 14. Nxe4 Bg7) 14. Qe2 Na6 15. e4 (15. Bc6 $142) 15...
Nc7 16. Bc4 Nxe4 (16... h6 $142 17. Nf3 fxe4) 17. Ngxe4 fxe4 18. Bd2 (18. Bg5
$142) 18... Bf5 (18... Ba6 $142) 19. Nxe4 Qb7 20. Bc3 ({Missing} 20. Nxc5)
20... Bxe4 21. Qxe4 e5 {I felt happier now. Fritz prefers 21.....e6, which is
much better. However, I was having a bad day.} 22. Bd2 Ne8 {Continuing my poor
play.} (22... Ne6 $142) 23. f4 Kh8 (23... Nf6 $142) 24. Qd3 (24. f5 $142) 24...
Qe7 25. fxe5 Rxf1+ 26. Qxf1 Bxe5 27. Kh1 Nf6 28. Bg5 Rf8 29. Qe2 Qg7 30. b3 Nh5
31. Bh4 Qf7 32. Rf1 Nf4 {My problem is that playing an opponent who has yet to
beat me in over 30 years :- he would be happy with a draw but I HAVE to win:
hence I can't play some "best" moves e.g.32.......Qxf1+ but have to "try for
something"} 33. Qd2 Qg7 34. Be1 g5 35. Bg3 Re8 {Trying to generate something
and hoping he doesn't take the a-Pawn.} ({Against a strong opponent I would
have played.} 35... Ra8) 36. Bb5 {There is no reason not to take the a-Pawn.}
Ra8 37. Bc4 a4 38. Qe3 axb3 39. Qxb3 Qa7 40. Rf3 Rb8 41. Bb5 Qa5 42. a4 {
He offered a draw here. We were both down on time, but he had less than me and
I felt that I had to create some play.} Qd2 {Threatening mate!} 43. Rf2 Qe1+ {
The rest of the game was played at an even faster rate as we ran short of time.
} 44. Rf1 Qe4 45. Rf2 Bd4 46. Qf3 Qf5 47. Rd2 Be5 48. Rf2 Qg6 49. Rd2 Kg7 50.
Rf2 Rf8 {He was just moving his Rook back and forth at high speed. I didn't
have time to do much calculation but felt that there must be a way of
complicating it.} 51. Qd1 Qe4 52. Qf3 Qg6 53. Bd3 Qf6 54. Qg4 h5 {A fast time
scramble with moves being played instantaneously.} 55. Qd7+ Rf7 56. Qb5 h4 57.
Bxf4 Bxf4 58. Qb1 Qd4 59. Qf1 Qxd5 $2 60. Rf3 $2 ({Missing} 60. Bc4) 60... Re7
61. a5 Rc7 (61... c4 $142) 62. a6 c4 63. Qa1+ Kh6 $4 64. a7 $4 {Missing the
choice of two mates.} (64. Qf6+ Kh5 65. Qg6#) (64. Qh8+ Rh7 65. Qxh7#) 64...
Rc8 $4 (64... cxd3 $1 65. Qh8+ Kg6 66. Rxf4 gxf4 67. a8=Q Qxa8 68. Qxa8 dxc2
69. Qg8+ $11) 65. Bf1 $4 (65. Qf6+ Kh5 66. Qg6#) 65... Qc6 {White lost on time}
0-1

