{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 c5 6. d5 O-O
7. Nf3 Bg4 8. Be2 Nbd7 9. O-O Bxf3 10. Bxf3 a6 11. a4 Ne8 12. g4 {Against an
opponent who is not familiar with this line, 12.g4 is good.} e6 13. Be3 {
I wasn't sure at all here, but this is best.} Rb8 14. Qd2 Qe7 (14... exd5 $142)
15. Rad1 h6 16. dxe6 fxe6 (16... Qxe6 17. Nd5 Kh7) 17. e5 Bxe5 {A touch of
desperation after much thought.} (17... Nb6 $142) 18. fxe5 Nxe5 19. Be2 Rxf1+
20. Rxf1 g5 21. Bf2 Nf6 22. h3 Rd8 23. Bg3 Nc6 24. Qd3 Kg7 25. Ne4 Nxe4 26.
Qxe4 d5 {Loses outright. However, he was short of time.} 27. Be5+ Nxe5 28.
Qxe5+ Kg8 {He now decided not to wait for 29.Rf6 and resigned.} 1-0

