{30' each/game} 1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. d3 O-O 5. g3 c6 6. Bg2 d6 7.
O-O e5 8. Be3 h6 9. h3 Nbd7 10. Qd2 Kh7 11. Ne4 Qc7 (11... Nxe4 {Leaves my
d-Pawn weak}) 12. Rac1 Ng8 {To play ........f5} (12... Ne8 {covering d6 is
better}) 13. c5 (13. Qb4 $142) 13... dxc5 (13... d5 $142 14. Nd6 d4 15. Bg5 f6
16. Bh4 g5) 14. Nxc5 Nb6 15. Ne1 Rd8 16. Qc2 Nd5 17. Bd2 Ngf6 18. Ne4 Nxe4 19.
Bxe4 $2 {Overlooking the loss of a pawn.} Bxh3 20. Ng2 Nf6 21. Rfd1 Nxe4 22.
dxe4 Rd7 23. Be3 a6 ({Fritz prefers} 23... Rxd1+ 24. Rxd1 Rd8 25. Rxd8 Qxd8 26.
Nh4 Be6 27. b3 Bf6 {However, in quickplay games one wants to "play safe" and
not leave the a-Pawn hanging.}) 24. Qc5 Rad8 25. Rxd7 Rxd7 26. a4 Qd8 27. Qb4
Bf8 (27... Rd1+ 28. Kh2 Rxc1 29. Bxc1 Qd1 30. Qd2 Qxd2 31. Bxd2) 28. Qb3 Be6
29. Qc2 Qa5 30. b3 Qb4 31. Rd1 $4 {Having to move fast now he blunders.} (31.
Rb1 f5 32. f3 fxe4 33. fxe4 g5 34. Ne1 g4) 31... Rxd1+ {A property of
quickplay games-having instantly seen that I could win the b-Pawn and probably
the a-Pawn I didn't spend further time and moved quickly.} ({Clearly} 31...
Bxb3 {wins straight off, but Black still has an easy win after the text.}) 32.
Qxd1 Bxb3 33. Qd7 Qe7 34. Qd2 Bxa4 35. Nh4 Qd6 36. Qb2 Bb5 37. Kg2 f6 38. f4 {
He was having to move fast now. The rest of the game was pretty rapid.} exf4
39. Bxf4 Qe6 40. Nf3 Qxe4 41. Kf2 Qe6 42. Nd4 Bc5 43. e3 Bxd4 44. Qxd4 Qa2+ 45.
Kg1 Qf7 46. Kf2 a5 47. g4 g5 48. Qe4+ Kg7 49. Bg3 a4 50. Bd6 a3 {He can't take
the a-Pawn and only had seconds left.} 0-1

