{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 f5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Bf4 g6 4. h3 Bg7 5. c3 O-O 6. e3 c6
7. Nbd2 d6 8. Be2 Be6 ({I should play} 8... h6 $142 {first}) 9. O-O Nbd7 (9...
h6 $142) 10. Ng5 Bf7 11. Nxf7 Rxf7 12. Qc2 Qe8 13. Rfe1 Kh8 14. Rac1 b5 ({
Better is} 14... e5 {which I considered. However, the story of the game (c.f v
Mitchell Preston Open Rd2 28/11/09) is that he is graded 39 pts below me. I
have to win, he wants a draw. The whole game is me ignoring the best, but
drawish, moves, playing very risky onesthat may allow me to complicate.}) 15.
b3 Nd5 16. Bh2 Rc8 17. a3 e5 18. c4 Ne7 19. Nf3 h6 20. Qb1 bxc4 21. Bxc4 Rf8
22. dxe5 Nxe5 23. Nxe5 dxe5 24. Red1 c5 {I wasn't happy.} 25. Qd3 f4 (25... Qd8
{is better but I don't want to exchange.}) 26. e4 Nc6 27. Bb5 Qe7 28. Bxc6 Rxc6
29. Qc4 Rd8 30. Rxd8+ (30. Rd5 $142) 30... Qxd8 31. f3 Bf8 32. Kh1 Qc7 ({
Against a strong opponent I would play} 32... Rd6 {then if} 33. Qxc5 Rd1+ 34.
Rxd1 Qxd1+ 35. Qg1 Qxb3 {and wins the a-Pawn but I though it might be drawn.})
33. Bg1 Qa5 34. a4 (34. b4 $142) 34... Kg7 35. Qd5 Qc7 {After much thought.}
36. Bf2 g5 37. Be1 Kf6 38. Ba5 Qc8 (38... Qd6 $142 {is better but I want to
keep Queens on.}) 39. Qd8+ $2 {At last I am winning!} (39. Bc3 $142) 39... Qxd8
40. Bxd8+ Ke6 41. Kg1 Ra6 42. h4 {His Bishop is stuck so he tries to get it
out.} Rd6 43. Ba5 gxh4 44. Be1 Rd3 {We were both getting short of time so play
speeded up.} 45. Rc3 Rd1 46. Kf2 Bd6 47. Ke2 Rb1 48. Bxh4 Rb2+ 49. Kf1 Kd7 50.
Bf2 Kc6 51. g3 $5 {Fritz says this is OK, but I get a passed Pawn.} Rb1+ 52.
Ke2 Be7 53. gxf4 exf4 54. Kd3 h5 55. e5 $2 {Loses it} ({Correct is} 55. Kc2 Rf1
56. Bxc5 Bxc5 57. b4 Kd6 58. Rxc5 $11) 55... h4 56. Kc2 Rf1 57. Bxh4 Bxh4 58.
Kd2 Be1+ 59. Ke2 Bxc3 60. Kxf1 Bxe5 61. Ke2 Kd5 62. Kd3 Bf6 63. Kc2 Kd4 64. Kd2
a5 0-1

