{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. b6 d6 6. Nc3 Qxb6
7. e4 g6 8. Bd3 Bg7 9. h3 O-O 10. Nf3 Nbd7 11. O-O a5 {I felt that this gives
me a nice hole on b5 but Fritz thinks it's OK.} 12. a4 Ba6 13. Re1 Bxd3 14.
Qxd3 {[9']} Ne8 {[32']} 15. Bg5 Nc7 (15... Qxb2 16. Nb5 Nef6 17. Rab1 Qa2 18.
Ra1 Qb2 $11) 16. Rab1 (16. Bxe7 Rfe8 17. Bg5 Qxb2 18. Bd2 Ne5 19. Nxe5 Bxe5 20.
Rab1 $14) 16... Rfe8 17. Nd2 Ne5 18. Qc2 h6 19. Be3 Na6 20. Nb5 Nb4 21. Qb3 g5
{To prevent f4.} 22. Kh1 ({22.Kh1 avoids lines like} 22. f4 gxf4 23. Bxf4 c4+)
22... Qb7 23. f4 gxf4 24. Bxf4 Ned3 25. Rf1 Rf8 26. Bg3 Qd7 27. Nc4 {[32']}
Rab8 {[1hr 15'] I felt this as wrong but Fritz says it's OK.} 28. Nxa5 Rxb5 $2
$18 {He played this very quickly and afterwards said he did it "to get some
play".} (28... Nxb2 29. Rxb2 Rxb5 30. axb5 Qxb5 31. Rbb1 Qxa5 $16) 29. axb5
Qxb5 30. Nc6 Re8 31. Nxb4 Nxb4 32. Be1 $4 {As I let go of the piece it hit me.
Once again, after very careful play, having achieved a won game I relaxed and
became casual. Ludicrous!} Qxf1+ 33. Kh2 {I should resign, of course, but
momentum made me move.} Be5+ 34. g3 {I was about to resign when he offered a
draw! I couldn't believe it. He said that I had outplayed him and he didn't
want to win on the basis of my blunder. Amazing! Very sporting but I
suggestedthat, in future, if money was involved he should be more ruthless.}
1/2-1/2

