{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. e3 Bg7 5. Be2 O-O 6. Nf3 c6
7. b4 Na6 8. a3 Nc7 9. Qc2 d6 10. O-O Qe8 11. Bb2 h6 12. Rad1 Be6 13. Rfe1 Qf7
14. Nb1 Ne4 15. Nbd2 g5 16. Rf1 ({Naturally not} 16. Nxe4 fxe4 17. Qxe4 Bf5 {
winning the Queen.}) 16... g4 17. Nh4 Nxd2 18. Rxd2 Bf6 $2 {Rubbish. I
realised immediately.} 19. d5 $2 {To my great relief.} ({Correct is} 19. Nxf5
Bg5 20. Ng3 d5 21. Bd3 Qe8) 19... Bxh4 20. dxe6 Nxe6 21. g3 Bg5 22. Bd3 Nc7 23.
Re2 e5 24. Qc3 Bf6 $2 {Unbelievable! I was having one of those days. Not only
do I blunder twice but both times with the same move!} ({Correct is.} 24... Qg6
) 25. Bxf5 Qh5 26. Qc2 Be7 27. e4 Ne8 28. f4 gxf3 29. Ref2 Ng7 30. Rxf3 Nxf5
31. Rxf5 Rxf5 32. Rxf5 Qg4 33. c5 {I was now getting short of time and had to
move quickly.} Rf8 34. Rf2 ({The spectators thought 33.......Rf8 was wrong as} 
34. cxd6 Rxf5 ({However} 34... Bxd6 35. Rxf8+ Kxf8 36. Bxe5 Bxe5 37. Qc5+ Kf7
38. Qxe5) 35. dxe7 {wins}) 34... Rxf2 35. Kxf2 Qe6 {I thought that it had to
be a draw now, especially as I was short of time. However, I felt that I had
to try to win, so carried on, playing fast. he had plenty of time but also 
(unnecessarily) speeded up.} 36. cxd6 Bxd6 37. Qe2 Bc7 38. Kg2 Kh7 39. Bc1 Bb6
40. Qf3 Qa2+ 41. Kh3 Qe6+ 42. Qf5+ Qxf5+ 43. exf5 c5 {The only chance lies in
my QS Pawn majority. We were moving quite fast now.} 44. bxc5 Bxc5 45. g4 b5
46. Kg3 a5 47. Kf3 b4 48. axb4 axb4 49. h4 (49. Bb2 {Draws more easily.}) 49...
b3 50. Ke4 Bd4 51. Kd5 b2 52. Bxb2 Bxb2 53. g5 h5 {Trying to keep the Pawn on.
Unfortunately the Queening square is the wrong colour.} 54. Ke4 Kg7 55. Kd5 Kf7
56. Ke4 Bc3 57. Kd5 Ke7 58. Ke4 {He now announced (in my time) that it was
clearly a draw unless anyone did anything silly and "what did I think?" I just
played on.} Kd6 {Not played with any expectation other than a draw. However,
it was going fast so maybe.........?} 59. Kd3 Bd4 60. Ke4 Bf2 61. g6 Ke7 62.
Kxe5 Bxh4 63. Ke4 Bf6 64. Kf4 Kf8 65. Kg3 Kg7 66. Kf4 Kh6 67. Ke4 Kg5 68. Kf3
Kxf5 69. Kg3 Ke4 70. Kh3 Kf5 71. Kg3 Ke4 72. Kh3 Kf3 73. Kh2 Kf2 74. Kh3 $4 {
Unbelieveable. [Dick did not analyse this with an engine, nor did he have
tablebases]} (74. Kh1 {and I would agree a draw.}) 74... Kg1 75. Kg3 Be7 76.
Kf4 (76. Kh3 h4 77. Kg4 Kg2 {etc Dick missed} 78. g7 $1 h3 79. g8=Q h2 80. Qd5+
Kg1 81. Qd1+ Kg2 82. Qd2+ Kg1 83. Kg3 Bd6+ 84. Qxd6 h1=Q (84... h1=N+ 85. Kf3)
85. Qd1#) 76... h4 77. Kg4 Kg2 78. Kh5 h3 {John Chibnall resigned!} 0-1

