1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 Be7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. O-O dxc4 {Fritz likes
this but it opens the long diagonal.} 7. Qc2 c6 8. Qxc4 Nbd7 9. Nc3 Nb6 10. Qb3
c5 11. Bf4 c4 (11... cxd4 12. Nb5 {would cause him some bother.}) 12. Qc2 Nbd5
13. Rfd1 Nxf4 14. gxf4 Qc7 15. e3 a6 16. a4 Bd7 17. Ne5 Rfd8 18. Ne4 Rac8 ({
Fritz prefers} 18... Nxe4 19. Bxe4 f5 {(else the c-Pawn goes)} 20. Bf3 Bd6 21.
Nxc4 Rac8) 19. Ng5 Be8 20. Ng4 {Effectively forcing him to weaken the KS Pawns.
} g6 21. Ne5 Bf8 22. Rdc1 b5 23. axb5 axb5 24. Ra2 Nd5 {Prevents 25.Rca1
because of 25......Nb4} 25. Bxd5 exd5 26. Rca1 {Fritz gives this -0.81 but I'd
rather be White!} Rb8 27. f5 Be7 28. f4 Bxg5 29. fxg5 gxf5 30. Qxf5 Qc8 31. Qf4
Rb7 32. Ng4 Bc6 {He seemed unsure what to do now and was getting short of time}
33. Nf6+ Kh8 34. Qh4 {Making life difficult for myself.} ({Correct is} 34. Ra8)
34... Qf5 35. Ra6 Rc7 36. Rf1 Qg6 37. Qg3 Rcc8 38. Qe5 Qg7 39. Rf4 {The threat
of 40.Rh4 is a bit of a killer. Also he had little time left.} Qg6 {Having to
move fast this leaves a discovered check but if I reply quickly with 40Rh4
then 40......Qb1+ offers some hope.} 40. Nxd5+ (40. Rh4 Qb1+) 40... Qg7 41. Nf6
1-0

