{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 3. Nf3 d6 4. Nc3 Nc6 5. Bb5 Bg4 6. d3
Nge7 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Qxf3 a6 9. Ba4 O-O {After his reply I felt that I'd gone
wrong, but Fritz gives 9......0-0 as best.} 10. f5 f6 {I spent a long time
over this. I felt that I was in trouble. Fritz gives it as OK.} ({Best is} 
10... Nd4 11. Qg4 b5 12. Bb3 Kh8) 11. Bb3+ Kh8 12. h4 Nd4 13. Qh3 Nxb3 14. axb3
c6 15. Be3 Bxe3 16. Qxe3 Re8 (16... d5 {Fritz}) 17. g4 Rc8 (17... d5) 18. g5
Ng8 (18... d5) 19. O-O-O Rc7 (19... d5) 20. Rdg1 Rd7 21. Rg2 Rf8 22. Rhg1 Qe8
23. Qf3 Qd8 24. Qf2 Qe8 {I offered a draw here.} 25. Na4 b5 26. Nc3 Qd8 ({
Fritz prefers} 26... Qb8 {or 26......Qb8 followed by} 27. Z0 a5) 27. Kd2 {
Fritz doesn't like this.} d5 {I was now getting short of time and started to
speed up.} 28. Qc5 Qc8 29. Ra1 Rfd8 30. exd5 cxd5 31. Qxc8 Rxc8 32. Rxa6 {
We were both having to move quickly now.} fxg5 33. hxg5 Ne7 {Although a Pawn
down I now felt I had some play.} 34. Rf2 b4 35. Nd1 e4 36. d4 Rdc7 37. Ne3 Nc6
38. c3 bxc3+ 39. bxc3 Nb8 40. Ra2 {Played instantly} (40. Re6 $142) 40... Rxc3
{here I offered a draw which he accepted immediately.} (40... Rxc3 {0.12/0
Draw accepted} 41. Nxd5 Rxb3 42. Rc2 Rxc2+ 43. Kxc2 Rd3 44. f6 gxf6 45. gxf6
Nd7 46. f7 Kg7 47. Nb6 Nf8 48. d5 Rf3 49. Re2 Kxf7 50. Rxe4 h5 51. d6 Kf6 52.
Kd2 Kg5 53. Ke2 Rf6 54. d7 Nxd7 55. Nxd7 $11) 1/2-1/2

