{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. h3 Nd7 5. Nc3 b6 6. Be3 Bb7
7. Bd3 e6 8. Qd2 a6 9. a3 Qe7 {With thoughts of QS castling........} 10. b4 {
.....but not now} Ngf6 11. Rd1 O-O 12. O-O Rfc8 13. Rfe1 Qf8 14. Qc1 Nh5 {
I had to win against this opponent and try to create complications rather than
anything solid but drawish.} 15. g4 Nhf6 16. Bg5 c5 17. bxc5 dxc5 18. Be3 $2 {
Not good.} (18. d5 $142 Nxg4 19. hxg4 Bxc3) 18... cxd4 {This seemed good so I
didn't look too hard for more.} (18... Nxg4 $142) 19. Bxd4 Qe7 {This threatens
......e5 but I wasn't happy with it.} (19... Nxg4 $142 20. Bxg7 Qxg7 21. Nd5
Nxf2 22. Ne7+ Kf8 23. Nxc8 Nxd1) 20. Nb1 Nc5 21. Bxc5 (21. Qb2 $142) (21. Nc3
$142) 21... Rxc5 22. Re2 Nd7 23. Qe3 Rac8 24. Red2 R5c7 25. g5 Nc5 26. h4 e5 {
I like this with Ne6-f4 a possibility or Qe6-g4} ({Fritz prefers} 26... Na4) ({
or} 26... b5) 27. Ne1 Qe6 28. Qf3 f5 {This works well although I had
overlooked one point.} 29. gxf6 (29. Nc3 $142) 29... Bxf6 {A little careless.}
30. Ng2 {Also missing the best move.......} ({.....which is} 30. Bc4 Qxc4 31.
Qxf6 Rf8 32. Rd8 Rcf7 33. Rxf8+ Rxf8 34. Rd8 Qf7) 30... Rf8 31. Qe3 Rcf7 32.
Qe2 b5 (32... Nxd3 33. Rxd3 Be7) 33. Qe3 Be7 {To recolocate on c5} 34. Rf1 Rf3
35. Qe2 Qg4 36. Qe1 Nxe4 (36... Ne6 {is even quicker}) 37. Bxe4 (37. Be2 Qh3 ({
I had intended} 37... Nxd2 38. Qxd2 {......Nxd2 looks better}) 38. Bxf3 Rxf3
39. Qxe4 Bxe4) 37... Bxe4 38. Qe2 Bc5 {End of storey. White has no move.} 39.
Nc3 Rxf2 40. Qxg4 Rxg2+ 41. Kh1 Rxf1# 0-1

