{1hr 30' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c6 4. Nc3 Bb4 5. Qb3 Ba5 6. e4 {
Fritz doesn't like this but it prevents ......d5} h6 7. Nge2 O-O 8. O-O d6 9.
d3 (9. d4 {Fritz}) (9. a3 {Fritz}) 9... Na6 10. a3 Nc5 11. Qc2 Rb8 $4 {Playing
too quickly he gives away a piece.} 12. b4 Nxd3 {He now played on in rather
dejected fashion and eventually blubders again.} 13. Qxd3 Bc7 14. Be3 b6 15. h3
Bb7 16. Kh2 {A piece up I keep everything neat and tidy before pushing on with
b5} Qe7 17. f4 exf4 18. Bxf4 {Fritz prefers 18.gxf4 but, a piece up, I keep it
simple.} Nh5 19. Rae1 Rbd8 20. Qe3 Nxf4 (20... g5 21. Qf3 {Might have been
worth a try.}) 21. Nxf4 Rfe8 22. b5 Qe5 (22... d5 $142 23. bxc6 d4 24. Ncd5
dxe3 25. Nxe7+ Rxe7 26. cxb7) 23. bxc6 Bxc6 24. Nfd5 Bb8 25. Rf5 Qe6 26. Ref1 (
{Quicker is} 26. Nf6+ Kf8 (26... gxf6 27. Qxh6) 27. Nxe8 {I briefly considered
all this but a piece up I kept it simple.}) 26... Rf8 27. Nf4 (27. Nf6+ Kh8 28.
Rh5 {is still on}) 27... Qxc4 {This leaves the Queen cut off from the KS.} 28.
Ncd5 Rde8 29. Rc1 Qa2 {The Bishop goes.} ({If} 29... Qa4 30. Nf6+ gxf6 (30...
Kh8 31. Rh5) 31. Nh5) 30. Rxc6 {This win gave me the club championship title
with 7.5/8} 1-0

