{30' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. g3 Bb4+ 4. Bd2 a5 5. Nc3 Bd7 6. Bg2 Nf6 7.
cxd5 Bxc3 8. bxc3 exd5 9. Qb3 Bc6 10. Nf3 O-O 11. O-O a4 12. Qc2 Bb5 13. Rab1 (
13. Rfb1 Bxe2 14. Rxb7) 13... Bxe2 14. Rfe1 Ba6 15. Qxa4 ({Fritz prefers} 15.
Ne5 {However, in a quickplay game it pays tokeep it simple and regain the Pawn.
}) 15... Nc6 16. Qc2 Na5 17. Bg5 Nc4 18. Qf5 Nd6 19. Qe5 Nde4 20. Nh4 {Trying
to work up some tactics, but Black gets on top.} Re8 21. Bxf6 Nxf6 22. Qf4 Bc4
23. Nf5 {Starting to feel that I had gone wrong. The a-pawn is going. However,
in a quickplay game, anything can happen.} Bd3 24. Rbc1 Rxa2 25. Ne3 {Prevents
.....Rc2} Ne4 {Leaving me no choice with f2 threatened.} 26. Bxe4 Bxe4 27. f3
Bg6 $2 {A mistake.} ({Correct is} 27... g5 28. Qg4 Bg6 29. f4 gxf4 30. gxf4 Re4
) 28. Nxd5 Ree2 (28... h5 $142) 29. Rxe2 Rxe2 30. Qxc7 Qa8 (30... Qe8 $142 {
then} 31. g4 Bd3 32. Qf4 h6 33. h4) 31. Ne7+ (31. Nf4 {is equally good.}) 31...
Kh8 32. Qc8+ Qxc8 33. Nxc8 h6 34. Nd6 b6 {Moving fast now.} 35. Nc4 b5 36. Nd6
Bd3 37. Nxf7+ Kg8 38. Ne5 Re3 39. h4 Bh7 $2 {Moving fast he overlooks the
reply.} (39... Bc4 $142) 40. Kf2 1-0

