{3.' each/game} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 Qb6 6. Bd3 Bd7 7.
Bc2 Rc8 8. O-O f5 9. a3 c4 10. Re1 Nge7 11. Nbd2 Ng6 $5 12. Nf1 $2 ({
Overlooking} 12. Bxf5 $1 exf5 13. e6) 12... Be7 13. Rb1 Qc7 14. Bg5 {[6']} O-O
{[6']} 15. Bxe7 Ncxe7 16. Qd2 h6 17. Ng3 Nh8 18. Nh5 Be8 19. Ng3 g5 20. Nf1 (
20. h4 $142) 20... Bh5 21. Bd1 Bg6 22. Bc2 Nc6 23. h3 Qe7 24. N3h2 Rf7 25. g3
Rcf8 26. Qe2 f4 27. g4 f3 28. Qd2 Kg7 29. Ng3 Nb8 {To answer Nh5-f6 with ......
Nd7} 30. Bxg6 Nxg6 31. Nhf1 Nd7 32. Nh5+ Kg8 33. Qc2 Nh4 34. Nfg3 Qe8 35. Re3
Re7 36. Qd1 Qf7 37. Qc2 Kh8 {Getting short of time I saw that 38......Ng2 wins
the exchange but was worried about 38.Rxf3. Having to move quickly I decided
toplay it safe.} (37... Ng2 38. Rxf3 Qxf3 39. Qg6+ Kh8 40. Qxh6+) 38. b4 $2 {
Missing the threat.} Ng2 39. Rbe1 Nxe1 40. Rxe1 Qh7 41. Qxh7+ {I'd heve kept
the Queens on, but he was moving fast now.} Kxh7 42. Re3 (42. Nf1 $142) 42...
Ref7 43. a4 a6 (43... a5 $142 {since} 44. b5 {loses to} Nb6) 44. Re1 Kg6 45.
Rb1 Ra8 46. Kf1 Nb6 47. a5 {Now it's easy for me to break throught.} Na4 48.
Rc1 Nb2 49. Rc2 Nd3 50. Rd2 b6 51. axb6 Rb7 52. Nf6 Rxb6 53. Kg1 a5 54. bxa5
Rxa5 55. Kh2 Rb3 56. Rc2 Raa3 57. Ne8 Rxc3 58. Rb2 $4 {Moving fast he blunders.
However, it was lost anyway.} Nxb2 59. Nc7 {Never resign in a time rush!} Kf7
60. Nh5 Rc2 61. Kg3 Rxf2 0-1

