{30' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. e4 {In quickplay it is often a good idea to play
"something different"} Nf6 3. Nc3 Nc6 4. Nf3 Bc5 5. Be2 d6 6. a3 a5 7. d3 h6 8.
Be3 Bd4 9. Bxd4 Nxd4 10. Nxd4 exd4 11. Nb5 c5 12. f4 O-O 13. O-O Ne8 14. Qd2 b6
15. f5 Ba6 16. a4 Bxb5 17. axb5 Nf6 18. h3 ({I wanted to play} 18. Rf3 {
and then to g3 or h3, but Black replies} Ng4 19. Rg3 Ne3) 18... Nd7 19. Rf3 (
19. g4 {Might be better.}) 19... Ne5 20. Rg3 Kh7 21. Rf1 Rg8 22. f6 g6 23. Qf4
{I was begining to wonder how I would break through. However, I was up on the
clock.} Qf8 24. h4 Re8 25. Rh3 Re6 26. g4 Nd7 27. Kh1 $6 {Moving fast I simply
overlook his reply. However, this will at least provide some way of opening up
the position.} Rxf6 28. Qg3 Rxf1+ 29. Bxf1 Ne5 30. Qf4 Qc8 31. Be2 h5 32. Rg3
hxg4 33. Bxg4 Nxg4 {Black's Knight was a better piece than the Bishop.} 34.
Rxg4 Qc7 35. Rg3 Kg7 36. Kg2 Rh8 37. Rf3 Qe7 38. Rh3 {I couldn't see how I was
going to make progress. However, he was getting very short of time so a
mistake could come.} f6 {and here is a small mistake} ({Much better is} 38...
Rh5) 39. Qg4 Kf7 40. Rg3 Rg8 41. h5 g5 42. h6 Qe6 43. Qh5+ Ke7 44. h7 Rh8 {
It is still 0.00. I was still hoping for a mistake.} 45. Rh3 Qf7 46. Qh6 Kd7
47. Rh1 Ke7 {He offered a draw here. I only carried on because he only now had
60'' left.} 48. Qh3 Qg6 49. Kg3 Kd8 $2 {51 The mistake at last! I felt I now
had a win. The big mistake is on move} 50. Qe6 Rxh7 51. Qxd6+ Kc8 $4 {He had
to play instantaneously.} (51... Ke8 52. Qe6+ Kf8 53. Rxh7 Qxh7 54. Qxf6+ Qf7
55. Qd8+ Kg7 56. Qxg5+ Qg6 57. Qxg6+ Kxg6 58. Kf3 Kf6) 52. Qc6+ Kd8 {It
doesn't really matter.} (52... Kb8 53. Qxb6+ Kc8 54. Qxc5+ Kb8 55. Qb6+ Kc8 56.
Qe6+ Kb8 57. Qd6+ Kc8) 53. Qxb6+ (53. Qa8+ {Dick's Fritz gives this mate in17!}
) 53... Kc8 54. Qxc5+ Rc7 55. Rh8+ Kd7 56. Qxd4+ {Black lost on time.} 1-0

