1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. h4 Bd7 ({of course he can't play} 4... e6 $2 {
.......}) ({.....but} 4... h6 {is fine}) 5. Bd3 e6 6. c3 c5 {Now we are in a
French Defence} 7. f4 Nc6 8. Nf3 c4 (8... Nh6 {Looks better.}) 9. Bc2 Qb6 10.
Nbd2 Nge7 11. Nf1 h5 12. Ne3 g6 13. Qe2 Bh6 14. g3 Nf5 15. Kf2 Nxe3 16. Qxe3
O-O-O 17. Nd2 Ne7 18. b3 cxb3 19. Nxb3 {I much prefer White's position!} ({
Fritz gives} 19. axb3) 19... Nf5 20. Qf3 Qc7 21. Rb1 Bc6 22. Ba3 Bf8 23. Bxf8
Rdxf8 24. Qe2 Ba4 $5 25. Nc5 Bc6 {Best} ({Not} 25... Bxc2 26. Rxb7 {and if}
Qxb7 27. Nxb7 Be4 28. Qa6 Bxh1 29. Qc6+ Kb8 30. Nc5 Z0 31. Na6#) 26. Rb2 Qa5
27. Qd2 b6 28. Nb3 Qa3 29. Rhb1 Qe7 30. Qd3 {Keeping it secure and ruling out
any threat of ......Nxh4} f6 $2 {Black tries to get some play but this fatally
weakens e6.} (30... Qa3 $142) 31. Qa6+ (31. Nc5 $142 Bb7 32. Rxb6 axb6 33. Rxb6
fxe5 34. Rxb7 Qxb7 35. Nxb7) 31... Qb7 {Best} 32. Qa3 Qe7 $2 (32... Rf7 $142
33. Nc5 Qa8 34. exf6 Rxf6 35. Qa6+ Bb7) 33. Nc5 $1 fxe5 (33... Rf7 34. Qa6+ Bb7
35. Qxa7) 34. Qa6+ Kd8 (34... Bb7 35. Qxa7 exd4 36. Qxb6 dxc3 37. Qxb7+ Qxb7
38. Rxb7 {is terminal}) 35. Rxb6 $1 {Not too difficult to spot but still a
nice move to play.} axb6 36. Qxb6+ Ke8 ({He can't play} 36... Qc7 {as e6 is
unprotected.}) 37. Qxc6+ Kf7 38. Rb7 Qxb7 39. Qxb7+ Kf6 {Mate in 1 but it
makes no difference.} ({If} 39... Kg8 40. Nxe6 exf4 41. Bxf5 Rh7 42. Qxh7+) ({
or} 39... Ne7 40. Qd7 Rh7 41. Nxe6 Kg8 42. Nxf8) 40. fxe5# 1-0

