{30' each/game} 1. g4 {I had already won the quickplay with this game to go.
Also, Brian tends to play a rather stodgy style, so I thought I'd try to make
it interesting.} e5 2. Bg2 d6 {This is his style. Rather than 2......d5} 3. h3
h6 4. c4 Nf6 5. d3 Be7 6. Nc3 Nc6 7. f4 {Fritz doesn't like this but it's Ok
for quickplay.} exf4 8. Bxf4 Be6 9. Nf3 d5 10. b3 (10. Qb3 {Fritz}) 10... a6 (
10... Bb4 $142 11. Bd2 O-O) 11. O-O O-O 12. Qc1 Bc5+ 13. Kh1 d4 14. Nd1 (14.
Na4 $142) (14. Nd5 $142) 14... Ne7 15. Ne5 c6 16. Bxh6 Ne8 ({Intending to
answer} 16... gxh6 {with} 17. Qxh6) (16... Bd6 $142) 17. Bf4 Bd6 18. Nf3 Bxf4
19. Qxf4 c5 20. Ng5 Ng6 21. Nxe6 Nxf4 $4 {This loses it. With time getting on
he played this very quickly} (21... fxe6 $142 22. Qg3 Rxf1+ 23. Bxf1 Qd6) 22.
Nxd8 Nxg2 23. Nxb7 Ne3 24. Nxe3 dxe3 25. Nxc5 Nd6 {It is hopeless but one
tends to carry on in a quickplay.} 26. Rf3 Rfe8 27. Rd1 a5 28. d4 Rad8 29. Rd3
Ne4 30. Nxe4 Rxe4 31. Rfxe3 Rde8 32. Rxe4 Rxe4 33. e3 Kf8 34. Kg2 Ke8 35. Kf3
Re7 36. e4 Kd8 37. e5 g6 38. Ke4 f6 39. Rf3 fxe5 40. dxe5 Rh7 41. Kd5 Re7 42.
Rf6 {This secured me 100% in the quickplay.} 1-0

