{1hr 30' each/game} 1. Nf3 f5 2. c4 Nf6 3. b3 g6 4. Bb2 Bg7 5. Nc3 d6 6. d4 O-O
7. e3 c6 8. Bd3 Qc7 9. O-O Rd8 {A bit artificial} 10. Rc1 Nbd7 11. e4 fxe4 12.
Nxe4 Nxe4 13. Bxe4 Nf6 14. Re1 Nxe4 15. Rxe4 Bf5 16. Re1 {[32']} Rf8 {[11']}
17. Nh4 Bc8 {Tyring to keep the 2 Bishops; also his Knight is offside on h4.}
18. Qd2 Bf6 19. Nf3 Bg4 20. Ng5 Qd7 21. h3 Bf5 22. Ne4 Bg7 23. g4 (23. d5 $142)
(23. Bc3 $142) 23... Bxe4 24. Rxe4 Rae8 25. Rf4 h5 {This was one of those
games where my opponent would be happy with a draw, but I am struggling to
create some play.} 26. Rxf8+ Rxf8 27. Qg5 (27. Qd3 $142) 27... Qe8 {This is OK
but.......} (27... Qe6 {is better}) 28. Rc2 hxg4 29. hxg4 Qf7 30. d5 e5 31.
dxc6 bxc6 32. Qe3 Qf4 33. Qe2 Qf3 ({Fritz prefers} 33... e4) 34. Qxf3 Rxf3 35.
Kg2 Rf7 {Slightly better is 35......Rd3 but I wanted my Rook behind the Pawns.
He was now getting short of time.} 36. Re2 Rd7 $2 {Too casual.} ({I realised
immediately the correct move.} 36... Re7) 37. Kg3 (37. c5 $142 dxc5 38. Bxe5 a5
39. Kg3 Bxe5+ 40. Rxe5 Rd2) 37... g5 38. b4 {He was really having to start
moving quickly now and hoping to simplify.} (38. c5 {is no longer an option, as
} d5 39. f3 (39. Rxe5) (39. Bxe5 Re7 40. f4 gxf4+ 41. Kxf4 d4 42. Bxg7 Rxe2)
39... Re7) 38... Kf7 39. Re3 Ke6 40. Bc3 d5 41. cxd5+ cxd5 42. Bd2 Bf6 {
I felt that I was clearly winning here, but it's 0.00! However, he was running
short of time and having to move very fast. I had 25' left.} 43. f3 (43. Ra3
$142) 43... Rc7 44. Rc3 (44. Ra3) 44... Rxc3 45. Bxc3 d4 46. Bb2 $2 {Big
mistake at last but he was having to move almost immediately.} (46. Bd2 $142)
46... Kd5 47. Kf2 Kc4 48. a3 ({If} 48. Ke2 e4 $1) ({If} 48. Bc1 Kxb4 49. Ke2
Kc3 50. Kd1 Bd8 51. Ba3 Kd3 52. Bc1 a5 53. Bd2 a4 54. Bc1 Bf6 55. Bd2 Be7 56.
Bc1 Kc3 57. Bd2+ Kb2) ({or} 48. Ke1 Kxb4 49. Kd2 Kc4 50. Ba3 Bd8 51. Bc1 a5 52.
Bb2 a4 53. Bc1 Be7 54. Kc2 d3+ 55. Kd2 Bb4+ 56. Kd1 {and now} d2 57. Bb2 ({or} 
57. Bxd2 Bxd2 58. Kxd2 Kd4 59. a3 Kc4 60. Kc2 e4 61. fxe4 Kd4 62. Kd2 Kxe4 63.
Ke2 Kf4 {etc.}) 57... Kd5 58. Ke2 a3 59. Ba1 e4 60. fxe4+ Kxe4) 48... Kd3 49.
Bc1 Kc2 50. Be3 dxe3+ 0-1

