{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. b6 Qxb6 6. Nc3
Bb7 {The Bishop simply blocks the half-open file.} 7. e4 d6 8. Nf3 g6 9. Be2
Bg7 10. O-O O-O 11. h3 Nbd7 12. Nd2 a5 {Leaves a hole on b5} (12... Qc7 $142)
13. Nc4 {[4']} Qd8 {[11']} 14. Qc2 Ba6 15. Rb1 Bxc4 {He is left weak on the QS
white squares.} 16. Bxc4 Nb6 17. Be2 Qb8 18. b3 Rc8 19. Bb5 {[11']} e6 {
[23'] Leaves the d-Pawn weak.} 20. Bc6 Ra7 ({Fritz prefers} 20... Rxc6 21. dxc6
Qc7 22. Rd1 Qxc6 {but a human player is unlikely to go for this.}) 21. Re1 ({
Fritz prefers} 21. Rd1 {because of the variation below}) 21... Re7 (21... Nxe4
22. Rxe4 exd5 23. Nxd5 Rxc6 24. Qe2 Be5 25. Nf6+ Kg7) 22. Bd2 {Connecting the
Rooks and eying the a-Pawn.} Nfd7 23. a4 Ne5 24. Bb5 Qa8 25. f4 Ned7 26. Bc6
Qa6 (26... Bd4+ $142 27. Kh2 Qb8 28. Qd3 Bf2 29. Rf1 Bh4 30. Qa6 Nf6) 27. Nb5
Nb8 (27... exd5 $142 28. exd5 Rxe1+ 29. Rxe1 Bd4+ 30. Kh2 Nf6) 28. Nxd6 Rcc7
29. Qxc5 (29. Bb5 Qa7 30. Bf1 exd5 31. Nb5 Bd4+ 32. Kh2 Qb7 33. Nxc7) 29...
Nxc6 30. dxc6 Qd3 {Threatens 31......Bd4+} 31. Be3 Na8 {He picked up the
Knight and I think that he was going to put it on d7 when he noticed 32......
cxd7} 32. Qxa5 Qxd6 33. Qxa8+ Bf8 34. Rec1 1-0

