{2hrs each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 {Not good.} ({I had
intended} 4. cxd5 {which is better.}) 4... dxc4 5. e3 b5 6. Be2 e6 7. Bf3 Nd5
8. Nge2 Bd6 (8... Be7 $142) 9. Bxd6 Qxd6 10. O-O (10. a4 $142 b4 11. Ne4 Qc7
12. Rc1) 10... Nd7 11. Qd2 O-O 12. Rfc1 Ba6 13. a3 Qe7 14. Na2 (14. h3 $142) (
14. g3 $142) 14... Bb7 15. Re1 a5 16. Qc2 c5 17. a4 (17. Nec3 $142) 17... Nb4 (
17... b4 $142 18. Qxc4 N5b6 19. Qb5 Ba6) 18. Nxb4 Bxf3 {Fritz is happy with
this but we get chances on the g-file.} 19. gxf3 cxb4 20. axb5 (20. Ng3 {Fritz}
) 20... Qg5+ 21. Kh1 Qxb5 22. Rg1 {I felt I was lost here when his KS Pawns
advance.} Nf6 (22... a4 $142 23. e4 c3 {However, a human player (getting short
of time) is likely to be concerned about a KS attack by White.}) 23. Nf4 {
A KS attack offers the best chance.} b3 (23... a4 $142) 24. Qc3 Nd5 25. Nxd5
exd5 26. e4 Rfe8 27. e5 Re6 {A degree of panic over his Kings position.} (27...
Qb4 $142) 28. f4 Rg6 29. f5 Rxg1+ 30. Rxg1 {After 3 Rook moves he has simply
replaced the g1 Rook with the other one.} Qd7 31. f6 {Missing the draw.} ({
Correct is} 31. Qg3 g6 32. e6 Qc6 33. Qh4 Qe8 34. Qh6 c3 35. exf7+ {0.00/0})
31... g6 32. Qe3 Qf5 {Now he goes wrong} ({Correct is} 32... Qc8 33. Qh6 Qf8
34. Qh5 c3 35. e6 Kh8) 33. Qh6 1/2-1/2

