{40 in 1hr 40' + 20'} 1. d4 Nf6 2. g4 Nxg4 {Bob had shown me this some time
ago.} 3. e4 d6 ({I considered} 3... d5 {which is better}) 4. Be2 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5
(5... d5 {Fritz}) (5... g6 {Fritz}) 6. d5 b6 7. Be3 Ba6 8. f3 Bxe2 9. Ngxe2 g6
10. Qd2 Bg7 11. O-O-O Nbd7 12. h4 Nh5 13. Rdg1 O-O 14. Ng3 Nxg3 15. Rxg3 h5 {
Best, but I had taken 37' against his 7'} 16. Bg5 Bf6 17. Ne2 Kh7 18. Kb1 Rh8
19. Rf1 Bxg5 20. hxg5 Kg7 21. Qc3 Kg8 22. Nc1 a5 23. Nd3 Rc8 24. f4 exf4 25.
Rxf4 Rh7 26. Rf1 Qe7 {I am running short of time.} 27. e5 {-0.81/0 This is in
Bob's intuitive style. However it is} (27. Re1 $142) (27. Rgg1 $142) 27... Nxe5
28. Re1 h4 {Having to move fairly quickly now but I find the best move.} 29.
Rge3 h3 30. Nxe5 dxe5 31. Rxh3 {panic now! Very little time left} Qb4 {About
the only move} (31... Rxh3 32. Qxh3) ({He also threatens} 31... Z0 32. Rxh7
Kxh7 33. Qh3+) (31... Rg7 {loses to} 32. Reh1 {what to do?}) 32. Reh1 {Panic
again. Same problems as before. Little time so have to move quickly.} Rh5 $2 ({
In the rush. missing} 32... Qxc3 {having failed to spot} 33. Rxh7 Qe1+ $1 34.
Rxe1 Kxh7) 33. Rxh5 gxh5 34. Qxe5 Qg4 35. a3 Rd8 36. Re1 Qc4 $2 {Moving very
fast it goes. With time to think his reply is obvious} (36... Rd6) 37. g6 Qxd5
38. gxf7+ Qxf7 39. Qg5+ 1-0

