{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bb5 Bb4 5. d3 d6 6. Bg5
a6 7. Bxc6+ bxc6 8. O-O h6 9. a3 (9. Bh4 {Fritz}) 9... hxg5 10. axb4 g4 11. Ng5
$4 {Loses the Knight.} Ng8 ({Fritz prefers} 11... Nh5 12. f4 exf4 13. Ra5 c5
14. bxc5 Qxg5 {I felt that 11.......Ng8 was simpler.}) 12. Nxf7 {Realising
that the Knight is a goner.} Kxf7 13. f4 Ke8 (13... Qh4 {is no doubt better
but, a piece up, it makes sense to play it safe and simple.}) 14. Ne2 Qh4 15.
Ng3 {He has no move.} Qxh2+ 16. Kf2 exf4 17. Qxg4 {He made a comment here
about either resigning or keeping the game going and had decided to do the
latter. A bit odd!} Bxg4 18. Ne2 Bxe2 19. Rh1 Qg3+ 20. Kg1 f3 21. Rh2 f2+ 22.
Kh1 Rxh2# 1-0

