{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. e3 d5 3. f4 Bf5 4. Bd3 e6 5. Bxf5 {Now he will be
left with a weak e-Pawn.} exf5 6. Nf3 Ne4 {Probably better to play against the
e-Pawn.} 7. Nc3 Bb4 8. Bd2 Nc6 9. Qe2 a6 10. Nxe4 fxe4 11. Ne5 Bxd2+ 12. Qxd2
Nxe5 (12... Ne7 $142) 13. fxe5 Qh4+ 14. g3 Qh3 15. O-O-O O-O-O 16. Kb1 ({
White should play against the f-Pawn with} 16. Rhf1 Rd7 17. Rf4) 16... Qh6 17.
Rdf1 Rhf8 18. Qc3 (18. Rf4 $142) 18... f6 19. exf6 Rxf6 20. Rxf6 Qxf6 21. Qc5
$2 {He has to try to confront my f-file play.} (21. Qd2 $142) 21... Qf3 22. Re1
Qf2 23. Qc3 (23. Qb4 $142) 23... Qxh2 24. g4 Qg2 25. Qc5 Qxg4 26. a3 {He was
having to speed up now and plays progressively faster.} Qf3 {Controlling the
f-file.} 27. Qe7 Qf8 28. Qe6+ Kb8 29. Qh3 h6 30. Rf1 Qe7 31. Rf4 Rf8 32. Rxf8+
Qxf8 33. Qe6 c6 34. c4 {Now, moving very quickly, another Pawn goes.} Qf1+ 35.
Ka2 Qxc4+ 36. Kb1 Qd3+ 37. Ka2 Qxe3 $4 {Also moving quickly I give away half a
point.} 38. Qg8+ $4 {But....moving quickly he misses the perpetual.} (38. Qd6+
$1 Ka7 (38... Kc8 39. Qf8+ Kd7 40. Qxg7+ Ke6 41. Qg6+ Ke7 42. Qg7+) (38... Ka8
39. Qf8+ Ka7 40. Qc5+) 39. Qc5+ b6 (39... Kb8 40. Qf8+ Kc7 41. Qe7+ Kb6 42.
Qc5+) 40. Qe7+) 38... Ka7 39. Qxg7 h5 40. Qf8 Qxd4 41. Qf1 e3 42. a4 Qc4+ 0-1

