{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. g4 {First time I have tried this} Nxg4 3. e4
d6 4. Be2 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Bg5 Bg7 7. Qd2 c6 8. O-O-O Na6 9. Kb1 Be6 10. h4 (
10. Nf3 {Fritz}) 10... h6 11. Bf4 Qa5 12. f3 (12. a3 $142) (12. Bf3 $142) 12...
Nh5 13. Be3 b5 {I wanted to play 14.Nxb5 but ........Qxa2 mates. However, I
now become overambitious.} 14. Nd5 $4 {Horrific! I haven't miscalculated like
this for a long time.} Qxd2 ({I decided that after 14.Nd5} 14... Qxd2 15. Rxd2
cxd5 16. Bxb5+ Kd8 17. Bxa6 {is OK because} Ng3 {is no problem because the
Bishop on a6 covers f1. Ridiculous he just plays the moves in a different
order.}) 15. Rxd2 Ng3 {I realised instantly.} 16. Rh2 Nxe2 {All I could do was
play on, moving quickly, and hope for the best.} 17. Nxe2 cxd5 18. Rg2 dxe4 19.
fxe4 h5 20. a3 Bg4 21. Nc3 Nc7 22. Rg1 Bh6 23. Bxh6 Rxh6 24. Re1 e6 25. Na2 a5
26. Nc1 Rh8 27. Re3 Ke7 28. Rf2 f5 29. exf5 gxf5 30. Nd3 Nd5 31. Re1 Kf6 32.
Kc1 Rac8 33. Kd2 Rhe8 34. c3 Re7 35. a4 b4 36. Rc1 bxc3+ 37. bxc3 Rec7 38. Nf4
Nxc3 39. Re1 Re7 40. Re3 Nd1 $5 ({He misses} 40... Nb1+ $1 41. Kd3 Rc3# {
so maybe there is a tiny chance of stalemate.}) 41. Re1 Nxf2 42. Nd5+ exd5 43.
Re6+ Kf7 $5 ({Avoiding} 43... Rxe6 $4 {stalemate}) ({but missing the perfectly
playable} 43... Kxe6) 44. Rf6+ Kg8 45. Rg6+ Rg7 0-1

