{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. cxd5 cxd5 4. Nc3 Bg4 {Very strange-a
sort of Trompovsky reversed. It simply loses a Pawn.} 5. Qb3 (5. h3 {Fritz})
5... e6 6. Qxb7 Nd7 7. e3 ({I considered} 7. Bf4) 7... Ngf6 8. f3 Bh5 (8... Bf5
$142) 9. Bd3 Be7 10. Qb3 {Continuing safety play.} O-O 11. Nge2 e5 $5 {He
decided that, a Pawn down, but up in development he could sacrifice a Pawn for
tactical chances.} 12. Nxd5 exd4 (12... Nxd5 $142 13. Qxd5 Nc5 14. Bc4 Nd3+ 15.
Kd2 Nb4) 13. Nxe7+ Qxe7 14. exd4 {To take c5 & d5 away from the Knight.} (14.
Nxd4 $142 Nc5 15. Qa3 Nxd3+ 16. Qxd3 Qb4+ 17. Kf2 Rfd8 18. Rd1) 14... Rab8 15.
Qc2 Rfc8 16. Qd2 Nb6 17. O-O {Black has got some play for his Pawn but not
enough.} Nc4 18. Bxc4 Rxc4 19. b3 Rc7 20. Bb2 Re8 21. Nf4 Qd6 22. Nxh5 Nxh5 23.
Rfe1 Rd8 24. Rac1 Rcd7 25. Rc4 Nf6 26. Qc1 Qa6 27. a3 Nd5 28. Re4 Qb5 29. Rc8
f5 ({Not} 29... Qxb3 $2 30. Rxd8+) 30. Re8+ Rxe8 31. Rxe8+ Kf7 32. Re5 Qxb3 33.
Rxf5+ Nf6 34. Qc3 Qd1+ 35. Kf2 Kg6 36. Re5 h5 37. Re1 Qa4 38. Qd3+ Kf7 39. Rc1
(39. Re2 $142) (39. Re5 $142) 39... Rb7 40. Rc2 Rb3 41. Qd2 ({Quickest is} 41.
Rc7+ Kg8 42. Bc3 Ne8 43. Rc8 Qd7 44. Qc4+) 41... Qb5 42. Bc1 Qf5 43. Rc7+ Kg6
44. Qc2 Rd3 $2 {We were both playing quickly now and he wanted to keep
tactical chances . Correct is to exchange Queens.} 45. Rc6 $2 {This wins but I
missed the quicker route. Short of time I was worried about Knight checks.
45Rc5 or 45Qc5 loses so I pinned the Knight. I knew that I threatened 46.Ke2
which would force 46.......Rxd4, when I win, so I didn't look any further.} ({
Correct is} 45. Ke2 {which wins as} Rxd4 {is answered by} 46. Rxg7+) 45... Rxd4
46. Qxf5+ Kxf5 47. Ra6 Rd7 48. Be3 Nd5 49. Rxa7 Rxa7 50. Bxa7 Nc3 51. Bd4 Nb5
52. Bb2 g6 53. a4 Nc7 54. a5 g5 55. Ke3 Ke6 56. Ke4 Na6 57. f4 gxf4 58. Kxf4
1-0

