{1hr 30' each/game} 1. Nf3 d5 2. c4 d4 3. e3 c5 4. exd4 cxd4 5. d3 Nc6 6. g3
Nf6 7. Bg2 e5 8. O-O Bd6 9. Re1 O-O 10. a3 a5 11. b3 Re8 12. Qc2 h6 13. Nbd2
Bf5 14. Bb2 Rc8 15. Rac1 b6 16. Qb1 Qd7 17. Nh4 Bh7 18. Ne4 Nxe4 19. Bxe4 Bxe4
20. Rxe4 g6 {Preventing Nf5} 21. Re2 Qe7 22. Qa1 Qf6 23. Rce1 g5 24. Ng2 Qg6
25. Qb1 f5 26. f3 h5 27. Kh1 Kf7 28. Bc1 f4 29. gxf4 exf4 30. Re4 Rxe4 31. Rxe4
Re8 32. Bb2 Rxe4 33. dxe4 Be5 34. Qd3 g4 35. Nh4 Qf6 36. Nf5 Kf8 ({I wanted to
play} 36... Qg6 {then if} 37. Nxd4 Nxd4 38. Bxd4 gxf3 {wins a piece.}) (36...
Qg6 {However he plays} 37. fxg4 {and I can't play} Qxg4 {because of the Knight
fork. So I move the King where it can't be attacked by the Knight}) ({However,
better} 36... Ne7 37. Bxd4 (37. Nxd4 Nc6) 37... Nxf5 38. Bxe5 Qxe5 39. exf5 Qe3
) 37. b4 gxf3 38. Qxf3 axb4 39. axb4 d3 {Trying to create some chances. he
would be happy with a draw but I wanted a win. I knew it was risky.} ({The
line given by Fritz was drawish.} 39... Ne7 40. Qxh5 Nxf5 41. Qxf5 Qxf5 42.
exf5 d3 43. Bc1 Bc3) 40. Bxe5 Nxe5 (40... Qxe5 41. Qxd3 Nxb4 42. Qf3 Nc2) 41.
Qxf4 Ke8 {I was hoping the Pawn on d3 would give me chances, especially as he
was short of time. The King moves accross to deal with his extra QS Pawn.} 42.
c5 bxc5 43. bxc5 Kd7 44. Qe3 Kc7 (44... Kc6 {is playable. but short of time
myself I didn't want to move to a square where the Knight could check me.}) 45.
Qd4 Ng4 {Best. A very useful move. The fork on f2 gaurds the d-Pawn and he
can't move his Queen where I can play ......Qa1+.} 46. Qxf6 Nxf6 {Short of
time he now wants to save the e-Pawn.} 47. e5 $2 {Loses. I had seen this and
was hoping for it in the rush.} ({He sees that} 47. Ng3 {is answered by} h4)
47... Nd5 48. Kg2 d2 0-1

