{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bc4 Bb4 5. d3 d6 6. Bd2
Na5 7. Bb3 Nxb3 8. axb3 Bg4 9. h3 Bh5 10. O-O a6 11. Nb1 Bc5 12. Be3 Nd7 13.
Bxc5 (13. Nc3) 13... Nxc5 14. Nbd2 O-O 15. Qe1 Ne6 16. c3 Bxf3 17. Nxf3 f5 {
Fritz prefers the alternatives but one needs to create play in this sort of
game.} (17... f6) (17... Qd7) 18. exf5 Rxf5 19. d4 $2 {This should lose
quickly. I was expecting.......} (19. Qe4 Rf6 20. Qxb7 Nf4) 19... Rxf3 20. gxf3
{He can't really play anything else but it allows mate in 7.} Qg5+ $5 {Played
almnost automatically.} (20... Nf4 21. Qxe5 (21. Kh2 Qh4 22. Rh1 Qxh3+ 23. Kg1
Qg2#) (21. Kh1 Qh4 22. Rg1 Qxh3#) (21. Qe4 Qg5+ 22. Kh1 Qg2#) (21. h4 Qxh4 22.
Qxe5 dxe5 23. Rfb1 Qh3 24. dxe5 Qg2#) 21... dxe5 22. Rfd1 Qg5+ 23. Kf1 Qg2+ 24.
Ke1 Qxf3 25. Kd2 Qd3+ 26. Kc1 Ne2#) 21. Kh2 Qf4+ 22. Kg2 Ng5 $2 ({Correct is} 
22... Qf5 23. Qe4 Nf4+ $19) 23. Qe3 Qh4 24. Rh1 Rf8 25. f4 {Unnecessarily
panicky. He wants to play Qg3} (25. dxe5 $142 dxe5 26. Ra4) 25... Rxf4 26. Qg3
Qh5 27. Raf1 $2 (27. dxe5 $142) 27... Ne4 28. Qe3 Qf5 ({Fritz prefers} 28...
Qg5+ 29. Kh2 Rxf2+ 30. Qxf2 Nxf2 31. Rxf2 exd4 {I thought about this but
didn't like it.}) 29. b4 exd4 30. cxd4 g5 {More fuzzy thinking.} ({Better,
according to Fritz, is} 30... Qg5+ 31. Kh2 Rxf2+ {but I still don't like it.})
31. Qb3+ (31. Rhg1 $142) 31... d5 32. Qe3 Qf6 {I wasn't really sure how to
proceed here.} 33. b3 Qd6 34. Qe1 Qf6 (34... g4 $142 35. Rh2 Qg6 36. h4) 35.
Qe2 $2 {Losing the d-pawn.} (35. f3 $142 Nd6 36. Qe5) 35... Qxd4 36. Qe1 (36.
f3 $142) 36... Kf7 (36... Nd2 $142 {I was playing too quickly}) 37. Rh2 (37.
Qe2 $142 Qxb4) 37... Nd2 38. Qd1 Nxf1 39. Qxd4 (39. Qh5+ Kf6 40. Qh6+ Ke7 41.
Qxh7+ Rf7) 39... Rxd4 40. Kxf1 0-1

