{1hr 40' for 40 then + 20'} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. cxd5 cxd5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Nf3
Nc6 6. Bf4 e6 7. e3 Bd6 8. Bg3 O-O 9. Bd3 Re8 10. O-O Bxg3 11. hxg3 a6 12. a3
b5 13. b4 e5 14. dxe5 Nxe5 15. Nxe5 Rxe5 16. Rc1 Ng4 {Black decides to attack.}
(16... Bg4 {Fritz}) 17. Be2 Qg5 (17... Nf6 {Fritz}) 18. f4 {After much thought.
} (18. Qd4 $142 Re8 19. Nxd5 Rd8 20. Rc5 Be6 21. f4) 18... Qh5 19. Bxg4 Bxg4
20. Qd4 Rf5 {Trying to hang on to the d-Pawn.} 21. Rfe1 ({Fritz prefers} 21.
Rc2 {then} Z0 22. Rd2) 21... Re8 (21... f6 {Fritz}) 22. Kf2 h6 (22... f6) 23.
Rh1 Qg6 24. Nxd5 Qe6 {To prevent e4} 25. e4 {Played anyway.} Rh5 ({If} 25...
Qxe4 26. Qxe4 Rxe4 27. Ne3 {Wins material.}) 26. Rhe1 Rd8 27. Rc6 Rhxd5 $5 {
Bang! I had thought that he couldn't play this and for a few seconds panicked.
However, it is OK.} (27... Qxc6 $142 28. Ne7+ Kf8 29. Qxd8+ Qe8 30. Qxe8+ Kxe8
31. Nf5 Kf8) 28. Qxd5 Rxd5 29. Rxe6 Rd2+ 30. Ke3 Rxg2 31. Rxa6 Rxg3+ 32. Kd4 h5
33. a4 bxa4 34. Rxa4 h4 (34... Rb3 $142 35. Kc4 Be6+ 36. Kc5 g6) 35. Ra2 (35.
Raa1 $142 {As a Rook can get behind the b-Pawn.}) (35. Rb1 $142) (35. b5 $142)
35... Rb3 36. Kc5 h3 (36... Rc3+ $142) 37. Rg1 (37. f5) 37... Bf3 (37... Bc8
$142 38. Ra8 Kh7 39. b5 (39. Rxc8 $4 Rc3+) 39... Bb7) 38. Rg3 1-0

