{40 in 1hr 40' + 20'} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nc6 3. Bg2 Nf6 4. Nc3 g6 5. Rb1 d6 6. b4
Bg7 7. d3 O-O 8. b5 Ne7 9. Nf3 Nd7 10. O-O Nc5 11. Be3 c6 12. bxc6 Nxc6 13.
Bxc5 dxc5 14. Nd2 f5 {After much thought. I was not happy here as I was going
to lose the c-Pawn to Na4 and Na3} 15. Bxc6 bxc6 16. Qc2 Re8 17. Nb3 Bf8 (17...
e4 $142 18. Nxc5 Qe7 19. N3a4 exd3 20. exd3 f4) 18. Na4 f4 (18... Rb8 $142) 19.
Naxc5 fxg3 (19... Bh3 $142) (19... Rb8 $142) 20. hxg3 ({Not} 20. fxg3 {which
loses a piece.}) 20... h5 21. Ne4 h4 (21... Bf5 $142) 22. Nbd2 Bh3 23. Rfe1
hxg3 (23... Bf5 {Fritz}) 24. Nxg3 Rb8 {Starting to get short of time I start
looking for "safe" moves.} 25. Rxb8 Qxb8 26. Nde4 Bg7 $2 {maybe the move that
loses it. I was looking for quick, safe, moves and this prevents any forks.}
27. Rb1 Qc7 {1hr 28' [12' for 13 moves]} 28. Rb3 Bc8 29. Qd2 Qe7 30. Rb8 Rf8
31. Qb4 Qc7 {1hr 34' [6' for 9 moves]} 32. Qd6 Qa5 $4 ({I saw that} 32... Qxd6
{would almost certainly lose me another pawn, so had to find a quick
alternative}) (32... Qa5 {Then maybe} 33. Z0 Qe1+ {and if} 34. Kh2 Rxf2+ {
offered some hope..........so I tried that. However, moving quickly, I
overlook the obvious reply.}) 33. Rxc8 1-0

