{1hr 30' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 d6 4. Nc3 c6 5. d3 Be7 6. e4 {
Fritz doesn't like this. However, in this sort of game, against a low graded
opponent, it is worth going for a direct attack, in this case based on f4.} Be6
7. Nge2 Nbd7 8. O-O O-O 9. f4 exf4 (9... Qb6+ {Fritz}) 10. gxf4 Bg4 (10... Qb6+
) 11. Qe1 h6 12. Ng3 Nh7 $4 {Simply losing a Piece. He played this very
quickly.} 13. h3 {[8']} Be6 14. f5 Bxc4 15. dxc4 Ne5 16. Qe2 Bh4 17. Bf4 Qb6+
18. Kh1 Nf6 19. b3 Qd4 20. Qc2 Qc5 21. Nce2 g5 {He decides that desperate
measures are called for.} 22. fxg6 fxg6 23. Qd2 (23. Bxh6 $142 {Being a piece
up I saw no reason to open the h-file.}) 23... Neg4 {Even more desperate
measures.} 24. hxg4 Nxg4 25. Qd4 Qa5 {Rather than resigning he started playing
very quickly, presumably in the hope that I might do the same and blunder.
However, the blunder comes from him.} 26. Qxd6 Rf6 27. Qd2 Raf8 $4 1-0

