{30' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c6 4. Nc3 Be7 5. e4 d6 6. d3 O-O 7.
Nge2 h6 8. O-O Be6 9. f4 exf4 10. gxf4 Nh7 {A different approach to 3 days ago.
} 11. Ng3 f5 12. exf5 (12. Bh3 $142) 12... Bxf5 13. Nxf5 Rxf5 14. Qg4 (14. Bh3
$142) (14. d4 $142) 14... Rf7 15. Ne4 (15. Be3 $142) 15... Qd7 (15... Nd7 $142)
16. Qg3 (16. Bh3 $142 {However, in these quick games one looks for tactical
chances and I wanted to keep the Queens on.}) 16... Nf6 $2 17. Bd2 $2 ({Missing
} 17. Bh3 Qd8 18. Be6) 17... Nxe4 18. Bxe4 ({I was aware that} 18. dxe4 {
was objectively better but again, in these quick games one can go for the
attacking option.}) 18... Bf6 $2 {The policy from the last note is rewarded.}
19. Qg6 Kf8 20. Rae1 Bd4+ 21. Kh1 Rf6 22. Qh5 $2 {I was aware that 22.Qh7 was
right but I didn't have time to check it out properly so I take the safe route.
Pity!} (22. Qh7 Na6 (22... Qf7 23. Bg6 Rxg6 24. Qh8+ Qg8 25. Re8+) (22... Kf7
23. Bc3 Bxc3 24. Rg1 Ke7 25. Bxc6+) 23. Qh8+ Kf7 24. Qxa8) 22... Qf7 23. Qh3
Nd7 24. b4 Re8 25. Qf3 Kg8 {Failing to realise that operations have switched
to the white squares on the QS.} (25... Nb6 $142) 26. b5 {Having played 25.....
.Kg8 he now can't capture the Pawn.} Nc5 {Playing quickly now as time runs out
he still doesn't realise that he has white square problems and he simply hopes
to exchange off the Bishop on e4.} 27. bxc6 Nxe4 $2 {Loses outright. He played
this instantly} (27... bxc6 $142) 28. Rxe4 Rxe4 29. Qxe4 Bb6 ({If} 29... Re6
30. cxb7) 30. cxb7 Bc7 31. Re1 Qh5 32. Qe8+ Qxe8 33. Rxe8+ Kh7 (33... Rf8 34.
Rc8 {doesn't help Black.}) 34. Rc8 Bb6 35. b8=Q 1-0

