{30' each/game} 1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Nxf6+ gxf6 6. Bf4
Bf5 7. c3 Qb6 {Doesn't achieve much.} 8. Bxb8 {White is playing for a draw and
takes the opportunity to exchange.} (8. Qb3 $142) 8... Rxb8 9. Qb3 Qc7 10. Nf3
e6 11. a4 Rg8 12. Bc4 $2 {The sort of oversight that happens in quickplay} Rxg2
(12... Qf4 $142 13. Bf1 Qe4+ 14. Kd1 Bh6 15. h3 Qf4 {However, in a quickplay
game one goes for the simple route.}) 13. Nh4 Rxh2 ({I considered} 13... Rg5) (
{Another line is} 13... Be4 14. Nxg2 Bxg2 15. Rg1 Qxh2) 14. Rxh2 Qxh2 15. Nxf5
exf5 {I didn't want to take too much time but...........} (15... Qg1+ 16. Bf1
exf5) 16. Bxf7+ Kd8 17. O-O-O (17. Ke2 $142) 17... Qxf2 18. Qe6 Qf4+ 19. Kb1
Qe4+ 20. Qxe4 fxe4 21. Re1 Ke7 22. Bg8 h6 {I used up a lot of time here and
started to run short. However................} (22... f5 23. Bxh7 Kf6 24. Rg1 {
is better. I missed this because of Rf1 instead of Rg1} (24. Rf1 e3 25. Rxf5+ {
loses the Bishop.})) 23. Rxe4+ Kd7 24. Be6+ Kd6 25. Bf5 b5 {Time was now
getting very short and I realised that I had gone wrong, so I needed something
active.} 26. Re6+ {He offered a draw here.} Kd5 27. axb5 Rxb5 $2 {Trying too
hard.} (27... cxb5 $142) (27... c5 $142) 28. Rxf6 (28. Kc2 $142) 28... Rb8 {
Playing fast now.} 29. Be6+ Ke4 30. Kc2 h5 31. Bf5+ Ke3 32. Rxc6 h4 33. Rc8 {
I was sure that I was lost now. However, we were both moving fast now.} Rxc8
34. Bxc8 Ke4 35. Be6 Bd6 36. Kb3 Kd3 37. Bf5+ Kd2 38. Kc4 Kc1 39. b4 Bc7 40.
Kd5 a5 41. bxa5 Bxa5 42. c4 Kb2 43. Kc6 (43. c5 $142) (43. Ke4 $142) (43. Ke5
$142) 43... Kc3 44. Kd5 Bd8 45. c5 Bf6 46. c6 Bd8 47. Bd7 $2 (47. Ke4 $142 Bb6
48. Bh3 Bc7 49. Bf1 Bg3 50. Kd5 Bb8 51. Kc5 Ba7+ 52. Kd6 Bb8+ 53. Kd5 Kb4)
47... Bc7 $2 (47... Kd3 $142) 48. Ke4 $2 ({Correct is} 48. Kc5 Bh2 49. Be6 Kd3
50. Bf5+ Kc3 51. d5 Bg1+ 52. Kd6 Kc4 53. Kd7 $18) 48... Kc4 49. d5 Kc5 50. Be6
Kd6 1/2-1/2

