{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. e3 b4 5. Bd3 g6 6. Nd2 Bg7
7. Rb1 O-O 8. Ngf3 d6 9. b3 Nbd7 10. Bb2 e5 11. e4 Nh5 12. g3 Qe8 (12... Qe8 {
To protect the Knight after......} 13. Z0 f5 14. exf5 gxf5 15. Nxe5) 13. Bc1 f5
14. O-O Nb6 15. Qc2 a5 16. Bb2 a4 17. Nh4 a3 18. Ba1 {How will the Bishop get
out?} f4 19. Ndf3 Bh3 20. Rfe1 Bf6 21. Bf1 Qd7 22. Qe2 fxg3 23. hxg3 Bxh4 24.
Bxh3 Qxh3 25. Nxh4 Rf7 26. Rf1 Raf8 27. Rbd1 Nf6 28. Rd3 {Else 28......Ng4 wins
} Qg4 (28... Nbd7 {is much better.}) 29. Qxg4 Nxg4 30. f3 Nh6 31. f4 {I
realised now that he was going to get his Bishop out.} exf4 32. Rdf3 fxg3 (
32... g5 $142) 33. Rxf7 Rxf7 34. e5 dxe5 35. Bxe5 Nd7 (35... Ng4 {is better.
However, we were both getting short of time now.}) 36. Bxg3 Ng4 37. Rxf7 Kxf7
38. Nf3 h6 39. Kg2 Kf6 {The rest of the game was played fairly fast.} 40. Nd2
Ne3+ (40... Kf5 $142) 41. Kf3 Nd1 {The wrong plan. I should advance the KS
Pawns.} (41... Nf5 $142) 42. Ne4+ Kf7 43. Be1 Nb2 (43... Nf6 $142) 44. Ke2 g5
45. Bf2 g4 {Short of time I was unsure what to do.} 46. Nxc5 Ne5 {I thought it
might be lost now.} 47. Bg3 Nf3 48. Na6 Nd4+ (48... Nxc4) 49. Kd2 {Missing the
threat.} (49. Ke3 $142) 49... Nxb3+ 50. Ke1 $2 (50. Ke3 $142) 50... Nxc4 $2 {
Played instantaneously} ({Correct is} 50... Nd3+ 51. Kd1 Nd4 52. Z0 b3) 51.
Nxb4 Nc5 52. Kf1 Ne4 53. Bh4 Ke8 (53... Kg6 $142) 54. Be1 Kd7 55. Nc2 Ned2+ (
55... h5 $142) 56. Kg2 Kd6 57. Nxa3 Kxd5 58. Nxc4 Nxc4 59. Kg3 Ne5 60. Kh4 Nf3+
61. Kxg4 1/2-1/2

