{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 f5 2. Bg5 g6 3. h3 {Rather a negation of his 2nd
move if he feels the need to play this.} Bg7 4. c3 Nf6 5. Nd2 O-O 6. e3 c6 7.
Ngf3 d6 8. Bc4+ d5 9. Be2 Nbd7 10. O-O Qe8 11. Bxf6 {White wants a draw. He
tries to achieve this by exchanging ecerything off and by blocking off the
Pawn position.} Nxf6 12. Ne5 Ne4 13. f4 Be6 {I wasn't sure about this but
Fritz gives it as best. I didn't fancy 13......Ng3 14.Rook moves Nxe2, as my
Knight is better than his Bishop.} 14. Qe1 Rc8 15. Ndf3 Bd7 {Intending ......
c5 and ......Bb5} 16. Nxd7 Qxd7 17. Ne5 Bxe5 {His Knight is better than my
Bishop.} 18. fxe5 c5 19. Bd3 c4 20. Bxe4 fxe4 21. Qe2 {He offered a draw here.}
Kg7 22. Rxf8 Rxf8 23. Rf1 Rxf1+ 24. Kxf1 a5 25. g4 h5 {Played to try to create
some sort of play.} 26. Kg2 hxg4 27. Qxg4 $5 {For practical purposes he should
keep the Queens on if he wants a draw.} Qxg4+ 28. hxg4 Kf7 29. Kg3 g5 30. a3 {
He offered a nother draw here. However, I felt that he might go wrong and I
have some "spare" Pawn moves.} Ke6 31. Kf2 Kd7 32. Ke2 Kc6 33. Kd2 $2 {The
first mistake.} ({Correct is} 33. a4 b5 34. Kd2 bxa4 35. Kc2) 33... Kb5 34. Kc2
Ka4 35. Kc1 $2 {Second mistake.} Kb3 36. Kb1 (36. e6 b5 37. Kb1 b4 38. cxb4
axb4 39. axb4 Kxb4 40. Kc2 Kb5 41. Kc1 Ka4 42. Kd1 Kb3 43. Kc1 c3) 36... b5 37.
Kc1 (37. e6 b4 38. cxb4 axb4 39. axb4 Kxb4 40. Kc2 Kb5 41. Kd2 Ka5 42. Kd1 Ka4
43. Kc2 Kb4 44. Kb1 Kb3) 37... b4 38. axb4 axb4 39. cxb4 Kxb4 40. Kc2 e6 41.
Kc1 Kb3 42. Kb1 c3 43. Kc1 cxb2+ 44. Kb1 Kc3 0-1

