{1hr 30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Ba5 6. d4
exd4 7. O-O {He played all this quickly so obviously knew more about the
opening than I did.} d6 (7... Nf6 $142 8. e5 Ne4 9. Qb3 O-O) 8. Qb3 Qd7 {
I began to regret this but Fritz gives this as best.} 9. Re1 dxc3 {After much
thought.} (9... Bb6 $142 10. cxd4 Na5) 10. Nxc3 (10. e5 $142 c2 11. e6) 10...
Bxc3 (10... f6 $142 11. Qb2 Nge7) 11. Qxc3 f6 12. Ba3 Nge7 13. Rad1 Ng6 14. e5
Ngxe5 $2 {loses.} (14... fxe5 $142) (14... Ncxe5 $142) 15. Nxe5 fxe5 16. f4 {
Had I not taken with the g6 Knight on move 14 he would not have had this.} Qf5
17. fxe5 Nxe5 $2 18. Bb5+ Bd7 19. Bxd7+ Kxd7 20. Rxe5 Qg4 $2 21. Ree1 $2 Rae8
22. Bb2 Rxe1+ 23. Rxe1 Re8 24. Rxe8 Kxe8 25. Qxg7 Qd1+ ({Fritz gives} 25...
Qxg7 26. Bxg7 c5 {I was short of time and exchanging Queens seemed too risky.})
26. Kf2 Qd2+ 27. Kg3 Qe3+ 28. Kh4 Qf4+ 29. Kh3 Qf5+ 30. Qg4 Qc2 31. Bf6 (31.
Qe6+ Kf8 32. Bd4 h5 33. Bxa7 b6 34. Bb8 Kg7 35. Qe7+) 31... Kf7 (31... Qxa2
$142) 32. Qg7+ (32. Bd8 $142 Qc3+ 33. g3 Qe5 34. Bxc7) 32... Ke6 33. Qe7+ Kd5
34. Qf7+ Kc6 35. Qe8+ Kb6 36. Bd4+ (36. Qe6 $142) 36... c5 37. Qd8+ Kc6 38. Bf6
Qf5+ 39. g4 Qf3+ 40. Kh4 Qf2+ 41. Kg5 Qe3+ 42. Kh4 1/2-1/2

