{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. e3 Nc6 4. Bd3 Bg4 5. h3 Bh5 6. O-O
Qd7 7. Nbd2 e6 8. c3 Bd6 9. Qc2 Bg6 10. e4 dxe4 11. Nxe4 Nxe4 12. Bxe4 O-O-O (
12... O-O $142) 13. Re1 Rde8 14. b4 Ne7 15. Bd2 Bxe4 16. Qxe4 h6 17. c4 Nc6 18.
c5 Be7 19. b5 Nd8 20. Rab1 Qd5 21. Qc2 Bf6 22. b6 (22. Qa4 $142) 22... a6 23.
bxc7 Nc6 24. Bf4 Nxd4 25. Nxd4 Bxd4 26. Bd6 e5 27. Qf5+ (27. Red1 $142) 27...
Qe6 28. Qe4 b5 {9 Allows mate in} 29. Qc6 (29. Rxb5 $142 axb5 30. Qa8+ Kd7 31.
Qb7 {6 and mate in}) ({Simply} 29. Qa8+ Kd7 30. c8=Q+ Rxc8 31. Qb7+ Ke8 32.
Bxe5) 29... Qxa2 30. Qf3 $2 {To conservative} ({Correct is} 30. Rbd1 Qxf2+ 31.
Kh1 f6 32. Qxa6+ Kd7 33. Qxb5+ Ke6 34. Qc4+ Kf5 35. Rf1) 30... f6 (30... e4
$142) 31. Rbd1 (31. Rbd1 {The threat is} Z0 32. Rxd4 exd4 33. Rxe8+ Rxe8 34.
Qa8+ Kd7 35. Qxe8+ Kxe8 36. c8=Q+) 31... Kd7 $2 32. Re2 $2 ({Correct is} 32.
Rxd4 exd4 33. c8=Q+ Rxc8 34. Qb7+ Rc7 35. Qxc7#) 32... Qc4 33. Red2 Re6 34. Qb7
{He was short of time now and I speeded up (foolishly)} (34. Kh2 $142) 34...
Rc8 35. Qxa6 $2 {Moving quickly I completely lose the thread.} (35. Ra1 $142 {
and if} Bxa1 36. Bxe5+ {wins}) 35... Rxc7 36. Rb1 $4 {Going completely off the
rails. I moved quickly and immediately realised that I was going to lose the
Bishop.} Rxc5 {I was sitting there horror-struck wondering if I had any hope
due to his time shortage (a few mins) when he offered a draw! With no time
left to think he had simply assumed that after 37.Qb7+ he had to block with
the Rook which is good for White, so he offered a draw. An awful game at the
end of the day a lucky escape!} (36... Rxc5 {Draw. he assumed that after} 37.
Qb7+ {ha has to play} Rc7) (36... Rxc5 {Draw} 37. Qb7+ {however Black plays}
Kxd6) 1/2-1/2

