{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 e5 $2 {
Simply loses a pawn.} 7. dxe5 dxe5 8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. Nxe5 Na6 10. Be3 Ng4 11.
Nxg4 Bxg4 12. h3 (12. Be2 $142) 12... Bxc3+ 13. bxc3 Bc8 14. c5 (14. Kf2 $142)
(14. Be2 $142) 14... b6 15. cxb6 axb6 16. Kf2 (16. a4 $142) 16... Bb7 17. e5
Nc5 18. Bxc5 bxc5 19. h4 $2 {Correct is 19.a4. The text was to allow the Rook
access to h3 defending the c-pawn after Black plays his Rook to a3.} (19. a4
$142) 19... Rd2+ 20. Be2 Raxa2 21. Rxa2 Rxa2 22. Rc1 Bxg2 23. Ke3 (23. Kxg2
Rxe2+ 24. Kf3) 23... Bd5 24. h5 Be6 25. hxg6 hxg6 26. Bf3 Kf8 {He offered draw
here.} 27. Be4 Ke7 28. Rc2 {It is clearly drawn but there seems little chance
of progress with his Rook on.} Rxc2 29. Bxc2 Bd5 30. Bd1 Ke6 31. Bg4+ Ke7 32.
Be2 f6 33. Bg4 fxe5 34. fxe5 g5 35. Bf5 Be6 36. Be4 Bc4 37. Bh7 Bd5 ({Avoiding
} 37... Ke6 $4) 38. Bf5 1/2-1/2

