{1hr 30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 {Apparently he was
hoping that I would play the Benko and had this ready.} 5. f3 d6 (5... e6 {
is the approved move.}) 6. e4 g6 7. Nc3 Bg7 8. a4 {This leaves holes on the
b-file. Fritz prefers 8.Nh3} O-O 9. Bc4 {This serves no useful purpose.} Nbd7
10. f4 (10. Be2 {Fritz}) 10... Nb6 11. Be2 axb5 12. Bxb5 Ba6 (12... Bd7 {Fritz}
) 13. Bc6 {The Bishop gets stuck here} (13. Bxa6 $142) 13... Rb8 14. Nge2 Nc4
15. Qc2 Qb6 16. Nb5 $2 {Loses at least a Pawn.} Na5 17. e5 {A touch of
desperation here.} (17. Nec3 $142) 17... Nxc6 18. exf6 {He played this
instaneously.} (18. dxc6 $142) 18... Nb4 19. Qe4 Bxf6 ({I briefly considered} 
19... exf6 {Fritz prefers it}) 20. Nec3 Qb7 21. O-O Bxc3 22. bxc3 Nxd5 23. Rf3
Nb6 24. Qxb7 {Keeping the Queens on seems better.} Rxb7 25. f5 {Hoping for
play on the KS.} (25. a5 $142) 25... Bxb5 26. axb5 Nc4 27. Bh6 Rfb8 28. fxg6
hxg6 29. Ra4 Ne5 30. Rh3 Rxb5 31. Rah4 f6 {Not necessary but playing it safe.}
(31... Rb1+ $142 32. Kf2 R8b2+ 33. Kg3 Rg1) 32. Be3 Kf7 33. g4 {He has no
constructive moves.} Rb1+ 34. Kg2 R8b2+ 35. Kg3 Re1 36. Rh7+ Ke6 37. Kf4 {
Ends it quickly} (37. Bf2 {is pointless.}) 37... g5+ 38. Ke4 d5# 0-1

