{2hr each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Bc5 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 h6 5. f4 d6 6. Nf3 Bg4 $2
{Simply losing it} 7. fxe5 ({I checked that he couldn't play} 7. Bxf7+ {
but gave it little further thought.}) 7... Bxf3 ({I now realised that} 7...
dxe5 {allows} 8. Bxf7+) 8. Qxf3 {Now it looks even worse!} dxe5 9. Qg3 Qe7 {
With a forlorn hope that I would be able to castle QS and bring the Queen's
Rook to the g-file.} 10. Nd5 {Came as a surprise.} Nxd5 11. Bxd5 Nc6 12. Rf1 (
12. Qxg7 $142 O-O-O 13. Qxf7 Qxf7 14. Bxf7 Rdf8) 12... f6 {I was more hopeful
now.} 13. Qg6+ Kd7 14. c3 Raf8 15. Qg4+ Kd8 16. Bd2 g5 {Weakening the f-Pawn
but I needed some space.} 17. Bxc6 {A surprise. He was so strong on the white
squares that I hadn't expected this.} (17. b4 $142) 17... bxc6 18. O-O-O Qd7
19. Rf5 Ke7 20. Qf3 Qe6 21. Rf1 $2 {Deciding that the attack on his a-Pawn was
uninportant in view of his pressure on f6.} (21. Kb1 $142) 21... Qxa2 $1 22. d4
({If} 22. Rxf6 Qa1+ 23. Kc2 Qxf1 $1) 22... Bd6 (22... Rb8 $142 23. b4 Rhd8) 23.
Kd1 Qxb2 24. Rxf6 Qb3+ 25. Ke2 Qb5+ 1/2-1/2

