{40 in 100' + 20'} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. Bg5 Bg7 4. e3 O-O 5. Bd3 d6 6. Nbd2
Nbd7 7. O-O c6 8. c3 Qc7 9. Re1 b6 10. e4 e5 (10... h6 {Fritz}) (10... Bb7 {
Fritz}) 11. dxe5 (11. a4 {Fritz}) 11... dxe5 12. Bc2 a5 {Fritz prefers ......
b5 which prevents Nc4} 13. a4 (13. Nc4 $142) 13... Ba6 14. b4 (14. b3 $142)
14... h6 15. Bxf6 Bxf6 16. Qb1 Rfd8 17. b5 $2 {Not good. I am left with a
protected passed a-Pawn and she gets a weak Pawn on c4.} cxb5 18. axb5 Bb7 19.
c4 Nc5 20. Nb3 Ne6 21. Nbd2 ({Not} 21. Nfd2 $2 a4) 21... g5 22. h3 Nf4 23. Qb3
Rd7 24. Nf1 Rc8 25. Ne3 Be7 {This leaves the e-Pawn weak.} (25... Qc5 $142) 26.
Kf1 (26. Nd5 $142 {I had not thought this possible because of} Nxd5 27. exd5
Bxd5 {but because I had played......Be7 my e-Pawn can be taken.}) 26... Kg7 27.
Nf5+ Kg6 28. Nxe7+ Rxe7 29. Rad1 (29. Ra4 $142) 29... Qxc4+ 30. Qxc4 Rxc4 31.
Rd6+ Kg7 32. Bb1 f6 33. Rxb6 Rd7 {White's Rook is short of squares} 34. Ng1 Ng6
35. g3 Ne7 36. Ba2 Rxe4 37. Rxe4 Bxe4 38. Ke1 Rc7 39. Ne2 Bd3 40. Kd2 $4 {
Moving quickly she blunders} Bxe2 41. Kxe2 Rc2+ 42. Ke3 Rxa2 43. Rb7 Kf8 44.
Rb8+ Kf7 45. Rb7 Ke6 46. Rb6+ Kd7 47. Rxf6 {Just bashing out moves
instantaneously now, she ends it quickly.} Nd5+ 48. Ke4 Nxf6+ 49. Kxe5 Rxf2 0-1

