{40 in 100' + 20'} 1. e4 g6 2. Nf3 Bg7 3. Bc4 d6 4. O-O e6 5. d4 h6 6. e5 b6 7.
Bb5+ Bd7 8. Qe2 Bxb5 9. Qxb5+ Qd7 10. Na3 Ne7 11. Qxd7+ Kxd7 ({If} 11... Nxd7
12. Nb5 {is a nuisance}) 12. exd6 cxd6 13. Bf4 {Aiming at d6 with Nb5 coming
but not best.} (13. c3 $142) 13... g5 14. Bg3 {After much thought. He wants o
keep the pressure on d6.} g4 {Makes it interesting.} (14... Nbc6 {Fritz}) (
14... f5 {Fritz}) 15. Nh4 Bxd4 {For practical purposes this gives good chances.
} 16. Rad1 Bc5 17. Nc4 Nd5 {This is the move that I was relying on.} (17... d5
$142) 18. Ne5+ $2 {When deciding on .....g4 I hadn't considered this. However
it is a mistake.} (18. Nf5 $142) 18... Ke8 ({Correct is} 18... dxe5 19. c4 Nc6
20. cxd5 exd5 21. Rxd5+ Ke6 {is -2.02 but I don't see why.}) 19. c4 ({I had
assumed that White couldn't play} 19. Nxg4 {because of} h5 20. Ne3 Bxe3) ({
Fritz gives} 19. Nxg4 h5 20. Rxd5 exd5 21. Nf6+ Kd8 22. c3) 19... Nf6 20. Nd3
Ne4 (20... Nh5 {Fritz}) (20... Nc6 {Fritz}) 21. Nxc5 Nxg3 22. Nxe6 {He thought
about this for a long time. It is best.} Ne2+ 23. Kh1 fxe6 24. Rfe1 Nf4 25. g3
Nh3 26. Rxe6+ Kd7 27. Rdxd6+ Kc7 28. Nf5 Nd7 {White has good play for his
piece and is picking up Pawns.} 29. Ne3 (29. Kg2 {Fritz}) 29... Rae8 30. Rc6+ (
{If} 30. Nd5+ Kb8 {and the back rank thret saves the Knight.}) 30... Kb7 31.
Nxg4 Rxe6 32. Rxe6 h5 33. Nf6 Nxf2+ 34. Kg2 Nxf6 35. Rxf6 Nd3 (35... Nd1 {Fritz
}) 36. b3 Rh7 37. h3 Ka6 38. a3 Re7 (38... Ne1+ $142 39. Kf2 Nc2) 39. g4 hxg4
40. hxg4 Nc5 41. b4 Nd7 42. Rf5 Ne5 43. Rf4 Rc7 44. g5 Nxc4 45. a4 Ne5 46. Rf5
Nd3 47. b5+ Ka5 48. Kf3 {He was running short of time now.} Re7 49. g6 {
Short of time and with his a-Pawn going he has no good move.} Ne5+ 50. Ke4
Nxg6+ 51. Kd5 Re5+ 0-1

