{30' each/game} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. c3 Nd7 5. Bd3 b6 6. O-O Bb7 7.
Bg5 h6 8. Bh4 g5 9. Bg3 e6 10. e5 d5 {In these games one has to play fairly
quickly. I gave no thought to 10.......Bxf3 & 10.......dxe5} 11. Qd2 Ne7 12. a4
a6 {Again played fairly quickly.} ({I briefly considered} 12... Nf5 {but} 13.
Bxf5 {is good for White. However, his Bishop on g3 would be buried.}) 13. b4 c5
14. bxc5 bxc5 15. Re1 g4 {I probably wouldn't play this in a standard play
game.} (15... Qa5 $142) 16. Nh4 h5 {ceding g5} (16... Rb8 $142) (16... Nc6 $142
) 17. Bf4 cxd4 18. cxd4 Nc6 19. Bg5 (19. Ng6 $142) 19... Qb6 20. Ng6 {One move
too late.} ({White's best line is} 20. Nc3 Qxd4 21. Nf5 exf5 22. Be3 Bh6 23.
Bxh6 Nc5 24. Bxf5) 20... Qxd4 21. Nxh8 Qxa1 22. Nc3 Qa3 23. Nxf7 $2 ({Correct
is} 23. Nxd5 Ncxe5 24. Nc7+ Kf8 25. Ng6+ fxg6 26. Bxg6 Rc8 27. Nxe6+) 23...
Kxf7 24. Nxd5 Ndxe5 {I take with this Knight so the c6 one covers e7} (24...
Ncxe5 $142 25. Qf4+ Kg8 26. Ne7+ Kh8) 25. Qf4+ (25. Be4 $142) 25... Kg8 26.
Nf6+ (26. Be4 {is still better but with time getting short White tries to open
up the position around my King.}) 26... Bxf6 ({Not} 26... Kh8 $4 27. Qe4 {
or so I thpught, but} Qxd3 {seems OK.}) 27. Bxf6 ({If} 27. Qxf6 Qxd3 28. Qxe6+
Nf7) 27... Qxd3 28. Bxe5 {White had very little time now and the rest of the
game was a rush.} (28. Qg5+ {can be answered by} Qg6) 28... Nxe5 29. Qxe5 Qd5
30. Qxe6+ Qxe6 31. Rxe6 Rc8 32. f3 gxf3 33. gxf3 Rc4 34. Rb6 Rc7 (34... Bc8 {
is quicker}) 35. Kf2 Rf7 36. Kg3 a5 37. f4 (37. Rb5 Bxf3 38. Rxa5 Bg4 {is
slightly better.}) 37... Be4 38. h3 Rf5 39. Re6 Bc2 40. Re8+ Kf7 41. Ra8 Bxa4 {
White lost on time} 0-1

