{90' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e3 c6 6. Nf3 Qa5 7.
Nd2 {I was at school when I was last involved with the Cambridge Springs. I
now managed to find the move given by MCO} (7. Qb3 Bb4 8. a3 {0.26/0 Fritz})
7... Bb4 8. Qc1 ({MCO & Fritz give} 8. Qc2) 8... O-O 9. Nb3 (9. a3 $142) (9.
Be2 $142) 9... Qc7 10. a3 dxc4 11. Bxc4 Bd6 12. Bh4 b6 13. Bg3 Bb7 14. O-O Bxg3
15. hxg3 a6 16. Be2 c5 17. dxc5 Nxc5 18. Nd4 $2 {Black would be happy with a
draw. I wanted to win. So, after much thought, I played this stupid move to
try to maintain some possibilities and it should lose. To make it more
ridiculous I had considered 18......e5} (18. Nxc5 {Looks very drawish}) ({
I considered} 18. Na4 {after} Qc6 19. Bf3 {it is again drawish}) 18... Rac8 (
18... e5 $19) 19. Qe1 {After much thought. I was aware of what was what.} (19.
Qc2 $142 Nce4 20. Rac1) 19... b5 20. Bf3 Bxf3 21. gxf3 {-1.26/0 Surprisingly
this is} (21. Nxf3 {-0.57/0}) 21... Nd3 {I wasn't too happy here.} 22. Qe2 Nxb2
{This came as a surprise.} (22... Ne5 $142) (22... Qc4 $142) 23. Ncxb5 axb5 24.
Qxb2 Rb8 25. Kg2 Qb6 26. Rfb1 Rb7 $2 (26... Rfc8 $142) 27. Qxb5 Qxb5 28. Rxb5
Ra7 29. a4 h6 30. a5 Rfa8 31. Nc6 Ra6 32. Rb8+ Rxb8 33. Nxb8 Ra8 34. Nc6 Nd5
35. a6 Nc7 36. a7 Nb5 (36... Kf8 {then if} 37. Rb1 Ke8 {and now} 38. Ne5 (38.
Rb8+ Kd7 39. Ne5+ Ke7 40. f4 f6 41. Rb7 $18) 38... Ke7 39. f4 f6 40. Rb7 Kd6
41. Nc4+ Kc6 42. Na5+ Kd6 43. e4 $18) 37. Rb1 (37. Ra5 $142 Nd6 38. Nd4 Kf8 39.
Ra6 Nc8 40. Nb5 Ke7 41. f4 Kd7 42. Kf3 $18 {etc}) 37... Nxa7 38. Ra1 g5 {
He seemed to give up here and played this quickly.} ({Much better, but harder
to win, is} 38... Nxc6 {the computer continues with} 39. Rxa8+ Kh7 40. f4 g5
41. Kf3 Kg6 42. e4 Nd4+ 43. Ke3 Nc2+ 44. Kd3 Nb4+ 45. Kc3 Nc6 46. Rc8 Ne7 47.
