{90' ach/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 Re8 7.
Be2 Nbd7 $2 8. h3 ({Correct is} 8. e5 Ng4 9. e6 fxe6 10. Ng5 Ndf6 11. Bxg4 Nxg4
12. Qxg4 e5 13. Ne6) 8... e5 9. fxe5 dxe5 10. dxe5 Nxe5 11. Qxd8 Nxf3+ 12. Bxf3
Rxd8 13. O-O Be6 14. Nd5 Ne8 (14... c6 $142 15. Nc7 Bxc4 16. Nxa8 Bxf1 17. Kxf1
Rxa8 18. Be3) 15. Rb1 f5 {After a long think.} (15... Bd4+ $142 16. Kh1 c6) 16.
exf5 gxf5 (16... Bd4+ $142 17. Kh2 Bxf5 18. Ne7+ Kg7 19. Nxf5+) 17. Bg5 Rd7 18.
Ne7+ (18. Rfe1 $142 Bf7 19. Ne7+) 18... Kf7 (18... Rxe7) 19. Bxb7 (19. Bh5+
$142 Kf8 20. Nxf5) 19... Rb8 20. Nxf5 (20. Bd5 $142) 20... Rxb7 21. Nd6+ Kg6
22. Nxb7 Kxg5 {[53']} 23. b3 {[70'] At the start of this combination I
intended..........} ({......} 23. Nc5 {but now saw} Bd4+) 23... c5 $2 24. Rbe1
$2 {With time getting short this is a serious mistake.} ({Correct is} 24. Nxc5
{then} Bd4+ 25. Kh1 Bxc5 26. Rbe1 Ng7 27. Re5+) 24... Bd4+ 25. Kh1 Ng7 26. Na5
$2 {Moving too quickly} (26. Nxc5 $142) 26... Bc3 {Now I am lost. Can I work a
swindle?} 27. h4+ {The only chance} Kg6 $2 {It worked. Now Ihave a fork on e5.}
28. Nc6 Bxe1 29. Ne5+ Kh5 30. Nxd7 Bxh4 31. Nxc5 Bg4 32. Rf7 Nf5 33. Ne4 Kg6
34. Rxa7 Nd4 35. Ra5 Bf5 36. Nd2 Be1 37. Ra6+ Ne6 38. Nf3 Bf2 39. b4 Kh5 40.
Kh2 Kg4 41. Ra3 Bg3+ 42. Kg1 Nf4 {We were both getting short of time and
moving quickly.} 43. c5 Ne2+ 44. Kf1 Nf4 45. c6 Bd3+ 46. Kg1 Ne2+ 47. Kh1 Bc4 (
47... Bb5 $142) 48. Nh2+ Kh4 49. Re3 Bf2 50. Rh3+ (50. Re4+ $142 Kg5 51. Nf3+
Kf5 52. Rxc4) 50... Kg5 51. Nf3+ Kg6 {With no time left he misses the fork.}
52. Ne5+ Kg7 53. Nxc4 Ng3+ 54. Rxg3+ Bxg3 55. b5 Kf7 56. b6 {Black lost on
time. Lancaster A lost the S.F. match v University Staff [16-2-12]. Dick did
not play in this match.} 1-0

