{90' each/game} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. Nc3 Nd7 5. Bc4 e6 6. Bg5 Ne7 7.
Qd2 h6 8. Be3 a6 9. Bb3 b6 10. O-O Bb7 {The classic Hippo position for Black.}
11. Ne1 Nf6 12. f3 g5 {Fritz gives this as 1.15 with........} ({.....} 12... d5
13. e5 Nd7 14. Nd3 Nf5 {as 0.28. However 12......g5 is a good practical move
against a weaker opponent}) 13. Rd1 Ng6 14. Nd3 Qe7 15. a4 Rc8 16. Ne2 c5 17.
dxc5 dxc5 (17... bxc5 $142) 18. Bc4 O-O 19. c3 Rfd8 20. Qc2 (20. Z0 {Threat} b5
21. axb5 axb5 22. Bxb5 c4) 20... Qc7 21. Bf2 Qc6 {Hoping to exploit the long
diagonal.} 22. Ng3 g4 23. Rd2 gxf3 24. gxf3 h5 25. Rfd1 (25. Re1 $142 {
[leaving a retreat for the d2 Rook] then} Bh6 26. Rdd1 h4 27. Nf1 b5 28. Ba2 c4
) 25... h4 26. Ne2 (26. Nf1 $142) 26... Nxe4 27. Nb4 {After much thought} ({
I had expected.} 27. Ne5) ({He probably gave up the idea of} 27. fxe4 Qxe4 28.
Kf1 Qxc4 {-3.51/0 qyuite quickly but it is best at}) 27... Rxd2 28. Rxd2 cxb4
29. Qxe4 Qxe4 {(-6.09)} ({Interestingly} 29... Qc7 30. Bd5 Bxd5 31. Qxb4 Ne5
32. Rxd5 exd5 33. Bxh4 Nxf3+ {-6.11/0 is}) 30. fxe4 Rxc4 31. Bxb6 bxc3 32. bxc3
Rxa4 0-1

