Threatening mate in 1!} 24. Rd1 Nb6 25. e5 $5 Nxd5 26. Bf2 Nb4 {Gains a tempo
but..........} ({.............} 26... Nb6 {blocking the b-Pawn is better.}) 27.
Qb3 Qxa4 28. Qxa4 Rxa4 29. Nc3 (29. b6 $142 Ra8 30. b7 Rb8 31. exd6 exd6 32.
Rxd6) 29... Ra5 30. b6 d5 $2 {A degree of panic here. trying to complicate as
I felt that I was lost.} 31. b7 Nc6 32. Rb1 Nb8 (32... d4 33. Ne4 Nb8) 33. Nxd5
e6 34. Nc3 (34. Ne7+ $142 Kf8 35. Nc8) 34... f6 35. Ne4 fxe5 36. Bxc5 exf4 37.
Bd6 Bd4+ 38. Kf1 Ba7 $2 (38... Nc6 39. b8=Q+ Nxb8 40. Rxb8+) 39. Bxf4 {
Throwing it away!} Rf5 40. g3 e5 41. Nd6 (41. Ra1 $142 exf4 (41... Bd4 42. Ra4
Bb6 43. Rc4 Ba7 44. Rc8+ Kg7 45. Nd6) 42. Rxa7) 41... Rf8 42. Nc8 {He offered
a draw here.} Bd4 43. Rc1 exf4 44. gxf4 Rxf4+ 45. Kg2 Rf2+ 46. Kh3 Be5 47. Nb6
h5 48. Kh4 Rxh2+ 49. Kg5 Rg2+ 50. Kh4 Rg4+ 51. Kh3 Rb4 52. Rc8+ Kg7 53. Nc4 Bf4
