{90' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5
7. Bb3 O-O 8. h3 {He had been practising the Marshall [I would not have done
better if Dick let me play it S.P.]} d6 9. c3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Nc6 (11...
Qc7 {Is more usual. Not being able to play the marshall he was unsure.}) 12.
Be3 Bb7 13. Nbd2 cxd4 14. cxd4 Re8 15. d5 Nb8 16. Qe2 Nbd7 17. b4 Nb6 18. Rec1
Rc8 19. Bb3 Nc4 $4 {I dodn't know why he played this. [Neither do I S.P.]} 20.
Nxc4 bxc4 21. Rxc4 Rxc4 22. Qxc4 Qc8 {Black would be happy with a draw, but
exchanging off when a Pawn down won't help.} 23. Rc1 Qxc4 24. Rxc4 Rc8 25. Nd2
Kf8 26. f3 Nd7 27. Ba4 Ke8 28. Rxc8+ Bxc8 29. Nc4 Kd8 30. Kf2 Kc7 31. Ke2 h6
32. Na5 Nb8 33. g4 {To prevent ......f5} Bg5 34. Be8 Bxe3 {He offered a draw
here.} 35. Kxe3 f6 36. h4 g5 {He now has 3 weak Pawns and I will be able to
get a Knight on f5.} 37. h5 Kd8 38. Ba4 Kc7 39. Kd3 Bd7 (39... Kd8 {is
slightly better. I think he missed my 42nd move. [I did S.P.]}) 40. Bxd7 Kxd7 {
I guess he wants to prevent Nc6} (40... Nxd7 $142 {Fritz gives} 41. Nc4 f5 42.
gxf5 Nf6 43. Ne3) (40... Nxd7 {However, I was intending} 41. Nc6 Z0 {then} 42.
Ne7 Z0 43. Nf5) (40... Nxd7 41. Nc6 {However, Fritz gives} f5 42. gxf5 Nf6 43.
Ne7 Kd8 44. Ng6 Nxh5 45. a4 {1.96/0}) 41. a4 {Too cautious. I had seen 41.Nc6
but wanted to "solidify" the Pawns first. However, 41.Nc6 immediately wins.}
Kc7 42. Nc6 $1 {He hadn't expected this.} a5 {Loses quickly} ({"Best" is} 42...
Nd7 43. Ne7 a5 44. bxa5 Kb7 45. Nf5 Ka6) 43. Nxb8 {Dick did not play in the
Rd4 match v Morecambe A on 23/11/11} Kxb8 44. bxa5 Kb7 45. Kc4 Ka6 46. Kb4 Kb7
47. Kb5 1-0

