{2hr each/game} 1. c4 Nf6 2. g3 e5 3. Bg2 g6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. e4 Nc6 6. Nge2 d6 7.
O-O O-O 8. h3 Be6 9. d3 Nd7 10. Kh2 f5 11. f4 ({Fritz prefers} 11. exf5 Rxf5
12. Be3 Rh5 {but a human player is unlikely to play this.}) 11... fxe4 12. Nxe4
Rb8 13. Be3 a6 {This is OK but I didn't realise the strength of his next move.}
14. Ng5 Qe7 $4 {Unbelieveable! How could I play this? However, it is very
difficult.} (14... Bf7 {Loses simply to} 15. Nxf7 Rxf7 16. Bd5 Qf8) ({Fritz
gives the only playable line as} 14... Bf5 {then if} 15. g4 exf4 16. Bd5+ Kh8
17. Bxf4 Bxg4 18. hxg4 Rxf4 19. Nxf4 Qxg5) 15. Nxe6 {I now had to decide
whether to resign or carry on.} exf4 ({Fritz gives} 15... Rf5 16. Be4 Rh5 {
as "best". However "best" moves aren't necessarily relevant now.}) 16. Bxf4
Rfe8 17. Nxg7 Qxg7 18. Qd2 Ne7 19. Bh6 Qe5 20. d4 Qe6 21. Nf4 Qxc4 22. Rac1 Qb5
23. Rxc7 Nf5 24. Nd5 Re2 {I didn't give this much thought. I felt that this
was my only hope.} 25. Rxd7 (25. Rxd7 {[0-1] An incredible position. he has
Queen, Rook & Knight en prise, and I can also take his Bishop but I have to
resign!} Rxd2 (25... Qxd7 26. Qxe2) (25... Kh8 26. Qxe2 Qxd7) (25... Nxh6 26.
Nf6+ Kf8 (26... Kh8 27. Rxh7#) 27. Qxh6#) (25... Qxd5 26. Qxe2 {5 and mate in})
(25... Rxg2+ 26. Qxg2) (25... Rf8 26. Ne7+ Rxe7 (26... Kf7 27. Nxf5+) (26...
Kh8 27. Bg7+ Kxg7 28. Nxf5+ Kf6 29. Ng7+ Rf2 30. Rxf2+ Qf5 31. Rxf5+ gxf5 32.
Qh6#) 27. Rxe7) 26. Nf6+ Kh8 27. Rxh7#) 1-0

