{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nc3 Bc5 4. Nxe5 Bd4 (4... Nc6 $142) 5.
Nf3 Bxc3 6. dxc3 O-O (6... Nxe4 $142) 7. Bd3 d6 8. h3 Re8 9. Bg5 (9. O-O $142)
9... Nc6 ({Correct is} 9... Nxe4 10. Bxd8 Nxc3+) 10. O-O Ne5 11. Re1 h6 12. Bf4
Nfd7 13. Nd4 Nxd3 14. cxd3 Ne5 15. Re3 a6 16. Rg3 Qf6 17. Qd2 Kh8 18. Ne2 Bd7
19. Be3 Rg8 20. f4 Nc6 21. Rf1 {Not really necessary but in a quickplay solid 
(quick) moves make sense.} Ne7 22. f5 {Again I was playing quick safe, solid} (
22. Bd4 $142 Qh4 23. f5 f6 24. Rg4 Qh5 25. Bxf6 gxf6 26. Ng3) 22... Nc6 23. Nf4
Ne5 24. b3 {To prevent ........Nc4 after d4.} Qh4 25. Bf2 g6 $2 {He is lost.}
26. Rxg6 Nf3+ (26... Nf3+ {Moving quickly he fails to notice that after} 27.
gxf3 Rxg6+ 28. Nxg6+ {is check}) 27. gxf3 Qd8 28. Rg4 (28. Ne6 {is quickest
but 28.Rg4 makes more sense in a quickplay if one is looking for quick, solid,
moves}) 28... Rxg4+ 29. fxg4 Qg5 30. Be3 Qh4 31. Kg2 Rg8 32. Bd4+ Kh7 33. Nh5
c5 34. Bf6 1-0

