{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 c5 4. d5 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. Nc3 g6 7.
Bg2 Bg7 8. Nf3 Na6 9. O-O O-O 10. Nd2 Nc7 {[1']} 11. a4 Bd7 12. Nc4 Nce8 13.
Bf4 Qc7 14. h3 (14. e4 Nh5 15. Be3 {Fritz}) 14... Nh5 15. Bg5 f6 16. Bd2 f5 17.
e4 f4 18. Kh2 {Being too careful} (18. g4 $142 f3 (18... Nhf6 {I had not
considered} 19. Re1 ({I only looked at} 19. Bxf4 Nxe4) 19... h5 20. g5) 19.
Bxf3) 18... fxg3+ 19. fxg3 Rxf1 20. Qxf1 Bd4 21. Qf3 Nef6 22. Bh6 Ng7 23. Ne2
Rf8 24. Qd3 b5 25. Nxd4 cxd4 26. Na3 bxa4 27. Qxd4 Qb6 $2 {Played quickly, as
with a number of his moves.} 28. Qxb6 axb6 29. Nc4 Nfe8 30. Nxb6 Bb5 31. Nxa4
Rf2 32. b3 {I was getting short of time now and having to move fairly quickly.}
Bd3 33. Kg1 Rc2 34. Nb6 (34. Rd1 Be2 35. Rc1 {Fritz}) 34... Nf6 35. Ra8+ (35.
e5 $142 dxe5 36. d6 Bb5 37. Ra8+ Nge8 38. d7 {With time short I was playing
the straightforward line.}) 35... Nge8 36. Nd7 Kf7 37. Ra7 Rc7 38. Rxc7 Nxc7
39. Nxf6 Kxf6 40. Bf4 Nb5 41. Bf1 $2 {Having to move quickly I try to exchange
his Bishop off. However it throws away the win. 41.Kf2 is best.} (41. Bf1 $2 {
Resigning in a drawn position with me short of time and he with plenty of
time! He should play......} Bxf1 42. Kxf1 g5 43. Bc1 Ke5 44. Bxg5 Kxe4 45. Bf6
Nc7 46. Ke2 Nxd5) 1-0

