{30' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. b6 Qxb6 6. Nc3 d6 7.
e4 g6 8. Bd3 Bg7 9. Nf3 O-O 10. Nd2 Nbd7 11. O-O Ne5 12. Be2 Bg4 {A bit odd,
it just gets pushed back.} 13. f3 Bd7 14. Kh1 Bb5 15. a4 Bxe2 16. Qxe2 Rfc8 $2
(16... Qb7 $142) (16... Qc7 $142) 17. f4 Neg4 ({If} 17... Ned7 18. e5 dxe5 19.
fxe5 Nxd5 20. Nxd5) 18. h3 $2 {Played quickly, I thought that I could win a
piece so played this without further thought.} ({Correct is} 18. e5 dxe5 19.
fxe5) 18... Nh6 19. g4 Kh8 20. g5 Nh5 21. gxh6 $5 {Making it interesting I get
3 pieces for the Queen.} (21. Nc4) (21. Kg2) 21... Ng3+ 22. Kh2 Nxe2 23. hxg7+
Kxg7 24. Nxe2 Qb4 25. Ra3 Rab8 26. Rff3 Qa5 27. Ng3 f6 28. Rfe3 (28. Nc4 $142 {
but I was concerned about.} Qe1) 28... c4 (28... Rxb2 $142 29. Bxb2 Qxd2+ 30.
Re2 Qxf4) 29. Ne2 Rb4 30. Nd4 Rxa4 (30... Rxb2 $142) 31. Nc6 $2 {Errors all
round as we were playing fast. I had played the move almost instantaneously.} (
{Correct is} 31. Rac3) 31... Rxc6 $2 (31... Rxa3 $142 32. bxa3 Qc5) 32. dxc6
Rxa3 33. Rxa3 Qb6 34. Rc3 ({I knew he was playing for a draw so} 34. Kg2 {
might have been preferable.}) 34... Qf2+ {Going for the draw.} (34... Qxc6 $145
) 35. Kh1 Qe1+ {He offered a draw here.} 36. Kg2 Qe2+ 37. Kg3 h5 38. h4 (38. c7
e5 39. fxe5 (39. Nxc4 h4+ $11 (39... exf4+ 40. Bxf4 $11)) 39... h4+ 40. Kxh4
Qf2+ $11) 38... Qg4+ 39. Kf2 {It's drawn. He has a perpetual and he can't try
to win as my c-pawn ensures at least a draw.} 1/2-1/2

