{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 d5 5. e3 b6 $2 6. Nf3 $2 {
Terrible. I was just playing solid developing moves. He was playing quickly so
I assumed that he knew the line and gave no thought to 6.Qa4+} ({However, after
} 6. Qa4+ Nc6 7. Qxc6+ Bd7 8. Qb7 a5 9. cxd5 {and the White Queen will get out.
}) 6... O-O 7. Be2 Bb7 8. O-O Nbd7 9. b3 Bxc3 10. Qxc3 Ne4 11. Qc2 f5 12. Ba3
Rf7 13. Rac1 g5 {Aggressive but losing a pawn and the c-file} 14. cxd5 Bxd5 15.
Qxc7 Qf6 16. Ne5 {Fritz prefers 16.Qc2 or16.Rc2} Nxe5 17. Qxe5 Qg6 {Black is
determined on a QS attack.} (17... Qxe5 $142) 18. f3 Nf6 19. Rc7 Raf8 $2 {
Simply forgetting about my Bishop} 20. Bxf8 Rxf8 21. Rfc1 g4 {His only hope.}
22. fxg4 Nxg4 23. Bxg4 Qxg4 24. Qg3 Qxg3 25. hxg3 a5 26. Rc8 a4 27. Rxf8+ Kxf8
28. bxa4 Bxa2 29. Rc6 1-0

