{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7.
d5 e6 8. Be2 exd5 9. exd5 Re8 10. O-O Bf5 11. Bd3 Ne4 (11... Bxd3 $142 12. Qxd3
Na6) 12. Nxe4 Bxe4 13. Bxe4 Rxe4 14. Qc2 Qe7 15. Bd2 Nd7 16. Rae1 Re8 17. Bc3 (
17. Rxe4 $142 Qxe4 18. Qb3) 17... Bxc3 18. Qxc3 Qf6 19. Qd2 b6 {To prevent
lines involving Qa5} (19... Rxe1 $142 20. Rxe1 Rxe1+ 21. Nxe1 Qf5 22. b3 b5)
20. b3 (20. g3 {Defending f4 is slightly better.}) 20... Rxe1 21. Rxe1 Rxe1+
22. Nxe1 {Had I have played 20.g3 I woulsd have been able to recapture with
the Queen.} Qa1 23. Kf2 Nf6 24. Kf3 Qb1 $11 (24... b5 25. cxb5 Qb1 26. Nd3 Qg1
27. Nf2 Qxh2 28. Nh3 h5 $11) 25. Qe2 Qf5 (25... b5 $142) 26. h3 g5 27. Nd3 h5
28. Qe3 g4+ 29. hxg4 hxg4+ ({I had expected} 29... Nxg4 {then} 30. Qe8+ Kg7 31.
Qe2 Qg6 32. g3 Nh6) 30. Ke2 Kf8 31. g3 (31. a4 {Preventing ......b5 is better})
31... Qh7 32. Nf2 Qb1 {Missing a chance.} (32... Qc2+ $142 33. Qd2 Qb1 34. Qd1
({If} 34. Ke3 Qg1) 34... Qxa2+) 33. a4 Kg7 34. Qc3 {I offered a draw here.}
Qa2+ 35. Kf1 Kg6 36. Qe3 Qb1+ 37. Kg2 Qc2 38. Kg1 Kf5 39. Kf1 Ne4 {Leads to a
completely drawn position.} 40. Nxe4 Qxe4 41. Kf2 Qc2+ {Neither side can
exchange Queens. (I lose, and he would draw if doing so)} 42. Kf1 Qd1+ 43. Kg2
a6 44. Kf2 Qh1 45. Qd3+ Qe4 46. Qe3 Qc2+ 47. Kf1 Qd1+ {[Dick did not play in
the RD9 LRGS v Lancaster A]} 1/2-1/2

