diagonal.} 9. h4 Bh6 $2 {He drops back to keep the diagonal. However he misses
the point of 9.h4} ({No doubt noting that} 9... Bxh4 10. Qh5 {is not playable})
10. exf5 Qf6 {He now threatens 11.......Bxf5 but walks into a fork on g5.} ({
Realising now that} 10... Bxf5 11. Bxf5 Rxf5 12. g4 {loses the Bishop.}) 11. g4
g5 12. Ne4 Qd8 13. Qd2 {Pinning the g-Pawn with hxg5 coming.} Bxf5 {Complete
desperation but he has no move} 14. gxf5 Rxf5 15. hxg5 Bxg5 16. Nxg5 Rxg5 17.
Bxh7+ Kg7 18. Nf3 1-0

