{40 in 1hr 40' + 20'} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 {For the first time ever.} 3. cxd5 Qxd5
4. Nc3 {Big surprise.} Qxd4 5. Bd2 (5. Qxd4 $142) 5... Bd6 6. Nf3 Qg4 7. Nb5
Qd7 8. Nxd6+ Qxd6 9. Qb3 Nc6 10. O-O-O Nge7 11. Bc3 Qe6 12. Qa4 (12. Qxe6 $142
Bxe6 13. Nxe5 Nd5 14. Nxc6 Nxc3 15. bxc3 bxc6) 12... O-O 13. e4 Qf6 14. Kb1 a6
15. Qa3 Be6 16. Bd3 Rfd8 17. h3 Ng6 18. Bd2 Nf4 19. Bc2 h6 (19... Nxg2 {
is just too dangerous.}) 20. g4 Nd3 (20... Bc4 {Fritz}) 21. Nh2 Qe7 (21... Nxf2
$142 22. Rhf1 Nd4 23. Rc1 Bc4 24. g5 Nxc2 25. Rxc2 Qb6 {I didn't fancy pinning
the Knight on f2}) 22. Qxe7 Nxe7 23. Be3 Nb4 24. b3 Nxc2 25. Kxc2 Nc6 26. Nf3
f6 27. Kc3 Kf7 28. Nh4 a5 29. f4 $2 {Losing a Pawn.} Rxd1 30. Rxd1 exf4 31. Bc1
g5 32. Nf5 Bxf5 (32... Rh8 $142) (32... h5 $142) 33. exf5 Ne5 34. Rd5 Ra6 (
34... c6 $142) (34... h5 $142) (34... Re8 $142) 35. Ba3 a4 36. Bc5 Rc6 37. Kd2
axb3 38. axb3 Ra6 39. Rd8 Rc6 (39... b6 $142 40. Bd4 Ra2+ 41. Kd1 f3) 40. Bf8
b6 {I was much too conservative around here} (40... f3 $142) 41. Rc8 Nd7 (41...
f3) 42. Bxh6 Nc5 (42... f3) 43. h4 Nxb3+ (43... Ne4+ $142) 44. Kd3 Nc5+ {
I started to realise that I had gone wrong} 45. Ke2 Ne4 46. Kf3 Nd6 47. Rf8+
Ke7 48. hxg5 fxg5 $2 ({Correct is} 48... Rc3+ 49. Ke2 (49. Kxf4 $2 fxg5+) 49...
f3+ 50. Kf1 Ne4 51. gxf6+ Nxf6 52. Rh8 Nxg4) 49. f6+ Ke6 {I was worried now.
Is it lost?} 50. Bxg5 Rc3+ {I was also running out of time} 51. Kxf4 Rc4+ {
It is 0.00 but I thought it was lost.} 52. Kf3 Rc3+ 53. Kg2 Rc5 {I was having
to move quickly now.} 54. Bh4 $2 {He had more time than me but also moved
quickly.} Rc2+ $2 {I was "prepairing" my moves so that I could move quickly
and miss the g-Pawn.} 55. Bf2 b5 56. g5 Kf5 ({I saw} 56... Ne4 57. Re8+) 57.
Rg8 Ne4 {With little time to think I initially thought that it was lost. ......
....Ne4 is the only hope.} 58. f7 Rxf2+ 59. Kg1 Ke6 60. g6 Rxf7 61. gxf7 Kxf7 {
with almost no time left I just wanted to consolidate for the half point.} 62.
Rb8 Nd6 63. Kf2 Ke6 64. Ke3 Kd5 {All a big rush now} 65. Kd3 Kc6 66. Kd4 Nb7
67. Rh8 Kb6 68. Rh6+ c6 69. Rg6 Na5 70. Rg8 Nb7 71. Rc8 Nd6 72. Rf8 Nb7 73. Ke5
Kc7 74. Ke6 Kb6 {I had given up recording moves some time back and cannot
reconstruct the ending exactly. Maybe 75........Rc8} 75. Rc8 Nc5+ 76. Kd6 Nb7+
77. Ke5 Na5 78. Rb8+ Nb7 1/2-1/2

