Nxc4 14. Qxc4 Rb8 15. Bf4 Nh5 16. Bd2 Bd7 17. Rfe1 b5 18. Qd3 (18. axb5 $142
axb5 19. Qb3) 18... b4 (18... c4 $142) 19. Nd1 a5 20. Ra2 Qb6 21. b3 Bc8 22.
Ne3 Ba6 23. Nc4 Qd8 24. Rc2 Rb7 25. Bf3 Nf6 26. Bf4 h6 27. Qd1 Bxc4 28. Rxc4 g5
29. Bc1 (29. Be3 {Looks better}) 29... Nd7 30. Bg2 Ne5 (30... Bc3 $142) 31. Rc2
Qb6 32. Bb2 Rbe7 33. e3 Qa6 34. Bxe5 Bxe5 35. Bf1 Qb6 36. Qh5 Kg7 37. Rc4 Bc3
38. Rd1 Re5 39. Bd3 $2 {Simply overlooking the d-Pawn.} (39. Qe2) (39. Bh3) (
39. h4) 39... Rxd5 40. h4 Qd8 41. hxg5 Rxg5 42. Rg4 Rxg4 43. Qxg4+ Qg5 44. Qd7
$2 {A big decieion point. I felt I could hold it a Pawn down with 44.Qxg5+
However, I decided to play "actively" but missed his reply.} Rxe3 $1 {I missed
this.} 45. Bc4 $2 {Still trying to play actively.} (45. Qxd6 $142 Be5 46. Qd7
Rxg3+ 47. fxg3 Qxg3+ 48. Kf1 Qf3+ 49. Ke1 {What I had failed to notice is that
after 45.Qxd6 the Queen is covering g3.}) 45... Rxg3+ {Now it is simply lost.
I knocked out some more fast moves but there is little hope of him going wrong.
} 46. fxg3 Qxg3+ 47. Kf1 Qf3+ 48. Kg1 Qxd1+ 49. Kg2 Qc2+ 50. Kf3 Qg6 51. Qc7 h5
52. Qxa5 Bd4 53. Qc7 Qg4# {In Rd5 I lost to Uwe Schmidt after a bad error.} 0-1

