{90' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Bc4 Bg7
7. f3 Nbd7 8. Be3 Ne5 9. Bb3 Bd7 10. Qd2 Rc8 11. O-O-O a6 12. Kb1 O-O 13. h4 b5
14. g4 e6 {This just seemed to leave the d-Pawn weak.} 15. h5 b4 {Louis had
decided to "give it a go" and played all this very quickly. Unfortunately this
caused me to speed up as well.} 16. Nce2 a5 17. c3 {Played fairly quickly.} (
17. hxg6 $142 a4 18. gxf7+ Kxf7 19. Bxe6+ Bxe6 20. Nxe6 Kxe6 21. Nd4+ Kf7 22.
g5 Nc4 23. Qd3) 17... a4 18. Bc2 (18. hxg6 $142 axb3 19. gxh7+ Nxh7 20. axb3)
18... Nc4 19. Qd3 {I now realised that ......e5 leaves the Knight with nowhere
to go.} Nxe3 (19... bxc3 $142 20. Qxc3 e5 21. h6 Bh8 22. Nf5 gxf5) 20. Qxe3
bxc3 (20... e5 $142 21. h6 exd4 22. Qxd4 Bh8 23. Qxb4 Ne8 24. Bxa4) 21. Nxc3 {
Played quickly with a sense of relief.} e5 {The tide turns} (21... a3 22. h6
Bh8 23. bxa3 Qa5 24. Rd3) 22. Ndb5 Bxb5 (22... d5 23. exd5 Bxb5 24. Nxb5 Qa5)
23. Nxb5 Rxc2 $5 {Still in "give it a go" mode.} (23... d5 $142 24. h6 Bh8 25.
exd5 Qa5) 24. Kxc2 Qc8+ 25. Kb1 d5 {Trying to open the long black diagonal.}
26. exd5 e4 27. hxg6 fxg6 28. g5 Qb8 $5 {Desperation mode: aiming at b2} 29.
gxf6 Bxf6 30. Nd4 ({I considered} 30. Qa7 {forcing the exchange of Queensbut
he gets 3 passed Pawns.}) 30... exf3 31. Rd2 Qb6 {He seemed to have given up
now and was just rattling off a few moves.} 32. Qe6+ Kg7 {Ending it quickly.
He gave this no thought. It was lost anyway.} 33. Qxb6 Bxd4 34. Qxd4+ Kg8 35.
Rxh7 Rf7 36. Rh8# 1-0

