{90' each/game} 1. Nf3 c5 2. c4 g6 3. d3 Bg7 4. Nc3 e6 5. e4 Nc6 6. Be3 d6 7.
Be2 Nge7 8. Qd2 h6 9. O-O b6 {Rather a waste of a move.} (9... Nd4 $142) (9...
e5 $142) 10. Rad1 (10. d4 $142) 10... e5 {To prevent 11.d4} 11. b3 f5 12. exf5
gxf5 {Fritz prefers 12......Nxf5 but I prefer my move against a weaker
opponent..} 13. g3 Ng6 14. Qc2 O-O {[13'] He thought for a long time here and
I was wondering if he would do something desperate like 15.g4, when he played
it.} 15. g4 $2 f4 16. Bd2 Bxg4 17. d4 Nh4 (17... Bf5 {is also good.}) 18. Nxh4
Qxh4 19. Bxg4 Qxg4+ 20. Kh1 Qf3+ 21. Kg1 Nxd4 ({I considered} 21... Rf6 22. Qe4
cxd4 (22... Nxd4)) 22. Qg6 $2 Rf6 $2 (22... Rf5 $142) 23. Qg2 Qxg2+ 24. Kxg2
Rg6+ 25. Kh1 Kf7 {[26']} 26. Ne4 Rd8 27. Bc3 Bf8 28. Rg1 {He is 2 Pawns down
but is happy to exchange pieces.} Rxg1+ 29. Rxg1 Be7 30. Kg2 d5 31. cxd5 Rxd5
32. Rd1 Rd8 33. f3 $2 (33. Bxd4 $142) 33... Ke6 ({If} 33... Nxf3 34. Rxd8 Nh4+
35. Kf2 Bxd8 {then White has} 36. Bxe5) ({However, correct is} 33... Rg8+ 34.
Kf2 Bh4+ 35. Kf1 Nxf3) 34. Rd3 Kf5 35. h3 Bh4 ({If} 35... Nxf3 36. Ng3+) 36.
Bxd4 Rxd4 37. Rxd4 exd4 38. Kf1 d3 $1 {I guess he missed this.} 39. Nd6+ Ke6 (
39... Ke5 {is quicker but I was playing ultra safe.}) 40. Nc4 Kd5 41. a4 Kd4
42. Nd6 Kc3 43. Nb5+ Kc2 44. Nxa7 d2 0-1

