{90' each/game} 1. d4 c5 2. d5 d6 3. c4 Nf6 4. Nc3 g6 5. e4 b5 {Not a good way
of playing the Benko.} 6. cxb5 a6 7. bxa6 Bxa6 8. Bxa6 Rxa6 9. Nge2 Bg7 10. O-O
O-O 11. Qc2 Nbd7 12. b3 Qb6 13. Rb1 Rb8 14. Bf4 Ne8 15. Be3 Qb7 16. Rfd1 Nc7
17. Bc1 Nb5 18. Nxb5 Qxb5 19. Bb2 $2 {I became rather obsessed with exchnging
the black squared Bishop.} (19. Bg5 $142) (19. h3 $142) (19. f3 $142) 19...
Rxa2 20. Nc3 Bxc3 21. Qxc3 f6 {I now started to feel that my position was
worse that I had expected. Black threatens 21.......c4 and also the b-Pawn.
The more I looked at it the worse it looked.} 22. Qh3 $2 {Deciding that I had
to do something active but missing the correct move.} (22. Qe1 $142) 22... Qe2
23. Qxd7 (23. Rf1 $142 Rxb2 24. Rxb2 Qxb2 25. Qe6+ Kf8 26. Qxd7 Qxb3 27. g3)
23... Rxb2 24. Qe6+ Kf8 25. Qh3 $4 {Suicide. I saw my error straight away and
had to sit there waiting for the killer blow.} (25. Rf1 $142 Rxb1 26. Rxb1 c4
27. Qh3 Qxe4 28. Rf1) 25... Rxb1 $2 ({After} 25... R8xb3 {I have to resign. He
had simply seen that the line wins the e4 Pawn so he didn't look for anything
better}) 26. Rxb1 Qxe4 27. Rd1 h5 {I felt that another Pawn is bound to go and
that my only hope was some sort of attack on his King. He knidly advances his
KS Pawns.} 28. Kf1 Qg4 29. Qd3 Qf5 30. Qe3 (30. Qxf5 gxf5 {I wasn't confident
I could hold with two weak Pawns.}) 30... g5 31. g3 Rb4 32. Re1 Rb7 33. Kg2 $2
{I have no idea why I did this.} Qxd5+ 34. Kg1 Qxb3 35. Qe4 {The d5 Pawn going
has opened up another line to his back rank.} e5 36. Qc6 Ke7 37. Ra1 {Now Ra8
is a serious threat.} Qb6 (37... Rd7 $142) 38. Qe4 Qb4 $2 {Losing half a point.
} (38... Ke6 $142) 39. Qh7+ Ke6 40. Qg8+ Kf5 41. Qc8+ Kg6 {Bringing the King
into the open is suicide.} 42. Qg8+ Rg7 43. Qe8+ Kh6 44. Qh8+ Kg6 45. Qe8+
1/2-1/2

