7. Bd2 Bxd2+ 8. Nbxd2 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Qb3 Nce7 {As played by Karpov} ({
I didn't like} 10... Na5 {aas after} 11. Qa4+ Nc6 {he has a draw by repetition.
}) 11. O-O O-O 12. Rfe1 Nb6 13. Bd3 Be6 $5 (13... Be6 {As I let go of the
Bishop I suddenly thought that} 14. Rxe6 {might be good for White. However,}
fxe6 15. Qxe6+ Kh8 16. Qe4 Ng6 17. Qxb7 {0.67/0 is only}) 14. Qc2 h6 15. a3 c6
16. Ne4 Bd5 17. Qc5 Ng6 18. Ned2 Nf4 19. Bf1 Ne6 20. Qc3 Re8 21. Re3 $2 Qd6 $2
{I was preoccupied with the wrong thing, namely challenging his doubling of
Rooks on the e-file. I was intending .......Nc7 nest move} (21... Bxf3 {
Wins the d-Pawn after} 22. Rxf3 (22. Nxf3 $2 {allows} Nd5)) 22. Rae1 Nc7 23.
Ne5 Be6 24. Rg3 Rad8 (24... Qd8 $142) 25. Ndf3 ({Missing} 25. Ne4 Qxd4 26. Nf6+
) 25... Ncd5 26. Qd2 Kf8 27. Rd1 {He offered a draw here. I commented that
although the room was freezing cold I'd carry on for a few moves.} Nf6 {
Threat 28......Nh5} 28. Ne1 {Played quite quickly, possibly off-guard, as my
last move was a "backward" move so not immediatley threatening.} Ne4 29. Qf4
Nxg3 30. Qxg3 Bf5 31. Qf4 $2 {Looking a bit shell-shocked he played this
quickly and ends it quickly.} Rxe5 32. dxe5 Qxd1 33. Qxf5 Qxe1 0-1

