{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 7.
d5 e6 8. Be2 exd5 9. exd5 Bg4 10. O-O Re8 11. h3 Bd7 12. Bd3 Nh5 13. g4 Bxc3
14. bxc3 Ng3 15. Re1 f5 16. g5 $2 (16. Ng5 $142 {then if} h6 17. Ne6 Qh4 18.
Kg2 Na6 19. Re3) 16... Na6 17. Kg2 Nh5 18. Bd2 Re7 19. Rxe7 Qxe7 20. Ne1 {
Realising that I had made a mess of it, I try to manoeuvre the Knight to b5.
If he were to capture my d2 Bishop may have a future.} Re8 21. Nc2 Ba4 22. Qc1
Qf7 23. Na3 Nc7 24. Rb1 $2 {Too casual} Nxd5 25. Nb5 Bxb5 26. cxb5 $4 {
Rubbish! Again played quickly.} Ndxf4+ 27. Bxf4 {I could resign.} Qd5+ 28. Kg1
Qxd3 29. Rb2 Nxf4 30. Qxf4 Re1+ 31. Kg2 Qe4+ 32. Qxe4 Rxe4 33. Rd2 {I played
the rest of the game at high speed.} Re6 34. h4 Kf7 35. Kf3 Ke7 36. h5 Re4 37.
hxg6 hxg6 38. Rh2 Kd7 39. Rh7+ Re7 40. Rh6 Rg7 41. Rh8 Ke6 42. c4 Ke5 43. Ke3 {
Threatening mate!} f4+ 44. Kf3 Kd4 45. Rd8 Kxc4 46. b6 axb6 47. Rxd6 Kb5 48.
Kxf4 Ka5 49. Ke3 b5 50. Kd2 b4 51. Kc2 Kb5 52. Kb2 Ka4 53. Re6 c4 54. Re8 c3+
55. Kc2 Rd7 ({Not} 55... Ka3 $4 56. Ra8#) 56. Ra8+ Kb5 57. a4+ bxa3 58. Rxa3
Rd5 59. Rb3+ Kc6 60. Kxc3 Rxg5 61. Kd4 b5 62. Rc3+ Kd6 63. Rc8 {Black was now
short of time and moving fast. He had stopped recording the moves and in the
rush put my Rook on c1 on his set. [Colin is partially sighted and uses a
braille set]} ({This is the position on Colin's braille set} 63. Rc1 Rd5+ 64.
Ke4 g5 {He was confused when Dick played 65.Rd8+}) 63... Rd5+ 64. Ke4 g5 65.
Rd8+ 1/2-1/2

