{90' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 Nbd7
7. Bd3 Nf8 8. Nge2 Ne6 9. Bh4 g6 10. O-O Ng7 11. Qb3 c6 12. Bg3 O-O 13. Rac1
Re8 14. h3 Bd6 15. Bh4 Be7 16. Qc2 Bf5 17. Bxf5 Nxf5 18. Bg5 Nd6 19. Nf4 Kg7
20. Nd3 Nfe4 21. Bxe7 Qxe7 22. Nxe4 Qxe4 23. Ne5 Qxc2 24. Rxc2 a5 25. Rfc1 {
It's dead level, but I have decided to play on in games like this, rather than
offer a draw, as I have been doing lately.} f6 26. Nd7 Kf7 27. Nc5 Ra7 28. b3
Re7 29. Na4 Ke8 30. g3 Kd8 31. Kg2 Ra6 32. h4 f5 33. Kf3 Ra8 34. Nc5 Ne4 35.
Na4 Nd6 36. Nb6 Ra6 37. Na4 Ne4 38. Nc5 {Deciding to try it with just the
Rooks on.} Nxc5 39. Rxc5 Kd7 40. Ke2 Kd6 41. Kd3 Re8 42. R5c3 Re7 43. R3c2 Re8
44. Rg1 {My only hope of winning is via the KS} ({If} 44. h5 {then} g5 {
after the text I can try g4}) 44... h5 45. f3 Raa8 46. g4 hxg4 (46... fxg4 {
is slightly better}) 47. fxg4 Rh8 {Now I get a passed Pawn} (47... fxg4 $142)
48. gxf5 gxf5 49. Rh2 Rag8 {A bit of a surprise. It's easier for him with two
Rooks on.} 50. Rxg8 Rxg8 51. h5 Ke6 52. Ke2 {I wondered about pushing the Pawn
but the King march is best.} Kf6 53. Kf3 Rh8 54. Kf4 Rh6 55. Rh1 Rh7 56. h6 Kg6
{He has no good move. Also he was short of time.} 57. Ke5 Rxh6 {With little
time he could lose on time, if he does nothing, so he felt that he had to do
something.} ({If} 57... Re7+ 58. Kd6 Rh7 59. Ke6 {and he has no move}) 58.
Rxh6+ Kxh6 59. Kxf5 Kh5 (59... Kg7 {also loses.}) 60. e4 dxe4 61. Kxe4 Kg4 62.
d5 cxd5+ 63. Kxd5 Kf4 64. Kc5 Ke4 65. Kb5 Kd4 66. Kxa5 Kc5 67. b4+ Kc4 68. a4
Kb3 69. Kb5 Ka3 70. a5 Kb3 71. Kc5 Ka4 72. Kc4 1-0

