{90' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. e4 Nc6 4. g3 Bc5 5. Bg2 d6 6. h3 Be6 7.
d3 Qd7 8. Be3 Nd4 9. Nge2 b5 $5 {Enterprising but very risky.} 10. Bxd4 exd4
11. Nxb5 Rb8 {Best, the threat was 12.e5} 12. Nbxd4 Rxb2 $5 {Fritz thinks this
is playable but in practice I think it's pretty suicidal.} (12... O-O {Must be
better.}) 13. e5 {The Knight is attacked and 14.Bc6 is threatened.} Bb4+ $2 ({
Fritz claims} 13... Rxe2+ 14. Nxe2 dxe5 {is 0.23. but White is the exchange up.
}) 14. Kf1 O-O {There is nothing better.} 15. exf6 Rb8 16. Nb3 Bf5 (16... Z0 {
The threat} 17. Qc1 Ba3 18. Qg5) 17. Ned4 Re8 18. Bc6 Bxh3+ {There is no good
move.} (18... Re1+ 19. Qxe1 Bxd3+ 20. Kg2 Bxe1 21. Rhxe1 Qc8 22. Re8+ Qxe8 23.
Bxe8) 19. Kg1 Ree2 {Resigns is the alternative.} 20. Qxe2 ({Also an easy win is
} 20. Bxd7 Rxf2 21. Bxh3) 1-0

