{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f4 O-O 6. Nf3 Bg4 7.
Be2 c5 8. d5 e6 9. O-O exd5 10. exd5 Re8 11. h3 {As in our Lancaster C.C.game
15/15/12.} (11. Bd2 $142) 11... Bd7 12. Bd3 Nh5 13. g4 {13.Re1 is better the
text simply fprces him to play the move he was going to play anyway.} Bxc3 14.
bxc3 Ng3 15. Re1 f5 16. Kh2 Ne4 17. Bxe4 Rxe4 18. Rxe4 fxe4 19. Ng5 Qe7 20. Qe2
(20. Qc2 $142) 20... Na6 21. Qxe4 Re8 22. Ne6 $5 (22. Qxe7 $142 Rxe7 23. Kg3)
22... Bxe6 23. dxe6 Qxe6 24. Qd5 $2 {Completely losing it.} (24. Qxe6+ $142
Rxe6 25. Rb1 b6 26. Kg3 Re4 27. Bb2) 24... Qxd5 {He offered a draw here 
(foolishly). Even more foolishly I declined.} 25. cxd5 Nc7 26. f5 {I now
realised that I was lost so I said I would accept a draw if he still wanted
one. he agreed!} ({It is completerly lost e.g.} 26. Kg3 Nxd5 27. Bb2 Nxc3 28.
Bxc3 Re3+) ({After} 26. f5 Nxd5 {I have no move.}) 1/2-1/2

