{90' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. g3 c6 4. Bg2 Bb4 5. a3 Bxc3 6. bxc3 d6 (
6... d5) 7. Rb1 Nbd7 8. d3 Qa5 9. Qc2 ({Alternatively} 9. Nf3 Qxc3+ 10. Bd2
Qxa3 11. Bb4 Qa6 12. Bxd6) 9... Nc5 10. Nf3 e4 11. Nd4 exd3 12. exd3 O-O 13.
O-O Re8 14. Bg5 {I spent a long time deciding to play this or 14.Bf4} Nce4 {
I had expected this reply.} (14... Ng4 $142) 15. Bf4 Qxc3 16. dxe4 Qxd4 17.
Rfd1 Qc5 18. Bxd6 Qh5 19. f3 {A solid move preventing ......Ng4 and defending
the e-Pawn.} (19. c5 $142 Ng4 20. h3) 19... Re6 {He needs to develop his
Queenside.} 20. Qf2 Nd7 (20... b6 $142) 21. f4 Rh6 {The attempt at attack is a
waste of time and the Rook risks getting stuck.} 22. Bf3 Qa5 23. f5 {
Threatening to win the exchange by 24.Bg5} Rxd6 $5 {Deciding that he can't
move the Rook.} (23... f6 $142) 24. Rxd6 Qxa3 25. Rbd1 Nf8 26. Rd8 Qe7 27. Qd4
a5 28. e5 f6 29. Qd6 Qxd6 {There is no move.} (29... Qf7 30. e6 {Wins the
Queen.}) 30. exd6 1-0

