{35 in 1hr 15' + 15'} 1. e4 c6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Qf3 e6 {I remembere this from 40
years ago and decided to play it safe.} 4. d4 dxe4 5. Nxe4 Nf6 {Still playing
it carefully} (5... Qxd4 $142 6. Ne2 Qb6 7. Be3 Qxb2 8. Bd4 Qxc2) 6. Bd3 Nxe4
7. Qxe4 Nd7 8. Nf3 Nf6 9. Qe2 Be7 10. Bd2 Bd7 11. Ne5 a6 12. c3 c5 {The
alternatives are slightly better.} (12... g5) (12... Qb6) (12... O-O) 13. dxc5
Bxc5 14. Bg5 Qc7 15. Bxf6 (15. O-O-O $142) 15... gxf6 16. Nxd7 Qxd7 17. O-O-O
Qc7 18. Be4 f5 $5 {Best, but I had overlooked his reply} 19. Bxb7 {Along think
now..} Qxb7 {Best.} 20. Qe5 Rg8 {Missing the best reply although I had
considered it............} (20... Ba3 $142) 21. Qxc5 Rc8 22. Qd6 Rxg2 23. Rhg1
Rg6 24. Rxg6 hxg6 25. Rd3 Qc6 26. Qd4 Qc7 27. Rh3 Ke7 28. Rh7 e5 (28... Qc4)
29. Qd5 Kf6 {I offered a draw here.} 30. f4 exf4 31. Qd4+ Ke6 32. Qb4 $2 {
I looked at my clock and had seconds left to move 35. The next moves were made
instantaneously.} f3 {I was having to move instantly.} 33. Rh3 Qe5 34. Qb6+ Ke7
35. Qf2 Rd8 {Made it! The general opinion (we had spectators) was that I had 1
or 2 seconds left.} 36. Rxf3 Qd5 37. Qh4+ Kd7 38. Rf4 Ke6 39. Qe1+ Qe5 40. Qf2
Qd5 41. Qe1+ Qe5 42. Qf2 Qd5 43. Qe1+ 1/2-1/2

