{90' each/game} 1. c4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. cxd5 cxd5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. Bf4 a6 6. e3 Nc6
7. Bd3 e6 8. Nge2 Bd7 9. Rc1 Qb6 10. O-O Be7 (10... Qxb2 {is not good}) 11. Qd2
Qa7 {Surprisingly this is best!} 12. h3 O-O 13. a3 Rac8 14. b4 b5 15. f3 g6 (
15... h6 {Fritz}) 16. Kh1 Rfd8 17. g4 {Aggresion is appropriate against this
opponent.} h5 (17... Ne8 $142) 18. Qe1 Kg7 19. Qf2 Rh8 20. Kg2 a5 (20... Qb7
$142) 21. Nxb5 Qb6 (21... Qa6 $142) 22. bxa5 Qxa5 23. Nec3 (23. g5 $142 Ne8 24.
h4) 23... Qd8 (23... Na7 $142) ({When playing 20......a5 he may have planned} 
23... Bxa3 {here, but it loses to} 24. Ra1) 24. e4 {Here, and for several
moves, Fritz prefers g5} Ra8 (24... dxe4 $142) 25. Ra1 Qf8 (25... dxe4) 26. g5
Ne8 27. exd5 exd5 28. a4 ({I have no idea why I didn't play} 28. Nxd5 {
presumably because of the attack on the a-Pawn.}) 28... Be6 29. Qe3 Kg8 (29...
Kh7 $142) 30. h4 ({I didn't play} 30. Bxg6 {because of} Bxh3+ {however, after}
31. Kxh3 fxg6 32. Qe6+ Kh7 33. Qxc6 {he can't play} Qxf4 {as the a8 Rook is en
prise. I hadn't spent long on this as time was getting on.}) 30... Ng7 31. Rfe1
Nb4 32. Bb1 Kh7 {he was now getting short of time.} 33. Re2 Qc8 34. Be5 Rd8 35.
Bxg7 Kxg7 36. Qe5+ {Play was speeding up.} Kg8 37. Kh1 {Threatening to capture
on h6 and sidestepping the capture in h3 with check.} Bf8 (37... Ra6 $142 {
but he was moving fast.}) 38. Bxg6 Bg7 39. Qe3 Bf5 40. Bxf5 ({I briefly
considered} 40. Bxf7+ {but missed the fact that after} Kxf7 41. Qe7+ {I was
attacking b4}) 40... Qxf5 41. Qf2 Nd3 42. Qh2 {Moving fast I overlook f3} Rac8
{Moving fast he misses it as well. The rest of his moves were "instantaneous".}
43. Rf1 Nf4 44. Rd2 Rc4 45. Qg3 Bf8 46. Re1 Rdc8 47. Re5 Qh3+ 48. Qxh3 Nxh3 49.
Nxd5 Rxa4 50. Kg2 Ra5 51. Kxh3 (51. Kxh3 Rxb5 {is answered by} 52. Nf6+ {
On 12/3/13 I beat Joseph Wood (LRGS) in the League.}) 1-0

