{90' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. f4 d5 3. exd5 exf4 4. Nf3 Bg4 5. Bb5+ Bd7 (5... c6
$142) 6. Bc4 Nf6 7. O-O Be7 8. d4 a6 (8... c6) 9. Bxf4 b5 10. Bb3 c5 $2 (10...
O-O $142) 11. dxc6 (11. Re1 $142 c4 12. d6 Be6 13. dxe7 {I was playing quite
fast, as usual against B.C.}) 11... Bxc6 (11... Nxc6 $142) 12. Bxb8 {
Objectively not best but I suspected that his reply would be automaticc.} Rxb8
$2 {I was right.} (12... Bxf3 $142) 13. Bxf7+ Kf8 14. Bb3 Bd5 15. c3 Qc7 (15...
g6 $142 {followed by .......Kg7}) 16. Ng5 Bc4 17. Nd2 Qc6 18. Nxc4 bxc4 19. Ba4
Qd5 20. Qd2 {Playing it solid since I am 2 Pawns up.} ({I briefly considered} 
20. Qh5 {but not long enough to notice that} g6 21. Rxf6+ Bxf6 22. Nxh7+ {
wins his Queen.}) 20... h6 21. Nh3 g5 22. Rae1 Qd6 23. Qe2 Rc8 24. Qe5 Qxe5 {
Loses the Knight but he had "given up"} 25. dxe5 Kf7 26. exf6 Bxf6 27. Nf2 Kg7
28. Ng4 Bd8 29. g3 Rb8 30. b4 cxb3 31. Bxb3 Bb6+ 32. Kg2 Rhd8 33. Re7+ Kh8 34.
Nf6 Rd2+ 35. Kh1 Rf8 36. Rh7# {Lancaster A had a bye in Rd1} 1-0

