{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 e5 6. Nb3 (6.
Nb5 $142 {which prevents 6......d5 e.g.} d5 $2 7. exd5 Nxd5 8. Qxd5 Qxd5 9.
Nc7+) 6... d5 7. exd5 Qxd5 8. Bd3 Be7 (8... Nb4 $142) 9. Nc3 Qd8 10. Qe2 O-O
11. O-O Be6 12. Rd1 Qc7 13. Nb5 Qb8 14. Be3 a6 15. Nc3 b5 16. Qf2 Qb7 17. g4 (
17. Nc5 {is more solid. however, in a quickplay (and he was already behind on
time) moves like 17.g4 offer better chances.}) 17... h6 18. h4 Nd4 {A touch of
panic with 19.g5 threatened. However 18.......Nb4 is better.} 19. Nxd4 exd4 20.
Bxd4 Bd5 $2 {Moving fast} 21. Nxd5 $2 {Also moving fast, I considered the
correct move but saw the line played which seemed OK. so didn't look further.}
({Correct is} 21. Bxf6 Bxf6 (21... Bc6 $142 22. Bxe7) 22. Nxd5 Qxd5 $4 23. Bh7+
) 21... Nxd5 22. Be4 Rad8 23. Kh1 Qb8 (23... Rfe8 $142) 24. Bxg7 Kxg7 25. Rxd5
(25. Bxd5 $142) 25... Rxd5 26. Bxd5 Qd8 27. Be4 Bxh4 28. Qe2 Qd6 29. Rd1 Qg3
30. Qh2 {he was down to 2' I had 15'} Qxh2+ ({He could have played} 30... Rd8 {
with a view of reaching an opposite coloured Bishop ending}) 31. Kxh2 Bg5 {
Prevents 32.Rd6} 32. Kg2 Bf6 33. b3 a5 (33... Rd8) 34. Rd5 Rb8 35. Bd3 (35. Bd3
{[1-0]} a4 36. Bxb5 Rd8 37. Rxd8 axb3 38. cxb3 Bxd8 39. b4 Bc7) 1-0

