{90' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 3. Nc3 b5 4. a3 Bb7 5. d4 {Played without
much thought. He loses a Pawn.} b4 6. axb4 cxb4 7. Ne2 Bxe4 8. Ng3 Bb7 9. Be2
e6 10. O-O Nf6 11. c4 bxc3 12. bxc3 Be7 13. Ba3 (13. Qb3 $142) 13... Bxa3 14.
Rxa3 O-O 15. Qb3 Qc7 16. Rb1 Bxf3 17. Bxf3 d5 18. Rc1 Nc6 19. Qa4 Rfb8 20. Ne2
Nd7 21. c4 $2 {Simply losing another Pawn.} Nb6 22. Qd1 Nxc4 23. Rac3 Rb4 24.
Rb1 (24. Be4 {is a possibility. Brian has a tendancy to try to exchange pieces
even when he is losing}) 24... Rxb1 25. Qxb1 Rb8 26. Qd3 Nb4 27. Qd1 g6 28. Nc1
Qb6 29. Be2 Nd6 30. Rb3 Qc7 31. f3 a5 32. Qd2 Rc8 33. Rb1 Qc3 34. Qxc3 {
Exchanging again. he is lost but keeping the Queens on must be his only hope.}
Rxc3 35. Nb3 Nc6 36. Rc1 $2 {Another error again moving very quickly.} Rxc1+ (
36... Nxd4 {is also good.}) 37. Nxc1 Nxd4 38. Bd3 a4 39. Kf2 e5 40. Ke3 f5 41.
h3 Kf7 42. g4 f4+ 43. Kf2 e4 44. fxe4 dxe4 45. Bf1 Kf6 46. Ne2 {Again wanting
to exchange pieces this puts an end to it.} Nxe2 47. Bxe2 a3 0-1

