{2hr each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 f5 {He played this very quickly, so
presumably he knows the line.} 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Bg5 c6 6. e3 Bd6 7. Bd3 O-O 8. O-O
Qe8 9. Bxf6 (9. Bf4 {Fritz}) 9... Rxf6 10. Ne5 b6 11. Rc1 Bb7 12. f4 Bxe5 $2 (
12... Nd7 $142) 13. fxe5 Rf7 14. cxd5 exd5 ({He didn't like} 14... cxd5 15. Nb5
Qd8 16. Nd6) 15. Rxf5 Rxf5 16. Bxf5 Nd7 17. Qg4 Nf8 ({Not} 17... Nf6 $2 18.
Be6+) 18. Nxd5 $1 {I felt that I could avoid the perpetual.} cxd5 19. Rc7 g6
20. Rxb7 Qc6 21. Re7 Qc1+ 22. Kf2 Qd2+ 23. Kf3 {I played this almost
automatically, assuming that the King could hide on h3.} Qd1+ {I now realised
that the King couldn't hide on h3. A bit of thought now sorted out the correct
route.} ({What I had missed originally was that after} 23... Qd1+ 24. Kg3 Qe1+
25. Kh3 Qxe3+ 26. g3 {he has} Qh6+) 24. Kf2 Qd2+ 25. Kf1 Qc1+ 26. Ke2 Qxb2+ 27.
Kf3 {Now it's easy.} Qd2 28. Be6+ Kh8 29. Qg5 Qd1+ 30. Kg3 Qf1 31. Qh6 1-0

