{90' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. Nc3 Bc5 5. a3 O-O 6. e3 Re8 7.
b4 Bf8 8. Nge2 d6 9. O-O Ne7 10. e4 Ng6 11. d3 c6 12. h3 Be6 {Fritz gives this
as best, but f4-f5 is going to push it away.} 13. f4 (13. Be3 {[Fritz] but it
pays to be active in this sort of game.}) 13... exf4 14. gxf4 {Fritz prefers
14.Nxf4 but an aggressive approach is best against this type of opponent.} Nh4
{I felt the Knight was now going to get stuck, but Fritz gives it as best.} 15.
f5 Bd7 16. Bh1 {Leaving the Knight on h4 stuck.} h6 {Else 17.Bg5. Fritz
prefers 16......Nh5} 17. Qe1 ({I wanted to play} 17. Be3 {but then} Nxf5) 17...
g5 (17... Nh5) 18. Qg3 (18. fxg6 Nxg6 19. Qg3 {Fritz}) 18... Nh7 (18... Kh7
$142) 19. Be3 Qe7 20. Bf2 Qe5 (20... Bg7 {Fritz}) 21. Qxe5 dxe5 22. Rad1 (22.
Rfd1 $142) 22... a5 {Missing the reply.} 23. Rb1 Red8 24. bxa5 c5 (24... Bc8
$142) 25. Rxb7 Rxa5 26. Ra1 Bc8 27. Rc7 (27. Rb8 {Fritz}) 27... Ba6 $2 {
This loses it. The Rook on a5 is stuck as is the Knight on h4.} (27... Nf6 $142
) 28. Nd5 Bd6 ({There is no move. If} 28... Rb8 29. Be1 Ra4 30. Nec3 Ra5 31. a4
) 29. Ra7 Nf8 30. Be1 1-0

