{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 d6 6. Be2 e6
7. c4 Be7 8. Nc3 O-O 9. O-O a6 ({Much too risky for a quickplay game is} 9...
Qb6 10. Be3 Qxb2 $2 11. Na4 Qa3 12. Bc1 Qb4 13. Bd2 Qa3 14. Nb5) 10. Be3 Bd7
11. a4 e5 (11... Qc7 $142) 12. Nc2 Be6 13. Kh1 Na5 14. Na3 {Against a strong
opponent I would play 14.Nd5 but in a quickplay against a weaker opponent I
keep it "fluid"} (14. Nd5) 14... Qc7 15. b3 Nc6 16. Qd2 Rfd8 17. Rfc1 Nb4 $2 {
This loses outright.} 18. Nd5 Qa5 $2 {Even worse} 19. Nxe7+ Kf8 20. Nd5 Nfxd5
21. cxd5 Bd7 22. Nc4 (22. Nc4 Qc7 23. Bb6 Qc8 24. Bxd8 Qxd8 25. Qxb4) 1-0

