{90' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. h3 d6 6. d3 Be6 {
Against an opponent who is playing for a draw, one needs to "create some
balance"} 7. Bxe6 ({Better is} 7. O-O {but Brian tends to exchange whenever he
can.}) 7... fxe6 8. a3 a6 9. Be3 Nd4 10. Bxd4 exd4 11. Ne2 e5 12. c4 (12. c3
$142) 12... b5 $5 {Still trying to mix it up but 12.....a5 is better.} 13. b4
Bb6 14. cxb5 (14. Qb3 $142) 14... axb5 15. Qb3 Qe7 $2 {I realised immediately
I should have played 15.......Qd7} 16. O-O Ra4 {To prevent 7.a4} 17. Nd2 $2 (
17. Ng5 $142 h6 18. Ne6 g5 19. Ng3) 17... Qd7 {Preventing 18.Nc4} 18. f4 Ke7 $2
{A nothing move} ({Correct is} 18... Qf7) 19. fxe5 dxe5 20. Nf3 (20. Rf5 $142
Qe6 21. Qxe6+ Kxe6 22. Nf3) 20... Qe6 21. Qxe6+ ({Better} 21. Qd1 {or 21.Qb2
but I "knew" that he would exchange. I felt that I was winning now with his
a-Pawn weak.}) 21... Kxe6 22. Rfc1 Kd6 23. Nd2 $2 {Losing the a-Pawn. Better
23.Ng3 or 23.Ng5} Rha8 24. Nb1 $2 (24. Ng3 $142) 24... Rxb4 25. Kh1 {Surely
the King should go the other way. He was concerned about ........Nxe4} Rb3 26.
Rd1 Bc5 27. Nc1 Rb2 28. Kg1 Ra4 29. Kf1 b4 30. Rd2 ({I was more concerned about
} 30. Nd2 {but then} bxa3 31. Nc4+ Rxc4 32. dxc4 Nxe4) 30... bxa3 31. Na2 Ra8
32. Re2 Rxe2 33. Kxe2 Nh5 34. g4 Nf4+ 35. Kd2 Nxh3 36. Kc2 Rb8 37. Nd2 Nf2 38.
Nc4+ ({Not} 38. Nc1 $4 Rb2#) 38... Ke6 39. g5 Nh3 40. Nc1 Nxg5 41. Nb3 Bb4 42.
Nba5 Ra8 43. Nc6 Bd6 44. Kb3 Nh3 45. Ka2 Nf4 46. Rd1 h5 0-1

