{35 in 75' + 15'} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c6 4. Nc3 Bc5 5. e4 O-O 6. Nge2 Re8
7. a3 a5 8. Rb1 Na6 9. O-O Nc7 10. b4 axb4 11. axb4 Bf8 12. d4 d6 13. d5 cxd5
14. cxd5 Bd7 15. Be3 (15. Qd3 {Fritz}) 15... Nb5 16. Qd3 Ra3 $5 17. Bc1 Qb6 $5
{After a long think. I had expected.........} ({..........} 17... Nxc3 18. Nxc3
Ra8) 18. Bxa3 Nxa3 19. Rb3 Nb5 20. Qd2 (20. Ra1 {Fritz}) 20... Ra8 21. Rc1 Ng4
22. Nd1 Be7 23. h3 Nf6 24. Ndc3 h6 25. Nxb5 Bxb5 26. Nc3 Bd7 27. Rb2 Nh5 {
Threatening 27.......Nxg3} 28. Qd3 Bg5 29. Rcb1 g6 30. Kh2 Ra3 31. h4 Be7 32.
Rc1 g5 33. Qe2 Nf6 34. hxg5 {Getting to the time control this was played too
quickly. Correct was 34.Bh3 or 34.Bf3} Ng4+ 35. Kg1 $2 {Last move to reach the
time control and a mistake. Correct is 35.Kh1} Bxg5 {15' were added to each
clock. Black then "played" Bxc1 much to the amusement amongst the spectators
as I pointed out it was my move.} 36. Rcc2 Nxf2 37. Kh2 Ng4+ 38. Kh1 Ne3 39.
Qf2 (39. Ra2 {Fritz}) 39... Qa7 $2 (39... Qd4 $142 40. Nb1 Nxc2 41. Qxd4) 40.
Ra2 b6 41. Bf3 $2 Nxc2 42. Rxc2 $2 {Playing quickly one error follows another.}
({Correct is} 42. Qxc2) 42... Ra1+ $2 ({Also playing quickly he misses.} 42...
Rxc3 43. Rxc3 Qa1+ 44. Kg2 Qxc3) 43. Kh2 Kg7 44. Bh5 f6 45. Nb5 $6 {Completely
unsound, but it works! With both of us under 5' I thought it worth a try.} Qa6
$2 ({Correct is} 45... Bxb5 46. Qf5 Ra2) 46. Nc7 {Both playing fast now.} Qd3
47. Ne6+ Bxe6 $2 (47... Kh8) (47... Kg8 $142 48. Rc7 Be3) 48. dxe6 Ra7 $2 (
48... f5 $142) 49. Re2 $2 {Defeends e4 and defended by the Bishop} (49. Ra2 $1)
49... Ra3 $2 50. e7 Bf4 {just a bigh rush now.} 51. e8=Q Bxg3+ (51... Qxg3+)
52. Kg2 Bxf2 53. Qg6+ Kh8 54. Qxf6+ Kg8 55. Bf7+ 1-0

