{40 in 1hr 40' + 20'} 1. d4 c6 2. c4 f6 {Mike Surtees "invented" this opening
which he calls "The crab" and is writing a book on it.} 3. Nc3 e5 4. e3 Nh6 5.
Bd3 d6 6. Nge2 g6 7. b3 Nf7 8. Bb2 Bg7 9. Qc2 {Doesn't turn out well. The
Bishop is stuck.} (9. O-O $142) (9. f4 $142) 9... Na6 10. a3 Nc7 11. Rd1 (11.
f4 {Fritz}) 11... Qe7 12. O-O f5 {I would like to play 13.f4 but it would lose
the Bishop.} 13. dxe5 (13. Qd2 {is slightly better.}) 13... dxe5 14. e4 (14. f3
{is a bit more flexible.}) 14... f4 15. f3 g5 16. Rf2 (16. Na4 $142) (16. b4
$142) 16... h5 17. Nb1 (17. b4) 17... Rg8 (17... g4 {would be met by} 18. Nxf4)
18. Kf1 {QS play was better.} g4 19. Ng1 $2 {Loses the h-Pawn.} (19. c5 $142) (
19. b4 $142) 19... Ne6 {He decided that the h-Pawn wasn't worth much.} 20. g3
$2 {Going from bad to worse. Better 20.Qd2} Bh6 21. Rg2 Bd7 22. Ke1 $2 O-O-O
23. Nd2 fxg3 24. hxg3 Be3 25. fxg4 hxg4 26. Nf1 Nd4 27. Bxd4 Bxd4 28. Ne2 (28.
b4 {Saves the a-Pawn but is not best.} Ng5 29. Nh2 c5 30. b5 Qh7 31. a4 Rdf8)
28... Qxa3 29. Nxd4 exd4 30. Qb1 {Short of time now. 30.Qb2 is better but
still lost.} Qb4+ 31. Ke2 Ne5 32. Nd2 Rdf8 33. Qc2 Rf3 34. Qb1 Qc3 35. Rh2 Nxd3
0-1

