{90' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. g3 Nc6 3. Bg2 d6 4. e4 Nf6 5. d3 Be7 6. Ne2 Bg4 7.
f3 Bd7 8. Be3 O-O 9. Nbc3 Qc8 10. Qd2 a6 11. h3 Rb8 12. f4 b5 13. f5 b4 14. Nd5
Nxd5 15. cxd5 Nd8 16. Rc1 a5 17. O-O f6 18. g4 Nf7 19. h4 Kh8 20. g5 {Probably
better to delay this. Fritz prefers 20.Ng3} fxg5 21. hxg5 Qd8 22. g6 Ng5 23.
gxh7 Nxh7 24. Ng3 (24. Rf3 $142) 24... Rc8 25. Bf3 Bg5 26. Bh5 (26. Kg2 $142)
26... Bxe3+ 27. Qxe3 Qg5 {Better is 27.......Nf6 However, Colin is playing for
a draw and wants to exchange whenever he can.} 28. Qxg5 Nxg5 29. Rc2 (29. Kg2)
29... Nh3+ {He offered a draw here.} 30. Kh2 Nf4 31. Be2 Bb5 32. Rf3 Rf6 33.
Bf1 (33. d4 $142) 33... Rh6+ 34. Kg1 Kg8 35. Rd2 (35. d4) 35... c5 36. d4 Bxf1
37. dxe5 dxe5 38. Nxf1 Kf7 39. Ne3 Rch8 40. Ng4 Rh1+ 41. Kf2 Nh3+ 42. Ke3 $6 {
He just wants a draw but I am trying to find some winning chances. However
this is just too crazy and should lose.} (42. Kg3 $142) 42... Re1+ 43. Kd3 ({
of course if} 43. Re2 Rxe2+ 44. Kxe2 Ng1+) 43... c4+ 44. Kc2 Rxe4 45. Nf2 Nxf2
46. Rfxf2 Re3 47. Rd1 Rd8 48. d6 e4 49. Rd4 b3+ 50. axb3 cxb3+ 51. Kd2 Rd3+ 52.
Rxd3 exd3 53. Kxd3 Rxd6+ 54. Kc3 Rb6 55. Rg2 {I knew that I was lost so was
playing very fast.} Rb5 56. Rg1 a4 57. Rg2 {Better 57.Ra1 but I was moving
fast.} Kf6 {He also started moving fast but finds the best move.} 58. Rg6+ Kxf5
59. Rxg7 (59. Rxg7 Ke6 $4 {His "drawing" hopes came to my rescue! He played 59.
.......Ke6?? instantaneously and offered a draw} 60. Ra7 {is drawn as, after I
win both Pawns, his King can reach the Queening square.}) 59... Ke6 $4 ({
However} 59... a3 {wins easily} 60. Ra7 a2 61. Ra4 Ke5 62. Kc4 Rb8) 1/2-1/2

