{30' each/game} 1. d4 f5 2. g3 Nf6 3. c4 g6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. Bg2 O-O 6. Nf3 d6 7.
O-O c6 8. b4 Na6 9. a3 Nc7 10. Bb2 Be6 11. Qd3 Kh8 ({Maybe} 11... h6 {is better
}) 12. Ng5 Bg8 13. e4 h6 (13... fxe4 $142) 14. Nh3 fxe4 15. Nxe4 Bh7 $2 {
Not good.} (15... Nxe4 $142 16. Bxe4 g5) 16. Nxf6 Bxf6 17. Qe2 Qe8 (17... g5
$142) 18. Nf4 Qf7 19. d5 {As I have mentioned in our C.C gamex (15/11/13) C.F.
always playes for a draw against me and 19.d5 is to facilitate exchanges.} cxd5
20. Bxf6+ (20. cxd5 Bxb2 21. Qxb2+) 20... exf6 21. cxd5 (21. Nxd5 $142) 21...
g5 {Several moves too late.} (21... Rfe8 $142) 22. Ne6 Rfe8 23. Qc4 Nxe6 24.
dxe6 Qxe6 25. Qxe6 Rxe6 26. Bxb7 Rd8 27. Rfd1 Re7 28. Bc6 {He was getting
short of time now. I had a little more but stillhad to move fairly fast.} Bg8
29. a4 d5 {I felt that to create winning chances I had to push the d-Pawn.} 30.
a5 d4 31. b5 Bc4 $2 (31... d3 $142) 32. Rd2 $2 (32. Ra4 {Wins the a-Pawn.})
32... d3 33. b6 Ba6 34. Kf1 Re6 35. Bf3 ({Better} 35. Rc1 {but it looks a
risky move in a quicjkplay.}) 35... axb6 36. axb6 Rxb6 {I haven't really won a
Pawn as the d-Pawn is too weak.} 37. Be4 Bc8 {With his time running out all I
can do is keep the pressure on.} 38. f3 {He offered a draw here.} ({he could
simply play} 38. Rxd3 {here, but "saw"} Ba6 {in reply, but then} 39. Rxa6 {
However, it is still drawn.}) 38... f5 39. Bxd3 ({Not} 39. Rxd3 $2 Re8 40. Bd5
Ba6) 39... Rbd6 40. Rad1 (40. Ra8 {is slightly better but difficult to spot in
a time rush.}) 40... Bb7 41. Kf2 g4 42. Bxf5 $2 {Short of time he has to make
a move and blunders.} (42. fxg4 fxg4 43. Ke1 Re8+ 44. Re2 $11) 42... Rxd2+ 0-1

