{30' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. Bc4 Be7 6. d3 Nf6
7. Nc3 O-O 8. Be3 d5 9. Bb3 Nc6 10. d4 Bb4 11. O-O Bxc3 12. bxc3 Ne4 13. c4
dxc4 14. Bxc4 Re8 15. h3 Be6 16. d5 {Fritz gives this a s best, but it is a
very tricky move in a quickplay.} Nc3 $6 {This is [3.77] but only because of a
line that a human player is unlikely to go for in a quickplay.} ({I had
expected} 16... Na5 17. dxe6 Nxc4 18. exf7+ Kxf7 19. Qd3) 17. Qd3 $6 (17. dxe6
$142 Nxd1 18. exf7+ Kh8 19. Raxd1 Qe7 20. fxe8=Q+ {is [3.77] but one doesn't
have time to work all this out in a quickplay.}) 17... Nxd5 18. Ng5 g6 ({If} 
18... Nxe3 19. Qxh7+ Kf8 20. Nxe6+ Rxe6 21. fxe3 Nd4 22. Qh8+ Ke7 23. Qxg7) 19.
Nxe6 Rxe6 $4 {Playing too quickly he blunders.} (19... fxe6 $142 20. Qe4) 20.
Qxd5 Qe7 {It being a quickplay he knocks out a few more rapid moves.} 21. Qb5
b6 22. Bxe6 Qxe6 23. Rfe1 Qe4 24. Bxb6 Qxc2 25. Rac1 Qxa2 26. Qxc6 Rd8 27. Qf6
Qd2 28. Bd4 Qxd4 29. Re8+ Rxe8 30. Qxd4 a5 31. Rxc7 Ra8 32. Rxf7 1-0

