{35 in 1hr 15' + 15'} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 d4 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. g3 Bc5 6. Bg2
Bg4 7. Nbd2 Qe7 8. Nb3 f6 9. Nxc5 Qxc5 10. exf6 Nxf6 11. b3 O-O ({I had
expected} 11... O-O-O) 12. O-O Rad8 13. Bf4 $6 {0.10/0 Leads to triuble. I
thought that I could gain a tempo by attacking his c-Pawn, but I had
overlooked his reply. However, Fritz gives the text as} Nh5 {I was now
convinced that I was lost.} 14. Bd2 {After much thought.} ({If} 14. Bxc7 Rd7
15. Bf4 Nxf4 {and my KS is shattered}) ({If} 14. h3 Bxf3 15. Bxf3 Nxf4 16. gxf4
Rxf4 {is horrid.}) 14... d3 {as expected. I knew that I was losing a piece.}
15. Be3 dxe2 $2 ({I had sat there expecting} 15... Qf5 {for 15' I was going to
reply} 16. exd3 {leaving me with 2 pawns for the piece. He hadn't played 15....
...Qf5 because of 16.Nh4} ({I had decided that} 16. Nh4 {was no good.} dxe2 {
then is followed by} 17. Qxe2 Bxe2 18. Nxf5 Rxf5 19. g4 Bxf1 20. Kxf1 {-0.97/0
is})) 16. Qxd8 exf1=Q+ 17. Rxf1 Nxd8 18. Bxc5 Bxf3 ({If} 18... Rxf3 19. h3) ({
If} 18... Rf5 19. Re1 Rxc5 20. Re8+) 19. Bxf8 Bxg2 20. Rd1 Kxf8 21. Kxg2 {
With Pawns on both sides of the board I felt that RvNN was better than RvBN} (
21. Rxd8+ Kf7 22. Ra8) 21... Ke7 22. f4 b6 23. Kf3 Nf6 24. g4 a5 25. h4 Nc6 26.
a3 Ke6 1/2-1/2

