{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. f3 d5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 O-O
7. Bg5 Nbd7 8. e4 dxe4 ({I wasn't concerned about} 8... h6 9. Bh4 g5 {etc as
it weakens his KS.}) 9. fxe4 e5 10. d5 Qe8 11. Bd3 Nc5 12. Qe2 Nxd3+ 13. Qxd3
Nd7 14. Be3 (14. Qg3 {Fritz}) 14... b6 15. Nf3 Nc5 16. Bxc5 bxc5 17. O-O f5 (
17... Qe7 $142) 18. exf5 $4 {Unbelieveable! How could I play this? The answer
is not taking my opponent seriously and playing too quickly. As I picked up
his Pawn I realised.} ({Correct is} 18. Qe3) 18... e4 19. Qd2 exf3 20. Rxf3
Rxf5 21. Re1 Qf8 (21... Qg6 $142) 22. Rfe3 {I carried on playing quickly. He
started to play slowly and carefully} Ba6 23. Qd3 Rf4 24. Re4 Rxe4 25. Qxe4 Kh8
{Fritz isn't much use here. I have to create some tactics.} 26. Rf1 Qe8 27. Qf4
Rd8 28. h4 Kg8 29. h5 h6 30. Qxc7 $5 {I have to try something.} Bxc4 31. Rf7
Qxf7 32. Qxd8+ Kh7 33. d6 {This is my only hope, even though it allows mate in
6.} Qf1+ 34. Kh2 Bd5 {That's it! Mate in 3.} 35. Kg3 Qxg2+ 36. Kh4 Qh2+ ({
Missing} 36... Qf2+ 37. Kg4 (37. Kh3 Be6#) 37... Be6#) 37. Kg4 Be6+ ({Missing} 
37... Qe2+ 38. Kg3 Qf3+ 39. Kh4 Qf2+ 40. Kh3 Be6#) 38. Kf3 Qxh5+ 39. Kf2 ({Not
} 39. Ke3 Qe5+) 39... Qf5+ 40. Ke1 Qb1+ {He now becomes obsessed with chasing
the King, and starts to get short of time. All he needs to do is push his KS
Pawns} 41. Kd2 Qb2+ 42. Kd3 c4+ 43. Kd4 Qd2+ {What is he doing?} 44. Kc5 Qd5+
45. Kb4 Qb7+ {Just push the KS Pawns!} 46. Kc5 a6 {Short of time he may have
thought he was threatening ......Qb5#} (46... h5) 47. a4 Qd5+ 48. Kb6 a5 49.
Qe7 Qe5 $5 {Playing quickly this is still winning but makes life difficult for
him as, short of time, he has to find the correct next move.} 50. d7 Qe3+ $4 {
Wrong square!} ({Correct is} 50... Qb8+ 51. Ka6 Bxd7 {and his KS Pawns win it
for him}) 51. Ka6 Qe4 52. d8=Q Qc6+ 53. Kxa5 Bc8 (53... Bc8 54. Qdd6 {[Time]
Had he played quicker he could have tried} Qa8+ 55. Kb4 Qb8+ {Hoping for} 56.
Ka3 $4 Qb3#) 54. Qed6 {Black lost on time.} 1-0

