{90' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 f5 3. e3 Nf6 4. Nge2 Be7 5. Ng3 d6 6. Be2 O-O
7. O-O Be6 8. f4 e4 9. d3 exd3 10. Qxd3 Qc8 11. e4 fxe4 12. Ncxe4 Nbd7 13. Bd2
d5 14. cxd5 Bxd5 15. b3 Re8 16. Rac1 $2 {Missing the threat.} (16. Bf3 $142)
16... Bxe4 17. Nxe4 Nxe4 18. Bg4 Nef6 19. Be6+ Kh8 20. f5 Nc5 21. Qc4 Nxe6 22.
fxe6 b6 23. Kh1 c5 24. Bc3 Qc6 25. Rcd1 Rad8 26. Qe2 Rxd1 27. Rxd1 Kg8 {
Being a piece up I play it very conservately.} (27... Ne4 $142 28. Be5 Qxe6)
28. Rf1 Qe4 29. Qb5 Rd8 {30.Rxf6 or 30.Bxf6 was threatened. However I could
have played .......Qxe6} 30. Re1 Qc2 (30... Qd3 {Would have forced the Queens
off.}) 31. Bxf6 gxf6 32. Qa4 Qe2 33. Qh4 Qd2 {This is OK and I still win but
being a piece up I prefer a clearer line.} ({When I played 32.......Qe2 I
intended} 33... Rd1 {However, after} 34. Qg3+ Kf8 35. Qb8+ Kg7 36. Qg3+ {
My King is chased all over the place.}) 34. Qg3+ Kh8 35. a4 {Again missing the
threat.} Rg8 0-1

