{90' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. Nc3 c6 3. e4 {So much for my attempt to play the
Blackmar-Diemer Gambit.} dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Bc4 Ngf6 6. Ng3 e5 $6 {Loses a
Pawn, better 6......Nb6} 7. Qe2 (7. Nf3 $142) 7... Bd6 $2 ({The Pawn was
saveable by} 7... Be7 8. dxe5 Qa5+ 9. Bd2 Qxe5) 8. Nf5 Bf8 9. dxe5 (9. Nf3)
9... Nd5 $2 (9... Qa5+ $142) 10. Bxd5 cxd5 11. Nd6+ Bxd6 12. exd6+ Kf8 13. Nf3
({If} 13. Bf4 Qf6) 13... Nf6 14. Bf4 Qe8 (14... Be6 $142) (14... Ne4 $142) 15.
Qxe8+ Kxe8 16. O-O-O Be6 17. Rhe1 Kd7 (17... Ne4) 18. Ne5+ Ke8 19. Bg5 Nd7 (
19... Rg8 $142) (19... Ne4 $2 20. d7+ Bxd7 21. Nxd7 Kxd7 22. Rxe4) 20. Nxd7 (
20. Nd3 $142) 20... Kxd7 21. Bf4 (21. Be7 {Fritz}) 21... Rac8 22. Rd4 Rc4 23.
Rxc4 dxc4 24. Kd2 f5 (24... f6 $142) 25. Kc3 h6 26. Be5 Rg8 27. b3 cxb3 28.
axb3 Rc8+ 29. Kd3 g5 30. f4 $2 (30. Ra1 $142) 30... g4 (30... Bd5 $142 {
with the threat of 31......Be4+}) 31. h3 $2 {Same error} ({Correct is} 31. c4)
31... h5 32. hxg4 fxg4 33. c4 a6 {A wasted move. I was concerned about.........
..} ({......................} 33... b5 {but} 34. cxb5 Rb8 35. Ra1 Rb7 36. g3
Bxb3 37. f5 {is OK}) 34. Rh1 Bf5+ 35. Kd4 Bg6 36. c5 Rc6 {So as to play ......
b6 but 36.......Rb8 is better} 37. f5 Bf7 38. Bf4 {Intending Re1 -e7} b6 $2 (
38... Rc8 $142) 39. b4 bxc5+ 40. bxc5 Rc8 41. Rb1 Be8 42. Rb6 ({Quicker is} 42.
Rb7+ Kc6 43. d7 {then if} Kxb7 44. c6+ {is mate in 8 [Dick notes mate in15]})
42... Rc6 43. Rb7+ Kd8 44. Rb8+ ({Quicker is} 44. f6) 44... Rc8 45. Rb7 Ra8 46.
Bg5+ Kc8 47. c6 Bxc6 48. Rc7+ Kb8 49. Rxc6 1-0

