{90' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 f5 {The first time I have played
the Jaenisch Gambit} 4. Nc3 fxe4 5. Bxc6 bxc6 6. Nxe5 Qg5 7. Ng4 d5 8. h3 Nf6 (
{Better, which I briefly considered was} 8... Qg6 9. f3 Ba6 10. fxe4 h5 11. Nf2
Qxg2) (8... Qh5) ({I also spent a lot of time on} 8... h5 {but was concerned
that after} 9. d4 Qg6 10. Ne3 {I had not made progress.}) 9. d3 Bxg4 (9... Qg6
$142) 10. hxg4 Qxg4 (10... e3 $142) 11. Qxg4 Nxg4 12. dxe4 Bb4 13. Bd2 O-O 14.
f3 Bxc3 ({After} 14... Nf6 {I was concerned about.} 15. e5 (15. O-O-O Bxc3))
15. Bxc3 Nh6 (15... Ne3 {can be answered by} 16. Kf2 {when} (16. Kd2 Nc4+)
16... Nxc2 17. Rac1 d4 18. Rxc2 {is good for White}) 16. exd5 (16. Rh4 Nf7 17.
O-O-O) 16... Rae8+ 17. Kf2 cxd5 {I felt that I was worse here with a poor
Knight and a weak a-Pawn.} 18. Rh5 (18. Rh4 $142) 18... c6 19. Rg5 g6 20. Rh1
Nf5 21. Re1 Rxe1 22. Bxe1 Nd4 23. c3 Ne6 24. Rg4 Nc5 25. Ke2 Re8+ 26. Kd2 {
Black is threatened with Bf2 and Ra4 winning the a-Pawn.} Nd7 {This solves the
problem.} (26... Nd3 $142 27. Kxd3 Rxe1) 27. Ra4 {He played this very quickly}
(27. Rb4 $142) 27... Nb6 28. Rxa7 Nc4+ 29. Kd1 Nxb2+ (29... Nxb2+ {[Draw] I
could have played on with} 30. Kd2 Nc4+ 31. Kd1 Ne3+ 32. Kd2 Nxg2 33. Bf2 h5
34. Ra6 Re6) 1/2-1/2

