{90' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Nxd7 5. c4 e6 6. Nc3 g6
7. O-O Bg7 8. d3 a6 9. Bf4 Be5 {A bit odd} (9... Qb6 $142) 10. Nxe5 dxe5 11.
Be3 f6 $2 {Even more odd.} 12. Qd2 (12. Rb1 Qa5 13. f4 {Fritz}) 12... Ne7 13.
Rae1 g5 (13... Nc6 $142) 14. g3 Nc6 15. f4 {Playing rather fast and casually
against a lowly graded opponent Fritz prefers 15.a3} gxf4 16. gxf4 exf4 17.
Rxf4 Rg8+ 18. Kh1 Qe7 19. Qf2 b6 20. a3 Rg6 {I wasn't happy at this stage and
wasn't sure how to make progress.} 21. Rg1 (21. Rd1 $142) 21... Rxg1+ 22. Qxg1
O-O-O 23. Rg4 Rf8 (23... Nce5 $142 24. Rg7 Qd6 25. Qd1 Nxd3 26. b3 h6) 24. Na4
Kb7 25. d4 (25. b4 $142 cxb4 26. Bxb6 bxa3 27. Nc5+ Ka8 28. Rg7) 25... cxd4 26.
Bxd4 Qd8 $2 {Now Black is lost.} (26... Nce5 $142) (26... f5 $142) 27. Rg7 e5 {
There is no move.} (27... Kb8 28. Bxb6 Nxb6 29. Nxb6 Ne5) 28. Bxb6 Qc8 29. Nc5+
{I preffered this to 29.Rxd7+} 1-0

