{90' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e5 3. cxd5 Qxd5 4. Nf3 e4 5. Nc3 Bb4 6. Qa4+ Nc6
7. Ng5 Qxd4 8. Qb3 Nh6 (8... Qf6 9. Ngxe4 Qg6 {Fritz. I don't see why I should
give up the e-Pawn.}) 9. Be3 (9. Bf4 $142 Qf6 10. e3 Qe7 11. O-O-O) 9... Qe5
10. g3 (10. O-O-O {is much better.}) 10... f6 11. Nh3 Be6 12. Qc2 O-O-O 13. Bg2
f5 14. O-O Nd4 (14... Ng4 {Fritz}) 15. Bxd4 Rxd4 16. a3 Ba5 ({Fritz prefers} 
16... Be7 {which covers g5}) 17. b4 Bb6 18. e3 Rd6 19. Nf4 Rhd8 20. Rfd1 Bg8
21. Bf1 Ng4 22. Rxd6 Rxd6 23. Rd1 $2 {Missing the threat.} Bxe3 $1 24. Nh3 ({
A little better is} 24. Rxd6 Bxf2+ 25. Kh1 Qxd6 26. Bh3) (24. fxe3 Nxe3 25. Qb2
Rxd1 26. Nxd1 Qxb2 27. Nxb2) 24... Rxd1 {2 Pawns up I keep it simple.} (24...
Nxf2 $142 25. Nxf2 Rc6) 25. Nxd1 Bh6 {Covering the escape square for the
Knight on h3.} 26. Qe2 Qd4 27. Nf4 Bxf4 28. gxf4 Nf6 29. Ne3 g6 30. Qb5 Qb6 31.
Qe5 Qd6 32. Qc3 c6 33. Bc4 Bxc4 34. Nxc4 Qe7 35. Qd4 Kb8 36. Ne5 Nd5 37. Qd2
Qh4 38. b5 Qxf4 39. Qb2 e3 40. Nxc6+ {Desperation.} (40. fxe3 Qxe3+ 41. Kg2
cxb5) 40... bxc6 41. bxc6+ Nb6 42. Qh8+ Kc7 43. Qxh7+ Kxc6 44. Qxg6+ Kc5 45.
fxe3 Qxe3+ 46. Kh1 Qe4+ 47. Qg2 ({If} 47. Kg1 Qg4+ 48. Qxg4 fxg4 {and then
something like} 49. Kg2 Nc4 50. a4 a5 51. Kg3 Ne5 52. Kf4 Nf7 53. Kxg4 Kb4 54.
Kf5 Kxa4 55. Kf6 Nh8 56. Kg7 Kb5 57. Kxh8 a4) 47... Kd4 48. Qxe4+ fxe4 49. h4
e3 50. Kg1 Kd3 51. Kf1 Kd2 0-1

