{30' each/game} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nf3 d6 4. Nc3 Nd7 5. Bc4 e6 6. O-O h6 7.
Be3 Ne7 8. Bb3 b6 9. Qd2 Bb7 10. Rfe1 Rc8 11. a3 g5 12. Qe2 Ng6 13. g3 Qe7 14.
Rad1 a6 15. Bc4 b5 16. Bb3 c5 17. dxc5 dxc5 18. Qd2 $2 {Amazingly this leads
to total collapse.} g4 19. Nh4 Nxh4 20. gxh4 Ne5 21. Qe2 $2 {Now it falls
apart completely} Nf3+ 22. Kh1 Bxc3 23. bxc3 c4 24. Ba2 Bxe4 25. Bf4 f5 26. Rf1
{He has no move.} Ng5+ (26... Nd4+ {Wins the Queen for Bishop & Knight, but I
felt that 26......Ng5+ was neater.}) (26... Qxh4 {also wins easily.}) 27. f3
gxf3 28. Qf2 Nh3 29. Qxf3 {This is even worse than at first sight as he also
loses the Bishop on f4.} Bxf3+ 30. Rxf3 Qb7 31. Rdf1 Nxf4 32. Kg1 Rg8+ 33. Kf2
Qe4 0-1

