{90' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 f5 4. d3 d6 5. O-O Nf6 6. Nc3 f4 $2
{Much too gung-ho even against this opponent [Dick says what he thinks! (SP)]
Better 6.......Be7 or 6.....a6} 7. d4 Nd7 $2 {I was unhappy now this is wrong.}
(7... Bd7 $142 8. dxe5 dxe5 9. Bxc6 Bxc6 10. Nxe5 Qxd1 11. Rxd1 Bxe4) 8. dxe5
$2 (8. d5 $142 Nd4 (8... Ne7 9. Ng5) 9. Nxd4 exd4 10. Ne2 Kf7 11. Nxf4) 8...
dxe5 9. Qd5 Qf6 10. a3 $2 a6 11. Be2 Nb6 12. Qd3 Be6 13. Nd5 Qd8 (13... Nxd5
$142 14. exd5 O-O-O 15. c4 Bf5) 14. Nxb6 ({Better} 14. Rd1 {However, White
just wanted a draw [not sure I did (SP)] and simply tries to maximise
exchanges.}) 14... Qxd3 15. Bxd3 cxb6 16. Bd2 Bd6 17. Bc3 Ke7 18. Rad1 Bg4 19.
Be2 h6 20. Rfe1 Be6 21. Nh4 Rhd8 22. Ng6+ Kf7 ({Not} 22... Kf6 $2 23. Nxf4) 23.
Bh5 Kg8 24. Be2 Kh7 25. Nh4 g6 26. Nf3 Kg7 27. h3 Kf6 28. Nh2 h5 29. h4 b5 30.
Nf3 b4 31. axb4 Bxb4 32. Bxb4 Nxb4 33. c3 Nc6 34. Rxd8 Rxd8 35. Rd1 {Still
trying to exchange.} (35. g3 $142) 35... Rxd1+ 36. Bxd1 {He offered a draw
here.} Na5 37. Nd2 Ke7 38. Kf1 Kd6 39. Be2 Bf7 40. Nf3 Nc4 41. Bxc4 {He took
this instantly.} (41. b3 $142) 41... Bxc4+ 42. Ke1 a5 43. Nd2 Bd3 44. f3 {
This is best! After the game we felt that it was wrong, as the Knight on the
f3 square attacks the e-Pawn and so keeps the King pinned down. However, 44.f3
is -0.55 [according to Dick's copy of Fritz]} a4 45. Kd1 Kc5 46. Kc1 b5 47. Kd1
$2 {This is the losing move.} ({Slightly better is} 47. b4+ {However, 47.b4+
doesn't look immediately attractive as I am left with a passed Pawn.}) 47... b4
48. cxb4+ Kxb4 49. Ke1 Kc5 50. Kf2 Kd4 51. g3 {Ends it quickly but it is lost
anyway.} ({e.g.} 51. Ke1 Ke3 52. Kd1 Kf2 53. Kc1 Kxg2) 51... fxg3+ 0-1

