Bd3 Nbd7 8. Nge2 dxc4 9. Bxc4 e5 10. O-O exd4 11. Nxd4 Ne5 12. Be2 Re8 13. Nc2
(13. a3 $142) 13... Bd6 14. Kh1 Bc7 15. e4 Ng6 16. Bc4 Nh5 17. Ne2 $2 {
Underestimating his attack.} Qh4 {I am now in trouble.} 18. f4 Rxe4 19. Be1 Qf6
20. Bd3 Re7 21. Bc3 Qh4 22. Be1 Qf6 23. Bc3 Qd6 24. Bxg6 $2 Qxg6 25. Be5 Bf5
26. Bxc7 $2 {Awful! Just too casual.} Bxc2 27. Qd2 Be4 28. Nc3 Rxc7 29. Rae1 {
He was getting short of time so I carried on at speed.} Rd7 30. Qe2 f5 31. Nxe4
fxe4 32. f5 Qf7 33. Qxe4 Nf6 34. Qa4 a6 35. g4 Re8 36. g5 Rxe1 37. Rxe1 Nd5 38.
Qg4 Re7 39. Rd1 Qe8 40. Qh4 Re4 41. Qg3 Re3 42. Qf2 Re2 43. Qg3 Qe4+ 44. Kg1
Qe3+ 45. Qxe3 Rxe3 46. Kf2 Re5 47. f6 gxf6 48. gxf6 Rf5+ 49. Kg3 Rxf6 50. Rd2
Kf7 51. a3 Rf4 $2 {Playing fast now he makes life more difficult for himself.}
52. Rxd5 cxd5 53. Kxf4 Ke6 54. Ke3 Ke5 55. b3 b5 56. a4 bxa4 57. bxa4 h5 {
He was now taking only a couple of seconds a move.} 58. Kd3 h4 59. Ke3 d4+ 60.
Kd3 h3 61. a5 Kd5 62. Kd2 Kc4 63. Kc2 d3+ 64. Kd2 Kd4 65. Kd1 Ke3 66. Ke1 d2+
67. Kd1 Kf3 $2 {Moving instantaneously he gives half a point away.} (67... Kd4
{going for the a-Pawn wins easily.}) (67... Ke4 {also wins}) 68. Kxd2 Kg2 69.
Ke2 Kxh2 70. Kf2 Kh1 71. Kf1 {Lancaster A lost the match on board count.}
