{90' each/game} 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. d3 g6 4. Bg2 Bg7 5. O-O O-O 6. Nbd2 c6
7. e4 (7. Nb3 {Fritz}) 7... dxe4 8. dxe4 Bg4 (8... c5 {Fritz}) 9. h3 Bxf3 10.
Qxf3 Nbd7 11. Qe2 e5 {I didn't like blocking the black diagonal, but felt that
12.e5 was good for him.} 12. Nb3 Re8 (12... a5 $142) 13. a4 Qc7 14. Be3 a6 $2 (
14... a5) 15. a5 Bf8 16. Rfd1 c5 $5 {I felt that I had to do something to gain
some space.} ({I considered} 16... Re6) 17. Nd2 Be7 18. Nc4 b5 $6 {A touch of
desperation.} (18... Rad8 {followed by Nb8-c6 is better}) 19. axb6 Nxb6 20.
Nxb6 (20. Bd2) (20. Na5) 20... Qxb6 21. b3 Qb5 22. Qf1 Rec8 {After much
thought. He commented that he thought this was a good move.} ({There were
various blunders to be made e.g.} 22... Red8 23. Rxd8+ Bxd8 (23... Rxd8 24.
Rxa6) 24. Qxb5) 23. g4 c4 $5 (23... Ne8 $142) 24. g5 Ne8 {I was convinced that
I was lost.} ({Much better was} 24... Nh5 25. Rd5 Qb8 26. Rd7 Rc7) 25. Rd5 Qc6
(25... Bc5 $142) 26. Rxe5 Bf8 {Assuming it was lost I started playing quickly.}
(26... Qc7 $142) 27. Rea5 Bg7 (27... cxb3 $142 28. cxb3 Qc3) 28. e5 Qe6 29.
Bxa8 Rxa8 30. Qg2 Rd8 31. Rxa6 Qxe5 32. Ra8 Qxa1+ 33. Rxa1 Bxa1 34. Qc6 cxb3
35. cxb3 Be5 36. b4 Bc7 37. b5 Rc8 38. Bf4 Kg7 39. Bxc7 Nxc7 40. b6 1-0

