{90' each/game} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 f5 3. g3 Nf6 4. d3 Be7 5. Bg2 O-O 6. Nf3 d6 7.
O-O c6 8. e4 Na6 9. Re1 Nc7 10. Rb1 a5 11. a3 Be6 12. Ng5 Bc8 13. a4 h6 14. Nf3
g5 {I wouldn't play this against a strong opponent} 15. d4 fxe4 16. dxe5 ({Not
} 16. Nxe4 Nxe4 17. Rxe4 Bf5 {Winning the exchange}) 16... exf3 17. exf6 Bxf6
18. Qxf3 $2 {Played to prevent his Pawns being disrupted.} ({After} 18. Bxf3
Bxc3 {it is fairly suicidal.}) 18... Bd4 19. Qd3 Bxf2+ 20. Kh1 Bf5 21. Be4 Bxe1
22. Bxf5 Qf6 23. g4 Rae8 24. Be3 Bxc3 25. bxc3 c5 $2 {Played to prevent 26.Bd4}
(25... Qe7 $142) 26. Rxb7 Re7 (26... Qe7) 27. Rb6 Qe5 28. Rxd6 $2 {This loses
although it gives him some chances.} ({Better is} 28. Bf2 {which I expected}
Qe2 29. Kg2) 28... Qxe3 29. Rg6+ Kf7 30. Qf1 Ke8 (30... Ne6 $142) (30... Qe2
$142) 31. Rb6 Kf7 32. Rxh6 Ke8 {Getting short of time I had decided to give
back the exchange. The text is Ok but 32.......Kg8 is better} ({At leat I
avoided} 32... Qe1 $4 33. Be6+) 33. Rb6 Rxf5 {Short of time this is the safest.
} (33... Re5) 34. Rb8+ Kd7 35. Qxf5+ Kc6 {Now he has no good move} 36. Rf8 {
Ends it quickly but if the Queens come off his Pawns fall.} Qc1+ 37. Kg2 Re2+
38. Kg3 Qg1+ 0-1

