{90' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 d6 4. O-O Be7 5. c3 Bd7 6. d4 a6 7.
Ba4 b5 8. Bc2 h6 9. Be3 Nf6 10. Nbd2 O-O 11. h3 Nh7 (11... Qb8) 12. Nh2 (12. d5
{Fritz}) 12... f5 (12... exd4 $142) 13. d5 (13. exf5 {F}) 13... Na5 (13... f4
14. dxc6 Bxc6 15. Bb3+ Kh8 16. Bd5) 14. b4 (14. exf5 {F}) 14... Nb7 15. f4 fxe4
16. fxe5 dxe5 17. Nxe4 Nd6 18. Ng4 Rxf1+ 19. Qxf1 Bxg4 20. hxg4 Ng5 21. Bxg5
Bxg5 22. Nxd6 $4 {Horrific! As usual I was plying much toocasually against a
weak opponent.} Qxd6 $4 (22... Be3+ {23.Resigns!}) 23. Qf5 Bf6 24. Rd1 Rd8 25.
Qe4 Qb6+ 26. Kh1 Qd6 {He offered a draw here.} 27. a4 Qd7 (27... bxa4 $142) 28.
axb5 axb5 29. Ra1 Kf8 30. Bb3 Rc8 31. Ra6 Qe8 32. Qf5 {Still taking it too
casually. I briefly considered 32.d6} ({In fact} 32. d6 cxd6 33. Qd5 Rd8 34.
Ra7 Ra8 {5.05/0 is}) 32... Rd8 33. Re6 (33. Rxf6+ gxf6 34. Qxf6+ Kg8 35. d6+
Kh7 36. dxc7 Rc8 37. Qd6) 33... Qd7 (33... Qf7 $142) 34. Kg1 {Intending to
simply move the King up before taking on e5 with the Rook.} ({However} 34. d6
cxd6 (34... Qxd6) 35. Rxf6+ gxf6 36. Qxf6+ Ke8 37. Qg6+ Kf8 38. Qg8+ Ke7 39.
Qf7#) 34... Ra8 $2 35. Rxf6+ 1-0

