{90' each/game} 1. d4 d6 2. c4 e5 3. d5 f5 4. Nc3 Nf6 5. g3 Be7 6. Bg2 O-O 7.
e4 fxe4 8. Nxe4 Nxe4 9. Bxe4 Nd7 10. Ne2 Nf6 11. Bg2 Bg4 {Fritz prefers 11.....
.Qd8 or 11........Bf5} 12. O-O Qd7 13. b3 {After a long think.} Bh3 14. Bb2
Bxg2 15. Kxg2 Rae8 {Fritz prefers 15......Ng4 I wanted to play 15.......Ne4 so
as to bring it back to g5. However, I was concerned that he wouldplay 16.f4.
Then after 16........exf4 Qd4 treatens mate and the Knight, so the text now
"defends" the Knight in this line.} (15... Ne4 16. f4 exf4 17. Qd4) 16. Nc3 Ng4
17. Ne4 $2 {Missing the threat. He played this quite quickly, centralising the
Knight and "overprotecting" f2.} Rxf2+ 18. Kg1 (18. Rxf2 $142) 18... Rxb2 ({
I wanted to play} 18... Ne3 {then if say He can still answer with} 19. Rxf2 {
so I decided to win the Bishop.} (19. Qc1 Rg2+ 20. Kh1 Qh3)) 0-1

