{35 in 75' + 15'} 1. Nf3 b6 2. e4 Bb7 3. Nc3 e6 4. d4 Bb4 5. Bd3 Nf6 6. Bg5 h6
7. Bxf6 Qxf6 8. O-O c5 $2 9. Ne2 $2 {Missing the best move.} ({Correct is} 9.
Nb5 {which I considered briefly} cxd4 10. Nc7+) 9... cxd4 10. Nexd4 Nc6 11.
Nxc6 dxc6 12. c3 Be7 13. h3 e5 ({13.h3 Threatening to win the Queen! e.g.} 
13... O-O $4 14. e5 Qf4 15. g3) 14. Qe2 Bc8 15. Rfd1 g5 16. Nh2 (16. Ba6 {Fritz
}) 16... h5 17. Qf3 (17. Ba6) 17... Be6 18. Qxf6 Bxf6 19. Be2 Be7 20. Nf3 f6
21. Nd2 O-O-O 22. Nf1 f5 (22... g4 $142) 23. exf5 Bxf5 24. Ne3 Be4 {Rather a
strange move, although we were both short of time and moving dairly quickly.
24......Bg6 is better.} 25. Nc4 Bc2 (25... Bd5 $142) 26. Rxd8+ Rxd8 $2 {
Played quickly but the h-Pawn is left hanging.} (26... Kxd8 $142) 27. Nxe5 Rd2
{Needing to move quickly this is the "active" move.} 28. Bxh5 {I played this
quickly but 28.Re1 is slightly better.} Bc5 29. Rf1 Bf5 (29... Bd3 {is
slightly better but a human player short of time is unlikely to play this.})
30. Nc4 Rc2 {Black attempts to stay active.} (30... Rd8 $142) 31. Ne3 ({
Moving fast I miss the best line.} 31. Bd1 Rc1 32. Bg4 {even though I
considered it}) 31... Bxe3 32. fxe3 Be6 33. Rf2 Rc1+ 34. Kh2 Bxa2 35. Kg3 Be6 (
35... Re1 $142) 36. Bg4 Kd7 $2 37. Bxe6+ {Still moving fast, I momentarily
considered the best line but saw 37.Bxe6+ was a straightforward win so went
for that.} (37. Rf7+ Kd6 38. Rf6 {wins the Bishop.}) 37... Kxe6 38. Kg4 Re1 (
38... a5 39. Z0 a4 40. Z0 a3 {is his only hope.}) 39. Kxg5 Rxe3 40. h4 Re5+ 41.
Kg6 a5 42. h5 Kd5 43. Rf5 1-0

