{40 in 2hr} 1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. c4 c6 4. Nc3 Bf5 5. Qb3 Qb6 6. Qxb6 axb6 7.
cxd5 Nxd5 8. Nxd5 cxd5 9. e3 e6 10. Bb5+ Nc6 11. Ne5 Rc8 {All this took no
time at all. This was the last round and England football was on TV in the
late afternoon. (Slovenia [2] England [3]) The board next to us had agreed a
draw and gone home after 3 moves. Dave was moving fast so I assumed that he
wanted to end as a draw.} 12. Bd2 f6 13. g4 {A bit of a surprise. I had
expected exchanges on c6.} Bg6 14. Nxg6 hxg6 15. f3 {A bit odd.} Bd6 16. Kf2
Kf7 17. Rac1 g5 {According to Fritz one can take on h2.} (17... Bxh2 18. f4 Rh4
19. Ke2 g5 {but it looked too risky}) 18. f4 $2 {Just playing too quickly.}
gxf4 {He now picked up his e-Pawn to take on f4, realised that I could capture
on d4 with the Knight and after a few seconds thought resigned!} (18... gxf4 {
[0-1] It could go} 19. exf4 Nxd4 20. Rxc8 Rxc8 21. Bd3 e5 {and whether he
captures or not I get two united passed Pawns.}) 0-1

