{90' each/game} 1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Bg5 Bf5 4. e3 e6 5. c4 c6 6. Nc3 Be7 7.
Be2 Nbd7 8. O-O O-O 9. a3 a5 10. Rc1 h6 11. Bh4 dxc4 12. Bxc4 Nd5 13. Bg3 N7b6
14. Be2 Nd7 15. Re1 Bh7 16. Bd3 f5 {I was well aware that this was not good.
However, JC just wants a draw and will "do nothing". Thus it is up to me to
create some tactics. I decided that a jS attack might be worth a try. 16......
f5 prevents 17.e4 in view of 17.......Nxc3 and ......f4} 17. Ne5 (17. e4 Nxc3
18. bxc3 f4) 17... N7f6 18. Nf3 Rc8 19. Nd2 Nd7 20. f4 N7f6 21. e4 {At last he
decides to do something.} Nxc3 {The game becomes a comedy of errors. My
"mind-set" that I had to create something didn't help. I saw immediately that
I could create an outside passed Pawn so I didn't look for anything else.} ({
Correct is} 21... Nxe4) 22. bxc3 fxe4 23. Nxe4 Bxe4 24. Bxe4 Nxe4 25. Rxe4 Bxa3
26. Rb1 Rf7 (26... b5 $142) 27. Rxe6 Qd5 ({Correct is} 27... Qd7) 28. Qe2 ({
Missing} 28. Rxh6) 28... Bf8 ({Better} 28... Bd6 {covering e5.}) 29. Re1 a4 30.
Qg4 {Threatening Rxh6 which was already playable.} Qf5 31. Qd1 Qa5 32. Qc2 b5
33. R1e5 a3 34. Qa2 $2 (34. Re1 {was correct.}) 34... Qa7 $2 ({Correct is} 
34... Qxc3 35. Bf2 Qb2) 35. Bf2 Kh8 36. f5 Qd7 37. h3 Bd6 $2 {Getting short of
time and playing quickly I blunder.} 38. Rxd6 Qxd6 39. Qxf7 Rf8 40. Re8 {
For practical purposes he might have done better to keep Rooks on.} Rxe8 41.
Qxe8+ Kh7 42. Qf7 Qd5 43. Qg6+ (43. Qa7 $142 {Threatening 44.f6}) 43... Kh8 $6
(43... Kg8 {is better but to win I have to be able to interpose with .......
Qg8. It works!}) 44. Qe8+ $2 (44. f6 {wins}) 44... Qg8 45. Qe2 (45. Qe7 $142)
45... a2 46. Qb2 Qd5 47. Bg3 Qc4 48. Be5 $2 ({Correct is} 48. Kh2 Qa4 49. Qe2
$1 {then if} a1=Q $2 50. Qe8+ Kh7 51. Qg6+ Kg8 52. f6 Qa7 53. Qe8+ Kh7 54. f7
$18) 48... Qa4 49. Qa1 Qc2 0-1

