c3 c5 8. b3 Ne7 9. Re1 Nc6 10. Ba3 Bh5 11. Be2 Be7 12. Nbd2 O-O 13. Bb2 Rc8 14.
h3 a6 15. Nh2 {Not a good idea} Bg6 16. Bh5 $2 {Leading to trouble} Bxh5 17.
Qxh5 cxd4 18. c4 $2 (18. cxd4 $142 Nb4 19. Red1 Qa5 20. Qe2 Rc2 21. Rdb1) 18...
Nb4 (18... g6 19. Qd1 Ndxe5 {is better.}) 19. Bxd4 $2 (19. Nhf3 {Defending the
e-Pawn is better.}) 19... Nc2 20. Be3 Nxa1 21. Rxa1 Nxe5 22. Ndf3 Nxf3+ 23.
Nxf3 dxc4 24. Ng5 Bxg5 25. Bxg5 Qa5 26. Qg4 Qf5 27. Qg3 cxb3 28. axb3 Qg6 29.
Qe3 h6 30. Bh4 Qh5 31. Bg3 Qc5 {Offering the exchange back. but only by
swapping off Queen & Bishop and leaving Black an easy Rook & Pawn ending.} 32.
Qe4 {He decides that keeping pieces on is his only hope.} Qd5 33. Qb4 Rfd8 34.
Ra5 {Desperation} Qd2 {I couldn't see a definite win based on Queen & Roo on
the 8th rank.} ({Fritz gives} 34... Qd1+ {as -15.54 but without a definite
quick win.} 35. Kh2 Rc1 36. Bd6 (36. Bf4 Qg1+ 37. Kg3 Rd3+ 38. Be3 Rxe3+ 39.
fxe3 Qxe3+ 40. Kh2 f5) 36... Rxd6) ({I felt that} 34... Qd2 {was much clearer
as} 35. Qa4 Rd4 36. Qa3 (36. Qa1 Qc1+) 36... Qc1+ {The Queens are forced off.})
35. Qb6 Rc6 36. Qxb7 0-1

