{90' each/game} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 c5 3. c3 e6 4. Bf4 d5 5. e3 Be7 6. Nbd2 O-O 7.
Be2 Nc6 8. Qc2 Bd7 9. h3 Rc8 10. O-O Nh5 11. Bh2 f5 12. Ne5 Nf6 13. Nxd7 Qxd7
14. dxc5 Bxc5 15. Nf3 Qe7 16. Qb3 $2 (16. Qa4 {is better as he plays it next
move.}) 16... Kh8 17. Qa4 Nd7 (17... Ne4 {Fritz}) 18. Qf4 $5 {A surprise the
Queen could get into trouble here.} a6 19. c4 {[45']} e5 {[62']} 20. Qg5 Qe8 {
20.......e4 is better but I couls see his Queen getting trapped.} 21. cxd5 $2 {
He played this almost instantly. It makes it interesting.} Be7 {He now had a
long think.} 22. dxc6 (22. Qg3 f4 23. Qg4 h5 {wins his Queen.}) 22... Rxc6 23.
Qg3 f4 (23... Rg6 24. Ng5 Rxg5 {is not as good as the text.}) 24. exf4 exf4 25.
Qg4 h5 26. Qxf4 Rxf4 27. Bxf4 Rc2 28. Nd4 $2 {He was now short of time and
this is not the best.} (28. Bd3 $142) 28... Rxb2 29. Rfe1 (29. Bf3 $142) 29...
Qf7 (29... Bb4 $142 30. Red1 Bc5 31. Bf1 Qf7) 30. Bxh5 $2 {Played quickly} (30.
Bc1 {Not the sort of move a human player would make.}) 30... Qxf4 ({Presumably
he only looked at} 30... Qxh5 31. Rxe7) 31. Rxe7 {Giving it up as he is lost.}
({If} 31. Nf3 Bc5 32. Kh1 Rxf2) 31... Qxf2+ {Clocks White (00:20)----Black (00:
46)} 0-1

