{90' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 e6 6. c4 Be7 7.
Be2 e5 8. Nc2 Qb6 9. b3 Be6 10. Be3 Qc7 11. O-O Nbd7 12. Nc3 a6 13. Rc1 Rc8 14.
Qd2 b5 $2 15. Nd5 (15. cxb5 Qxc3 16. Nb4 Qxd2 17. Rxc8+ {So Black can't answer
15.cxb5 with the Queen capture on c3.}) 15... Bxd5 16. cxd5 Qb7 17. g4 (17. Nb4
$142) 17... Bd8 18. Kh1 h6 19. Bg1 ({Fritz prefers} 19. Nb4 {but I wanted,
with the text, to free e3 for the Knight.}) 19... g5 $2 {Leaves a big hole on
f5} 20. Ne3 Kf8 21. Nf5 Ne8 22. Rxc8 Qxc8 23. Rc1 Qb7 24. Rc6 (24. Qb4) 24...
Nb8 25. Rc1 h5 $2 {Trying to get some play.} 26. gxh5 Rxh5 27. f4 Rh7 28. fxg5
Ng7 29. Bg4 ({The more straightforward} 29. Nxd6 {is better}) 29... Nxf5 30.
Bxf5 Rh8 31. Qc2 {Setting a little trap.} Bxg5 {Missing what follows. This
hastens the end.} 32. Qc8+ Qxc8 33. Rxc8+ Kg7 34. Rxh8 Kxh8 35. Ba7 1-0

