{90' each/ game} 1. c4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. d3 h6 5. g3 Bc5 6. Bg2 O-O
7. O-O a6 (7... d6 $142) 8. a3 (8. Nxe5 {Fritz}) 8... d6 9. b4 Ba7 10. Bb2 Rb8
11. e3 Bg4 12. Qc2 Qd7 13. Rac1 Bh3 (13... Be6 $142) (13... a5 $142) 14. Nd5
Bxg2 15. Kxg2 {After a long think, he was already taking a lot of time better
is 15.Nxf6+} Nh7 16. b5 ({I was more worries about} 16. d4 {and 17.c5 blocking
my Bishop.}) 16... Ne7 17. Nxe7+ Qxe7 18. Nh4 Qd7 19. a4 Ng5 20. Qe2 Rfe8 21.
Nf3 Qh3+ 22. Kh1 Qg4 23. Ng1 Qd7 24. h4 Ne6 25. Qg4 {-0.44/0 Looks aggresiive
but} Qe7 {Now 26......Nc5 hits the d & a Pawns} 26. Rfd1 {Defending the d-Pawn
but leaving f2 weak.} f5 27. Qf3 Rf8 28. d4 {He was now getting short of time
and clearly felt that he had to do something definite. 28.Nh3 is better.} f4 (
28... axb5 29. axb5 e4 {Fritz}) 29. Ne2 (29. exf4 $142 exf4 30. Qe4) 29... fxg3
30. Qxg3 exd4 31. Bxd4 ({Not} 31. exd4 Rf5 32. Re1 Rbf8) ({He didn't like} 31.
Nxd4 {because of} Nc5) 31... Nxd4 (31... Bxd4 32. Nxd4 Nc5 {Fritz}) 32. Nxd4
Rf6 33. bxa6 {Short of time he has to find moves. However, 31.bxa6 gives my
Rook access to the b-file.} Qe4+ 34. f3 Qxe3 35. Rg1 Qe7 36. Rge1 {Unpinning
the Knight but relieving the threat to g7.} Qf7 37. Nb5 Rxf3 {White lost on
time.} (37... Rxf3 38. Qg4 Rf4 39. Re7 Rxg4) 0-1

