9. O-O b6 10. Rc1 Bb7 11. Bxf6 Bxf6 12. cxd5 exd5 13. Re1 Re8 14. Qd2 Qd7 (
14... Qd6 {Fritz}) 15. Bb5 a6 16. Bf1 Rxe1 (16... Qd6 $142) 17. Rxe1 Re8 $2 {
Ludicrous. Completely forgetting about the d-Pawn.} 18. Rxe8+ Qxe8 {(=)} 19.
Nxd5 Bd8 20. Nc3 Ne7 (20... b5 {F}) 21. d5 {The further he pushes the d-Pawn
the harder it is to defend.} (21. Ne5 $142) 21... Qd7 22. Ne5 Qd6 23. Nc4 Qc5
24. d6 Nf5 25. d7 $2 {One push too far.} Bc6 (25... b5 $142 26. Na5 Bxa5 27.
d8=Q+ Bxd8 28. Qxd8+ Qf8) 26. Qd3 (26. b4 Qxb4 27. Ne5 Qc5 28. Nxc6 Qxc6 29.
Qd5 {is better for White}) 26... b5 27. Ne3 ({I thought he might try} 27. Na5 {
then} Bxa5 28. d8=Q+ Bxd8 29. Qxd8+ Qf8 30. Qb6 Qc8 $14) 27... Nxe3 28. Qxe3
1/2-1/2

