{90' each/game} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O Bc5 5. d3 O-O 6. h3 (6.
Bxc6 bxc6 7. Nxe5 {is playable but I wanted to keep it "safe"}) 6... d6 7. Nc3
Bd7 8. Bg5 Qc8 $2 {Now his KS Pawns will be weak.} 9. Bxc6 bxc6 10. Na4 {
Equal best with 10.Bxf6 but I wanted to remove the black squared Bishop.} Bb6
11. Nxb6 cxb6 12. Bxf6 gxf6 13. g4 ({Fritz prefers} 13. Qd2 {then} f5 $2 14.
Qg5+ Kh8 15. Qf6+ Kg8 16. Ng5) 13... Kh8 14. Nh2 Rg8 15. Kh1 d5 16. f3 Rg6 17.
Rg1 Rh6 18. Rg3 Qg8 19. Kg2 Qg5 20. Qe1 Qf4 21. Qf2 d4 22. Nf1 c5 23. Nd2 Be6
24. b3 b5 25. Rh1 Qg5 26. Kf1 a5 27. Ke2 {This is all too slow for White.} a4
28. Rgg1 axb3 29. axb3 Ra2 30. h4 ({I was concerned about lines like} 30. Rc1
c4 31. dxc4 bxc4 32. Nxc4 Rxh3 {so I move the h-Pawn to where the Queen
protects it.}) 30... Qe3+ $2 (30... Qf4 $142) 31. Qxe3 dxe3 32. Kxe3 Rxc2 {
I thought that this was wrong as 32......Rg6 would get his other Rook out.
However, Fritz gives 32.......Rxc2 as best.} (32... Rg6 33. c4 Rg8 34. Ra1 {
is better for White}) 33. h5 {Now his Rook is stuck.} Rb2 {After this he is
lost.} (33... c4 $142) 34. Rb1 Rc2 35. Rhc1 Rxc1 36. Rxc1 c4 37. dxc4 bxc4 38.
Nxc4 1-0

