{90' each/game} 1. c4 g6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 c6 5. e3 Bg7 6. Nf3 O-O 7.
Bd3 Bg4 8. h3 Bxf3 9. Qxf3 e6 10. O-O Nbd7 11. cxd5 Nxd5 12. Nxd5 ({I was
expecting} 12. Bd6 {which is best.}) 12... exd5 (12... cxd5 $142) 13. b4 a6 (
13... Nf6 $142) 14. a4 Nb6 15. Rfc1 {After much thought.} ({I intended to
answer} 15. b5 {with} axb5 16. axb5 Rxa1 17. Rxa1 c5 {as the d-Pawn is pinned.}
) 15... Qd7 16. Qe2 Rfe8 17. Qc2 Qe6 18. b5 cxb5 19. axb5 Rec8 20. Qb3 Rxc1+
21. Rxc1 axb5 ({I also considered} 21... a5) 22. Qxb5 Bf8 23. Rb1 Nd7 ({Best is
} 23... Ra6 {which I considered but it just looks too risky.}) 24. Qxb7 {
I felt that I was lost.} Re8 25. Rb5 Nf6 {I have 3 pieces to defend the d-Pwn
and he has 3 pieces to attack it. However, he would be able to swap his black
squared Bishop for Knight and I would lose the Pawn.} 26. Be5 Re7 27. Qb6 {
Salvation!} (27. Qa8 $142) 27... Nd7 {Getting it wrong in return. The Queen
exchange was best.} 28. Qxe6 fxe6 29. Bf4 {I was quite happy here.} Bg7 30. Rb7
Rf7 31. Bb5 Nf8 32. Rxf7 Kxf7 33. Kf1 Bf6 34. Ke2 g5 {Best to provide g6 for
the Knight.} 35. Bd6 Be7 36. Bxe7 Kxe7 37. Kd3 Kf6 38. e4 dxe4+ 39. Kxe4 Ng6
40. g3 h6 {(=)} 41. Be8 Ne7 42. f4 {With time getting short he makes an awful
move. The Knight forks everything.} Nf5 43. fxg5+ hxg5 44. Kd3 1/2-1/2

