{30' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. a3 {Carlsen played this a week ago.} Nc6 3. b4 cxb4
4. axb4 Nxb4 5. d4 e6 (5... d5 {is usual.}) 6. c3 Nc6 7. d5 {I wouldn't
necessarily play this in a normal game.} exd5 8. exd5 Qe7+ (8... Ne5 $142) 9.
Be2 Ne5 10. f4 Ng4 11. Qd4 (11. Qd3 $142) 11... N8h6 12. Nf3 Nf5 13. Qd3 Nfe3
$2 (13... g6 $142) 14. h3 (14. Ra4 $142 {Not an easy move to spot in a
quickplay}) 14... Nxg2+ 15. Kf1 N4e3+ 16. Kf2 Nxf4 17. Qxe3 Qxe3+ 18. Bxe3 Nxd5
19. Bd4 {Black has 4 Pawns for his piece but is position is awful.} b6 (19...
Be7 $142 {then if} 20. Bxg7 Rg8 21. Bd4 Nf4) 20. Bc4 Bb7 21. Re1+ Ne7 (21...
Kd8 {is better, but after} 22. Ng5 {it is awkward for him}) 22. Ng5 Bc6 {
Played because after 23.Nxf7 24.Nd6+ forks King and Bishop.} ({Fritz prefers} 
22... f6 23. Nf7 d5) 23. Nxf7 (23. Bxf7+ $142 Kd8 24. Bc4) 23... d5 24. Nxh8
dxc4 25. Nd2 Bd5 (25... b5 26. Ra6) 26. Re5 Kd7 (26... O-O-O $142) 27. Bxb6
axb6 28. Rxd5+ Nxd5 29. Rxa8 Bc5+ 30. Kf3 Nxc3 31. Nxc4 b5 32. Ne5+ Ke6 33. Nd3
Bd4 {Time was getting short now.} 34. Ra6+ Kd5 35. Nf7 Kc4 36. Nfe5+ Kb3 37.
Nc6 Kc4 {All this was played quickly 37.......Bf6 is better.} 38. Nxd4 Kxd4 39.
Nb4 (39. Nc1 $142) 39... Kc4 40. Nc6 {I had decided to give up the Knight for
the b-Pawn and then win his KS Pawns.} b4 41. Rb6 Kc5 42. Rxb4 Nd5 43. Rb7 Kxc6
44. Rxg7 Nf6 45. Rf7 Nd5 46. Rxh7 Kd6 47. Ra7 Nf6 48. Kf4 Nd5+ 49. Kg5 Ke5 50.
Ra5 {Black lost on time.} 1-0

