{40 in 1hr 40' + 50' + 30'' increment} 1. e4 c6 2. c4 d5 3. cxd5 cxd5 4. exd5
Nf6 {Better than the 4.......Qxd5 that I played against Nigel Short.} 5. Nc3
Nxd5 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. Bb5 Nxc3 (7... g6 {Fritz}) 8. bxc3 Bd7 (8... g6) 9. O-O e6
10. d4 a6 11. Bd3 Qc7 {Amongst other things this prevents 12.Bf4} 12. Re1 Be7 (
{I was tempted to play} 12... Bd6 {then if} 13. d5 Ne5 {However it looked
risky but Fritz gives it as OK}) 13. Ng5 {He thought about this for 20'} Bxg5 {
After much thought.} 14. Bxg5 Ne7 (14... O-O {Fritz}) 15. Bxe7 Kxe7 16. Qf3 (
16. d5 Kf8 17. Qb3 {Fritz}) 16... h5 ({Fritz likes} 16... Qxc3 {but it looked
risky.}) 17. d5 Rh6 18. Rab1 Rb8 19. Bf5 (19. Qe4 {F}) 19... Rf6 20. dxe6 (20.
Qxh5) 20... fxe6 21. Qxh5 Qc5 ({or} 21... Qf4) 22. Bg4 ({Fritz prefers} 22. g4
Bc6 23. Rbd1 {but 22.g4 looks risky}) 22... Qxf2+ (22... Qxf2+ 23. Kh1 Bc6 24.
Rg1 Rbf8 25. h3 $15) 1/2-1/2

