{90' each/game} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bd7 6. Be2 Qb6 7.
a3 f6 8. O-O fxe5 9. dxe5 Nge7 10. Bd3 g6 11. Qe2 Bg7 12. b4 c4 13. Bc2 O-O-O
14. a4 Nf5 15. Na3 {Too conservative} (15. Be3 $142 Qc7 16. Bc5 Be8 17. Nd4)
15... Nce7 16. g4 Nh6 17. h3 Kb8 18. Be3 Qc7 19. Nb5 Bxb5 20. axb5 b6 21. Ra6
Nf7 22. Bd4 (22. Rfa1 $142 Qb7 ({If} 22... Nc8 23. Nd4) 23. Qe1 Rd7 24. Rxa7
Qxa7 25. Rxa7 Rxa7 26. Bxb6 {I was unsure about goin into Queen v 2 Rook even
though I had the better position.}) 22... Rhf8 23. Rfa1 Nc8 24. Qe3 Rd7 25. Re1
{Deciding that I couldn't breakthrough on the QS.} (25. Rxa7 $142 Qxa7 26. Rxa7
Kxa7 27. Kg2 {but again I wasn't confident about this.}) 25... Qd8 26. h4 {
Time was now getting short. He had less than me and play starts to speed up.}
Nh6 27. Ng5 Re8 28. Qg3 Bh8 29. Be3 Qc7 30. Nf3 Nf7 31. Bf4 Nd8 32. Nd4 Rf7 33.
Bg5 {Threatens 34.Bxd8 and 35.Nc6+} Ka8 34. Qe3 Bg7 35. Qg3 h6 $2 36. Bd2 (36.
Bxd8 Qxd8 37. Nc6 Qd7 38. Bxg6 {I didn't have time to work it all out and
played a "safe" move.}) 36... Ref8 37. f4 g5 38. hxg5 hxg5 39. f5 {With no
time to analyze properly I felt I had to play this if I was going to win.} exf5
40. gxf5 {he was running out of time.} (40. Bxf5 $142) 40... Re8 41. Nf3 g4 42.
Qxg4 Bxe5 43. Kf1 (43. f6 {I was playing "safe" moves.}) 43... Rh7 $2 (43...
Rg7 $142) {Again after a few seconds thought.} 44. Qg6 (44. Rxe5 Rxe5 45. Bf4 {
which I immediately considered is better.}) 44... Rh1+ 45. Kg2 Rxe1 46. Bxe1
Rh8 47. Nxe5 Qxe5 48. Qg3 $2 {Disaster! but he doesn't have time to spot it.}
Nf7 $2 (48... Qe2+ $1) 49. Qxe5 Nxe5 50. Ra1 Ne7 51. Rd1 {I now stopped
recording in a time scramble. It went something like} Rg8+ 52. Kf1 Rf8 53. Rxd5
Nxf5 54. Rxe5 Nd4+ 55. Bf2 Nxc2 56. Ke2 Rh8 57. Kd2 Na3 58. Kc1 {and Black
resigned with only a few seconds left.} 1-0

