1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. Ne2 {A bit unusual. The Knight will not be well
placed on g3.} e6 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. Bd3 (6. Nc3 $142) 6... Bxd3 7. Qxd3 Qd7 {
To prevent 9.Qb5+ after 8........c5} 8. Nd2 c5 9. Nf3 Nc6 10. c3 cxd4 (10... h5
{Fritz}) 11. cxd4 Bb4+ 12. Nd2 ({Better} 12. Bd2 {. However after.......} Rc8 {
he can't play} 13. Bxb4 {because of} Nxb4 14. Qb3 Nc2+) 12... Rc8 13. O-O Nge7
14. Nb3 Na5 $5 {Fritz doesn't like this.} 15. a3 (15. Nxa5 Bxa5 16. Nh5 Kf8 17.
Bg5 {Fritz}) 15... Nxb3 16. Qxb3 Ba5 17. Bg5 {Threatening 18.Bxe7 when 18......
.Qxe7 would lose the Bishop on a5 to 19.Qb5+} Bb6 18. Qd3 h6 19. Bd2 Qa4 20.
Bc3 O-O 21. Rac1 Nc6 (21... Qc4) (21... Rc4 {Fritz}) 22. Ne2 Rc7 23. Kh1 {
After much thought. However, 23.Qd1 is better.} Rfc8 24. f4 $2 {Missing the
threat. 24.Qd1 was best.} Nxd4 25. Rcd1 Nf5 26. Rf3 (26. Bd4 $142) 26... Qc4 (
26... d4 27. Bb4 Ne3 {However in these short time limit matches it is better
to play safe solid moves}) 27. g4 Ne7 {Again I play it solid.} (27... Nh4 {
Fritz}) 28. f5 {he was now very short of time and decides a KS attack might be
best} Qxd3 {Again playing it solid.} (28... Qxg4 {Opens the g-file and is not
the thing to play in these time conditions}) 29. Rdxd3 Rc4 30. fxe6 fxe6 31.
Nf4 R8c6 {Still playing it solid} (31... Nc6 32. Nxe6 d4 33. Rf4 Nxe5 {etc is
the choice of Fritz}) 32. h4 Kh7 33. Nh5 {Trying to muddy the waters at the
cost of the g-Pawn.} Rxg4 34. Rf7 Nf5 {Still playing it safe 34.......Rxh4+ is
no doubt best. However, his h-Pawn is a goner.} 35. Nf6+ Kg6 36. Nxg4 Kxf7 37.
h5 Rc4 38. Nh2 Rh4 39. Kg2 Rxh5 40. Ng4 Rh4 41. Kf3 Rh3+ 1-0

