5. d4 cxd4 6. Nxd4 Be7 7. Be2 O-O 8. O-O b6 9. Be3 Bb7 10. f3 a6 11. Rc1 Nbd7
12. Kh1 Rc8 13. Qd2 Qc7 14. Rfd1 Qb8 15. b3 Rfe8 16. Bd3 Nc5 17. Nde2 Red8 18.
Qe1 ({Fritz prefers} 18. Bc2 {or 18.Bb1}) 18... Ba8 19. Bb1 (19. Nd4 {F}) 19...
b5 20. cxb5 axb5 21. Nd4 b4 22. Nce2 d5 23. exd5 (23. Bf4 {Fritz. Then if} e5
24. Nf5) 23... Nxd5 24. Bf2 (24. Bd2 $142) 24... Bg5 25. Nc6 {This surprised
him!} (25. Rxc5 Rxc5 26. Nxe6 fxe6 27. Bxc5) 25... Bxc6 26. Rxc5 Be7 27. Rcc1
Bd6 28. Bg3 Bxg3 29. hxg3 Bb5 30. Kh2 Bxe2 31. Qxe2 g6 32. Rxc8 Rxc8 33. Qe1
Qa7 34. Rd2 Nc3 35. Bd3 {I could try to defend the a-pawn but decided that
activating my Bishop was better. If the a-pawn goes he has an extra Pawn on
the KS but if my pieces are ative I should be OK. Fritz says 35.Bd3 is best.}
Nxa2 $2 {Losing a piece} 36. Qa1 {Pins the Knight and he assumes that.....} Rc5
{....Threatening mate, will allow him time to play 37.Ra5} 37. Bf5 $1 Qe7 {
Shell shocked he fails to find the best move..........} (37... Rc3 $142 38.
Rxa2 Qe3 39. Bc2 {However, it must be a win for White.}) 38. Rxa2 1-0

