{90' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 e6
7. Qd2 Be7 8. a4 b6 9. f3 (9. Bc4 $142) 9... Qc7 10. Be2 Bb7 11. O-O Nbd7 12.
Kh1 O-O 13. Nb3 Rac8 14. Bd3 Ne5 15. Bf4 d5 16. exd5 Nxd5 17. Nxd5 Bxd5 $6 {
Going for some play at the cost of a Pawn. Better is 17.......exd5} 18. Bxa6
Nc4 19. Qc1 ({Alternatively} 19. Bxc8) ({........and} 19. Bxc7 Nxd2 20. Bxc8
Nxf1 21. Bd7 {are about the same.}) 19... e5 20. Bxc8 exf4 21. Ba6 Ne3 {
This Knight is very strong and worth the exchange.} 22. Rf2 Rd8 23. Rd2 Ra8 24.
Bd3 Rc8 {Threat 25.......Bxb3} 25. Nd4 Bc5 26. Nb5 Qc6 $5 {Deciding to go all
out for the attack} (26... Qe5 $142) 27. Na7 {With time running down I wasn't
sure about this.} Qb7 28. Nxc8 Bxf3 {Looks scary but +-} 29. Ne7+ {Trying a
diversion as either Queen or Bishop takes would gain me a tempo.} Kf8 (29...
Bxe7 {Fritz}) 30. b4 {Short of time another diversion to gain a tempo. 30.Bf1
is better} Bxg2+ 31. Kg1 {Very scary!} Bxb4 32. Rf2 {Moving fairly quickly now.
} (32. Ba6 {Fritz}) 32... Bc5 33. Qd2 Ng4 34. Raf1 {I knew that I was lost.}
Bh1 $4 {Threatening 35.......Qg2# but moving quickly he misses the reply.} (
34... Bxf1 {and I have to resign.}) 35. Be4 {He looked shell-shocked and
resigned almost straight away.} ({However,} 35. Be4 Qxe7 36. Bxh1 Qg5 37. Bg2
g6 38. h3 Nxf2 39. Rxf2 Qe5 40. c4 Be3 41. Qc2 Qe6 {1.52/0 is}) 1-0

