{90' each/game} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. f3 e5 6. Nb3 a6
7. a4 Be7 8. Be3 O-O 9. Be2 d6 10. O-O Be6 11. c4 Rc8 12. Nc3 Na5 13. Nxa5 Qxa5
14. Nd5 Nxd5 15. exd5 {Against a strong opponent I'd play 15.cxd5 but I felt
that I could frighten Andre on the KS} Bf5 16. f4 (16. Qb3 {Fritz}) 16... Bd7 (
16... exf4 $142) 17. fxe5 dxe5 18. b3 {Playing carefully. Fritz prefers 18.d6}
Bc5 19. Bxc5 Qxc5+ 20. Kh1 f6 ({If} 20... f5 {then} 21. b4) 21. Bg4 {Now 21....
...f5 is best but as he just wants a draw and has just played ......f6. I
expected 21.......Bxg4} Bxg4 22. Qxg4 Qe7 {He offered a draw here.} 23. Rf3
Rcd8 24. Raf1 Rd6 25. h4 f5 $2 {Simply loses. As is often the case a player
facing an attack feels that they have to "do something".} 26. Rxf5 Rxf5 27.
Rxf5 Rg6 28. Qe4 Rh6 29. g3 Qd7 30. Kg2 Rf6 31. Rxe5 h6 32. c5 Rf7 1-0

