prefers} 28... f3+ 29. Nxf3 h5) 29. Nf3 Ng5 30. Nxg5 Qxg5 31. Qf3 h5 32. Rc1
Kf7 (32... Kg7 $142) 33. Rg1 Qg6 34. Qe2 hxg4 35. hxg4 Ke7 36. f3 Rh8 37. Qd1
Rc8 38. Rf1 Qh7 {Getting very short of time I repeat moves to get to move 40.}
39. Rf2 Qg6 40. Rf1 Qh7 41. Rf2 Kf6 42. Qh1 Qg6 43. Qd1 Qh7 44. Qh1 Qg6 45. Qd1
Qg5 46. Qh1 Kg7 47. Kg1 Qg6 48. Kg2 Rh8 49. Qd1 Qh7 50. Kf1 Qg6 51. Kg2 Rh6 {
I now realised that I needed the Rook in front of the Queen on the h-file.} 52.
Qc2 Qe8 {Else 53.Qc6 is a problem.} 53. Kf1 {The losing move. Better is 53.Kg1}
Rh1+ 54. Ke2 Qb5+ 55. Kd2 Bb4+ 56. Bc3 Qa5 57. Bxb4 Qxb4+ 58. Kd3 Re1 59. Re2
$4 {After 5 hours he blunders.} (59. Qc7+ $142 Kg6 60. Qxf4 Rd1+ 61. Rd2 $11)
59... Qb5+ 0-1

