{30' each/game} 1. e4 d5 {He used to play this a lot.} 2. e5 Bf5 3. d4 e6 4. h4
h6 5. Bd3 Bxd3 6. Qxd3 c5 7. c3 Nc6 8. a3 cxd4 9. cxd4 Qa5+ 10. Bd2 Qb6 11. Bc3
Nge7 12. g4 {OK in a quickplay.} Ng6 13. Ne2 Be7 14. h5 Nf8 (14... Nh4 {Fritz})
15. Nd2 Nd7 16. f4 O-O-O 17. b4 f6 18. Nb3 fxe5 (18... a6 {Fritz}) ({If, say,
instead, he played} 18... Rhf8 {then} 19. b5 Ncb8 20. Ba5 {traps his Queen})
19. fxe5 (19. dxe5 {Fritz}) 19... a6 {Forced} 20. Nf4 Na7 (20... Bg5 $142) 21.
Ng6 Rhe8 22. Rc1 (22. O-O {Fritz}) 22... Nb5 (22... Kb8 $142) 23. Bd2+ Kb8 24.
a4 Na3 25. Nc5 Nc4 26. Nxe7 Nxd2 (26... Rxe7) 27. Nxd5 ({Better is} 27. Nxa6+ {
but hard to spot in a quickplay.}) 27... Nxc5 28. bxc5 Qb2 29. Qxd2 Qxd2+ 30.
Kxd2 Rxd5 31. Ke3 Red8 32. Rcd1 Kc7 33. Rhf1 R8d7 34. Ke4 b6 35. cxb6+ Kxb6 36.
Rf2 Ka5 37. Rfd2 Rc7 38. Ra2 Rc4 {Both short of time I stopped scoring here.
However, he captures my a-Pawn but I got his e-Pawn. Rooks on a6 and the
second rank stopped his a-Pawn and I queened my e-Pawn to win.} 1-0

